#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"This is a free Rust course developed by the Android team at Google. The "
"course covers the full spectrum of Rust, from basic syntax to advanced "
"topics like generics and error handling."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah kursus Rust gratis yang dikembangkan tim Android di Google. "
"Kursus ini membahas Rust secara menyeluruh, mulai dari sintaks dasar hingga "
"topik lanjutan seperti generics dan error handling."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"The latest version of the course can be found at "
"<https://google.github.io/comprehensive-rust/>. If you are reading somewhere"
" else, please check there for updates."
msgstr ""
"Versi terbaru kursus tersedia di <https://google.github.io/comprehensive-"
"rust/>. Jika Anda membacanya di tempat lain, periksa situs tersebut untuk "
"mendapatkan pembaruan."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"The course is available in other languages. Select your preferred language "
"in the top right corner of the page or check the [Translations](running-the-"
"course/translations.md) page for a list of all available translations."
msgstr ""
"Kursus ini tersedia dalam bahasa lain. Pilih bahasa yang Anda inginkan di "
"sudut kanan atas halaman atau lihat halaman [Terjemahan](running-the-"
"course/translations.md) untuk daftar seluruh terjemahan yang tersedia."

#: src/index.md
msgid "The course is also available [as a PDF](comprehensive-rust.pdf)."
msgstr "Kursus ini juga tersedia [dalam bentuk PDF](comprehensive-rust.pdf)."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"The goal of the course is to teach you Rust. We assume you don't know "
"anything about Rust and hope to:"
msgstr ""
"Kursus ini bertujuan mengajarkan Rust kepada Anda. Kami menganggap Anda "
"belum mengenal Rust dan berharap dapat:"

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"Give you a comprehensive understanding of the Rust syntax and language."
msgstr "Memberikan pemahaman menyeluruh tentang sintaks dan bahasa Rust."

#: src/index.md
msgid "Enable you to modify existing programs and write new programs in Rust."
msgstr ""
"Membekali Anda untuk mengubah program yang ada dan menulis program baru "
"dalam Rust."

#: src/index.md
msgid "Show you common Rust idioms."
msgstr "Memperkenalkan idiom Rust yang umum digunakan."

#: src/index.md
msgid "We call the first four course days Rust Fundamentals."
msgstr "Kami menyebut empat hari pertama kursus ini Rust Fundamentals."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"Building on this, you're invited to dive into one or more specialized "
"topics:"
msgstr ""
"Setelah itu, Anda dapat mendalami satu atau beberapa topik khusus berikut:"

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"[Android](android.md): a half-day course on using Rust for Android platform "
"development (AOSP). This includes interoperability with C, C++, and Java."
msgstr ""
"[Android](android.md): kursus setengah hari tentang penggunaan Rust untuk "
"pengembangan platform Android (AOSP), termasuk interoperabilitas dengan C, "
"C++, dan Java."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"[Chromium](chromium.md): a half-day course on using Rust in Chromium-based "
"browsers. This includes interoperability with C++ and how to include third-"
"party crates in Chromium."
msgstr ""
"[Chromium](chromium.md): kursus setengah hari tentang penggunaan Rust dalam "
"browser berbasis Chromium, termasuk interoperabilitas dengan C++ dan cara "
"menyertakan crate pihak ketiga dalam Chromium."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"[Bare-metal](bare-metal.md): a whole-day class on using Rust for bare-metal "
"(embedded) development. Both microcontrollers and application processors are"
" covered."
msgstr ""
"[Bare-metal](bare-metal.md): kelas sehari penuh tentang penggunaan Rust "
"untuk pengembangan bare-metal (embedded), mencakup microcontroller dan "
"application processor."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"[Concurrency](concurrency/welcome.md): a whole-day class on concurrency in "
"Rust. We cover both classical concurrency (preemptively scheduling using "
"threads and mutexes) and async/await concurrency (cooperative multitasking "
"using futures)."
msgstr ""
"[Concurrency](concurrency/welcome.md): kelas sehari penuh tentang "
"concurrency dalam Rust. Kami membahas concurrency klasik (penjadwalan "
"preemptive menggunakan thread dan mutex) serta concurrency async/await "
"(cooperative multitasking menggunakan future)."

#: src/index.md
msgid "Non-Goals"
msgstr "Di Luar Tujuan Kursus"

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"Rust is a large language and we won't be able to cover all of it in a few "
"days. Some non-goals of this course are:"
msgstr ""
"Rust merupakan bahasa yang luas dan tidak dapat kami bahas seluruhnya dalam "
"beberapa hari. Hal-hal berikut berada di luar tujuan kursus ini:"

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"Learning how to develop macros: please see [the Rust Book](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/book/) and [Rust by Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-"
"example/macros.html) instead."
msgstr ""
"Mempelajari cara mengembangkan macro: silakan merujuk [the Rust "
"Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/) dan [Rust by "
"Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/macros.html)."

#: src/index.md
msgid "Assumptions"
msgstr "Prasyarat"

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"The course assumes that you already know how to program. Rust is a "
"statically-typed language and we will sometimes make comparisons with C and "
"C++ to better explain or contrast the Rust approach."
msgstr ""
"Kursus ini menganggap Anda sudah bisa memprogram. Rust adalah bahasa dengan "
"static typing. Terkadang kami membandingkannya dengan C dan C++ untuk "
"memperjelas pendekatan Rust atau menunjukkan perbedaannya."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"If you know how to program in a dynamically-typed language such as Python or"
" JavaScript, then you will be able to follow along just fine too."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda bisa memprogram dalam bahasa dengan dynamic typing seperti Python "
"atau JavaScript, Anda juga dapat mengikuti kursus ini dengan baik."

#: src/index.md
msgid ""
"This is an example of a _speaker note_. We will use these to add additional "
"information to the slides. This could be key points which the instructor "
"should cover as well as answers to typical questions which come up in class."
msgstr ""
"Ini contoh _catatan pengajar_. Kami menggunakannya untuk menambahkan "
"informasi pada slide, seperti hal-hal utama yang sebaiknya dibahas pengajar "
"dan jawaban atas pertanyaan yang sering muncul di kelas."

#: src/running-the-course.md src/running-the-course/course-structure.md
msgid "This page is for the course instructor."
msgstr "Halaman ini ditujukan bagi pengajar kursus."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"Here is a bit of background information about how we've been running the "
"course internally at Google."
msgstr ""
"Berikut sedikit latar belakang tentang cara kami menyelenggarakan kursus ini"
" secara internal di Google."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"We typically run classes from 9:00 am to 4:00 pm, with a 1 hour lunch break "
"in the middle. This leaves 3 hours for the morning class and 3 hours for the"
" afternoon class. Both sessions contain multiple breaks and time for "
"students to work on exercises."
msgstr ""
"Kami biasanya menyelenggarakan kelas dari pukul 9:00 pagi hingga 4:00 sore, "
"dengan istirahat makan siang selama 1 jam di tengahnya. Dengan demikian, "
"kelas pagi dan sore masing-masing memiliki waktu 3 jam. Kedua sesi mencakup "
"beberapa waktu istirahat serta waktu bagi peserta untuk mengerjakan latihan."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid "Before you run the course, you will want to:"
msgstr "Sebelum menyelenggarakan kursus, sebaiknya Anda:"

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"Make yourself familiar with the course material. We've included speaker "
"notes to help highlight the key points (please help us by contributing more "
"speaker notes!). When presenting, you should make sure to open the speaker "
"notes in a popup (click the link with a little arrow next to \"Speaker "
"Notes\"). This way you have a clean screen to present to the class."
msgstr ""
"Pelajari materi kursus hingga Anda memahaminya. Kami menyertakan catatan "
"pengajar untuk menyoroti hal-hal utama; bantu kami dengan menambahkan "
"catatan pengajar! Saat mengajar, pastikan catatan dibuka dalam popup: klik "
"tautan berpanah kecil di samping “Speaker Notes”. Dengan begitu, layar yang "
"ditampilkan kepada peserta tetap bersih."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"Decide on the dates. Since the course takes four days, we recommend that you"
" schedule the days over two weeks. Course participants have said that they "
"find it helpful to have a gap in the course since it helps them process all "
"the information we give them."
msgstr ""
"Tentukan tanggalnya. Karena kursus berlangsung empat hari, kami menyarankan "
"menyebarkan jadwalnya selama dua minggu. Menurut peserta, jeda di antara "
"pertemuan membantu mereka mencerna semua informasi yang kami berikan."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"Find a room large enough for your in-person participants. We recommend a "
"class size of 15-25 people. That's small enough that people are comfortable "
"asking questions --- it's also small enough that one instructor will have "
"time to answer the questions. Make sure the room has _desks_ for yourself "
"and for the students: you will all need to be able to sit and work with your"
" laptops. In particular, you will be doing significant live-coding as an "
"instructor, so a lectern won't be very helpful for you."
msgstr ""
"Cari ruangan yang cukup luas untuk peserta tatap muka. Kami menyarankan "
"15-25 orang per kelas. Jumlah ini cukup kecil agar peserta nyaman bertanya "
"dan satu pengajar masih punya waktu menjawab pertanyaan. Pastikan tersedia "
"_meja_ untuk Anda dan peserta: semua orang perlu duduk dan bekerja "
"menggunakan laptop. Sebagai pengajar, Anda akan banyak melakukan live "
"coding, sehingga podium tidak terlalu membantu."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"On the day of your course, show up to the room a little early to set things "
"up. We recommend presenting directly using `mdbook serve` running on your "
"laptop (see the [installation "
"instructions](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-rust#building)). This "
"ensures optimal performance with no lag as you change pages. Using your "
"laptop will also allow you to fix typos as you or the course participants "
"spot them."
msgstr ""
"Pada hari pelaksanaan, datanglah lebih awal untuk menyiapkan ruangan. Kami "
"menyarankan presentasi langsung menggunakan `mdbook serve` yang berjalan di "
"laptop Anda; lihat [petunjuk "
"instalasi](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-rust#building). Dengan "
"cara ini, performa optimal tanpa jeda saat berpindah halaman. Menggunakan "
"laptop sendiri juga memungkinkan Anda memperbaiki typo yang ditemukan oleh "
"Anda atau peserta."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"Let people solve the exercises by themselves or in small groups. We "
"typically spend 30-45 minutes on exercises in the morning and in the "
"afternoon (including time to review the solutions). Make sure to ask people "
"if they're stuck or if there is anything you can help with. When you see "
"that several people have the same problem, call it out to the class and "
"offer a solution, e.g., by showing people where to find the relevant "
"information in the standard library."
msgstr ""
"Biarkan peserta mengerjakan latihan sendiri atau dalam kelompok kecil. Kami "
"biasanya menyediakan 30-45 menit untuk latihan pada sesi pagi dan sore, "
"termasuk pembahasan solusi. Tanyakan apakah mereka kesulitan atau "
"membutuhkan bantuan. Jika beberapa orang mengalami masalah yang sama, "
"sampaikan kepada seluruh kelas dan tawarkan solusi, misalnya dengan "
"menunjukkan tempat menemukan informasi yang relevan dalam standard library."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"That is all, good luck running the course! We hope it will be as much fun "
"for you as it has been for us!"
msgstr ""
"Itu saja. Semoga kursusnya berjalan lancar! Kami berharap Anda menikmatinya "
"seperti kami!"

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"Please [provide feedback](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-"
"rust/discussions/86) afterwards so that we can keep improving the course. We"
" would love to hear what worked well for you and what can be made better. "
"Your students are also very welcome to [send us "
"feedback](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-rust/discussions/100)!"
msgstr ""
"Setelahnya, silakan [berikan "
"feedback](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-rust/discussions/86) agar "
"kami dapat terus memperbaiki kursus. Kami ingin mengetahui apa yang berjalan"
" baik dan apa yang dapat ditingkatkan. Peserta Anda juga sangat dipersilakan"
" [mengirimkan feedback](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-"
"rust/discussions/100)!"

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid "Instructor Preparation"
msgstr "Persiapan Pengajar"

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"**Go through all the material:** Before teaching the course, make sure you "
"have gone through all the slides and exercises yourself. This will help you "
"anticipate questions and potential difficulties."
msgstr ""
"**Pelajari seluruh materi:** Sebelum mengajar, pastikan Anda sudah "
"mempelajari semua slide dan mengerjakan latihan sendiri. Ini membantu Anda "
"mengantisipasi pertanyaan dan kesulitan yang mungkin muncul."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"**Prepare for live coding:** The course involves significant live coding. "
"Practice the examples and exercises beforehand to ensure you can type them "
"out smoothly during the class. Have the solutions ready in case you get "
"stuck."
msgstr ""
"**Siapkan live coding:** Kursus ini melibatkan banyak live coding. Latih "
"contoh dan latihan terlebih dahulu agar Anda dapat mengetiknya dengan lancar"
" di kelas. Siapkan solusi untuk berjaga-jaga jika mengalami kesulitan."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"**Familiarize yourself with `mdbook`:** The course is presented using "
"`mdbook`. Knowing how to navigate, search, and use its features will make "
"the presentation smoother."
msgstr ""
"**Pelajari `mdbook`:** Kursus disajikan menggunakan `mdbook`. Mengetahui "
"cara bernavigasi, mencari, dan menggunakan fiturnya akan memperlancar "
"presentasi."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"**Slice size helper:** Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Alt</kbd> + <kbd>B</kbd>"
" to toggle a visual guide showing the amount of space available when "
"presenting. Expect any content outside of the red box to be hidden "
"initially. Use this as a guide when editing slides. You can also [enable it "
"via this link](?show-red-box=true)."
msgstr ""
"**Panduan ukuran slide:** Tekan <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Alt</kbd> + "
"<kbd>B</kbd> untuk menampilkan atau menyembunyikan panduan visual luas area "
"presentasi. Konten di luar kotak merah pada awalnya akan tersembunyi. "
"Gunakan panduan ini saat mengedit slide. Anda juga dapat [mengaktifkannya "
"melalui tautan ini](?show-red-box=true)."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid "Creating a Good Learning Environment"
msgstr "Menciptakan Lingkungan Belajar yang Baik"

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"**Encourage questions:** Reiterate that there are no \"stupid\" questions. A"
" welcoming atmosphere for questions is crucial for learning."
msgstr ""
"**Dorong pertanyaan:** Tegaskan kembali bahwa tidak ada pertanyaan “bodoh”. "
"Suasana yang membuat orang nyaman bertanya sangat penting untuk belajar."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"**Manage time effectively:** Keep an eye on the schedule, but be flexible. "
"It's more important that students understand the concepts than sticking "
"rigidly to the timeline."
msgstr ""
"**Kelola waktu dengan efektif:** Perhatikan jadwal, tetapi tetap fleksibel. "
"Pemahaman konsep oleh peserta lebih penting daripada mengikuti jadwal secara"
" kaku."

#: src/running-the-course.md
msgid ""
"**Facilitate group work:** During exercises, encourage students to work "
"together. This can help them learn from each other and feel less stuck."
msgstr ""
"**Fasilitasi kerja kelompok:** Saat latihan, dorong peserta bekerja sama. "
"Ini membantu mereka saling belajar dan mengurangi kebuntuan."

