msgid "Key points:"
msgstr "Hal-hal utama:"

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"Rust has a rapid release schedule with a new release coming out every six "
"weeks. New releases maintain backwards compatibility with old releases --- "
"plus they enable new functionality."
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki jadwal rilis cepat: versi baru hadir setiap enam minggu. Rilis"
" baru mempertahankan backward compatibility dengan rilis lama sekaligus "
"menyediakan fungsionalitas baru."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid "There are three release channels: \"stable\", \"beta\", and \"nightly\"."
msgstr "Ada tiga release channel: “stable”, “beta”, dan “nightly”."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"New features are being tested on \"nightly\", \"beta\" is what becomes "
"\"stable\" every six weeks."
msgstr ""
"Fitur baru diuji pada “nightly”, sedangkan “beta” menjadi “stable” setiap "
"enam minggu."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"Dependencies can also be resolved from alternative "
"[registries](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/registries.html), "
"git, folders, and more."
msgstr ""
"Dependency juga dapat diperoleh dari [registry](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/cargo/reference/registries.html) alternatif, git, direktori, dan "
"sumber lainnya."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"Rust also has [editions](https://doc.rust-lang.org/edition-guide/): the "
"current edition is Rust 2024. Previous editions were Rust 2015, Rust 2018 "
"and Rust 2021."
msgstr ""
"Rust juga memiliki [edition](https://doc.rust-lang.org/edition-guide/): "
"edition saat ini adalah Rust 2024. Edition sebelumnya adalah Rust 2015, Rust"
" 2018, dan Rust 2021."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"The editions are allowed to make backwards incompatible changes to the "
"language."
msgstr ""
"Edition diperbolehkan membawa perubahan bahasa yang tidak backward-"
"compatible."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"To prevent breaking code, editions are opt-in: you select the edition for "
"your crate via the `Cargo.toml` file."
msgstr ""
"Agar kode yang ada tidak rusak, penggunaan edition bersifat opt-in: Anda "
"memilih edition untuk crate melalui berkas `Cargo.toml`."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"To avoid splitting the ecosystem, Rust compilers can mix code written for "
"different editions."
msgstr ""
"Agar ekosistem tidak terpecah, compiler Rust dapat menggabungkan kode yang "
"ditulis untuk edition berbeda."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"Mention that it is quite rare to ever use the compiler directly not through "
"`cargo` (most users never do)."
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa penggunaan compiler secara langsung tanpa `cargo` sangat "
"jarang; sebagian besar pengguna tidak pernah melakukannya."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"It might be worth alluding that Cargo itself is an extremely powerful and "
"comprehensive tool. It is capable of many advanced features including but "
"not limited to:"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menyinggung bahwa Cargo sendiri merupakan tool yang sangat andal "
"dan lengkap. Cargo memiliki banyak fitur lanjutan, antara lain:"

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid "Project/package structure"
msgstr "Struktur proyek/package"

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"[workspaces](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/workspaces.html)"
msgstr ""
"[workspace](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/workspaces.html)"

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid "Dev Dependencies and Runtime Dependency management/caching"
msgstr "Pengelolaan/cache dev dependency dan runtime dependency"

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"[build scripting](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-"
"scripts.html)"
msgstr ""
"[build scripting](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-"
"scripts.html)"

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"[global installation](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-"
"install.html)"
msgstr ""
"[instalasi global](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-"
"install.html)"

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"It is also extensible with sub command plugins as well (such as [cargo "
"clippy](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy))."
msgstr ""
"Fungsinya juga dapat diperluas melalui plugin subcommand, seperti [cargo "
"clippy](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy)."

#: src/cargo/rust-ecosystem.md
msgid ""
"Read more from the [official Cargo Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/)"
msgstr ""
"Baca lebih lanjut dalam [Cargo Book resmi](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/)"

#: src/cargo/code-samples.md
msgid "Code Samples in This Training"
msgstr "Contoh Kode dalam Pelatihan Ini"

#: src/cargo/code-samples.md
msgid ""
"For this training, we will mostly explore the Rust language through examples"
" which can be executed through your browser. This makes the setup much "
"easier and ensures a consistent experience for everyone."
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelatihan ini, kita terutama mempelajari Rust melalui contoh yang "
"dapat dijalankan di browser. Ini sangat mempermudah persiapan dan memastikan"
" pengalaman yang konsisten bagi semua peserta."

#: src/cargo/code-samples.md
msgid ""
"Installing Cargo is still encouraged: it will make it easier for you to do "
"the exercises. On the last day, we will do a larger exercise that shows you "
"how to work with dependencies and for that you need Cargo."
msgstr ""
"Anda tetap dianjurkan memasang Cargo karena akan mempermudah pengerjaan "
"latihan. Pada hari terakhir, kita akan mengerjakan latihan lebih besar yang "
"memperlihatkan cara menggunakan dependency. Untuk itu, Anda membutuhkan "
"Cargo."

