msgid "\"Hello 🌍!\""
msgstr "\"Hello 🌍!\""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "What you see:"
msgstr "Yang Anda lihat:"

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "Functions are introduced with `fn`."
msgstr "Fungsi dideklarasikan dengan `fn`."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "The `main` function is the entry point of the program."
msgstr "Fungsi `main` adalah entry point program."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "Blocks are delimited by curly braces like in C and C++."
msgstr "Blok dibatasi kurung kurawal, seperti dalam C dan C++."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "Statements end with `;`."
msgstr "Statement diakhiri dengan `;`."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "`println` is a macro, indicated by the `!` in the invocation."
msgstr "`println` adalah macro, yang ditandai dengan `!` saat dipanggil."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "Rust strings are UTF-8 encoded and can contain any Unicode character."
msgstr ""
"String Rust menggunakan encoding UTF-8 dan dapat memuat karakter Unicode apa"
" pun."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid ""
"This slide tries to make the students comfortable with Rust code. They will "
"see a ton of it over the next four days so we start small with something "
"familiar."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini bertujuan membiasakan peserta dengan kode Rust. Mereka akan "
"melihat banyak kode Rust selama empat hari berikutnya, jadi kita mulai dari "
"contoh kecil yang sudah dikenal."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid ""
"Rust is very much like other languages in the C/C++/Java tradition. It is "
"imperative and it doesn't try to reinvent things unless absolutely "
"necessary."
msgstr ""
"Rust sangat mirip dengan bahasa lain dalam tradisi C/C++/Java. Rust bersifat"
" imperatif dan tidak mencoba menciptakan ulang sesuatu kecuali benar-benar "
"diperlukan."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid "Rust is modern with full support for Unicode."
msgstr "Rust merupakan bahasa modern dengan dukungan penuh untuk Unicode."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid ""
"Rust uses macros for situations where you want to have a variable number of "
"arguments (no function [overloading](../control-flow-basics/functions.md))."
msgstr ""
"Rust menggunakan macro ketika Anda memerlukan jumlah argumen yang "
"bervariasi; tidak ada [overloading](../control-flow-basics/functions.md) "
"fungsi."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid ""
"`println!` is a macro because it needs to handle an arbitrary number of "
"arguments based on the format string, which can't be done with a regular "
"function. Otherwise it can be treated like a regular function."
msgstr ""
"`println!` merupakan macro karena perlu menangani jumlah argumen yang "
"bervariasi berdasarkan format string, sesuatu yang tidak dapat dilakukan "
"fungsi biasa. Selain hal itu, penggunaannya dapat diperlakukan seperti "
"fungsi biasa."

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md
msgid ""
"Rust is multi-paradigm. For example, it has powerful [object-oriented "
"programming features](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch17-00-oop.html), and,"
" while it is not a functional language, it includes a range of [functional "
"concepts](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch13-00-functional-features.html)."
msgstr ""
"Rust mendukung beberapa paradigma. Misalnya, Rust memiliki [fitur object-"
"oriented programming](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch17-00-oop.html) yang "
"kuat. Meskipun bukan bahasa fungsional, Rust juga menyediakan beragam "
"[konsep fungsional](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch13-00-functional-"
"features.html)."

#: src/types-and-values/variables.md
msgid ""
"Rust provides type safety via static typing. Variable bindings are made with"
" `let`:"
msgstr ""
"Rust memberikan type safety melalui static typing. Variable binding dibuat "
"dengan `let`:"

