msgid "There are a few syntaxes that are not shown above:"
msgstr "Ada beberapa sintaks yang tidak ditampilkan di atas:"

#: src/types-and-values/values.md
msgid ""
"All underscores in numbers can be left out, they are for legibility only. So"
" `1_000` can be written as `1000` (or `10_00`), and `123_i64` can be written"
" as `123i64`."
msgstr ""
"Semua underscore dalam angka dapat dihilangkan karena hanya membantu "
"keterbacaan. Jadi, `1_000` dapat ditulis sebagai `1000` (atau `10_00`), dan "
"`123_i64` dapat ditulis sebagai `123i64`."

#: src/types-and-values/arithmetic.md
msgid "\"result: {}\""
msgstr "\"result: {}\""

#: src/types-and-values/arithmetic.md
msgid ""
"This is the first time we've seen a function other than `main`, but the "
"meaning should be clear: it takes three integers, and returns an integer. "
"Functions will be covered in more detail later."
msgstr ""
"Ini pertama kalinya kita melihat fungsi selain `main`, tetapi maksudnya "
"seharusnya jelas: fungsi ini menerima tiga integer dan mengembalikan satu "
"integer. Fungsi akan dibahas lebih terperinci nanti."

#: src/types-and-values/arithmetic.md
msgid ""
"Arithmetic is very similar to other languages, with similar precedence."
msgstr ""
"Aritmetika sangat mirip dengan bahasa lain, dengan urutan prioritas operator"
" yang serupa."

#: src/types-and-values/arithmetic.md
msgid ""
"What about integer overflow? In C and C++ overflow of _signed_ integers is "
"actually undefined, and might do unknown things at runtime. In Rust, it's "
"defined."
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana dengan integer overflow? Dalam C dan C++, overflow pada _signed_ "
"integer sebenarnya tidak memiliki perilaku yang ditentukan dan dapat "
"melakukan hal yang tidak diketahui saat runtime. Dalam Rust, perilakunya "
"ditentukan."

#: src/types-and-values/arithmetic.md
msgid ""
"Change the `i32`'s to `i16` to see an integer overflow, which panics "
"(checked) in a debug build and wraps in a release build. There are other "
"options, such as overflowing, saturating, and carrying. These are accessed "
"with method syntax, e.g., `(a * b).saturating_add(b * c).saturating_add(c * "
"a)`."
msgstr ""
"Ubah `i32` menjadi `i16` untuk melihat integer overflow, yang memicu panic "
"(diperiksa) dalam debug build dan wrap-around dalam release build. Ada "
"pilihan lain, seperti overflowing, saturating, dan carrying, yang diakses "
"melalui sintaks method, misalnya `(a * b).saturating_add(b * "
"c).saturating_add(c * a)`."

#: src/types-and-values/arithmetic.md
msgid ""
"In fact, the compiler will detect overflow of constant expressions, which is"
" why the example requires a separate function."
msgstr ""
"Compiler sebenarnya akan mendeteksi overflow pada ekspresi konstan. Karena "
"itulah contoh ini membutuhkan fungsi terpisah."

#: src/types-and-values/inference.md
msgid "Rust will look at how the variable is _used_ to determine the type:"
msgstr "Rust melihat bagaimana variabel _digunakan_ untuk menentukan tipenya:"

#: src/types-and-values/inference.md
msgid ""
"This slide demonstrates how the Rust compiler infers types based on "
"constraints given by variable declarations and usages."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini menunjukkan cara compiler Rust menyimpulkan tipe berdasarkan "
"batasan dari deklarasi dan penggunaan variabel."

#: src/types-and-values/inference.md
msgid ""
"It is very important to emphasize that variables declared like this are not "
"of some sort of dynamic \"any type\" that can hold any data. The machine "
"code generated by such declaration is identical to the explicit declaration "
"of a type. The compiler does the job for us and helps us write more concise "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa variabel yang dideklarasikan seperti ini bukan tipe dinamis "
"“any type” yang dapat menampung data apa pun. Machine code yang dihasilkan "
"identik dengan deklarasi tipe secara eksplisit. Compiler mengerjakannya "
"untuk kita dan membantu kita menulis kode yang lebih ringkas."

#: src/types-and-values/inference.md
msgid ""
"When nothing constrains the type of an integer literal, Rust defaults to "
"`i32`. This sometimes appears as `{integer}` in error messages. Similarly, "
"floating-point literals default to `f64`."
msgstr ""
"Jika tidak ada yang membatasi tipe suatu literal integer, Rust menggunakan "
"`i32` secara default. Ini terkadang ditampilkan sebagai `{integer}` dalam "
"pesan error. Demikian pula, literal floating-point menggunakan `f64` secara "
"default."

#: src/types-and-values/inference.md
msgid "// ERROR: no implementation for `{float} == {integer}`\n"
msgstr "// ERROR: no implementation for `{float} == {integer}`\n"

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The Fibonacci sequence begins with `[0, 1]`. For `n > 1`, the next number is"
" the sum of the previous two."
msgstr ""
"Deret Fibonacci dimulai dengan `[0, 1]`. Untuk `n > 1`, bilangan berikutnya "
"adalah jumlah dua bilangan sebelumnya."

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Write a function `fib(n)` that calculates the nth Fibonacci number. When "
"will this function panic?"
msgstr ""
"Tulis fungsi `fib(n)` yang menghitung bilangan Fibonacci ke-n. Kapan fungsi "
"ini akan mengalami panic?"

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid "// The base case.\n"
msgstr "// The base case.\n"

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "\"Implement this\""
msgstr "\"Implement this\""

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid "// The recursive case.\n"
msgstr "// The recursive case.\n"

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid "\"fib({n}) = {}\""
msgstr "\"fib({n}) = {}\""

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid "This exercise is a classic introduction to recursion."
msgstr "Latihan ini merupakan pengantar klasik untuk rekursi."

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Encourage students to think about the base cases and the recursive step."
msgstr "Dorong peserta memikirkan base case dan langkah rekursif."

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The question \"When will this function panic?\" is a hint to think about "
"integer overflow. The Fibonacci sequence grows quickly!"
msgstr ""
"Pertanyaan “Kapan fungsi ini akan mengalami panic?” merupakan petunjuk untuk"
" memikirkan integer overflow. Deret Fibonacci bertambah dengan cepat!"

#: src/types-and-values/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Students might come up with an iterative solution as well, which is a great "
"opportunity to discuss the trade-offs between recursion and iteration (e.g.,"
" performance, stack overflow for deep recursion)."
msgstr ""
"Peserta mungkin juga mengusulkan solusi iteratif. Ini kesempatan yang baik "
"untuk membahas trade-off antara rekursi dan iterasi, misalnya performa dan "
"stack overflow pada rekursi yang dalam."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid ""
"We use the `return` syntax here to return values from the function. Later in"
" the course, we will see that the last expression in a block is "
"automatically returned, allowing us to omit the `return` keyword for a more "
"concise style."
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita menggunakan sintaks `return` untuk mengembalikan nilai dari "
"fungsi. Nanti, kita akan melihat bahwa ekspresi terakhir dalam blok otomatis"
" dikembalikan, sehingga keyword `return` dapat dihilangkan agar kode lebih "
"ringkas."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid ""
"The `if` condition `n < 2` does not need parentheses, which is standard Rust"
" style."
msgstr ""
"Kondisi `if` berupa `n < 2` tidak memerlukan tanda kurung, sesuai style "
"standar Rust."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid "Panic"
msgstr "Panic"

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid ""
"The exercise asks when this function will panic. The Fibonacci sequence "
"grows very rapidly. With `u32`, the calculated values will overflow the "
"32-bit integer limit (4,294,967,295) when `n` reaches 48."
msgstr ""
"Latihan ini menanyakan kapan fungsi akan mengalami panic. Deret Fibonacci "
"bertambah sangat cepat. Dengan `u32`, nilai yang dihitung akan melampaui "
"batas integer 32-bit (4,294,967,295) ketika `n` mencapai 48."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid ""
"In Rust, integer arithmetic checks for overflow in _debug mode_ (which is "
"the default when using `cargo run`). If an overflow occurs, the program will"
" panic (crash with an error message). In _release mode_ (`cargo run "
"--release`), overflow checks are disabled by default, and the number will "
"wrap around (modular arithmetic), producing incorrect results."
msgstr ""
"Dalam Rust, aritmetika integer memeriksa overflow pada _debug mode_, yaitu "
"mode default saat menggunakan `cargo run`. Jika overflow terjadi, program "
"mengalami panic, berhenti dengan pesan error. Pada _release mode_ (`cargo "
"run --release`), pemeriksaan overflow dinonaktifkan secara default dan angka"
" mengalami wrap-around (aritmetika modular), sehingga menghasilkan nilai "
"yang salah."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid "Walk through the solution step-by-step."
msgstr "Jelaskan solusi langkah demi langkah."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid "Explain the recursive calls and how they lead to the final result."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan pemanggilan rekursif dan bagaimana pemanggilan tersebut "
"menghasilkan nilai akhir."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid ""
"Discuss the integer overflow issue. With `u32`, the function will panic for "
"`n` around 47. You can demonstrate this by changing the input to `main`."
msgstr ""
"Bahas masalah integer overflow. Dengan `u32`, fungsi akan mengalami panic "
"untuk `n` sekitar 47. Anda dapat memperagakannya dengan mengubah input pada "
"`main`."

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md
msgid ""
"Show an iterative solution as an alternative and compare its performance and"
" memory usage with the recursive one. An iterative solution will be much "
"more efficient."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan solusi iteratif sebagai alternatif dan bandingkan performa serta "
"penggunaan memorinya dengan solusi rekursif. Solusi iteratif akan jauh lebih"
" efisien."

