msgid "if Expressions"
msgstr "Ekspresi if"

#: src/control-flow-basics.md src/pattern-matching.md src/concurrency/async.md
#: src/concurrency/async-control-flow.md
msgid "4 minutes"
msgstr "4 menit"

#: src/control-flow-basics.md
msgid "match Expressions"
msgstr "Ekspresi match"

#: src/control-flow-basics.md
msgid "break and continue"
msgstr "break dan continue"

#: src/control-flow-basics.md
msgid "We will now cover the many kinds of flow control found in Rust."
msgstr "Sekarang kita akan membahas berbagai bentuk control flow dalam Rust."

#: src/control-flow-basics.md
msgid ""
"Most of this will be very familiar to what you have seen in other "
"programming languages."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar akan terasa sangat familier dari bahasa pemrograman lain yang"
" pernah Anda gunakan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"A block in Rust contains a sequence of expressions, enclosed by braces `{}`."
msgstr ""
"Block dalam Rust berisi rangkaian ekspresi yang diapit kurung kurawal `{}`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"The final expression of a block determines the value and type of the whole "
"block."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi terakhir dalam block menentukan nilai dan tipe keseluruhan block."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid "// dbg!(y);\n"
msgstr "// dbg!(y);\n"

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"If the last expression ends with `;`, then the resulting value and type is "
"`()`."
msgstr ""
"Jika ekspresi terakhir diakhiri `;`, nilai dan tipe yang dihasilkan adalah "
"`()`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid "A variable's scope is limited to the enclosing block."
msgstr "Scope variabel terbatas pada block yang melingkupinya."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"You can explain that dbg! is a Rust macro that prints and returns the value "
"of a given expression for quick and dirty debugging."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menjelaskan bahwa dbg! adalah macro Rust yang mencetak dan "
"mengembalikan nilai ekspresi untuk debugging cepat dan sederhana."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"You can show how the value of the block changes by changing the last line in"
" the block. For instance, adding/removing a semicolon or using a `return`."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bagaimana nilai block berubah ketika baris terakhirnya diubah, "
"misalnya dengan menambahkan atau menghapus titik koma, atau menggunakan "
"`return`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate that attempting to access `y` outside of its scope won't "
"compile."
msgstr ""
"Peragakan bahwa upaya mengakses `y` di luar scope-nya tidak dapat "
"dikompilasi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"Values are effectively \"deallocated\" when they go out of their scope, even"
" if their data on the stack is still there."
msgstr ""
"Nilai secara efektif “didealokasi” ketika keluar dari scope, meskipun "
"datanya masih berada pada stack."

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "`if` expressions"
msgstr "Ekspresi `if`"

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"You use [`if` expressions](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/expressions/if-expr.html#if-expressions) exactly like "
"`if` statements in other languages:"
msgstr ""
"Anda menggunakan [ekspresi `if`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/expressions/if-expr.html#if-expressions) seperti "
"statement `if` dalam bahasa lain:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"zero!\""
msgstr "\"zero!\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"biggish\""
msgstr "\"biggish\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"huge\""
msgstr "\"huge\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"In addition, you can use `if` as an expression. The last expression of each "
"block becomes the value of the `if` expression:"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, Anda dapat menggunakan `if` sebagai ekspresi. Ekspresi terakhir "
"dari setiap block menjadi nilai ekspresi `if`:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"small\""
msgstr "\"small\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"large\""
msgstr "\"large\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"number size: {}\""
msgstr "\"number size: {}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"Because `if` is an expression and must have a particular type, both of its "
"branch blocks must have the same type. Show what happens if you add `;` "
"after `\"small\"` in the second example."
msgstr ""
"Karena `if` merupakan ekspresi dan harus memiliki tipe tertentu, kedua block"
" cabangnya harus memiliki tipe yang sama. Tunjukkan apa yang terjadi jika "
"Anda menambahkan `;` setelah `\"small\"` pada contoh kedua."

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"An `if` expression should be used in the same way as the other expressions. "
"For example, when it is used in a `let` statement, the statement must be "
"terminated with a `;` as well. Remove the `;` before `println!` to see the "
"compiler error."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi `if` sebaiknya digunakan seperti ekspresi lain. Misalnya, ketika "
"digunakan dalam statement `let`, statement tersebut juga harus diakhiri `;`."
" Hapus `;` sebelum `println!` untuk melihat error compiler."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "`match` can be used to check a value against one or more options:"
msgstr ""
"`match` dapat digunakan untuk memeriksa nilai terhadap satu atau beberapa "
"pilihan:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"one\""
msgstr "\"one\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"ten\""
msgstr "\"ten\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"one hundred\""
msgstr "\"one hundred\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"something else\""
msgstr "\"something else\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"Like `if` expressions, `match` also takes on the value of the branch it "
"chooses;"
msgstr ""
"Seperti ekspresi `if`, `match` juga menghasilkan nilai dari cabang yang "
"dipilih;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"The value of {flag} is {val}\""
msgstr "\"The value of {flag} is {val}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"`match` arms are evaluated from top to bottom, and the first one that "
"matches has its corresponding body executed."
msgstr ""
"Arm `match` diperiksa dari atas ke bawah. Isi arm pertama yang cocok akan "
"dijalankan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"There is no fall-through between cases the way that `switch` works in other "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Tidak ada fall-through antar-case seperti pada `switch` dalam bahasa lain."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"The body of a `match` arm can be a single expression or a block. Technically"
" this is the same thing, since blocks are also expressions, but students may"
" not fully understand that symmetry at this point."
msgstr ""
"Isi arm `match` dapat berupa satu ekspresi atau block. Secara teknis "
"keduanya sama karena block juga merupakan ekspresi, tetapi peserta mungkin "
"belum sepenuhnya memahami kesetaraan itu pada tahap ini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"`match` expressions need to be exhaustive, meaning they either need to cover"
" all possible values or they need to have a default case such as `_`. "
"Exhaustiveness is easiest to demonstrate with enums, but enums haven't been "
"introduced yet. Instead we demonstrate matching on a `bool`, which is the "
"simplest primitive type."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi `match` harus exhaustive: mencakup seluruh kemungkinan nilai atau "
"memiliki default case seperti `_`. Exhaustiveness paling mudah diperagakan "
"dengan enum, tetapi enum belum diperkenalkan. Karena itu, kita memperagakan "
"pencocokan pada `bool`, tipe primitif paling sederhana."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"This slide introduces `match` without talking about pattern matching, giving"
" students a chance to get familiar with the syntax without front-loading too"
" much information. We'll be talking about pattern matching in more detail "
"tomorrow, so try not to go into too much detail here."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini memperkenalkan `match` tanpa membahas pattern matching, agar "
"peserta dapat membiasakan diri dengan sintaksnya tanpa menerima terlalu "
"banyak informasi sekaligus. Kita akan membahas pattern matching lebih "
"terperinci besok, jadi usahakan tidak membahas terlalu banyak detail di "
"sini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"To further motivate the usage of `match`, you can compare the examples to "
"their equivalents written with `if`. In the second case, matching on a "
"`bool`, an `if {} else {}` block is pretty similar. But in the first example"
" that checks multiple cases, a `match` expression can be more concise than "
"`if {} else if {} else if {} else`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk memperjelas manfaat `match`, bandingkan contoh dengan versi setaranya "
"menggunakan `if`. Pada contoh kedua, yaitu pencocokan `bool`, block `if {} "
"else {}` cukup serupa. Namun, pada contoh pertama yang memeriksa beberapa "
"case, ekspresi `match` dapat lebih ringkas daripada `if {} else if {} else "
"if {} else`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"`match` also supports match guards, which allow you to add an arbitrary "
"logical condition that will get evaluated to determine if the match arm "
"should be taken. However talking about match guards requires explaining "
"about pattern matching, which we're trying to avoid on this slide."
msgstr ""
"`match` juga mendukung match guard untuk menambahkan kondisi logis yang "
"dievaluasi guna menentukan apakah arm tersebut dipilih. Namun, membahas "
"match guard memerlukan penjelasan pattern matching, yang sengaja belum kita "
"bahas dalam slide ini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops.md
msgid "There are three looping keywords in Rust: `while`, `loop`, and `for`:"
msgstr "Rust memiliki tiga keyword untuk loop: `while`, `loop`, dan `for`:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops.md
msgid "`while`"
msgstr "`while`"

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops.md
msgid ""
"The [`while` keyword](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-"
"expr.html#predicate-loops) works much like in other languages, executing the"
" loop body as long as the condition is true."
msgstr ""
"[Keyword `while`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-"
"expr.html#predicate-loops) bekerja seperti dalam bahasa lain: menjalankan "
"isi loop selama kondisinya benar."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"The [`for` loop](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.for.html) iterates "
"over ranges of values or the items in a collection:"
msgstr ""
"[Loop `for`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.for.html) mengiterasi "
"rentang nilai atau elemen dalam collection:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"`for` loops can be given any sequence of values and will iterate through "
"that sequence."
msgstr ""
"Loop `for` dapat menerima rangkaian nilai apa pun dan akan mengiterasi "
"rangkaian tersebut."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"Note that the first `for` loop only iterates to `4`. Show the `1..=5` syntax"
" for an inclusive range."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa loop `for` pertama hanya mengiterasi hingga `4`. Tunjukkan "
"sintaks `1..=5` untuk rentang inklusif."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"Under the hood `for` loops use a concept called \"iterators\" to handle "
"iterating over different kinds of ranges/collections. Iterators will be "
"discussed in more detail later."
msgstr ""
"Di balik layar, loop `for` menggunakan konsep “iterator” untuk mengiterasi "
"berbagai jenis rentang/collection. Iterator akan dibahas lebih terperinci "
"nanti."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/loop.md
msgid ""
"The [`loop` expression](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.loop.html) "
"just loops forever, until a `break`."
msgstr ""
"[Ekspresi `loop`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.loop.html) terus "
"berulang hingga ada `break`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/loop.md
msgid ""
"The `loop` expression works like a `while true` loop. Use it for things like"
" servers that will serve connections forever."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi `loop` bekerja seperti loop `while true`. Gunakan untuk hal seperti"
" server yang terus melayani koneksi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue.md
msgid ""
"If you want to immediately start the next iteration use "
"[`continue`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-"
"expr.html#continue-expressions)."
msgstr ""
"Jika ingin langsung memulai iterasi berikutnya, gunakan "
"[`continue`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-"
"expr.html#continue-expressions)."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue.md
msgid ""
"If you want to exit any kind of loop early, use [`break`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-expr.html#break-expressions). With "
"`loop`, this can take an optional expression that becomes the value of the "
"`loop` expression."
msgstr ""
"Jika ingin keluar lebih awal dari jenis loop apa pun, gunakan "
"[`break`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-"
"expr.html#break-expressions). Pada `loop`, Anda boleh menyertakan ekspresi "
"yang menjadi nilai ekspresi `loop`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue.md
msgid ""
"Note that `loop` is the only looping construct that may evaluate to a non-"
"trivial value. This is because control flow of a `loop` only proceeds to its"
" context via a `break` expression (unlike `while` and `for` loops, which can"
" also exit when the condition fails)."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `loop` adalah satu-satunya konstruksi loop yang dapat "
"menghasilkan nilai nontrivial. Sebab, control flow `loop` hanya berlanjut ke"
" konteks di luarnya melalui ekspresi `break`, berbeda dengan `while` dan "
"`for` yang juga dapat berakhir ketika kondisi tidak terpenuhi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue/labels.md
msgid ""
"Both `continue` and `break` can optionally take a label argument that is "
"used to break out of nested loops:"
msgstr ""
"`continue` dan `break` boleh menerima argumen label untuk mengatur "
"perpindahan keluar dari loop bersarang:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue/labels.md
msgid "Labeled break also works on arbitrary blocks, e.g."
msgstr "Break berlabel juga dapat digunakan pada block biasa, misalnya"

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue/labels.md
msgid "\"This line gets skipped\""
msgstr "\"This line gets skipped\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Declaration parameters are followed by a type (the reverse of some "
"programming languages), then a return type."
msgstr ""
"Parameter dalam deklarasi diikuti tipe, berkebalikan dengan sebagian bahasa "
"pemrograman, lalu tipe nilai kembalian."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"The last expression in a function body (or any block) becomes the return "
"value. Simply omit the `;` at the end of the expression. The `return` "
"keyword can be used for early return, but the \"bare value\" form is "
"idiomatic at the end of a function (refactor `gcd` to use a `return`)."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi terakhir dalam isi fungsi atau block apa pun menjadi nilai "
"kembalian. Cukup hilangkan `;` di akhir ekspresi. Keyword `return` dapat "
"digunakan untuk mengembalikan nilai lebih awal, tetapi bentuk “nilai "
"langsung” merupakan idiom yang umum pada akhir fungsi. Lakukan refactoring "
"pada `gcd` agar menggunakan `return`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Some functions have no return value, and return the 'unit type', `()`. The "
"compiler will infer this if the return type is omitted."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian fungsi tidak memiliki nilai kembalian dan mengembalikan “unit "
"type”, `()`. Compiler akan menyimpulkannya jika tipe nilai kembalian tidak "
"ditulis."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Overloading is not supported -- each function has a single implementation."
msgstr "Overloading tidak didukung—setiap fungsi memiliki satu implementasi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Always takes a fixed number of parameters. Default arguments are not "
"supported. Macros can be used to support variadic functions."
msgstr ""
"Selalu menerima jumlah parameter yang tetap. Default argument tidak "
"didukung. Macro dapat digunakan untuk mendukung fungsi variadic."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Always takes a single set of parameter types. These types can be generic, "
"which will be covered later."
msgstr ""
"Selalu menerima satu himpunan tipe parameter. Tipe-tipe ini dapat bersifat "
"generic, yang akan dibahas nanti."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"Macros are expanded into Rust code during compilation, and can take a "
"variable number of arguments. They are distinguished by a `!` at the end. "
"The Rust standard library includes an assortment of useful macros."
msgstr ""
"Macro diekspansi menjadi kode Rust selama kompilasi dan dapat menerima "
"jumlah argumen yang bervariasi. Macro ditandai dengan `!` di bagian akhir. "
"Standard library Rust menyediakan berbagai macro yang berguna."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"`println!(format, ..)` prints a line to standard output, applying formatting"
" described in [`std::fmt`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fmt/index.html)."
msgstr ""
"`println!(format, ..)` mencetak satu baris ke standard output dengan format "
"yang dijelaskan dalam [`std::fmt`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/fmt/index.html)."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"`format!(format, ..)` works just like `println!` but returns the result as a"
" string."
msgstr ""
"`format!(format, ..)` bekerja seperti `println!`, tetapi mengembalikan "
"hasilnya sebagai string."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid "`dbg!(expression)` logs the value of the expression and returns it."
msgstr ""
"`dbg!(expression)` mencatat nilai ekspresi ke log dan mengembalikannya."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"`todo!()` marks a bit of code as not-yet-implemented. If executed, it will "
"panic."
msgstr ""
"`todo!()` menandai bagian kode yang belum diimplementasikan. Jika "
"dijalankan, kode tersebut akan mengalami panic."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid "\"{n}! = {}\""
msgstr "\"{n}! = {}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"The takeaway from this section is that these common conveniences exist, and "
"how to use them. Why they are defined as macros, and what they expand to, is"
" not especially critical."
msgstr ""
"Hal utama dalam bagian ini adalah mengetahui bahwa fasilitas umum tersebut "
"tersedia dan memahami cara menggunakannya. Alasan fasilitas itu "
"didefinisikan sebagai macro dan hasil ekspansinya bukan hal yang terlalu "
"penting di sini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"The course does not cover defining macros, but a later section will describe"
" use of derive macros."
msgstr ""
"Kursus ini tidak membahas cara mendefinisikan macro, tetapi bagian "
"selanjutnya akan menjelaskan penggunaan derive macro."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md src/pattern-matching/match.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "More To Explore"
msgstr "Untuk Dipelajari Lebih Lanjut"

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"There are a number of other useful macros provided by the standard library. "
"Some other examples you can share with students if they want to know more:"
msgstr ""
"Standard library menyediakan sejumlah macro berguna lainnya. Berikut "
"beberapa contoh yang dapat Anda bagikan jika peserta ingin mengetahui lebih "
"lanjut:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"[`assert!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.assert.html) and "
"related macros can be used to add assertions to your code. These are used "
"heavily in writing tests."
msgstr ""
"[`assert!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.assert.html) dan "
"macro terkait dapat digunakan untuk menambahkan assertion ke kode. Macro ini"
" banyak digunakan saat menulis test."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"[`unreachable!`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/macro.unreachable.html) is used to mark a branch of "
"control flow that should never be hit."
msgstr ""
"[`unreachable!`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/macro.unreachable.html) menandai cabang control flow "
"yang seharusnya tidak pernah dicapai."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"[`eprintln!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.eprintln.html) "
"allows you to print to stderr."
msgstr ""
"[`eprintln!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.eprintln.html) "
"memungkinkan Anda mencetak ke stderr."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The [Collatz Sequence](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collatz_conjecture) is "
"defined as follows, for an arbitrary n<sub>1</sub> greater than zero:"
msgstr ""
"[Deret Collatz](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collatz_conjecture) "
"didefinisikan sebagai berikut, untuk sembarang n<sub>1</sub> yang lebih "
"besar dari nol:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"If _n<sub>i</sub>_ is 1, then the sequence terminates at _n<sub>i</sub>_."
msgstr "Jika _n<sub>i</sub>_ adalah 1, deret berakhir pada _n<sub>i</sub>_."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"If _n<sub>i</sub>_ is even, then _n<sub>i+1</sub> = n<sub>i</sub> / 2_."
msgstr ""
"Jika _n<sub>i</sub>_ genap, maka _n<sub>i+1</sub> = n<sub>i</sub> / 2_."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"If _n<sub>i</sub>_ is odd, then _n<sub>i+1</sub> = 3 * n<sub>i</sub> + 1_."
msgstr ""
"Jika _n<sub>i</sub>_ ganjil, maka _n<sub>i+1</sub> = 3 * n<sub>i</sub> + 1_."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "For example, beginning with _n<sub>1</sub>_ = 3:"
msgstr "Misalnya, dimulai dari _n<sub>1</sub>_ = 3:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "3 is odd, so _n<sub>2</sub>_ = 3 * 3 + 1 = 10;"
msgstr "3 ganjil, jadi _n<sub>2</sub>_ = 3 * 3 + 1 = 10;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "10 is even, so _n<sub>3</sub>_ = 10 / 2 = 5;"
msgstr "10 genap, jadi _n<sub>3</sub>_ = 10 / 2 = 5;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "5 is odd, so _n<sub>4</sub>_ = 3 * 5 + 1 = 16;"
msgstr "5 ganjil, jadi _n<sub>4</sub>_ = 3 * 5 + 1 = 16;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "16 is even, so _n<sub>5</sub>_ = 16 / 2 = 8;"
msgstr "16 genap, jadi _n<sub>5</sub>_ = 16 / 2 = 8;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "8 is even, so _n<sub>6</sub>_ = 8 / 2 = 4;"
msgstr "8 genap, jadi _n<sub>6</sub>_ = 8 / 2 = 4;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "4 is even, so _n<sub>7</sub>_ = 4 / 2 = 2;"
msgstr "4 genap, jadi _n<sub>7</sub>_ = 4 / 2 = 2;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "2 is even, so _n<sub>8</sub>_ = 1; and"
msgstr "2 genap, jadi _n<sub>8</sub>_ = 1; dan"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "the sequence terminates."
msgstr "deret berakhir."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Write a function to calculate the length of the Collatz sequence for a given"
" initial `n`."
msgstr ""
"Tulis fungsi untuk menghitung panjang deret Collatz dari nilai awal `n` yang"
" diberikan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid "/// Determine the length of the collatz sequence beginning at `n`.\n"
msgstr "/// Determine the length of the collatz sequence beginning at `n`.\n"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "\"Length: {}\""
msgstr "\"Length: {}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid "// should be 15\n"
msgstr "// should be 15\n"

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid "This solution demonstrates a few key Rust features:"
msgstr "Solusi ini menunjukkan beberapa fitur utama Rust:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"**`mut` arguments:** The `n` argument is declared as `mut n`. This makes the"
" local variable `n` mutable within the function scope. It does _not_ affect "
"the caller's value, as integers are `Copy` types passed by value."
msgstr ""
"**Argumen `mut`:** Argumen `n` dideklarasikan sebagai `mut n`. Ini membuat "
"variabel lokal `n` bersifat mutable dalam scope fungsi. Ini _tidak_ "
"memengaruhi nilai milik caller karena integer merupakan tipe `Copy` yang "
"diteruskan by value."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"**`if` expressions:** Rust's `if` is an expression, meaning it produces a "
"value. We assign the result of the `if`/`else` block directly to `n`. This "
"is more concise than writing `n = ...` inside each branch."
msgstr ""
"**Ekspresi `if`:** Dalam Rust, `if` merupakan ekspresi, artinya menghasilkan"
" nilai. Kita langsung menetapkan hasil block `if`/`else` ke `n`. Ini lebih "
"ringkas daripada menulis `n = ...` pada setiap cabang."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Implicit return:** The function ends with `len` (without a semicolon), "
"which is automatically returned."
msgstr ""
"**Implicit return:** Fungsi diakhiri `len` tanpa titik koma, yang nilainya "
"otomatis dikembalikan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"Note that `n` must be strictly greater than 0 for the Collatz sequence to be"
" valid. The function signature takes `i32`, but the problem description "
"implies positive integers. A more robust implementation might use `u32` or "
"return an `Option` or `Result` to handle invalid inputs (0 or negative "
"numbers), but panic or infinite loops are potential outcomes here if `n <= "
"0`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `n` harus benar-benar lebih besar dari 0 agar deret Collatz"
" valid. Signature fungsi menerima `i32`, tetapi deskripsi masalah "
"mengisyaratkan integer positif. Implementasi yang lebih andal mungkin "
"menggunakan `u32` atau mengembalikan `Option` atau `Result` untuk menangani "
"input tidak valid, yaitu 0 atau angka negatif. Namun, dalam implementasi "
"ini, `n <= 0` dapat menyebabkan panic atau loop tanpa akhir."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"The overflow is a potential issue if `n` grows too large, similar to the "
"Fibonacci exercise."
msgstr ""
"Overflow dapat menjadi masalah jika `n` terlalu besar, seperti pada latihan "
"Fibonacci."

#: src/welcome-day-1-afternoon.md src/welcome-day-2-afternoon.md
#: src/welcome-day-3-afternoon.md src/welcome-day-4-afternoon.md
msgid "Welcome Back"
msgstr "Selamat Datang Kembali"

#: src/welcome-day-1-afternoon.md
msgid ""
"Including 10 minute breaks, this session should take about 2 hours and 45 "
"minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Termasuk istirahat 10 menit, sesi ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar"
" 2 jam dan 45 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays.md
msgid "This segment should take about 35 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr "Bagian ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar 35 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays.md
msgid ""
"We have seen how primitive types work in Rust. Now it's time for you to "
"start building new composite types."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah melihat cara kerja tipe primitif dalam Rust. Sekarang saatnya "
"mulai membuat tipe komposit baru."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Arrays can also be initialized using the shorthand syntax, e.g. `[0; 1024]`."
" This can be useful when you want to initialize all elements to the same "
"value, or if you have a large array that would be hard to initialize "
"manually."
msgstr ""
"Array juga dapat diinisialisasi menggunakan sintaks singkat, misalnya `[0; "
"1024]`. Cara ini berguna ketika Anda ingin menginisialisasi semua elemen "
"dengan nilai yang sama atau ketika array berukuran besar sulit "
"diinisialisasi secara manual."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"A value of the array type `[T; N]` holds `N` (a compile-time constant) "
"elements of the same type `T`. Note that the length of the array is _part of"
" its type_, which means that `[u8; 3]` and `[u8; 4]` are considered two "
"different types. Slices, which have a size determined at runtime, are "
"covered later."
msgstr ""
"Nilai bertipe array `[T; N]` menyimpan `N` elemen dengan tipe yang sama, "
"yaitu `T`; jumlah elemennya merupakan konstanta compile-time. Perhatikan "
"bahwa panjang array merupakan _bagian dari tipenya_, sehingga `[u8; 3]` dan "
"`[u8; 4]` dianggap dua tipe berbeda. Slice, yang ukurannya ditentukan saat "
"runtime, dibahas nanti."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Try accessing an out-of-bounds array element. The compiler is able to "
"determine that the index is unsafe, and will not compile the code:"
msgstr ""
"Coba akses elemen array di luar batas. Compiler dapat menentukan bahwa "
"indeks tersebut tidak aman dan menolak mengompilasi kodenya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid "\"a: {a:?}\""
msgstr "\"a: {a:?}\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Array accesses are checked at runtime. Rust optimizes these checks away when"
" possible; meaning if the compiler can prove the access is safe, it removes "
"the runtime check for better performance. They can be avoided using unsafe "
"Rust. The optimization is so good that it's hard to give an example of "
"runtime checks failing. The following code will compile but panic at "
"runtime:"
msgstr ""
"Akses array diperiksa saat runtime. Rust menghilangkan pemeriksaan ini "
"melalui optimasi bila memungkinkan: jika compiler dapat membuktikan aksesnya"
" aman, pemeriksaan runtime dihapus untuk meningkatkan performa. Pemeriksaan "
"juga dapat dihindari menggunakan unsafe Rust. Optimasinya begitu baik "
"sehingga contoh pemeriksaan runtime yang gagal sulit dibuat. Kode berikut "
"dapat dikompilasi, tetapi akan mengalami panic saat runtime:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid "We can use literals to assign values to arrays."
msgstr "Kita dapat menggunakan literal untuk memberikan nilai pada array."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Arrays are not heap-allocated. They are regular values with a fixed size "
"known at compile time, meaning they go on the stack. This can be different "
"from what students expect if they come from a garbage-collected language, "
"where arrays may be heap allocated by default."
msgstr ""
"Array tidak dialokasikan pada heap. Array merupakan nilai biasa dengan "
"ukuran tetap yang diketahui saat compile time, sehingga ditempatkan pada "
"stack. Ini mungkin berbeda dari perkiraan peserta yang terbiasa dengan "
"bahasa bergarbage collector, yang mungkin mengalokasikan array pada heap "
"secara default."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"There is no way to remove elements from an array, nor add elements to an "
"array. The length of an array is fixed at compile-time, and so its length "
"cannot change at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Elemen array tidak dapat dihapus atau ditambahkan. Panjang array tetap saat "
"compile time, sehingga tidak dapat berubah saat runtime."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid "Debug Printing"
msgstr "Pencetakan untuk Debug"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"The `println!` macro asks for the debug implementation with the `?` format "
"parameter: `{}` gives the default output, `{:?}` gives the debug output. "
"Types such as integers and strings implement the default output, but arrays "
"only implement the debug output. This means that we must use debug output "
"here."
msgstr ""
"Macro `println!` menggunakan implementasi debug melalui parameter format "
"`?`: `{}` menghasilkan output default, sedangkan `{:?}` menghasilkan output "
"debug. Tipe seperti integer dan string mengimplementasikan output default, "
"tetapi array hanya mengimplementasikan output debug. Karena itu, kita harus "
"menggunakan output debug di sini."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Adding `#`, eg `{a:#?}`, invokes a \"pretty printing\" format, which can be "
"easier to read."
msgstr ""
"Menambahkan `#`, misalnya `{a:#?}`, menggunakan format “pretty printing” "
"yang dapat lebih mudah dibaca."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid "Like arrays, tuples have a fixed length."
msgstr "Seperti array, tuple memiliki panjang tetap."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid "Tuples group together values of different types into a compound type."
msgstr ""
"Tuple mengelompokkan nilai dengan tipe berbeda menjadi satu tipe compound."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"Fields of a tuple can be accessed by the period and the index of the value, "
"e.g. `t.0`, `t.1`."
msgstr ""
"Field tuple dapat diakses menggunakan titik dan indeks nilainya, misalnya "
"`t.0`, `t.1`."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"The empty tuple `()` is referred to as the \"unit type\" and signifies "
"absence of a meaningful value, akin to `void` in other languages."
msgstr ""
"Tuple kosong `()` disebut “unit type” dan menandakan tidak adanya nilai yang"
" bermakna, serupa dengan `void` dalam bahasa lain."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"Unlike arrays, tuples cannot be used in a `for` loop. This is because a "
"`for` loop requires all the elements to have the same type, which may not be"
" the case for a tuple."
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dari array, tuple tidak dapat digunakan dalam loop `for`. Sebab, "
"loop `for` mengharuskan semua elemen memiliki tipe yang sama, sedangkan "
"tuple belum tentu demikian."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"There is no way to add or remove elements from a tuple. The number of "
"elements and their types are fixed at compile time and cannot be changed at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""
"Elemen tuple tidak dapat ditambahkan atau dihapus. Jumlah elemen dan tipenya"
" tetap saat compile time dan tidak dapat diubah saat runtime."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/iteration.md
msgid "The `for` statement supports iterating over arrays (but not tuples)."
msgstr ""
"Statement `for` mendukung iterasi pada array, tetapi tidak pada tuple."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/iteration.md
msgid ""
"This functionality uses the `IntoIterator` trait, but we haven't covered "
"that yet."
msgstr ""
"Fungsionalitas ini menggunakan trait `IntoIterator`, tetapi kita belum "
"membahasnya."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/iteration.md
msgid ""
"The `assert_ne!` macro is new here. There are also `assert_eq!` and "
"`assert!` macros. These are always checked, while debug-only variants like "
"`debug_assert!` compile to nothing in release builds."
msgstr ""
"Macro `assert_ne!` baru diperkenalkan di sini. Ada pula macro `assert_eq!` "
"dan `assert!`. Ketiganya selalu diperiksa, sedangkan varian khusus debug "
"seperti `debug_assert!` tidak menghasilkan kode pada release build."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"Rust supports using pattern matching to destructure a larger value like a "
"tuple into its constituent parts:"
msgstr ""
"Rust mendukung pattern matching untuk melakukan destructuring nilai besar "
"seperti tuple menjadi bagian-bagian penyusunnya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid "\"{tuple:?}: {}\""
msgstr "\"{tuple:?}: {}\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid "\"ordered\""
msgstr "\"ordered\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid "\"unordered\""
msgstr "\"unordered\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"The patterns used here are \"irrefutable\", meaning that the compiler can "
"statically verify that the value on the right of `=` has the same structure "
"as the pattern."
msgstr ""
"Pattern yang digunakan di sini bersifat “irrefutable”: compiler dapat "
"memverifikasi secara statis bahwa nilai di sebelah kanan `=` memiliki "
"struktur yang sama dengan pattern."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"A variable name is an irrefutable pattern that always matches any value, "
"hence why we can also use `let` to declare a single variable."
msgstr ""
"Nama variabel merupakan irrefutable pattern yang selalu cocok dengan nilai "
"apa pun. Karena itulah `let` juga dapat digunakan untuk mendeklarasikan satu"
" variabel."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"Rust also supports using patterns in conditionals, allowing for equality "
"comparison and destructuring to happen at the same time. This form of "
"pattern matching will be discussed in more detail later."
msgstr ""
"Rust juga mendukung penggunaan pattern dalam conditional agar perbandingan "
"kesamaan dan destructuring dapat dilakukan bersamaan. Bentuk pattern "
"matching ini dibahas lebih terperinci nanti."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"Edit the examples above to show the compiler error when the pattern doesn't "
"match the value being matched on."
msgstr ""
"Edit contoh di atas untuk menunjukkan error compiler ketika pattern tidak "
"cocok dengan nilai yang diperiksa."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid "Arrays can contain other arrays:"
msgstr "Array dapat memuat array lain:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid "What is the type of this variable?"
msgstr "Apa tipe variabel ini?"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Use an array such as the above to write a function `transpose` that "
"transposes a matrix (turns rows into columns):"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan array seperti di atas untuk menulis fungsi `transpose` yang "
"melakukan transposisi matriks, yaitu mengubah baris menjadi kolom:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Copy the code below to <https://play.rust-lang.org/> and implement the "
"function. This function only operates on 3×3 matrices."
msgstr ""
"Salin kode berikut ke <https://play.rust-lang.org/> dan implementasikan "
"fungsinya. Fungsi ini hanya bekerja pada matriks 3×3."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid "// <-- the comment makes rustfmt add a newline\n"
msgstr "// <-- the comment makes rustfmt add a newline\n"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid "\"Original:\""
msgstr "\"Original:\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid "\"{row:?}\""
msgstr "\"{row:?}\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid "\"\\nTransposed:\""
msgstr "\"\\nTransposed:\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Array Types:** The type `[[i32; 3]; 3]` represents an array of size 3, "
"where each element is itself an array of 3 `i32`s. This is how multi-"
"dimensional arrays are typically represented in Rust."
msgstr ""
"**Tipe Array:** Tipe `[[i32; 3]; 3]` merepresentasikan array berukuran 3 "
"yang setiap elemennya juga merupakan array berisi 3 nilai `i32`. Inilah cara"
" umum merepresentasikan array multidimensi dalam Rust."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Initialization:** We initialize `result` with zeros (`[[0; 3]; 3]`) before"
" filling it. Rust requires all variables to be initialized before use; there"
" is no concept of \"uninitialized memory\" in safe Rust."
msgstr ""
"**Inisialisasi:** Kita menginisialisasi `result` dengan nol (`[[0; 3]; 3]`) "
"sebelum mengisinya. Rust mengharuskan semua variabel diinisialisasi sebelum "
"digunakan; tidak ada konsep “memori yang belum diinisialisasi” dalam safe "
"Rust."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Copy Semantics:** Arrays of `Copy` types (like `i32`) are themselves "
"`Copy`. When we pass `matrix` to the function, it is copied by value. The "
"`result` variable is a new, separate array."
msgstr ""
"**Copy Semantics:** Array berisi tipe `Copy`, seperti `i32`, juga bersifat "
"`Copy`. Saat `matrix` diteruskan ke fungsi, nilainya disalin. Variabel "
"`result` merupakan array baru yang terpisah."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Iteration:** We use standard `for` loops with ranges (`0..3`) to iterate "
"over indices. Rust also has powerful iterators, which we will see later, but"
" indexing is straightforward for this matrix transposition."
msgstr ""
"**Iterasi:** Kita menggunakan loop `for` standar dengan rentang (`0..3`) "
"untuk mengiterasi indeks. Rust juga memiliki iterator yang andal, yang akan "
"kita lihat nanti, tetapi pengindeksan cukup sederhana untuk transposisi "
"matriks ini."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid ""
"Mention that `[i32; 3]` is a distinct type from `[i32; 4]`. Array sizes are "
"part of the type signature."
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa `[i32; 3]` merupakan tipe berbeda dari `[i32; 4]`. Ukuran "
"array merupakan bagian dari signature tipe."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/solution.md
msgid ""
"Ask students what would happen if they tried to return `matrix` directly "
"after modifying it (if they changed the signature to `mut matrix`). (Answer:"
" It would work, but it would return a modified _copy_, leaving the original "
"in `main` unchanged)."
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan apa yang terjadi jika peserta langsung mengembalikan `matrix` "
"setelah mengubahnya, dengan mengganti signature menjadi `mut matrix`. "
"Jawaban: cara itu bekerja, tetapi mengembalikan _salinan_ yang diubah, "
"sedangkan nilai asli dalam `main` tetap sama."

#: src/references.md src/smart-pointers.md src/iterators.md
#: src/error-handling.md src/concurrency/async-pitfalls.md
msgid "This segment should take about 55 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr "Bagian ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar 55 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A reference provides a way to access another value without taking ownership "
"of the value, and is also called \"borrowing\". Shared references are read-"
"only, and the referenced data cannot change."
msgstr ""
"Reference menyediakan cara mengakses nilai lain tanpa mengambil ownership "
"atas nilai tersebut; ini juga disebut “borrowing”. Shared reference bersifat"
" read-only, dan data yang dirujuk tidak dapat berubah."

#: src/references/shared.md src/std-traits/solution.md
msgid "'A'"
msgstr "'A'"

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid "'B'"
msgstr "'B'"

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A shared reference to a type `T` has type `&T`. A reference value is made "
"with the `&` operator. The `*` operator \"dereferences\" a reference, "
"yielding its value."
msgstr ""
"Shared reference ke tipe `T` memiliki tipe `&T`. Nilai reference dibuat "
"dengan operator `&`. Operator `*` melakukan “dereference” untuk memperoleh "
"nilai yang dirujuk."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"References can never be null in Rust, so null checking is not necessary."
msgstr ""
"Reference dalam Rust tidak pernah null, sehingga pemeriksaan null tidak "
"diperlukan."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A reference is said to \"borrow\" the value it refers to, and this is a good"
" model for students not familiar with pointers: code can use the reference "
"to access the value, but is still \"owned\" by the original variable. The "
"course will get into more detail on ownership in day 3."
msgstr ""
"Reference dikatakan “meminjam” nilai yang dirujuknya. Ini model yang baik "
"bagi peserta yang belum mengenal pointer: kode dapat mengakses nilai melalui"
" reference, tetapi nilai tersebut tetap “dimiliki” variabel asal. Kursus ini"
" membahas ownership lebih mendalam pada hari 3."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"References are implemented as pointers, and a key advantage is that they can"
" be much smaller than the thing they point to. Students familiar with C or "
"C++ will recognize references as pointers. Later parts of the course will "
"cover how Rust prevents the memory-safety bugs that come from using raw "
"pointers."
msgstr ""
"Reference diimplementasikan sebagai pointer. Salah satu keunggulannya adalah"
" ukurannya dapat jauh lebih kecil daripada nilai yang dirujuk. Peserta yang "
"mengenal C atau C++ akan mengenalinya sebagai pointer. Bagian selanjutnya "
"membahas cara Rust mencegah bug memory safety akibat penggunaan raw pointer."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"Explicit referencing with `&` is required, except when invoking methods, "
"where Rust performs automatic referencing and dereferencing."
msgstr ""
"Pembuatan reference secara eksplisit dengan `&` diwajibkan, kecuali saat "
"memanggil method: Rust melakukan referencing dan dereferencing secara "
"otomatis."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"Rust will auto-dereference in some cases, in particular when invoking "
"methods (try `r.is_ascii()`). There is no need for an `->` operator like in "
"C++."
msgstr ""
"Rust melakukan auto-dereference dalam beberapa keadaan, khususnya saat "
"memanggil method; coba `r.is_ascii()`. Operator `->` seperti dalam C++ tidak"
" diperlukan."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"In this example, `r` is mutable so that it can be reassigned (`r = &b`). "
"Note that this re-binds `r`, so that it refers to something else. This is "
"different from C++, where assignment to a reference changes the referenced "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, `r` bersifat mutable agar dapat diberi nilai baru (`r = "
"&b`). Perhatikan bahwa ini mengubah binding `r` sehingga merujuk nilai lain."
" Ini berbeda dari C++, ketika assignment ke reference mengubah nilai yang "
"dirujuk."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A shared reference does not allow modifying the value it refers to, even if "
"that value was mutable. Try `*r = 'X'`."
msgstr ""
"Shared reference tidak mengizinkan perubahan nilai yang dirujuk, meskipun "
"nilai itu bersifat mutable. Coba `*r = 'X'`."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"Rust is tracking the lifetimes of all references to ensure they live long "
"enough. Dangling references cannot occur in safe Rust."
msgstr ""
"Rust melacak lifetime semua reference untuk memastikan masa berlakunya cukup"
" panjang. Dangling reference tidak dapat terjadi dalam safe Rust."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"We will talk more about borrowing and preventing dangling references when we"
" get to ownership."
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membahas borrowing dan pencegahan dangling reference lebih lanjut "
"saat membahas ownership."

#: src/references/exclusive.md
msgid ""
"Exclusive references, also known as mutable references, allow changing the "
"value they refer to. They have type `&mut T`."
msgstr ""
"Exclusive reference, yang juga disebut mutable reference, memungkinkan "
"perubahan nilai yang dirujuk. Tipenya adalah `&mut T`."

#: src/references/exclusive.md
msgid ""
"\"Exclusive\" means that only this reference can be used to access the "
"value. No other references (shared or exclusive) can exist at the same time,"
" and the referenced value cannot be accessed while the exclusive reference "
"exists. Try making an `&point.0` or changing `point.0` while `x_coord` is "
"alive."
msgstr ""
"“Exclusive” berarti hanya reference ini yang dapat digunakan untuk mengakses"
" nilai. Reference lain, baik shared maupun exclusive, tidak boleh ada pada "
"saat yang sama, dan nilai yang dirujuk tidak dapat diakses selama exclusive "
"reference masih ada. Coba buat `&point.0` atau ubah `point.0` ketika "
"`x_coord` masih berlaku."

#: src/references/exclusive.md
msgid ""
"Be sure to note the difference between `let mut x_coord: &i32` and `let "
"x_coord: &mut i32`. The first one is a shared reference that can be bound to"
" different values, while the second is an exclusive reference to a mutable "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Pastikan Anda menjelaskan perbedaan `let mut x_coord: &i32` dan `let "
"x_coord: &mut i32`. Yang pertama adalah shared reference yang binding-nya "
"dapat diarahkan ke nilai berbeda; yang kedua adalah exclusive reference ke "
"nilai yang dapat diubah."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid "A slice gives you a view into a larger collection:"
msgstr ""
"Slice memberikan akses ke suatu bagian dari collection yang lebih besar:"

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid "Slices borrow data from the sliced type."
msgstr "Slice meminjam data dari tipe yang diambil bagiannya."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"We create a slice by borrowing `a` and specifying the starting and ending "
"indexes in brackets."
msgstr ""
"Kita membuat slice dengan meminjam `a` dan menentukan indeks awal serta "
"akhir dalam kurung siku."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"If the slice starts at index 0, Rust’s range syntax allows us to drop the "
"starting index, meaning that `&a[0..a.len()]` and `&a[..a.len()]` are "
"identical."
msgstr ""
"Jika slice dimulai dari indeks 0, sintaks rentang Rust memungkinkan kita "
"menghilangkan indeks awal. Jadi, `&a[0..a.len()]` dan `&a[..a.len()]` "
"identik."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"The same is true for the last index, so `&a[2..a.len()]` and `&a[2..]` are "
"identical."
msgstr ""
"Hal yang sama berlaku untuk indeks akhir, sehingga `&a[2..a.len()]` dan "
"`&a[2..]` identik."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"To easily create a slice of the full array, we can therefore use `&a[..]`."
msgstr ""
"Karena itu, untuk membuat slice dari seluruh array dengan mudah, kita dapat "
"menggunakan `&a[..]`."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"`s` is a reference to a slice of `i32`s. Notice that the type of `s` "
"(`&[i32]`) no longer mentions the array length. This allows us to perform "
"computation on slices of different sizes."
msgstr ""
"`s` merupakan reference ke slice berisi nilai `i32`. Perhatikan bahwa tipe "
"`s` (`&[i32]`) tidak lagi menyebut panjang array. Dengan begitu, kita dapat "
"melakukan komputasi pada slice berukuran berbeda."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"Slices always borrow from another object. In this example, `a` has to remain"
" 'alive' (in scope) for at least as long as our slice."
msgstr ""
"Slice selalu meminjam dari objek lain. Dalam contoh ini, `a` harus tetap "
"“hidup” dalam scope setidaknya selama slice kita masih berlaku."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid "You can't \"grow\" a slice once it's created:"
msgstr "Anda tidak dapat “memperbesar” slice setelah dibuat:"

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"You can't append elements of the slice, since it doesn't own the backing "
"buffer."
msgstr ""
"Anda tidak dapat menambahkan elemen ke slice karena slice tidak memiliki "
"ownership atas buffer yang mendasarinya."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"You can't grow a slice to point to a larger section of the backing buffer. A"
" slice does not have information about the length of the underlying buffer "
"and so you can't know how large the slice can be grown."
msgstr ""
"Anda tidak dapat memperbesar slice agar merujuk bagian buffer yang lebih "
"luas. Slice tidak menyimpan informasi panjang buffer yang mendasarinya, "
"sehingga Anda tidak dapat mengetahui sampai sebesar apa slice boleh "
"diperbesar."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"To get a larger slice you have to go back to the original buffer and create "
"a larger slice from there."
msgstr ""
"Untuk memperoleh slice yang lebih besar, Anda harus kembali ke buffer asal "
"dan membuat slice yang lebih besar dari sana."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "We can now understand the two string types in Rust:"
msgstr "Sekarang kita dapat memahami dua tipe string dalam Rust:"

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "`&str` is a slice of UTF-8 encoded bytes, similar to `&[u8]`."
msgstr ""
"`&str` merupakan slice byte dengan encoding UTF-8, serupa dengan `&[u8]`."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"`String` is an owned buffer of UTF-8 encoded bytes, similar to `Vec<T>`."
msgstr ""
"`String` merupakan buffer byte dengan encoding UTF-8 yang memiliki ownership"
" atas datanya, serupa dengan `Vec<T>`."

#: src/references/strings.md src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid "\"World\""
msgstr "\"World\""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "\"s1: {s1}\""
msgstr "\"s1: {s1}\""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "\"Hello \""
msgstr "\"Hello \""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "\"s2: {s2}\""
msgstr "\"s2: {s2}\""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "\"s3: {s3}\""
msgstr "\"s3: {s3}\""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"`&str` introduces a string slice, which is an immutable reference to UTF-8 "
"encoded string data stored in a block of memory. String literals "
"(`\"Hello\"`), are stored in the program’s binary."
msgstr ""
"`&str` memperkenalkan string slice, yaitu immutable reference ke data string"
" dengan encoding UTF-8 yang tersimpan dalam suatu blok memori. Literal "
"string (`\"Hello\"`) disimpan dalam binary program."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"Rust's `String` type is a wrapper around a vector of bytes. As with a "
"`Vec<T>`, it is owned."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `String` dalam Rust membungkus vector byte. Seperti `Vec<T>`, tipe ini "
"memiliki ownership atas datanya."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"As with many other types `String::from()` creates a string from a string "
"literal; `String::new()` creates a new empty string, to which string data "
"can be added using the `push()` and `push_str()` methods."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada banyak tipe lain, `String::from()` membuat string dari literal "
"string. `String::new()` membuat string kosong baru, yang dapat ditambahi "
"data string menggunakan method `push()` dan `push_str()`."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"The `format!()` macro is a convenient way to generate an owned string from "
"dynamic values. It accepts the same format specification as `println!()`."
msgstr ""
"Macro `format!()` merupakan cara praktis menghasilkan owned string dari "
"nilai dinamis. Macro ini menerima spesifikasi format yang sama dengan "
"`println!()`."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"You can borrow `&str` slices from `String` via `&` and optionally range "
"selection. If you select a byte range that is not aligned to character "
"boundaries, the expression will panic. The `chars` iterator iterates over "
"characters and is preferred over trying to get character boundaries right."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat meminjam slice `&str` dari `String` menggunakan `&`, dengan "
"pilihan rentang bila diperlukan. Jika rentang byte yang dipilih tidak "
"sejajar dengan batas karakter, ekspresi akan mengalami panic. Iterator "
"`chars` mengiterasi karakter dan lebih disarankan daripada mencoba "
"menentukan batas karakter sendiri."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"For C++ programmers: think of `&str` as `std::string_view` from C++, but the"
" one that always points to a valid string in memory. Rust `String` is a "
"rough equivalent of `std::string` from C++ (main difference: it can only "
"contain UTF-8 encoded bytes and will never use a small-string optimization)."
msgstr ""
"Bagi programmer C++: bayangkan `&str` seperti `std::string_view` dalam C++, "
"tetapi selalu merujuk string yang valid dalam memori. `String` Rust kurang "
"lebih setara dengan `std::string` dalam C++. Perbedaan utamanya: hanya dapat"
" memuat byte dengan encoding UTF-8 dan tidak pernah menggunakan small-string"
" optimization."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "Byte strings literals allow you to create a `&[u8]` value directly:"
msgstr ""
"Literal byte string memungkinkan Anda membuat nilai `&[u8]` secara langsung:"

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"Raw strings allow you to create a `&str` value with escapes disabled: "
"`r\"\\n\" == \"\\\\n\"`. You can embed double-quotes by using an equal "
"amount of `#` on either side of the quotes:"
msgstr ""
"Raw string memungkinkan Anda membuat nilai `&str` tanpa pemrosesan escape: "
"`r\"\\n\" == \"\\\\n\"`. Anda dapat menyertakan tanda kutip ganda dengan "
"menggunakan jumlah `#` yang sama di kedua sisi tanda kutip:"

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"Rust enforces a number of rules for references that make them always safe to"
" use. One rule is that references can never be `null`, making them safe to "
"use without `null` checks. The other rule we'll look at for now is that "
"references can't _outlive_ the data they point to."
msgstr ""
"Rust menerapkan sejumlah aturan agar reference selalu aman digunakan. Salah "
"satunya, reference tidak pernah `null`, sehingga aman digunakan tanpa "
"pemeriksaan `null`. Aturan lain yang kita bahas sekarang adalah bahwa "
"reference tidak boleh _berlaku lebih lama_ daripada data yang dirujuk."

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"This slide gets students thinking about references as not simply being "
"pointers, since Rust has different rules for references than other "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini mengajak peserta memahami bahwa reference bukan sekadar pointer, "
"karena Rust memiliki aturan reference yang berbeda dari bahasa lain."

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"We'll look at the rest of Rust's borrowing rules on day 3 when we talk about"
" Rust's ownership system."
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membahas aturan borrowing Rust lainnya pada hari 3 saat "
"mempelajari sistem ownership Rust."

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"Rust's equivalent of nullability is the `Option` type, which can be used to "
"make any type \"nullable\" (not just references/pointers). We haven't yet "
"introduced enums or pattern matching, though, so try not to go into too much"
" detail about this here."
msgstr ""
"Padanan nullability dalam Rust adalah tipe `Option`, yang dapat membuat tipe"
" apa pun “nullable”, bukan hanya reference/pointer. Namun, kita belum "
"memperkenalkan enum atau pattern matching, jadi usahakan tidak membahasnya "
"terlalu terperinci di sini."

#: src/references/exercise.md
msgid ""
"We will create a few utility functions for 3-dimensional geometry, "
"representing a point as `[f64;3]`. It is up to you to determine the function"
" signatures."
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membuat beberapa fungsi bantu untuk geometri 3 dimensi, dengan "
"titik direpresentasikan sebagai `[f64;3]`. Anda menentukan sendiri signature"
" fungsinya."

#: src/references/exercise.md
msgid ""
"// Calculate the magnitude of a vector by summing the squares of its coordinates\n"
"// and taking the square root. Use the `sqrt()` method to calculate the square\n"
"// root, like `v.sqrt()`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Calculate the magnitude of a vector by summing the squares of its coordinates\n"
"// and taking the square root. Use the `sqrt()` method to calculate the square\n"
"// root, like `v.sqrt()`.\n"

#: src/references/exercise.md
msgid ""
"// Normalize a vector by calculating its magnitude and dividing all of its\n"
"// coordinates by that magnitude.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Normalize a vector by calculating its magnitude and dividing all of its\n"
"// coordinates by that magnitude.\n"

