#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid "Structs work like in C or C++."
msgstr "Struct bekerja seperti dalam C atau C++."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid "Like in C++, and unlike in C, no typedef is needed to define a type."
msgstr ""
"Seperti C++, dan berbeda dari C, typedef tidak diperlukan untuk "
"mendefinisikan tipe."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid "Unlike in C++, there is no inheritance between structs."
msgstr "Berbeda dari C++, tidak ada inheritance antar-struct."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid ""
"This may be a good time to let people know there are different types of "
"structs."
msgstr ""
"Ini mungkin saat yang tepat untuk menjelaskan bahwa ada beberapa jenis "
"struct."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid ""
"Zero-sized structs (e.g. `struct Foo;`) might be used when implementing a "
"trait on some type but don’t have any data that you want to store in the "
"value itself."
msgstr ""
"Zero-sized struct, misalnya `struct Foo;`, dapat digunakan ketika Anda "
"mengimplementasikan trait untuk suatu tipe tetapi tidak memiliki data yang "
"ingin disimpan pada nilainya sendiri."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid ""
"The next slide will introduce Tuple structs, used when the field names are "
"not important."
msgstr ""
"Slide berikutnya memperkenalkan tuple struct, yang digunakan ketika nama "
"field tidak penting."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid ""
"If you already have variables with the right names, then you can create the "
"struct using a shorthand."
msgstr ""
"Jika sudah memiliki variabel dengan nama yang sesuai, Anda dapat membuat "
"struct menggunakan sintaks singkat."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid ""
"Struct fields do not support default values. Default values are specified by"
" implementing the `Default` trait which we will cover later."
msgstr ""
"Field struct tidak mendukung nilai default. Nilai default ditentukan dengan "
"mengimplementasikan trait `Default`, yang akan kita bahas nanti."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid "You can also demonstrate the struct update syntax here:"
msgstr "Anda juga dapat memperagakan sintaks struct update di sini:"

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid "\"Jackie\""
msgstr "\"Jackie\""

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid ""
"It allows us to copy the majority of the fields from the old struct without "
"having to explicitly type it all out. It must always be the last element."
msgstr ""
"Sintaks ini memungkinkan kita menyalin sebagian besar field dari struct lama"
" tanpa perlu mengetik semuanya secara eksplisit. Sintaks tersebut harus "
"selalu menjadi elemen terakhir."

#: src/user-defined-types/named-structs.md
msgid ""
"It is mainly used in combination with the `Default` trait. We will talk "
"about struct update syntax in more detail on the slide on the `Default` "
"trait, so we don't need to talk about it here unless students ask about it."
msgstr ""
"Sintaks ini terutama digunakan bersama trait `Default`. Kita akan membahas "
"struct update lebih terperinci pada slide trait `Default`, sehingga tidak "
"perlu membahasnya di sini kecuali peserta bertanya."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid "If the field names are unimportant, you can use a tuple struct:"
msgstr "Jika nama field tidak penting, Anda dapat menggunakan tuple struct:"

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid "\"({}, {})\""
msgstr "\"({}, {})\""

