#: src/methods-and-traits/deriving.md
msgid ""
"Derivation is implemented with macros, and many crates provide useful derive"
" macros to add useful functionality. For example, `serde` can derive "
"serialization support for a struct using `#[derive(Serialize)]`."
msgstr ""
"Derivation diimplementasikan menggunakan macro. Banyak crate menyediakan "
"derive macro untuk menambahkan fungsionalitas yang berguna. Misalnya, "
"`serde` dapat menghasilkan dukungan serialization bagi struct melalui "
"`#[derive(Serialize)]`."

#: src/methods-and-traits/deriving.md
msgid ""
"Derivation is usually provided for traits that have a common boilerplate "
"implementation that is correct for most cases. For example, demonstrate how "
"a manual `Clone` impl can be repetitive compared to deriving the trait:"
msgstr ""
"Derivation biasanya disediakan bagi trait yang memiliki implementasi "
"boilerplate umum yang benar untuk sebagian besar kasus. Misalnya, peragakan "
"bagaimana implementasi `Clone` manual lebih repetitif dibandingkan deriving "
"trait:"

#: src/methods-and-traits/deriving.md
msgid ""
"Not all of the `.clone()`s in the above are necessary in this case, but this"
" demonstrates the generally boilerplate-y pattern that manual impls would "
"follow, which should help make the use of `derive` clear to students."
msgstr ""
"Tidak semua pemanggilan `.clone()` di atas diperlukan dalam kasus ini. "
"Namun, contoh ini menunjukkan pola boilerplate yang umumnya diikuti "
"implementasi manual, sehingga membantu memperjelas penggunaan `derive` "
"kepada peserta."

#: src/methods-and-traits/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Let's design a simple logging utility, using a trait `Logger` with a `log` "
"method. Code that might log its progress can then take an `&impl Logger`. In"
" testing, this might put messages in the test logfile, while in a production"
" build it would send messages to a log server."
msgstr ""
"Mari merancang utilitas logging sederhana menggunakan trait `Logger` dengan "
"method `log`. Kode yang mungkin mencatat progresnya kemudian dapat menerima "
"`&impl Logger`. Saat testing, pesan dapat dimasukkan ke logfile test, "
"sedangkan pada production build pesan dikirim ke server log."

#: src/methods-and-traits/exercise.md
msgid ""
"However, the `StderrLogger` given below logs all messages, regardless of "
"verbosity. Your task is to write a `VerbosityFilter` type that will ignore "
"messages above a maximum verbosity."
msgstr ""
"Namun, `StderrLogger` berikut mencatat semua pesan tanpa mempertimbangkan "
"verbosity. Tugas Anda adalah menulis tipe `VerbosityFilter` yang mengabaikan"
" pesan di atas tingkat verbosity maksimum."

#: src/methods-and-traits/exercise.md
msgid ""
"This is a common pattern: a struct wrapping a trait implementation and "
"implementing that same trait, adding behavior in the process. In the "
"\"Generics\" segment, we will see how to make the wrapper generic over the "
"wrapped type."
msgstr ""
"Ini pola yang umum: struct membungkus implementasi trait, "
"mengimplementasikan trait yang sama, dan menambahkan perilaku. Pada bagian "
"“Generics”, kita melihat cara membuat wrapper yang generic terhadap tipe "
"yang dibungkus."

