#: src/closures.md src/concurrency/threads.md src/concurrency/shared-state.md
msgid "This segment should take about 30 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr "Bagian ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar 30 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid "Closures are created with vertical bars: `|..| ..`."
msgstr "Closure dibuat menggunakan garis vertikal: `|..| ..`."

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid "// Argument and return type can be inferred for lightweight syntax:\n"
msgstr "// Argument and return type can be inferred for lightweight syntax:\n"

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid "// Or we can specify types and bracket the body to be fully explicit:\n"
msgstr "// Or we can specify types and bracket the body to be fully explicit:\n"

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid ""
"The arguments go between the `|..|`. The body can be surrounded by `{ .. }`,"
" but if it is a single expression these can be omitted."
msgstr ""
"Argumen diletakkan di antara `|..|`. Isinya dapat diapit `{ .. }`, tetapi "
"kurung kurawal dapat dihilangkan jika hanya berisi satu ekspresi."

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid ""
"Argument types are optional, and are inferred if not given. The return type "
"is also optional, but can only be written if using `{ .. }` around the body."
msgstr ""
"Tipe argumen bersifat opsional dan akan disimpulkan jika tidak ditulis. Tipe"
" nilai kembalian juga opsional, tetapi hanya dapat ditulis jika isi closure "
"diapit `{ .. }`."

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid ""
"The examples can both be written as mere nested functions instead -- they do"
" not capture any variables from their lexical environment. We will see "
"captures next."
msgstr ""
"Kedua contoh juga dapat ditulis sebagai fungsi bersarang biasa karena tidak "
"menangkap variabel dari lexical environment-nya. Kita membahas penangkapan "
"variabel berikutnya."

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid ""
"The ability to store functions in variables doesn't just apply to closures, "
"regular functions can be put in variables and then invoked the same way that"
" closures can: [Example in the playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=817cbeeefc49f3d0d180a3d6d54c8bda)."
msgstr ""
"Kemampuan menyimpan fungsi dalam variabel tidak hanya berlaku untuk closure."
" Fungsi biasa juga dapat disimpan dalam variabel dan dipanggil dengan cara "
"yang sama: [contoh di playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=817cbeeefc49f3d0d180a3d6d54c8bda)."

#: src/closures/syntax.md
msgid ""
"The linked example also demonstrates that closures that don't capture "
"anything can also coerce to a regular function pointer."
msgstr ""
"Contoh pada tautan tersebut juga menunjukkan bahwa closure yang tidak "
"menangkap apa pun dapat mengalami coercion menjadi function pointer biasa."

#: src/closures/capturing.md
msgid ""
"A closure can capture variables from the environment where it was defined."
msgstr ""
"Closure dapat menangkap variabel dari environment tempatnya didefinisikan."

#: src/closures/capturing.md
msgid ""
"By default, a closure captures values by reference. Here `max_value` is "
"captured by `clamp`, but still available to `main` for printing. Try making "
"`max_value` mutable, changing it, and printing the clamped values again. Why"
" doesn't this work?"
msgstr ""
"Secara default, closure menangkap nilai by reference. Di sini, `max_value` "
"ditangkap oleh `clamp`, tetapi tetap tersedia bagi `main` untuk dicetak. "
"Coba jadikan `max_value` mutable, ubah nilainya, lalu cetak kembali nilai "
"hasil clamp. Mengapa ini tidak bekerja?"

#: src/closures/capturing.md
msgid ""
"If a closure mutates values, it will capture them by mutable reference. Try "
"adding `max_value += 1` to `clamp`."
msgstr ""
"Jika closure mengubah nilai, nilai tersebut ditangkap melalui mutable "
"reference. Coba tambahkan `max_value += 1` ke `clamp`."

#: src/closures/capturing.md
msgid ""
"You can force a closure to move values instead of referencing them with the "
"`move` keyword. This can help with lifetimes, for example if the closure "
"must outlive the captured values (more on lifetimes later)."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat memaksa closure memindahkan nilai, alih-alih merujuknya, "
"menggunakan keyword `move`. Ini dapat membantu menangani lifetime, misalnya "
"jika closure harus berlaku lebih lama daripada nilai yang ditangkap. "
"Lifetime dibahas lebih lanjut nanti."

#: src/closures/capturing.md
msgid ""
"This looks like `move |v| ..`. Try adding this keyword and see if `main` can"
" still access `max_value` after defining `clamp`."
msgstr ""
"Bentuknya adalah `move |v| ..`. Coba tambahkan keyword ini dan periksa "
"apakah `main` masih dapat mengakses `max_value` setelah `clamp` "
"didefinisikan."

#: src/closures/capturing.md
msgid ""
"By default, closures will capture each variable from an outer scope by the "
"least demanding form of access they can (by shared reference if possible, "
"then exclusive reference, then by move). The `move` keyword forces capture "
"by value."
msgstr ""
"Secara default, closure menangkap setiap variabel dari scope luar dengan "
"bentuk akses paling ringan yang memungkinkan: shared reference jika bisa, "
"kemudian exclusive reference, lalu move. Keyword `move` memaksa penangkapan "
"by value."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "Closure traits"
msgstr "Trait closure"

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"Closures or lambda expressions have types that cannot be named. However, "
"they implement special [`Fn`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/ops/trait.Fn.html), [`FnMut`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/ops/trait.FnMut.html), and [`FnOnce`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/ops/trait.FnOnce.html) traits:"
msgstr ""
"Closure atau ekspresi lambda memiliki tipe yang tidak dapat disebutkan "
"namanya. Namun, tipe tersebut mengimplementasikan trait khusus "
"[`Fn`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ops/trait.Fn.html), "
"[`FnMut`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ops/trait.FnMut.html), dan "
"[`FnOnce`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ops/trait.FnOnce.html):"

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"The special types `fn(..) -> T` refer to function pointers - either the "
"address of a function, or a closure that captures nothing."
msgstr ""
"Tipe khusus `fn(..) -> T` merujuk function pointer, baik alamat suatu fungsi"
" maupun closure yang tidak menangkap apa pun."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"Calling {func_name}({input}): {}\""
msgstr "\"Calling {func_name}({input}): {}\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"-itis\""
msgstr "\"-itis\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"{x}{suffix}\""
msgstr "\"{x}{suffix}\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"add_suffix\""
msgstr "\"add_suffix\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"senior\""
msgstr "\"senior\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"appendix\""
msgstr "\"appendix\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"/\""
msgstr "\"/\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"accumulate\""
msgstr "\"accumulate\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"red\""
msgstr "\"red\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"green\""
msgstr "\"green\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"blue\""
msgstr "\"blue\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"take_and_reverse\""
msgstr "\"take_and_reverse\""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid "\"reversed: \""
msgstr "\"reversed: \""

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"An `Fn` (e.g. `add_suffix`) neither consumes nor mutates captured values. It"
" can be called needing only a shared reference to the closure, which means "
"the closure can be executed repeatedly and even concurrently."
msgstr ""
"`Fn`, misalnya `add_suffix`, tidak mengonsumsi atau mengubah nilai yang "
"ditangkap. Pemanggilannya hanya memerlukan shared reference ke closure, "
"sehingga closure dapat dijalankan berulang kali, bahkan secara concurrent."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"An `FnMut` (e.g. `accumulate`) might mutate captured values. The closure "
"object is accessed via exclusive reference, so it can be called repeatedly "
"but not concurrently."
msgstr ""
"`FnMut`, misalnya `accumulate`, dapat mengubah nilai yang ditangkap. Objek "
"closure diakses melalui exclusive reference, sehingga dapat dipanggil "
"berulang kali, tetapi tidak secara concurrent."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"If you have an `FnOnce` (e.g. `take_and_reverse`), you may only call it "
"once. Doing so consumes the closure and any values captured by move."
msgstr ""
"Jika memiliki `FnOnce`, misalnya `take_and_reverse`, Anda hanya dapat "
"memanggilnya sekali. Pemanggilan ini mengonsumsi closure dan semua nilai "
"yang ditangkap melalui move."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"`FnMut` is a subtype of `FnOnce`. `Fn` is a subtype of `FnMut` and `FnOnce`."
" I.e. you can use an `FnMut` wherever an `FnOnce` is called for, and you can"
" use an `Fn` wherever an `FnMut` or `FnOnce` is called for."
msgstr ""
"`FnMut` merupakan subtype dari `FnOnce`. `Fn` merupakan subtype dari `FnMut`"
" dan `FnOnce`. Artinya, `FnMut` dapat digunakan ketika `FnOnce` diperlukan, "
"dan `Fn` dapat digunakan ketika `FnMut` atau `FnOnce` diperlukan."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"When you define a function that takes a closure, you should take `FnOnce` if"
" you can (i.e. you call it once), or `FnMut` else, and last `Fn`. This "
"allows the most flexibility for the caller."
msgstr ""
"Saat mendefinisikan fungsi yang menerima closure, sebaiknya terima `FnOnce` "
"jika memungkinkan, yaitu jika closure dipanggil sekali. Jika tidak, gunakan "
"`FnMut`, lalu `Fn` sebagai pilihan terakhir. Ini memberikan fleksibilitas "
"terbesar bagi caller."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"In contrast, when you have a closure, the most flexible you can have is `Fn`"
" (which can be passed to a consumer of any of the three closure traits), "
"then `FnMut`, and lastly `FnOnce`."
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, ketika Anda memiliki closure, bentuk paling fleksibel adalah "
"`Fn`, yang dapat diteruskan ke penerima salah satu dari ketiga trait "
"closure, kemudian `FnMut`, dan terakhir `FnOnce`."

#: src/closures/traits.md
msgid ""
"The compiler also infers `Copy` (e.g. for `add_suffix`) and `Clone` (e.g. "
"`take_and_reverse`), depending on what the closure captures. Function "
"pointers (references to `fn` items) implement `Copy` and `Fn`."
msgstr ""
"Compiler juga menyimpulkan `Copy`, misalnya untuk `add_suffix`, dan `Clone`,"
" misalnya untuk `take_and_reverse`, sesuai nilai yang ditangkap closure. "
"Function pointer, yaitu reference ke item `fn`, mengimplementasikan `Copy` "
"dan `Fn`."

