#: src/std-types/std.md
msgid ""
"Rust comes with a standard library that helps establish a set of common "
"types used by Rust libraries and programs. This way, two libraries can work "
"together smoothly because they both use the same `String` type."
msgstr ""
"Rust menyediakan standard library yang menetapkan sejumlah tipe umum untuk "
"library dan program Rust. Dengan demikian, dua library dapat bekerja sama "
"dengan lancar karena sama-sama menggunakan tipe `String`."

#: src/std-types/std.md
msgid ""
"In fact, Rust contains several layers of the Standard Library: `core`, "
"`alloc` and `std`."
msgstr ""
"Standard Library Rust sebenarnya terdiri atas beberapa lapisan: `core`, "
"`alloc`, dan `std`."

#: src/std-types/std.md
msgid ""
"`core` includes the most basic types and functions that don't depend on "
"`libc`, allocator or even the presence of an operating system."
msgstr ""
"`core` memuat tipe dan fungsi paling dasar yang tidak bergantung pada "
"`libc`, allocator, bahkan keberadaan sistem operasi."

#: src/std-types/std.md
msgid ""
"`alloc` includes types that require a global heap allocator, such as `Vec`, "
"`Box` and `Arc`."
msgstr ""
"`alloc` memuat tipe yang memerlukan global heap allocator, seperti `Vec`, "
"`Box`, dan `Arc`."

#: src/std-types/std.md
msgid ""
"Embedded Rust applications typically only use `core`, and sometimes `alloc`."
msgstr ""
"Aplikasi embedded Rust biasanya hanya menggunakan `core`, dan terkadang "
"`alloc`."

