"Termasuk istirahat 10 menit, sesi ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar"
" 2 jam dan 20 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/memory-management.md
msgid "Drop"
msgstr "Drop"

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Programs allocate memory in two ways:"
msgstr "Program mengalokasikan memori dengan dua cara:"

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Stack: Continuous area of memory for local variables."
msgstr "Stack: area memori berurutan untuk variabel lokal."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Values have fixed sizes known at compile time."
msgstr "Nilai memiliki ukuran tetap yang diketahui saat compile time."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Extremely fast: just move a stack pointer."
msgstr "Sangat cepat: cukup menggeser stack pointer."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Easy to manage: follows function calls."
msgstr "Mudah dikelola: mengikuti pemanggilan fungsi."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Great memory locality."
msgstr "Memory locality yang sangat baik."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Heap: Storage of values outside of function calls."
msgstr "Heap: penyimpanan nilai di luar pemanggilan fungsi."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Values have dynamic sizes determined at runtime."
msgstr "Nilai memiliki ukuran dinamis yang ditentukan saat runtime."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "Slightly slower than the stack: some bookkeeping needed."
msgstr ""
"Sedikit lebih lambat daripada stack: memerlukan pencatatan pengelolaan "
"memori."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "No guarantee of memory locality."
msgstr "Tidak ada jaminan memory locality."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid ""
"Creating a `String` puts fixed-sized metadata on the stack and dynamically "
"sized data, the actual string, on the heap:"
msgstr ""
"Membuat `String` menempatkan metadata berukuran tetap pada stack dan data "
"berukuran dinamis, yaitu isi string, pada heap:"

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid ""
"Mention that a `String` is backed by a `Vec`, so it has a capacity and "
"length and can grow if mutable via reallocation on the heap."
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa `String` menggunakan `Vec` sebagai penyimpanan, sehingga "
"memiliki capacity dan length serta dapat bertambah ukurannya melalui "
"realokasi pada heap jika bersifat mutable."

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid ""
"If students ask about it, you can mention that the underlying memory is heap"
" allocated using the [System Allocator](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/alloc/struct.System.html) and custom allocators can be "
"implemented using the [Allocator API](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/alloc/index.html)"
msgstr ""
"Jika peserta bertanya, sampaikan bahwa memori yang mendasarinya dialokasikan"
" pada heap menggunakan [System Allocator](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/alloc/struct.System.html), dan allocator khusus dapat "
"diimplementasikan menggunakan [Allocator API](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/alloc/index.html)"

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid ""
"We can inspect the memory layout with `unsafe` Rust. However, you should "
"point out that this is rightfully unsafe!"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat memeriksa memory layout menggunakan Rust `unsafe`. Namun, "
"tegaskan bahwa cara ini memang tidak aman!"

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "\"world\""
msgstr "\"world\""

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid ""
"// DON'T DO THIS AT HOME! For educational purposes only.\n"
"    // String provides no guarantees about its layout, so this could lead to\n"
"    // undefined behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"// DON'T DO THIS AT HOME! For educational purposes only.\n"
"    // String provides no guarantees about its layout, so this could lead to\n"
"    // undefined behavior.\n"

#: src/memory-management/review.md
msgid "\"capacity = {capacity}, ptr = {ptr:#x}, len = {len}\""
msgstr "\"capacity = {capacity}, ptr = {ptr:#x}, len = {len}\""

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Traditionally, languages have fallen into two broad categories:"
msgstr ""
"Secara tradisional, bahasa pemrograman terbagi menjadi dua kategori besar:"

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Full control via manual memory management: C, C++, Pascal, ..."
msgstr "Kendali penuh melalui pengelolaan memori manual: C, C++, Pascal, ..."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Programmer decides when to allocate or free heap memory."
msgstr "Programmer menentukan kapan memori heap dialokasikan atau dibebaskan."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Programmer must determine whether a pointer still points to valid memory."
msgstr ""
"Programmer harus menentukan apakah pointer masih merujuk memori yang valid."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Studies show, programmers make mistakes."
msgstr "Penelitian menunjukkan bahwa programmer melakukan kesalahan."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Full safety via automatic memory management at runtime: Java, Python, Go, "
"Haskell, ..."
msgstr ""
"Keamanan penuh melalui pengelolaan memori otomatis saat runtime: Java, "
"Python, Go, Haskell, ..."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"A runtime system ensures that memory is not freed until it can no longer be "
"referenced."
msgstr ""
"Sistem runtime memastikan memori tidak dibebaskan sampai tidak dapat dirujuk"
" lagi."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Typically implemented with reference counting or garbage collection."
msgstr ""
"Biasanya diimplementasikan menggunakan reference counting atau garbage "
"collection."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Rust offers a new mix:"
msgstr "Rust menawarkan kombinasi baru:"

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Full control _and_ safety via compile time enforcement of correct memory "
"management."
msgstr ""
"Kendali penuh _dan_ keamanan melalui penegakan pengelolaan memori yang benar"
" saat compile time."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "It does this with an explicit ownership concept."
msgstr "Rust melakukannya melalui konsep ownership yang eksplisit."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"This slide is intended to help students coming from other languages to put "
"Rust in context."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini membantu peserta yang terbiasa dengan bahasa lain memahami posisi "
"Rust."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"C must manage heap manually with `malloc` and `free`. Common errors include "
"forgetting to call `free`, calling it multiple times for the same pointer, "
"or dereferencing a pointer after the memory it points to has been freed."
msgstr ""
"Dalam C, heap harus dikelola secara manual menggunakan `malloc` dan `free`. "
"Kesalahan umum meliputi lupa memanggil `free`, memanggilnya beberapa kali "
"untuk pointer yang sama, atau melakukan dereference setelah memori yang "
"dirujuk dibebaskan."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"C++ has tools like smart pointers (`unique_ptr`, `shared_ptr`) that take "
"advantage of language guarantees about calling destructors to ensure memory "
"is freed when a function returns. It is still quite easy to misuse these "
"tools and create similar bugs to C."
msgstr ""
"C++ memiliki fasilitas seperti smart pointer (`unique_ptr`, `shared_ptr`) "
"yang memanfaatkan jaminan bahasa tentang pemanggilan destructor agar memori "
"dibebaskan saat fungsi selesai. Fasilitas ini masih cukup mudah "
"disalahgunakan sehingga menimbulkan bug serupa dengan C."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Java, Go, and Python rely on the garbage collector to identify memory that "
"is no longer reachable and discard it. This guarantees that any pointer can "
"be dereferenced, eliminating use-after-free and other classes of bugs. But, "
"GC has a runtime cost and is difficult to tune properly."
msgstr ""
"Java, Go, dan Python mengandalkan garbage collector untuk mengidentifikasi "
"dan membuang memori yang tidak lagi dapat dijangkau. Ini menjamin setiap "
"pointer dapat di-dereference, sehingga menghilangkan use-after-free dan "
"kategori bug lainnya. Namun, GC memiliki biaya runtime dan sulit disetel "
"dengan tepat."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Rust's ownership and borrowing model can, in many cases, get the performance"
" of C, with alloc and free operations precisely where they are required -- "
"zero-cost. It also provides tools similar to C++'s smart pointers. When "
"required, other options such as reference counting are available, and there "
"are even crates available to support runtime garbage collection (not covered"
" in this class)."
msgstr ""
"Dalam banyak kasus, model ownership dan borrowing Rust dapat mencapai "
"performa C, dengan operasi alloc dan free tepat di tempat yang "
"diperlukan—zero-cost. Rust juga menyediakan fasilitas serupa smart pointer "
"C++. Jika diperlukan, tersedia pilihan lain seperti reference counting, "
"bahkan crate yang mendukung garbage collection saat runtime, yang tidak "
"dibahas dalam kelas ini."

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"All variable bindings have a _scope_ where they are valid and it is an error"
" to use a variable outside its scope:"
msgstr ""
"Semua variable binding memiliki _scope_ tempat binding tersebut valid. "
"Menggunakan variabel di luar scope merupakan error:"

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"We say that the variable _owns_ the value. Every Rust value has precisely "
"one owner at all times."
msgstr ""
"Kita menyebut variabel sebagai _pemilik_ nilai. Setiap nilai Rust selalu "
"memiliki tepat satu owner."

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"At the end of the scope, the variable is _dropped_ and the data is freed. A "
"destructor can run here to free up resources."
msgstr ""
"Pada akhir scope, variabel _di-drop_ dan datanya dibebaskan. Destructor "
"dapat dijalankan di sini untuk membebaskan resource."

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"Students familiar with garbage collection implementations will know that a "
"garbage collector starts with a set of \"roots\" to find all reachable "
"memory. Rust's \"single owner\" principle is a similar idea."
msgstr ""
"Peserta yang mengenal implementasi garbage collection mengetahui bahwa "
"garbage collector berawal dari sekumpulan “root” untuk menemukan semua "
"memori yang dapat dijangkau. Prinsip “single owner” Rust merupakan gagasan "
"serupa."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "An assignment will transfer _ownership_ between variables:"
msgstr "Assignment memindahkan _ownership_ antarvariabel:"

#: src/memory-management/move.md src/concurrency/async-control-flow/select.md
