#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid ""
"As we saw before, instead of transferring ownership when calling a function,"
" you can let a function _borrow_ the value:"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang telah kita lihat, alih-alih memindahkan ownership saat "
"memanggil fungsi, Anda dapat membiarkan fungsi _meminjam_ nilai tersebut:"

#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid "The `add` function _borrows_ two points and returns a new point."
msgstr "Fungsi `add` _meminjam_ dua titik dan mengembalikan titik baru."

#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid "The caller retains ownership of the inputs."
msgstr "Caller tetap memiliki ownership atas input."

#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid ""
"This slide is a review of the material on references from day 1, expanding "
"slightly to include function arguments and return values."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini meninjau kembali materi reference dari hari 1 dengan sedikit "
"perluasan ke argumen fungsi dan nilai kembalian."

#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid "Notes on stack returns and inlining:"
msgstr "Catatan tentang pengembalian nilai pada stack dan inlining:"

#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate that the return from `add` is cheap because the compiler can "
"eliminate the copy operation, by inlining the call to add into main. Change "
"the above code to print stack addresses and run it on the "
"[Playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=release&edition=2024&gist=0cb13be1c05d7e3446686ad9947c4671)"
" or look at the assembly in [Godbolt](https://rust.godbolt.org/). In the "
"\"DEBUG\" optimization level, the addresses should change, while they stay "
"the same when changing to the \"RELEASE\" setting:"
msgstr ""
"Peragakan bahwa pengembalian nilai dari `add` berbiaya rendah karena "
"compiler dapat menghilangkan penyalinan dengan melakukan inlining "
"pemanggilan add ke main. Ubah kode di atas agar mencetak alamat stack, lalu "
"jalankan di [Playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=release&edition=2024&gist=0cb13be1c05d7e3446686ad9947c4671)"
" atau lihat assembly di [Godbolt](https://rust.godbolt.org/). Pada tingkat "
"optimasi “DEBUG”, alamat seharusnya berubah, sedangkan pada pengaturan "
"“RELEASE” alamat tetap sama:"

#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid ""
"The Rust compiler can do automatic inlining, that can be disabled on a "
"function level with `#[inline(never)]`."
msgstr ""
"Compiler Rust dapat melakukan inlining otomatis, yang dapat dinonaktifkan "
"untuk fungsi tertentu menggunakan `#[inline(never)]`."

#: src/borrowing/shared.md
msgid ""
"Once disabled, the printed address will change on all optimization levels. "
"Looking at Godbolt or Playground, one can see that in this case, the return "
"of the value depends on the ABI, e.g. on amd64 the two i32 that is making up"
" the point will be returned in 2 registers (eax and edx)."
msgstr ""
"Setelah dinonaktifkan, alamat yang dicetak berubah pada semua tingkat "
"optimasi. Melalui Godbolt atau Playground, terlihat bahwa pengembalian nilai"
" pada kasus ini bergantung pada ABI. Misalnya, pada amd64, dua nilai i32 "
"penyusun titik dikembalikan melalui 2 register, yaitu eax dan edx."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Rust's _borrow checker_ puts constraints on the ways you can borrow values. "
"We've already seen that a reference cannot _outlive_ the value it borrows:"
msgstr ""
"_Borrow checker_ Rust membatasi cara nilai dapat dipinjam. Kita telah "
"melihat bahwa reference tidak boleh _berlaku lebih lama_ daripada nilai yang"
" dipinjam:"

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"There's also a second main rule that the borrow checker enforces: The "
"_aliasing_ rule. For a given value, at any time:"
msgstr ""
"Borrow checker juga menegakkan aturan utama kedua, yaitu aturan _aliasing_. "
"Untuk suatu nilai, pada setiap saat:"

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid "You can have one or more shared references to the value, _or_"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat memiliki satu atau beberapa shared reference ke nilai tersebut, "
"_atau_"

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid "You can have exactly one exclusive reference to the value."
msgstr "Anda dapat memiliki tepat satu exclusive reference ke nilai tersebut."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"The \"outlives\" rule was demonstrated previously when we first looked at "
"references. We review it here to show students that the borrow checking is "
"following a few different rules to validate borrowing."
msgstr ""
"Aturan “outlives” telah diperagakan ketika kita pertama kali membahas "
"reference. Kita meninjaunya kembali untuk menunjukkan bahwa borrow checking "
"mengikuti beberapa aturan berbeda untuk memvalidasi borrowing."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"The above code does not compile because `a` is borrowed as mutable (through "
"`c`) and as immutable (through `b`) at the same time."
msgstr ""
"Kode di atas tidak dapat dikompilasi karena `a` dipinjam secara mutable "
"melalui `c` dan immutable melalui `b` pada saat yang sama."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Note that the requirement is that conflicting references not _exist_ at the "
"same point. It does not matter where the reference is dereferenced. Try "
"commenting out `*c = 20` and show that the compiler error still occurs even "
"if we never use `c`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa persyaratannya adalah reference yang bertentangan tidak "
"boleh _ada_ pada saat yang sama. Tempat reference di-dereference tidak "
"memengaruhi hal ini. Coba komentari `*c = 20` dan tunjukkan bahwa error "
"compiler tetap muncul meskipun kita tidak pernah menggunakan `c`."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Note that the intermediate reference `c` isn't necessary to trigger a borrow"
" conflict. Replace `c` with a direct mutation of `a` and demonstrate that "
"this produces a similar error. This is because direct mutation of a value "
"effectively creates a temporary mutable reference."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa reference perantara `c` tidak diperlukan untuk memicu "
"konflik borrow. Ganti `c` dengan perubahan langsung terhadap `a` dan "
"peragakan error serupa yang muncul. Sebab, perubahan langsung suatu nilai "
"secara efektif membuat mutable reference sementara."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Move the `dbg!` statement for `b` before the scope that introduces `c` to "
"make the code compile."
msgstr ""
"Pindahkan statement `dbg!` untuk `b` ke sebelum scope yang memperkenalkan "
"`c` agar kode dapat dikompilasi."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"After that change, the compiler realizes that `b` is only ever used before "
"the new mutable borrow of `a` through `c`. This is a feature of the borrow "
"checker called \"non-lexical lifetimes\"."
msgstr ""
"Setelah perubahan itu, compiler mengetahui bahwa `b` hanya digunakan sebelum"
" mutable borrow baru atas `a` melalui `c`. Fitur borrow checker ini disebut "
"“non-lexical lifetime”."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Technically, multiple mutable references to a piece of data can exist at the"
" same time via re-borrowing. This is what allows you to pass a mutable "
"reference into a function without invalidating the original reference. [This"
" playground example](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=8f5896878611566845fe3b0f4dc5af68)"
" demonstrates that behavior."
msgstr ""
"Secara teknis, beberapa mutable reference ke suatu data dapat ada bersamaan "
"melalui re-borrowing. Inilah yang memungkinkan mutable reference diteruskan "
"ke fungsi tanpa membatalkan reference aslinya. [Contoh playground "
"ini](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=8f5896878611566845fe3b0f4dc5af68)"
" memperagakan perilaku tersebut."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Rust uses the exclusive reference constraint to ensure that data races do "
"not occur in multi-threaded code, since only one thread can have mutable "
"access to a piece of data at a time."
msgstr ""
"Rust menggunakan batasan exclusive reference untuk memastikan data race "
"tidak terjadi pada kode multithread, karena hanya satu thread yang dapat "
"memiliki akses mutable ke suatu data pada satu waktu."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Rust also uses this constraint to optimize code. For example, a value behind"
" a shared reference can be safely cached in a register for the lifetime of "
"that reference."
msgstr ""
"Rust juga menggunakan batasan ini untuk mengoptimalkan kode. Misalnya, nilai"
" di balik shared reference dapat disimpan dalam cache register dengan aman "
"selama lifetime reference tersebut."

#: src/borrowing/borrowck.md
msgid ""
"Fields of a struct can be borrowed independently of each other, but calling "
"a method on a struct will borrow the whole struct, potentially invalidating "
"references to individual fields. See [this playground "
"snippet](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=f293a31f2d4d0d31770486247c2e8437)"
" for an example of this."
msgstr ""
"Field struct dapat dipinjam secara terpisah, tetapi memanggil method pada "
"struct meminjam seluruh struct dan berpotensi membatalkan reference ke field"
" tertentu. Lihat [cuplikan playground ini](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=f293a31f2d4d0d31770486247c2e8437)"
" untuk contohnya."

#: src/borrowing/examples.md
msgid ""
"As a concrete example of how these borrowing rules prevent memory errors, "
"consider the case of modifying a collection while there are references to "
"its elements:"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh konkret bagaimana aturan borrowing mencegah error memori, "
"perhatikan perubahan collection ketika masih ada reference ke elemennya:"

#: src/borrowing/examples.md
msgid "Similarly, consider the case of iterator invalidation:"
msgstr "Demikian pula, perhatikan kasus iterator invalidation:"

#: src/borrowing/examples.md
msgid ""
"In both of these cases, modifying the collection by pushing new elements "
"into it can potentially invalidate existing references to the collection's "
"elements if the collection has to reallocate."
msgstr ""
"Dalam kedua kasus ini, perubahan collection dengan menambahkan elemen baru "
"berpotensi membatalkan reference ke elemen yang ada jika collection perlu "
"melakukan realokasi."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability.md
msgid ""
"In some situations, it's necessary to modify data behind a shared (read-"
"only) reference. For example, a shared data structure might have an internal"
" cache, and wish to update that cache from read-only methods."
msgstr ""
"Dalam beberapa situasi, data di balik shared reference yang read-only perlu "
"diubah. Misalnya, struktur data bersama memiliki cache internal yang perlu "
"diperbarui melalui method read-only."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability.md
msgid ""
"The \"interior mutability\" pattern allows exclusive (mutable) access behind"
" a shared reference. The standard library provides several ways to do this, "
"all while still ensuring safety, typically by performing a runtime check."
msgstr ""
"Pola “interior mutability” memungkinkan akses eksklusif (mutable) di balik "
"shared reference. Standard library menyediakan beberapa cara untuk "
"melakukannya dengan tetap menjamin keamanan, biasanya melalui pemeriksaan "
"runtime."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability.md
msgid ""
"The main thing to take away from this slide is that Rust provides _safe_ "
"ways to modify data behind a shared reference. There are a variety of ways "
"to ensure that safety, and the next sub-slides present a few of them."
msgstr ""
"Hal utama dari slide ini adalah bahwa Rust menyediakan cara _aman_ untuk "
"mengubah data di balik shared reference. Ada berbagai cara menjamin keamanan"
" tersebut, dan beberapa di antaranya dijelaskan pada subslide berikutnya."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/cell.md
msgid ""
"`Cell` wraps a value and allows getting or setting the value using only a "
"shared reference to the `Cell`. However, it does not allow any references to"
" the inner value. Since there are no references, borrowing rules cannot be "
"broken."
msgstr ""
"`Cell` membungkus nilai dan memungkinkan pengambilan atau pengaturan nilai "
"hanya melalui shared reference ke `Cell`. Namun, reference ke nilai di "
"dalamnya tidak diizinkan. Karena tidak ada reference, aturan borrowing tidak"
" dapat dilanggar."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/cell.md
#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid "// Note that `cell` is NOT declared as mutable.\n"
msgstr "// Note that `cell` is NOT declared as mutable.\n"

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/cell.md
msgid ""
"`Cell` is a simple means to ensure safety: it has a `set` method that takes "
"`&self`. This needs no runtime check, but requires moving values, which can "
"have its own cost."
msgstr ""
"`Cell` merupakan cara sederhana menjamin keamanan: method `set` miliknya "
"menerima `&self`. Ini tidak memerlukan pemeriksaan runtime, tetapi "
"membutuhkan perpindahan nilai, yang dapat memiliki biaya tersendiri."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid ""
"`RefCell` allows accessing and mutating a wrapped value by providing "
"alternative types `Ref` and `RefMut` that emulate `&T`/`&mut T` without "
"actually being Rust references."
msgstr ""
"`RefCell` memungkinkan akses dan perubahan nilai yang dibungkus dengan "
"menyediakan tipe alternatif `Ref` dan `RefMut`, yang meniru `&T`/`&mut T` "
"tanpa benar-benar menjadi reference Rust."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid ""
"These types perform dynamic checks using a counter in the `RefCell` to "
"prevent existence of a `RefMut` alongside another `Ref`/`RefMut`."
msgstr ""
"Tipe-tipe ini melakukan pemeriksaan dinamis menggunakan penghitung dalam "
"`RefCell` untuk mencegah `RefMut` hadir bersamaan dengan `Ref`/`RefMut` "
"lain."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid ""
"By implementing `Deref` (and `DerefMut` for `RefMut`), these types allow "
"calling methods on the inner value without allowing references to escape."
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengimplementasikan `Deref`, serta `DerefMut` untuk `RefMut`, tipe-"
"tipe ini memungkinkan pemanggilan method nilai di dalamnya tanpa membiarkan "
"reference lolos keluar."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid ""
"// This triggers an error at runtime.\n"
"        // let other = cell.borrow();\n"
"        // println!(\"{}\", other);\n"
msgstr ""
"// This triggers an error at runtime.\n"
"        // let other = cell.borrow();\n"
"        // println!(\"{}\", other);\n"

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid "\"{cell:?}\""
msgstr "\"{cell:?}\""

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid ""
"`RefCell` enforces Rust's usual borrowing rules (either multiple shared "
"references or a single exclusive reference) with a runtime check. In this "
"case, all borrows are very short and never overlap, so the checks always "
"succeed."
msgstr ""
"`RefCell` menegakkan aturan borrowing Rust yang biasa, yaitu beberapa shared"
" reference atau satu exclusive reference, melalui pemeriksaan runtime. Dalam"
" kasus ini, semua borrow sangat singkat dan tidak tumpang tindih, sehingga "
"pemeriksaan selalu berhasil."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid ""
"The extra block in the example is to end the borrow created by the call to "
"`borrow_mut` before we print the cell. Trying to print a borrowed `RefCell` "
"just shows the message `\"{borrowed}\"`."
msgstr ""
"Block tambahan dalam contoh mengakhiri borrow dari pemanggilan `borrow_mut` "
"sebelum cell dicetak. Mencoba mencetak `RefCell` yang sedang dipinjam hanya "
"menampilkan pesan `\"{borrowed}\"`."

#: src/borrowing/interior-mutability/refcell.md
msgid ""
"There are also `OnceCell` and `OnceLock`, which allow initialization on "
"first use. Making these useful requires some more knowledge than students "
"have at this time."
msgstr ""
"Tersedia pula `OnceCell` dan `OnceLock`, yang memungkinkan inisialisasi saat"
" pertama digunakan. Pemanfaatannya memerlukan pengetahuan tambahan yang "
"belum dimiliki peserta pada tahap ini."

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will manage a wizard's inventory using what you have "
"learned about borrowing and ownership."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda mengelola inventaris penyihir menggunakan "
"pengetahuan tentang borrowing dan ownership."

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The wizard has a collection of spells. You need to implement functions to "
"add spells to the inventory and to cast spells from them."
msgstr ""
"Penyihir memiliki collection berisi mantra. Anda perlu mengimplementasikan "
"fungsi untuk menambahkan mantra ke inventaris dan menggunakannya."

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Spells have a limited number of uses. When a spell has no uses left, it must"
" be removed from the wizard's inventory."
msgstr ""
"Mantra memiliki jumlah penggunaan terbatas. Ketika jatah penggunaannya "
"habis, mantra harus dihapus dari inventaris penyihir."

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md
msgid ""
"// TODO: Implement `add_spell` to take ownership of a spell and add it to\n"
"    // the wizard's inventory.\n"
msgstr ""
"// TODO: Implement `add_spell` to take ownership of a spell and add it to\n"
"    // the wizard's inventory.\n"

