msgstr "// Also accepts an array.\n"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "Motivating Iterators"
msgstr "Alasan Menggunakan Iterator"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"If you want to iterate over the contents of an array, you'll need to define:"
msgstr "Untuk mengiterasi isi array, Anda perlu menentukan:"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"Some state to keep track of where you are in the iteration process, e.g. an "
"index."
msgstr "State untuk mencatat posisi dalam proses iterasi, misalnya indeks."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "A condition to determine when iteration is done."
msgstr "Kondisi untuk menentukan kapan iterasi selesai."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "Logic for updating the state of iteration each loop."
msgstr "Logika untuk memperbarui state iterasi setiap putaran."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "Logic for fetching each element using that iteration state."
msgstr "Logika untuk mengambil setiap elemen berdasarkan state iterasi."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "In a C-style for loop you declare these things directly:"
msgstr "Dalam for loop bergaya C, semua hal ini dideklarasikan langsung:"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"In Rust we bundle this state and logic together into an object known as an "
"\"iterator\"."
msgstr ""
"Dalam Rust, state dan logika tersebut digabungkan ke dalam objek yang "
"disebut “iterator”."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"This slide provides context for what Rust iterators do under the hood. We "
"use the (hopefully) familiar construct of a C-style `for` loop to show how "
"iteration requires some state and some logic, that way on the next slide we "
"can show how an iterator bundles these together."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini memberi konteks tentang cara kerja iterator Rust di balik layar. "
"Kita menggunakan loop `for` bergaya C yang diharapkan sudah familier untuk "
"menunjukkan bahwa iterasi memerlukan state dan logika. Pada slide "
"berikutnya, kita dapat menunjukkan cara iterator menggabungkan keduanya."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"Rust doesn't have a C-style `for` loop, but we can express the same thing "
"with `while`:"
msgstr ""
"Rust tidak memiliki loop `for` bergaya C, tetapi hal yang sama dapat "
"dinyatakan menggunakan `while`:"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"There's another way to express array iteration using `for` in C and C++: You"
" can use a pointer to the front and a pointer to the end of the array and "
"then compare those pointers to determine when the loop should end."
msgstr ""
"Ada cara lain untuk menyatakan iterasi array menggunakan `for` dalam C dan "
"C++: gunakan pointer ke awal dan akhir array, lalu bandingkan keduanya untuk"
" menentukan kapan loop berakhir."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"If students ask, you can point out that this is how Rust's slice and array "
"iterators work under the hood (though implemented as a Rust iterator)."
msgstr ""
"Jika peserta bertanya, sampaikan bahwa beginilah cara kerja iterator slice "
"dan array Rust di balik layar, meskipun diimplementasikan sebagai iterator "
"Rust."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html) "
"trait defines how an object can be used to produce a sequence of values. For"
" example, if we wanted to create an iterator that can produce the elements "
"of a slice it might look something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Trait [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html) "
"mendefinisikan cara objek menghasilkan rangkaian nilai. Misalnya, iterator "
"yang menghasilkan elemen slice dapat berbentuk seperti berikut:"

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The `SliceIter` example implements the same logic as the C-style `for` loop "
"demonstrated on the last slide."
msgstr ""
"Contoh `SliceIter` mengimplementasikan logika yang sama dengan loop `for` "
"bergaya C pada slide sebelumnya."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"Point out to the students that iterators are lazy: Creating the iterator "
"just initializes the struct but does not otherwise do any work. No work "
"happens until the `next` method is called."
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa iterator bersifat lazy: pembuatannya hanya menginisialisasi "
"struct, tanpa melakukan pekerjaan lain. Pekerjaan baru dilakukan ketika "
"method `next` dipanggil."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"Iterators don't need to be finite! It's entirely valid to have an iterator "
"that will produce values forever. For example, a half open range like `0..` "
"will keep going until integer overflow occurs."
msgstr ""
"Iterator tidak harus berhingga! Iterator yang terus menghasilkan nilai tetap"
" valid. Misalnya, rentang terbuka di salah satu sisi seperti `0..` terus "
"berjalan sampai terjadi integer overflow."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The \"real\" version of `SliceIter` is the [`slice::Iter`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/slice/struct.Iter.html) type in the standard library, "
"however the real version uses pointers under the hood instead of an index in"
" order to eliminate bounds checks."
msgstr ""
"Versi “sebenarnya” dari `SliceIter` adalah tipe "
"[`slice::Iter`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/slice/struct.Iter.html)"
" dalam standard library. Namun, versi ini menggunakan pointer, bukan indeks,"
" untuk menghilangkan pemeriksaan batas."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The `SliceIter` example is a good example of a struct that contains a "
"reference and therefore uses lifetime annotations."
msgstr ""
"`SliceIter` merupakan contoh yang baik dari struct yang memuat reference, "
"sehingga menggunakan anotasi lifetime."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"You can also demonstrate adding a generic parameter to `SliceIter` to allow "
"it to work with any kind of slice (not just `&[i32]`)."
msgstr ""
"Anda juga dapat memperagakan penambahan parameter generic pada `SliceIter` "
"agar dapat digunakan pada slice bertipe apa pun, bukan hanya `&[i32]`."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"In addition to the `next` method that defines how an iterator behaves, the "
"`Iterator` trait provides 70+ helper methods that can be used to build "
"customized iterators."
msgstr ""
"Selain method `next` yang menentukan perilaku iterator, trait `Iterator` "
"menyediakan 70+ method bantu untuk membuat iterator sesuai kebutuhan."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Create a range from 1 to 10\n"
msgstr "// Create a range from 1 to 10\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Keep only even numbers\n"
msgstr "// Keep only even numbers\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Square each number\n"
msgstr "// Square each number\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Sum up all the squared numbers\n"
msgstr "// Sum up all the squared numbers\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "\"The sum of squares of even numbers from 1 to 10 is: {}\""
msgstr "\"The sum of squares of even numbers from 1 to 10 is: {}\""

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"The `Iterator` trait implements many common functional programming "
"operations over collections (e.g. `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, etc). This is "
"the trait where you can find all the documentation about them."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Iterator` mengimplementasikan banyak operasi pemrograman fungsional "
"yang umum pada collection, seperti `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, dan lainnya. "
"Seluruh dokumentasinya dapat ditemukan pada trait ini."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"Many of these helper methods take the original iterator and produce a new "
"iterator with different behavior. These are know as \"iterator adapter "
"methods\"."
msgstr ""
"Banyak method bantu menerima iterator asal dan menghasilkan iterator baru "
"dengan perilaku berbeda. Method ini dikenal sebagai “iterator adapter "
"method”."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"Some methods, like `sum` and `count`, consume the iterator and pull all of "
"the elements out of it."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian method, seperti `sum` dan `count`, mengonsumsi iterator dan "
"mengambil seluruh elemennya."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"These methods are designed to be chained together so that it's easy to build"
" a custom iterator that does exactly what you need."
msgstr ""
"Method-method ini dirancang untuk dirangkai agar mudah membuat iterator "
"khusus yang melakukan tepat apa yang Anda butuhkan."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"Rust's iterators are extremely efficient and highly optimizable. Even "
"complex iterators made by combining many adapter methods will still result "
"in code as efficient as equivalent imperative implementations."
msgstr ""
"Iterator Rust sangat efisien dan mudah dioptimalkan. Bahkan iterator "
"kompleks yang menggabungkan banyak adapter method tetap menghasilkan kode "
"seefisien implementasi imperatif yang setara."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"The [`enumerate`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html#method.enumerate) helper gives "
"us a way to get the index of each element for any iterator."
msgstr ""
"Method bantu [`enumerate`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html#method.enumerate) menyediakan "
"cara mendapatkan indeks setiap elemen pada iterator apa pun."

