msgstr "'e'"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "// By default iterating over an array just gives its elements.\n"
msgstr "// By default iterating over an array just gives its elements.\n"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "\"The element is {letter:?}, but what's its index?\""
msgstr "\"The element is {letter:?}, but what's its index?\""

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "// `enumerate` gives both the element and its index.\n"
msgstr "// `enumerate` gives both the element and its index.\n"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "\"{letter:?} has index {i}\""
msgstr "\"{letter:?} has index {i}\""

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"A nuance of Rust's iterators and `for` loops is that an iterator by default "
"does not give you the index of each element. This is fine when all you need "
"are e.g. the values in an array, but it's common to also want the index of "
"each element as you iterate."
msgstr ""
"Salah satu detail iterator Rust dan loop `for` adalah bahwa secara default "
"iterator tidak memberikan indeks setiap elemen. Ini cukup jika Anda hanya "
"memerlukan nilai dalam array, tetapi sering kali indeks setiap elemen juga "
"diperlukan saat iterasi."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"`enumerate` creates an iterator that produces a tuple where the first "
"element is the index and the second element is the original iterator's item."
msgstr ""
"`enumerate` membuat iterator yang menghasilkan tuple dengan indeks sebagai "
"elemen pertama dan item iterator asal sebagai elemen kedua."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"Point out that we can use a pattern for the loop variable in a `for` loop. "
"This allows us to destructure the tuple produced by `enumerate`."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bahwa pattern dapat digunakan untuk variabel loop `for`. Dengan "
"demikian, kita dapat melakukan destructuring tuple yang dihasilkan "
"`enumerate`."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"Note that we had to do `.iter()` first; `enumerate` is an iterator method, "
"not a method on the array type itself."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa kita harus memanggil `.iter()` lebih dahulu: `enumerate` "
"merupakan method iterator, bukan method tipe array itu sendiri."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"The [`collect`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html#method.collect) method lets you build "
"a collection from an [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html)."
msgstr ""
"Method [`collect`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html#method.collect) memungkinkan pembuatan"
" collection dari [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html)."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid "\"prime_squares: {prime_squares:?}\""
msgstr "\"prime_squares: {prime_squares:?}\""

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"Any iterator can be collected in to a `Vec`, `VecDeque`, or `HashSet`. "
"Iterators that produce key-value pairs (i.e. a two-element tuple) can also "
"be collected into `HashMap` and `BTreeMap`."
msgstr ""
"Iterator apa pun dapat dikumpulkan menjadi `Vec`, `VecDeque`, atau "
"`HashSet`. Iterator yang menghasilkan pasangan key-value, yaitu tuple berisi"
" dua elemen, juga dapat dikumpulkan menjadi `HashMap` dan `BTreeMap`."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"Show the students the definition for `collect` in the standard library docs."
" There are two ways to specify the generic type `B` for this method:"
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan definisi `collect` dalam dokumentasi standard library kepada "
"peserta. Ada dua cara menentukan tipe generic `B` untuk method ini:"

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"With the \"turbofish\": `some_iterator.collect::<COLLECTION_TYPE>()`, as "
"shown. The `_` shorthand used here lets Rust infer the type of the `Vec` "
"elements."
msgstr ""
"Dengan “turbofish”: `some_iterator.collect::<COLLECTION_TYPE>()`, seperti "
"pada contoh. Bentuk singkat `_` memungkinkan Rust menyimpulkan tipe elemen "
"`Vec`."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"With type inference: `let prime_squares: Vec<_> = some_iterator.collect()`. "
"Rewrite the example to use this form."
msgstr ""
"Dengan type inference: `let prime_squares: Vec<_> = "
"some_iterator.collect()`. Tulis ulang contoh menggunakan bentuk ini."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"If students are curious about how this works, you can bring up the "
"[`FromIterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.FromIterator.html)"
" trait, which defines how each type of collection gets built from an "
"iterator."
msgstr ""
"Jika peserta ingin mengetahui cara kerjanya, tunjukkan trait "
"[`FromIterator`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.FromIterator.html), yang mendefinisikan cara setiap "
"tipe collection dibuat dari iterator."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"In addition to the basic implementations of `FromIterator` for `Vec`, "
"`HashMap`, etc., there are also more specialized implementations which let "
"you do cool things like convert an `Iterator<Item = Result<V, E>>` into a "
"`Result<Vec<V>, E>`."
msgstr ""
"Selain implementasi dasar `FromIterator` untuk `Vec`, `HashMap`, dan "
"lainnya, ada implementasi yang lebih khusus untuk hal menarik seperti "
"mengonversi `Iterator<Item = Result<V, E>>` menjadi `Result<Vec<V>, E>`."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"The reason type annotations are often needed with `collect` is because it's "
"generic over its return type. This makes it harder for the compiler to infer"
" the correct type in many cases."
msgstr ""
"Anotasi tipe sering diperlukan pada `collect` karena tipe nilai kembaliannya"
" bersifat generic. Dalam banyak kasus, ini mempersulit compiler menyimpulkan"
" tipe yang tepat."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"The `Iterator` trait tells you how to _iterate_ once you have created an "
"iterator. The related trait [`IntoIterator`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.IntoIterator.html) defines how to create an iterator"
" for a type. It is used automatically by the `for` loop."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Iterator` menentukan cara _mengiterasi_ setelah iterator dibuat. "
"Trait terkait, [`IntoIterator`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.IntoIterator.html), mendefinisikan cara membuat "
"iterator bagi suatu tipe. Trait ini digunakan otomatis oleh loop `for`."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "\"point = {x}, {y}\""
msgstr "\"point = {x}, {y}\""

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "// dbg!(&grid.x_coords); // ❌ The grid was consumed by the loop.\n"
msgstr "// dbg!(&grid.x_coords); // ❌ The grid was consumed by the loop.\n"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"`IntoIterator` is the trait that makes for loops work. It is implemented by "
"collection types such as `Vec<T>` and references to them such as `&Vec<T>` "
"and `&[T]`. Ranges also implement it. This is why you can iterate over a "
"vector with `for i in some_vec { .. }` but `some_vec.next()` doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"`IntoIterator` merupakan trait yang memungkinkan for loop bekerja. Tipe "
"collection seperti `Vec<T>` dan reference-nya, seperti `&Vec<T>` dan `&[T]`,"
" mengimplementasikan trait ini. Rentang juga mengimplementasikannya. Karena "
"itu, Anda dapat mengiterasi vector menggunakan `for i in some_vec { .. }`, "
"meskipun `some_vec.next()` tidak tersedia."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"Click through to the docs for `IntoIterator`. Every implementation of "
"`IntoIterator` must declare two types:"
msgstr ""
"Buka dokumentasi `IntoIterator`. Setiap implementasi `IntoIterator` harus "
"mendeklarasikan dua tipe:"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "`Item`: the type to iterate over, such as `i8`,"
msgstr "`Item`: tipe yang diiterasi, misalnya `i8`,"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "`IntoIter`: the `Iterator` type returned by the `into_iter` method."
msgstr "`IntoIter`: tipe `Iterator` yang dikembalikan method `into_iter`."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"Note that `IntoIter` and `Item` are linked: the iterator must have the same "
"`Item` type, which means that it returns `Option<Item>`"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `IntoIter` dan `Item` saling terkait: iterator harus "
"memiliki tipe `Item` yang sama, sehingga mengembalikan `Option<Item>`"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "The example iterates over all combinations of x and y coordinates."
msgstr "Contoh ini mengiterasi semua kombinasi koordinat x dan y."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"Uncomment the commented line in `main` and show the compiler error. Note "
"that `IntoIterator::into_iter` takes ownership of `self`. The next slide "
"shows how we can avoid this by iterating over `&Grid` with an additional "
"`IntoIterator` implementation."
msgstr ""
"Hapus penanda komentar pada baris di `main` dan tampilkan error compiler. "
"Perhatikan bahwa `IntoIterator::into_iter` mengambil ownership atas `self`. "
"Slide berikutnya menunjukkan cara menghindarinya dengan mengiterasi `&Grid` "
"melalui implementasi `IntoIterator` tambahan."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"Implementing `IntoIterator` directly on a type means that creating the "
"iterator takes ownership of the object, so a common pattern is to implement "
"it on a reference to allow for the creation of borrowing iterators."
msgstr ""
"Mengimplementasikan `IntoIterator` langsung pada tipe berarti pembuatan "
"iterator mengambil ownership objek. Karena itu, pola yang umum adalah "
"mengimplementasikannya pada reference agar dapat membuat borrowing iterator."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "// The loop can borrow the grid without taking ownership.\n"
msgstr "// The loop can borrow the grid without taking ownership.\n"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "// The grid remains accessible after the loop.\n"
msgstr "// The grid remains accessible after the loop.\n"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"By implementing `IntoIterator` on `&Grid`, we can pass a reference into a "
"`for` loop and get a borrowing iterator. This allows us to borrow the grid "
"object in the loop without taking ownership of it."
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengimplementasikan `IntoIterator` pada `&Grid`, kita dapat "
"meneruskan reference ke loop `for` dan memperoleh borrowing iterator. Dengan"
" demikian, loop dapat meminjam objek grid tanpa mengambil ownership."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"[This playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=c3c29974bac8cc2065ca1b6608d5c8b9)"
" shows that we can have both `GridIter` and `GridRefIter` at the same time."
msgstr ""
"[Playground ini](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=c3c29974bac8cc2065ca1b6608d5c8b9)"
" menunjukkan bahwa kita dapat memiliki `GridIter` dan `GridRefIter` "
"sekaligus."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"This pattern is used heavily in the standard library for its collection "
"types, allowing for owning and borrowing iterators to be created implicitly "
"based on whether you pass the object in by value, by reference, or by "
"mutable reference."
msgstr ""
"Pola ini banyak digunakan pada tipe collection dalam standard library. "
"Owning iterator dan borrowing iterator dapat dibuat secara implisit sesuai "
"cara objek diteruskan: by value, by reference, atau melalui mutable "
"reference."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"Pull up the [`IntoIterator`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.IntoIterator.html) docs and show the implementations"
" for `[T; N]`, `&[T; N]`, and `&mut [T; N]`. Show that they produce "
"different iterators with different item types:"
msgstr ""
"Buka dokumentasi [`IntoIterator`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.IntoIterator.html) dan tunjukkan implementasi untuk "
"`[T; N]`, `&[T; N]`, dan `&mut [T; N]`. Tunjukkan bahwa ketiganya "
"menghasilkan iterator berbeda dengan tipe item berbeda:"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "The iterator for `[T; N]` produces `T` by value."
msgstr "Iterator untuk `[T; N]` menghasilkan `T` by value."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "The iterator for `&[T; N]` produces `&T`."
msgstr "Iterator untuk `&[T; N]` menghasilkan `&T`."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "The iterator for `&mut [T; N]` produces `&mut T`."
msgstr "Iterator untuk `&mut [T; N]` menghasilkan `&mut T`."

#: src/iterators/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will need to find and use some of the provided methods"
" in the [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html)"
" trait to implement a complex calculation."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda perlu menemukan dan menggunakan beberapa method pada"
" trait [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html) "
"untuk mengimplementasikan perhitungan kompleks."

#: src/iterators/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Copy the following code to <https://play.rust-lang.org/> and make the tests "
"pass. Use an iterator expression and `collect` the result to construct the "
"return value."
msgstr ""
"Salin kode berikut ke <https://play.rust-lang.org/> dan buat semua test "
"lulus. Gunakan ekspresi iterator, lalu kumpulkan hasilnya dengan `collect` "
"untuk membentuk nilai kembalian."

#: src/iterators/exercise.md src/iterators/solution.md
msgid ""
"/// Calculate the differences between elements of `values` offset by `offset`,\n"
"/// wrapping around from the end of `values` to the beginning.\n"
"///\n"
"/// Element `n` of the result is `values[(n+offset)%len] - values[n]`.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Calculate the differences between elements of `values` offset by `offset`,\n"
"/// wrapping around from the end of `values` to the beginning.\n"
"///\n"
"/// Element `n` of the result is `values[(n+offset)%len] - values[n]`.\n"

#: src/modules.md src/modules/paths.md
msgid "use, super, self"
msgstr "use, super, self"

#: src/modules/modules.md
msgid "We have seen how `impl` blocks let us namespace functions to a type."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah melihat cara block `impl` menempatkan fungsi dalam namespace "
"suatu tipe."

#: src/modules/modules.md
msgid "Similarly, `mod` lets us namespace types and functions:"
msgstr ""
"Demikian pula, `mod` memungkinkan penempatan tipe dan fungsi dalam "
"namespace:"

#: src/modules/modules.md
msgid "\"In the foo module\""
msgstr "\"In the foo module\""

#: src/modules/modules.md
msgid "\"In the bar module\""
msgstr "\"In the bar module\""

#: src/modules/modules.md
msgid ""
"Packages provide functionality and include a `Cargo.toml` file that "
"describes how to build a bundle of 1+ crates."
msgstr ""
"Package menyediakan fungsionalitas dan menyertakan berkas `Cargo.toml` yang "
"menjelaskan cara melakukan build satu atau beberapa crate."

#: src/modules/modules.md
msgid ""
"Crates are a tree of modules, where a binary crate creates an executable and"
" a library crate compiles to a library."
msgstr ""
"Crate merupakan tree yang tersusun dari module. Binary crate menghasilkan "
"executable, sedangkan library crate dikompilasi menjadi library."

#: src/modules/modules.md
msgid "Modules define organization, scope, and are the focus of this section."
msgstr ""
"Module menentukan pengorganisasian dan scope, serta menjadi fokus bagian "
"ini."

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"Omitting the module content will tell Rust to look for it in another file:"
msgstr ""
"Tidak menuliskan isi module akan meminta Rust mencarinya dalam berkas lain:"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"This tells Rust that the `garden` module content is found in a `garden.rs` "
"file in the same directory as the file that declared the module. If the "
"`garden` module similarly declares a `vegetables` submodule, then the "
"content of `garden::vegetables` would be found at `garden/vegetables.rs`."
msgstr ""
"Ini memberi tahu Rust bahwa isi module `garden` berada dalam berkas "
"`garden.rs` di direktori yang sama dengan berkas yang mendeklarasikan "
"module. Jika module `garden` juga mendeklarasikan submodule `vegetables`, "
"isi `garden::vegetables` berada di `garden/vegetables.rs`."

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "The `crate` root is in:"
msgstr "Root `crate` berada di:"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "`src/lib.rs` (for a library crate)"
msgstr "`src/lib.rs` untuk library crate"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "`src/main.rs` (for a binary crate)"
msgstr "`src/main.rs` untuk binary crate"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"This is the starting point from which the compiler identifies additional "
"modules."
msgstr "Inilah titik awal compiler mengidentifikasi module tambahan."

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"Modules defined in files can be documented, too, using \"inner doc "
"comments\". These document the item that contains them -- in this case, a "
"module."
msgstr ""
"Module yang didefinisikan dalam berkas juga dapat didokumentasikan "
"menggunakan “inner doc comment”. Komentar ini mendokumentasikan item yang "
"memuatnya, yaitu module dalam kasus ini."

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"//! This module implements the garden, including a highly performant germination\n"
"//! implementation.\n"
msgstr ""
"//! This module implements the garden, including a highly performant germination\n"
"//! implementation.\n"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "// Declare submodules.\n"
msgstr "// Declare submodules.\n"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "// Re-export types from this module.\n"
msgstr "// Re-export types from this module.\n"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "/// Sow the given seed packets.\n"
msgstr "/// Sow the given seed packets.\n"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "/// Harvest the produce in the garden that is ready.\n"
msgstr "/// Harvest the produce in the garden that is ready.\n"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"Before Rust 2018, modules needed to be located at `module/mod.rs` instead of"
" `module.rs`, and this is still a working alternative for editions after "
"2018."
msgstr ""
"Sebelum Rust 2018, module harus diletakkan di `module/mod.rs`, bukan "
"`module.rs`. Cara ini masih dapat digunakan sebagai alternatif pada edition "
"setelah 2018."

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"The main reason to introduce `filename.rs` as alternative to "
"`filename/mod.rs` was because many files named `mod.rs` can be hard to "
"distinguish in IDEs."
msgstr ""
"Alasan utama memperkenalkan `filename.rs` sebagai alternatif "
"`filename/mod.rs` adalah banyaknya berkas bernama `mod.rs` dapat menyulitkan"
" pembedaan dalam IDE."

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "Deeper nesting can use folders, even if the main module is a file:"
msgstr ""
"Module bersarang lebih dalam dapat menggunakan direktori, meskipun module "
"utamanya berupa berkas:"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"The place Rust will look for modules can be changed with a compiler "
"directive:"
msgstr "Lokasi Rust mencari module dapat diubah melalui directive compiler:"

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid "\"some/path.rs\""
msgstr "\"some/path.rs\""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md
msgid ""
"This is useful, for example, if you would like to place tests for a module "
"in a file named `some_module_test.rs`, similar to the convention in Go."
msgstr ""
"Ini berguna, misalnya, jika Anda ingin menempatkan test module dalam berkas "
"bernama `some_module_test.rs`, serupa dengan konvensi Go."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "Modules are a privacy boundary:"
msgstr "Module merupakan batas privacy:"

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "Module items are private by default (hides implementation details)."
msgstr ""
"Item module bersifat private secara default untuk menyembunyikan detail "
"implementasi."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "Parent and sibling items are always visible."
msgstr "Item induk dan saudara selalu terlihat."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid ""
"In other words, if an item is visible in module `foo`, it's visible in all "
"the descendants of `foo`."
msgstr ""
"Dengan kata lain, jika item terlihat dalam module `foo`, item itu juga "
"terlihat dalam semua turunan `foo`."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "\"outer::private\""
msgstr "\"outer::private\""

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "\"outer::public\""
msgstr "\"outer::public\""

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "\"outer::inner::private\""
msgstr "\"outer::inner::private\""

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "\"outer::inner::public\""
msgstr "\"outer::inner::public\""

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "Use the `pub` keyword to make modules public."
msgstr "Gunakan keyword `pub` untuk menjadikan module public."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid ""
"Additionally, there are advanced `pub(...)` specifiers to restrict the scope"
" of public visibility."
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, tersedia specifier lanjutan `pub(...)` untuk membatasi cakupan "
"visibility public."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid ""
"See the [Rust Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/visibility-and-"
"privacy.html#pubin-path-pubcrate-pubsuper-and-pubself)."
msgstr ""
"Lihat [Rust Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/visibility-and-"
"privacy.html#pubin-path-pubcrate-pubsuper-and-pubself)."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "Configuring `pub(crate)` visibility is a common pattern."
msgstr "Pengaturan visibility `pub(crate)` merupakan pola yang umum."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid "Less commonly, you can give visibility to a specific path."
msgstr ""
"Walaupun lebih jarang, Anda dapat memberikan visibility ke path tertentu."

#: src/modules/visibility.md
msgid ""
"In any case, visibility must be granted to an ancestor module (and all of "
"its descendants)."
msgstr ""
"Dalam semua kasus, visibility harus diberikan kepada module leluhur beserta "
"semua turunannya."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid "Visibility and Encapsulation"
msgstr "Visibility dan Encapsulation"

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"Like with items in a module, struct fields are also private by default. "
"Private fields are likewise visible within the rest of the module (including"
" child modules). This allows us to encapsulate implementation details of "
"struct, controlling what data and functionality is visible externally."
msgstr ""
"Seperti item dalam module, field struct juga bersifat private secara "
"default. Field private tetap terlihat di bagian lain module, termasuk module"
" anak. Dengan demikian, kita dapat melakukan encapsulation terhadap detail "
"implementasi struct dan mengatur data serta fungsionalitas yang terlihat "
"dari luar."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid "\"Is {} big? {}\""
msgstr "\"Is {} big? {}\""

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid "\"foo.val = {}\""
msgstr "\"foo.val = {}\""

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid "// let foo = Foo { val: 42, is_big: true };\n"
msgstr "// let foo = Foo { val: 42, is_big: true };\n"

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid "// println!(\"Is {} big? {}\", foo.val, foo.is_big);\n"
msgstr "// println!(\"Is {} big? {}\", foo.val, foo.is_big);\n"

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"This slide demonstrates how privacy in structs is module-based. Students "
"coming from object-oriented languages may be used to types being the "
"encapsulation boundary, so this demonstrates how Rust behaves differently "
"while showing how we can still achieve encapsulation."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini menunjukkan bahwa privacy struct berbasis module. Peserta yang "
"terbiasa dengan bahasa object-oriented mungkin menganggap tipe sebagai batas"
" encapsulation. Contoh ini menunjukkan perbedaan perilaku Rust sekaligus "
"cara tetap mencapai encapsulation."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"Note how the `is_big` field is fully controlled by `Foo`, allowing `Foo` to "
"control how it's initialized and enforce any invariants it needs to (e.g. "
"that `is_big` is only `true` if `val > 100`)."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa field `is_big` sepenuhnya dikendalikan `Foo`, sehingga "
"`Foo` dapat mengatur inisialisasi dan menegakkan invariant yang diperlukan. "
"Misalnya, `is_big` hanya bernilai `true` jika `val > 100`."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"Point out how helper functions can be defined in the same module (including "
"child modules) in order to get access to the type's private fields/methods."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bahwa fungsi bantu dapat didefinisikan dalam module yang sama, "
"termasuk module anak, untuk mengakses field/method private suatu tipe."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"The first commented out line demonstrates that you cannot initialize a "
"struct with private fields. The second one demonstrates that you also can't "
"directly access private fields."
msgstr ""
"Baris komentar pertama menunjukkan bahwa Anda tidak dapat menginisialisasi "
"struct dengan field private. Baris kedua menunjukkan bahwa field private "
"juga tidak dapat diakses langsung."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"Enums do not support privacy: Variants and data within those variants is "
"always public."
msgstr ""
"Enum tidak mendukung privacy: variant dan data di dalamnya selalu public."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"If students want more information about privacy (or lack thereof) in enums, "
"you can bring up `#[doc_hidden]` and `#[non_exhaustive]` and show how "
"they're used to limit what can be done with an enum."
msgstr ""
"Jika peserta ingin mengetahui lebih lanjut tentang privacy atau ketiadaannya"
" pada enum, tunjukkan `#[doc_hidden]` dan `#[non_exhaustive]`, serta cara "
"keduanya membatasi penggunaan enum."

#: src/modules/encapsulation.md
msgid ""
"Module privacy still applies when there are `impl` blocks in other modules "
"[(example in the playground)](https://play.rust-"
