#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "In case of a fatal runtime error, Rust triggers a \"panic\":"
msgstr "Jika terjadi error runtime yang fatal, Rust memicu “panic”:"

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "Panics are for unrecoverable and unexpected errors."
msgstr ""
"Panic ditujukan untuk error yang tidak dapat dipulihkan dan tidak "
"diharapkan."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "Panics are symptoms of bugs in the program."
msgstr "Panic merupakan gejala adanya bug dalam program."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "Runtime failures like failed bounds checks can panic."
msgstr ""
"Kegagalan runtime, seperti pemeriksaan batas yang gagal, dapat memicu panic."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "Assertions (such as `assert!`) panic on failure."
msgstr "Assertion, seperti `assert!`, memicu panic jika gagal."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "Purpose-specific panics can use the `panic!` macro."
msgstr "Panic untuk tujuan tertentu dapat menggunakan macro `panic!`."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid ""
"A panic will \"unwind\" the stack, dropping values just as if the functions "
"had returned."
msgstr ""
"Panic melakukan “unwind” pada stack, melakukan drop nilai seolah-olah fungsi"
" telah selesai."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid ""
"Use non-panicking APIs (such as `Vec::get`) if crashing is not acceptable."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan API yang tidak memicu panic, seperti `Vec::get`, jika crash tidak "
"dapat diterima."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid ""
"By default, a panic will cause the stack to unwind. The unwinding can be "
"caught:"
msgstr ""
"Secara default, panic menyebabkan stack di-unwind. Proses unwinding ini "
"dapat ditangkap:"

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "\"No problem here!\""
msgstr "\"No problem here!\""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "\"oh no!\""
msgstr "\"oh no!\""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid ""
"Catching is unusual; do not attempt to implement exceptions with "
"`catch_unwind`!"
msgstr ""
"Menangkap panic jarang dilakukan; jangan mencoba mengimplementasikan "
"exception menggunakan `catch_unwind`!"

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid ""
"This can be useful in servers which should keep running even if a single "
"request crashes."
msgstr ""
"Ini dapat berguna pada server yang sebaiknya tetap berjalan meskipun satu "
"request mengalami crash."

#: src/error-handling/panics.md
msgid "This does not work if `panic = 'abort'` is set in your `Cargo.toml`."
msgstr ""
"Cara ini tidak bekerja jika `panic = 'abort'` diatur dalam `Cargo.toml`."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"Our primary mechanism for error handling in Rust is the "
"[`Result`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/result/enum.Result.html) "
"enum, which we briefly saw when discussing standard library types."
msgstr ""
"Mekanisme utama error handling dalam Rust adalah enum "
"[`Result`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/result/enum.Result.html), "
"yang sempat kita lihat saat membahas tipe standard library."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"`Result` has two variants: `Ok` which contains the success value, and `Err` "
"which contains an error value of some kind."
msgstr ""
"`Result` memiliki dua variant: `Ok`, yang memuat nilai keberhasilan, dan "
"`Err`, yang memuat suatu nilai error."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"Whether or not a function can produce an error is encoded in the function's "
"type signature by having the function return a `Result` value."
msgstr ""
"Kemungkinan fungsi menghasilkan error dinyatakan dalam signature tipenya "
"dengan mengembalikan nilai `Result`."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"Like with `Option`, there is no way to forget to handle an error: You cannot"
" access either the success value or the error value without first pattern "
"matching on the `Result` to check which variant you have. Methods like "
"`unwrap` make it easier to write quick-and-dirty code that doesn't do robust"
" error handling, but means that you can always see in your source code where"
" proper error handling is being skipped."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada `Option`, penanganan error tidak dapat terlupakan begitu saja: "
"nilai keberhasilan maupun error tidak dapat diakses sebelum melakukan "
"pattern matching pada `Result` untuk memeriksa variant-nya. Method seperti "
"`unwrap` memudahkan penulisan kode cepat dan sederhana yang belum menangani "
"error secara andal, tetapi Anda selalu dapat melihat tempat penanganan error"
" yang semestinya dilewati dalam source code."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"It may be helpful to compare error handling in Rust to error handling "
"conventions that students may be familiar with from other programming "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Membandingkan error handling Rust dengan konvensi pada bahasa lain yang "
"sudah dikenal peserta dapat membantu."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid "Many languages use exceptions, e.g. C++, Java, Python."
msgstr "Banyak bahasa menggunakan exception, misalnya C++, Java, dan Python."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"In most languages with exceptions, whether or not a function can throw an "
"exception is not visible as part of its type signature. This generally means"
" that you can't tell when calling a function if it may throw an exception or"
" not."
msgstr ""
"Pada sebagian besar bahasa dengan exception, kemungkinan fungsi melempar "
"exception tidak terlihat dalam signature tipenya. Karena itu, saat memanggil"
" fungsi, umumnya Anda tidak dapat mengetahui apakah fungsi mungkin melempar "
"exception."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"Exceptions generally unwind the call stack, propagating upward until a `try`"
" block is reached. An error originating deep in the call stack may impact an"
" unrelated function further up."
msgstr ""
"Exception umumnya melakukan unwind pada call stack dan merambat ke atas "
"hingga mencapai block `try`. Error dari bagian dalam call stack dapat "
"memengaruhi fungsi yang tidak berkaitan di tingkat atas."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid "Error Numbers"
msgstr "Nomor Error"

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"Some languages have functions return an error number (or some other error "
"value) separately from the successful return value of the function. Examples"
" include C and Go."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian bahasa memiliki fungsi yang mengembalikan nomor error atau nilai "
"error lain secara terpisah dari nilai keberhasilan. Contohnya C dan Go."

#: src/error-handling/result.md
msgid ""
"Depending on the language it may be possible to forget to check the error "
"value, in which case you may be accessing an uninitialized or otherwise "
"invalid success value."
msgstr ""
"Bergantung pada bahasanya, Anda mungkin dapat lupa memeriksa nilai error, "
"sehingga mengakses nilai keberhasilan yang belum diinisialisasi atau tidak "
"valid."

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid ""
"Runtime errors like connection-refused or file-not-found are handled with "
"the `Result` type, but matching this type on every call can be cumbersome. "
"The try-operator `?` is used to return errors to the caller. It lets you "
"turn the common"
msgstr ""
"Error runtime seperti connection-refused atau file-not-found ditangani "
"dengan tipe `Result`, tetapi melakukan pencocokan pada setiap pemanggilan "
"dapat merepotkan. Operator try `?` digunakan untuk mengembalikan error "
"kepada caller. Operator ini mengubah bentuk yang umum"

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid "into the much simpler"
msgstr "menjadi bentuk yang jauh lebih sederhana"

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid "We can use this to simplify our error handling code:"
msgstr "Kita dapat menggunakannya untuk menyederhanakan kode error handling:"

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid "//fs::write(\"config.dat\", \"alice\").unwrap();\n"
msgstr "//fs::write(\"config.dat\", \"alice\").unwrap();\n"

#: src/error-handling/try.md src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "\"config.dat\""
msgstr "\"config.dat\""

#: src/error-handling/try.md src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid "\"username or error: {username:?}\""
msgstr "\"username or error: {username:?}\""

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid "Simplify the `read_username` function to use `?`."
msgstr "Sederhanakan fungsi `read_username` agar menggunakan `?`."

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid "The `username` variable can be either `Ok(string)` or `Err(error)`."
msgstr "Variabel `username` dapat berupa `Ok(string)` atau `Err(error)`."

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid ""
"Use the `fs::write` call to test out the different scenarios: no file, empty"
" file, file with username."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan pemanggilan `fs::write` untuk mencoba berbagai skenario: berkas "
"tidak ada, berkas kosong, dan berkas berisi username."

#: src/error-handling/try.md
msgid ""
"Note that `main` can return a `Result<(), E>` as long as it implements "
"`std::process::Termination`. In practice, this means that `E` implements "
"`Debug`. The executable will print the `Err` variant and return a nonzero "
"exit status on error."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `main` dapat mengembalikan `Result<(), E>` selama tipe ini "
"mengimplementasikan `std::process::Termination`. Dalam praktiknya, `E` harus"
" mengimplementasikan `Debug`. Ketika error terjadi, executable mencetak "
"variant `Err` dan mengembalikan exit status bukan nol."

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid ""
"The effective expansion of `?` is a little more complicated than previously "
"indicated:"
msgstr ""
"Ekspansi `?` sebenarnya sedikit lebih rumit daripada penjelasan sebelumnya:"

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid "works the same as"
msgstr "bekerja sama seperti"

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid ""
"The `From::from` call here means we attempt to convert the error type to the"
" type returned by the function. This makes it easy to encapsulate errors "
"into higher-level errors."
msgstr ""
"Pemanggilan `From::from` di sini mencoba mengonversi tipe error menjadi tipe"
" yang dikembalikan fungsi. Ini mempermudah pembungkusan error menjadi error "
"tingkat lebih tinggi."

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid "//std::fs::write(\"config.dat\", \"\").unwrap();\n"
msgstr "//std::fs::write(\"config.dat\", \"\").unwrap();\n"

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid ""
"The `?` operator must return a value compatible with the return type of the "
"function. For `Result`, it means that the error types have to be compatible."
" A function that returns `Result<T, ErrorOuter>` can only use `?` on a value"
" of type `Result<U, ErrorInner>` if `ErrorOuter` and `ErrorInner` are the "
"same type or if `ErrorOuter` implements `From<ErrorInner>`."
msgstr ""
"Operator `?` harus mengembalikan nilai yang kompatibel dengan tipe nilai "
"kembalian fungsi. Untuk `Result`, tipe error harus kompatibel. Fungsi yang "
"mengembalikan `Result<T, ErrorOuter>` hanya dapat menggunakan `?` pada nilai"
" bertipe `Result<U, ErrorInner>` jika `ErrorOuter` dan `ErrorInner` "
"merupakan tipe yang sama atau jika `ErrorOuter` mengimplementasikan "
"`From<ErrorInner>`."

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid ""
"A common alternative to a `From` implementation is `Result::map_err`, "
"especially when the conversion only happens in one place."
msgstr ""
"Alternatif umum untuk implementasi `From` adalah `Result::map_err`, terutama"
" ketika konversi hanya dilakukan pada satu tempat."

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid ""
"There is no compatibility requirement for `Option`. A function returning "
"`Option<T>` can use the `?` operator on `Option<U>` for arbitrary `T` and "
"`U` types."
msgstr ""
"Tidak ada persyaratan kompatibilitas untuk `Option`. Fungsi yang "
"mengembalikan `Option<T>` dapat menggunakan operator `?` pada `Option<U>` "
"untuk tipe `T` dan `U` apa pun."

#: src/error-handling/try-conversions.md
msgid ""
"A function that returns `Result` cannot use `?` on `Option` and vice versa. "
"However, `Option::ok_or` converts `Option` to `Result` whereas `Result::ok` "
"turns `Result` into `Option`."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi yang mengembalikan `Result` tidak dapat menggunakan `?` pada "
"`Option`, dan sebaliknya. Namun, `Option::ok_or` mengonversi `Option` "
"menjadi `Result`, sedangkan `Result::ok` mengubah `Result` menjadi `Option`."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"When defining a custom error type, there are some common conventions to "
"follow in order to be compatible with the broader ecosystem:"
msgstr ""
"Saat mendefinisikan tipe error khusus, ikuti beberapa konvensi umum agar "
"kompatibel dengan ekosistem yang lebih luas:"

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"Implement the standard library's [`Error`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/error/trait.Error.html) trait."
msgstr ""
"Implementasikan trait [`Error`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/error/trait.Error.html) dari standard library."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid "Derive `Debug` and implement `Display` (required by `Error`)."
msgstr ""
"Lakukan derive `Debug` dan implementasikan `Display`, yang diwajibkan oleh "
"`Error`."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"Implement `From` conversions for underlying error types to support automatic"
" error type conversion with `?`."
msgstr ""
"Implementasikan konversi `From` untuk tipe error yang mendasari agar "
"mendukung konversi tipe error otomatis melalui `?`."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid "\"I/O error: {e}\""
msgstr "\"I/O error: {e}\""

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid "\"Username file was empty\""
msgstr "\"Username file was empty\""

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"Any type can be used as the error type for `Result`: There are no trait "
"requirements, structs and enums are both valid, and we can even use "
"empty/zero-sized types like `()` when the error doesn't need to cary any "
"data."
msgstr ""
"Tipe apa pun dapat digunakan sebagai tipe error untuk `Result`: tidak ada "
"persyaratan trait, struct maupun enum sama-sama valid, dan tipe kosong/zero-"
"sized seperti `()` pun dapat digunakan ketika error tidak perlu memuat data."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"While there aren't any strict requirements for error types, there are a "
"couple of conventions to follow for ecosystem compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Walaupun tidak ada persyaratan ketat untuk tipe error, beberapa konvensi "
"perlu diikuti agar kompatibel dengan ekosistem."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"We've already seen how the `From` trait can be used to support automatic "
"error type conversion with the `?` operator."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah melihat penggunaan trait `From` untuk mendukung konversi tipe "
"error otomatis melalui operator `?`."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"The standard library provides the `Error` marker trait for indicating that a"
" type represents an error."
msgstr ""
"Standard library menyediakan marker trait `Error` untuk menandakan bahwa "
"suatu tipe merepresentasikan error."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"`Error` depends on `Debug` (which can be derived) and `Display` (which must "
"be implemented manually). These ensure that an error can always be turned "
"into a string for the purpose of logging or displaying the error to a user."
msgstr ""
"`Error` bergantung pada `Debug`, yang dapat di-derive, dan `Display`, yang "
"harus diimplementasikan manual. Keduanya memastikan error selalu dapat "
"diubah menjadi string untuk logging atau ditampilkan kepada pengguna."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"The `Error` trait doesn't provide any functionality of its own, but in a "
"couple of slides we will look at how `Error` can be used to create dynamic "
"error types."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Error` tidak menyediakan fungsionalitas sendiri, tetapi beberapa "
"slide lagi kita melihat cara menggunakan `Error` untuk membuat tipe error "
"dinamis."

#: src/error-handling/compatibility.md
msgid ""
"These trait implementations represent a bit of boilerplate that needs to be "
"written for each custom error type. On the next slide we'll look at a crate "
"in the ecosystem that can be used to cut down on this boilerplate."
msgstr ""
"Implementasi trait ini merupakan boilerplate yang perlu ditulis untuk setiap"
" tipe error khusus. Pada slide berikutnya, kita melihat crate yang dapat "
"mengurangi boilerplate tersebut."

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md
msgid ""
"The [`thiserror`](https://docs.rs/thiserror/) crate provides macros to help "
"avoid boilerplate when defining error types. It provides derive macros that "
"assist in implementing `From<T>`, `Display`, and the `Error` trait."
msgstr ""
"Crate [`thiserror`](https://docs.rs/thiserror/) menyediakan macro untuk "
"menghindari boilerplate saat mendefinisikan tipe error. Derive macro-nya "
"membantu mengimplementasikan `From<T>`, `Display`, dan trait `Error`."

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md
msgid "\"I/O error: {0}\""
msgstr "\"I/O error: {0}\""

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "\"Found no username in {0}\""
msgstr "\"Found no username in {0}\""

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "//fs::write(\"config.dat\", \"\").unwrap();\n"
msgstr "//fs::write(\"config.dat\", \"\").unwrap();\n"

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "\"Username: {username}\""
msgstr "\"Username: {username}\""

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md src/error-handling/error.md
#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "\"Error: {err}\""
msgstr "\"Error: {err}\""

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md
msgid ""
"The `Error` derive macro is provided by `thiserror`, and has lots of useful "
"attributes to help define error types in a compact way."
msgstr ""
"Derive macro `Error` disediakan oleh `thiserror` dan memiliki banyak atribut"
" berguna untuk mendefinisikan tipe error secara ringkas."

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md
msgid "The message from `#[error]` is used to derive the `Display` trait."
msgstr ""
"Pesan dari `#[error]` digunakan untuk menghasilkan implementasi trait "
"`Display` melalui derive."

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md
msgid ""
"Note that the (`thiserror::`)`Error` derive macro, while it has the effect "
"of implementing the (`std::error::`)`Error` trait, is not the same this; "
"traits and macros do not share a namespace."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa derive macro (`thiserror::`)`Error` berbeda dari trait "
"(`std::error::`)`Error`, meskipun macro itu mengimplementasikan trait "
"tersebut; trait dan macro tidak menggunakan namespace yang sama."

#: src/error-handling/thiserror.md
msgid ""
"`thiserror` also supports deriving `Error` on structs for error types that "
"only need to represent a single error case."
msgstr ""
"`thiserror` juga mendukung deriving `Error` pada struct untuk tipe error "
"yang hanya perlu merepresentasikan satu kasus."

#: src/error-handling/error.md
msgid ""
"Sometimes we want to allow any type of error to be returned without writing "
"our own enum covering all the different possibilities. The "
"`std::error::Error` trait makes it easy to create a trait object that can "
"contain any error."
msgstr ""
"Terkadang kita ingin mengizinkan tipe error apa pun dikembalikan tanpa "
"menulis enum sendiri yang mencakup semua kemungkinan. Trait "
"`std::error::Error` mempermudah pembuatan trait object yang dapat memuat "
"error apa pun."

#: src/error-handling/error.md
msgid "\"count.dat\""
msgstr "\"count.dat\""

#: src/error-handling/error.md
msgid "\"1i3\""
msgstr "\"1i3\""

#: src/error-handling/error.md
msgid "\"Count: {count}\""
msgstr "\"Count: {count}\""

#: src/error-handling/error.md
msgid ""
"The `read_count` function can return `std::io::Error` (from file operations)"
" or `std::num::ParseIntError` (from `String::parse`)."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `read_count` dapat mengembalikan `std::io::Error` dari operasi berkas"
" atau `std::num::ParseIntError` dari `String::parse`."

#: src/error-handling/error.md
msgid ""
"Boxing errors saves on code, but gives up the ability to cleanly handle "
"different error cases differently in the program. As such it's generally not"
" a good idea to use `Box<dyn Error>` in the public API of a library, but it "
"can be a good option in a program where you just want to display the error "
"message somewhere."
msgstr ""
"Membungkus error dalam box mengurangi kode, tetapi mengorbankan kemudahan "
"menangani kasus error berbeda secara terpisah. Karena itu, `Box<dyn Error>` "
"umumnya bukan pilihan yang baik untuk API publik library, tetapi dapat cocok"
" bagi program yang hanya ingin menampilkan pesan error."

#: src/error-handling/error.md
msgid ""
"Make sure to implement the `std::error::Error` trait when defining a custom "
"error type so it can be boxed."
msgstr ""
"Pastikan tipe error khusus mengimplementasikan trait `std::error::Error` "
"agar dapat dibungkus dalam box."

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid ""
"The [`anyhow`](https://docs.rs/anyhow/) crate provides a rich error type "
"with support for carrying additional contextual information, which can be "
"used to provide a semantic trace of what the program was doing leading up to"
" the error."
msgstr ""
"Crate [`anyhow`](https://docs.rs/anyhow/) menyediakan tipe error kaya fitur "
"yang dapat membawa konteks tambahan. Konteks ini membantu menelusuri secara "
"semantik apa yang dilakukan program menjelang terjadinya error."

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid ""
"This can be combined with the convenience macros from "
"[`thiserror`](https://docs.rs/thiserror/) to avoid writing out trait impls "
"explicitly for custom error types."
msgstr ""
"Cara ini dapat digabungkan dengan macro praktis dari "
"[`thiserror`](https://docs.rs/thiserror/) agar tidak perlu menulis "
"implementasi trait secara eksplisit untuk tipe error khusus."

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "\"Failed to open {path}\""
msgstr "\"Failed to open {path}\""

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "\"Failed to read\""
msgstr "\"Failed to read\""

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid ""
"`anyhow::Error` is essentially a wrapper around `Box<dyn Error>`. As such "
"it's again generally not a good choice for the public API of a library, but "
"is widely used in applications."
msgstr ""
"`anyhow::Error` pada dasarnya membungkus `Box<dyn Error>`. Karena itu, tipe "
"ini umumnya juga kurang tepat untuk API publik library, tetapi banyak "
"digunakan dalam aplikasi."

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid "`anyhow::Result<V>` is a type alias for `Result<V, anyhow::Error>`."
msgstr ""
"`anyhow::Result<V>` merupakan type alias untuk `Result<V, anyhow::Error>`."

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid ""
"Functionality provided by `anyhow::Error` may be familiar to Go developers, "
"as it provides similar behavior to the Go `error` type and `Result<T, "
"anyhow::Error>` is much like a Go `(T, error)` (with the convention that "
"only one element of the pair is meaningful)."
msgstr ""
"Fungsionalitas `anyhow::Error` mungkin familier bagi developer Go karena "
"perilakunya serupa dengan tipe `error` Go. `Result<T, anyhow::Error>` sangat"
" mirip dengan `(T, error)` dalam Go, dengan konvensi bahwa hanya satu elemen"
" pasangan yang bermakna."

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid ""
"`anyhow::Context` is a trait implemented for the standard `Result` and "
"`Option` types. `use anyhow::Context` is necessary to enable `.context()` "
"and `.with_context()` on those types."
msgstr ""
"`anyhow::Context` merupakan trait yang diimplementasikan untuk tipe standar "
"`Result` dan `Option`. `use anyhow::Context` diperlukan untuk mengaktifkan "
"`.context()` dan `.with_context()` pada kedua tipe tersebut."

#: src/error-handling/anyhow.md
msgid ""
"`anyhow::Error` has support for downcasting, much like `std::any::Any`; the "
"specific error type stored inside can be extracted for examination if "
"desired with "
"[`Error::downcast`](https://docs.rs/anyhow/latest/anyhow/struct.Error.html#method.downcast)."
msgstr ""
"`anyhow::Error` mendukung downcasting, serupa dengan `std::any::Any`. Tipe "
"error spesifik di dalamnya dapat diambil untuk diperiksa menggunakan "
"[`Error::downcast`](https://docs.rs/anyhow/latest/anyhow/struct.Error.html#method.downcast)."

#: src/error-handling/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise we're revisiting the expression evaluator exercise that we "
"did in day 2. Our initial solution ignores a possible error case: Dividing "
"by zero! Rewrite `eval` to instead use idiomatic error handling to handle "
"this error case and return an error when it occurs. We provide a simple "
"`DivideByZeroError` type to use as the error type for `eval`."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, kita kembali ke evaluator ekspresi pada hari 2. Solusi "
"awal mengabaikan satu kemungkinan error: pembagian dengan nol! Tulis ulang "
"`eval` menggunakan error handling idiomatis agar mengembalikan error ketika "
"kasus ini terjadi. Kami menyediakan tipe sederhana `DivideByZeroError` "
"sebagai tipe error untuk `eval`."

#: src/error-handling/exercise.md
msgid ""
"// The original implementation of the expression evaluator. Update this to\n"
"// return a `Result` and produce an error when dividing by 0.\n"
msgstr ""
"// The original implementation of the expression evaluator. Update this to\n"
"// return a `Result` and produce an error when dividing by 0.\n"

#: src/error-handling/exercise.md
msgid "\"Cannot divide by zero!\""
msgstr "\"Cannot divide by zero!\""

#: src/error-handling/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The starting code here isn't exactly the same as the previous exercise's "
"solution: We've added in an explicit panic to show students where the error "
"case is. Point this out if students get confused."
msgstr ""
"Kode awal di sini tidak persis sama dengan solusi latihan sebelumnya: kami "
"menambahkan panic eksplisit untuk menunjukkan letak kasus error. Jelaskan "
"hal ini jika peserta bingung."

#: src/error-handling/solution.md
msgid ""
"**`Result` Return Type:** The function signature changes to return "
"`Result<i64, DivideByZeroError>`. This explicit type signature forces the "
"caller to handle the possibility of failure."
msgstr ""
"**Tipe Nilai Kembalian `Result`:** Signature fungsi diubah agar "
"mengembalikan `Result<i64, DivideByZeroError>`. Signature eksplisit ini "
"mengharuskan caller menangani kemungkinan kegagalan."

#: src/error-handling/solution.md
msgid ""
"**The `?` Operator:** We use `?` on the recursive calls: `eval(*left)?`. "
"This cleanly propagates errors. If `eval` returns `Err`, the function "
"immediately returns that `Err`. If it returns `Ok(v)`, `v` is assigned to "
"`left` (or `right`)."
msgstr ""
"**Operator `?`:** Kita menggunakan `?` pada pemanggilan rekursif: "
"`eval(*left)?`. Ini meneruskan error dengan rapi. Jika `eval` mengembalikan "
"`Err`, fungsi langsung mengembalikan `Err` tersebut. Jika menghasilkan "
"`Ok(v)`, `v` di-assign ke `left` atau `right`."

#: src/error-handling/solution.md
msgid "**`Ok` Wrapping:** Successful results must be wrapped in `Ok(...)`."
msgstr ""
"**Pembungkusan `Ok`:** Hasil yang berhasil harus dibungkus dalam `Ok(...)`."

#: src/error-handling/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Handling Division by Zero:** We explicitly check for `right == 0` and "
"return `Err(DivideByZeroError)`. This replaces the panic in the original "
"code."
msgstr ""
"**Menangani Pembagian dengan Nol:** Kita secara eksplisit memeriksa `right "
"== 0` dan mengembalikan `Err(DivideByZeroError)`. Ini menggantikan panic "
"pada kode asli."

#: src/error-handling/solution.md
msgid ""
"Mention that `DivideByZeroError` is a unit struct (no fields), which is "
"sufficient here since there's no extra context to provide about the error."
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa `DivideByZeroError` merupakan unit struct tanpa field, yang "
"sudah memadai karena tidak ada konteks tambahan tentang error yang perlu "
"disediakan."

#: src/error-handling/solution.md
msgid ""
"Discuss how `?` makes error handling almost as concise as exceptions, but "
"with explicit control flow."
msgstr ""
"Bahas bagaimana `?` membuat error handling hampir seringkas exception, "
"tetapi dengan control flow yang eksplisit."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "The Rust language has two parts:"
msgstr "Bahasa Rust memiliki dua bagian:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "**Safe Rust:** memory safe, no undefined behavior possible."
msgstr ""
"**Safe Rust:** aman dari sisi memori, tidak memungkinkan undefined behavior."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid ""
"**Unsafe Rust:** can trigger undefined behavior if preconditions are "
"violated."
msgstr ""
"**Unsafe Rust:** dapat memicu undefined behavior jika prasyarat dilanggar."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid ""
"We saw mostly safe Rust in this course, but it's important to know what "
"Unsafe Rust is."
msgstr ""
"Dalam kursus ini, kita lebih banyak membahas safe Rust, tetapi penting juga "
"untuk mengetahui apa itu Unsafe Rust."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid ""
"Unsafe code should be small and isolated, and its correctness should be "
"carefully documented. It should be wrapped in a safe abstraction layer."
msgstr ""
"Kode unsafe sebaiknya berukuran kecil dan terisolasi, dan kebenarannya "
"sebaiknya didokumentasikan dengan cermat. Kode tersebut sebaiknya dibungkus "
"dalam lapisan safe abstraction."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "Unsafe Rust gives you access to five new capabilities:"
msgstr "Unsafe Rust memberi akses ke lima kemampuan baru:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "Dereference raw pointers."
msgstr "Melakukan dereference raw pointer."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "Access or modify mutable static variables."
msgstr "Mengakses atau mengubah variabel static mutable."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "Access `union` fields."
msgstr "Mengakses field `union`."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "Call `unsafe` functions, including `extern` functions."
msgstr "Memanggil fungsi `unsafe`, termasuk fungsi `extern`."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid "Implement `unsafe` traits."
msgstr "Mengimplementasikan trait `unsafe`."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid ""
"We will briefly cover unsafe capabilities next. For full details, please see"
" [Chapter 19.1 in the Rust Book](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/book/ch19-01-unsafe-rust.html) and the "
"[Rustonomicon](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/)."
msgstr ""
"Berikutnya, kita membahas kemampuan unsafe secara singkat. Untuk penjelasan "
"lengkap, lihat [Bab 19.1 dalam Rust Book](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/book/ch19-01-unsafe-rust.html) dan [Rustonomicon](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/nomicon/)."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe.md
msgid ""
"Unsafe Rust does not mean the code is incorrect. It means that developers "
"have turned off some compiler safety features and have to write correct code"
" by themselves. It means the compiler no longer enforces Rust's memory-"
"safety rules."
msgstr ""
"Unsafe Rust tidak berarti kodenya salah. Artinya, developer menonaktifkan "
"sebagian fitur keamanan compiler dan harus memastikan sendiri kebenaran "
"kode. Ini berarti compiler tidak lagi menegakkan aturan memory safety Rust."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid "Creating pointers is safe, but dereferencing them requires `unsafe`:"
msgstr ""
"Membuat pointer aman, tetapi melakukan dereference memerlukan `unsafe`:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: p1 and p2 were created by taking raw pointers to a local, so they\n"
"    // are guaranteed to be non-null, aligned, and point into a single (stack-)\n"
"    // allocated object.\n"
"    //\n"
"    // The object underlying the raw pointers lives for the entire function, so\n"
"    // it is not deallocated while the raw pointers still exist. It is not\n"
"    // accessed through references while the raw pointers exist, nor is it\n"
"    // accessed from other threads concurrently.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: p1 and p2 were created by taking raw pointers to a local, so they\n"
"    // are guaranteed to be non-null, aligned, and point into a single (stack-)\n"
"    // allocated object.\n"
"    //\n"
"    // The object underlying the raw pointers lives for the entire function, so\n"
"    // it is not deallocated while the raw pointers still exist. It is not\n"
"    // accessed through references while the raw pointers exist, nor is it\n"
"    // accessed from other threads concurrently.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid "// Mutation may soundly be observed through a raw pointer, like in C.\n"
msgstr "// Mutation may soundly be observed through a raw pointer, like in C.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid ""
"// UNSOUND. DO NOT DO THIS.\n"
"    /*\n"
"    let r: &i32 = unsafe { &*p1 };\n"
"    dbg!(r);\n"
"    x = 50;\n"
"    dbg!(r); // Object underlying the reference has been mutated. This is UB.\n"
"    */"
msgstr ""
"// UNSOUND. DO NOT DO THIS.\n"
"    /*\n"
"    let r: &i32 = unsafe { &*p1 };\n"
"    dbg!(r);\n"
"    x = 50;\n"
"    dbg!(r); // Object underlying the reference has been mutated. This is UB.\n"
"    */"

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid ""
"It is good practice (and required by the Android Rust style guide) to write "
"a comment for each `unsafe` block explaining how the code inside it "
"satisfies the safety requirements of the unsafe operations it is doing."
msgstr ""
"Menulis komentar untuk setiap block `unsafe` merupakan praktik yang baik dan"
" diwajibkan style guide Rust Android. Komentar tersebut menjelaskan "
"bagaimana kode di dalamnya memenuhi persyaratan keamanan operasi unsafe yang"
" dilakukan."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid ""
"In the case of pointer dereferences, this means that the pointers must be "
"[_valid_](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ptr/index.html#safety), i.e.:"
msgstr ""
"Untuk dereference pointer, pointer harus [_valid_](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/ptr/index.html#safety), yaitu:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid "The pointer must be non-null."
msgstr "Pointer harus non-null."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid ""
"The pointer must be _dereferenceable_ (within the bounds of a single "
"allocated object)."
msgstr ""
"Pointer harus _dereferenceable_, yaitu berada dalam batas satu objek yang "
"dialokasikan."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid "The object must not have been deallocated."
msgstr "Objek tidak boleh sudah didealokasi."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid "There must not be concurrent accesses to the same location."
msgstr "Tidak boleh ada akses concurrent ke lokasi yang sama."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid ""
"If the pointer was obtained by casting a reference, the underlying object "
"must be live and no reference may be used to access the memory."
msgstr ""
"Jika pointer diperoleh melalui casting reference, objek yang mendasarinya "
"harus masih berlaku dan tidak boleh ada reference yang digunakan untuk "
"mengakses memori tersebut."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid "In most cases the pointer must also be properly aligned."
msgstr ""
"Dalam sebagian besar kasus, pointer juga harus memiliki alignment yang "
"tepat."

#: src/unsafe-rust/dereferencing.md
msgid ""
"The \"UNSOUND\" section gives an example of a common kind of UB bug: naïvely"
" taking a reference to the dereference of a raw pointer sidesteps the "
"compiler's knowledge of what object the reference is actually pointing to. "
"As such, the borrow checker does not freeze `x` and so we are able to modify"
" it despite the existence of a reference to it. Creating a reference from a "
"pointer requires _great care_."
msgstr ""
"Bagian “UNSOUND” memberikan contoh jenis bug UB yang umum: secara naif "
"membuat reference dari hasil dereference raw pointer melewati pengetahuan "
"compiler tentang objek yang sebenarnya dirujuk. Akibatnya, borrow checker "
"tidak membekukan `x`, sehingga kita dapat mengubahnya meskipun reference ke "
"nilai itu masih ada. Membuat reference dari pointer memerlukan _kehati-"
"hatian tinggi_."

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid "It is safe to read an immutable static variable:"
msgstr "Membaca variabel static immutable aman:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid "\"Hello, world!\""
msgstr "\"Hello, world!\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid "\"HELLO_WORLD: {HELLO_WORLD}\""
msgstr "\"HELLO_WORLD: {HELLO_WORLD}\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid ""
"However, mutable static variables are unsafe to read and write because "
"multiple threads could do so concurrently without synchronization, "
"constituting a data race."
msgstr ""
"Namun, membaca dan menulis variabel static mutable tidak aman karena "
"beberapa thread dapat melakukannya secara concurrent tanpa sinkronisasi, "
"sehingga terjadi data race."

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid ""
"Using mutable statics soundly requires reasoning about concurrency without "
"the compiler's help:"
msgstr ""
"Penggunaan static mutable secara sound memerlukan penalaran concurrency "
"tanpa bantuan compiler:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: There are no other threads which could be accessing `COUNTER`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: There are no other threads which could be accessing `COUNTER`.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid ""
"The program here is sound because it is single-threaded. However, the Rust "
"compiler reasons about functions individually so can't assume that. Try "
"removing the `unsafe` and see how the compiler explains that it is undefined"
" behavior to access a mutable static from multiple threads."
msgstr ""
"Program di sini sound karena bersifat single-threaded. Namun, compiler Rust "
"menalar setiap fungsi secara terpisah, sehingga tidak dapat menganggap "
"demikian. Coba hapus `unsafe` dan perhatikan penjelasan compiler bahwa akses"
" static mutable dari beberapa thread merupakan undefined behavior."

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid ""
"The 2024 Rust edition goes further and makes accessing a mutable static by "
"reference an error by default."
msgstr ""
"Rust edition 2024 melangkah lebih jauh dengan menjadikan akses static "
"mutable melalui reference sebagai error secara default."

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid ""
"Using a mutable static is rarely a good idea, you should use interior "
"mutability instead."
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan static mutable jarang menjadi pilihan yang baik; sebaiknya "
"gunakan interior mutability."

#: src/unsafe-rust/mutable-static.md
msgid ""
"There are some cases where it might be necessary in low-level `no_std` code,"
" such as implementing a heap allocator or working with some C APIs. In this "
"case you should use pointers rather than references."
msgstr ""
"Dalam beberapa kasus, static mutable mungkin diperlukan pada kode low-level "
"`no_std`, misalnya untuk mengimplementasikan heap allocator atau menggunakan"
" API C tertentu. Dalam keadaan ini, sebaiknya gunakan pointer, bukan "
"reference."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unions.md
msgid ""
"Unions are like enums, but you need to track the active field yourself:"
msgstr ""
"Union serupa dengan enum, tetapi Anda perlu melacak sendiri field yang "
"aktif:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unions.md
msgid "\"int: {}\""
msgstr "\"int: {}\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unions.md
msgid "\"bool: {}\""
msgstr "\"bool: {}\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unions.md
msgid "// Undefined behavior!\n"
msgstr "// Undefined behavior!\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unions.md
msgid ""
"Unions are rarely needed in Rust as enums provide a superior alternative. "
"They are occasionally needed for interacting with C library APIs."
msgstr ""
"Union jarang diperlukan dalam Rust karena enum menyediakan alternatif yang "
"lebih baik. Union terkadang diperlukan untuk berinteraksi dengan API library"
" C."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unions.md
msgid ""
"If you just want to reinterpret bytes as a different type, you probably want"
" [`std::mem::transmute`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/mem/fn.transmute.html) or a safe wrapper such as the "
"[`zerocopy`](https://crates.io/crates/zerocopy) crate."
msgstr ""
"Jika hanya ingin menafsirkan ulang byte sebagai tipe berbeda, Anda mungkin "
"memerlukan [`std::mem::transmute`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/mem/fn.transmute.html) atau safe wrapper seperti crate "
"[`zerocopy`](https://crates.io/crates/zerocopy)."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions.md
msgid ""
"A function or method can be marked `unsafe` if it has extra preconditions "
"you must uphold to avoid undefined behaviour."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi atau method dapat ditandai `unsafe` jika memiliki prasyarat tambahan "
"yang harus dipenuhi untuk menghindari undefined behavior."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions.md
msgid "Unsafe functions may come from two places:"
msgstr "Fungsi unsafe dapat berasal dari dua tempat:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions.md
msgid "Rust functions declared unsafe."
msgstr "Fungsi Rust yang dideklarasikan unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions.md
msgid "Unsafe foreign functions in `extern \"C\"` blocks."
msgstr "Foreign function unsafe dalam block `extern \"C\"`."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions.md
msgid "We will look at the two kinds of unsafe functions next."
msgstr "Berikutnya, kita membahas kedua jenis fungsi unsafe ini."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md
msgid ""
"You can mark your own functions as `unsafe` if they require particular "
"preconditions to avoid undefined behaviour."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menandai fungsi sendiri sebagai `unsafe` jika memerlukan "
"prasyarat tertentu untuk menghindari undefined behavior."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md
msgid ""
"/// Swaps the values pointed to by the given pointers.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// The pointers must be valid, properly aligned, and not otherwise accessed for\n"
"/// the duration of the function call.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Swaps the values pointed to by the given pointers.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// The pointers must be valid, properly aligned, and not otherwise accessed for\n"
"/// the duration of the function call.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: Our caller promised that the pointers are valid, properly aligned\n"
"    // and have no other access.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: Our caller promised that the pointers are valid, properly aligned\n"
"    // and have no other access.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: The pointers must be valid, aligned and unique because they came\n"
"    // from references.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: The pointers must be valid, aligned and unique because they came\n"
"    // from references.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md
msgid "\"a = {}, b = {}\""
msgstr "\"a = {}, b = {}\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md
msgid ""
"We wouldn't actually use pointers for a `swap` function --- it can be done "
"safely with references."
msgstr ""
"Dalam praktiknya, kita tidak akan menggunakan pointer untuk fungsi `swap` "
"karena ini dapat dilakukan dengan aman melalui reference."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md
msgid ""
"Note that Rust 2021 and earlier allow unsafe code within an unsafe function "
"without an `unsafe` block. This changed in the 2024 edition. We can prohibit"
" it in older editions with `#[deny(unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn)]`. Try adding it "
"and see what happens."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa Rust 2021 dan sebelumnya mengizinkan kode unsafe dalam "
"fungsi unsafe tanpa block `unsafe`. Ini berubah pada edition 2024. Pada "
"edition lama, kita dapat melarangnya melalui "
"`#[deny(unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn)]`. Coba tambahkan dan lihat hasilnya."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"You can declare foreign functions for access from Rust with `unsafe extern`."
" This is unsafe because the compiler has no way to reason about their "
"behavior. Functions declared in an `extern` block must be marked as `safe` "
"or `unsafe`, depending on whether they have preconditions for safe use:"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mendeklarasikan foreign function agar dapat diakses dari Rust "
"menggunakan `unsafe extern`. Ini unsafe karena compiler tidak dapat menalar "
"perilakunya. Fungsi dalam block `extern` harus ditandai `safe` atau "
"`unsafe`, bergantung pada ada atau tidaknya prasyarat penggunaan aman:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md
#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
#: src/android/interoperability/with-c/rust-library.md
#: src/android/interoperability/cpp/cpp-bridge.md
#: src/exercises/chromium/build-rules.md src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart/using.md src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/using.md
#: src/bare-metal/aps/logging/using.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/semantics.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/c-library-example.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/cpp-library-example.md
msgid "\"C\""
msgstr "\"C\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"// `abs` doesn't deal with pointers and doesn't have any safety "
"requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `abs` doesn't deal with pointers and doesn't have any safety "
"requirements.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"/// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// `s` must be a pointer to a NUL-terminated C string which is valid and\n"
"    /// not modified for the duration of this function call.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// `s` must be a pointer to a NUL-terminated C string which is valid and\n"
"    /// not modified for the duration of this function call.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid "\"Absolute value of -3 according to C: {}\""
msgstr "\"Absolute value of -3 according to C: {}\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: We pass a pointer to a C string literal which is valid for the\n"
"    // duration of the program.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: We pass a pointer to a C string literal which is valid for the\n"
"    // duration of the program.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid "\"String length: {}\""
msgstr "\"String length: {}\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md
msgid "\"String\""
msgstr "\"String\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"Rust used to consider all extern functions unsafe, but this changed in Rust "
"1.82 with `unsafe extern` blocks."
msgstr ""
"Rust sebelumnya menganggap semua fungsi extern unsafe, tetapi ini berubah "
"pada Rust 1.82 melalui block `unsafe extern`."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"`abs` must be explicitly marked as `safe` because it is an external function"
" (FFI). Calling external functions is only a problem when those functions do"
" things with pointers which might violate Rust's memory model, but in "
"general any C function might have undefined behaviour under any arbitrary "
"circumstances."
msgstr ""
"`abs` harus secara eksplisit ditandai `safe` karena merupakan fungsi "
"eksternal (FFI). Pemanggilan fungsi eksternal hanya menjadi masalah ketika "
"fungsi melakukan operasi pointer yang mungkin melanggar model memori Rust. "
"Namun, secara umum, fungsi C apa pun dapat memiliki undefined behavior dalam"
" keadaan tertentu."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"The `\"C\"` in this example is the ABI; [other ABIs are available "
"too](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/external-blocks.html)."
msgstr ""
"`\"C\"` pada contoh ini adalah ABI; [ABI lain juga "
"tersedia](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/external-blocks.html)."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/extern-c.md
msgid ""
"Note that there is no verification that the Rust function signature matches "
"that of the function definition -- that's up to you!"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa kecocokan signature fungsi Rust dengan definisi fungsi "
"tidak diverifikasi; Anda yang harus memastikannya!"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid "Failing to uphold the safety requirements breaks memory safety!"
msgstr "Gagal memenuhi persyaratan keamanan melanggar memory safety!"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid "// 8 bytes\n"
msgstr "// 8 bytes\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid "\"{pk:?}\""
msgstr "\"{pk:?}\""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid ""
"Always include a safety comment for each `unsafe` block. It must explain why"
" the code is actually safe. This example is missing a safety comment and is "
"unsound."
msgstr ""
"Selalu sertakan safety comment untuk setiap block `unsafe`. Komentar harus "
"menjelaskan mengapa kode benar-benar aman. Contoh ini tidak memiliki safety "
"comment dan bersifat unsound."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid ""
"The second argument to `slice::from_raw_parts` is the number of _elements_, "
"not bytes! This example demonstrates unexpected behavior by reading past the"
" end of one array and into another."
msgstr ""
"Argumen kedua `slice::from_raw_parts` adalah jumlah _elemen_, bukan byte! "
"Contoh ini menunjukkan perilaku tak terduga dengan membaca melewati akhir "
"suatu array hingga masuk ke array lain."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid ""
"This is undefined behavior because we're reading past the end of the array "
"that the pointer was derived from."
msgstr ""
"Ini merupakan undefined behavior karena pembacaan melewati akhir array asal "
"pointer."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid ""
"`log_public_key` should be unsafe, because `pk_ptr` must meet certain "
"prerequisites to avoid undefined behaviour. A safe function which can cause "
"undefined behaviour is said to be `unsound`. What should its safety "
"documentation say?"
msgstr ""
"`log_public_key` sebaiknya unsafe karena `pk_ptr` harus memenuhi prasyarat "
"tertentu agar tidak terjadi undefined behavior. Fungsi safe yang dapat "
"menyebabkan undefined behavior disebut `unsound`. Apa yang seharusnya "
"dijelaskan dokumentasi keamanannya?"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid ""
"The standard library contains a number of low-level unsafe functions. Prefer"
" the safe alternatives when possible!"
msgstr ""
"Standard library memuat sejumlah fungsi unsafe low-level. Utamakan "
"alternatif yang safe jika memungkinkan!"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/calling.md
msgid ""
"If you use an unsafe function as an optimization, make sure to add a "
"benchmark to demonstrate the gain."
msgstr ""
"Jika menggunakan fungsi unsafe untuk optimasi, pastikan Anda menambahkan "
"benchmark yang menunjukkan peningkatannya."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md
msgid "Implementing Unsafe Traits"
msgstr "Mengimplementasikan Trait Unsafe"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md
msgid ""
"Like with functions, you can mark a trait as `unsafe` if the implementation "
"must guarantee particular conditions to avoid undefined behaviour."
msgstr ""
"Seperti fungsi, trait dapat ditandai `unsafe` jika implementasinya harus "
"menjamin kondisi tertentu untuk menghindari undefined behavior."

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md
msgid ""
"For example, the `zerocopy` crate has an unsafe trait that looks [something "
"like this](https://docs.rs/zerocopy/latest/zerocopy/trait.IntoBytes.html):"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, crate `zerocopy` memiliki trait unsafe yang berbentuk [kurang "
"lebih seperti "
"ini](https://docs.rs/zerocopy/latest/zerocopy/trait.IntoBytes.html):"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md
msgid ""
"/// ...\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"/// The type must have a defined representation and no padding.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// ...\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"/// The type must have a defined representation and no padding.\n"

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md
