#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Safety Comments:** Each `unsafe` block is preceded by a `// SAFETY:` "
"comment explaining why the operation is safe. This is standard practice in "
"Rust to aid auditing."
msgstr ""
"**Safety Comment:** Setiap block `unsafe` diawali komentar `// SAFETY:` yang"
" menjelaskan mengapa operasi tersebut aman. Ini merupakan praktik standar "
"Rust untuk membantu audit."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid ""
"**String conversions:** The code demonstrates the conversions required for "
"FFI:"
msgstr ""
"**Konversi String:** Kode ini memperagakan konversi yang diperlukan untuk "
"FFI:"

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid "`&str` -> `CString`: To create a null-terminated string for C."
msgstr "`&str` -> `CString`: Membuat string null-terminated untuk C."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid "`CString` -> `*const c_char`: To pass the pointer to C."
msgstr "`CString` -> `*const c_char`: Meneruskan pointer ke C."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid "`*const c_char` -> `&CStr`: To wrap the returned C string."
msgstr "`*const c_char` -> `&CStr`: Membungkus string C yang dikembalikan."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid ""
"`&CStr` -> `&[u8]` -> `&OsStr` -> `OsString`: To convert the bytes back to a"
" Rust OS string."
msgstr ""
"`&CStr` -> `&[u8]` -> `&OsStr` -> `OsString`: Mengonversi byte kembali "
"menjadi OS string Rust."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid ""
"**RAII (`Drop`):** We implement `Drop` to call `closedir` automatically when"
" the iterator goes out of scope. This ensures we don't leak file "
"descriptors."
msgstr ""
"**RAII (`Drop`):** Kita mengimplementasikan `Drop` untuk otomatis memanggil "
"`closedir` ketika iterator keluar dari scope. Dengan demikian, file "
"descriptor tidak bocor."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Iterator Interface:** We wrap the C API in a Rust `Iterator`, providing a "
"safe and idiomatic interface (`next` returns `Option<OsString>`) to the "
"underlying unsafe C functions."
msgstr ""
"**Antarmuka Iterator:** Kita membungkus API C dalam `Iterator` Rust, "
"sehingga fungsi C unsafe di dalamnya dapat diakses melalui antarmuka yang "
"safe dan idiomatis, dengan `next` yang mengembalikan `Option<OsString>`."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid ""
"Explain that `CString` owns the data (like `String`), while `CStr` is a "
"borrowed reference (like `&str`)."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa `CString` memiliki ownership atas data, seperti `String`, "
"sedangkan `CStr` merupakan reference pinjaman, seperti `&str`."

#: src/unsafe-rust/solution.md
msgid ""
"The `OsStrExt` trait is needed on Unix systems to convert bytes directly to "
"`OsStr`."
msgstr ""
"Trait `OsStrExt` diperlukan pada sistem Unix untuk mengonversi byte langsung"
" menjadi `OsStr`."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid "Welcome to Macros in Rust"
msgstr "Selamat Datang di Macro di Rust"

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Welcome to the course on **Macros in Rust**. Macros are a powerful tool for "
"meta-programming, allowing to abbreviate and generate code without runtime "
"overhead."
msgstr ""
"Selamat datang di kursus **Macro di Rust**. Macro adalah alat yang ampuh "
"untuk meta-programming, yang memungkinkan Anda menyingkat dan menghasilkan "
"kode tanpa overhead runtime."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid "In this course, we will cover:"
msgstr "Dalam kursus ini, kami akan membahas:"

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid "What macros are and why they are useful."
msgstr "Apa itu macro dan mengapa macro berguna."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid "The distinction between **declarative** and **procedural** macros."
msgstr "Perbedaan antara macro **declarative** dan **procedural**."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid "How the compiler processes tokens and constructs syntax trees."
msgstr "Cara compiler memproses token dan membangun syntax tree."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"How to define Macros By Example and how they are matched, and expanded."
msgstr ""
"Cara mendefinisikan Macro by Example serta cara pencocokan dan perluasannya."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid "Advanced declarative macro techniques."
msgstr "Teknik macro deklaratif tingkat lanjut."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid "Macro hygiene and scoping."
msgstr "Hygiene dan scoping macro."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"How to write procedural macros, along with typical structure and patterns."
msgstr "Cara menulis macro prosedural, beserta struktur dan pola yang umum."

#: src/macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Including 10 minute breaks, this session should take about 6 hours and 5 "
"minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Termasuk jeda 10 menit, sesi ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 6 jam 5 "
"menit. Sesi ini berisi:"

#: src/macros/welcome.md src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid "1 hour and 35 minutes"
msgstr "1 jam 35 menit"

#: src/macros/intro.md
msgid ""
"Before looking at macros in detail, it is helpful to build a conceptual "
"model of what macros are and how they fit into the compilation pipeline."
msgstr ""
"Sebelum membahas macro secara terperinci, akan membantu untuk membangun "
"model konseptual tentang apa itu macro dan bagaimana posisinya dalam alur "
"kompilasi."

#: src/macros/intro.md
msgid "At their core, macros are **meta-programming**:"
msgstr "Pada intinya, macro adalah **meta-programming**:"

#: src/macros/intro.md
msgid "They take input code (expressed as tokens) and emit output code."
msgstr ""
"Macro menerima kode input (yang dinyatakan sebagai token) dan mengeluarkan "
"kode output."

#: src/macros/intro.md
msgid ""
"They execute during compilation, expanding before type checking and semantic"
" analysis."
msgstr ""
"Macro dieksekusi selama kompilasi, diperluas sebelum pemeriksaan tipe dan "
"analisis semantik."

#: src/macros/intro.md
msgid ""
"They allow expressing patterns and abstractions that cannot be written with "
"generics or standard functions."
msgstr ""
"Macro memungkinkan pengekspresian pola dan abstraksi yang tidak dapat "
"ditulis dengan generic atau fungsi standar."

#: src/macros/intro.md
msgid ""
"We will explore how compilers process source code, and how different macro "
"systems hook into this process."
msgstr ""
"Kami akan menelusuri cara compiler memproses kode sumber, dan cara berbagai "
"sistem macro terhubung ke proses ini."

#: src/macros/intro.md
msgid ""
"Ask students if they have used macros in other languages (e.g., C/C++ "
"preprocessor, Lisp, or Clojure)."
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada siswa apakah mereka pernah menggunakan macro di bahasa lain "
"(misalnya, preprocessor C/C++, Lisp, atau Clojure)."

#: src/macros/intro/why.md
msgid ""
"Macros are a powerful tool, but carry their own complexity and should be "
"used only when worthwhile. They are used to solve problems that cannot be "
"easily solved with standard Rust language features:"
msgstr ""
"Macro adalah alat yang ampuh, tetapi membawa kompleksitasnya sendiri dan "
"sebaiknya digunakan hanya jika memang bermanfaat. Macro digunakan untuk "
"menyelesaikan masalah yang tidak dapat diselesaikan dengan mudah menggunakan"
" fitur bahasa Rust standar:"

#: src/macros/intro/why.md
msgid ""
"**Reducing Boilerplate:** Implementing traits via `#[derive(...)]` or "
"reducing syntactic repetition."
msgstr ""
"**Mengurangi Boilerplate:** Mengimplementasikan trait melalui "
"`#[derive(...)]` atau mengurangi pengulangan sintaksis."

#: src/macros/intro/why.md
msgid ""
"**Variadic Interfaces:** Functions that take a variable number of arguments "
"of different types (like `println!` and `vec!`)."
msgstr ""
"**Antarmuka Variadik:** Fungsi yang menerima jumlah argumen bervariasi "
"dengan tipe berbeda (seperti `println!` dan `vec!`)."

#: src/macros/intro/why.md
msgid ""
"**Domain-Specific Languages (DSLs):** Creating custom syntax inside Rust "
"(e.g., `println!`'s format strings, or macros that statically expand HTML "
"templates or parse SQL queries)."
msgstr ""
"**Domain-Specific Languages (DSLs):** Membuat sintaks khusus di dalam Rust "
"(misalnya, format string `println!`, atau macro yang secara statis "
"memperluas template HTML atau mengurai kueri SQL)."

#: src/macros/intro/why.md
msgid ""
"**Compile-Time Computation:** Inspecting configuration files, environment "
"variables, or data at build time (e.g., `include_str!`, `env!`)."
msgstr ""
"**Komputasi Waktu Kompilasi:** Memeriksa berkas konfigurasi, variabel "
"environment, atau data pada waktu build (misalnya, `include_str!`, `env!`)."

#: src/macros/intro/why.md
msgid ""
"Because each macro can define its own input syntax and can perform "
"operations not available to normal Rust code, macros can make code harder to"
" read than it would be otherwise. Try to avoid using macros when the same "
"abstraction can be achieved in another way, and when defining macros, try to"
" align with syntactic and naming patterns followed in non-macro Rust code."
msgstr ""
"Karena setiap macro dapat mendefinisikan sintaks inputnya sendiri dan dapat "
"melakukan operasi yang tidak tersedia bagi kode Rust biasa, macro dapat "
"membuat kode lebih sulit dibaca daripada seharusnya. Hindari penggunaan "
"macro jika abstraksi yang sama dapat dicapai dengan cara lain, dan saat "
"mendefinisikan macro, usahakan selaras dengan pola sintaksis dan penamaan "
"yang diikuti dalam kode Rust non-macro."

#: src/macros/intro/why.md
msgid ""
"Contrast with limitations of normal Rust code: functions have a fixed "
"signature (fixed number of arguments of specific types) and cannot generate "
"new types or modules."
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan dengan keterbatasan kode Rust biasa: fungsi memiliki signature "
"tetap (jumlah argumen tetap dengan tipe tertentu) dan tidak dapat "
"menghasilkan tipe atau modul baru."

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid ""
"To understand how macros work, it helps to look at the pipeline of how a "
"compiler processes your code:"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memahami cara kerja macro, akan membantu untuk melihat alur bagaimana "
"compiler memproses kode Anda:"

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid ""
"**Source Code:** The raw text files written by the programmer, consisting of"
" a sequence of characters in some character set (in Rust, Unicode characters"
" in UTF-8)."
msgstr ""
"**Kode Sumber:** Berkas teks mentah yang ditulis oleh programmer, terdiri "
"atas rangkaian karakter dalam suatu character set (di Rust, karakter Unicode"
" dalam UTF-8)."

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid ""
"**Lexical Analysis (Lexing):** The compiler delimits the raw text into a "
"sequence of **tokens** (e.g., `fn`, `main`, identifiers, punctuation, "
"literals)."
msgstr ""
"**Analisis Leksikal (Lexing):** Compiler memecah teks mentah menjadi "
"rangkaian **token** (misalnya, `fn`, `main`, identifier, tanda baca, "
"literal)."

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid ""
"**Syntactic Analysis (Parsing):** Based on the language's grammar, the "
"compiler organizes the sequence of tokens into an **Abstract Syntax Tree "
"(AST)** that captures the hierarchical structure of the program."
msgstr ""
"**Analisis Sintaksis (Parsing):** Berdasarkan tata bahasa, compiler menyusun"
" rangkaian token menjadi **Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)** yang menangkap "
"struktur hierarkis program."

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid "Source Code"
msgstr "Kode Sumber"

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid "Tokenized Rust (Approx.)"
msgstr "Rust yang Di-tokenisasi (Perkiraan)"

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid "AST Rust (Approx.)"
msgstr "AST Rust (Perkiraan)"

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid "`fn main() {}`"
msgstr "`fn main() {}`"

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid "`Ident: fn`, `Ident: main`, `Group: ()`, `Group: {}`"
msgstr "`Ident: fn`, `Ident: main`, `Group: ()`, `Group: {}`"

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid "`Fn: ident=main, block=...`"
msgstr "`Fn: ident=main, block=...`"

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid ""
"Different macro systems hook into different parts of this pipeline, offering"
" different tradeoffs between expressiveness and safety."
msgstr ""
"Berbagai sistem macro terhubung ke bagian berbeda dari alur ini, menawarkan "
"trade-off yang berbeda antara ekspresivitas dan keamanan."

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid ""
"We'll look at the macro system used in C and C++ via the C Preprocessor, "
"which is well-known, and contrast this with Rust's macro system."
msgstr ""
"Kami akan melihat sistem macro yang digunakan di C dan C++ melalui "
"Preprocessor C, yang sudah dikenal luas, lalu membandingkannya dengan sistem"
" macro Rust."

#: src/macros/intro/how.md
msgid ""
"Explain that the AST is a structured tree that represents what the program "
"actually means semantically."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa AST adalah pohon terstruktur yang merepresentasikan makna "
"semantik program sebenarnya."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"The fundamental difference between C-style preprocessor macros and Rust "
"macros lies in **where they hook into compilation**:"
msgstr ""
"Perbedaan mendasar antara macro preprocessor bergaya C dan macro Rust "
"terletak pada **titik masuknya ke dalam kompilasi**:"

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "C Preprocessor Macros"
msgstr "Macro Preprocessor C"

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "Hook into the **Tokenizing** step."
msgstr "Masuk pada langkah **Tokenizing**."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"Cannot inspect tokens in detail, but can rearrange and duplicate them (and "
"sometimes append them)."
msgstr ""
"Tidak dapat memeriksa token secara terperinci, tetapi dapat menata ulang dan"
" menduplikasinya (dan kadang menambahkannya di akhir)."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "Can create syntactically invalid output."
msgstr "Dapat menghasilkan output yang tidak valid secara sintaksis."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"Lack scoping and hygiene, so constructing robust abstractions is difficult."
msgstr ""
"Tidak memiliki scoping dan hygiene, sehingga membangun abstraksi yang kokoh "
"menjadi sulit."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "Rust Macros"
msgstr "Macro Rust"

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "Hook into the **Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)** generation step."
msgstr "Masuk pada langkah pembuatan **Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)**."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "Operate on structured **Token Trees** rather than raw text."
msgstr "Beroperasi pada **Token Tree** terstruktur, bukan teks mentah."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "Must emit valid Rust syntax."
msgstr "Harus mengeluarkan sintaks Rust yang valid."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid "Maintain **partial hygiene** to prevent accidental name collisions."
msgstr ""
"Mempertahankan **partial hygiene** untuk mencegah tabrakan nama yang tidak "
"disengaja."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"Explain that C macros must guess unused identifiers for internal use, and "
"can access variables not mentioned in their arguments."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa macro C harus menebak identifier yang tidak terpakai untuk "
"penggunaan internal, dan dapat mengakses variabel yang tidak disebutkan "
"dalam argumennya."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"Emphasize that C preprocessor macros don't have access to information from "
"later in compilation, i.e. C syntax or types; they are basically dumb copy-"
"paste."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa macro preprocessor C tidak memiliki akses ke informasi dari "
"tahap kompilasi berikutnya, yaitu sintaks atau tipe C; pada dasarnya mereka "
"hanya copy-paste tanpa pemahaman."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"To provide better error reporting, the C Preprocessor is actually integrated"
" into the Clang and GCC compilers, but its semantics also constrain it to be"
" usable as a separate pass, so this integration can't be used to improve the"
" behavior of C macros."
msgstr ""
"Untuk memberikan pelaporan error yang lebih baik, Preprocessor C sebenarnya "
"diintegrasikan ke dalam compiler Clang dan GCC, tetapi semantiknya juga "
"membatasinya agar tetap dapat digunakan sebagai pass terpisah, sehingga "
"integrasi ini tidak dapat dipakai untuk memperbaiki perilaku macro C."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"Contrast this with Rust, where macro expansion is inherently part of the "
"compilation process. This lets Rust macros work structurally."
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan dengan Rust, tempat ekspansi macro secara inheren merupakan "
"bagian dari proses kompilasi. Hal ini memungkinkan macro Rust bekerja secara"
" struktural."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md
msgid ""
"Introduce the concept of \"partial hygiene,\" explaining that local variable"
" bindings inside Rust macros do not bleed out into the surrounding code (and"
" vice versa) by default."
msgstr ""
"Perkenalkan konsep \"partial hygiene\", dengan menjelaskan bahwa binding "
"variabel lokal di dalam macro Rust tidak merembes ke kode di sekitarnya (dan"
" sebaliknya) secara default."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid "C and C++ macros perform literal, raw text replacement."
msgstr "Macro C dan C++ melakukan penggantian teks mentah secara literal."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid ""
"This allows developers substantial freedom to write C or C++ programs as "
"sequences of tokens that look little like normal code before preprocessing:"
msgstr ""
"Hal ini memberi developer kebebasan besar untuk menulis program C atau C++ "
"sebagai rangkaian token yang tampak jauh berbeda dari kode normal sebelum "
"preprocessing:"

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid "<iostream>"
msgstr "<iostream>"

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md src/macros/intro/rust-example.md
msgid "\"Uh-Oh!\""
msgstr "\"Uh-Oh!\""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid "Key takeaways from this example:"
msgstr "Pelajaran utama dari contoh ini:"

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid ""
"**Custom Syntax:** Using `BEGIN` and `END` in place of braces is not "
"permitted by C itself, and would surprise most readers, but as the "
"preprocessing runs before compilation, the compiler just sees the braces to "
"which these macros expand."
msgstr ""
"**Sintaks Khusus:** Penggunaan `BEGIN` dan `END` sebagai pengganti kurung "
"kurawal tidak diizinkan oleh C sendiri, dan akan mengejutkan sebagian besar "
"pembaca, tetapi karena preprocessing berjalan sebelum kompilasi, compiler "
"hanya melihat kurung kurawal hasil ekspansi macro tersebut."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid ""
"**Unhygienic State Access:** The `EXPECT` macro implicitly accesses `idx`, "
"which is defined in `main` and not passed into the macro. This makes the "
"macro's effect depend on the context in which it is invoked (e.g., suppose "
"`idx` was a pointer to a `struct BTreeIndex`)."
msgstr ""
"**Akses State yang Tidak Higienis:** Macro `EXPECT` secara implisit "
"mengakses `idx`, yang didefinisikan di `main` dan tidak diteruskan ke dalam "
"macro. Ini membuat efek macro bergantung pada konteks tempat macro dipanggil"
" (misalnya, andaikan `idx` adalah pointer ke `struct BTreeIndex`)."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid ""
"Explain the C preprocessor operates as a pure copy-paste system. It replaces"
" tokens line by line without any syntactic structure check."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa preprocessor C beroperasi sebagai sistem copy-paste murni. "
"Preprocessor mengganti token baris demi baris tanpa pemeriksaan struktur "
"sintaksis apa pun."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid ""
"Notice how `EXPECT(< 10)` expands to `if (idx < 10) {}`. The macro assumes "
"`idx` exists and is accessible."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bagaimana `EXPECT(< 10)` diperluas menjadi `if (idx < 10) {}`. "
"Macro mengasumsikan `idx` ada dan dapat diakses."

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-example.md
msgid ""
"If someone uses `EXPECT` inside a function without `idx`, they get a "
"compiler error at the _expansion site_, not the macro definition site, which"
" can lead to confusing and hard-to-debug compiler errors."
msgstr ""
"Jika seseorang menggunakan `EXPECT` di dalam fungsi tanpa `idx`, mereka akan"
" mendapatkan error compiler di _lokasi ekspansi_, bukan di lokasi definisi "
"macro, yang dapat menghasilkan error compiler yang membingungkan dan sulit "
"di-debug."

#: src/macros/intro/rust-example.md
msgid ""
"Here is a comparable implementation of the previous custom syntax example "
"written in Rust:"
msgstr ""
"Berikut implementasi yang sebanding dengan contoh sintaks khusus sebelumnya,"
" ditulis dalam Rust:"

