#: src/macros/intro/rust-example.md
msgid "Compared to C:"
msgstr "Dibandingkan dengan C:"

#: src/macros/intro/rust-example.md
msgid ""
"**Syntactic Safety:** The input is structurally validated. `$code` must be a"
" valid Rust statement and `$name` must be a valid Rust identifier."
msgstr ""
"**Keamanan Sintaksis:** Input divalidasi secara struktural. `$code` harus "
"berupa statement Rust yang valid dan `$name` harus berupa identifier Rust "
"yang valid."

#: src/macros/intro/rust-example.md
msgid ""
"**Hygiene:** In `expect!`, the test `idx < 10` is explicitly passed as an "
"expression `$test`, rather than having the macro rely on a hidden, "
"implicitly named local variable."
msgstr ""
"**Hygiene:** Pada `expect!`, pengujian `idx < 10` diteruskan secara "
"eksplisit sebagai ekspresi `$test`, alih-alih membuat macro bergantung pada "
"variabel lokal tersembunyi yang namanya implisit."

#: src/macros/intro/rust-example.md
msgid ""
"Walk through how `procedure!` defines a pattern that matches an identifier "
"`$name`, followed by the literal token `BEGIN`, followed by a statement "
"`$code`, a semicolon (which is required to separate a statement from the "
"next syntactic construct) and then our `END` token."
msgstr ""
"Telusuri bagaimana `procedure!` mendefinisikan pattern yang mencocokkan "
"identifier `$name`, diikuti token literal `BEGIN`, diikuti statement "
"`$code`, titik koma (yang diperlukan untuk memisahkan statement dari "
"konstruk sintaksis berikutnya), lalu token `END` kita."

#: src/macros/intro/rust-example.md
msgid ""
"Note that even though the syntax is custom, the Rust compiler ensures that "
"the inputs to macros are well-formed before passing them to the macro."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa meskipun sintaksnya khusus, compiler Rust memastikan input "
"ke macro terbentuk dengan benar sebelum meneruskannya ke macro."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"Rust macros provide structured code generation. There are **three kinds** of"
" macros, and **two ways** they are implemented."
msgstr ""
"Macro Rust menyediakan pembuatan kode yang terstruktur. Ada **tiga jenis** "
"macro, dan **dua cara** penerapannya."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid "Kinds of Macros"
msgstr "Jenis-Jenis Macro"

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"**Derive Macros:** Added to type definitions (structs, enums, unions) to "
"auto-implement traits (e.g., `#[derive(Default)]`)."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Derive:** Ditambahkan ke definisi tipe (struct, enum, union) untuk "
"mengimplementasikan trait secara otomatis (misalnya, `#[derive(Default)]`)."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"**Function-Like Macros:** Invoked with an exclamation mark in "
"item/statement/expr context (e.g., `println!(\"Hello!\")`, `vec![1, 2, 3]`, "
"or `include_bytes!(\"manifest.bin\")`)."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Mirip Fungsi:** Dipanggil dengan tanda seru dalam konteks "
"item/statement/expr (misalnya, `println!(\"Hello!\")`, `vec![1, 2, 3]`, atau"
" `include_bytes!(\"manifest.bin\")`)."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"**Attribute Macros:** Attached as custom attributes to any item, like "
"functions or modules (e.g., `#[tokio::main]`)."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Atribut:** Dilekatkan sebagai atribut khusus pada item apa pun, "
"seperti fungsi atau modul (misalnya, `#[tokio::main]`)."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid "Implementation Forms"
msgstr "Bentuk Implementasi"

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"**Declarative Macros (AKA \"Macros By Example\"):** Part of the language "
"itself, based on pattern matching; these can only be used to define "
"function-like macros."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Deklaratif (alias \"Macros By Example\"):** Bagian dari bahasa itu "
"sendiri, berbasis pattern matching; macro ini hanya dapat digunakan untuk "
"mendefinisikan macro mirip fungsi."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"**Procedural Macros:** Rust functions running as compiler plugins that "
"transform token streams. These can perform arbitrary operations at compile "
"time, including I/O if desired."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Prosedural:** Fungsi Rust yang berjalan sebagai plugin compiler dan "
"mentransformasi token stream. Macro ini dapat melakukan operasi arbitrer "
"pada waktu kompilasi, termasuk I/O jika diinginkan."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"Highlight that students have already used function-like macros (like "
"`println!`, `vec!`, `format!`) and derive macros (like `#[derive(Clone, "
"Debug)]`)."
msgstr ""
"Soroti bahwa siswa sudah menggunakan macro mirip fungsi (seperti `println!`,"
" `vec!`, `format!`) dan macro derive (seperti `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]`)."

#: src/macros/design.md
msgid ""
"Explain that attribute macros are very popular in libraries like Tokio or "
"Axum, often transforming functions similar to Python decorators."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa macro atribut sangat populer di library seperti Tokio atau "
"Axum, yang sering mentransformasi fungsi serupa decorator Python."

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid ""
"There are two separate ways of implementing macros in Rust. Each has "
"distinct advantages and trade-offs:"
msgstr ""
"Ada dua cara terpisah untuk mengimplementasikan macro di Rust. Masing-masing"
" memiliki keunggulan dan trade-off yang berbeda:"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "Feature"
msgstr "Fitur"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "Declarative Macros"
msgstr "Macro Deklaratif"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "**Usage**"
msgstr "**Penggunaan**"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "Function-like macros only"
msgstr "Hanya macro mirip fungsi"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "All three kinds (Derive, Attr, Function-like)"
msgstr "Ketiga jenisnya (Derive, Attr, Mirip Fungsi)"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "**Location**"
msgstr "**Lokasi**"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "Implemented within your normal crate"
msgstr "Diimplementasikan di dalam crate normal Anda"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "Must be defined in a separate `proc-macro` crate"
msgstr "Harus didefinisikan dalam crate `proc-macro` terpisah"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "**Pros**"
msgstr "**Kelebihan**"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid ""
"\\- Low boilerplate<br>\\- No extra compilation step<br>\\- Easy to write "
"and reuse"
msgstr ""
"\\- Boilerplate rendah<br>\\- Tidak ada langkah kompilasi tambahan<br>\\- "
"Mudah ditulis dan digunakan kembali"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid ""
"\\- Extremely powerful and expressive<br>\\- Written in standard Rust<br>\\-"
" Full programmatic control"
msgstr ""
"\\- Sangat ampuh dan ekspresif<br>\\- Ditulis dalam Rust standar<br>\\- "
"Kontrol programatik penuh"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "**Cons**"
msgstr "**Kekurangan**"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid ""
"\\- Bespoke pattern-matching syntax<br>\\- Cannot inspect arbitrary token "
"structures"
msgstr ""
"\\- Sintaks pattern matching yang khusus<br>\\- Tidak dapat memeriksa "
"struktur token arbitrer"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "\\- Can slow down build time<br>\\- Substantial boilerplate required"
msgstr ""
"\\- Dapat memperlambat waktu build<br>\\- Memerlukan boilerplate yang cukup "
"besar"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "**Hygiene**"
msgstr "**Hygiene**"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "Partially/mixed hygienic by default"
msgstr "Sebagian/campuran higienis secara default"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid "Configurable / custom hygiene"
msgstr "Hygiene yang dapat dikonfigurasi / khusus"

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid ""
"Explain that procedural macros are literally compiled as libraries and "
"executed _inside_ the compiler while compiling the consuming code. This is "
"why they require a separate crate."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa macro prosedural secara harfiah dikompilasi sebagai library "
"dan dieksekusi _di dalam_ compiler saat mengompilasi kode yang "
"mengonsumsinya. Inilah sebabnya macro tersebut memerlukan crate terpisah."

#: src/macros/defining.md
msgid ""
"Emphasize that you should always prefer declarative macros for simple code "
"generation due to their much smaller impact on build times."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa Anda sebaiknya selalu memilih macro deklaratif untuk "
"pembuatan kode sederhana karena dampaknya jauh lebih kecil terhadap waktu "
"build."

#: src/macros/kinds.md
msgid ""
"Macros can be attached to or invoked at different positions in your code. "
"There are three major cases to consider:"
msgstr ""
"Macro dapat dilekatkan atau dipanggil pada berbagai posisi dalam kode Anda. "
"Ada tiga kasus utama yang perlu dipertimbangkan:"

#: src/macros/kinds.md
msgid ""
"**Function-Like Macros:** Invoked as expressions, statements, types, "
"patterns, or items, expanding to any syntax that could occupy the invocation"
" position."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Mirip Fungsi:** Dipanggil sebagai expression, statement, tipe, "
"pattern, atau item, dan diperluas menjadi sintaks apa pun yang dapat "
"menempati posisi pemanggilan."

#: src/macros/kinds.md
msgid ""
"**Derive Macros:** Attached specifically to `struct`, `enum`, or `union` "
"items, to generate trait impls based on the type definition."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Derive:** Dilekatkan secara khusus pada item `struct`, `enum`, atau "
"`union`, untuk menghasilkan implementasi trait berdasarkan definisi tipe."

#: src/macros/kinds.md
msgid ""
"**Attribute Macros:** Attached to any standard Rust `item` (including "
"functions, modules, structs, etc.), allowing complete replacement of the "
"attached item."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Atribut:** Dilekatkan pada `item` Rust standar apa pun (termasuk "
"fungsi, modul, struct, dan sebagainya), sehingga item yang dilekati dapat "
"diganti sepenuhnya."

#: src/macros/kinds.md
msgid "We will now see how each of these looks and behaves."
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan melihat bagaimana masing-masing tampak dan berperilaku."

#: src/macros/kinds.md
msgid ""
"Mention that \"items\" in Rust are top-level declarations (which can nest!) "
"such as structs, modules, traits, and functions."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa \"item\" di Rust adalah deklarasi tingkat atas (yang dapat "
"bersarang!) seperti struct, modul, trait, dan fungsi."

#: src/macros/kinds.md
msgid ""
"Clarify that some macro positions are more restricted than others: e.g., "
"derive macros cannot modify the structs they are attached to, but only "
"append new implementations alongside; meanwhile, attribute macros can "
"rewrite their targets entirely."
msgstr ""
"Perjelas bahwa sebagian posisi macro lebih terbatas daripada yang lain: "
"misalnya, macro derive tidak dapat mengubah struct yang dilekatinya, tetapi "
"hanya menambahkan implementasi baru di sampingnya; sementara itu, macro "
"atribut dapat menulis ulang targetnya sepenuhnya."

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Function-like macros** are invoked with an exclamation mark (`!`) "
"following their identifier. They look like function calls, but they can "
"accept arbitrary tokens inside their brackets."
msgstr ""
"**Macro mirip fungsi** dipanggil dengan tanda seru (`!`) setelah identifier-"
"nya. Macro ini tampak seperti pemanggilan fungsi, tetapi dapat menerima "
"token arbitrer di dalam kurungnya."

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid "// Invoked as an expression:\n"
msgstr "// Invoked as an expression:\n"

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid "// Invoked as a statement:\n"
msgstr "// Invoked as a statement:\n"

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid "\"Hello, World! {:?}\""
msgstr "\"Hello, World! {:?}\""

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Flexible brackets:** Can be invoked with parentheses `()`, square brackets"
" `[]`, or curly braces `{}`."
msgstr ""
"**Kurung yang fleksibel:** Dapat dipanggil dengan tanda kurung `()`, kurung "
"siku `[]`, atau kurung kurawal `{}`."

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Input:** Can contain any sequence of Rust tokens, but unmatched "
"opening/closing brackets are forbidden (so the compiler can tell where the "
"macro invocation ends, regardless of how the macro processes those tokens)."
msgstr ""
"**Input:** Dapat berisi rangkaian token Rust apa pun, tetapi kurung "
"buka/tutup yang tidak berpasangan dilarang (agar compiler dapat mengetahui "
"di mana pemanggilan macro berakhir, terlepas dari bagaimana macro memproses "
"token tersebut)."

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Placement:** Can appear as expressions, statements, types, patterns, or "
"items."
msgstr ""
"**Penempatan:** Dapat muncul sebagai expression, statement, tipe, pattern, "
"atau item."

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Implementation:** These are the only kind of macro that can be implemented"
" as either a **declarative** macro (`macro_rules!`) or a **procedural** "
"macro."
msgstr ""
"**Implementasi:** Ini satu-satunya jenis macro yang dapat diimplementasikan "
"sebagai macro **deklaratif** (`macro_rules!`) maupun macro **prosedural**."

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid ""
"Mention that while they look like function calls, they are expanded during "
"compilation. They do not exist at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa meskipun tampak seperti pemanggilan fungsi, macro diperluas "
"selama kompilasi. Macro tidak ada pada waktu runtime."

#: src/macros/kinds/function-like.md
msgid ""
"The choice of brackets is a matter of stylistic convention: `vec!` uses `[]`"
" because it behaves like an array, `println!` uses `()` because it behaves "
"like a function call, and custom macros defining items often use `{}`."
msgstr ""
"Pemilihan kurung adalah soal konvensi gaya: `vec!` menggunakan `[]` karena "
"berperilaku seperti array, `println!` menggunakan `()` karena berperilaku "
"seperti pemanggilan fungsi, dan macro khusus yang mendefinisikan item sering"
" menggunakan `{}`."

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md
msgid ""
"**Derive macros** are attached to structs, enums, or unions by preceding "
"them with the `#[derive(...)]` attribute. They generate new code next to the"
" type, typically implementing traits automatically."
msgstr ""
"**Macro derive** dilekatkan pada struct, enum, atau union dengan "
"mendahuluinya dengan atribut `#[derive(...)]`. Macro ini menghasilkan kode "
"baru di samping tipe tersebut, biasanya mengimplementasikan trait secara "
"otomatis."

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md
msgid "\"Default result: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"Default result: {:?}\""

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md
msgid ""
"**Targeted:** Can only be applied to type definitions using the `struct`, "
"`enum`, or `union` keywords."
msgstr ""
"**Bertarget:** Hanya dapat diterapkan pada definisi tipe yang menggunakan "
"keyword `struct`, `enum`, atau `union`."

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md
msgid ""
"**Additive:** They cannot modify or delete the original type definition; "
"they can only output additional code (such as `impl` blocks)."
msgstr ""
"**Aditif:** Macro ini tidak dapat mengubah atau menghapus definisi tipe "
"asli; mereka hanya dapat mengeluarkan kode tambahan (seperti block `impl`)."

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid "**Implementation:** Always implemented as procedural macros."
msgstr "**Implementasi:** Selalu diimplementasikan sebagai macro prosedural."

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md
msgid ""
"Explain that `#[derive(Debug)]` generates an implementation of "
"`std::fmt::Debug` for the struct."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa `#[derive(Debug)]` menghasilkan implementasi "
"`std::fmt::Debug` untuk struct tersebut."

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md
msgid ""
"Note that derive macros can also support \"helper attributes\" (attributes "
"placed on struct fields, like `#[serde(rename = \"name\")]` or `#[default]` "
"in the example), which configure the generated code."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa macro derive juga dapat mendukung \"helper attribute\" "
"(atribut yang ditempatkan pada field struct, seperti `#[serde(rename = "
"\"name\")]` atau `#[default]` pada contoh), yang mengonfigurasi kode yang "
"dihasilkan."

#: src/macros/kinds/derive.md
msgid ""
"Mention that derive macros are compiled together in the same module as the "
"type. Any items they generate (like helper functions or helper traits) exist"
" in the same namespace, so they must be designed carefully to avoid "
"namespace collisions."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa macro derive dikompilasi bersama dalam modul yang sama dengan"
" tipe tersebut. Item apa pun yang dihasilkan (seperti fungsi atau trait "
"helper) berada dalam namespace yang sama, sehingga macro harus dirancang "
"dengan cermat untuk menghindari tabrakan namespace."

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid ""
"**Attribute macros** are attached as custom attributes to any standard Rust "
"`item` (including functions, modules, structs, etc.). They have full power "
"to inspect, rewrite, or completely replace the item they are attached to."
msgstr ""
"**Macro atribut** dilekatkan sebagai atribut khusus pada `item` Rust standar"
" apa pun (termasuk fungsi, modul, struct, dan sebagainya). Macro ini "
"memiliki kekuatan penuh untuk memeriksa, menulis ulang, atau sepenuhnya "
"mengganti item yang dilekatinya."

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid "// A popular example from the Tokio library:\n"
msgstr "// A popular example from the Tokio library:\n"

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid "\"Hello from an async main!\""
msgstr "\"Hello from an async main!\""

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid "**Universal:** Can be applied to any declaration/item."
msgstr "**Universal:** Dapat diterapkan pada deklarasi/item apa pun."

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid ""
"**Transformational:** Unlike derive macros, they can entirely replace their "
"target with different code."
msgstr ""
"**Transformatif:** Berbeda dari macro derive, macro atribut dapat sepenuhnya"
" mengganti targetnya dengan kode yang berbeda."

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid ""
"**Parameters:** Can optionally accept custom metadata parameters, e.g., "
"`#[route(GET, \"/\")]`."
msgstr ""
"**Parameter:** Dapat secara opsional menerima parameter metadata khusus, "
"misalnya, `#[route(GET, \"/\")]`."

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid ""
"Discuss how `#[tokio::main]` converts an `async fn main()` into a "
"synchronous `fn main()` that instantiates and runs the Tokio runtime, blocks"
" on the future, and executes the async block. This completely rewrites the "
"function signature!"
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan bagaimana `#[tokio::main]` mengubah `async fn main()` menjadi `fn"
" main()` sinkron yang menginstansiasi dan menjalankan runtime Tokio, "
"memblokir pada future, dan mengeksekusi block async. Ini sepenuhnya menulis "
"ulang signature fungsi!"

#: src/macros/kinds/attr.md
msgid ""
"Emphasize that because attribute macros can entirely rewrite items, they are"
" extremely powerful but require careful error handling to avoid completely "
"obscuring compile errors for the user."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa karena macro atribut dapat sepenuhnya menulis ulang item, "
"macro ini sangat ampuh tetapi memerlukan penanganan error yang cermat agar "
"tidak sepenuhnya menutupi error kompilasi bagi pengguna."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"Rather than manipulating raw text, Rust macros operate on **tokens** and "
"**token trees**."
msgstr ""
"Alih-alih memanipulasi teks mentah, macro Rust beroperasi pada **token** dan"
" **token tree**."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"**Tokens** are the smallest indivisible lexical elements of the language "
"(e.g., identifiers like `foo`, operators like `+`, punctuation like `,`, and"
" literals like `123`)."
msgstr ""
"**Token** adalah elemen leksikal terkecil yang tidak dapat dibagi dari "
"bahasa (misalnya, identifier seperti `foo`, operator seperti `+`, tanda baca"
" seperti `,`, dan literal seperti `123`)."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"**Token trees** are formed by grouping streams of tokens and token groups."
msgstr ""
"**Token tree** dibentuk dengan mengelompokkan stream token dan grup token."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid "When a macro is called, the compiler passes it such a stream."
msgstr "Saat macro dipanggil, compiler meneruskannya stream semacam itu."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"The macro processes this input stream and must return another stream of "
"tokens-and-groups that replaces the macro invocation."
msgstr ""
"Macro memproses stream input ini dan harus mengembalikan stream token-dan-"
"grup lain yang menggantikan pemanggilan macro."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"This structure allows the compiler to validate lexical boundaries and "
"ensures that macros can never construct or return syntactically invalid, un-"
"lexable text."
msgstr ""
"Struktur ini memungkinkan compiler memvalidasi batas leksikal dan memastikan"
" macro tidak pernah dapat membangun atau mengembalikan teks yang tidak valid"
" secara sintaksis dan tidak dapat di-lex."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"Reiterate that because macro expansion happens _during_ AST generation, the "
"macro receives structured tokens, not characters."
msgstr ""
"Tegaskan kembali bahwa karena ekspansi macro terjadi _selama_ pembuatan AST,"
" macro menerima token terstruktur, bukan karakter."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"Explain that this differs completely from preprocessors (like C/C++), which "
"perform string/text-level substitution before tokenization."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa ini sangat berbeda dari preprocessor (seperti C/C++), yang "
"melakukan substitusi pada tingkat string/teks sebelum tokenisasi."

#: src/macros/tokens.md
msgid ""
"Mention that this token-level manipulation is what makes Rust macros more "
"robust and syntax-safe."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa manipulasi pada tingkat token inilah yang membuat macro Rust "
"lebih kokoh dan aman secara sintaksis."

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid ""
"A **token tree** can represent either a single token, or a **group** of "
"tokens enclosed by matching delimiters (brackets):"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah **token tree** dapat merepresentasikan satu token tunggal, atau "
"**grup** token yang diapit delimiter (kurung) yang berpasangan:"

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid "**Single tokens (leaf nodes):** `foo`, `+`, `,`, `123`."
msgstr "**Token tunggal (leaf node):** `foo`, `+`, `,`, `123`."

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid ""
"**Grouped tokens (internal nodes):** Enclosed by parentheses `()`, braces "
"`{}`, or square brackets `[]`."
msgstr ""
"**Token yang dikelompokkan (internal node):** Diapit tanda kurung `()`, "
"kurung kurawal `{}`, atau kurung siku `[]`."

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid "For example, the token stream: `foo + (bar * baz)`"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, token stream: `foo + (bar * baz)`"

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid "Is parsed into **3 separate token trees**:"
msgstr "Diurai menjadi **3 token tree terpisah**:"

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid "`foo` (a single token)"
msgstr "`foo` (satu token tunggal)"

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid "`+` (a single token)"
msgstr "`+` (satu token tunggal)"

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid ""
"`(bar * baz)` (a token group containing three child token trees: `bar`, `*`,"
" and `baz`)"
msgstr ""
"`(bar * baz)` (grup token yang berisi tiga token tree anak: `bar`, `*`, dan "
"`baz`)"

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid ""
"Because grouping happens _during_ lexical analysis, **unbalanced groups are "
"strictly disallowed**. You cannot pass unbalanced parentheses or braces into"
" or out of a macro!"
msgstr ""
"Karena pengelompokan terjadi _selama_ analisis leksikal, **grup yang tidak "
"seimbang dilarang keras**. Anda tidak dapat meneruskan tanda kurung atau "
"kurung kurawal yang tidak berpasangan ke dalam atau ke luar macro!"

#: src/macros/brackets.md
msgid ""
"Note that this means you cannot use a macro to generate half a block, like "
"`let x = {` and close it with another macro or tokens outside the macro. The"
" entire block must be passed or returned as a single, well-formed token "
"group."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa ini berarti Anda tidak dapat menggunakan macro untuk "
"menghasilkan setengah block, seperti `let x = {`, lalu menutupnya dengan "
"macro lain atau token di luar macro. Seluruh block harus diteruskan atau "
"dikembalikan sebagai satu grup token yang terbentuk dengan benar."

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"A **token stream** is a sequence of token trees. It is the fundamental input"
" and output format for both declarative and procedural macros in Rust:"
msgstr ""
"**Token stream** adalah rangkaian token tree. Ini adalah format input dan "
"output fundamental bagi macro deklaratif maupun prosedural di Rust:"

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"**Macro Input:** The tokens passed inside the brackets of the macro "
"invocation."
msgstr ""
"**Input Macro:** Token yang diteruskan di dalam kurung pemanggilan macro."

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"**Macro Output:** The new tokens returned by the macro that replace the "
"macro invocation."
msgstr ""
"**Output Macro:** Token baru yang dikembalikan macro untuk menggantikan "
"pemanggilan macro."

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"For declarative macros, the output is structured not just as a token stream,"
" but also must be syntactically valid Rust. The generated syntax is inserted"
" into the AST of the program where the macro is invoked."
msgstr ""
"Untuk macro deklaratif, output tidak hanya terstruktur sebagai token stream,"
" tetapi juga harus valid secara sintaksis sebagai Rust. Sintaks yang "
"dihasilkan disisipkan ke AST program di tempat macro dipanggil."

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"// The input token stream does not need to be valid Rust syntax, as long as it\n"
"// tokenizes (which requires any brackets to be balanced).\n"
msgstr ""
"// The input token stream does not need to be valid Rust syntax, as long as it\n"
"// tokenizes (which requires any brackets to be balanced).\n"

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"// The macro returns tokens: 1 + 2\n"
"    // Since expansion inserts a structured AST fragment, precedence is preserved!\n"
msgstr ""
"// The macro returns tokens: 1 + 2\n"
"    // Since expansion inserts a structured AST fragment, precedence is preserved!\n"

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid "\"3 * 10 = {}\""
msgstr "\"3 * 10 = {}\""

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid "// Outputs \"30\"\n"
msgstr "// Outputs \"30\"\n"

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"Because macro output is inserted as an AST subtree, we don't need to wrap "
"expansions in safety parentheses (unlike C macros, where literal replacement"
" would cause `1 + 2 * 10` to equal `21`)."
msgstr ""
"Karena output macro disisipkan sebagai subtree AST, kita tidak perlu "
"membungkus ekspansi dengan tanda kurung pengaman (berbeda dari macro C, "
"tempat penggantian literal akan membuat `1 + 2 * 10` bernilai `21`)."

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"This slide shows `macro_rules!` defining a declarative macro. We do not need"
" to visit this in detail yet, as we will do so on the next slide."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini menunjukkan `macro_rules!` yang mendefinisikan macro deklaratif. "
"Kita belum perlu membahasnya secara terperinci, karena akan dilakukan pada "
"slide berikutnya."

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"Explain that a Token Stream can contain arbitrary sequences of tokens. The "
"tokens do not need to form valid Rust code on their own (for example, "
"`special_print!(#foo(bar:123))` uses `#` and `:` in custom ways)."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa Token Stream dapat berisi rangkaian token arbitrer. Token-"
"token tersebut tidak perlu membentuk kode Rust yang valid dengan sendirinya "
"(misalnya, `special_print!(#foo(bar:123))` menggunakan `#` dan `:` dengan "
"cara khusus)."

#: src/macros/streams.md
msgid ""
"When a macro expands, the _emitted_ token stream must make syntactic sense "
"at the position where the macro is invoked."
msgstr ""
"Saat macro diperluas, token stream yang _dikeluarkan_ harus masuk akal "
"secara sintaksis pada posisi tempat macro dipanggil."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"**Macros by Example** (also known as **Declarative Macros** or "
"`macro_rules!` macros) are the most common form of macros in Rust and the "
"easiest to write."
msgstr ""
"**Macros by Example** (juga dikenal sebagai **Macro Deklaratif** atau macro "
"`macro_rules!`) adalah bentuk macro paling umum di Rust dan paling mudah "
"ditulis."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid "They are defined using the `macro_rules!` construct."
msgstr "Macro ini didefinisikan menggunakan konstruk `macro_rules!`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"They allow you to write custom pattern matches on tokens, expanding them "
"into standard Rust code."
msgstr ""
"Macro ini memungkinkan Anda menulis pattern matching khusus pada token, lalu"
" memperluasnya menjadi kode Rust standar."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"They are partially hygienic: local variables and labels defined inside them "
"do not leak outside."
msgstr ""
"Macro ini bersifat sebagian higienis: variabel lokal dan label yang "
"didefinisikan di dalamnya tidak bocor ke luar."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"They introduce minimal compile-time overhead and have no external crate "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""
"Macro ini menimbulkan overhead waktu kompilasi minimal dan tidak memiliki "
"dependensi crate eksternal."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"We will learn how to write, configure, and match patterns in declarative "
"macros."
msgstr ""
"Kami akan mempelajari cara menulis, mengonfigurasi, dan mencocokkan pattern "
"dalam macro deklaratif."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Mention that declarative macros are sometimes called \"macros by example\" "
"because you write an example of the syntax you want to match, and an example"
" of the output you want to produce. This is much like C preprocessor macros,"
" but with richer pattern matching."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa macro deklaratif kadang disebut \"macros by example\" karena "
"Anda menulis contoh sintaks yang ingin dicocokkan dan contoh output yang "
"ingin dihasilkan. Ini sangat mirip dengan macro preprocessor C, tetapi "
"dengan pattern matching yang lebih kaya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Highlight that they are defined directly in your standard code, making them "
"convenient to add without extra setup."
msgstr ""
"Soroti bahwa macro ini didefinisikan langsung dalam kode standar Anda, "
"sehingga mudah ditambahkan tanpa persiapan tambahan."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/welcome.md
msgid ""
"This slide acts as a transition into how declarative macros are defined and "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini menjadi transisi menuju cara macro deklaratif didefinisikan dan "
"digunakan."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid ""
"Let's look at a simple declarative macro that mimics the behavior of "
"`vec![]` for empty vector creation:"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita lihat macro deklaratif sederhana yang meniru perilaku `vec![]` "
"untuk membuat vector kosong:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid "\"Vector: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"Vector: {:?}\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid ""
"The macro is introduced with the `macro_rules!` construct, declaring a macro"
" named `my_vec`."
msgstr ""
"Macro diperkenalkan dengan konstruk `macro_rules!`, yang mendeklarasikan "
"macro bernama `my_vec`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid ""
"**Match Arm:** The left-hand side `()` is the matcher. The pattern here "
"matches only empty inputs."
msgstr ""
"**Match Arm:** Sisi kiri `()` adalah matcher. Pattern di sini hanya cocok "
"dengan input kosong."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid ""
"**Transcriber:** The right-hand side `{ Vec::new() }` is the transcriber. It"
" specifies what the macro invocation will expand to for this pattern."
msgstr ""
"**Transcriber:** Sisi kanan `{ Vec::new() }` adalah transcriber. Bagian ini "
"menentukan hasil ekspansi pemanggilan macro untuk pattern tersebut."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid ""
"Explain that `macro_rules!` is itself a macro, which uses a special, unique "
"language syntax for defining declarative macros."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa `macro_rules!` sendiri adalah macro, yang menggunakan sintaks"
" bahasa khusus dan unik untuk mendefinisikan macro deklaratif."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid ""
"Recall that although `my_vec![]` is invoked with square brackets "
"(conventional for array-like objects), any brackets (`my_vec!()` or "
"`my_vec!{}`) would also work."
msgstr ""
"Ingatkan bahwa meskipun `my_vec![]` dipanggil dengan kurung siku (konvensi "
"untuk objek mirip array), kurung apa pun (`my_vec!()` atau `my_vec!{}`) juga"
" akan berfungsi."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/example.md
msgid ""
"In this case, `my_vec![]` matches empty tokens and transcribes directly to "
"`Vec::new()`."
msgstr ""
"Dalam kasus ini, `my_vec![]` mencocokkan token kosong dan mentranskripsinya "
"langsung menjadi `Vec::new()`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid ""
"A declarative macro consists of one or more **macro rules**, similar to how "
"a Rust `match` expression consists of a sequence of match arms:"
msgstr ""
"Macro deklaratif terdiri atas satu atau beberapa **macro rule**, serupa "
"dengan bagaimana expression `match` di Rust terdiri atas rangkaian match "
"arm:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid "// Left-side: Matcher        Right-side: Transcriber\n"
msgstr "// Left-side: Matcher        Right-side: Transcriber\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid ""
"**Macro Rule:** An arm of the macro containing a Matcher and a Transcriber "
"separated by `=>`."
msgstr ""
"**Macro Rule:** Salah satu arm macro yang berisi Matcher dan Transcriber "
"yang dipisahkan oleh `=>`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid "**Matcher:** A pattern that matches an input token stream."
msgstr "**Matcher:** Pattern yang mencocokkan token stream input."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid "**Transcriber:** The code segment template that expands when matched."
msgstr ""
"**Transcriber:** Template segmen kode yang diperluas saat pattern cocok."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid ""
"**Meta-variables:** Variables defined on the left and expanded on the right,"
" prefixed with `$` (e.g., `$bar`)."
msgstr ""
"**Meta-variabel:** Variabel yang didefinisikan di sisi kiri dan diperluas di"
" sisi kanan, diawali `$` (misalnya, `$bar`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid ""
"**Fragment Specifiers:** Indicate to which syntactic category the meta-"
"variable is restricted (e.g., `ident` or `expr`)."
msgstr ""
"**Fragment Specifier:** Menunjukkan kategori sintaksis tempat meta-variabel "
"dibatasi (misalnya, `ident` atau `expr`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid ""
"Like `match` in normal Rust, the compiler attempts to match each rule "
"sequentially, from top to bottom."
msgstr ""
"Seperti `match` pada Rust biasa, compiler mencoba mencocokkan setiap rule "
"secara berurutan, dari atas ke bawah."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid ""
"If a rule matches the input token stream completely, it selects that arm and"
" transcribes the output."
msgstr ""
"Jika suatu rule mencocokkan token stream input secara lengkap, compiler "
"memilih arm tersebut dan mentranskripsikan outputnya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md
msgid ""
"If no arms match, or if any pattern is ambiguous when matching tokens (there"
" is no backtrack or lookahead), the compiler emits an error."
msgstr ""
"Jika tidak ada arm yang cocok, atau jika ada pattern yang ambigu saat "
"mencocokkan token (tidak ada backtrack atau lookahead), compiler "
"mengeluarkan error."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching.md
msgid ""
"You can match on exact, literal tokens inside macro patterns. This is "
"extremely useful for building custom DSLs or structured syntax matching:"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mencocokkan token literal secara persis di dalam pattern macro. "
"Ini sangat berguna untuk membangun DSL khusus atau pencocokan sintaks "
"terstruktur:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching.md
msgid "\"Starting...\""
msgstr "\"Starting...\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching.md
msgid "\"Stopping...\""
msgstr "\"Stopping...\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching.md
msgid ""
"In this example, the tokens `start`, `stop`, and `restart` are matched "
"exactly as literal identifiers. Literal identifiers and custom symbols (such"
" as `=>`, `,`, `:`, etc.) can be sequenced to design readable and mnemonic "
"input syntax for your macros."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh ini, token `start`, `stop`, dan `restart` dicocokkan persis "
"sebagai identifier literal. Identifier literal dan simbol khusus (seperti "
"`=>`, `,`, `:`, dan sebagainya) dapat diurutkan untuk merancang sintaks "
"input yang mudah dibaca dan diingat bagi macro Anda."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching.md
msgid ""
"Note that the macro in the example invokes itself recursively in its "
"transcriber body."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa macro pada contoh memanggil dirinya sendiri secara rekursif"
" di dalam tubuh transcriber-nya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching.md
msgid ""
"Point out that because macros parse token streams, standard Rust rules (like"
" variables needing to be declared or modules needing to exist) do not apply "
"to the literal tokens being matched. They are treated purely as structural "
"matches."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bahwa karena macro mengurai token stream, aturan Rust standar "
"(seperti variabel harus dideklarasikan atau modul harus ada) tidak berlaku "
"bagi token literal yang dicocokkan. Token tersebut diperlakukan murni "
"sebagai pencocokan struktural."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching.md
msgid ""
"Macros can invoke themselves and other macros, which can be useful for some "
"more advanced macro design patterns which will be discussed later."
msgstr ""
"Macro dapat memanggil dirinya sendiri dan macro lain, yang berguna untuk "
"beberapa pola desain macro yang lebih lanjut yang akan dibahas kemudian."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In standard Rust, there is some unavoidable syntactic boilerplate when "
"defining functions (the `fn` keyword, specification of arguments and return "
"types, and the body). Using macros, we can reduce this boilerplate for "
"repetitive function definitions to just the tokens that might vary between "
"the repetitive definitions; the resulting boilerplate is only the handful of"
" tokens required to invoke a macro."
msgstr ""
"Dalam Rust standar, ada boilerplate sintaksis yang tidak terhindarkan saat "
"mendefinisikan fungsi (keyword `fn`, spesifikasi argumen dan tipe kembalian,"
" serta body). Dengan macro, kita dapat mengurangi boilerplate untuk definisi"
" fungsi yang berulang menjadi hanya token yang mungkin berbeda di antara "
"definisi-definisi tersebut; boilerplate yang dihasilkan hanyalah beberapa "
"token yang diperlukan untuk memanggil macro."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching/exercise.md
msgid ""
"For example, if we define functions for various math operations (such as "
"`add`, `sub`, and `mul`), their types and general structure will be "
"identical, with only the name and operation varying."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, jika kita mendefinisikan fungsi untuk berbagai operasi "
"matematika (seperti `add`, `sub`, dan `mul`), tipe dan struktur umumnya akan"
" identik, dengan hanya nama dan operasinya yang berbeda."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In some contexts, we might avoid syntactic repetition by passing in "
"closures, e.g. `|a, b| a + b`, but this has the possibility of runtime "
"overhead if the closure is not inlined. Macros can similarly avoid "
"repetition without the possibility of runtime overhead."
msgstr ""
"Dalam beberapa konteks, kita mungkin menghindari pengulangan sintaksis "
"dengan meneruskan closure, misalnya `|a, b| a + b`, tetapi ini berpotensi "
"menimbulkan overhead runtime jika closure tidak di-inline. Macro juga dapat "
"menghindari pengulangan tanpa kemungkinan overhead runtime."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will implement a macro called `define_op!` to generate"
" arithmetic function definitions using pattern matching on identifiers and "
"operator tokens."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda akan mengimplementasikan macro bernama `define_op!` "
"untuk menghasilkan definisi fungsi aritmetika menggunakan pattern matching "
"pada identifier dan token operator."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Recall that matching on arbitrary tokens in the input is achieved with meta-"
"variables, introduced via `$`, a variable name, and a fragment specifier, "
"e.g. `$var: ident` or `$e: expr`. We will cover the various fragment "
"specifiers in detail in the coming sections."
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa pencocokan token arbitrer pada input dilakukan dengan meta-"
"variabel, yang diperkenalkan melalui `$`, nama variabel, dan fragment "
"specifier, misalnya `$var: ident` atau `$e: expr`. Kami akan membahas "
"berbagai fragment specifier secara terperinci pada bagian berikutnya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/pattern-matching/exercise.md
msgid "The syntax for `define_op!` should support accept input like this:"
msgstr "Sintaks untuk `define_op!` seharusnya mendukung input seperti ini:"

