#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"**Fragment specifiers** tell the macro compiler what category of syntax to "
"expect and capture as a meta-variable. Here are the most commonly used "
"specifiers:"
msgstr ""
"**Fragment specifier** memberi tahu compiler macro kategori sintaks apa yang"
" diharapkan dan ditangkap sebagai meta-variabel. Berikut specifier yang "
"paling umum digunakan:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`ident`: An identifier (i.e., variable or item names such as `foo` or `_x`)."
msgstr ""
"`ident`: Identifier (yaitu, nama variabel atau item seperti `foo` atau "
"`_x`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`expr`: A single expression (e.g., `2 + 2`, `a.method()`, `match x { ... "
"}`)."
msgstr ""
"`expr`: Satu expression (misalnya, `2 + 2`, `a.method()`, `match x { ... "
"}`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`literal`: A literal value (e.g., `\"hello\"`, `42`, `true`, or `-4.0_f32`)."
msgstr ""
"`literal`: Nilai literal (misalnya, `\"hello\"`, `42`, `true`, atau "
"`-4.0_f32`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid "`stmt`: A single statement without a semicolon (e.g., `let x = 5`)."
msgstr "`stmt`: Satu statement tanpa titik koma (misalnya, `let x = 5`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid "`pat`: A pattern (e.g., `[_, 0, ..]`)."
msgstr "`pat`: Pattern (misalnya, `[_, 0, ..]`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid "`ty`: A type (e.g., `i32`, `Vec<String>`, `&str`)."
msgstr "`ty`: Tipe (misalnya, `i32`, `Vec<String>`, `&str`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`path`: A path of segments separated by `::` (e.g., "
"`std::collections::HashMap`)."
msgstr ""
"`path`: Path berisi segmen yang dipisahkan `::` (misalnya, "
"`std::collections::HashMap`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`item`: A complete item definition (e.g., `fn foo() {}`, `struct Bar;`)."
msgstr ""
"`item`: Definisi item lengkap (misalnya, `fn foo() {}`, `struct Bar;`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`tt`: A single token tree (recall that this is either a single token or a "
"bracketed token group)."
msgstr ""
"`tt`: Satu token tree (ingat bahwa ini adalah satu token tunggal atau grup "
"token dalam kurung)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid "Less common specifiers include:"
msgstr "Specifier yang lebih jarang digunakan meliputi:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid "`lifetime`: A lifetime like `'a`."
msgstr "`lifetime`: Lifetime seperti `'a`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`block`: A block of statements enclosed in braces (e.g., `{ let x = 5; x "
"}`)."
msgstr ""
"`block`: Block statement yang diapit kurung kurawal (misalnya, `{ let x = 5;"
" x }`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`vis`: An optional visibility specifier in an item, e.g. `pub` or "
"`pub(crate)`, or nothing."
msgstr ""
"`vis`: Specifier visibilitas opsional pada suatu item, misalnya `pub` atau "
"`pub(crate)`, atau tidak ada."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"`meta`: The possible _contents_ of a `#[...]` attribute (not the full "
"attribute with hash and brackets)."
msgstr ""
"`meta`: Kemungkinan _isi_ atribut `#[...]` (bukan atribut lengkap dengan "
"tanda pagar dan kurung)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"Explain that fragment specifiers act like type annotations for macro "
"parameters. They restrict what tokens can match."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa fragment specifier berperan seperti anotasi tipe untuk "
"parameter macro. Specifier membatasi token apa yang dapat cocok."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"For example, if you use `$x:expr`, the input must be parsable as a valid "
"Rust expression."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, jika Anda menggunakan `$x:expr`, input harus dapat diurai "
"sebagai expression Rust yang valid."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"When the macro is expanded, the compiler inserts the matched AST fragment "
"directly, which guarantees semantic structure and operator precedence."
msgstr ""
"Saat macro diperluas, compiler menyisipkan fragmen AST yang cocok secara "
"langsung, yang menjamin struktur semantik dan prioritas operator."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"There is overlap between a number of these specifiers, e.g. we could write "
"our own pattern for blocks using `stmt` instead of using `block` directly. "
"In general, try to reach for the most semantically appropriate fragment "
"specifier where possible, which will catch more syntactic edge cases and "
"integrate more seamlessly into the language."
msgstr ""
"Ada tumpang tindih antara sejumlah specifier ini, misalnya kita dapat "
"menulis pattern sendiri untuk block menggunakan `stmt` alih-alih menggunakan"
" `block` secara langsung. Secara umum, usahakan memilih fragment specifier "
"yang paling sesuai secara semantik bila memungkinkan, karena akan menangkap "
"lebih banyak kasus tepi sintaksis dan berintegrasi lebih mulus dengan "
"bahasa."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers.md
msgid ""
"There are some additional, obscure fragment specifiers such as `expr_2021` "
"and `pat_param`."
msgstr ""
"Ada beberapa fragment specifier tambahan yang jarang diketahui, seperti "
"`expr_2021` dan `pat_param`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will implement a macro named `pair!` that takes a "
"single syntactic element and doubles it into a tuple pair containing two of "
"that element: `(x, x)`."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda akan mengimplementasikan macro bernama `pair!` yang "
"menerima satu elemen sintaksis dan menggandakannya menjadi pasangan tuple "
"yang berisi dua elemen tersebut: `(x, x)`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Your `pair!` macro should work across three different syntactic contexts:"
msgstr ""
"Macro `pair!` Anda seharusnya berfungsi dalam tiga konteks sintaksis "
"berbeda:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid "**Types:** `pair!(i32)` expands to `(i32, i32)`."
msgstr "**Tipe:** `pair!(i32)` diperluas menjadi `(i32, i32)`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"**Patterns:** `pair!(7)` and `pair!(_)` expand to `(7, 7)` and `(_, _)`, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""
"**Pattern:** `pair!(7)` dan `pair!(_)` diperluas menjadi `(7, 7)` dan `(_, "
"_)`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid "**Expressions:** `pair!(1 + 2)` expands to `(1 + 2, 1 + 2)`."
msgstr "**Expression:** `pair!(1 + 2)` diperluas menjadi `(1 + 2, 1 + 2)`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Define the `pair!` macro with rules for types (`ty`), patterns (`pat`), and "
"expressions (`expr`)."
msgstr ""
"Definisikan macro `pair!` dengan rule untuk tipe (`ty`), pattern (`pat`), "
"dan expression (`expr`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Order the rules appropriately so that type names, patterns, and expressions "
"are correctly captured."
msgstr ""
"Urutkan rule dengan tepat agar nama tipe, pattern, dan expression tertangkap"
" dengan benar."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
msgid "// TODO: Implement the `pair!` macro.\n"
msgstr "// TODO: Implement the `pair!` macro.\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/exercise.md
