#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/solution.md
msgid ""
"Here is the implementation of the `pair!` macro using the `ty`, `pat`, and "
"`expr` fragment specifiers:"
msgstr ""
"Berikut implementasi macro `pair!` menggunakan fragment specifier `ty`, "
"`pat`, dan `expr`:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Context Flexibility:** Because declarative macros can expand in type, "
"pattern, and expression positions, a single macro like `pair!` can be used "
"in different locations in a codebase with the specific meaning varying based"
" on its argument."
msgstr ""
"**Fleksibilitas Konteks:** Karena macro deklaratif dapat diperluas pada "
"posisi tipe, pattern, dan expression, satu macro seperti `pair!` dapat "
"digunakan di berbagai lokasi dalam basis kode dengan makna spesifik yang "
"bervariasi menurut argumennya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/fragment-specifiers/solution.md
msgid ""
"There is something subtle happening here: the expansion depends on the "
"input, not the context: `pair!(7)` always expands into a pattern, because "
"`pat` is the first pattern that can match the token `7`. The expression "
"invocation passes an `as` cast, which cannot appear in patterns."
msgstr ""
"Ada hal halus yang terjadi di sini: ekspansi bergantung pada input, bukan "
"konteks: `pair!(7)` selalu diperluas menjadi pattern, karena `pat` adalah "
"pattern pertama yang dapat mencocokkan token `7`. Pemanggilan expression "
"meneruskan cast `as`, yang tidak dapat muncul dalam pattern."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid ""
"Declarative macros can match and expand lists of items of arbitrary length. "
"This is defined using the repetition syntax on both the left and right sides"
" of the match rules:"
msgstr ""
"Macro deklaratif dapat mencocokkan dan memperluas daftar item dengan panjang"
" arbitrer. Ini didefinisikan menggunakan sintaks repetisi pada sisi kiri dan"
" kanan rule pencocokan:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "`$( ... ) SEPARATOR OPERATOR`"
msgstr "`$( ... ) SEPARATOR OPERATOR`"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid ""
"**Separator:** An optional token separating each matched item (typically `,`"
" or `;`)."
msgstr ""
"**Separator:** Token opsional yang memisahkan setiap item yang cocok "
"(biasanya `,` atau `;`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "**Operators:**"
msgstr "**Operator:**"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "`*`: Match zero or more repetitions."
msgstr "`*`: Cocokkan nol atau lebih repetisi."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "`+`: Match one or more repetitions."
msgstr "`+`: Cocokkan satu atau lebih repetisi."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "`?`: Match zero or one (optional)."
msgstr "`?`: Cocokkan nol atau satu (opsional)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "// Match one or more expressions separated by commas:\n"
msgstr "// Match one or more expressions separated by commas:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "// Expand the repetition:\n"
msgstr "// Expand the repetition:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "\"Value: {}\""
msgstr "\"Value: {}\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid ""
"Explain that the repetition block on the right-hand side `$( ... )*` must "
"contain the exact meta-variables defined inside the left-hand side's "
"repetition block."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa block repetisi di sisi kanan `$( ... )*` harus berisi meta-"
"variabel yang sama persis dengan yang didefinisikan di dalam block repetisi "
"sisi kiri."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid ""
"Note that the separator on the left-hand side (the comma `,` in `$( "
"$val:expr ),+`), which is used to parse the input stream, may differ from "
"that used on the right-hand side to join elements in the output stream. "
"Here, the output separator is empty, resulting in sequential statements."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa separator di sisi kiri (koma `,` pada `$( $val:expr ),+`), "
"yang digunakan untuk mengurai stream input, dapat berbeda dari separator "
"yang digunakan di sisi kanan untuk menggabungkan elemen dalam stream output."
" Di sini, separator output kosong, sehingga menghasilkan statement "
"berurutan."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid "You can use any punctuation token (except delimiters) as a separator."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menggunakan token tanda baca apa pun (kecuali delimiter) sebagai "
"separator."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md
msgid ""
"Most syntactic constructs in Rust itself accept separators as terminators as"
" well. To allow a trailing separator with repetition syntax, an optional "
"separator may be accepted explicitly after a `*` or `+` repetition operator:"
" `$($e:expr),+ $(,)?`"
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar konstruk sintaksis di Rust sendiri juga menerima separator "
"sebagai terminator. Untuk mengizinkan separator di akhir dengan sintaks "
"repetisi, separator opsional dapat diterima secara eksplisit setelah "
"operator repetisi `*` atau `+`: `$($e:expr),+ $(,)?`"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In the earlier pattern matching exercise, you created a `define_op!` macro "
"that defined a single binary operation for `i32` at a time."
msgstr ""
"Pada latihan pattern matching sebelumnya, Anda membuat macro `define_op!` "
"yang mendefinisikan satu operasi biner untuk `i32` dalam satu waktu."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will generalize that concept into a `define_ops!` "
"macro using the repetition constructs of macro matchers. The new macro "
"should allow implementing an arbitrary number of `std::ops` traits for a "
"generic wrapper type across multiple underlying numeric types in a single "
"macro invocation."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda akan menggeneralisasi konsep tersebut menjadi macro "
"`define_ops!` menggunakan konstruk repetisi pada matcher macro. Macro baru "
"seharusnya memungkinkan pengimplementasian sejumlah trait `std::ops` secara "
"arbitrer untuk tipe wrapper generic pada beberapa tipe numerik dasar dalam "
"satu pemanggilan macro."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid "The desired macro syntax is:"
msgstr "Sintaks macro yang diinginkan adalah:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid ""
"This invocation should implement `std::ops::Add`, `std::ops::Sub`, and "
"`std::ops::Mul` for `Scalar<i32>`, `Scalar<f32>`, and `Scalar<f64>`."
msgstr ""
"Pemanggilan ini seharusnya mengimplementasikan `std::ops::Add`, "
"`std::ops::Sub`, dan `std::ops::Mul` untuk `Scalar<i32>`, `Scalar<f32>`, dan"
" `Scalar<f64>`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Given a wrapper struct `#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)] struct Scalar<T>(pub "
"T);`, implement the `define_ops!` macro."
msgstr ""
"Diberikan struct wrapper `#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)] struct Scalar<T>(pub "
"T);`, implementasikan macro `define_ops!`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Parse a comma-separated list of types (`$( $t:ty ),+`) followed by a colon "
"(`:`)."
msgstr ""
"Urai daftar tipe yang dipisahkan koma (`$( $t:ty ),+`) diikuti titik dua "
"(`:`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Parse a comma-separated list of trait mappings (`$( $trait_name:ident :: "
"$fn_name:ident => $op:tt ),*`)."
msgstr ""
"Urai daftar pemetaan trait yang dipisahkan koma (`$( $trait_name:ident :: "
"$fn_name:ident => $op:tt ),*`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In the macro expansion, use nested repetition `$($( ... )*)*` to generate "
"`impl std::ops::$trait_name for Scalar<$t>` blocks."
msgstr ""
"Pada ekspansi macro, gunakan repetisi bersarang `$($( ... )*)*` untuk "
"menghasilkan block `impl std::ops::$trait_name for Scalar<$t>`."

