#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"As your declarative macros become more sophisticated, simple patterns may "
"not be enough to express your intended logic."
msgstr ""
"Saat macro deklaratif Anda menjadi lebih canggih, pattern sederhana mungkin "
"tidak cukup untuk mengekspresikan logika yang Anda maksud."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"Rust programmers have established several design patterns for structuring "
"more complex macros:"
msgstr ""
"Programmer Rust telah menetapkan beberapa pola desain untuk menyusun macro "
"yang lebih kompleks:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"**Optional Parameters:** Using multiple match arms or optional matchers to "
"handle default values."
msgstr ""
"**Parameter Opsional:** Menggunakan beberapa match arm atau matcher opsional"
" untuk menangani nilai default."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"**Named Parameters:** Explicitly labeling parameters at the callsite (e.g., "
"`key=value`) to improve readability."
msgstr ""
"**Parameter Bernama:** Melabeli parameter secara eksplisit di lokasi "
"pemanggilan (misalnya, `key=value`) untuk meningkatkan keterbacaan."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"**Internal Rules:** Prefixing helper match arms with a unique symbol (like "
"`@`) to modularize code."
msgstr ""
"**Aturan Internal:** Memberi awalan simbol unik (seperti `@`) pada match arm"
" helper untuk memodularkan kode."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"**Incremental Token Munchers:** Eating tokens off the front of a stream "
"recursively."
msgstr ""
"**Incremental Token Munchers:** Memakan token dari depan stream secara "
"rekursif."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"**Push-Down Accumulators:** Collecting tokens recursively into a buffer to "
"build a structured output."
msgstr ""
"**Akumulator Push-Down:** Mengumpulkan token secara rekursif ke dalam buffer"
" untuk membangun output terstruktur."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"**TT Bundling:** Grouping multiple arguments inside a single Token Tree to "
"simplify passing them down."
msgstr ""
"**Penggabungan TT:** Mengelompokkan beberapa argumen di dalam satu Token "
"Tree untuk menyederhanakan penerusannya ke bawah."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid "We will consider each of these advanced techniques in turn."
msgstr "Kami akan membahas masing-masing teknik lanjutan ini satu per satu."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"Reassure students that these patterns are standard idioms in advanced Rust "
"code bases, but not necessary for simple macros. A programmer must use their"
" discretion to choose between a complex declarative macro and implementing "
"logic in a procedural macro, which may be more straightforward at the cost "
"of additional ceremony."
msgstr ""
"Yakinkan siswa bahwa pola-pola ini adalah idiom standar dalam basis kode "
"Rust tingkat lanjut, tetapi tidak diperlukan untuk macro sederhana. "
"Programmer harus menggunakan pertimbangannya untuk memilih antara macro "
"deklaratif yang kompleks dan mengimplementasikan logika dalam macro "
"prosedural, yang mungkin lebih lugas dengan konsekuensi penyiapan tambahan."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md
msgid ""
"Explain that because declarative macros don't have standard local variables "
"or mutable state during expansion, recursion and token-level manipulation "
"are the primary ways to achieve complex code generation."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa karena macro deklaratif tidak memiliki variabel lokal standar"
" atau state yang dapat diubah selama ekspansi, rekursi dan manipulasi "
"tingkat token adalah cara utama untuk mencapai pembuatan kode yang kompleks."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid ""
"The `?` repetition operator can be used for optional parameters, but in "
"older Rust editions (2018 and 2015) it must be emulated; this can be done by"
" defining multiple matcher arms that cascade. Their right-hand sides may "
"reuse each other via recursion, which is a common pattern in declarative "
"macros regardless of edition."
msgstr ""
"Operator repetisi `?` dapat digunakan untuk parameter opsional, tetapi pada "
"edisi Rust yang lebih lama (2018 dan 2015) operator ini harus ditiru; hal "
"tersebut dapat dilakukan dengan mendefinisikan beberapa matcher arm yang "
"berjenjang. Sisi kanannya dapat saling menggunakan kembali melalui rekursi, "
"yang merupakan pola umum dalam macro deklaratif terlepas dari edisinya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid "// Single parameter:\n"
msgstr "// Single parameter:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid "// Recurse instead of `println!(\"{}:{}: {}\", file!(), line!(), $msg)`:\n"
msgstr "// Recurse instead of `println!(\"{}:{}: {}\", file!(), line!(), $msg)`:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid "// With optional formatting parameters:\n"
msgstr "// With optional formatting parameters:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid "\"{}:{}: \""
msgstr "\"{}:{}: \""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid "\"my message\""
msgstr "\"my message\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid "\"my message with param {}!\""
msgstr "\"my message with param {}!\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid ""
"Highlight how `concat!` is used at compile time to combine the file/line "
"prefix with the user's log message literal."
msgstr ""
"Soroti bagaimana `concat!` digunakan pada waktu kompilasi untuk "
"menggabungkan prefiks berkas/baris dengan literal pesan log pengguna."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/optional-params.md
msgid ""
"Recall that the order of arms is significant, just like in a `match`. The "
"compiler matches sequentially, and if a broader arm is placed above a "
"narrower one, the narrower arm may never be reached."
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa urutan arm penting, seperti pada `match`. Compiler mencocokkan "
"secara berurutan, dan jika arm yang lebih luas ditempatkan di atas arm yang "
"lebih sempit, arm yang lebih sempit mungkin tidak pernah tercapai."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/named-params.md
msgid ""
"Using literal identifiers as key-value descriptors allows you to build "
"declarative macro APIs with named parameters. For macros with many "
"arguments, this may significantly increase readability at the callsite:"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan identifier literal sebagai deskriptor key-value memungkinkan "
"Anda membangun API macro deklaratif dengan parameter bernama. Untuk macro "
"dengan banyak argumen, ini dapat meningkatkan keterbacaan di lokasi "
"pemanggilan secara signifikan:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/named-params.md
msgid "// Callers pass named parameters:\n"
msgstr "// Callers pass named parameters:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/named-params.md
msgid "// Calls zero()\n"
msgstr "// Calls zero()\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/named-params.md
msgid "// Calls clear()\n"
msgstr "// Calls clear()\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/named-params.md
msgid ""
"**Structural Identifiers:** `type:` and `function:` are matched as literal "
"tokens."
msgstr ""
"**Identifier Struktural:** `type:` dan `function:` dicocokkan sebagai token "
"literal."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/named-params.md
msgid ""
"**Improved Intent:** The callsite clearly documents which identifier is the "
"type and which is the method, instead of relying on positional parameter "
"index ordering."
msgstr ""
"**Maksud yang Lebih Jelas:** Lokasi pemanggilan mendokumentasikan dengan "
"jelas identifier mana yang merupakan tipe dan mana yang merupakan method, "
"alih-alih bergantung pada urutan indeks parameter posisional."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid ""
"A common pattern for implementing complex macros is to define helper arms "
"(often called **internal rules**) prefixed with a unique, non-standard "
"token, such as `@`."
msgstr ""
"Pola umum untuk mengimplementasikan macro kompleks adalah mendefinisikan arm"
" helper (sering disebut **aturan internal**) dengan awalan token unik non-"
"standar, seperti `@`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid ""
"These internal arms are not meant to be called by users, but are used "
"internally by the macro's public entry points to delegate and reuse logic:"
msgstr ""
"Arm internal ini tidak dimaksudkan untuk dipanggil oleh pengguna, tetapi "
"digunakan secara internal oleh entry point publik macro untuk mendelegasikan"
" dan menggunakan kembali logika:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid "// Internal helper rules:\n"
msgstr "// Internal helper rules:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid "\"all-lit: {}\""
msgstr "\"all-lit: {}\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid "\"some-lit: {}\""
msgstr "\"some-lit: {}\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid "// Public entrypoints:\n"
msgstr "// Public entrypoints:\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid "\"format: {} {}\""
msgstr "\"format: {} {}\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid "\"wow\""
msgstr "\"wow\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid "\"non-literal\""
msgstr "\"non-literal\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid ""
"Note that `@` is purely a convention, which works well because `@` cannot "
"begin a standard Rust item or expression, ensuring public users don't "
"accidentally invoke these helper arms."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `@` murni sebuah konvensi, yang berfungsi baik karena `@` "
"tidak dapat memulai item atau expression Rust standar, sehingga pengguna "
"publik tidak akan tanpa sengaja memanggil arm helper tersebut."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md
msgid ""
"Trace the public matcher arms' flow through the recursive call to "
"(`print_literals!`) while selecting the next branch to take using the "
"`@`\\-prefixed tokens."
msgstr ""
"Telusuri alur matcher arm publik melalui pemanggilan rekursif ke "
"(`print_literals!`) sambil memilih cabang berikutnya menggunakan token "
"berawalan `@`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"An **Incremental TT Muncher** is a recursive macro pattern that processes "
"input token streams by \"eating\" (matching) one or more tokens off the "
"front of the stream, and recursively passing the remainder back to itself."
msgstr ""
"**Incremental TT Muncher** adalah pola macro rekursif yang memproses token "
"stream input dengan \"memakan\" (mencocokkan) satu atau lebih token dari "
"depan stream, lalu meneruskan sisanya kembali ke dirinya sendiri secara "
"rekursif."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid "// Base case: Only one method call remains\n"
msgstr "// Base case: Only one method call remains\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid "\"Hello, World\""
msgstr "\"Hello, World\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid "// Expands recursively to: s.len().trailing_zeros()\n"
msgstr "// Expands recursively to: s.len().trailing_zeros()\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid "\"Trailing zeros in length: {}\""
msgstr "\"Trailing zeros in length: {}\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"TT munchers can parse complex custom grammars, but on the other hand, they "
"can be difficult to read and debug. For small embedded DSLs, they are "
"probably the right choice, but for more complex parsers other techniques may"
" be more appropriate."
msgstr ""
"TT muncher dapat mengurai tata bahasa khusus yang kompleks, tetapi di sisi "
"lain, mereka bisa sulit dibaca dan di-debug. Untuk DSL embedded kecil, TT "
"muncher mungkin pilihan yang tepat, tetapi untuk parser yang lebih kompleks,"
" teknik lain mungkin lebih sesuai."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr "Keterbatasan"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"Because the recursive call passes down the entire rest of the input, while "
"each step only removes a fixed-size portion of it, TT munchers are quadratic"
" in the size of their input. For large inputs, compile times can bloat, and "
"you might exceed the compiler's default macro recursion limit."
msgstr ""
"Karena pemanggilan rekursif meneruskan seluruh sisa input, sementara setiap "
"langkah hanya menghapus sebagian input dengan ukuran tetap, TT muncher "
"bersifat kuadratik terhadap ukuran inputnya. Untuk input besar, waktu "
"kompilasi dapat membengkak, dan Anda mungkin melewati batas rekursi macro "
"default compiler."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"There are also some limits around the compiler's built-in follow-set "
"restrictions (on which fragment specifiers are allowed immediately preceding"
" a trailing `tt`), needed to prevent parser ambiguity. If we follow the "
"pattern of sticking to `tt` matchers on the left, we mostly avoid this "
"limitation."
msgstr ""
"Ada juga beberapa batasan seputar restriksi follow-set bawaan compiler "
"(mengenai fragment specifier mana yang diizinkan tepat sebelum `tt` di "
"akhir), yang diperlukan untuk mencegah ambiguitas parser. Jika kita "
"mengikuti pola dengan tetap menggunakan matcher `tt` di sisi kiri, sebagian "
"besar batasan ini dapat dihindari."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"Explain that the `tt` specifier is key here because it matches any single "
"token tree (including identifiers, literals, or bracketed groups), allowing "
"the recursive call to accept \"anything else\" in `$tail`."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa specifier `tt` menjadi kunci di sini karena mencocokkan token"
" tree tunggal apa pun (termasuk identifier, literal, atau grup dalam "
"kurung), sehingga pemanggilan rekursif dapat menerima \"apa pun sisanya\" "
"pada `$tail`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"Note how `chain!(s, len, trailing_zeros)` matches the recursive case, "
"expanding to `chain!(s.len(), trailing_zeros)`, which then matches the base "
"case, expanding to `s.len().trailing_zeros()`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bagaimana `chain!(s, len, trailing_zeros)` mencocokkan kasus "
"rekursif, diperluas menjadi `chain!(s.len(), trailing_zeros)`, yang kemudian"
" mencocokkan kasus dasar dan diperluas menjadi `s.len().trailing_zeros()`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"Warn about rule ordering: a repeated `tt` matcher will also match a single "
"`tt`, so rules expecting the latter should come first."
msgstr ""
"Peringatkan tentang urutan rule: matcher `tt` yang diulang juga akan "
"mencocokkan satu `tt`, sehingga rule yang mengharapkan yang terakhir harus "
"diletakkan lebih dahulu."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers.md
msgid ""
"Discuss tradeoffs: if a macro is complex enough to require a TT muncher, "
"there is a chance it may be better expressed as a procedural macro."
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan trade-off: jika macro cukup kompleks hingga memerlukan TT "
"muncher, ada kemungkinan lebih baik mengekspresikannya sebagai macro "
"prosedural."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will create an incremental TT muncher macro called "
"`turtle_directions!`."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda akan membuat macro TT muncher inkremental bernama "
"`turtle_directions!`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Your macro will parse a domain-specific language (DSL) for turtle graphics "
"instructions which maintains its old-school style by omitting any "
"punctuation between instructions. This DSL will be used to construct a "
"`cons`\\-list-style `TurtleProgram` value."
msgstr ""
"Macro Anda akan mengurai domain-specific language (DSL) untuk instruksi "
"grafika turtle yang mempertahankan gaya old-school dengan menghilangkan "
"tanda baca apa pun di antara instruksi. DSL ini akan digunakan untuk "
"membangun nilai `TurtleProgram` bergaya `cons`\\-list."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid "Turtle Operation DSL"
msgstr "DSL Operasi Turtle"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The `turtle_directions!` macro should parse the following unpunctuated "
"commands:"
msgstr ""
"Macro `turtle_directions!` seharusnya mengurai perintah tanpa tanda baca "
"berikut:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"`FWD n`: moves forward by `n` steps (`TurtleProgram::Forward(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""
"`FWD n`: bergerak maju sejauh `n` langkah (`TurtleProgram::Forward(n, "
"rest)`)"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"`REV n`: moves backward by `n` steps (`TurtleProgram::Reverse(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""
"`REV n`: bergerak mundur sejauh `n` langkah (`TurtleProgram::Reverse(n, "
"rest)`)"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid "`LEFT n`: turns left by `n` degrees (`TurtleProgram::Left(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""
"`LEFT n`: berbelok ke kiri sebesar `n` derajat (`TurtleProgram::Left(n, "
"rest)`)"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"`RIGHT n`: turns right by `n` degrees (`TurtleProgram::Right(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""
"`RIGHT n`: berbelok ke kanan sebesar `n` derajat (`TurtleProgram::Right(n, "
"rest)`)"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid "`PEN UP`: lifts the pen (`TurtleProgram::PenUp(rest)`)"
msgstr "`PEN UP`: mengangkat pena (`TurtleProgram::PenUp(rest)`)"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid "`PEN DOWN`: lowers the pen (`TurtleProgram::PenDown(rest)`)"
msgstr "`PEN DOWN`: menurunkan pena (`TurtleProgram::PenDown(rest)`)"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"`RED` and `BLACK`: set the pen color (`TurtleProgram::SetColor(color, "
"rest)`)"
msgstr ""
"`RED` dan `BLACK`: mengatur warna pena (`TurtleProgram::SetColor(color, "
"rest)`)"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Where `rest` is a `Box<TurtleProgram>` representing the remaining steps of "
"the program."
msgstr ""
"Dengan `rest` adalah `Box<TurtleProgram>` yang merepresentasikan langkah-"
"langkah program yang tersisa."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid "Implement the `turtle_directions!` macro in the following program:"
msgstr "Implementasikan macro `turtle_directions!` pada program berikut:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid "// TODO: Implement the `turtle_directions!` macro.\n"
msgstr "// TODO: Implement the `turtle_directions!` macro.\n"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Highlight how matching on specific keyword token sequences (e.g. `PEN UP`, "
"`RED`, or `FWD n`) at the head of the token stream allows parsing each "
"command according to the number and kind of expected tokens to follow."
msgstr ""
"Soroti bagaimana pencocokan rangkaian token keyword tertentu (misalnya `PEN "
"UP`, `RED`, atau `FWD n`) di awal token stream memungkinkan penguraian "
"setiap perintah sesuai jumlah dan jenis token yang diharapkan mengikutinya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid ""
"Here is the implementation of the `turtle_directions!` TT muncher macro:"
msgstr "Berikut implementasi macro TT muncher `turtle_directions!`:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid "The macro processes the input sequence incrementally:"
msgstr "Macro memproses rangkaian input secara inkremental:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid ""
"Each rule matches a specific command pattern at the head of the token stream"
" (such as `FWD $n:tt`, `PEN UP`, or `PEN DOWN`)."
msgstr ""
"Setiap rule mencocokkan pattern perintah tertentu di awal token stream "
"(seperti `FWD $n:tt`, `PEN UP`, atau `PEN DOWN`)."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid ""
"The matched command is wrapped into its corresponding `TurtleProgram` "
"variant, passing `Box::new(turtle_directions!($($rest)*))` as the rest of "
"the program."
msgstr ""
"Perintah yang cocok dibungkus ke dalam varian `TurtleProgram` yang sesuai, "
"dengan meneruskan `Box::new(turtle_directions!($($rest)*))` sebagai sisa "
"program."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid ""
"Recursion continues on the remaining tokens `$($rest:tt)*` until no tokens "
"remain, matching the empty `()` base case and giving `TurtleProgram::Done`."
msgstr ""
"Rekursi berlanjut pada token yang tersisa `$($rest:tt)*` hingga tidak ada "
"token tersisa, mencocokkan kasus dasar `()` yang kosong dan menghasilkan "
"`TurtleProgram::Done`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid ""
"Note that `$n:tt` is used for numeric arguments because the built-in follow-"
"set rules prohibit `$($rest:tt)*` from directly following `$n:expr` without "
"punctuation."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `$n:tt` digunakan untuk argumen numerik karena aturan "
"follow-set bawaan melarang `$($rest:tt)*` mengikuti `$n:expr` secara "
"langsung tanpa tanda baca."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid "Extra Credit"
msgstr "Kredit Tambahan"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/solution.md
msgid ""
"Consider how the definition of this macro could be further factored to avoid"
" the repetition of `TurtleProgram::$OPERATION($ARG, "
"Box::new(turtle_directions!(` in most of its arms."
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan bagaimana definisi macro ini dapat difaktorkan lebih lanjut "
"untuk menghindari pengulangan `TurtleProgram::$OPERATION($ARG, "
"Box::new(turtle_directions!(` pada sebagian besar arm-nya."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid ""
"Because all function-like macro calls must evaluate to valid Rust syntax "
"(most frequently, expressions), we cannot directly generate and return loose"
" token lists like `a, b, c` from helper macros to be embedded inside "
"templates."
msgstr ""
"Karena semua pemanggilan macro mirip fungsi harus menghasilkan sintaks Rust "
"yang valid (paling sering expression), kita tidak dapat secara langsung "
"menghasilkan dan mengembalikan daftar token lepas seperti `a, b, c` dari "
"macro helper untuk disematkan di dalam template."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid ""
"A **Push-Down Accumulator** is a pattern designed to bypass this expression "
"constraint by recursively accumulating tokens inside a dedicated buffer "
"structure (such as a bracketed list) and feeding that buffer into subsequent"
" macro calls:"
msgstr ""
"**Akumulator Push-Down** adalah pola yang dirancang untuk melewati batasan "
"expression ini dengan mengakumulasi token secara rekursif di dalam struktur "
"buffer khusus (seperti daftar dalam kurung) dan meneruskan buffer tersebut "
"ke pemanggilan macro berikutnya:"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid "\"hi!\""
msgstr "\"hi!\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid "\"Array: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"Array: {:?}\""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid ""
"**Token Accumulation:** The right-hand side `[]` buffer accumulates "
"expression clones sequentially."
msgstr ""
"**Akumulasi Token:** Buffer `[]` di sisi kanan mengakumulasi clone "
"expression secara berurutan."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid ""
"**AST Soundness:** Every intermediate macro recursion is structured as a "
"valid macro call expression, which keeps the AST parser happy."
msgstr ""
"**Soundness AST:** Setiap rekursi macro perantara terstruktur sebagai "
"expression pemanggilan macro yang valid, sehingga parser AST tetap senang."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid ""
"Explain why helper macros like `params!() => { \"foo\", \"bar\" }` fail: the"
" compiler expects the macro to expand into a single valid expression, but a "
"list of comma-separated expressions is not a single expression."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan mengapa macro helper seperti `params!() => { \"foo\", \"bar\" }` "
"gagal: compiler mengharapkan macro diperluas menjadi satu expression valid, "
"tetapi daftar expression yang dipisahkan koma bukanlah satu expression."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid ""
"Show how the push-down accumulator avoids this: `init_array!` delegates to "
"`accum!`, which keeps passing a structured macro call containing a growing "
"list inside `[]` until it reaches the base case `[0, ...]`, which finally "
"returns the completed array `[...]`."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bagaimana akumulator push-down menghindari hal ini: `init_array!` "
"mendelegasikan ke `accum!`, yang terus meneruskan pemanggilan macro "
"terstruktur berisi daftar yang bertambah di dalam `[]` hingga mencapai kasus"
" dasar `[0, ...]`, yang akhirnya mengembalikan array lengkap `[...]`."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md
msgid ""
"Mention that this pattern is exceptionally powerful for complex template "
"formatting, but has a high cognitive overhead to write and maintain."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa pola ini sangat ampuh untuk pemformatan template yang "
"kompleks, tetapi memiliki beban kognitif yang tinggi untuk ditulis dan "
"dipelihara."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md
msgid "Exercise: Turtle Graphics Vector"
msgstr "Latihan: Vector Grafika Turtle"

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In the previous exercise, you built a recursively nested `TurtleProgram` "
"using a TT muncher."
msgstr ""
"Pada latihan sebelumnya, Anda membangun `TurtleProgram` bersarang secara "
"rekursif menggunakan TT muncher."

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will adapt the `turtle_directions!` macro to use a "
"**Push-Down Accumulator**. Instead of nesting enum variants, your macro will"
" accumulate parsed `TurtleOp` variants in a bracketed buffer `[ "
"$($acc:expr),* ]` as it munches the input stream, ultimately constructing a "
"`Vec<TurtleOp>`."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda akan menyesuaikan macro `turtle_directions!` untuk "
"menggunakan **Akumulator Push-Down**. Alih-alih menyusun varian enum secara "
"bersarang, macro Anda akan mengakumulasi varian `TurtleOp` yang telah diurai"
" ke dalam buffer dalam kurung `[ $($acc:expr),* ]` saat memakan stream "
"input, dan akhirnya membangun `Vec<TurtleOp>`."

