msgid "// Unhygienic: intent is to leak `local` to callsite\n"
msgstr "// Unhygienic: intent is to leak `local` to callsite\n"

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"In Rust, **neither of these examples compile**. Both produce the error: "
"`error[E0425]: cannot find value 'local' in this scope`."
msgstr ""
"Di Rust, **kedua contoh ini tidak dapat dikompilasi**. Keduanya menghasilkan"
" error: `error[E0425]: cannot find value 'local' in this scope`."

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"Rust's macro system treats variables hygienically, protecting from silent "
"namespace pollution."
msgstr ""
"Sistem macro Rust memperlakukan variabel secara higienis, melindungi dari "
"pencemaran namespace yang terjadi diam-diam."

#: src/macros/hygiene/what-is-hygiene.md
msgid "However, declarative macros in Rust are not fully hygienic!"
msgstr "Namun, macro deklaratif di Rust tidak sepenuhnya higienis!"

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid "Declarative macros in Rust are partially hygienic."
msgstr "Macro deklaratif di Rust bersifat sebagian higienis."

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"They are hygienic with respect to: local variables, parameters, loop labels,"
" and the special `$crate` variable."
msgstr ""
"Macro tersebut higienis terhadap: variabel lokal, parameter, label loop, dan"
" variabel khusus `$crate`."

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"They are **not** hygienic with respect to: items, types, methods, and "
"traits."
msgstr ""
"Macro tersebut **tidak** higienis terhadap: item, tipe, method, dan trait."

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr "Alasannya"

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"Frequently, rust macros are used as shorthand to refer to existing types and"
" traits, e.g. when defining `impl`s. In this situation, hygienic macros "
"would always need to accept all relevant items as arguments, imposing a "
"floor beneath which we could not decrease lexical boilerplate."
msgstr ""
"Sering kali, macro Rust digunakan sebagai singkatan untuk merujuk tipe dan "
"trait yang sudah ada, misalnya saat mendefinisikan `impl`. Dalam situasi "
"ini, macro higienis akan selalu perlu menerima semua item relevan sebagai "
"argumen, sehingga menetapkan batas bawah yang tidak dapat kita turunkan lagi"
" untuk boilerplate leksikal."

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"On the other hand, hygiene helps us write reliable code, so it is desirable "
"for any internal operations that a macro may want to perform. Luckily for "
"us, Rust does provide a solution for hygienic references to items."
msgstr ""
"Di sisi lain, hygiene membantu kita menulis kode yang andal, sehingga "
"diinginkan untuk operasi internal apa pun yang mungkin ingin dilakukan "
"macro. Untungnya, Rust memang menyediakan solusi untuk referensi item yang "
"higienis."

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid "Example: Non-Hygienic Paths"
msgstr "Contoh: Path yang Tidak Higienis"

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"// Item reference is not hygienic! This macro may refer to a different \"print\"\n"
"// function when invoked in different contexts.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Item reference is not hygienic! This macro may refer to a different \"print\"\n"
"// function when invoked in different contexts.\n"

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid "\"::a::print()\""
msgstr "\"::a::print()\""

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid "\"::print()\""
msgstr "\"::print()\""

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"The two expansions of the `call_print` macro refer to different items, "
"depending on the calling context. This could be useful as mere shorthand, "
"but is not robustly useful for referring to one particular item."
msgstr ""
"Dua ekspansi macro `call_print` merujuk item yang berbeda, bergantung pada "
"konteks pemanggilannya. Ini mungkin berguna sebagai singkatan semata, tetapi"
" tidak cukup andal untuk merujuk satu item tertentu."

#: src/macros/hygiene/rust-macro-hygiene.md
msgid ""
"Explain that to enforce hygiene on local variables, the compiler keeps track"
" of \"syntax contexts.\" A local variable defined inside the macro has a "
"different syntax context than a variable of the same name defined outside, "
"which prevents collisions."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa untuk menegakkan hygiene pada variabel lokal, compiler "
"melacak \"syntax context\". Variabel lokal yang didefinisikan di dalam macro"
" memiliki syntax context berbeda dari variabel bernama sama yang "
"didefinisikan di luar, sehingga mencegah tabrakan."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"**Procedural macros** are far more powerful than declarative macros. Instead"
" of matching syntax templates, they are literal compiler plugins:"
msgstr ""
"**Macro prosedural** jauh lebih ampuh daripada macro deklaratif. Alih-alih "
"mencocokkan template sintaks, macro ini benar-benar plugin compiler:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"They are implemented as functions that receive one or two **token streams** "
"and return a **token stream**."
msgstr ""
"Macro ini diimplementasikan sebagai fungsi yang menerima satu atau dua "
"**token stream** dan mengembalikan satu **token stream**."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid "They are written in standard, fully featured Rust."
msgstr "Macro ini ditulis dalam Rust standar dengan fitur lengkap."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"They have complete programmatic access to the incoming token stream, "
"allowing you to parse, modify, or generate complex code structures."
msgstr ""
"Macro ini memiliki akses programatik penuh ke token stream yang masuk, "
"sehingga Anda dapat mengurai, mengubah, atau menghasilkan struktur kode yang"
" kompleks."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"They require a dedicated library crate configured with `proc-macro = true` "
"in its `Cargo.toml`."
msgstr ""
"Macro ini memerlukan crate library khusus yang dikonfigurasi dengan `proc-"
"macro = true` pada `Cargo.toml`-nya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"We will explore how procedural macros are defined, how they compile, and how"
" to write them."
msgstr ""
"Kami akan menelusuri cara macro prosedural didefinisikan, cara kompilasinya,"
" dan cara menulisnya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Explain that procedural macros are called \"procedural\" because they "
"execute standard Rust procedures (functions) to transform code at compile "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa macro prosedural disebut \"procedural\" karena mengeksekusi "
"prosedur Rust standar (fungsi) untuk mentransformasi kode pada waktu "
"kompilasi."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Emphasize that because they are compiled as libraries and loaded by the "
"compiler during build time, they have a heavier impact on compilation speed "
"compared to declarative macros."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa karena dikompilasi sebagai library dan dimuat oleh compiler "
"selama waktu build, macro ini berdampak lebih berat pada kecepatan kompilasi"
" dibandingkan macro deklaratif."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md
msgid ""
"This slide serves as a transition into the detailed mechanics of procedural "
"macros."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini menjadi transisi menuju mekanisme terperinci macro prosedural."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/basics.md
msgid ""
"To write a procedural macro, you must define it in a separate library crate "
"dedicated solely to macros."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menulis macro prosedural, Anda harus mendefinisikannya dalam crate "
"library terpisah yang khusus untuk macro."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/basics.md
msgid "Cargo.toml configuration"
msgstr "Konfigurasi Cargo.toml"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/basics.md
msgid "Compiler Plugin Architecture"
msgstr "Arsitektur Plugin Compiler"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/basics.md
msgid ""
"**Build-Time Execution:** The macro crate is compiled first as a dynamic "
"library. The compiler loads this library and runs the macro functions during"
" the compilation of the consuming crate."
msgstr ""
"**Eksekusi Waktu Build:** Crate macro dikompilasi terlebih dahulu sebagai "
"library dinamis. Compiler memuat library ini dan menjalankan fungsi macro "
"selama kompilasi crate yang mengonsumsinya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/basics.md
msgid ""
"**Dependency Isolation:** Because macro functions execute during "
"compilation, any dependencies imported by your macro crate (like parsing "
"helper libraries) are **build-time dependencies**, and are not compiled into"
" the final client binary."
msgstr ""
"**Isolasi Dependensi:** Karena fungsi macro dieksekusi selama kompilasi, "
"dependensi apa pun yang diimpor crate macro Anda (seperti library helper "
"parsing) adalah **dependensi waktu build**, dan tidak dikompilasi ke binary "
"client akhir."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/basics.md
msgid ""
"Explain that because the macro code runs _inside_ the compiler, it cannot be"
" mixed into standard library crates. If you try to define a procedural macro"
" in a standard crate, the compiler will emit a compile-time error."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa karena kode macro berjalan _di dalam_ compiler, kode tersebut"
" tidak dapat dicampur ke dalam crate library standar. Jika Anda mencoba "
"mendefinisikan macro prosedural dalam crate standar, compiler akan "
"mengeluarkan error waktu kompilasi."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/basics.md
msgid ""
"Point out that this architecture guarantees that procedural macro logic can "
"leverage the complete Rust standard library (file access, networking, multi-"
"threading) to perform compile-time tasks, though doing so should be kept to "
"a minimum to keep compiles fast and secure."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bahwa arsitektur ini menjamin logika macro prosedural dapat "
"memanfaatkan standard library Rust secara lengkap (akses berkas, jaringan, "
"multi-threading) untuk menjalankan tugas waktu kompilasi, meskipun "
"penggunaannya sebaiknya diminimalkan agar kompilasi tetap cepat dan aman."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Function-like procedural macros** look and feel like declarative macros to"
" the caller, but their implementation is a Rust function decorated with the "
"`#[proc_macro]` attribute:"
msgstr ""
"**Macro prosedural mirip fungsi** tampak dan terasa seperti macro deklaratif"
" bagi pemanggil, tetapi implementasinya adalah fungsi Rust yang didekorasi "
"dengan atribut `#[proc_macro]`:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid ""
"// Process input tokens and return output tokens...\n"
"    \"42\""
msgstr ""
"// Process input tokens and return output tokens...\n"
"    \"42\""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid "Key properties:"
msgstr "Properti utama:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid "**Declaration:** Decorated with `#[proc_macro]`."
msgstr "**Deklarasi:** Didekorasi dengan `#[proc_macro]`."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Function Signature:** Must accept a single `TokenStream` (the tokens "
"inside the brackets of the callsite) and return a `TokenStream`."
msgstr ""
"**Signature Fungsi:** Harus menerima satu `TokenStream` (token di dalam "
"kurung pada lokasi pemanggilan) dan mengembalikan `TokenStream`."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid ""
"**Flexible Invocation:** Like other function-like macros, callers can invoke"
" them with any kind of brackets."
msgstr ""
"**Pemanggilan Fleksibel:** Seperti macro mirip fungsi lainnya, pemanggil "
"dapat memanggilnya dengan jenis kurung apa pun."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid ""
"Note that the `input` TokenStream contains only the tokens _inside_ the "
"brackets, not the macro name or the exclamation mark."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa TokenStream `input` hanya berisi token _di dalam_ kurung, "
"bukan nama macro atau tanda seru."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid ""
"Emphasize that function-like procedural macros are useful when you need to "
"parse complex custom DSLs that cannot be expressed easily with declarative "
"`macro_rules!` pattern-matching."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa macro prosedural mirip fungsi berguna ketika Anda perlu "
"mengurai DSL khusus yang kompleks yang tidak dapat diekspresikan dengan "
"mudah menggunakan pattern matching `macro_rules!` deklaratif."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md
msgid "Mention that they may expand to expressions, statements, or items."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa macro ini dapat diperluas menjadi expression, statement, atau"
" item."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md
msgid ""
"**Derive procedural macros** are decorated with the "
"`#[proc_macro_derive(TraitName)]` attribute. They take in the token stream "
"of a type definition and return a token stream containing additional "
"implementations:"
msgstr ""
"**Macro prosedural derive** didekorasi dengan atribut "
"`#[proc_macro_derive(TraitName)]`. Macro ini menerima token stream dari "
"definisi tipe dan mengembalikan token stream yang berisi implementasi "
"tambahan:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md
msgid "// Parse the struct/enum item, generate `MyDebug` implementation...\n"
msgstr "// Parse the struct/enum item, generate `MyDebug` implementation...\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md
msgid ""
"**Additive Output:** The returned token stream is compiled alongside the "
"type definition in the same scope. It does not replace the type definition "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"**Output Aditif:** Token stream yang dikembalikan dikompilasi bersama "
"definisi tipe dalam scope yang sama. Output ini tidak menggantikan definisi "
"tipe itu sendiri."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md
msgid ""
"**Helper Attributes:** Derive macros can declare optional helper attributes "
"that can be used on struct fields or enum variants, configured in the derive"
" declaration: `#[proc_macro_derive(MyTrait, attributes(my_helper))]`"
msgstr ""
"**Helper Attribute:** Macro derive dapat mendeklarasikan helper attribute "
"opsional yang dapat digunakan pada field struct atau varian enum, "
"dikonfigurasi dalam deklarasi derive: `#[proc_macro_derive(MyTrait, "
"attributes(my_helper))]`"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md
msgid ""
"The `item` TokenStream represents the entire struct, enum, or union "
"definition, including its attributes, generic parameters, braces, and "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"TokenStream `item` merepresentasikan seluruh definisi struct, enum, atau "
"union, termasuk atribut, parameter generic, kurung kurawal, dan field-nya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md
msgid ""
"Discuss helper attributes: helper attributes are matched by the derive macro"
" to let users customize the code generation (e.g., `#[my_helper(rename = "
"\"field\")]`)."
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan helper attribute: helper attribute dicocokkan oleh macro derive "
"agar pengguna dapat menyesuaikan pembuatan kode (misalnya, "
"`#[my_helper(rename = \"field\")]`)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md
msgid ""
"Note that the argument to `proc_macro_derive` dictates how this derive macro"
" is imported and triggered, but does not actually constrain which items it "
"generates `impl` blocks for. Some derive macros may impl multiple traits (as"
" does `thiserror::Error`, for example); derive macros must be well behaved "
"and document their effects."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa argumen `proc_macro_derive` menentukan bagaimana macro "
"derive ini diimpor dan dipicu, tetapi tidak benar-benar membatasi item mana "
"yang akan dibuatkan block `impl`. Sebagian macro derive dapat "
"mengimplementasikan beberapa trait (seperti `thiserror::Error`, misalnya); "
"macro derive harus berperilaku baik dan mendokumentasikan efeknya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid ""
"**Attribute procedural macros** are decorated with the "
"`#[proc_macro_attribute]` attribute. They allow you to define custom "
"attributes that completely replace the items they are attached to:"
msgstr ""
"**Macro prosedural atribut** didekorasi dengan atribut "
"`#[proc_macro_attribute]`. Macro ini memungkinkan Anda mendefinisikan "
"atribut khusus yang sepenuhnya menggantikan item yang dilekatinya:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid ""
"// Process parameters in `attr` (e.g., GET, \"/path\")\n"
"    // Process the attached function/item in `item`\n"
"    // Return the new, fully rewritten item...\n"
msgstr ""
"// Process parameters in `attr` (e.g., GET, \"/path\")\n"
"    // Process the attached function/item in `item`\n"
"    // Return the new, fully rewritten item...\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid "**Two Parameters:**"
msgstr "**Dua Parameter:**"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid ""
"`attr`: The token stream containing any metadata parameters passed into the "
"attribute (e.g., `GET, \"/\"` inside `#[route(GET, \"/\")]`)."
msgstr ""
"`attr`: Token stream yang berisi parameter metadata apa pun yang diteruskan "
"ke atribut (misalnya, `GET, \"/\"` di dalam `#[route(GET, \"/\")]`)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid ""
"`item`: The token stream representing the entire attached item (e.g., a "
"function or struct definition)."
msgstr ""
"`item`: Token stream yang merepresentasikan seluruh item yang dilekati "
"(misalnya, definisi fungsi atau struct)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid ""
"**Replacement:** The returned token stream entirely replaces the input "
"`item` in the AST."
msgstr ""
"**Penggantian:** Token stream yang dikembalikan sepenuhnya menggantikan "
"`item` input di AST."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid ""
"Explain that because attribute macros completely replace the input item, you"
" must make sure to output the rewritten item (along with any generated "
"auxiliary code) so that it remains visible to the rest of the program, "
"unless your specific intention is to delete it!"
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa karena macro atribut sepenuhnya menggantikan item input, Anda"
" harus memastikan untuk mengeluarkan item yang telah ditulis ulang (beserta "
"kode bantu yang dihasilkan) agar tetap terlihat oleh bagian program lainnya,"
" kecuali niat spesifik Anda memang menghapusnya!"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/attr.md
msgid ""
"Discuss how popular libraries (such as Axum or Rocket) use attribute macros "
"to register route functions into global dispatch tables, or rewrite "
"signatures for dependency injection."
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan bagaimana library populer (seperti Axum atau Rocket) menggunakan "
"macro atribut untuk mendaftarkan fungsi route ke tabel dispatch global, atau"
" menulis ulang signature untuk dependency injection."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid ""
"Because procedural macros execute during compilation, standard runtime error"
" reporting strategies do not apply. If a macro receives malformed input, it "
"must signal the error to the compiler."
msgstr ""
"Karena macro prosedural dieksekusi selama kompilasi, strategi pelaporan "
"error runtime standar tidak berlaku. Jika macro menerima input yang cacat, "
"macro harus memberi sinyal error kepada compiler."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid "There are two main ways to report errors in procedural macros:"
msgstr "Ada dua cara utama untuk melaporkan error dalam macro prosedural:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid "1. Panicking"
msgstr "1. Panic"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid ""
"If your macro code panics, the compiler will catch the panic, halt "
"compilation, and print the panic message as a compiler error:"
msgstr ""
"Jika kode macro Anda panic, compiler akan menangkap panic tersebut, "
"menghentikan kompilasi, dan mencetak pesan panic sebagai error compiler:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid "\"Invalid struct name\""
msgstr "\"Invalid struct name\""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid ""
"This may occur by default if there are any bugs or programming errors in "
"your procedural macro."
msgstr ""
"Ini dapat terjadi secara default jika ada bug atau kesalahan pemrograman "
"dalam macro prosedural Anda."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid "2. Emitting `compile_error!` (Preferred)"
msgstr "2. Mengeluarkan `compile_error!` (Disarankan)"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid ""
"A more friendly approach is to return a `TokenStream` containing a call to "
"the built-in `compile_error!` macro. This allows the compiler to highlight "
"the exact span where the error occurred:"
msgstr ""
"Pendekatan yang lebih ramah adalah mengembalikan `TokenStream` yang berisi "
"pemanggilan macro bawaan `compile_error!`. Ini memungkinkan compiler "
"menyorot span persis tempat error terjadi:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid "// Returning an explicit compile error TokenStream:\n"
msgstr "// Returning an explicit compile error TokenStream:\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid "\"Expected a valid identifier\""
msgstr "\"Expected a valid identifier\""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid "// Generates compile_error!(\"...\")\n"
msgstr "// Generates compile_error!(\"...\")\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid ""
"Explain that panicking is easy but has a terrible developer experience. It "
"halts the entire compilation and doesn't tell the developer where they made "
"a mistake (the error is tracked to the macro definition site rather than the"
" particular call site)."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa panic mudah dilakukan tetapi memberikan pengalaman developer "
"yang buruk. Panic menghentikan seluruh kompilasi dan tidak memberi tahu "
"developer di mana kesalahannya (error dilacak ke lokasi definisi macro, "
"bukan ke lokasi pemanggilan tertentu)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/errors.md
msgid ""
"Emphasize that emitting `compile_error!` is the standard, idiomatic way to "
"handle user input validation. The error message is attached to a specific "
"`Span` (the location of the bad token), which allows IDEs and compiler error"
" messages to draw a red squiggly line directly under the offending code."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa mengeluarkan `compile_error!` adalah cara standar dan "
"idiomatis untuk menangani validasi input pengguna. Pesan error dilekatkan "
"pada `Span` tertentu (lokasi token yang bermasalah), sehingga IDE dan pesan "
"error compiler dapat menggambar garis bergelombang merah tepat di bawah kode"
" yang bermasalah."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md
msgid ""
"Many of the most popular and foundational libraries in the Rust ecosystem "
"rely heavily on procedural macros to provide elegant, declarative, and type-"
"safe APIs:"
msgstr ""
"Banyak library paling populer dan fundamental di ekosistem Rust sangat "
"bergantung pada macro prosedural untuk menyediakan API yang elegan, "
"deklaratif, dan type-safe:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md
msgid ""
"**Serde (`#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]`):** Automatically generates "
"code to convert Rust types to/from JSON, YAML, or binary formats based on "
"field names and structural nesting."
msgstr ""
"**Serde (`#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]`):** Secara otomatis "
"menghasilkan kode untuk mengonversi tipe Rust ke/dari format JSON, YAML, "
"atau binary berdasarkan nama field dan struktur bersarang."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md
msgid ""
"**Tokio (`#[tokio::main]`):** Sets up runtime environments, wrapping "
"standard main entry points asynchronously."
msgstr ""
"**Tokio (`#[tokio::main]`):** Menyiapkan lingkungan runtime, membungkus "
"entry point main standar secara asinkron."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md
msgid ""
"**Clap (`#[derive(Parser)]`):** Automatically builds complete, robust CLI "
"command-line argument parsers based on struct declarations and doc comments."
msgstr ""
"**Clap (`#[derive(Parser)]`):** Secara otomatis membangun parser argumen "
"command-line CLI yang lengkap dan kokoh berdasarkan deklarasi struct dan doc"
" comment."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md
msgid ""
"**SQLx (`query!`):** Validates SQL query strings against a live database at "
"build time, converting database schemas directly to static Rust types."
msgstr ""
"**SQLx (`query!`):** Memvalidasi string kueri SQL terhadap database aktif "
"pada waktu build, mengonversi skema database langsung menjadi tipe Rust "
"statis."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md
msgid ""
"Highlight the impact of procedural macros for Rust's ergonomics--"
"serialization, for example, requires explicit compiler support in many "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Soroti dampak macro prosedural bagi ergonomi Rust--serialisasi, misalnya, "
"memerlukan dukungan compiler eksplisit di banyak bahasa."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md
msgid ""
"SQLx's compile-time query verification is a prime example of compile-time "
"code validation that is only possible with procedural macros."
msgstr ""
"Verifikasi kueri pada waktu kompilasi dari SQLx adalah contoh utama validasi"
" kode waktu kompilasi yang hanya mungkin dilakukan dengan macro prosedural."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid ""
"Writing procedural macros is basically about learning how to work with the "
"standard helper libraries designed specifically to parse and generate Rust "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Menulis macro prosedural pada dasarnya adalah mempelajari cara bekerja "
"dengan library helper standar yang dirancang khusus untuk mengurai dan "
"menghasilkan kode Rust."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid ""
"Because dealing with raw, low-level `TokenStream`s manually is tedious and "
"difficult, we use a standard suite of specialized helper libraries:"
msgstr ""
"Karena menangani `TokenStream` mentah tingkat rendah secara manual itu "
"melelahkan dan sulit, kami menggunakan rangkaian standar library helper "
"khusus:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid "**`proc_macro`:** Provided by the compiler to interface token streams."
msgstr ""
"**`proc_macro`:** Disediakan oleh compiler untuk berinteraksi dengan token "
"stream."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid ""
"**`proc_macro2`:** Wraps `proc_macro` to allow unit testing and out-of-"
"compiler executions."
msgstr ""
"**`proc_macro2`:** Membungkus `proc_macro` agar unit testing dan eksekusi di"
" luar compiler dapat dilakukan."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid ""
"**`syn`:** A complete parser library that parses Rust token streams into "
"structured Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) structures."
msgstr ""
"**`syn`:** Library parser lengkap yang mengurai token stream Rust menjadi "
"struktur Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) yang terstruktur."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid ""
"**`quote`:** A templated code generation library that turns your Rust "
"structures back into token streams."
msgstr ""
"**`quote`:** Library pembuatan kode berbasis template yang mengubah struktur"
" Rust Anda kembali menjadi token stream."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid "We will look at how each of these crates builds on top of one another."
msgstr ""
"Kami akan melihat bagaimana masing-masing crate ini dibangun di atas satu "
"sama lain."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid ""
"Consider how writing a proc macro is essentially writing a mini-compiler: "
"you parse a string of tokens (lexical analysis), match its structure "
"(parsing), and generate a new string of tokens (transformation and code "
"emission)."
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan bahwa menulis proc macro pada dasarnya adalah menulis compiler"
" mini: Anda mengurai rangkaian token (analisis leksikal), mencocokkan "
"strukturnya (parsing), dan menghasilkan rangkaian token baru (transformasi "
"dan emisi kode)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing.md
msgid ""
"Reassure students that you rarely ever work with raw tokens directly. The "
"`syn` and `quote` crates do 95% of the heavy parsing and formatting work for"
" you, allowing you to write more-readable macro code."
msgstr ""
"Yakinkan siswa bahwa Anda jarang sekali bekerja langsung dengan token "
"mentah. Crate `syn` dan `quote` melakukan 95% pekerjaan parsing dan "
"pemformatan yang berat untuk Anda, sehingga Anda dapat menulis kode macro "
"yang lebih mudah dibaca."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md
msgid ""
"Here is how the standard dependency tree of a modern procedural macro crate "
"is structured:"
msgstr ""
"Berikut struktur pohon dependensi standar dari crate macro prosedural "
"modern:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md
msgid "Each library builds on top of the layer below."
msgstr "Setiap library dibangun di atas lapisan di bawahnya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md
msgid ""
"Using `syn` and `quote` increases macro build times slightly, but greatly "
"simplifies implementation, making macro code safer and much easier to "
"maintain."
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan `syn` dan `quote` sedikit meningkatkan waktu build macro, tetapi"
" sangat menyederhanakan implementasi, membuat kode macro lebih aman dan jauh"
" lebih mudah dipelihara."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md
msgid ""
"Explain that `proc_macro` is provided by the standard distribution, but is "
"restricted to compiler execution."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa `proc_macro` disediakan oleh distribusi standar, tetapi "
"dibatasi untuk eksekusi di dalam compiler."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md
msgid ""
"`proc_macro2` is a standard third-party crate that replicates all "
"`proc_macro` types, but does not depend on the compiler's private internals."
" This is why testing libraries or other tools can work with token streams."
msgstr ""
"`proc_macro2` adalah crate pihak ketiga standar yang mereplikasi semua tipe "
"`proc_macro`, tetapi tidak bergantung pada internal privat compiler. Inilah "
"sebabnya library pengujian atau alat lain dapat bekerja dengan token stream."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md
msgid ""
"`syn` and `quote` operate fully on `proc_macro2` types, allowing seamless "
"integration."
msgstr ""
"`syn` dan `quote` sepenuhnya beroperasi pada tipe `proc_macro2`, sehingga "
"memungkinkan integrasi yang mulus."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid ""
"The compiler-provided `proc_macro` crate defines the primary low-level types"
" for procedural macro manipulation. These are the actual types underlying "
"the tokens we match in declarative macros:"
msgstr ""
"Crate `proc_macro` yang disediakan compiler mendefinisikan tipe tingkat "
"rendah utama untuk manipulasi macro prosedural. Ini adalah tipe sebenarnya "
"yang mendasari token yang kita cocokkan dalam macro deklaratif:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid "**`TokenStream`:** An iterator over a sequence of `TokenTree` values."
msgstr "**`TokenStream`:** Iterator atas rangkaian nilai `TokenTree`."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid ""
"**`TokenTree`:** An enum representing individual lexical units. It has four "
"variants:"
msgstr ""
"**`TokenTree`:** Enum yang merepresentasikan unit leksikal individual. Enum "
"ini memiliki empat varian:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid "`Group`: A bracketed group of tokens (e.g., `(a + b)`, `{ ... }`)."
msgstr "`Group`: Grup token dalam kurung (misalnya, `(a + b)`, `{ ... }`)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid "`Ident`: An identifier or keyword (e.g., `foo`, `fn`, `let`, `false`)."
msgstr ""
"`Ident`: Identifier atau keyword (misalnya, `foo`, `fn`, `let`, `false`)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid ""
"`Punct`: A single punctuation character (e.g., `+`, `,`, `:`, but _not_ "
"combined operators like `+=`, nor brackets)."
msgstr ""
"`Punct`: Satu karakter tanda baca (misalnya, `+`, `,`, `:`, tetapi _bukan_ "
"operator gabungan seperti `+=`, dan bukan kurung)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid "`Literal`: A literal value (e.g., `\"hello\"`, `42`, `3.14`)."
msgstr "`Literal`: Nilai literal (misalnya, `\"hello\"`, `42`, `3.14`)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid ""
"Discuss that `proc_macro` is a built-in crate, so you don't need to add it "
"to your `Cargo.toml` dependencies (just defining `proc-macro = true` makes "
"it automatically available)."
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan bahwa `proc_macro` adalah crate bawaan, jadi Anda tidak perlu "
"menambahkannya ke dependensi `Cargo.toml` (cukup mendefinisikan `proc-macro "
"= true` agar crate ini tersedia secara otomatis)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro.md
msgid ""
"`TokenStream` can be converted to and from strings via `to_string()` and "
"`parse()`, but doing so breaks its relation to its original source code "
"location (`Span`), which should be preserved so compiler error messages can "
"point at the relevant code."
msgstr ""
"`TokenStream` dapat dikonversi ke dan dari string melalui `to_string()` dan "
"`parse()`, tetapi hal itu memutus hubungannya dengan lokasi kode sumber "
"aslinya (`Span`), yang sebaiknya dipertahankan agar pesan error compiler "
"dapat menunjuk ke kode yang relevan."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"The built-in `proc_macro` crate is tightly coupled to the compiler "
"internals, meaning its types cannot be instantiated or manipulated outside "
"of the compiler's plugin environment."
msgstr ""
"Crate bawaan `proc_macro` terikat erat dengan internal compiler, yang "
"berarti tipe-tipenya tidak dapat diinstansiasi atau dimanipulasi di luar "
"lingkungan plugin compiler."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"The **`proc_macro2`** library is a standard third-party crate that mirrors "
"the entire API of the built-in `proc_macro` crate, with some key advantages:"
msgstr ""
"Library **`proc_macro2`** adalah crate pihak ketiga standar yang "
"mencerminkan seluruh API crate bawaan `proc_macro`, dengan beberapa "
"keunggulan utama:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"**Unit testing:** You can write standard unit tests for your procedural "
"macros because `proc_macro2::TokenStream` can be instantiated and asserted "
"on in standard library tests."
msgstr ""
"**Unit testing:** Anda dapat menulis unit test standar untuk macro "
"prosedural karena `proc_macro2::TokenStream` dapat diinstansiasi dan diuji "
"dalam test standard library."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"**Standalone execution:** It allows libraries to work with token streams in "
"other execution contexts, such as build scripts (`build.rs`) or binary CLI "
"tools."
msgstr ""
"**Eksekusi mandiri:** Library dapat bekerja dengan token stream dalam "
"konteks eksekusi lain, seperti build script (`build.rs`) atau alat CLI "
"binary."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"**Seamless interoperability:** Types from `proc_macro2` are easily converted"
" to and from standard `proc_macro` types using `.into()`."
msgstr ""
"**Interoperabilitas mulus:** Tipe dari `proc_macro2` mudah dikonversi ke dan"
" dari tipe `proc_macro` standar menggunakan `.into()`."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"Mention that `proc_macro2` is an essential dependency for almost any "
"procedural macro crate."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa `proc_macro2` adalah dependensi penting bagi hampir semua "
"crate macro prosedural."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"This is because testing is incredibly important for macro development, and "
"`proc_macro2` makes it possible to write unit tests that parse strings into "
"token streams and assert on the outputs."
msgstr ""
"Ini karena pengujian sangat penting untuk pengembangan macro, dan "
"`proc_macro2` memungkinkan penulisan unit test yang mengurai string menjadi "
"token stream dan memeriksa outputnya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md
msgid ""
"Popular libraries like `syn` and `quote` fully rely on `proc_macro2` types "
"as their base inputs/outputs."
msgstr ""
"Library populer seperti `syn` dan `quote` sepenuhnya bergantung pada tipe "
"`proc_macro2` sebagai input/output dasarnya."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid ""
"Working directly with `TokenStream`s is low-level and tedious. To write "
"procedural macros effectively, authors often rely on **`syn`** (a parser for"
" Rust syntax) and **`quote`** (which constructs `syn` values from literal "
"code fragments) to do the heavy lifting of parsing and code generation."
msgstr ""
"Bekerja langsung dengan `TokenStream` bersifat tingkat rendah dan "
"melelahkan. Untuk menulis macro prosedural secara efektif, penulis sering "
"mengandalkan **`syn`** (parser sintaks Rust) dan **`quote`** (yang membangun"
" nilai `syn` dari fragmen kode literal) untuk melakukan pekerjaan berat "
"parsing dan pembuatan kode."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid "The workflow of a typical procedural macro is:"
msgstr "Alur kerja macro prosedural yang umum adalah:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid "**Input:** Accept a raw `proc_macro::TokenStream` from the compiler."
msgstr "**Input:** Menerima `proc_macro::TokenStream` mentah dari compiler."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid ""
"**Parsing (`syn`):** Convert the token stream into a structured, type-safe "
"Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) representing Rust language items (e.g., structs, "
"fields, functions)."
msgstr ""
"**Parsing (`syn`):** Mengonversi token stream menjadi Abstract Syntax Tree "
"(AST) yang terstruktur dan type-safe yang merepresentasikan item bahasa Rust"
" (misalnya, struct, field, fungsi)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid ""
"**Processing:** Inspect the AST struct and perform your custom logic to "
"decide what code needs to be generated."
msgstr ""
"**Pemrosesan:** Memeriksa struct AST dan menjalankan logika khusus Anda "
"untuk menentukan kode apa yang perlu dihasilkan."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid ""
"**Generation (`quote`):** Use a templated macro to generate a new "
"`proc_macro2::TokenStream`."
msgstr ""
"**Pembuatan (`quote`):** Menggunakan macro berbasis template untuk "
"menghasilkan `proc_macro2::TokenStream` baru."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid ""
"**Output:** Convert it back to `proc_macro::TokenStream` and return it to "
"the compiler."
msgstr ""
"**Output:** Mengonversinya kembali menjadi `proc_macro::TokenStream` dan "
"mengembalikannya ke compiler."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md
msgid "We will look at how `syn` parses code and how `quote` generates code."
msgstr ""
"Kami akan melihat bagaimana `syn` mengurai kode dan bagaimana `quote` "
"menghasilkan kode."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid ""
"The **`syn`** crate provides a complete, robust parser that parses a raw "
"`TokenStream` into structured, AST types that can represent any element of "
"Rust code. `syn` has a wide API surface, but it should feel relatively "
"straightforward as it mirrors the structure of Rust syntax itself. Here we "
"illustrate the use of `syn` for a Derive macro:"
msgstr ""
"Crate **`syn`** menyediakan parser lengkap dan kokoh yang mengurai "
"`TokenStream` mentah menjadi tipe AST terstruktur yang dapat "
"merepresentasikan elemen kode Rust apa pun. `syn` memiliki permukaan API "
"yang luas, tetapi seharusnya terasa cukup lugas karena mencerminkan struktur"
" sintaks Rust itu sendiri. Berikut kami ilustrasikan penggunaan `syn` untuk "
"macro Derive:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid "// Parse raw tokens into a structured `DeriveInput` AST:\n"
msgstr "// Parse raw tokens into a structured `DeriveInput` AST:\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid "// Inspect struct metadata:\n"
msgstr "// Inspect struct metadata:\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid ""
"**`DeriveInput`:** The standard AST structure for a struct, enum, or union."
msgstr ""
"**`DeriveInput`:** Struktur AST standar untuk struct, enum, atau union."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid ""
"**`parse_macro_input!`:** A specialized macro helper provided by `syn` to "
"easily parse the input token stream. It automatically handles compile-time "
"syntax errors if the input is malformed. This macro accepts the name of the "
"type into which to parse the token stream after an `as` separator, notation "
"that resembles a Rust cast."
msgstr ""
"**`parse_macro_input!`:** Macro helper khusus yang disediakan `syn` untuk "
"memudahkan penguraian token stream input. Macro ini secara otomatis "
"menangani error sintaks waktu kompilasi jika input cacat. Macro ini menerima"
" nama tipe tujuan penguraian token stream setelah separator `as`, notasi "
"yang menyerupai cast Rust."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid "Explore `DeriveInput`, which three main components:"
msgstr "Telusuri `DeriveInput`, yang memiliki tiga komponen utama:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid "`ident`: The name of the struct/enum."
msgstr "`ident`: Nama struct/enum."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid "`generics`: Generic parameters, lifetemes, and constraints."
msgstr "`generics`: Parameter generic, lifetime, dan constraint."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md
msgid ""
"`data`: An enum containing `syn::DataStruct`, `syn::DataEnum`, or "
"`syn::DataUnion`, which lets you iterate over variants and fields."
msgstr ""
"`data`: Enum yang berisi `syn::DataStruct`, `syn::DataEnum`, atau "
"`syn::DataUnion`, yang memungkinkan Anda mengiterasi varian dan field."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid ""
"The **`quote`** crate provides the `quote!` macro, which is a powerful "
"templating engine for generating Rust code. It lets you write standard Rust "
"syntax and interpolate existing code from variables in scope:"
msgstr ""
"Crate **`quote`** menyediakan macro `quote!`, yaitu mesin template yang "
"ampuh untuk menghasilkan kode Rust. Macro ini memungkinkan Anda menulis "
"sintaks Rust standar dan menginterpolasi kode yang sudah ada dari variabel "
"di scope:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid "// e.g. \"Student\"\n"
msgstr "// e.g. \"Student\"\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid "// Generate a TokenStream using standard Rust syntax as a template:\n"
msgstr "// Generate a TokenStream using standard Rust syntax as a template:\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid "\"My name is {}\""
msgstr "\"My name is {}\""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid "// Convert to proc_macro::TokenStream:\n"
msgstr "// Convert to proc_macro::TokenStream:\n"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid ""
"**Interpolation:** Use `#var_name` to insert a variable (like an identifier,"
" type, or other token stream) directly into the template."
msgstr ""
"**Interpolasi:** Gunakan `#var_name` untuk menyisipkan variabel (seperti "
"identifier, tipe, atau token stream lain) langsung ke dalam template."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid ""
"**Repetitions:** Use `#(#var_list),*` to expand a list of variables "
"separated by commas, similar to how repetitions work in declarative macros."
msgstr ""
"**Repetisi:** Gunakan `#(#var_list),*` untuk memperluas daftar variabel yang"
" dipisahkan koma, serupa dengan cara repetisi bekerja dalam macro "
"deklaratif."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid ""
"Note that `quote!` returns a `proc_macro2::TokenStream`. We call `.into()` "
"at the end of our procedural macro function to convert it to a standard "
"`proc_macro::TokenStream` for the compiler."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `quote!` mengembalikan `proc_macro2::TokenStream`. Kami "
"memanggil `.into()` di akhir fungsi macro prosedural untuk mengonversinya "
"menjadi `proc_macro::TokenStream` standar bagi compiler."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid ""
"Highlight how clean this makes code generation. Instead of manually pushing "
"string slices or tokens, you write literal Rust code blocks with templates."
msgstr ""
"Soroti betapa bersihnya hal ini membuat pembuatan kode. Alih-alih mendorong "
"string slice atau token secara manual, Anda menulis block kode Rust literal "
"dengan template."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md
msgid ""
"Mention that repetition is often useful when iterating over all fields of a "
"struct."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa repetisi sering berguna saat mengiterasi semua field struct."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will walk through the conceptual implementation of a "
"custom **`Display` derive macro** using the `syn` and `quote` crates."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda akan menelusuri implementasi konseptual **macro "
"derive `Display`** khusus menggunakan crate `syn` dan `quote`."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Since we are running this in a single-file environment without a separate "
"`proc-macro = true` crate setup, we will write a normal Rust function that "
"takes simulated token streams (using `proc_macro2` and `quote!`), parses "
"them with `syn`, generates the output with `quote!`, and asserts that the "
"generated code is correct."
msgstr ""
"Karena kami menjalankan ini di lingkungan satu berkas tanpa penyiapan crate "
"`proc-macro = true` terpisah, kami akan menulis fungsi Rust normal yang "
"menerima token stream simulasi (menggunakan `proc_macro2` dan `quote!`), "
"mengurainya dengan `syn`, menghasilkan output dengan `quote!`, dan "
"memastikan kode yang dihasilkan benar."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid "Your task:"
msgstr "Tugas Anda:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid "Implement the `derive_display_impl` function to:"
msgstr "Implementasikan fungsi `derive_display_impl` untuk:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Parse the incoming token stream `input` into a `syn::DeriveInput` struct."
msgstr ""
"Mengurai token stream `input` yang masuk menjadi struct `syn::DeriveInput`."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid "Extract the name (identifier) of the struct."
msgstr "Mengekstrak nama (identifier) struct."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Generate and return a token stream implementing `std::fmt::Display` for that"
" struct name, which formats the struct using its name, names of its fields, "
"and their values. (e.g., printing `MyAwesomeType { a: 50, }`)."
msgstr ""
"Menghasilkan dan mengembalikan token stream yang mengimplementasikan "
"`std::fmt::Display` untuk nama struct tersebut, yang memformat struct "
"menggunakan namanya, nama field-nya, dan nilainya. (misalnya, mencetak "
"`MyAwesomeType { a: 50, }`)."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The names of the struct's fields can be obtained with the provided "
"`struct_fields` function."
msgstr ""
"Nama field struct dapat diperoleh dengan fungsi `struct_fields` yang "
"disediakan."

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid "This will rely on a `Cargo.toml` resembling:"
msgstr "Ini akan bergantung pada `Cargo.toml` yang menyerupai:"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"proc-macro-exercise\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"publish = false\n"
"\n"
"[[bin]]\n"
"name = \"proc-macro-exercise\"\n"
"path = \"exercise.rs\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"proc-macro2 = \"1.0\"\n"
"quote = \"1.0\"\n"
"syn = \"2.0\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"proc-macro-exercise\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"publish = false\n"
"\n"
"[[bin]]\n"
"name = \"proc-macro-exercise\"\n"
"path = \"exercise.rs\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"proc-macro2 = \"1.0\"\n"
"quote = \"1.0\"\n"
"syn = \"2.0\"\n"
"```"

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md src/macros/proc-macros/solution.md
msgid "\"named field name\""
msgstr "\"named field name\""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md
msgid ""
"// TODO: Parse the input TokenStream into DeriveInput.\n"
"    // TODO: Extract the identifier of the struct.\n"
"    // TODO: Generate the impl std::fmt::Display using quote!.\n"
msgstr ""
"// TODO: Parse the input TokenStream into DeriveInput.\n"
"    // TODO: Extract the identifier of the struct.\n"
"    // TODO: Generate the impl std::fmt::Display using quote!.\n"

