#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"For mocking, [Mockall](https://docs.rs/mockall/) is a widely used library. "
"You need to refactor your code to use traits, which you can then quickly "
"mock:"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mocking, [Mockall](https://docs.rs/mockall/) adalah library yang "
"banyak digunakan. Anda perlu merefaktor kode agar menggunakan trait, yang "
"kemudian dapat dengan cepat di-mock:"

#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"Mockall is the recommended mocking library in Android (AOSP). There are "
"other [mocking libraries available on "
"crates.io](https://crates.io/keywords/mock), in particular in the area of "
"mocking HTTP services. The other mocking libraries work in a similar fashion"
" as Mockall, meaning that they make it easy to get a mock implementation of "
"a given trait."
msgstr ""
"Mockall adalah library mocking yang direkomendasikan di Android (AOSP). Ada "
"[library mocking lain yang tersedia di "
"crates.io](https://crates.io/keywords/mock), khususnya di area mocking "
"layanan HTTP. Library mocking lainnya bekerja dengan cara yang serupa dengan"
" Mockall, yaitu memudahkan Anda mendapatkan implementasi mock dari trait "
"tertentu."

#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"Note that mocking is somewhat _controversial_: mocks allow you to completely"
" isolate a test from its dependencies. The immediate result is faster and "
"more stable test execution. On the other hand, the mocks can be configured "
"wrongly and return output different from what the real dependencies would "
"do."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa mocking agak _kontroversial_: mock memungkinkan Anda "
"mengisolasi test sepenuhnya dari dependensinya. Hasil langsungnya adalah "
"eksekusi test yang lebih cepat dan lebih stabil. Di sisi lain, mock dapat "
"dikonfigurasi secara keliru dan mengembalikan output yang berbeda dari yang "
"akan dilakukan dependensi nyata."

#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"If at all possible, it is recommended that you use the real dependencies. As"
" an example, many databases allow you to configure an in-memory backend. "
"This means that you get the correct behavior in your tests, plus they are "
"fast and will automatically clean up after themselves."
msgstr ""
"Jika memungkinkan, disarankan untuk menggunakan dependensi nyata. Sebagai "
"contoh, banyak database memungkinkan Anda mengonfigurasi backend in-memory. "
"Ini berarti Anda mendapatkan perilaku yang benar dalam test, ditambah test "
"menjadi cepat dan otomatis membersihkan dirinya sendiri."

#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"Similarly, many web frameworks allow you to start an in-process server which"
" binds to a random port on `localhost`. Always prefer this over mocking away"
" the framework since it helps you test your code in the real environment."
msgstr ""
"Serupa dengan itu, banyak web framework memungkinkan Anda menjalankan server"
" dalam proses yang terikat ke port acak pada `localhost`. Selalu utamakan "
"ini daripada mem-mock framework karena membantu Anda menguji kode di "
"lingkungan nyata."

#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"Mockall is not part of the Rust Playground, so you need to run this example "
"in a local environment. Use `cargo add mockall` to quickly add Mockall to an"
" existing Cargo project."
msgstr ""
"Mockall bukan bagian dari Rust Playground, jadi Anda perlu menjalankan "
"contoh ini di lingkungan lokal. Gunakan `cargo add mockall` untuk "
"menambahkan Mockall dengan cepat ke proyek Cargo yang sudah ada."

#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"Mockall has extensive functionality. In particular, you can set up "
"expectations which depend on the arguments passed. Here we use this to mock "
"a cat which becomes hungry 3 hours after the last time it was fed:"
msgstr ""
"Mockall memiliki fungsionalitas yang ekstensif. Secara khusus, Anda dapat "
"menyiapkan ekspektasi yang bergantung pada argumen yang diteruskan. Di sini "
"kami menggunakannya untuk mem-mock kucing yang menjadi lapar 3 jam setelah "
"terakhir diberi makan:"

#: src/android/testing/mocking.md
msgid ""
"You can use `.times(n)` to limit the number of times a mock method can be "
"called to `n` --- the mock will automatically panic when dropped if this "
"isn't satisfied."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menggunakan `.times(n)` untuk membatasi jumlah pemanggilan method"
" mock menjadi `n` --- mock akan otomatis panic saat di-drop jika batasan ini"
" tidak terpenuhi."

