#: src/android/interoperability.md
msgid ""
"Rust has excellent support for interoperability with other languages. This "
"means that you can:"
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki dukungan sangat baik untuk interoperabilitas dengan bahasa "
"lain. Ini berarti Anda dapat:"

#: src/android/interoperability.md
msgid "Call Rust functions from other languages."
msgstr "Memanggil fungsi Rust dari bahasa lain."

#: src/android/interoperability.md
msgid "Call functions written in other languages from Rust."
msgstr "Memanggil fungsi yang ditulis dalam bahasa lain dari Rust."

#: src/android/interoperability.md
msgid ""
"When you call functions in a foreign language, you're using a _foreign "
"function interface_, also known as FFI."
msgstr ""
"Saat Anda memanggil fungsi dalam bahasa asing, Anda menggunakan _foreign "
"function interface_, yang juga dikenal sebagai FFI."

#: src/android/interoperability.md
msgid ""
"This is a key ability of Rust: compiled code becomes indistinguishable from "
"compiled C or C++ code."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah kemampuan kunci Rust: kode yang dikompilasi menjadi tidak dapat "
"dibedakan dari kode C atau C++ yang dikompilasi."

#: src/android/interoperability.md
msgid ""
"Technically, we say that Rust can be compiled to the same "
"[ABI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_binary_interface) "
"(application binary interface) as C code."
msgstr ""
"Secara teknis, kita mengatakan bahwa Rust dapat dikompilasi ke "
"[ABI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_binary_interface) "
"(application binary interface) yang sama dengan kode C."

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid "Interoperability with C"
msgstr "Interoperabilitas dengan C"

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid ""
"Rust has full support for linking object files with a C calling convention. "
"Similarly, you can export Rust functions and call them from C."
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki dukungan penuh untuk menautkan object file dengan calling "
"convention C. Serupa dengan itu, Anda dapat mengekspor fungsi Rust dan "
"memanggilnya dari C."

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid "You can do it by hand if you want:"
msgstr "Anda dapat melakukannya secara manual jika mau:"

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "\"{x}, {abs_x}\""
msgstr "\"{x}, {abs_x}\""

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid ""
"We already saw this in the [Safe FFI Wrapper exercise](../../unsafe-"
"rust/exercise.md)."
msgstr ""
"Kami sudah melihat ini pada [latihan Safe FFI Wrapper](../../unsafe-"
"rust/exercise.md)."

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid ""
"This assumes full knowledge of the target platform. Not recommended for "
"production."
msgstr ""
"Ini mengasumsikan pengetahuan penuh tentang platform target. Tidak "
"direkomendasikan untuk produksi."

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid "We will look at better options next."
msgstr "Kami akan melihat opsi yang lebih baik selanjutnya."

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid ""
"The [`\"C\"` part](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/external-"
"blocks.html#abi) of the `extern` block tells Rust that `abs` can be called "
"using the C "
"[ABI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_binary_interface) "
"(application binary interface)."
msgstr ""
"Bagian [`\"C\"`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/external-"
"blocks.html#abi) pada block `extern` memberi tahu Rust bahwa `abs` dapat "
"dipanggil menggunakan "
"[ABI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_binary_interface) C "
"(application binary interface)."

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md
msgid ""
"The `safe fn abs` part tells Rust that `abs` is a safe function. By default,"
" extern functions are unsafe, but since `abs(x)` can't trigger undefined "
"behavior with any `x`, we can declare it safe."
msgstr ""
"Bagian `safe fn abs` memberi tahu Rust bahwa `abs` adalah fungsi safe. "
"Secara default, fungsi extern bersifat unsafe, tetapi karena `abs(x)` tidak "
"dapat memicu undefined behavior dengan `x` apa pun, kita dapat "
"mendeklarasikannya safe."

