#: src/android/interoperability/java.md
msgid ""
"The `unsafe(no_mangle)` attribute instructs Rust to emit the "
"`Java_HelloWorld_hello` symbol exactly as written. This is important so that"
" Java can recognize the symbol as a `hello` method on the `HelloWorld` "
"class."
msgstr ""
"Atribut `unsafe(no_mangle)` menginstruksikan Rust untuk mengeluarkan simbol "
"`Java_HelloWorld_hello` persis seperti yang ditulis. Ini penting agar Java "
"dapat mengenali simbol tersebut sebagai method `hello` pada class "
"`HelloWorld`."

#: src/android/interoperability/java.md
msgid ""
"By default, Rust will mangle (rename) symbols so that a binary can link in "
"two versions of the same Rust crate."
msgstr ""
"Secara default, Rust akan melakukan mangling (mengganti nama) simbol agar "
"binary dapat menautkan dua versi crate Rust yang sama."

#: src/chromium.md
msgid "Welcome to Rust in Chromium"
msgstr "Selamat Datang di Rust di Chromium"

#: src/chromium.md
msgid ""
"Rust is supported for third-party libraries in Chromium, with first-party "
"glue code to connect between Rust and existing Chromium C++ code."
msgstr ""
"Rust didukung untuk library pihak ketiga di Chromium, dengan kode glue "
"first-party untuk menghubungkan Rust dan kode C++ Chromium yang sudah ada."

#: src/chromium.md
msgid ""
"Today, we'll call into Rust to do something silly with strings. If you've "
"got a corner of the code where you're displaying a UTF-8 string to the user,"
" feel free to follow this recipe in your part of the codebase instead of the"
" exact part we talk about."
msgstr ""
"Hari ini, kita akan memanggil Rust untuk melakukan sesuatu yang iseng dengan"
" string. Jika Anda memiliki bagian kode tempat menampilkan string UTF-8 "
"kepada pengguna, silakan ikuti resep ini di bagian basis kode Anda alih-alih"
" di bagian persis yang kami bahas."

#: src/chromium/setup.md
msgid ""
"Make sure you can build and run Chromium. Any platform and set of build "
"flags is OK, so long as your code is relatively recent (commit position "
"1223636 onwards, corresponding to November 2023):"
msgstr ""
"Pastikan Anda dapat membangun dan menjalankan Chromium. Platform dan "
"rangkaian build flag apa pun boleh, asalkan kode Anda relatif baru (posisi "
"commit 1223636 dan seterusnya, yang sesuai dengan November 2023):"

#: src/chromium/setup.md
msgid ""
"(A component, debug build is recommended for quickest iteration time. This "
"is the default!)"
msgstr ""
"(Build debug komponen disarankan untuk waktu iterasi tercepat. Ini adalah "
"default!)"

#: src/chromium/setup.md
msgid ""
"See [How to build Chromium](https://www.chromium.org/developers/how-tos/get-"
"the-code/) if you aren't already at that point. Be warned: setting up to "
"build Chromium takes time."
msgstr ""
"Lihat [Cara Membangun Chromium](https://www.chromium.org/developers/how-"
"tos/get-the-code/) jika Anda belum sampai di tahap itu. Perlu diperhatikan: "
"menyiapkan build Chromium membutuhkan waktu."

#: src/chromium/setup.md
msgid "It's also recommended that you have Visual Studio code installed."
msgstr "Disarankan juga agar Anda memasang Visual Studio Code."

#: src/chromium/setup.md
msgid "About the exercises"
msgstr "Tentang Latihan"

#: src/chromium/setup.md
msgid ""
"This part of the course has a series of exercises that build on each other. "
"We'll be doing them spread throughout the course instead of just at the end."
" If you don't have time to complete a certain part, don't worry: you can "
"catch up in the next slot."
msgstr ""
"Bagian kursus ini memiliki rangkaian latihan yang saling membangun. Kami "
"akan mengerjakannya tersebar sepanjang kursus, bukan hanya di akhir. Jika "
"Anda tidak sempat menyelesaikan bagian tertentu, jangan khawatir: Anda dapat"
" mengejar ketertinggalan pada sesi berikutnya."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"The Rust community typically uses `cargo` and libraries from "
"[crates.io](https://crates.io/). Chromium is built using `gn` and `ninja` "
"and a curated set of dependencies."
msgstr ""
"Komunitas Rust biasanya menggunakan `cargo` dan library dari "
"[crates.io](https://crates.io/). Chromium dibangun menggunakan `gn` dan "
"`ninja` serta rangkaian dependensi yang dikurasi."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "When writing code in Rust, your choices are:"
msgstr "Saat menulis kode dalam Rust, pilihan Anda adalah:"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Use `gn` and `ninja` with the help of the templates from "
"`//build/rust/*.gni` (e.g. `rust_static_library` that we'll meet later). "
"This uses Chromium's audited toolchain and crates."
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan `gn` dan `ninja` dengan bantuan template dari "
"`//build/rust/*.gni` (misalnya `rust_static_library` yang akan kita temui "
"nanti). Ini menggunakan toolchain dan crate Chromium yang telah diaudit."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Use `cargo`, but [restrict yourself to Chromium's audited toolchain and "
"crates](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/docs/rust.md#Using-"
"cargo)"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan `cargo`, tetapi [batasi diri Anda pada toolchain dan crate "
"Chromium yang telah "
"diaudit](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/docs/rust.md#Using-"
"cargo)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Use `cargo`, trusting a [toolchain](https://rustup.rs/) and/or [crates "
"downloaded from the internet](https://crates.io/)"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan `cargo`, dengan mempercayai [toolchain](https://rustup.rs/) "
"dan/atau [crate yang diunduh dari internet](https://crates.io/)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"From here on we'll be focusing on `gn` and `ninja`, because this is how Rust"
" code can be built into the Chromium browser. At the same time, Cargo is an "
"important part of the Rust ecosystem and you should keep it in your toolbox."
msgstr ""
"Mulai dari sini kami akan berfokus pada `gn` dan `ninja`, karena demikian "
"cara kode Rust dapat dibangun ke dalam browser Chromium. Pada saat yang "
"sama, Cargo adalah bagian penting dari ekosistem Rust dan sebaiknya tetap "
"Anda simpan dalam kotak alat Anda."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "Mini exercise"
msgstr "Latihan Mini"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "Split into small groups and:"
msgstr "Bagi menjadi kelompok kecil dan:"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Brainstorm scenarios where `cargo` may offer an advantage and assess the "
"risk profile of these scenarios."
msgstr ""
"Curahkan ide tentang skenario ketika `cargo` mungkin menawarkan keunggulan, "
"dan nilai profil risiko skenario tersebut."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Discuss which tools, libraries, and groups of people need to be trusted when"
" using `gn` and `ninja`, offline `cargo`, etc."
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan alat, library, dan kelompok orang mana yang perlu dipercaya saat "
"menggunakan `gn` dan `ninja`, `cargo` offline, dan sebagainya."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Ask students to avoid peeking at the speaker notes before completing the "
"exercise. Assuming folks taking the course are physically together, ask them"
" to discuss in small groups of 3-4 people."
msgstr ""
"Minta siswa menghindari mengintip catatan pembicara sebelum menyelesaikan "
"latihan. Dengan asumsi peserta kursus berada di lokasi yang sama, minta "
"mereka berdiskusi dalam kelompok kecil berisi 3-4 orang."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Notes/hints related to the first part of the exercise (\"scenarios where "
"Cargo may offer an advantage\"):"
msgstr ""
"Catatan/petunjuk terkait bagian pertama latihan (\"skenario ketika Cargo "
"mungkin menawarkan keunggulan\"):"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"It's fantastic that when writing a tool, or prototyping a part of Chromium, "
"one has access to the rich ecosystem of crates.io libraries. There is a "
"crate for almost anything and they are typically quite pleasant to use. "
"(`clap` for command-line parsing, `serde` for serializing/deserializing "
"to/from various formats, `itertools` for working with iterators, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Sangat menyenangkan bahwa saat menulis alat atau membuat prototipe bagian "
"Chromium, seseorang memiliki akses ke ekosistem library crates.io yang kaya."
" Hampir semua kebutuhan memiliki crate, dan biasanya cukup menyenangkan "
"digunakan. (`clap` untuk parsing command-line, `serde` untuk "
"serialisasi/deserialisasi ke/dari berbagai format, `itertools` untuk bekerja"
" dengan iterator, dan sebagainya.)."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"`cargo` makes it easy to try a library (just add a single line to "
"`Cargo.toml` and start writing code)"
msgstr ""
"`cargo` memudahkan untuk mencoba library (cukup tambahkan satu baris ke "
"`Cargo.toml` dan mulai menulis kode)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"It may be worth comparing how CPAN helped make `perl` a popular choice. Or "
"comparing with `python` + `pip`."
msgstr ""
"Mungkin bermanfaat untuk membandingkan bagaimana CPAN membantu menjadikan "
"`perl` pilihan populer. Atau membandingkannya dengan `python` + `pip`."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Development experience is made really nice not only by core Rust tools (e.g."
" using `rustup` to switch to a different `rustc` version when testing a "
"crate that needs to work on nightly, current stable, and older stable) but "
"also by an ecosystem of third-party tools (e.g. Mozilla provides `cargo vet`"
" for streamlining and sharing security audits; `criterion` crate gives a "
"streamlined way to run benchmarks)."
msgstr ""
"Pengalaman pengembangan menjadi sangat menyenangkan bukan hanya karena alat "
"inti Rust (misalnya menggunakan `rustup` untuk beralih ke versi `rustc` lain"
" saat menguji crate yang perlu berjalan di nightly, stable saat ini, dan "
"stable lama), tetapi juga karena ekosistem alat pihak ketiga (misalnya "
"Mozilla menyediakan `cargo vet` untuk merampingkan dan berbagi audit "
"keamanan; crate `criterion` menyediakan cara ramping untuk menjalankan "
"benchmark)."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"`cargo` makes it easy to add a tool via `cargo install --locked cargo-vet`."
msgstr ""
"`cargo` memudahkan penambahan alat melalui `cargo install --locked cargo-"
"vet`."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "It may be worth comparing with Chrome Extensions or VScode extensions."
msgstr ""
"Mungkin bermanfaat untuk membandingkannya dengan Chrome Extension atau "
"ekstensi VSCode."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Broad, generic examples of projects where `cargo` may be the right choice:"
msgstr ""
"Contoh umum dan luas untuk proyek ketika `cargo` mungkin menjadi pilihan "
"yang tepat:"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Perhaps surprisingly, Rust is becoming increasingly popular in the industry "
"for writing command line tools. The breadth and ergonomics of libraries is "
"comparable to Python, while being more robust (thanks to the rich type "
"system) and running faster (as a compiled, rather than interpreted "
"language)."
msgstr ""
"Mungkin mengejutkan, Rust semakin populer di industri untuk menulis alat "
"command line. Keluasan dan ergonomi library-nya sebanding dengan Python, "
"sekaligus lebih kokoh (berkat sistem tipe yang kaya) dan berjalan lebih "
"cepat (sebagai bahasa terkompilasi, bukan interpreted)."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Participating in the Rust ecosystem requires using standard Rust tools like "
"Cargo. Libraries that want to get external contributions, and want to be "
"used outside of Chromium (e.g. in Bazel or Android/Soong build environments)"
" should use Cargo."
msgstr ""
"Berpartisipasi dalam ekosistem Rust mengharuskan penggunaan alat Rust "
"standar seperti Cargo. Library yang ingin mendapatkan kontribusi eksternal "
"dan ingin digunakan di luar Chromium (misalnya di lingkungan build Bazel "
"atau Android/Soong) sebaiknya menggunakan Cargo."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "Examples of Chromium-related projects that are `cargo`\\-based:"
msgstr "Contoh proyek terkait Chromium yang berbasis `cargo`:"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"`serde_json_lenient` (experimented with in other parts of Google which "
"resulted in PRs with performance improvements)"
msgstr ""
"`serde_json_lenient` (dieksperimenkan di bagian lain Google dan menghasilkan"
" PR dengan peningkatan performa)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "Fontations libraries like `font-types`"
msgstr "Library Fontations seperti `font-types`"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"`gnrt` tool (we will meet it later in the course) which depends on `clap` "
"for command-line parsing and on `toml` for configuration files."
msgstr ""
"Alat `gnrt` (akan kita temui nanti dalam kursus) yang bergantung pada `clap`"
" untuk parsing command-line dan pada `toml` untuk berkas konfigurasi."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Disclaimer: a unique reason for using `cargo` was unavailability of `gn` "
"when building and bootstrapping Rust standard library when building Rust "
"toolchain."
msgstr ""
"Disclaimer: alasan unik penggunaan `cargo` adalah tidak tersedianya `gn` "
"saat membangun dan melakukan bootstrap standard library Rust ketika "
"membangun toolchain Rust."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"`run_gnrt.py` uses Chromium's copy of `cargo` and `rustc`. `gnrt` depends on"
" third-party libraries downloaded from the internet, but `run_gnrt.py` asks "
"`cargo` that only `--locked` content is allowed via `Cargo.lock`.)"
msgstr ""
"`run_gnrt.py` menggunakan salinan `cargo` dan `rustc` milik Chromium. `gnrt`"
" bergantung pada library pihak ketiga yang diunduh dari internet, tetapi "
"`run_gnrt.py` meminta `cargo` agar hanya konten `--locked` yang diizinkan "
"melalui `Cargo.lock`.)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Students may identify the following items as being implicitly or explicitly "
"trusted:"
msgstr ""
"Siswa mungkin mengidentifikasi hal berikut sebagai sesuatu yang dipercaya "
"secara implisit atau eksplisit:"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"`rustc` (the Rust compiler) which in turn depends on the LLVM libraries, the"
" Clang compiler, the `rustc` sources (fetched from GitHub, reviewed by Rust "
"compiler team), binary Rust compiler downloaded for bootstrapping"
msgstr ""
"`rustc` (compiler Rust) yang selanjutnya bergantung pada library LLVM, "
"compiler Clang, sumber `rustc` (diambil dari GitHub, ditinjau oleh tim "
"compiler Rust), serta compiler Rust binary yang diunduh untuk bootstrap"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"`rustup` (it may be worth pointing out that `rustup` is developed under the "
"umbrella of the https://github.com/rust-lang/ organization - same as "
"`rustc`)"
msgstr ""
"`rustup` (mungkin perlu ditunjukkan bahwa `rustup` dikembangkan di bawah "
"naungan organisasi https://github.com/rust-lang/ - sama seperti `rustc`)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "`cargo`, `rustfmt`, etc."
msgstr "`cargo`, `rustfmt`, dan sebagainya."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Various internal infrastructure (bots that build `rustc`, system for "
"distributing the prebuilt toolchain to Chromium engineers, etc.)"
msgstr ""
"Berbagai infrastruktur internal (bot yang membangun `rustc`, sistem "
"distribusi toolchain prebuilt kepada engineer Chromium, dan sebagainya.)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid "Cargo tools like `cargo audit`, `cargo vet`, etc."
msgstr "Alat Cargo seperti `cargo audit`, `cargo vet`, dan sebagainya."

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Rust libraries vendored into `//third_party/rust` (audited by "
"security@chromium.org)"
msgstr ""
"Library Rust yang di-vendor ke `//third_party/rust` (diaudit oleh "
"security@chromium.org)"

#: src/chromium/cargo.md
msgid ""
"Other Rust libraries (some niche, some quite popular and commonly used)"
msgstr ""
"Library Rust lainnya (sebagian niche, sebagian cukup populer dan umum "
"digunakan)"

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid "Chromium Rust policy"
msgstr "Kebijakan Rust Chromium"

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid ""
"Chromium's Rust policy can be found "
"[here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:docs/rust.md;l=22)."
" Rust can be used for both first-party and third-party code."
msgstr ""
"Kebijakan Rust Chromium dapat ditemukan [di "
"sini](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:docs/rust.md;l=22)."
" Rust dapat digunakan untuk kode first-party maupun pihak ketiga."

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid "Using Rust for pure first-party code looks like this:"
msgstr "Penggunaan Rust untuk kode first-party murni tampak seperti ini:"

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid ""
"```bob\n"
"\"C++\"                           Rust\n"
".- - - - - - - - - -.           .- - - - - - - - - - -.\n"
":                   :           :                     :\n"
": Existing Chromium :           :  Chromium Rust      :\n"
": \"C++\"             :           :  code               :\n"
": +---------------+ :           : +----------------+  :\n"
": |               | :           : |                |  :\n"
": |         o-----+-+-----------+-+->              |  :\n"
": |               | : Language  : |                |  :\n"
": +---------------+ : boundary  : +----------------+  :\n"
":                   :           :                     :\n"
"`- - - - - - - - - -'           `- - - - - - - - - - -'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```bob\n"
"\"C++\"                           Rust\n"
".- - - - - - - - - -.           .- - - - - - - - - - -.\n"
":                   :           :                     :\n"
": Existing Chromium :           :  Chromium Rust      :\n"
": \"C++\"             :           :  code               :\n"
": +---------------+ :           : +----------------+  :\n"
": |               | :           : |                |  :\n"
": |         o-----+-+-----------+-+->              |  :\n"
": |               | : Language  : |                |  :\n"
": +---------------+ : boundary  : +----------------+  :\n"
":                   :           :                     :\n"
"`- - - - - - - - - -'           `- - - - - - - - - - -'\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid ""
"The third-party case is also common. You will typically also need a small "
"amount of first-party glue code, because very few Rust libraries directly "
"expose a C/C++ API."
msgstr ""
"Kasus pihak ketiga juga umum. Biasanya Anda juga memerlukan sedikit kode "
"glue first-party, karena sangat sedikit library Rust yang langsung "
"mengekspos API C/C++."

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid ""
"```bob\n"
"\"C++\"                           Rust\n"
".- - - - - - - - - -.           .- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -.\n"
":                   :           :                                             :\n"
": Existing Chromium :           :  Chromium Rust              Existing Rust   :\n"
": \"C++\"             :           :  \"wrapper\"                  crate           :\n"
": +---------------+ :           : +----------------+          +-------------+ :\n"
": |               | :           : |                |          |             | :\n"
": |         o-----+-+-----------+-+->            o-+----------+-->          | :\n"
": |               | : Language  : |                | Crate    |             | :\n"
": +---------------+ : boundary  : +----------------+ API      +-------------+ :\n"
":                   :           :                                             :\n"
"`- - - - - - - - - -'           `- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```bob\n"
"\"C++\"                           Rust\n"
".- - - - - - - - - -.           .- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -.\n"
":                   :           :                                             :\n"
": Existing Chromium :           :  Chromium Rust              Existing Rust   :\n"
": \"C++\"             :           :  \"wrapper\"                  crate           :\n"
": +---------------+ :           : +----------------+          +-------------+ :\n"
": |               | :           : |                |          |             | :\n"
": |         o-----+-+-----------+-+->            o-+----------+-->          | :\n"
": |               | : Language  : |                | Crate    |             | :\n"
": +---------------+ : boundary  : +----------------+ API      +-------------+ :\n"
":                   :           :                                             :\n"
"`- - - - - - - - - -'           `- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -'\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid ""
"The scenario of using a third-party crate is the more complex one, so "
"today's course will focus on:"
msgstr ""
"Skenario penggunaan crate pihak ketiga lebih kompleks, jadi kursus hari ini "
"akan berfokus pada:"

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid "Bringing in third-party Rust libraries (\"crates\")"
msgstr "Memasukkan library Rust pihak ketiga (\"crate\")"

#: src/chromium/policy.md
msgid ""
"Writing glue code to be able to use those crates from Chromium C++. (The "
"same techniques are used when working with first-party Rust code)."
msgstr ""
"Menulis kode glue agar crate tersebut dapat digunakan dari C++ Chromium. "
"(Teknik yang sama digunakan saat bekerja dengan kode Rust first-party)."

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid "Build rules"
msgstr "Aturan Build"

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"Rust code is typically built using `cargo`. Chromium builds with `gn` and "
"`ninja` for efficiency --- its static rules allow maximum parallelism. Rust "
"is no exception."
msgstr ""
"Kode Rust biasanya dibangun menggunakan `cargo`. Chromium melakukan build "
"dengan `gn` dan `ninja` untuk efisiensi --- aturan statisnya memungkinkan "
"paralelisme maksimum. Rust bukan pengecualian."

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid "Adding Rust code to Chromium"
msgstr "Menambahkan Kode Rust ke Chromium"

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"In some existing Chromium `BUILD.gn` file, declare a `rust_static_library`:"
msgstr ""
"Di berkas `BUILD.gn` Chromium yang sudah ada, deklarasikan "
"`rust_static_library`:"

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"```gn\n"
"import(\"//build/rust/rust_static_library.gni\")\n"
"\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib\") {\n"
"  crate_root = \"lib.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [ \"lib.rs\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```gn\n"
"import(\"//build/rust/rust_static_library.gni\")\n"
"\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib\") {\n"
"  crate_root = \"lib.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [ \"lib.rs\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"You can also add `deps` on other Rust targets. Later we'll use this to "
"depend upon third party code."
msgstr ""
"Anda juga dapat menambahkan `deps` pada target Rust lainnya. Nanti kami akan"
" menggunakan ini untuk bergantung pada kode pihak ketiga."

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"You must specify _both_ the crate root, _and_ a full list of sources. The "
"`crate_root` is the file given to the Rust compiler representing the root "
"file of the compilation unit --- typically `lib.rs`. `sources` is a complete"
" list of all source files which `ninja` needs in order to determine when "
"rebuilds are necessary."
msgstr ""
"Anda harus menentukan _baik_ crate root _maupun_ daftar lengkap berkas "
"sumber. `crate_root` adalah berkas yang diberikan kepada compiler Rust yang "
"merepresentasikan berkas root unit kompilasi --- biasanya `lib.rs`. "
"`sources` adalah daftar lengkap semua berkas sumber yang dibutuhkan `ninja` "
"untuk menentukan kapan rebuild diperlukan."

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"(There's no such thing as a Rust `source_set`, because in Rust, an entire "
"crate is a compilation unit. A `static_library` is the smallest unit.)"
msgstr ""
"(Tidak ada yang namanya `source_set` Rust, karena di Rust, seluruh crate "
"adalah satu unit kompilasi. `static_library` adalah unit terkecil.)"

#: src/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"Students might be wondering why we need a gn template, rather than using "
"[gn's built-in support for Rust static "
"libraries](https://gn.googlesource.com/gn/+/main/docs/reference.md#func_static_library)."
" The answer is that this template provides support for CXX interop, Rust "
"features, and unit tests, some of which we'll use later."
msgstr ""
"Siswa mungkin bertanya-tanya mengapa kita memerlukan template gn, alih-alih "
"menggunakan [dukungan bawaan gn untuk library statis "
"Rust](https://gn.googlesource.com/gn/+/main/docs/reference.md#func_static_library)."
" Jawabannya adalah template ini menyediakan dukungan untuk interop CXX, "
"fitur Rust, dan unit test, yang sebagian akan kita gunakan nanti."

#: src/chromium/build-rules/unsafe.md
msgid "Including `unsafe` Rust Code"
msgstr "Menyertakan Kode Rust `unsafe`"

#: src/chromium/build-rules/unsafe.md
msgid ""
"Unsafe Rust code is forbidden in `rust_static_library` by default --- it "
"won't compile. If you need unsafe Rust code, add `allow_unsafe = true` to "
"the gn target. (Later in the course we'll see circumstances where this is "
"necessary.)"
msgstr ""
"Kode Rust unsafe dilarang dalam `rust_static_library` secara default --- "
"kode tidak akan dikompilasi. Jika Anda memerlukan kode Rust unsafe, "
"tambahkan `allow_unsafe = true` ke target gn. (Nanti dalam kursus kita akan "
"melihat situasi yang mengharuskan hal ini.)"

#: src/chromium/build-rules/unsafe.md
msgid ""
"```gn\n"
"import(\"//build/rust/rust_static_library.gni\")\n"
"\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib\") {\n"
"  crate_root = \"lib.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [\n"
"    \"lib.rs\",\n"
"    \"hippopotamus.rs\"\n"
"  ]\n"
"  allow_unsafe = true\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```gn\n"
"import(\"//build/rust/rust_static_library.gni\")\n"
"\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib\") {\n"
"  crate_root = \"lib.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [\n"
"    \"lib.rs\",\n"
"    \"hippopotamus.rs\"\n"
"  ]\n"
"  allow_unsafe = true\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/build-rules/depending.md
msgid "Simply add the above target to the `deps` of some Chromium C++ target."
msgstr ""
"Cukup tambahkan target di atas ke `deps` target C++ Chromium tertentu."

#: src/chromium/build-rules/depending.md
msgid ""
"```gn\n"
"import(\"//build/rust/rust_static_library.gni\")\n"
"\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib\") {\n"
"  crate_root = \"lib.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [ \"lib.rs\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"# or source_set, static_library etc.\n"
"component(\"preexisting_cpp\") {\n"
"  deps = [ \":my_rust_lib\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```gn\n"
"import(\"//build/rust/rust_static_library.gni\")\n"
"\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib\") {\n"
"  crate_root = \"lib.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [ \"lib.rs\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"# or source_set, static_library etc.\n"
"component(\"preexisting_cpp\") {\n"
"  deps = [ \":my_rust_lib\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/build-rules/vscode.md
msgid ""
"Types are elided in Rust code, which makes a good IDE even more useful than "
"for C++. Visual Studio code works well for Rust in Chromium. To use it,"
