#: src/exercises/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"This example is unusual because it boils down to the lowest-common-"
"denominator interop language, C. Both C++ and Rust can natively declare and "
"call C ABI functions. Later in the course, we'll connect C++ directly to "
"Rust."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini tidak biasa karena pada dasarnya menggunakan bahasa interop "
"penyebut terkecil, yaitu C. Baik C++ maupun Rust dapat secara native "
"mendeklarasikan dan memanggil fungsi ABI C. Nanti dalam kursus, kami akan "
"menghubungkan C++ langsung ke Rust."

#: src/exercises/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"`allow_unsafe = true` is required here because `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` might "
"allow Rust to generate two functions with the same name, and Rust can no "
"longer guarantee that the right one is called."
msgstr ""
"`allow_unsafe = true` diperlukan di sini karena `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` dapat"
" memungkinkan Rust menghasilkan dua fungsi dengan nama yang sama, dan Rust "
"tidak lagi dapat menjamin bahwa fungsi yang benar yang dipanggil."

#: src/exercises/chromium/build-rules.md
msgid ""
"If you need a pure Rust executable, you can also do that using the "
"`rust_executable` gn template."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda memerlukan executable Rust murni, Anda juga dapat melakukannya "
"menggunakan template gn `rust_executable`."

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"Rust community typically authors unit tests in a module placed in the same "
"source file as the code being tested. This was covered "
"[earlier](../testing.md) in the course and looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Komunitas Rust biasanya menulis unit test dalam modul yang ditempatkan pada "
"berkas sumber yang sama dengan kode yang diuji. Ini telah dibahas "
"[sebelumnya](../testing.md) dalam kursus dan tampak seperti ini:"

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"In Chromium we place unit tests in a separate source file and we continue to"
" follow this practice for Rust --- this makes tests consistently "
"discoverable and helps to avoid rebuilding `.rs` files a second time (in the"
" `test` configuration)."
msgstr ""
"Di Chromium kami menempatkan unit test pada berkas sumber terpisah dan kami "
"terus mengikuti praktik ini untuk Rust --- ini membuat test selalu dapat "
"ditemukan dan membantu menghindari build ulang berkas `.rs` untuk kedua "
"kalinya (pada konfigurasi `test`)."

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"This results in the following options for testing Rust code in Chromium:"
msgstr "Ini menghasilkan opsi berikut untuk menguji kode Rust di Chromium:"

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"Native Rust tests (i.e. `#[test]`). Discouraged outside of "
"`//third_party/rust`."
msgstr ""
"Test Rust native (yaitu `#[test]`). Tidak dianjurkan di luar "
"`//third_party/rust`."

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"`gtest` tests authored in C++ and exercising Rust via FFI calls. Sufficient "
"when Rust code is just a thin FFI layer and the existing unit tests provide "
"sufficient coverage for the feature."
msgstr ""
"Test `gtest` yang ditulis dalam C++ dan menguji Rust melalui pemanggilan "
"FFI. Cukup ketika kode Rust hanya lapisan FFI tipis dan unit test yang ada "
"memberikan cakupan yang memadai untuk fitur tersebut."

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"`gtest` tests authored in Rust and using the crate under test through its "
"public API (using `pub mod for_testing { ... }` if needed). This is the "
"subject of the next few slides."
msgstr ""
"Test `gtest` yang ditulis dalam Rust dan menggunakan crate yang diuji "
"melalui API publiknya (menggunakan `pub mod for_testing { ... }` jika "
"perlu). Ini adalah topik beberapa slide berikutnya."

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"Mention that native Rust tests of third-party crates should eventually be "
"exercised by Chromium bots. (Such testing is needed rarely --- only after "
"adding or updating third-party crates.)"
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa test Rust native untuk crate pihak ketiga pada akhirnya "
"sebaiknya dijalankan oleh bot Chromium. (Pengujian semacam itu jarang "
"diperlukan --- hanya setelah menambahkan atau memperbarui crate pihak "
"ketiga.)"

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"Some examples may help illustrate when C++ `gtest` vs Rust `gtest` should be"
" used:"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa contoh dapat membantu mengilustrasikan kapan `gtest` C++ versus "
"`gtest` Rust sebaiknya digunakan:"

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"QR has very little functionality in the first-party Rust layer (it's just a "
"thin FFI glue) and therefore uses the existing C++ unit tests for testing "
"both the C++ and the Rust implementation (parameterizing the tests so they "
"enable or disable Rust using a `ScopedFeatureList`)."
msgstr ""
"QR memiliki sangat sedikit fungsionalitas pada lapisan Rust first-party "
"(hanya glue FFI tipis) dan karena itu menggunakan unit test C++ yang sudah "
"ada untuk menguji implementasi C++ maupun Rust (dengan memparameterkan test "
"agar mengaktifkan atau menonaktifkan Rust menggunakan `ScopedFeatureList`)."

#: src/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"Hypothetical/WIP PNG integration may need memory-safe implementations of "
"pixel transformations that are provided by `libpng` but missing in the `png`"
" crate - e.g. RGBA => BGRA, or gamma correction. Such functionality may "
"benefit from separate tests authored in Rust."
msgstr ""
"Integrasi PNG hipotetis/WIP mungkin memerlukan implementasi transformasi "
"piksel yang aman terhadap memori, yang disediakan `libpng` tetapi tidak ada "
"di crate `png` - misalnya RGBA => BGRA, atau koreksi gamma. Fungsionalitas "
"semacam itu mungkin memperoleh manfaat dari test terpisah yang ditulis dalam"
" Rust."

#: src/chromium/testing/rust-gtest-interop.md
msgid ""
"The "
"[`rust_gtest_interop`](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/testing/rust_gtest_interop/README.md)"
" library provides a way to:"
msgstr ""
"Library "
"[`rust_gtest_interop`](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/testing/rust_gtest_interop/README.md)"
" menyediakan cara untuk:"

#: src/chromium/testing/rust-gtest-interop.md
msgid ""
"Use a Rust function as a `gtest` testcase (using the `#[gtest(...)]` "
"attribute)"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan fungsi Rust sebagai testcase `gtest` (menggunakan atribut "
"`#[gtest(...)]`)"

#: src/chromium/testing/rust-gtest-interop.md
msgid ""
"Use `expect_eq!` and similar macros (similar to `assert_eq!` but not "
"panicking and not terminating the test when the assertion fails)."
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan `expect_eq!` dan macro serupa (serupa dengan `assert_eq!` tetapi"
" tidak panic dan tidak menghentikan test ketika assertion gagal)."

#: src/chromium/testing/rust-gtest-interop.md
msgid "Example:"
msgstr "Contoh:"

#: src/chromium/testing/build-gn.md
msgid ""
"The simplest way to build Rust `gtest` tests is to add them to an existing "
"test binary that already contains tests authored in C++. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cara paling sederhana untuk membangun test `gtest` Rust adalah "
"menambahkannya ke binary test yang sudah ada dan sudah berisi test yang "
"ditulis dalam C++. Sebagai contoh:"

#: src/chromium/testing/build-gn.md
msgid ""
"```gn\n"
"test(\"ui_base_unittests\") {\n"
"  ...\n"
"  sources += [ \"my_rust_lib_unittest.rs\" ]\n"
"  deps += [ \":my_rust_lib\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```gn\n"
"test(\"ui_base_unittests\") {\n"
"  ...\n"
"  sources += [ \"my_rust_lib_unittest.rs\" ]\n"
"  deps += [ \":my_rust_lib\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/testing/build-gn.md
msgid ""
"Authoring Rust tests in a separate `static_library` also works, but requires"
" manually declaring the dependency on the support libraries:"
msgstr ""
"Menulis test Rust dalam `static_library` terpisah juga dapat dilakukan, "
"tetapi mengharuskan deklarasi dependensi pada library pendukung secara "
"manual:"

#: src/chromium/testing/build-gn.md
msgid ""
"```gn\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib_unittests\") {\n"
"  testonly = true\n"
"  is_gtest_unittests = true\n"
"  crate_root = \"my_rust_lib_unittest.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [ \"my_rust_lib_unittest.rs\" ]\n"
"  deps = [\n"
"    \":my_rust_lib\",\n"
"    \"//testing/rust_gtest_interop\",\n"
"  ]\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"test(\"ui_base_unittests\") {\n"
"  ...\n"
"  deps += [ \":my_rust_lib_unittests\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```gn\n"
"rust_static_library(\"my_rust_lib_unittests\") {\n"
"  testonly = true\n"
"  is_gtest_unittests = true\n"
"  crate_root = \"my_rust_lib_unittest.rs\"\n"
"  sources = [ \"my_rust_lib_unittest.rs\" ]\n"
"  deps = [\n"
"    \":my_rust_lib\",\n"
"    \"//testing/rust_gtest_interop\",\n"
"  ]\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"test(\"ui_base_unittests\") {\n"
"  ...\n"
"  deps += [ \":my_rust_lib_unittests\" ]\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/testing/chromium-import-macro.md
msgid ""
"After adding `:my_rust_lib` to GN `deps`, we still need to learn how to "
"import and use `my_rust_lib` from `my_rust_lib_unittest.rs`. We haven't "
"provided an explicit `crate_name` for `my_rust_lib` so its crate name is "
"computed based on the full target path and name. Fortunately we can avoid "
"working with such an unwieldy name by using the `chromium::import!` macro "
"from the automatically-imported `chromium` crate:"
msgstr ""
"Setelah menambahkan `:my_rust_lib` ke `deps` GN, kita masih perlu "
"mempelajari cara mengimpor dan menggunakan `my_rust_lib` dari "
"`my_rust_lib_unittest.rs`. Kami belum menyediakan `crate_name` eksplisit "
"untuk `my_rust_lib`, sehingga nama crate-nya dihitung berdasarkan path dan "
"nama target lengkap. Untungnya kita dapat menghindari penggunaan nama yang "
"tidak praktis tersebut dengan menggunakan macro `chromium::import!` dari "
"crate `chromium` yang diimpor secara otomatis:"

#: src/chromium/testing/chromium-import-macro.md
msgid "\"//ui/base:my_rust_lib\""
msgstr "\"//ui/base:my_rust_lib\""

#: src/chromium/testing/chromium-import-macro.md
msgid "Under the covers the macro expands to something similar to:"
msgstr ""
"Di balik layar, macro tersebut diperluas menjadi sesuatu yang serupa dengan:"

#: src/chromium/testing/chromium-import-macro.md
msgid ""
"More information can be found in [the doc "
"comment](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/rust/chromium_prelude/chromium_prelude.rs?q=f:chromium_prelude.rs%20pub.use.*%5Cbimport%5Cb;%20-f:third_party&ss=chromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc)"
" of the `chromium::import` macro."
msgstr ""
"Informasi lebih lanjut dapat ditemukan di [doc "
"comment](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/rust/chromium_prelude/chromium_prelude.rs?q=f:chromium_prelude.rs%20pub.use.*%5Cbimport%5Cb;%20-f:third_party&ss=chromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc)"
" macro `chromium::import`."

#: src/chromium/testing/chromium-import-macro.md
msgid ""
"`rust_static_library` supports specifying an explicit name via `crate_name` "
"property, but doing this is discouraged. And it is discouraged because the "
"crate name has to be globally unique. crates.io guarantees uniqueness of its"
" crate names so `cargo_crate` GN targets (generated by the `gnrt` tool "
"covered in a later section) use short crate names."
msgstr ""
"`rust_static_library` mendukung penentuan nama eksplisit melalui properti "
"`crate_name`, tetapi hal ini tidak dianjurkan. Tidak dianjurkan karena nama "
"crate harus unik secara global. crates.io menjamin keunikan nama crate-nya, "
"sehingga target GN `cargo_crate` (yang dihasilkan oleh alat `gnrt` yang "
"dibahas di bagian selanjutnya) menggunakan nama crate pendek."

#: src/exercises/chromium/testing.md
msgid "Testing exercise"
msgstr "Latihan Testing"

#: src/exercises/chromium/testing.md
msgid "Time for another exercise!"
msgstr "Waktunya latihan lagi!"

#: src/exercises/chromium/testing.md
msgid "In your Chromium build:"
msgstr "Pada build Chromium Anda:"

#: src/exercises/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"Add a testable function next to `hello_from_rust`. Some suggestions: adding "
"two integers received as arguments, computing the nth Fibonacci number, "
"summing integers in a slice, etc."
msgstr ""
"Tambahkan fungsi yang dapat diuji di samping `hello_from_rust`. Beberapa "
"saran: menjumlahkan dua integer yang diterima sebagai argumen, menghitung "
"bilangan Fibonacci ke-n, menjumlahkan integer dalam slice, dan sebagainya."

#: src/exercises/chromium/testing.md
msgid ""
"Add a separate `..._unittest.rs` file with a test for the new function."
msgstr ""
"Tambahkan berkas `..._unittest.rs` terpisah dengan test untuk fungsi baru "
"tersebut."

#: src/exercises/chromium/testing.md
msgid "Add the new tests to `BUILD.gn`."
msgstr "Tambahkan test baru ke `BUILD.gn`."

#: src/exercises/chromium/testing.md
msgid "Build the tests, run them, and verify that the new test works."
msgstr "Build test, jalankan, dan verifikasi bahwa test baru berfungsi."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"The Rust community offers multiple options for C++/Rust interop, with new "
"tools being developed all the time. At the moment, Chromium uses a tool "
"called CXX."
msgstr ""
"Komunitas Rust menawarkan beberapa opsi untuk interop C++/Rust, dengan alat "
"baru yang terus dikembangkan. Saat ini, Chromium menggunakan alat bernama "
"CXX."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"You describe your whole language boundary in an interface definition "
"language (which closely resembles Rust) and then CXX tools generate "
"declarations for functions and types in both Rust and C++."
msgstr ""
"Anda mendeskripsikan seluruh batas bahasa dalam interface definition "
"language (yang sangat mirip dengan Rust), lalu alat CXX menghasilkan "
"deklarasi fungsi dan tipe di Rust maupun C++."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"See the [CXX tutorial](https://cxx.rs/tutorial.html) for a full example of "
"using this."
msgstr ""
"Lihat [tutorial CXX](https://cxx.rs/tutorial.html) untuk contoh lengkap "
"penggunaannya."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Talk through the diagram. Explain that behind the scenes, this is doing just"
" the same as you previously did. Point out that automating the process has "
"the following benefits:"
msgstr ""
"Bahas diagramnya. Jelaskan bahwa di balik layar, ini melakukan hal yang sama"
" seperti yang Anda lakukan sebelumnya. Tunjukkan bahwa mengotomatiskan "
"proses tersebut memiliki manfaat berikut:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"The tool guarantees that the C++ and Rust sides match (e.g. you get compile "
"errors if the `#[cxx::bridge]` doesn't match the actual C++ or Rust "
"definitions, but with out-of-sync manual bindings you'd get Undefined "
"Behavior)"
msgstr ""
"Alat ini menjamin sisi C++ dan Rust sesuai (misalnya Anda mendapatkan error "
"kompilasi jika `#[cxx::bridge]` tidak sesuai dengan definisi C++ atau Rust "
"yang sebenarnya, sedangkan dengan binding manual yang tidak sinkron Anda "
"akan mendapatkan Undefined Behavior)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"The tool automates generation of FFI thunks (small, C-ABI-compatible, free "
"functions) for non-C features (e.g. enabling FFI calls into Rust or C++ "
"methods; manual bindings would require authoring such top-level, free "
"functions manually)"
msgstr ""
"Alat ini mengotomatiskan pembuatan thunk FFI (fungsi bebas kecil yang "
"kompatibel dengan C-ABI) untuk fitur non-C (misalnya memungkinkan "
"pemanggilan FFI ke method Rust atau C++; binding manual akan mengharuskan "
"penulisan fungsi bebas tingkat atas semacam itu secara manual)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "The tool and the library can handle a set of core types - for example:"
msgstr "Alat dan library dapat menangani sekumpulan tipe inti - misalnya:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"`&[T]` can be passed across the FFI boundary, even though it doesn't "
"guarantee any particular ABI or memory layout. With manual bindings "
"`std::span<T>` / `&[T]` have to be manually destructured and rebuilt out of "
"a pointer and length - this is error-prone given that each language "
"represents empty slices slightly differently)"
msgstr ""
"`&[T]` dapat diteruskan melintasi batas FFI, meskipun tidak menjamin ABI "
"atau layout memori tertentu. Dengan binding manual, `std::span<T>` / `&[T]` "
"harus di-destructure dan dibangun kembali secara manual dari pointer dan "
"panjang - ini rawan error karena setiap bahasa merepresentasikan slice "
"kosong sedikit berbeda)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Smart pointers like `std::unique_ptr<T>`, `std::shared_ptr<T>`, and/or `Box`"
" are natively supported. With manual bindings, one would have to pass C-ABI-"
"compatible raw pointers, which would increase lifetime and memory-safety "
"risks."
msgstr ""
"Smart pointer seperti `std::unique_ptr<T>`, `std::shared_ptr<T>`, dan/atau "
"`Box` didukung secara native. Dengan binding manual, seseorang harus "
"meneruskan raw pointer yang kompatibel dengan C-ABI, yang akan meningkatkan "
"risiko lifetime dan keamanan memori."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"`rust::String` and `CxxString` types understand and maintain differences in "
"string representation across the languages (e.g. `rust::String::lossy` can "
"build a Rust string from non-UTF-8 input and `rust::String::c_str` can NUL-"
"terminate a string)."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `rust::String` dan `CxxString` memahami dan mempertahankan perbedaan "
"representasi string antarbahasa (misalnya `rust::String::lossy` dapat "
"membangun string Rust dari input non-UTF-8 dan `rust::String::c_str` dapat "
"memberi terminator NUL pada string)."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid ""
"CXX requires that the whole C++/Rust boundary is declared in `cxx::bridge` "
"modules inside `.rs` source code."
msgstr ""
"CXX mengharuskan seluruh batas C++/Rust dideklarasikan dalam modul "
"`cxx::bridge` di dalam kode sumber `.rs`."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid "\"example/include/blobstore.h\""
msgstr "\"example/include/blobstore.h\""

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid "// Definitions of Rust types and functions go here\n"
msgstr "// Definitions of Rust types and functions go here\n"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid "Point out:"
msgstr "Tunjukkan:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid ""
"Although this looks like a regular Rust `mod`, the `#[cxx::bridge]` "
"procedural macro does complex things to it. The generated code is quite a "
"bit more sophisticated - though this does still result in a `mod` called "
"`ffi` in your code."
msgstr ""
"Meskipun ini tampak seperti `mod` Rust biasa, macro prosedural "
"`#[cxx::bridge]` melakukan hal-hal kompleks terhadapnya. Kode yang "
"dihasilkan jauh lebih canggih - meskipun ini tetap menghasilkan `mod` "
"bernama `ffi` dalam kode Anda."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid "Native support for C++'s `std::unique_ptr` in Rust"
msgstr "Dukungan native untuk `std::unique_ptr` milik C++ di Rust"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid "Native support for Rust slices in C++"
msgstr "Dukungan native untuk slice Rust di C++"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid "Calls from C++ to Rust, and Rust types (in the top part)"
msgstr "Pemanggilan dari C++ ke Rust, dan tipe Rust (pada bagian atas)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid "Calls from Rust to C++, and C++ types (in the bottom part)"
msgstr "Pemanggilan dari Rust ke C++, dan tipe C++ (pada bagian bawah)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/example-bindings.md
msgid ""
"**Common misconception:** It _looks_ like a C++ header is being parsed by "
"Rust, but this is misleading. This header is never interpreted by Rust, but "
"simply `#include`d in the generated C++ code for the benefit of C++ "
"compilers."
msgstr ""
"**Kesalahpahaman umum:** Ini _terlihat_ seperti header C++ sedang diurai "
"oleh Rust, tetapi hal itu menyesatkan. Header ini tidak pernah "
"diinterpretasikan oleh Rust, melainkan hanya di-`#include` dalam kode C++ "
"yang dihasilkan untuk kepentingan compiler C++."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid ""
"By far the most useful page when using CXX is the [type "
"reference](https://cxx.rs/bindings.html)."
msgstr ""
"Halaman yang jauh paling berguna saat menggunakan CXX adalah [referensi "
"tipe](https://cxx.rs/bindings.html)."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid "CXX fundamentally suits cases where:"
msgstr "CXX secara fundamental cocok untuk kasus ketika:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid ""
"Your Rust-C++ interface is sufficiently simple that you can declare all of "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Antarmuka Rust-C++ Anda cukup sederhana sehingga Anda dapat mendeklarasikan "
"seluruhnya."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid ""
"You're using only the types natively supported by CXX already, for example "
"`std::unique_ptr`, `std::string`, `&[u8]` etc."
msgstr ""
"Anda hanya menggunakan tipe yang sudah didukung secara native oleh CXX, "
"misalnya `std::unique_ptr`, `std::string`, `&[u8]`, dan sebagainya."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid ""
"It has many limitations --- for example lack of support for Rust's `Option` "
"type."
msgstr ""
"CXX memiliki banyak keterbatasan --- misalnya kurangnya dukungan untuk tipe "
"`Option` milik Rust."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid ""
"These limitations constrain us to using Rust in Chromium only for well "
"isolated \"leaf nodes\" rather than for arbitrary Rust-C++ interop. When "
"considering a use-case for Rust in Chromium, a good starting point is to "
"draft the CXX bindings for the language boundary to see if it appears simple"
" enough."
msgstr ""
"Keterbatasan ini membatasi kami untuk menggunakan Rust di Chromium hanya "
"pada \"leaf node\" yang terisolasi baik, bukan untuk interop Rust-C++ "
"arbitrer. Saat mempertimbangkan kasus penggunaan Rust di Chromium, titik "
"awal yang baik adalah menyusun draf binding CXX untuk batas bahasa tersebut "
"guna melihat apakah tampak cukup sederhana."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid ""
"You should also discuss some of the other sticky points with CXX, for "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Anda juga sebaiknya mendiskusikan beberapa titik rumit lain dengan CXX, "
"misalnya:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid ""
"Its error handling is based around C++ exceptions (given on the next slide)"
msgstr ""
"Penanganan error-nya berbasis exception C++ (dijelaskan pada slide "
"berikutnya)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/limitations-of-cxx.md
msgid "Function pointers are awkward to use."
msgstr "Function pointer sulit digunakan."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid ""
"CXX's [support for `Result<T,E>`](https://cxx.rs/binding/result.html) relies"
" on C++ exceptions, so we can't use that in Chromium. Alternatives:"
msgstr ""
"[Dukungan CXX untuk `Result<T,E>`](https://cxx.rs/binding/result.html) "
"bergantung pada exception C++, sehingga kami tidak dapat menggunakannya di "
"Chromium. Alternatifnya:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid "The `T` part of `Result<T, E>` can be:"
msgstr "Bagian `T` dari `Result<T, E>` dapat:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid ""
"Returned via out parameters (e.g. via `&mut T`). This requires that `T` can "
"be passed across the FFI boundary - for example `T` has to be:"
msgstr ""
"Dikembalikan melalui out parameter (misalnya melalui `&mut T`). Ini "
"mengharuskan `T` dapat diteruskan melintasi batas FFI - misalnya `T` harus:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid "A primitive type (like `u32` or `usize`)"
msgstr "Tipe primitif (seperti `u32` atau `usize`)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid ""
"A type natively supported by `cxx` (like `UniquePtr<T>`) that has a suitable"
" default value to use in a failure case (_unlike_ `Box<T>`)."
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang didukung secara native oleh `cxx` (seperti `UniquePtr<T>`) yang "
"memiliki nilai default sesuai untuk digunakan pada kasus kegagalan (_berbeda"
" dengan_ `Box<T>`)."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid ""
"Retained on the Rust side, and exposed via reference. This may be needed "
"when `T` is a Rust type, which cannot be passed across the FFI boundary, and"
" cannot be stored in `UniquePtr<T>`."
msgstr ""
"Dipertahankan di sisi Rust, dan diekspos melalui reference. Ini mungkin "
"diperlukan ketika `T` adalah tipe Rust, yang tidak dapat diteruskan "
"melintasi batas FFI, dan tidak dapat disimpan dalam `UniquePtr<T>`."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid "The `E` part of `Result<T, E>` can be:"
msgstr "Bagian `E` dari `Result<T, E>` dapat:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid ""
"Returned as a boolean (e.g. `true` representing success, and `false` "
"representing failure)"
msgstr ""
"Dikembalikan sebagai boolean (misalnya `true` merepresentasikan "
"keberhasilan, dan `false` merepresentasikan kegagalan)"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling.md
msgid ""
"Preserving error details is in theory possible, but so far hasn't been "
"needed in practice."
msgstr ""
"Mempertahankan detail error secara teori mungkin dilakukan, tetapi sejauh "
"ini belum diperlukan dalam praktik."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-qr.md
msgid "CXX Error Handling: QR Example"
msgstr "Penanganan Error CXX: Contoh QR"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-qr.md
msgid ""
"The QR code generator is [an "
"example](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:components/qr_code_generator/qr_code_generator_ffi_glue.rs;l=13-18;drc=7bf1b75b910ca430501b9c6a74c1d18a0223ecca)"
" where a boolean is used to communicate success vs failure, and where the "
"successful result can be passed across the FFI boundary:"
msgstr ""
"Generator kode QR adalah "
"[contoh](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:components/qr_code_generator/qr_code_generator_ffi_glue.rs;l=13-18;drc=7bf1b75b910ca430501b9c6a74c1d18a0223ecca)"
" ketika boolean digunakan untuk mengomunikasikan keberhasilan versus "
"kegagalan, dan ketika hasil yang berhasil dapat diteruskan melintasi batas "
"FFI:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-qr.md
msgid "\"qr_code_generator\""
msgstr "\"qr_code_generator\""

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-qr.md
msgid ""
"Students may be curious about the semantics of the `out_qr_size` output. "
"This is not the size of the vector, but the size of the QR code (and "
"admittedly it is a bit redundant - this is the square root of the size of "
"the vector)."
msgstr ""
"Siswa mungkin penasaran dengan semantik output `out_qr_size`. Ini bukan "
"ukuran vector, melainkan ukuran kode QR (dan memang agak redundan - ini "
"adalah akar kuadrat dari ukuran vector)."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-qr.md
msgid ""
"It may be worth pointing out the importance of initializing `out_qr_size` "
"before calling into the Rust function. Creation of a Rust reference that "
"points to uninitialized memory results in Undefined Behavior (unlike in C++,"
" when only the act of dereferencing such memory results in UB)."
msgstr ""
"Mungkin perlu ditunjukkan pentingnya menginisialisasi `out_qr_size` sebelum "
"memanggil fungsi Rust. Pembuatan reference Rust yang menunjuk ke memori yang"
" belum diinisialisasi menghasilkan Undefined Behavior (berbeda dari C++, "
"ketika hanya tindakan melakukan dereference memori tersebut yang "
"menghasilkan UB)."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-qr.md
msgid ""
"If students ask about `Pin`, then explain why CXX needs it for mutable "
"references to C++ data: the answer is that C++ data can’t be moved around "
"like Rust data, because it may contain self-referential pointers."
msgstr ""
"Jika siswa bertanya tentang `Pin`, jelaskan mengapa CXX memerlukannya untuk "
"mutable reference ke data C++: jawabannya adalah data C++ tidak dapat "
"dipindahkan seperti data Rust, karena mungkin berisi pointer yang "
"mereferensikan dirinya sendiri."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid "CXX Error Handling: PNG Example"
msgstr "Penanganan Error CXX: Contoh PNG"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid ""
"A prototype of a PNG decoder illustrates what can be done when the "
"successful result cannot be passed across the FFI boundary:"
msgstr ""
"Prototipe decoder PNG mengilustrasikan apa yang dapat dilakukan ketika hasil"
" yang berhasil tidak dapat diteruskan melintasi batas FFI:"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid "\"gfx::rust_bindings\""
msgstr "\"gfx::rust_bindings\""

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid ""
"/// This returns an FFI-friendly equivalent of `Result<PngReader<'a>,\n"
"        /// ()>`.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// This returns an FFI-friendly equivalent of `Result<PngReader<'a>,\n"
"        /// ()>`.\n"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid "/// C++ bindings for the `crate::png::ResultOfPngReader` type.\n"
msgstr "/// C++ bindings for the `crate::png::ResultOfPngReader` type.\n"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid "/// C++ bindings for the `crate::png::PngReader` type.\n"
msgstr "/// C++ bindings for the `crate::png::PngReader` type.\n"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid ""
"`PngReader` and `ResultOfPngReader` are Rust types --- objects of these "
"types cannot cross the FFI boundary without indirection of a `Box<T>`. We "
"can't have an `out_parameter: &mut PngReader`, because CXX doesn't allow C++"
" to store Rust objects by value."
msgstr ""
"`PngReader` dan `ResultOfPngReader` adalah tipe Rust --- objek bertipe ini "
"tidak dapat melintasi batas FFI tanpa indirection berupa `Box<T>`. Kita "
"tidak dapat memiliki `out_parameter: &mut PngReader`, karena CXX tidak "
"mengizinkan C++ menyimpan objek Rust by value."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/error-handling-png.md
msgid ""
"This example illustrates that even though CXX doesn't support arbitrary "
"generics nor templates, we can still pass them across the FFI boundary by "
"manually specializing / monomorphizing them into a non-generic type. In the "
"example `ResultOfPngReader` is a non-generic type that forwards into "
"appropriate methods of `Result<T, E>` (e.g. into `is_err`, `unwrap`, and/or "
"`as_mut`)."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini mengilustrasikan bahwa meskipun CXX tidak mendukung generic atau "
"template arbitrer, kita tetap dapat meneruskannya melintasi batas FFI dengan"
" melakukan spesialisasi / monomorphization secara manual menjadi tipe non-"
"generic. Dalam contoh, `ResultOfPngReader` adalah tipe non-generic yang "
"meneruskan ke method yang sesuai dari `Result<T, E>` (misalnya ke `is_err`, "
"`unwrap`, dan/atau `as_mut`)."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid "Using cxx in Chromium"
msgstr "Menggunakan cxx di Chromium"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid ""
"In Chromium, we define an independent `#[cxx::bridge] mod` for each leaf-"
"node where we want to use Rust. You'd typically have one for each "
"`rust_static_library`. Just add"
msgstr ""
"Di Chromium, kami mendefinisikan `#[cxx::bridge] mod` independen untuk "
"setiap leaf node tempat kami ingin menggunakan Rust. Biasanya Anda memiliki "
"satu untuk setiap `rust_static_library`. Cukup tambahkan"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid ""
"```gn\n"
"cxx_bindings = [ \"my_rust_file.rs\" ]\n"
"   # list of files containing #[cxx::bridge], not all source files\n"
"allow_unsafe = true\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```gn\n"
"cxx_bindings = [ \"my_rust_file.rs\" ]\n"
"   # list of files containing #[cxx::bridge], not all source files\n"
"allow_unsafe = true\n"
"```"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid ""
"to your existing `rust_static_library` target alongside `crate_root` and "
"`sources`."
msgstr ""
"ke target `rust_static_library` yang sudah ada, bersama `crate_root` dan "
"`sources`."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid "C++ headers will be generated at a sensible location, so you can just"
msgstr "Header C++ akan dihasilkan di lokasi yang sesuai, jadi Anda cukup"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid "\"ui/base/my_rust_file.rs.h\""
msgstr "\"ui/base/my_rust_file.rs.h\""

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid ""
"You will find some utility functions in `//base` to convert to/from Chromium"
" C++ types to CXX Rust types --- for example "
"[`SpanToRustSlice`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:base/containers/span_rust.h;l=21)."
msgstr ""
"Anda akan menemukan beberapa fungsi utilitas di `//base` untuk mengonversi "
"ke/dari tipe C++ Chromium ke tipe Rust CXX --- misalnya "
"[`SpanToRustSlice`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:base/containers/span_rust.h;l=21)."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid "Students may ask --- why do we still need `allow_unsafe = true`?"
msgstr ""
"Siswa mungkin bertanya --- mengapa kita masih memerlukan `allow_unsafe = "
"true`?"

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid ""
"The broad answer is that no C/C++ code is \"safe\" by the normal Rust "
"standards. Calling back and forth to C/C++ from Rust may do arbitrary things"
" to memory, and compromise the safety of Rust's own data layouts. Presence "
"of _too many_ `unsafe` keywords in C/C++ interop can harm the signal-to-"
"noise ratio of such a keyword, and is "
"[controversial](https://steveklabnik.com/writing/the-cxx-debate), but "
"strictly, bringing any foreign code into a Rust binary can cause unexpected "
"behavior from Rust's perspective."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban luasnya adalah tidak ada kode C/C++ yang \"safe\" menurut standar "
"Rust normal. Memanggil bolak-balik ke C/C++ dari Rust dapat melakukan hal "
"arbitrer terhadap memori, dan mengompromikan keamanan layout data Rust "
"sendiri. Kehadiran _terlalu banyak_ keyword `unsafe` dalam interop C/C++ "
"dapat merusak rasio signal-to-noise keyword tersebut, dan hal ini "
"[kontroversial](https://steveklabnik.com/writing/the-cxx-debate), tetapi "
"secara ketat, membawa kode asing apa pun ke dalam binary Rust dapat "
"menyebabkan perilaku tak terduga dari perspektif Rust."

#: src/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp/using-cxx-in-chromium.md
msgid ""
"The narrow answer lies in the diagram at the top of [this "
"page](../interoperability-with-cpp.md) --- behind the scenes, CXX generates "
"Rust `unsafe` and `extern \"C\"` functions just like we did manually in the "
"previous section."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban sempitnya terletak pada diagram di bagian atas [halaman "
"ini](../interoperability-with-cpp.md) --- di balik layar, CXX menghasilkan "
"fungsi Rust `unsafe` dan `extern \"C\"` seperti yang kami lakukan secara "
"manual pada bagian sebelumnya."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Exercise: Interoperability with C++"
msgstr "Latihan: Interoperabilitas dengan C++"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Part one"
msgstr "Bagian satu"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"In the Rust file you previously created, add a `#[cxx::bridge]` which "
"specifies a single function, to be called from C++, called "
"`hello_from_rust`, taking no parameters and returning no value."
msgstr ""
"Pada berkas Rust yang Anda buat sebelumnya, tambahkan `#[cxx::bridge]` yang "
"menentukan satu fungsi untuk dipanggil dari C++, bernama `hello_from_rust`, "
"tanpa parameter dan tanpa nilai kembalian."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Modify your previous `hello_from_rust` function to remove `extern \"C\"` and"
" `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`. This is now just a standard Rust function."
msgstr ""
"Ubah fungsi `hello_from_rust` sebelumnya dengan menghapus `extern \"C\"` dan"
" `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`. Sekarang ini hanyalah fungsi Rust standar."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Modify your `gn` target to build these bindings."
msgstr "Ubah target `gn` Anda untuk membangun binding tersebut."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"In your C++ code, remove the forward-declaration of `hello_from_rust`. "
"Instead, include the generated header file."
msgstr ""
"Pada kode C++ Anda, hapus forward declaration `hello_from_rust`. Sebagai "
"gantinya, sertakan berkas header yang dihasilkan."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Build and run!"
msgstr "Build dan jalankan!"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Part two"
msgstr "Bagian dua"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"It's a good idea to play with CXX a little. It helps you think about how "
"flexible Rust in Chromium actually is."
msgstr ""
"Ide bagus untuk sedikit bermain dengan CXX. Ini membantu Anda memikirkan "
"seberapa fleksibel Rust di Chromium sebenarnya."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Some things to try:"
msgstr "Beberapa hal untuk dicoba:"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Call back into C++ from Rust. You will need:"
msgstr "Memanggil balik ke C++ dari Rust. Anda akan memerlukan:"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"An additional header file which you can `include!` from your `cxx::bridge`. "
"You'll need to declare your C++ function in that new header file."
msgstr ""
"Berkas header tambahan yang dapat Anda `include!` dari `cxx::bridge` Anda. "
"Anda perlu mendeklarasikan fungsi C++ Anda di berkas header baru tersebut."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"An `unsafe` block to call such a function, or alternatively specify the "
"`unsafe` keyword in your `#[cxx::bridge]` [as described "
"here](https://cxx.rs/extern-c++.html#functions-and-member-functions)."
msgstr ""
"Block `unsafe` untuk memanggil fungsi tersebut, atau sebagai alternatif "
"tentukan keyword `unsafe` pada `#[cxx::bridge]` Anda [seperti dijelaskan di "
"sini](https://cxx.rs/extern-c++.html#functions-and-member-functions)."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"You may also need to `#include "
"\"third_party/rust/cxx/v1/crate/include/cxx.h\"`"
msgstr ""
"Anda mungkin juga perlu `#include "
"\"third_party/rust/cxx/v1/crate/include/cxx.h\"`"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Pass a C++ string from C++ into Rust."
msgstr "Meneruskan string C++ dari C++ ke Rust."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Pass a reference to a C++ object into Rust."
msgstr "Meneruskan reference ke objek C++ ke Rust."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Intentionally get the Rust function signatures mismatched from the "
"`#[cxx::bridge]`, and get used to the errors you see."
msgstr ""
"Sengaja membuat signature fungsi Rust tidak cocok dengan `#[cxx::bridge]`, "
"dan biasakan diri dengan error yang Anda lihat."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Intentionally get the C++ function signatures mismatched from the "
"`#[cxx::bridge]`, and get used to the errors you see."
msgstr ""
"Sengaja membuat signature fungsi C++ tidak cocok dengan `#[cxx::bridge]`, "
"dan biasakan diri dengan error yang Anda lihat."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Pass a `std::unique_ptr` of some type from C++ into Rust, so that Rust can "
"own some C++ object."
msgstr ""
"Meneruskan `std::unique_ptr` bertipe tertentu dari C++ ke Rust, sehingga "
"Rust dapat memiliki objek C++."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Create a Rust object and pass it into C++, so that C++ owns it. (Hint: you "
"need a `Box`)."
msgstr ""
"Membuat objek Rust dan meneruskannya ke C++, sehingga C++ memilikinya. "
"(Petunjuk: Anda memerlukan `Box`)."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Declare some methods on a C++ type. Call them from Rust."
msgstr "Mendeklarasikan beberapa method pada tipe C++. Panggil dari Rust."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Declare some methods on a Rust type. Call them from C++."
msgstr "Mendeklarasikan beberapa method pada tipe Rust. Panggil dari C++."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Part three"
msgstr "Bagian tiga"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Now you understand the strengths and limitations of CXX interop, think of a "
"couple of use-cases for Rust in Chromium where the interface would be "
"sufficiently simple. Sketch how you might define that interface."
msgstr ""
"Sekarang Anda memahami kekuatan dan keterbatasan interop CXX, pikirkan "
"beberapa kasus penggunaan Rust di Chromium ketika antarmukanya cukup "
"sederhana. Buat sketsa bagaimana Anda mungkin mendefinisikan antarmuka "
"tersebut."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "The [`cxx` binding reference](https://cxx.rs/bindings.html)"
msgstr "Referensi binding [`cxx`](https://cxx.rs/bindings.html)"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"The [`rust_static_library` gn "
"template](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/rust/rust_static_library.gni;l=16)"
msgstr ""
"Template gn "
"[`rust_static_library`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/rust/rust_static_library.gni;l=16)"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid "Some of the questions you may encounter:"
msgstr "Beberapa pertanyaan yang mungkin Anda temui:"

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"I'm seeing a problem initializing a variable of type X with type Y, where X "
"and Y are both function types. This is because your C++ function doesn't "
"quite match the declaration in your `cxx::bridge`."
msgstr ""
"Saya melihat masalah saat menginisialisasi variabel bertipe X dengan tipe Y,"
" di mana X dan Y keduanya tipe fungsi. Ini karena fungsi C++ Anda tidak "
"sepenuhnya cocok dengan deklarasi di `cxx::bridge` Anda."

#: src/exercises/chromium/interoperability-with-cpp.md
msgid ""
"I seem to be able to freely convert C++ references into Rust references. "
"Doesn't that risk UB? For CXX's _opaque_ types, no, because they are zero-"
"sized. For CXX trivial types yes, it's _possible_ to cause UB, although "
"CXX's design makes it quite difficult to craft such an example."
msgstr ""
"Sepertinya saya dapat dengan bebas mengonversi reference C++ menjadi "
"reference Rust. Bukankah itu berisiko UB? Untuk tipe _opaque_ CXX, tidak, "
"karena tipe tersebut berukuran nol. Untuk tipe trivial CXX, ya, _mungkin_ "
"menyebabkan UB, meskipun desain CXX membuatnya cukup sulit untuk membuat "
"contoh semacam itu."

