msgstr "`std` mengekspor ulang isi `core` maupun `alloc`."

#: src/bare-metal/minimal.md
msgid "A minimal `no_std` program"
msgstr "Program `no_std` minimal"

#: src/bare-metal/minimal.md
msgid "This will compile to an empty binary."
msgstr "Ini akan dikompilasi menjadi binary kosong."

#: src/bare-metal/minimal.md
msgid "`std` provides a panic handler; without it we must provide our own."
msgstr ""
"`std` menyediakan panic handler; tanpanya kita harus menyediakan sendiri."

#: src/bare-metal/minimal.md
msgid "It can also be provided by another crate, such as `panic-halt`."
msgstr ""
"Handler tersebut juga dapat disediakan oleh crate lain, seperti `panic-"
"halt`."

#: src/bare-metal/minimal.md
msgid ""
"Depending on the target, you may need to compile with `panic = \"abort\"` to"
" avoid an error about `eh_personality`."
msgstr ""
"Bergantung pada target, Anda mungkin perlu mengompilasi dengan `panic = "
"\"abort\"` untuk menghindari error tentang `eh_personality`."

#: src/bare-metal/minimal.md
msgid ""
"Note that there is no `main` or any other entry point; it's up to you to "
"define your own entry point. This will typically involve a linker script and"
" some assembly code to set things up ready for Rust code to run."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa tidak ada `main` atau entry point lain; terserah Anda untuk"
" mendefinisikan entry point sendiri. Ini biasanya melibatkan linker script "
"dan sejumlah kode assembly untuk menyiapkan semuanya agar kode Rust siap "
"berjalan."

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid ""
"To use `alloc` you must implement a [global (heap) "
"allocator](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/alloc/trait.GlobalAlloc.html)."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menggunakan `alloc`, Anda harus mengimplementasikan [global (heap) "
"allocator](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/alloc/trait.GlobalAlloc.html)."

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid "// SAFETY: `HEAP` is only used here and `entry` is only called once.\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: `HEAP` is only used here and `entry` is only called once.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid "// Give the allocator some memory to allocate.\n"
msgstr "// Give the allocator some memory to allocate.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid "// Now we can do things that require heap allocation.\n"
msgstr "// Now we can do things that require heap allocation.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid "\"A string\""
msgstr "\"A string\""

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid ""
"`buddy_system_allocator` is a crate implementing a basic buddy system "
"allocator. Other crates are available, or you can write your own or hook "
"into your existing allocator."
msgstr ""
"`buddy_system_allocator` adalah crate yang mengimplementasikan allocator "
"buddy system dasar. Tersedia crate lain, atau Anda dapat menulis sendiri "
"atau menghubungkan ke allocator yang sudah ada."

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid ""
"The const parameter of `LockedHeap` is the max order of the allocator; i.e. "
"in this case it can allocate regions of up to 2\\*\\*32 bytes."
msgstr ""
"Parameter const `LockedHeap` adalah orde maksimum allocator; yaitu dalam "
"kasus ini allocator dapat mengalokasikan region hingga 2\\*\\*32 byte."

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid ""
"If any crate in your dependency tree depends on `alloc` then you must have "
"exactly one global allocator defined in your binary. Usually this is done in"
" the top-level binary crate."
msgstr ""
"Jika ada crate dalam pohon dependensi Anda yang bergantung pada `alloc`, "
"maka Anda harus memiliki tepat satu global allocator yang didefinisikan "
"dalam binary Anda. Biasanya ini dilakukan pada crate binary tingkat atas."

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid ""
"`extern crate panic_halt as _` is necessary to ensure that the `panic_halt` "
"crate is linked in so we get its panic handler."
msgstr ""
"`extern crate panic_halt as _` diperlukan untuk memastikan crate "
"`panic_halt` ditautkan sehingga kita mendapatkan panic handler-nya."

#: src/bare-metal/alloc.md
msgid ""
"This example will build but not run, as it doesn't have an entry point."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini akan berhasil di-build tetapi tidak berjalan, karena tidak "
"memiliki entry point."

#: src/bare-metal/microcontrollers.md
msgid ""
"The `cortex_m_rt` crate provides (among other things) a reset handler for "
"Cortex M microcontrollers."
msgstr ""
"Crate `cortex_m_rt` menyediakan (antara lain) reset handler untuk "
"mikrokontroler Cortex M."

#: src/bare-metal/microcontrollers.md
msgid ""
"Next we'll look at how to access peripherals, with increasing levels of "
"abstraction."
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya kita akan melihat cara mengakses peripheral, dengan tingkat "
"abstraksi yang semakin meningkat."

#: src/bare-metal/microcontrollers.md
msgid ""
"The `cortex_m_rt::entry` macro requires that the function have type `fn() ->"
" !`, because returning to the reset handler doesn't make sense."
msgstr ""
"Macro `cortex_m_rt::entry` mengharuskan fungsi bertipe `fn() -> !`, karena "
"kembali ke reset handler tidak masuk akal."

#: src/bare-metal/microcontrollers.md
msgid "Run the example with `cargo embed --bin minimal`"
msgstr "Jalankan contoh dengan `cargo embed --bin minimal`"

