#: src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
msgid ""
"(If you actually want to do this, use the "
"[`smccc`](https://crates.io/crates/smccc) crate which has wrappers for all "
"these functions.)"
msgstr ""
"(Jika Anda benar-benar ingin melakukan ini, gunakan crate "
"[`smccc`](https://crates.io/crates/smccc) yang memiliki wrapper untuk semua "
"fungsi tersebut.)"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
msgid ""
"PSCI is the Arm Power State Coordination Interface, a standard set of "
"functions to manage system and CPU power states, among other things. It is "
"implemented by EL3 firmware and hypervisors on many systems."
msgstr ""
"PSCI adalah Arm Power State Coordination Interface, sekumpulan fungsi "
"standar untuk mengelola state daya sistem dan CPU, antara lain. PSCI "
"diimplementasikan oleh firmware EL3 dan hypervisor pada banyak sistem."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
msgid ""
"The `0 => _` syntax means initialize the register to 0 before running the "
"inline assembly code, and ignore its contents afterwards. We need to use "
"`inout` rather than `in` because the call could potentially clobber the "
"contents of the registers."
msgstr ""
"Sintaks `0 => _` berarti menginisialisasi register menjadi 0 sebelum "
"menjalankan kode assembly inline, dan mengabaikan isinya setelahnya. Kita "
"perlu menggunakan `inout` alih-alih `in` karena pemanggilan tersebut "
"berpotensi menimpa isi register."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
msgid ""
"This `main` function needs to be `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` and `extern \"C\"` "
"because it is called from our entry point in `entry.S`."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `main` ini perlu `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` dan `extern \"C\"` karena "
"dipanggil dari entry point kami di `entry.S`."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
msgid ""
"Just `#[no_mangle]` would be sufficient but [RFC3325](https://rust-"
"lang.github.io/rfcs/3325-unsafe-attributes.html) uses this notation to draw "
"reviewer attention to attributes that might cause undefined behavior if used"
" incorrectly."
msgstr ""
"Cukup `#[no_mangle]` saja sebenarnya memadai, tetapi [RFC3325](https://rust-"
"lang.github.io/rfcs/3325-unsafe-attributes.html) menggunakan notasi ini "
"untuk menarik perhatian reviewer terhadap atribut yang mungkin menyebabkan "
"undefined behavior jika digunakan secara keliru."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
msgid ""
"`_x0`–`_x3` are the values of registers `x0`–`x3`, which are conventionally "
"used by the bootloader to pass things like a pointer to the device tree. "
"According to the standard aarch64 calling convention (which is what `extern "
"\"C\"` specifies to use), registers `x0`–`x7` are used for the first 8 "
"arguments passed to a function, so `entry.S` doesn't need to do anything "
"special except make sure it doesn't change these registers."
msgstr ""
"`_x0`–`_x3` adalah nilai register `x0`–`x3`, yang secara konvensi digunakan "
"bootloader untuk meneruskan hal-hal seperti pointer ke device tree. Menurut "
"calling convention aarch64 standar (yang ditentukan penggunaan oleh `extern "
"\"C\"`), register `x0`–`x7` digunakan untuk 8 argumen pertama yang "
"diteruskan ke fungsi, sehingga `entry.S` tidak perlu melakukan hal khusus "
"selain memastikan tidak mengubah register tersebut."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/inline-assembly.md
msgid ""
"Run the example in QEMU with `make qemu_psci` under `src/bare-"
"metal/aps/examples`."
msgstr ""
"Jalankan contoh di QEMU dengan `make qemu_psci` di bawah `src/bare-"
"metal/aps/examples`."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid "Volatile memory access for MMIO"
msgstr "Akses Memori Volatile untuk MMIO"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid ""
"Use [`pointer::read_volatile`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/core/primitive.pointer.html#method.read_volatile) and "
"[`pointer::write_volatile`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/core/primitive.pointer.html#method.write_volatile)."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan [`pointer::read_volatile`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/core/primitive.pointer.html#method.read_volatile) dan "
"[`pointer::write_volatile`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/core/primitive.pointer.html#method.write_volatile)."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid ""
"Never hold a reference to a location being accessed with these methods. Rust"
" may read from (or write to, for `&mut`) a reference at any time."
msgstr ""
"Jangan pernah menyimpan reference ke lokasi yang diakses dengan method ini. "
"Rust dapat membaca dari (atau menulis ke, untuk `&mut`) sebuah reference "
"kapan saja."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid ""
"Use `&raw` to get fields of structs without creating an intermediate "
"reference."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `&raw` untuk mendapatkan field struct tanpa membuat reference "
"perantara."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid "// SAFETY: Some device is mapped at this address.\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: Some device is mapped at this address.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid ""
"Volatile access: read or write operations may have side-effects, so prevent "
"the compiler or hardware from reordering, duplicating or eliding them."
msgstr ""
"Akses volatile: operasi baca atau tulis mungkin memiliki efek samping, jadi "
"cegah compiler atau hardware mengurutkan ulang, menduplikasi, atau "
"menghilangkannya."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid ""
"If you write and then read, e.g. via a mutable reference, the compiler may "
"assume that the value read is the same as the value just written, and not "
"bother actually reading memory."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda menulis lalu membaca, misalnya melalui mutable reference, compiler"
" dapat mengasumsikan nilai yang dibaca sama dengan nilai yang baru ditulis, "
"dan tidak perlu benar-benar membaca memori."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid ""
"Some existing crates for volatile access to hardware do hold references, but"
" this is unsound. Whenever a reference exists, the compiler may choose to "
"dereference it."
msgstr ""
"Beberapa crate yang sudah ada untuk akses volatile ke hardware memang "
"menyimpan reference, tetapi itu tidak sound. Setiap kali reference ada, "
"compiler dapat memilih untuk melakukan dereference."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid "Use `&raw` to get struct field pointers from a pointer to the struct."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `&raw` untuk mendapatkan pointer field struct dari pointer ke "
"struct."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/mmio.md
msgid ""
"For compatibility with old versions of Rust you can use the "
"[`addr_of!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/ptr/macro.addr_of.html) "
"macro instead."
msgstr ""
"Untuk kompatibilitas dengan versi Rust lama, Anda dapat menggunakan macro "
"[`addr_of!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/ptr/macro.addr_of.html)."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid "Let's write a UART driver"
msgstr "Mari Menulis Driver UART"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid ""
"The QEMU 'virt' machine has a "
"[PL011](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0183/g) UART, so let's "
"write a driver for that."
msgstr ""
"Mesin 'virt' QEMU memiliki UART "
"[PL011](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0183/g), jadi mari kita "
"tulis driver untuk itu."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid "/// Minimal driver for a PL011 UART.\n"
msgstr "/// Minimal driver for a PL011 UART.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid ""
"/// Constructs a new instance of the UART driver for a PL011 device at the\n"
"    /// given base address.\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// The given base address must point to the 8 MMIO control registers of a\n"
"    /// PL011 device, which must be mapped into the address space of the process\n"
"    /// as device memory and not have any other aliases.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Constructs a new instance of the UART driver for a PL011 device at the\n"
"    /// given base address.\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// The given base address must point to the 8 MMIO control registers of a\n"
"    /// PL011 device, which must be mapped into the address space of the process\n"
"    /// as device memory and not have any other aliases.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md src/bare-metal/aps/better-uart/driver.md
#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid "/// Writes a single byte to the UART.\n"
msgstr "/// Writes a single byte to the UART.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md src/bare-metal/aps/better-uart/driver.md
#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid "// Wait until there is room in the TX buffer.\n"
msgstr "// Wait until there is room in the TX buffer.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: We know that the base address points to the control\n"
"        // registers of a PL011 device which is appropriately mapped.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: We know that the base address points to the control\n"
"        // registers of a PL011 device which is appropriately mapped.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md src/bare-metal/aps/better-uart/driver.md
#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid "// Write to the TX buffer.\n"
msgstr "// Write to the TX buffer.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md src/bare-metal/aps/better-uart/driver.md
#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid "// Wait until the UART is no longer busy.\n"
msgstr "// Wait until the UART is no longer busy.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid ""
"Note that `Uart::new` is unsafe while the other methods are safe. This is "
"because as long as the caller of `Uart::new` guarantees that its safety "
"requirements are met (i.e. that there is only ever one instance of the "
"driver for a given UART, and nothing else aliasing its address space), then "
"it is always safe to call `write_byte` later because we can assume the "
"necessary preconditions."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `Uart::new` bersifat unsafe sementara method lainnya safe. "
"Ini karena selama pemanggil `Uart::new` menjamin persyaratan keamanannya "
"terpenuhi (yaitu hanya ada satu instance driver untuk UART tertentu, dan "
"tidak ada hal lain yang menjadi alias ruang alamatnya), maka selalu aman "
"memanggil `write_byte` nanti karena kita dapat mengasumsikan prasyarat yang "
"diperlukan."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid ""
"We could have done it the other way around (making `new` safe but "
"`write_byte` unsafe), but that would be much less convenient to use as every"
" place that calls `write_byte` would need to reason about the safety"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa melakukannya sebaliknya (membuat `new` safe tetapi `write_byte` "
"unsafe), tetapi itu akan jauh kurang nyaman digunakan karena setiap tempat "
"yang memanggil `write_byte` perlu menalar tentang keamanannya"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart.md
msgid ""
"This is a common pattern for writing safe wrappers of unsafe code: moving "
"the burden of proof for soundness from a large number of places to a smaller"
" number of places."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah pola umum untuk menulis wrapper safe bagi kode unsafe: "
"memindahkan beban pembuktian soundness dari banyak tempat ke jumlah tempat "
"yang lebih sedikit."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart/traits.md
msgid "More traits"
msgstr "Trait Lainnya"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart/traits.md
msgid ""
"We derived the `Debug` trait. It would be useful to implement a few more "
"traits too."
msgstr ""
"Kami melakukan derive trait `Debug`. Akan berguna untuk mengimplementasikan "
"beberapa trait lagi juga."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart/traits.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: `Uart` just contains a pointer to device memory, which can be\n"
"// accessed from any context.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: `Uart` just contains a pointer to device memory, which can be\n"
"// accessed from any context.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart/traits.md
msgid ""
"Implementing `Write` lets us use the `write!` and `writeln!` macros with our"
" `Uart` type."
msgstr ""
"Mengimplementasikan `Write` memungkinkan kita menggunakan macro `write!` dan"
" `writeln!` dengan tipe `Uart` kami."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/uart/traits.md
msgid ""
"`Send` is an auto-trait, but not implemented automatically because it is not"
" implemented for pointers."
msgstr ""
"`Send` adalah auto-trait, tetapi tidak diimplementasikan secara otomatis "
"karena tidak diimplementasikan untuk pointer."

