msgid ""
"The difference between `ReadPure` or `ReadOnly` (and likewise between "
"`ReadPureWrite` and `ReadWrite`) is whether reading a register can have "
"side-effects that change the state of the device, e.g., reading the data "
"register pops a byte from the receive FIFO. `ReadPure` means that reads have"
" no side-effects, they are purely reading data."
msgstr ""
"Perbedaan antara `ReadPure` atau `ReadOnly` (demikian pula antara "
"`ReadPureWrite` dan `ReadWrite`) adalah apakah membaca register dapat "
"memiliki efek samping yang mengubah state perangkat, misalnya membaca data "
"register mengeluarkan satu byte dari receive FIFO. `ReadPure` berarti "
"pembacaan tidak memiliki efek samping, murni membaca data."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid ""
"/// Constructs a new instance of the UART driver for a PL011 device with the\n"
"    /// given set of registers.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Constructs a new instance of the UART driver for a PL011 device with the\n"
"    /// given set of registers.\n"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid "The driver no longer needs any unsafe code!"
msgstr "Driver tidak lagi memerlukan kode unsafe!"

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid ""
"`UniqueMmioPointer` is a wrapper around a raw pointer to an MMIO device or "
"register. The caller of `UniqueMmioPointer::new` promises that it is valid "
"and unique for the given lifetime, so it can provide safe methods to read "
"and write fields."
msgstr ""
"`UniqueMmioPointer` adalah wrapper di sekitar raw pointer ke perangkat atau "
"register MMIO. Pemanggil `UniqueMmioPointer::new` menjanjikan bahwa pointer "
"valid dan unik selama lifetime yang diberikan, sehingga dapat menyediakan "
"method safe untuk membaca dan menulis field."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid ""
"Note that `Uart::new` is now safe; `UniqueMmioPointer::new` is unsafe "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `Uart::new` sekarang safe; `UniqueMmioPointer::new` yang "
"bersifat unsafe."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid ""
"These MMIO accesses are generally a wrapper around `read_volatile` and "
"`write_volatile`, though on aarch64 they are instead implemented in assembly"
" to work around a bug where the compiler can emit instructions that prevent "
"MMIO virtualization."
msgstr ""
"Akses MMIO ini umumnya merupakan wrapper di sekitar `read_volatile` dan "
"`write_volatile`, meskipun pada aarch64 akses tersebut diimplementasikan "
"dalam assembly untuk mengatasi bug ketika compiler dapat mengeluarkan "
"instruksi yang mencegah virtualisasi MMIO."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid ""
"The `field!` and `field_shared!` macros internally use `&raw mut` and `&raw "
"const` to get pointers to individual fields without creating an intermediate"
" reference, which would be unsound."
msgstr ""
"Macro `field!` dan `field_shared!` secara internal menggunakan `&raw mut` "
"dan `&raw const` untuk mendapatkan pointer ke field individual tanpa membuat"
" reference perantara, yang akan tidak sound."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid ""
"`field!` needs a mutable reference to a `UniqueMmioPointer`, and returns a "
"`UniqueMmioPointer` that allows reads with side effects and writes."
msgstr ""
"`field!` memerlukan mutable reference ke `UniqueMmioPointer`, dan "
"mengembalikan `UniqueMmioPointer` yang memungkinkan pembacaan dengan efek "
"samping dan penulisan."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/driver.md
msgid ""
"`field_shared!` works with a shared reference to either a "
"`UniqueMmioPointer` or a `SharedMmioPointer`. It returns a "
"`SharedMmioPointer` that only allows pure reads."
msgstr ""
"`field_shared!` bekerja dengan shared reference ke `UniqueMmioPointer` atau "
"`SharedMmioPointer`. Macro ini mengembalikan `SharedMmioPointer` yang hanya "
"memungkinkan pembacaan pure."

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/using.md
msgid ""
"Let's write a small program using our driver to write to the serial console,"
" and echo incoming bytes."
msgstr ""
"Mari tulis program kecil yang menggunakan driver kami untuk menulis ke "
"konsol serial, dan menggemakan byte yang masuk."

