#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/tinyvec.md
msgid ""
"Sometimes you want something that can be resized like a `Vec`, but without "
"heap allocation. [`tinyvec`](https://crates.io/crates/tinyvec) provides "
"this: a vector backed by an array or slice, which could be statically "
"allocated or on the stack, that keeps track of how many elements are used "
"and panics if you try to use more than are allocated."
msgstr ""
"Kadang Anda menginginkan sesuatu yang dapat diubah ukurannya seperti `Vec`, "
"tetapi tanpa alokasi heap. [`tinyvec`](https://crates.io/crates/tinyvec) "
"menyediakan ini: vector yang didukung array atau slice, yang dapat "
"dialokasikan secara statis atau berada di stack, yang melacak berapa banyak "
"elemen yang digunakan dan panic jika Anda mencoba menggunakan lebih dari "
"yang dialokasikan."

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/tinyvec.md
msgid ""
"`tinyvec` requires that the element type implement `Default` for "
"initialization."
msgstr ""
"`tinyvec` mengharuskan tipe elemen mengimplementasikan `Default` untuk "
"inisialisasi."

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/tinyvec.md
msgid ""
"The Rust Playground includes `tinyvec`, so this example will run fine "
"inline."
msgstr ""
"Rust Playground menyertakan `tinyvec`, jadi contoh ini akan berjalan baik "
"secara inline."

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/spin.md
msgid ""
"`std::sync::Mutex` and the other synchronisation primitives from `std::sync`"
" are not available in `core` or `alloc`. How can we manage synchronisation "
"or interior mutability, such as for sharing state between different CPUs?"
msgstr ""
"`std::sync::Mutex` dan primitif sinkronisasi lain dari `std::sync` tidak "
"tersedia di `core` atau `alloc`. Bagaimana kita dapat mengelola sinkronisasi"
" atau interior mutability, misalnya untuk berbagi state antarcPU yang "
"berbeda?"

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/spin.md
msgid ""
"The [`spin`](https://crates.io/crates/spin) crate provides spinlock-based "
"equivalents of many of these primitives."
msgstr ""
"Crate [`spin`](https://crates.io/crates/spin) menyediakan padanan berbasis "
"spinlock untuk banyak primitif tersebut."

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/spin.md
msgid "Be careful to avoid deadlock if you take locks in interrupt handlers."
msgstr ""
"Berhati-hatilah agar tidak deadlock jika Anda mengambil lock di interrupt "
"handler."

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/spin.md
msgid ""
"`spin` also has a ticket lock mutex implementation; equivalents of `RwLock`,"
" `Barrier` and `Once` from `std::sync`; and `Lazy` for lazy initialization."
msgstr ""
"`spin` juga memiliki implementasi mutex ticket lock; padanan `RwLock`, "
"`Barrier`, dan `Once` dari `std::sync`; serta `Lazy` untuk inisialisasi "
"lazy."

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/spin.md
msgid ""
"The [`once_cell`](https://crates.io/crates/once_cell) crate also has some "
"useful types for late initialization with a slightly different approach to "
"`spin::once::Once`."
msgstr ""
"Crate [`once_cell`](https://crates.io/crates/once_cell) juga memiliki "
"beberapa tipe berguna untuk inisialisasi tertunda dengan pendekatan yang "
"sedikit berbeda dari `spin::once::Once`."

#: src/bare-metal/useful-crates/spin.md
msgid ""
"The Rust Playground includes `spin`, so this example will run fine inline."
msgstr ""
"Rust Playground menyertakan `spin`, jadi contoh ini akan berjalan baik "
"secara inline."

#: src/bare-metal/android.md
msgid ""
"To build a bare-metal Rust binary in AOSP, you need to use a "
"`rust_ffi_static` Soong rule to build your Rust code, then a `cc_binary` "
"with a linker script to produce the binary itself, and then a `raw_binary` "
"to convert the ELF to a raw binary ready to be run."
msgstr ""
"Untuk membangun binary Rust bare-metal di AOSP, Anda perlu menggunakan "
"aturan Soong `rust_ffi_static` untuk membangun kode Rust, lalu `cc_binary` "
"dengan linker script untuk menghasilkan binary itu sendiri, kemudian "
"`raw_binary` untuk mengonversi ELF menjadi binary mentah yang siap "
"dijalankan."

#: src/bare-metal/android/vmbase.md
msgid "vmbase"
msgstr "vmbase"

#: src/bare-metal/android/vmbase.md
msgid ""
"For VMs running under crosvm on aarch64, the "
"[vmbase](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/refs/heads/main/libs/libvmbase/)"
" library provides a linker script and useful defaults for the build rules, "
"along with an entry point, UART console logging and more."
msgstr ""
"Untuk VM yang berjalan di bawah crosvm pada aarch64, library "
"[vmbase](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/refs/heads/main/libs/libvmbase/)"
" menyediakan linker script dan default berguna untuk aturan build, beserta "
"entry point, logging konsol UART, dan lainnya."

#: src/bare-metal/android/vmbase.md
msgid ""
"The `main!` macro marks your main function, to be called from the `vmbase` "
"entry point."
msgstr ""
"Macro `main!` menandai fungsi main Anda, untuk dipanggil dari entry point "
"`vmbase`."

#: src/bare-metal/android/vmbase.md
msgid ""
"The `vmbase` entry point handles console initialisation, and issues a "
"PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF to shutdown the VM if your main function returns."
msgstr ""
"Entry point `vmbase` menangani inisialisasi konsol, dan mengeluarkan "
"PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF untuk mematikan VM jika fungsi main Anda kembali."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/afternoon.md
msgid "We will write a driver for the PL031 real-time clock device."
msgstr "Kami akan menulis driver untuk perangkat real-time clock PL031."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/afternoon.md
msgid ""
"After looking at the exercises, you can look at the [solutions](solutions-"
"afternoon.md) provided."
msgstr ""
"Setelah melihat latihan, Anda dapat melihat [solusi](solutions-afternoon.md)"
" yang disediakan."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
#: src/exercises/bare-metal/solutions-afternoon.md
msgid "RTC driver"
msgstr "Driver RTC"

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
msgid ""
"The QEMU aarch64 virt machine has a "
"[PL031](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0224/c) real-time clock "
"at 0x9010000. For this exercise, you should write a driver for it."
msgstr ""
"Mesin virt aarch64 QEMU memiliki real-time clock "
"[PL031](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0224/c) di 0x9010000. "
"Untuk latihan ini, Anda sebaiknya menulis driver untuk perangkat tersebut."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
msgid ""
"Use it to print the current time to the serial console. You can use the "
"[`chrono`](https://crates.io/crates/chrono) crate for date/time formatting."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan driver tersebut untuk mencetak waktu saat ini ke konsol serial. Anda"
" dapat menggunakan crate [`chrono`](https://crates.io/crates/chrono) untuk "
"pemformatan tanggal/waktu."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
msgid ""
"Use the match register and raw interrupt status to busy-wait until a given "
"time, e.g. 3 seconds in the future. (Call "
"[`core::hint::spin_loop`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/core/hint/fn.spin_loop.html) inside the loop.)"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan match register dan raw interrupt status untuk busy-wait hingga waktu"
" tertentu, misalnya 3 detik ke depan. (Panggil "
"[`core::hint::spin_loop`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/core/hint/fn.spin_loop.html) di dalam loop.)"

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
msgid ""
"_Extension if you have time:_ Enable and handle the interrupt generated by "
"the RTC match. You can use the driver provided in the [`arm-"
"gic`](https://docs.rs/arm-gic/) crate to configure the Arm Generic Interrupt"
" Controller."
msgstr ""
"_Ekstensi jika Anda punya waktu:_ Aktifkan dan tangani interrupt yang "
"dihasilkan oleh match RTC. Anda dapat menggunakan driver yang disediakan "
"dalam crate [`arm-gic`](https://docs.rs/arm-gic/) untuk mengonfigurasi Arm "
"Generic Interrupt Controller."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
msgid "Use the RTC interrupt, which is wired to the GIC as `IntId::spi(2)`."
msgstr "Gunakan interrupt RTC, yang terhubung ke GIC sebagai `IntId::spi(2)`."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
msgid ""
"Once the interrupt is enabled, you can put the core to sleep via "
"`arm_gic::wfi()`, which will cause the core to sleep until it receives an "
"interrupt."
msgstr ""
"Setelah interrupt diaktifkan, Anda dapat menidurkan core melalui "
"`arm_gic::wfi()`, yang akan membuat core tidur hingga menerima interrupt."

#: src/exercises/bare-metal/rtc.md
msgid ""
"Download the [exercise template](../../comprehensive-rust-exercises.zip) and"
" look in the `rtc` directory for the following files."
msgstr ""
"Unduh [template latihan](../../comprehensive-rust-exercises.zip) dan lihat "
"di direktori `rtc` untuk berkas berikut."

