#: src/concurrency/welcome.md
msgid "Welcome to Concurrency in Rust"
msgstr "Selamat Datang di Konkurensi di Rust"

#: src/concurrency/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Rust has full support for concurrency using OS threads with mutexes and "
"channels."
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki dukungan penuh untuk konkurensi menggunakan thread OS dengan "
"mutex dan channel."

#: src/concurrency/welcome.md
msgid ""
"The Rust type system plays an important role in making many concurrency bugs"
" compile time errors. This idea is known as _fearless concurrency_ since you"
" can rely on the compiler to ensure correctness at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Sistem tipe Rust berperan penting dalam menjadikan banyak bug konkurensi "
"sebagai error waktu kompilasi. Gagasan ini dikenal sebagai _fearless "
"concurrency_ karena Anda dapat mengandalkan compiler untuk memastikan "
"kebenaran pada waktu runtime."

#: src/concurrency/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Including 10 minute breaks, this session should take about 3 hours and 20 "
"minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Termasuk jeda 10 menit, sesi ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 3 jam 20 "
"menit. Sesi ini berisi:"

#: src/concurrency/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Rust lets us access OS concurrency toolkit: threads, sync. primitives, etc."
msgstr ""
"Rust memungkinkan kita mengakses toolkit konkurensi OS: thread, primitif "
"sinkronisasi, dan sebagainya."

#: src/concurrency/welcome.md
msgid ""
"The type system gives us safety for concurrency without any special "
"features."
msgstr ""
"Sistem tipe memberi kita keamanan untuk konkurensi tanpa fitur khusus."

#: src/concurrency/welcome.md
msgid ""
"The same tools that help with \"concurrent\" access in a single thread "
"(e.g., a called function that might mutate an argument or save references to"
" it to read later) save us from multi-threading issues."
msgstr ""
"Alat yang sama yang membantu akses \"konkuren\" dalam satu thread (misalnya,"
" fungsi yang dipanggil mungkin mengubah argumen atau menyimpan referensinya "
"untuk dibaca nanti) menyelamatkan kita dari masalah multi-threading."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Rust threads work similarly to threads in other languages:"
msgstr "Thread Rust bekerja serupa dengan thread di bahasa lain:"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "\"Count in thread: {i}!\""
msgstr "\"Count in thread: {i}!\""

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "\"Main thread: {i}\""
msgstr "\"Main thread: {i}\""

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"Spawning new threads does not automatically delay program termination at the"
" end of `main`."
msgstr ""
"Melahirkan thread baru tidak secara otomatis menunda penghentian program di "
"akhir `main`."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Thread panics are independent of each other."
msgstr "Panic pada thread bersifat independen satu sama lain."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"Panics can carry a payload, which can be unpacked with "
"[`Any::downcast_ref`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/any/trait.Any.html#method.downcast_ref)."
msgstr ""
"Panic dapat membawa payload, yang dapat dibongkar dengan "
"[`Any::downcast_ref`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/any/trait.Any.html#method.downcast_ref)."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Run the example."
msgstr "Jalankan contoh."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"5ms timing is loose enough that main and spawned threads stay mostly in "
"lockstep."
msgstr ""
"Timing 5ms cukup longgar sehingga thread main dan thread yang dilahirkan "
"sebagian besar tetap seiring."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Notice that the program ends before the spawned thread reaches 10!"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa program berakhir sebelum thread yang dilahirkan mencapai "
"10!"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"This is because `main` ends the program and spawned threads do not make it "
"persist."
msgstr ""
"Ini karena `main` mengakhiri program dan thread yang dilahirkan tidak "
"membuat program tetap bertahan."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Compare to `pthreads`/C++ `std::thread`/`boost::thread` if desired."
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan dengan `pthreads`/C++ `std::thread`/`boost::thread` jika "
"diinginkan."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "How do we wait around for the spawned thread to complete?"
msgstr "Bagaimana kita menunggu thread yang dilahirkan selesai?"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"[`thread::spawn`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html) "
"returns a `JoinHandle`. Look at the docs."
msgstr ""
"[`thread::spawn`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html) "
"mengembalikan `JoinHandle`. Lihat dokumentasinya."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"`JoinHandle` has a [`.join()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join) method that blocks."
msgstr ""
"`JoinHandle` memiliki method [`.join()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join) yang memblokir."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"Use `let handle = thread::spawn(...)` and later `handle.join()` to wait for "
"the thread to finish and have the program count all the way to 10."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `let handle = thread::spawn(...)` dan nanti `handle.join()` untuk "
"menunggu thread selesai dan membuat program menghitung hingga 10."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Now what if we want to return a value?"
msgstr "Sekarang bagaimana jika kita ingin mengembalikan nilai?"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Look at docs again:"
msgstr "Lihat dokumentasi lagi:"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"[`thread::spawn`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html)'s "
"closure returns `T`"
msgstr ""
"Closure [`thread::spawn`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html) mengembalikan `T`"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"`JoinHandle` [`.join()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join) returns "
"`thread::Result<T>`"
msgstr ""
"`JoinHandle` [`.join()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join) mengembalikan "
"`thread::Result<T>`"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"Use the `Result` return value from `handle.join()` to get access to the "
"returned value."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan nilai kembalian `Result` dari `handle.join()` untuk mengakses nilai "
"yang dikembalikan."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Ok, what about the other case?"
msgstr "Baik, bagaimana dengan kasus lainnya?"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Trigger a panic in the thread. Note that this doesn't panic `main`."
msgstr ""
"Picu panic di thread. Perhatikan bahwa ini tidak membuat `main` panic."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"Access the panic payload. This is a good time to talk about "
"[`Any`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/any/index.html)."
msgstr ""
"Akses payload panic. Ini saat yang tepat untuk membahas "
"[`Any`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/any/index.html)."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Now we can return values from threads! What about taking inputs?"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita dapat mengembalikan nilai dari thread! Bagaimana dengan "
"menerima input?"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Capture something by reference in the thread closure."
msgstr "Tangkap sesuatu by reference dalam closure thread."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "An error message indicates we must move it."
msgstr "Pesan error menunjukkan bahwa kita harus memindahkannya."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "Move it in, see we can compute and then return a derived value."
msgstr ""
"Pindahkan ke dalam, lihat bahwa kita dapat menghitung lalu mengembalikan "
"nilai turunan."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "If we want to borrow?"
msgstr "Bagaimana jika kita ingin meminjam?"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid ""
"Main kills child threads when it returns, but another function would just "
"return and leave them running."
msgstr ""
"Main menghentikan thread anak saat kembali, tetapi fungsi lain hanya akan "
"kembali dan membiarkan thread tersebut tetap berjalan."

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "That would be stack use-after-return, which violates memory safety!"
msgstr ""
"Itu akan menjadi stack use-after-return, yang melanggar keamanan memori!"

#: src/concurrency/threads/plain.md
msgid "How do we avoid this? See next slide."
msgstr "Bagaimana kita menghindarinya? Lihat slide berikutnya."

#: src/concurrency/threads/scoped.md
msgid "Normal threads cannot borrow from their environment:"
msgstr "Thread normal tidak dapat meminjam dari environment-nya:"

#: src/concurrency/threads/scoped.md
msgid ""
"However, you can use a [scoped thread](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/thread/fn.scope.html) for this:"
msgstr ""
"Namun, Anda dapat menggunakan [scoped thread](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/thread/fn.scope.html) untuk ini:"

#: src/concurrency/threads/scoped.md
msgid ""
"The reason for that is that when the `thread::scope` function completes, all"
" the threads are guaranteed to be joined, so they can return borrowed data."
msgstr ""
"Alasannya adalah ketika fungsi `thread::scope` selesai, semua thread dijamin"
" telah di-join, sehingga thread dapat mengembalikan data yang dipinjam."

#: src/concurrency/threads/scoped.md
msgid ""
"Normal Rust borrowing rules apply: you can either borrow mutably by one "
"thread, or immutably by any number of threads."
msgstr ""
"Aturan borrowing Rust normal berlaku: Anda dapat meminjam secara mutable "
"oleh satu thread, atau secara immutable oleh sejumlah thread."

#: src/concurrency/channels.md src/concurrency/async-control-flow.md
msgid "This segment should take about 20 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Segmen ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 20 menit. Segmen ini berisi:"

#: src/concurrency/channels/senders-receivers.md
msgid ""
"Rust channels have two parts: a [`Sender<T>`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Sender.html) and a "
"[`Receiver<T>`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html). The two parts are connected "
"via the channel, but you only see the end-points."
msgstr ""
"Channel Rust memiliki dua bagian: [`Sender<T>`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Sender.html) dan "
"[`Receiver<T>`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html). Kedua bagian terhubung melalui"
" channel, tetapi Anda hanya melihat endpoint-nya."

#: src/concurrency/channels/senders-receivers.md
msgid "\"Received: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"Received: {:?}\""

#: src/concurrency/channels/senders-receivers.md
msgid ""
"[`mpsc`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/index.html) stands for "
"Multi-Producer, Single-Consumer. `Sender` and `SyncSender` implement `Clone`"
" (so you can make multiple producers) but `Receiver` does not."
msgstr ""
"[`mpsc`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/index.html) adalah "
"singkatan dari Multi-Producer, Single-Consumer. `Sender` dan `SyncSender` "
"mengimplementasikan `Clone` (sehingga Anda dapat membuat beberapa producer),"
" tetapi `Receiver` tidak."

#: src/concurrency/channels/senders-receivers.md
msgid ""
"[`send()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Sender.html#method.send) and "
"[`recv()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html#method.recv) return `Result`. If"
" they return `Err`, it means the counterpart `Sender` or `Receiver` is "
"dropped and the channel is closed."
msgstr ""
"[`send()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Sender.html#method.send) dan "
"[`recv()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html#method.recv) mengembalikan "
"`Result`. Jika mengembalikan `Err`, artinya pasangan `Sender` atau "
"`Receiver` di-drop dan channel ditutup."

#: src/concurrency/channels/unbounded.md
msgid ""
"You get an unbounded and asynchronous channel with "
"[`mpsc::channel()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/fn.channel.html):"
msgstr ""
"Anda mendapatkan channel unbounded dan asinkron dengan "
"[`mpsc::channel()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/fn.channel.html):"

#: src/concurrency/channels/unbounded.md src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid "\"Message {i}\""
msgstr "\"Message {i}\""

#: src/concurrency/channels/unbounded.md src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid "\"{thread_id:?}: sent Message {i}\""
msgstr "\"{thread_id:?}: sent Message {i}\""

#: src/concurrency/channels/unbounded.md src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid "\"{thread_id:?}: done\""
msgstr "\"{thread_id:?}: done\""

#: src/concurrency/channels/unbounded.md src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid "\"Main: got {msg}\""
msgstr "\"Main: got {msg}\""

#: src/concurrency/channels/unbounded.md
msgid ""
"An unbounded channel will allocate as much space as is necessary to store "
"pending messages. The `send()` method will not block the calling thread."
msgstr ""
"Channel unbounded akan mengalokasikan ruang sebanyak yang diperlukan untuk "
"menyimpan pesan tertunda. Method `send()` tidak akan memblokir thread "
"pemanggil."

#: src/concurrency/channels/unbounded.md
msgid ""
"A call to `send()` will abort with an error (that is why it returns "
"`Result`) if the channel is closed. A channel is closed when the receiver is"
" dropped."
msgstr ""
"Pemanggilan `send()` akan gagal dengan error (itulah sebabnya mengembalikan "
"`Result`) jika channel ditutup. Channel ditutup ketika receiver di-drop."

#: src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid ""
"With bounded (synchronous) channels, [`send()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.SyncSender.html#method.send) can block the "
"current thread:"
msgstr ""
"Dengan channel bounded (sinkron), [`send()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.SyncSender.html#method.send) dapat memblokir "
"thread saat ini:"

#: src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid ""
"Calling `send()` will block the current thread until there is space in the "
"channel for the new message. The thread can be blocked indefinitely if there"
" is nobody who reads from the channel."
msgstr ""
"Memanggil `send()` akan memblokir thread saat ini hingga ada ruang di "
"channel untuk pesan baru. Thread dapat terblokir tanpa batas jika tidak ada "
"yang membaca dari channel."

#: src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid ""
"Like unbounded channels, a call to `send()` will abort with an error if the "
"channel is closed."
msgstr ""
"Seperti channel unbounded, pemanggilan `send()` akan gagal dengan error jika"
" channel ditutup."

#: src/concurrency/channels/bounded.md
msgid ""
"A bounded channel with a size of zero is called a \"rendezvous channel\". "
"Every send will block the current thread until another thread calls "
"[`recv()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html#method.recv)."
msgstr ""
"Channel bounded berukuran nol disebut \"rendezvous channel\". Setiap send "
"akan memblokir thread saat ini hingga thread lain memanggil "
"[`recv()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html#method.recv)."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync.md
msgid "Send"
msgstr "Send"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync.md
msgid "Sync"
msgstr "Sync"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/marker-traits.md
msgid ""
"How does Rust know to forbid shared access across threads? The answer is in "
"two traits:"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana Rust mengetahui cara melarang akses bersama antar-thread? "
"Jawabannya ada pada dua trait:"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/marker-traits.md
msgid ""
"[`Send`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/marker/trait.Send.html): a type `T` "
"is `Send` if it is safe to move a `T` across a thread boundary."
msgstr ""
"[`Send`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/marker/trait.Send.html): tipe `T` "
"bersifat `Send` jika aman memindahkan `T` melintasi batas thread."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/marker-traits.md
msgid ""
"[`Sync`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/marker/trait.Sync.html): a type `T` "
"is `Sync` if it is safe to move a `&T` across a thread boundary."
msgstr ""
"[`Sync`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/marker/trait.Sync.html): tipe `T` "
"bersifat `Sync` jika aman memindahkan `&T` melintasi batas thread."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/marker-traits.md
msgid ""
"`Send` and `Sync` are [unsafe traits](../../unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md). "
"The compiler will automatically derive them for your types as long as they "
"only contain `Send` and `Sync` types. You can also implement them manually "
"when you know it is valid."
msgstr ""
"`Send` dan `Sync` adalah [unsafe trait](../../unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md)."
" Compiler akan secara otomatis melakukan derive untuk tipe Anda selama tipe "
"tersebut hanya berisi tipe `Send` dan `Sync`. Anda juga dapat "
"mengimplementasikannya secara manual ketika Anda tahu hal itu valid."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/marker-traits.md
msgid ""
"One can think of these traits as markers that the type has certain thread-"
"safety properties."
msgstr ""
"Kedua trait ini dapat dianggap sebagai penanda bahwa tipe memiliki properti "
"thread-safety tertentu."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/marker-traits.md
msgid "They can be used in the generic constraints as normal traits."
msgstr ""
"Keduanya dapat digunakan dalam constraint generic seperti trait biasa."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/send.md
msgid ""
"A type `T` is [`Send`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/marker/trait.Send.html)"
" if it is safe to move a `T` value to another thread."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `T` bersifat [`Send`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/marker/trait.Send.html) jika aman memindahkan nilai `T` ke "
"thread lain."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/send.md
msgid ""
"The effect of moving ownership to another thread is that _destructors_ will "
"run in that thread. So the question is when you can allocate a value in one "
"thread and deallocate it in another."
msgstr ""
"Efek memindahkan ownership ke thread lain adalah _destructor_ akan berjalan "
"di thread tersebut. Jadi pertanyaannya adalah kapan Anda dapat "
"mengalokasikan nilai di satu thread dan membebaskannya di thread lain."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/send.md
msgid ""
"As an example, a connection to the SQLite library must only be accessed from"
" a single thread."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, koneksi ke library SQLite hanya boleh diakses dari satu "
"thread."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/sync.md
msgid ""
"A type `T` is [`Sync`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/marker/trait.Sync.html)"
" if it is safe to access a `T` value from multiple threads at the same time."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `T` bersifat [`Sync`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/marker/trait.Sync.html) jika aman mengakses nilai `T` dari "
"beberapa thread secara bersamaan."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/sync.md
msgid "More precisely, the definition is:"
msgstr "Lebih tepatnya, definisinya adalah:"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/sync.md
msgid "`T` is `Sync` if and only if `&T` is `Send`"
msgstr "`T` bersifat `Sync` jika dan hanya jika `&T` bersifat `Send`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/sync.md
msgid ""
"This statement is essentially a shorthand way of saying that if a type is "
"thread-safe for shared use, it is also thread-safe to pass references of it "
"across threads."
msgstr ""
"Pernyataan ini pada dasarnya adalah cara singkat untuk mengatakan bahwa jika"
" suatu tipe thread-safe untuk penggunaan bersama, maka juga thread-safe "
"untuk meneruskan referensinya antar-thread."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/sync.md
msgid ""
"This is because if a type is Sync it means that it can be shared across "
"multiple threads without the risk of data races or other synchronization "
"issues, so it is safe to move it to another thread. A reference to the type "
"is also safe to move to another thread, because the data it references can "
"be accessed from any thread safely."
msgstr ""
"Ini karena jika suatu tipe bersifat Sync, artinya tipe tersebut dapat "
"dibagikan antar beberapa thread tanpa risiko data race atau masalah "
"sinkronisasi lainnya, sehingga aman memindahkannya ke thread lain. Reference"
" ke tipe tersebut juga aman dipindahkan ke thread lain, karena data yang "
"direferensikannya dapat diakses dari thread mana pun dengan aman."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`Send + Sync`"
msgstr "`Send + Sync`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "Most types you come across are `Send + Sync`:"
msgstr "Sebagian besar tipe yang Anda temui bersifat `Send + Sync`:"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`i8`, `f32`, `bool`, `char`, `&str`, ..."
msgstr "`i8`, `f32`, `bool`, `char`, `&str`, ..."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`(T1, T2)`, `[T; N]`, `&[T]`, `struct { x: T }`, ..."
msgstr "`(T1, T2)`, `[T; N]`, `&[T]`, `struct { x: T }`, ..."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`String`, `Option<T>`, `Vec<T>`, `Box<T>`, ..."
msgstr "`String`, `Option<T>`, `Vec<T>`, `Box<T>`, ..."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`Arc<T>`: Explicitly thread-safe via atomic reference count."
msgstr ""
"`Arc<T>`: Secara eksplisit thread-safe melalui atomic reference count."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`Mutex<T>`: Explicitly thread-safe via internal locking."
msgstr "`Mutex<T>`: Secara eksplisit thread-safe melalui locking internal."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`mpsc::Sender<T>`: As of 1.72.0."
msgstr "`mpsc::Sender<T>`: Sejak 1.72.0."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`AtomicBool`, `AtomicU8`, ...: Uses special atomic instructions."
msgstr "`AtomicBool`, `AtomicU8`, ...: Menggunakan instruksi atomik khusus."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid ""
"The generic types are typically `Send + Sync` when the type parameters are "
"`Send + Sync`."
msgstr ""
"Tipe generic biasanya `Send + Sync` ketika parameter tipenya `Send + Sync`."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`Send + !Sync`"
msgstr "`Send + !Sync`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid ""
"These types can be moved to other threads, but they're not thread-safe. "
"Typically because of interior mutability:"
msgstr ""
"Tipe ini dapat dipindahkan ke thread lain, tetapi tidak thread-safe. "
"Biasanya karena interior mutability:"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`mpsc::Receiver<T>`"
msgstr "`mpsc::Receiver<T>`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`Cell<T>`"
msgstr "`Cell<T>`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`RefCell<T>`"
msgstr "`RefCell<T>`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`!Send + Sync`"
msgstr "`!Send + Sync`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid ""
"These types are safe to access (via shared references) from multiple "
"threads, but they cannot be moved to another thread:"
msgstr ""
"Tipe ini aman diakses (melalui shared reference) dari beberapa thread, "
"tetapi tidak dapat dipindahkan ke thread lain:"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid ""
"`MutexGuard<T>`: Uses OS level primitives which must be deallocated on the "
"thread which created them. However, an already-locked mutex can have its "
"guarded variable read by any thread with which the guard is shared (unless "
"`T` itself is `!Sync`)."
msgstr ""
"`MutexGuard<T>`: Menggunakan primitif tingkat OS yang harus dibebaskan pada "
"thread yang membuatnya. Namun, mutex yang sudah terkunci dapat membuat "
"variabel yang dijaganya dibaca oleh thread mana pun yang berbagi guard "
"tersebut (kecuali `T` sendiri bersifat `!Sync`)."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "`!Send + !Sync`"
msgstr "`!Send + !Sync`"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid "These types are not thread-safe and cannot be moved to other threads:"
msgstr ""
"Tipe ini tidak thread-safe dan tidak dapat dipindahkan ke thread lain:"

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid ""
"`Rc<T>`: each `Rc<T>` has a reference to an `RcBox<T>`, which contains a "
"non-atomic reference count."
msgstr ""
"`Rc<T>`: setiap `Rc<T>` memiliki reference ke `RcBox<T>`, yang berisi "
"reference count non-atomik."

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md
msgid ""
"`*const T`, `*mut T`: Rust assumes raw pointers may have special concurrency"
" considerations."
msgstr ""
"`*const T`, `*mut T`: Rust mengasumsikan raw pointer mungkin memiliki "
"pertimbangan konkurensi khusus."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state.md
msgid "Arc"
msgstr "Arc"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid ""
"[`Arc<T>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Arc.html) allows "
"shared, read-only ownership via `Arc::clone`:"
msgstr ""
"[`Arc<T>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Arc.html) memungkinkan "
"ownership bersama yang read-only melalui `Arc::clone`:"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid "/// A struct that prints which thread drops it.\n"
msgstr "/// A struct that prints which thread drops it.\n"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid "\"Dropped by {:?}\""
msgstr "\"Dropped by {:?}\""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid "// Sleep for 0-500ms.\n"
msgstr "// Sleep for 0-500ms.\n"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid "\"{thread_id:?}: {v:?}\""
msgstr "\"{thread_id:?}: {v:?}\""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid "// Now only the spawned threads will hold clones of `v`.\n"
msgstr "// Now only the spawned threads will hold clones of `v`.\n"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid "// When the last spawned thread finishes, it will drop `v`'s contents.\n"
msgstr ""
"// When the last spawned thread finishes, it will drop `v`'s contents.\n"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid ""
"`Arc` stands for \"Atomic Reference Counted\", a thread safe version of `Rc`"
" that uses atomic operations."
msgstr ""
"`Arc` adalah singkatan dari \"Atomic Reference Counted\", versi thread-safe "
"dari `Rc` yang menggunakan operasi atomik."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid ""
"`Arc<T>` implements `Clone` whether or not `T` does. It implements `Send` "
"and `Sync` if and only if `T` implements them both."
msgstr ""
"`Arc<T>` mengimplementasikan `Clone` terlepas dari apakah `T` "
"mengimplementasikannya. Tipe ini mengimplementasikan `Send` dan `Sync` jika "
"dan hanya jika `T` mengimplementasikan keduanya."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid ""
"`Arc::clone()` has the cost of atomic operations that get executed, but "
"after that the use of the `T` is free."
msgstr ""
"`Arc::clone()` memiliki biaya operasi atomik yang dieksekusi, tetapi setelah"
" itu penggunaan `T` gratis."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid ""
"Beware of reference cycles, `Arc` does not use a garbage collector to detect"
" them."
msgstr ""
"Waspadai reference cycle, `Arc` tidak menggunakan garbage collector untuk "
"mendeteksinya."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md
msgid "`std::sync::Weak` can help."
msgstr "`std::sync::Weak` dapat membantu."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid ""
"[`Mutex<T>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html) ensures "
"mutual exclusion _and_ allows mutable access to `T` behind a read-only "
"interface (another form of [interior mutability](../../borrowing/interior-"
"mutability.md)):"
msgstr ""
"[`Mutex<T>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html) "
"memastikan mutual exclusion _dan_ memungkinkan akses mutable ke `T` di balik"
" antarmuka read-only (bentuk lain dari [interior "
"mutability](../../borrowing/interior-mutability.md)):"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid "\"v: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"v: {:?}\""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid ""
"Notice how we have a [`impl<T: Send> Sync for Mutex<T>`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html#impl-Sync-for-Mutex%3CT%3E) blanket "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa kita memiliki implementasi blanket [`impl<T: Send> Sync for"
" Mutex<T>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html#impl-Sync-"
"for-Mutex%3CT%3E)."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid ""
"`Mutex` in Rust looks like a collection with just one element --- the "
"protected data."
msgstr ""
"`Mutex` di Rust tampak seperti koleksi dengan hanya satu elemen --- data "
"yang dilindungi."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid ""
"It is not possible to forget to acquire the mutex before accessing the "
"protected data."
msgstr ""
"Tidak mungkin lupa memperoleh mutex sebelum mengakses data yang dilindungi."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid ""
"You can get an `&mut T` from an `&Mutex<T>` by taking the lock. The "
"`MutexGuard` ensures that the `&mut T` doesn't outlive the lock being held."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat memperoleh `&mut T` dari `&Mutex<T>` dengan mengambil lock. "
"`MutexGuard` memastikan `&mut T` tidak hidup lebih lama daripada lock yang "
"dipegang."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid ""
"`Mutex<T>` implements both `Send` and `Sync` if and only if `T` implements "
"`Send`."
msgstr ""
"`Mutex<T>` mengimplementasikan `Send` maupun `Sync` jika dan hanya jika `T` "
"mengimplementasikan `Send`."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid "A read-write lock counterpart: `RwLock`."
msgstr "Padanan read-write lock: `RwLock`."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid "Why does `lock()` return a `Result`?"
msgstr "Mengapa `lock()` mengembalikan `Result`?"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/mutex.md
msgid ""
"If the thread that held the `Mutex` panicked, the `Mutex` becomes "
"\"poisoned\" to signal that the data it protected might be in an "
"inconsistent state. Calling `lock()` on a poisoned mutex fails with a "
"[`PoisonError`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.PoisonError.html)."
" You can call `into_inner()` on the error to recover the data regardless."
msgstr ""
"Jika thread yang memegang `Mutex` panic, `Mutex` menjadi \"poisoned\" untuk "
"menandakan bahwa data yang dilindunginya mungkin berada dalam state tidak "
"konsisten. Memanggil `lock()` pada mutex yang poisoned gagal dengan "
"[`PoisonError`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.PoisonError.html)."
" Anda dapat memanggil `into_inner()` pada error tersebut untuk memulihkan "
"data bagaimanapun."

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/example.md
msgid "Let us see `Arc` and `Mutex` in action:"
msgstr "Mari kita lihat `Arc` dan `Mutex` beraksi:"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/example.md
msgid "// use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\n"
msgstr "// use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\n"

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/example.md
msgid "\"v: {v:?}\""
msgstr "\"v: {v:?}\""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/example.md
