#: src/concurrency/welcome-async.md
msgid ""
"\"Async\" is a concurrency model where multiple tasks are executed "
"concurrently by executing each task until it would block, then switching to "
"another task that is ready to make progress. The model allows running a "
"larger number of tasks on a limited number of threads. This is because the "
"per-task overhead is typically very low and operating systems provide "
"primitives for efficiently identifying I/O that is able to proceed."
msgstr ""
"\"Async\" adalah model konkurensi ketika beberapa task dieksekusi secara "
"konkuren dengan menjalankan setiap task hingga akan memblokir, lalu beralih "
"ke task lain yang siap membuat kemajuan. Model ini memungkinkan menjalankan "
"lebih banyak task pada jumlah thread yang terbatas. Ini karena overhead per "
"task biasanya sangat rendah dan sistem operasi menyediakan primitif untuk "
"mengidentifikasi I/O yang dapat dilanjutkan secara efisien."

#: src/concurrency/welcome-async.md
msgid ""
"Rust's asynchronous operation is based on \"futures\", which represent work "
"that may be completed in the future. Futures are \"polled\" until they "
"signal that they are complete."
msgstr ""
"Operasi asinkron Rust berbasis \"future\", yang merepresentasikan pekerjaan "
"yang mungkin selesai di masa mendatang. Future di-\"poll\" hingga memberi "
"sinyal bahwa pekerjaannya selesai."

#: src/concurrency/welcome-async.md
msgid ""
"Futures are polled by an async runtime, and several different runtimes are "
"available."
msgstr ""
"Future di-poll oleh async runtime, dan tersedia beberapa runtime yang "
"berbeda."

#: src/concurrency/welcome-async.md
msgid ""
"Python has a similar model in its `asyncio`. However, its `Future` type is "
"callback-based, and not polled. Async Python programs require a \"loop\", "
"similar to a runtime in Rust."
msgstr ""
"Python memiliki model serupa pada `asyncio`-nya. Namun, tipe `Future` Python"
" berbasis callback, bukan poll. Program Python async memerlukan \"loop\", "
"serupa dengan runtime di Rust."

#: src/concurrency/welcome-async.md
msgid ""
"JavaScript's `Promise` is similar, but again callback-based. The language "
"runtime implements the event loop, so the majority of the details of Promise"
" resolution are hidden."
msgstr ""
"`Promise` JavaScript serupa, tetapi juga berbasis callback. Runtime bahasa "
"mengimplementasikan event loop, sehingga sebagian besar detail penyelesaian "
"Promise tersembunyi."

#: src/concurrency/welcome-async.md
msgid ""
"Including 10 minute breaks, this session should take about 3 hours and 30 "
"minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Termasuk jeda 10 menit, sesi ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 3 jam 30 "
"menit. Sesi ini berisi:"

#: src/concurrency/async.md
msgid "async/await"
msgstr "async/await"

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid ""
"At a high level, async Rust code looks very much like \"normal\" sequential "
"code:"
msgstr ""
"Secara garis besar, kode Rust async tampak sangat mirip kode sekuensial "
"\"normal\":"

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid "\"Count is: {i}!\""
msgstr "\"Count is: {i}!\""

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid ""
"Note that this is a simplified example to show the syntax. There is no long "
"running operation or any real concurrency in it!"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa ini adalah contoh yang disederhanakan untuk menunjukkan "
"sintaks. Tidak ada operasi berjalan lama atau konkurensi nyata di dalamnya!"

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid ""
"The \"async\" keyword is syntactic sugar. The compiler replaces the return "
"type with a future."
msgstr ""
"Keyword \"async\" adalah syntactic sugar. Compiler mengganti tipe kembalian "
"dengan future."

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid ""
"You cannot make `main` async, without additional instructions to the "
"compiler on how to use the returned future."
msgstr ""
"Anda tidak dapat membuat `main` async tanpa instruksi tambahan kepada "
"compiler tentang cara menggunakan future yang dikembalikan."

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid ""
"You need an executor to run async code. `block_on` blocks the current thread"
" until the provided future has run to completion."
msgstr ""
"Anda memerlukan executor untuk menjalankan kode async. `block_on` memblokir "
"thread saat ini hingga future yang diberikan selesai dijalankan."

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid ""
"`.await` asynchronously waits for the completion of another operation. "
"Unlike `block_on`, `.await` doesn't block the current thread."
msgstr ""
"`.await` menunggu penyelesaian operasi lain secara asinkron. Berbeda dari "
"`block_on`, `.await` tidak memblokir thread saat ini."

#: src/concurrency/async/async-await.md
msgid ""
"`.await` can only be used inside an `async` function (or block; these are "
"introduced later)."
msgstr ""
"`.await` hanya dapat digunakan di dalam fungsi `async` (atau block; ini "
"diperkenalkan nanti)."

#: src/concurrency/async/futures.md
msgid ""
"[`Future`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/future/trait.Future.html) is a "
"trait, implemented by objects that represent an operation that may not be "
"complete yet. A future can be polled, and `poll` returns a "
"[`Poll`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/task/enum.Poll.html)."
msgstr ""
"[`Future`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/future/trait.Future.html) adalah "
"trait, yang diimplementasikan oleh objek yang merepresentasikan operasi yang"
" mungkin belum selesai. Future dapat di-poll, dan `poll` mengembalikan "
"[`Poll`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/task/enum.Poll.html)."

#: src/concurrency/async/futures.md
msgid ""
"An async function returns an `impl Future`. It's also possible (but "
"uncommon) to implement `Future` for your own types. For example, the "
"`JoinHandle` returned from `tokio::spawn` implements `Future` to allow "
"joining to it."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi async mengembalikan `impl Future`. Dimungkinkan juga (tetapi tidak "
"umum) mengimplementasikan `Future` untuk tipe Anda sendiri. Misalnya, "
"`JoinHandle` yang dikembalikan `tokio::spawn` mengimplementasikan `Future` "
"agar dapat di-join."

#: src/concurrency/async/futures.md
msgid ""
"The `.await` keyword, applied to a Future, causes the current async function"
" to pause until that Future is ready, and then evaluates to its output."
msgstr ""
"Keyword `.await`, yang diterapkan pada Future, menyebabkan fungsi async saat"
" ini berhenti sementara hingga Future tersebut siap, lalu mengevaluasi ke "
"output-nya."

#: src/concurrency/async/futures.md
msgid ""
"The `Future` and `Poll` types are implemented exactly as shown; click the "
"links to show the implementations in the docs."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `Future` dan `Poll` diimplementasikan persis seperti yang ditunjukkan; "
"klik tautan untuk menampilkan implementasinya di dokumentasi."

#: src/concurrency/async/futures.md
msgid ""
"`Context` allows a Future to schedule itself to be polled again when an "
"event such as a timeout occurs."
msgstr ""
"`Context` memungkinkan Future menjadwalkan dirinya untuk di-poll kembali "
"ketika suatu event seperti timeout terjadi."

#: src/concurrency/async/futures.md
msgid ""
"`Pin` ensures that the Future isn't moved in memory, so that pointers into "
"that future remain valid. This is required to allow references to remain "
"valid after an `.await`. We will address `Pin` in the \"Pitfalls\" segment."
msgstr ""
"`Pin` memastikan Future tidak dipindahkan di memori, sehingga pointer ke "
"future tersebut tetap valid. Ini diperlukan agar reference tetap valid "
"setelah `.await`. Kami akan membahas `Pin` pada segmen \"Pitfalls\"."

