"gagal. Mengapa `send` juga gagal dalam situasi ini?"

#: src/concurrency/async-control-flow/select.md
msgid ""
"`select!` is also frequently used in a loop in \"actor\" architectures, "
"where a task reacts to events in a loop. That has some pitfalls, which will "
"be discussed in the next segment."
msgstr ""
"`select!` juga sering digunakan dalam loop pada arsitektur \"actor\", ketika"
" suatu task bereaksi terhadap event dalam loop. Pola ini memiliki beberapa "
"jebakan, yang akan dibahas pada segmen berikutnya."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls.md
msgid ""
"Async / await provides convenient and efficient abstraction for concurrent "
"asynchronous programming. However, the async/await model in Rust also comes "
"with its share of pitfalls and footguns. We illustrate some of them in this "
"chapter."
msgstr ""
"Async / await menyediakan abstraksi yang nyaman dan efisien untuk "
"pemrograman asinkron yang konkuren. Namun, model async/await di Rust juga "
"memiliki jebakan dan footgun tersendiri. Kami mengilustrasikan beberapa di "
"antaranya pada bab ini."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls.md
msgid "Pin"
msgstr "Pin"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid "Blocking the executor"
msgstr "Memblokir Executor"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid ""
"Most async runtimes only allow IO tasks to run concurrently. This means that"
" CPU blocking tasks will block the executor and prevent other tasks from "
"being executed. An easy workaround is to use async equivalent methods where "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar async runtime hanya mengizinkan task IO berjalan secara "
"konkuren. Ini berarti task yang memblokir CPU akan memblokir executor dan "
"mencegah task lain dieksekusi. Solusi mudahnya adalah menggunakan method "
"setara async bila memungkinkan."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid "\"future {id} slept for {duration_ms}ms, finished after {}ms\""
msgstr "\"future {id} slept for {duration_ms}ms, finished after {}ms\""

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid "\"current_thread\""
msgstr "\"current_thread\""

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid ""
"Run the code and see that the sleeps happen consecutively rather than "
"concurrently."
msgstr ""
"Jalankan kode dan lihat bahwa sleep terjadi secara berurutan, bukan "
"konkuren."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid ""
"The `\"current_thread\"` flavor puts all tasks on a single thread. This "
"makes the effect more obvious, but the bug is still present in the multi-"
"threaded flavor."
msgstr ""
"Varian `\"current_thread\"` menempatkan semua task pada satu thread. Ini "
"membuat efeknya lebih jelas, tetapi bug tetap ada pada varian multi-thread."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid ""
"Switch the `std::thread::sleep` to `tokio::time::sleep` and await its "
"result."
msgstr ""
"Ganti `std::thread::sleep` menjadi `tokio::time::sleep` dan await hasilnya."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid ""
"Another fix would be to `tokio::task::spawn_blocking` which spawns an actual"
" thread and transforms its handle into a future without blocking the "
"executor."
msgstr ""
"Perbaikan lain adalah `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`, yang melahirkan thread "
"sungguhan dan mentransformasi handle-nya menjadi future tanpa memblokir "
"executor."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid ""
"You should not think of tasks as OS threads. They do not map 1 to 1 and "
"executors will allow multiple tasks to run on a single OS thread. This is "
"particularly problematic when interacting with other libraries via FFI, "
"where that library might depend on thread-local storage or map to specific "
"OS threads (e.g., CUDA). Prefer `tokio::task::spawn_blocking` in such "
"situations."
msgstr ""
"Anda tidak seharusnya menganggap task sebagai thread OS. Keduanya tidak "
"berkorespondensi 1 banding 1, dan executor memungkinkan beberapa task "
"berjalan pada satu thread OS. Ini sangat bermasalah saat berinteraksi dengan"
" library lain melalui FFI, karena library tersebut mungkin bergantung pada "
"thread-local storage atau memetakan ke thread OS tertentu (misalnya CUDA). "
"Utamakan `tokio::task::spawn_blocking` dalam situasi seperti itu."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/blocking-executor.md
msgid ""
"Use sync mutexes with care. Holding a mutex over an `.await` may cause "
"another task to block, and that task may be running on the same thread."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan mutex sync dengan hati-hati. Menahan mutex selama `.await` dapat "
"menyebabkan task lain terblokir, dan task tersebut mungkin berjalan pada "
"thread yang sama."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"Recall an async function or block creates a type implementing `Future` and "
"containing all of the local variables. Some of those variables can hold "
"references (pointers) to other local variables. To ensure those remain "
"valid, the future can never be moved to a different memory location."
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa fungsi atau block async membuat tipe yang mengimplementasikan "
"`Future` dan berisi semua variabel lokal. Sebagian variabel tersebut dapat "
"menyimpan reference (pointer) ke variabel lokal lain. Untuk memastikan "
"reference tetap valid, future tidak boleh pernah dipindahkan ke lokasi "
"memori lain."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"To prevent moving the future type in memory, it can only be polled through a"
" pinned pointer. `Pin` is a wrapper around a reference that disallows all "
"operations that would move the instance it points to into a different memory"
" location."
msgstr ""
"Untuk mencegah pemindahan tipe future di memori, future hanya dapat di-poll "
"melalui pinned pointer. `Pin` adalah wrapper di sekitar reference yang "
"melarang semua operasi yang akan memindahkan instance yang ditunjuknya ke "
"lokasi memori lain."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
