msgstr "\"work result for iteration {i}: {resp}\""

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"You may recognize this as an example of the actor pattern. Actors typically "
"call `select!` in a loop."
msgstr ""
"Anda mungkin mengenali ini sebagai contoh pola actor. Actor biasanya "
"memanggil `select!` dalam loop."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"This serves as a summation of a few of the previous lessons, so take your "
"time with it."
msgstr ""
"Ini berfungsi sebagai rangkuman beberapa pelajaran sebelumnya, jadi luangkan"
" waktu untuk memahaminya."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"Naively add a `_ = sleep(Duration::from_millis(100)) => { println!(..) }` to"
" the `select!`. This will never execute. Why?"
msgstr ""
"Tambahkan secara naif `_ = sleep(Duration::from_millis(100)) => { "
"println!(..) }` ke `select!`. Ini tidak akan pernah dieksekusi. Mengapa?"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"Instead, add a `timeout_fut` containing that future outside of the `loop`:"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai gantinya, tambahkan `timeout_fut` yang berisi future tersebut di "
"luar `loop`:"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"This still doesn't work. Follow the compiler errors, adding `&mut` to the "
"`timeout_fut` in the `select!` to work around the move, then using "
"`Box::pin`:"
msgstr ""
"Ini masih tidak berfungsi. Ikuti error compiler, tambahkan `&mut` pada "
"`timeout_fut` di `select!` untuk mengakali move, lalu gunakan `Box::pin`:"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"This compiles, but once the timeout expires it is `Poll::Ready` on every "
"iteration (a fused future would help with this). Update to reset "
"`timeout_fut` every time it expires:"
msgstr ""
"Ini dapat dikompilasi, tetapi setelah timeout habis, future tersebut menjadi"
" `Poll::Ready` pada setiap iterasi (fused future akan membantu hal ini). "
"Perbarui agar `timeout_fut` di-reset setiap kali timeout habis:"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"Box allocates on the heap. In some cases, `std::pin::pin!` (only recently "
"stabilized, with older code often using `tokio::pin!`) is also an option, "
"but that is difficult to use for a future that is reassigned."
msgstr ""
"Box mengalokasikan di heap. Dalam beberapa kasus, `std::pin::pin!` (baru "
"distabilkan, dengan kode lama sering menggunakan `tokio::pin!`) juga menjadi"
" opsi, tetapi sulit digunakan untuk future yang ditetapkan ulang."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"Another alternative is to not use `pin` at all but spawn another task that "
"will send to a `oneshot` channel every 100ms."
msgstr ""
"Alternatif lain adalah tidak menggunakan `pin` sama sekali, melainkan "
"melahirkan task lain yang akan mengirim ke channel `oneshot` setiap 100ms."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"Data that contains pointers to itself is called self-referential. Normally, "
"the Rust borrow checker would prevent self-referential data from being "
"moved, as the references cannot outlive the data they point to. However, the"
" code transformation for async blocks and functions is not verified by the "
"borrow checker."
msgstr ""
"Data yang berisi pointer ke dirinya sendiri disebut self-referential. "
"Biasanya, borrow checker Rust akan mencegah data self-referential "
"dipindahkan, karena reference tidak boleh hidup lebih lama daripada data "
"yang ditunjuknya. Namun, transformasi kode untuk block dan fungsi async "
"tidak diverifikasi oleh borrow checker."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"`Pin` is a wrapper around a reference. An object cannot be moved from its "
"place using a pinned pointer. However, it can still be moved through an "
"unpinned pointer."
msgstr ""
"`Pin` adalah wrapper di sekitar reference. Objek tidak dapat dipindahkan "
"dari tempatnya menggunakan pinned pointer. Namun, objek tetap dapat "
"dipindahkan melalui pointer yang tidak di-pin."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/pin.md
msgid ""
"The `poll` method of the `Future` trait uses `Pin<&mut Self>` instead of "
"`&mut Self` to refer to the instance. That's why it can only be called on a "
"pinned pointer."
msgstr ""
"Method `poll` pada trait `Future` menggunakan `Pin<&mut Self>` alih-alih "
"`&mut Self` untuk merujuk instance. Itulah sebabnya method ini hanya dapat "
"dipanggil pada pinned pointer."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
msgid ""
"Async methods in traits were stabilized in the 1.75 release. This required "
"support for using return-position `impl Trait` in traits, as the desugaring "
"for `async fn` includes `-> impl Future<Output = ...>`."
msgstr ""
"Method async dalam trait distabilkan pada rilis 1.75. Ini memerlukan "
"dukungan penggunaan return-position `impl Trait` dalam trait, karena "
"desugaring untuk `async fn` mencakup `-> impl Future<Output = ...>`."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
msgid ""
"However, even with the native support, there are specific pitfalls around "
"`async fn`:"
msgstr ""
"Namun, bahkan dengan dukungan native, ada jebakan khusus seputar `async fn`:"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
msgid ""
"Return-position `impl Trait` captures all in-scope lifetimes (so certain "
"patterns of borrowing cannot be expressed)."
msgstr ""
"Return-position `impl Trait` menangkap semua lifetime dalam scope (sehingga "
"pola borrowing tertentu tidak dapat diekspresikan)."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
msgid ""
"Async traits cannot be used with [trait objects](../../smart-pointers/trait-"
"objects.md) (`dyn Trait` support)."
msgstr ""
"Async trait tidak dapat digunakan dengan [trait object](../../smart-"
"pointers/trait-objects.md) (dukungan `dyn Trait`)."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
msgid ""
"The [async_trait](https://docs.rs/async-trait/) crate provides a workaround "
"for `dyn` support through a macro, with specific caveats:"
msgstr ""
"Crate [async_trait](https://docs.rs/async-trait/) menyediakan solusi untuk "
"dukungan `dyn` melalui macro, dengan peringatan khusus:"

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
msgid "\"Running all sleepers...\""
msgstr "\"Running all sleepers...\""

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
