#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/async-traits.md
msgid ""
"Try creating a new sleeper struct that will sleep for a random amount of "
"time and adding it to the `Vec`."
msgstr ""
"Coba buat struct sleeper baru yang akan tidur selama waktu acak dan "
"tambahkan ke `Vec`."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid ""
"Dropping a future implies it can never be polled again. This is called "
"_cancellation_ and it can occur at any `await` point. Care is needed to "
"ensure the system works correctly even when futures are cancelled. For "
"example, it shouldn't deadlock or lose data."
msgstr ""
"Men-drop future berarti future tersebut tidak akan pernah dapat di-poll "
"lagi. Ini disebut _cancellation_ dan dapat terjadi pada titik `await` mana "
"pun. Diperlukan kehati-hatian agar sistem tetap bekerja dengan benar bahkan "
"ketika future dibatalkan. Misalnya, sistem tidak boleh deadlock atau "
"kehilangan data."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid "\"not UTF-8\""
msgstr "\"not UTF-8\""

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid "\"hi\\nthere\\n\""
msgstr "\"hi\\nthere\\n\""

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid "\"tick!\""
msgstr "\"tick!\""

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid ""
"The compiler doesn't help with cancellation-safety. You need to read API "
"documentation and consider what state your `async fn` holds."
msgstr ""
"Compiler tidak membantu soal cancellation-safety. Anda perlu membaca "
"dokumentasi API dan mempertimbangkan state apa yang dipegang `async fn` "
"Anda."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid ""
"Unlike `panic` and `?`, cancellation is part of normal control flow (vs "
"error-handling)."
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dari `panic` dan `?`, cancellation adalah bagian dari alur kontrol "
"normal (bukan penanganan error)."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid "The example loses parts of the string."
msgstr "Contoh tersebut kehilangan sebagian string."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid ""
"Whenever the `tick()` branch finishes first, `next()` and its `buf` are "
"dropped."
msgstr ""
"Setiap kali cabang `tick()` selesai lebih dahulu, `next()` dan `buf`-nya di-"
"drop."

#: src/concurrency/async-pitfalls/cancellation.md
msgid ""
"`LinesReader` can be made cancellation-safe by making `buf` part of the "
"struct:"
msgstr ""
"`LinesReader` dapat dibuat cancellation-safe dengan menjadikan `buf` bagian "
"dari struct:"

