#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Welcome to Idiomatic Rust"
msgstr "Selamat Datang di Idiomatic Rust"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"[Rust Fundamentals](../welcome-day-1.md) introduced Rust syntax and core "
"concepts. We now want to go one step further: how do you use Rust "
"_effectively_ in your projects? What does _idiomatic_ Rust look like?"
msgstr ""
"[Rust Fundamentals](../welcome-day-1.md) memperkenalkan sintaks dan konsep "
"inti Rust. Sekarang kami ingin melangkah lebih jauh: bagaimana Anda "
"menggunakan Rust secara _efektif_ dalam proyek Anda? Seperti apa _idiomatic_"
" Rust?"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"This course is opinionated: we will nudge you towards some patterns, and "
"away from others. Nonetheless, we do recognize that some projects may have "
"different needs. We always provide the necessary information to help you "
"make informed decisions within the context and constraints of your own "
"projects."
msgstr ""
"Kursus ini bersikap opinionated: kami akan mendorong Anda menuju pola "
"tertentu, dan menjauh dari pola lain. Meskipun demikian, kami menyadari "
"bahwa sebagian proyek mungkin memiliki kebutuhan berbeda. Kami selalu "
"menyediakan informasi yang diperlukan untuk membantu Anda membuat keputusan "
"yang tepat dalam konteks dan batasan proyek Anda sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "⚠️ This course is under **active development**."
msgstr "⚠️ Kursus ini sedang dalam **pengembangan aktif**."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"The material may change frequently and there might be errors that have not "
"yet been spotted. Nonetheless, we encourage you to browse through and "
"provide early feedback!"
msgstr ""
"Materi dapat berubah sering dan mungkin ada error yang belum ditemukan. "
"Meskipun demikian, kami mendorong Anda untuk menelusurinya dan memberikan "
"umpan balik awal!"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Including 10 minute breaks, this session should take about 13 hours and 55 "
"minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Termasuk jeda 10 menit, sesi ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 13 jam 55 "
"menit. Sesi ini berisi:"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"The course will cover the topics listed below. Each topic may be covered in "
"one or more slides, depending on its complexity and relevance."
msgstr ""
"Kursus akan membahas topik-topik yang tercantum di bawah. Setiap topik dapat"
" dibahas dalam satu atau lebih slide, bergantung pada kompleksitas dan "
"relevansinya."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Target Audience"
msgstr "Target Audiens"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Engineers with at least 2-3 years of coding experience in C, C++11 or newer,"
" Java 7 or newer, Python 2 or 3, Go or any other similar imperative "
"programming language. We have no expectation of experience with more modern "
"or feature-rich languages like Swift, Kotlin, C#, or TypeScript."
msgstr ""
"Engineer dengan pengalaman coding setidaknya 2-3 tahun dalam C, C++11 atau "
"lebih baru, Java 7 atau lebih baru, Python 2 atau 3, Go, atau bahasa "
"pemrograman imperatif serupa lainnya. Kami tidak mengharapkan pengalaman "
"dengan bahasa yang lebih modern atau kaya fitur seperti Swift, Kotlin, C#, "
"atau TypeScript."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Foundations of API design"
msgstr "Dasar-Dasar Desain API"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Golden rule: prioritize clarity and readability at the callsite. People will"
" spend much more time reading the call sites than declarations of the "
"functions being called."
msgstr ""
"Aturan emas: utamakan kejelasan dan keterbacaan di lokasi pemanggilan. Orang"
" akan menghabiskan jauh lebih banyak waktu membaca call site daripada "
"deklarasi fungsi yang dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Make your API predictable"
msgstr "Buat API Anda Dapat Diprediksi"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Follow naming conventions (case conventions, prefer vocabulary precedented "
"in the standard library - e.g., methods should be called \"push\" not "
"\"push_back\", \"is_empty\" not \"empty\" etc.)"
msgstr ""
"Ikuti konvensi penamaan (konvensi kapitalisasi, utamakan kosakata yang sudah"
" ada presedennya di standard library - misalnya, method sebaiknya dinamai "
"\"push\" bukan \"push_back\", \"is_empty\" bukan \"empty\", dan sebagainya.)"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Know the vocabulary types and traits in the standard library, and use them "
"in your APIs. If something feels like a basic type/algorithm, check in the "
"standard library first."
msgstr ""
"Kenali tipe dan trait kosakata di standard library, dan gunakan dalam API "
"Anda. Jika sesuatu terasa seperti tipe/algoritma dasar, periksa dulu di "
"standard library."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Use well-established API design patterns that we will discuss later in this "
"class (e.g., newtype, owned/view type pairs, error handling)"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan pola desain API yang sudah mapan yang akan kami bahas nanti di kelas"
" ini (misalnya, newtype, pasangan tipe owned/view, penanganan error)"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Write meaningful and effective doc comments (e.g., don't merely repeat the "
"method name with spaces instead of underscores, don't repeat the same "
"information just to fill out every markdown tag, provide usage examples)"
msgstr ""
"Tulis doc comment yang bermakna dan efektif (misalnya, jangan sekadar "
"mengulang nama method dengan spasi alih-alih garis bawah, jangan mengulang "
"informasi yang sama hanya untuk mengisi setiap tag markdown, berikan contoh "
"penggunaan)"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Leveraging the type system"
msgstr "Memanfaatkan Sistem Tipe"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Short recap on enums, structs and type aliases"
msgstr "Rekap singkat tentang enum, struct, dan type alias"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Newtype pattern and encapsulation: parse, don't validate"
msgstr "Pola newtype dan enkapsulasi: parse, jangan validasi"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Extension traits: avoid the newtype pattern when you want to provide "
"additional behaviour"
msgstr ""
"Extension trait: hindari pola newtype ketika Anda ingin menyediakan perilaku"
" tambahan"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"RAII, scope guards and drop bombs: using `Drop` to clean up resources, "
"trigger actions or enforce invariants"
msgstr ""
"RAII, scope guard, dan drop bomb: menggunakan `Drop` untuk membersihkan "
"resource, memicu tindakan, atau menegakkan invariant"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "\"Token\" types: force users to prove they've performed a specific action"
msgstr ""
"Tipe \"token\": memaksa pengguna membuktikan bahwa mereka telah melakukan "
"tindakan tertentu"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"The typestate pattern: enforce correct state transitions at compile-time"
msgstr ""
"Pola typestate: menegakkan transisi state yang benar pada waktu kompilasi"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Using the borrow checker to enforce invariants that have nothing to do with "
"memory ownership"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan borrow checker untuk menegakkan invariant yang tidak ada "
"hubungannya dengan ownership memori"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "OwnedFd/BorrowedFd in the standard library"
msgstr "OwnedFd/BorrowedFd di standard library"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "[Branded types](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/paper.pdf)"
msgstr "[Branded types](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/paper.pdf)"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Don't fight the borrow checker"
msgstr "Jangan Melawan Borrow Checker"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"\"Owned\" types and \"view\" types: `&str` and `String`, `Path` and "
"`PathBuf`, etc."
msgstr ""
"Tipe \"owned\" dan tipe \"view\": `&str` dan `String`, `Path` dan `PathBuf`,"
" dan sebagainya."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Don't hide ownership requirements: avoid hidden `.clone()`, learn to love "
"`Cow`"
msgstr ""
"Jangan sembunyikan persyaratan ownership: hindari `.clone()` tersembunyi, "
"belajarlah menyukai `Cow`"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Split types along ownership boundaries"
msgstr "Pisahkan tipe menurut batas ownership"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Structure your ownership hierarchy like a tree"
msgstr "Susun hierarki ownership Anda seperti pohon"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Strategies to manage circular dependencies: reference counting, using "
"indexes instead of references"
msgstr ""
"Strategi mengelola dependensi sirkular: reference counting, menggunakan "
"indeks alih-alih reference"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Interior mutability (Cell, RefCell)"
msgstr "Interior mutability (Cell, RefCell)"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Working with lifetime parameters on user-defined data types"
msgstr ""
"Bekerja dengan parameter lifetime pada tipe data yang ditentukan pengguna"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Polymorphism in Rust"
msgstr "Polimorfisme di Rust"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "A quick refresher on traits and generic functions"
msgstr "Penyegaran singkat tentang trait dan fungsi generic"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Rust has no inheritance: what are the implications?"
msgstr "Rust tidak memiliki inheritance: apa implikasinya?"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Using enums for polymorphism"
msgstr "Menggunakan enum untuk polimorfisme"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Using traits for polymorphism"
msgstr "Menggunakan trait untuk polimorfisme"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Using composition"
msgstr "Menggunakan komposisi"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "How do I pick the most appropriate pattern?"
msgstr "Bagaimana Saya Memilih Pola yang Paling Tepat?"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Working with generics"
msgstr "Bekerja dengan Generic"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Generic type parameter in a function or trait object as an argument?"
msgstr ""
"Parameter tipe generic dalam fungsi atau trait object sebagai argumen?"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Trait bounds don't have to refer to the generic parameter"
msgstr "Trait bound tidak harus merujuk parameter generic"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Type parameters in traits: should it be a generic parameter or an associated"
" type?"
msgstr ""
"Parameter tipe dalam trait: sebaiknya parameter generic atau associated "
"type?"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Macros: a valuable tool to DRY up code when traits are not enough (or too "
"complex)"
msgstr ""
"Macro: alat berharga untuk menerapkan DRY pada kode ketika trait tidak cukup"
" (atau terlalu kompleks)"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "What is the purpose of errors? Recovery vs. reporting."
msgstr "Apa tujuan error? Pemulihan vs. pelaporan."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Result vs. Option"
msgstr "Result vs. Option"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Designing good errors:"
msgstr "Merancang Error yang Baik:"

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Determine the error scope."
msgstr "Tentukan cakupan error."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Capture additional context as the error flows upwards, crossing scope "
"boundaries."
msgstr ""
"Tangkap konteks tambahan saat error mengalir ke atas, melintasi batas scope."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Leverage the `Error` trait to keep track of the full error chain."
msgstr "Manfaatkan trait `Error` untuk melacak rantai error secara lengkap."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Leverage `thiserror` to reduce boilerplate when defining error types."
msgstr ""
"Manfaatkan `thiserror` untuk mengurangi boilerplate saat mendefinisikan tipe"
" error."

#: src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid ""
"Distinguish fatal errors from recoverable errors using `Result<Result<T, "
"RecoverableError>, FatalError>`."
msgstr ""
"Bedakan error fatal dari error yang dapat dipulihkan menggunakan "
"`Result<Result<T, RecoverableError>, FatalError>`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design.md
msgid "This segment should take about 3 hours and 15 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Segmen ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 3 jam 15 menit. Segmen ini "
