msgid ""
"// expert writes for newcomers\n"
"/// Prepares the Mid-level IR (MIR) for borrow checking.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// The borrow checker operates on a simplified, \"canonical\" form of the MIR.  \n"
"/// This function performs that transformation. It is a prerequisite for the  \n"
"/// final stages of code generation.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// For more about Rust's intermediate representations, see the  \n"
"/// [rustc-dev-guide](https://rustc-dev-guide.rust-lang.org/mir/index.html).  \n"
msgstr ""
"// expert writes for newcomers\n"
"/// Prepares the Mid-level IR (MIR) for borrow checking.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// The borrow checker operates on a simplified, \"canonical\" form of the MIR.  \n"
"/// This function performs that transformation. It is a prerequisite for the  \n"
"/// final stages of code generation.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// For more about Rust's intermediate representations, see the  \n"
"/// [rustc-dev-guide](https://rustc-dev-guide.rust-lang.org/mir/index.html).  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Background: The [curse of "
"knowledge](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curse_of_knowledge) is a cognitive "
"bias where experts assume that others have the same level of expertise and "
"perspective."
msgstr ""
"Latar belakang: [curse of "
"knowledge](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curse_of_knowledge) adalah bias "
"kognitif ketika ahli mengasumsikan orang lain memiliki tingkat keahlian dan "
"perspektif yang sama."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: Your reader does not have the same level of expertise and the "
"same perspective as you. Don't write for people like yourself, write for "
"others."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Pembaca Anda tidak memiliki tingkat keahlian dan perspektif yang "
"sama dengan Anda. Jangan menulis untuk orang seperti diri Anda sendiri, "
"tulislah untuk orang lain."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Unintentionally writing for yourself can lead to people not understanding a "
"point you're trying to make or the concept you're trying to articulate."
msgstr ""
"Menulis untuk diri sendiri tanpa sengaja dapat menyebabkan orang lain tidak "
"memahami poin yang Anda sampaikan atau konsep yang Anda artikulasikan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Imagine a version of you, or others you've known, struggling to find "
"practical information while going through documentation."
msgstr ""
"Bayangkan versi diri Anda, atau orang lain yang Anda kenal, yang kesulitan "
"menemukan informasi praktis saat menelusuri dokumentasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Keep this idea of a person in mind when thinking about what areas of a "
"codebase need attention for doc comments."
msgstr ""
"Ingatlah gambaran orang tersebut ketika memikirkan bagian basis kode mana "
"yang perlu diperhatikan untuk doc comment."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Also imagine a version of you, or others you've known, who is struggling to "
"find the important details in winding, extensive doc comments. Don't give "
"too much information."
msgstr ""
"Bayangkan juga versi diri Anda, atau orang lain yang Anda kenal, yang "
"kesulitan menemukan detail penting dalam doc comment yang berbelit dan "
"panjang. Jangan memberikan terlalu banyak informasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Always ask: Is this documentation making it difficult for the API user? Are "
"they able to quickly grasp what they need or find out where they could need "
"it?"
msgstr ""
"Selalu tanyakan: Apakah dokumentasi ini mempersulit pengguna API? Apakah "
"mereka dapat dengan cepat memahami apa yang mereka butuhkan atau mengetahui "
"di mana mereka mungkin membutuhkannya?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/who-are-you-writing-for.md
msgid ""
"Always consider: Experts also read API level documentation. Doc comments "
"might not be the right place to educate your audience about the basics of "
"your domain. In that case, signpost and name-drop. Divert people to long-"
"form documentation."
msgstr ""
"Selalu pertimbangkan: Ahli juga membaca dokumentasi tingkat API. Doc comment"
" mungkin bukan tempat yang tepat untuk mengedukasi audiens tentang dasar-"
"dasar domain Anda. Dalam kasus itu, beri penunjuk dan sebutkan nama. Arahkan"
" orang ke dokumentasi panjang."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "Library vs application docs"
msgstr "Dokumentasi Library vs Aplikasi"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid ""
"You might see elaborate documentation for fundamental APIs that repeats the "
"names and type signatures. Stable and highly reusable code can afford this "
"with a positive RoI."
msgstr ""
"Anda mungkin melihat dokumentasi yang rinci untuk API fundamental yang "
"mengulang nama dan signature tipe. Kode yang stabil dan sangat dapat "
"digunakan kembali dapat menanggung hal ini dengan RoI yang positif."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "Library code:"
msgstr "Kode library:"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "has a high number of users,"
msgstr "memiliki banyak pengguna,"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "solves a whole range of related problems,"
msgstr "menyelesaikan berbagai masalah terkait,"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "often has stable APIs."
msgstr "sering memiliki API yang stabil."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "Application code is the opposite:"
msgstr "Kode aplikasi adalah kebalikannya:"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "few users,"
msgstr "sedikit pengguna,"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "solves a specific problem,"
msgstr "menyelesaikan masalah tertentu,"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid "changes often."
msgstr "sering berubah."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid ""
"You might have seen elaborate documentation that repeats code, looks at the "
"same API multiple times with many examples and case studies. Context is key:"
" who wrote it, for whom, and what material it is covering, and what "
"resources did they have."
msgstr ""
"Anda mungkin pernah melihat dokumentasi rinci yang mengulang kode, membahas "
"API yang sama berkali-kali dengan banyak contoh dan studi kasus. Konteks "
"adalah kunci: siapa yang menulisnya, untuk siapa, materi apa yang dibahas, "
"dan sumber daya apa yang mereka miliki."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid ""
"Fundamental library code often has elaborate documentation, for example, the"
" standard library, highly reusable frameworks like Serde and Tokio. Teams "
"responsible for this code often have appropriate resources to write and "
"maintain elaborate documentation."
msgstr ""
"Kode library fundamental sering memiliki dokumentasi rinci, misalnya "
"standard library, framework yang sangat dapat digunakan kembali seperti "
"Serde dan Tokio. Tim yang bertanggung jawab atas kode ini sering memiliki "
"sumber daya yang memadai untuk menulis dan memelihara dokumentasi yang "
"rinci."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid ""
"Library code is often stable, so the community is going to extract a "
"significant benefit from elaborate documentation before it needs to be "
"reworked."
msgstr ""
"Kode library sering stabil, sehingga komunitas akan memperoleh manfaat "
"signifikan dari dokumentasi yang rinci sebelum dokumentasi perlu dirombak."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/library-vs-application-docs.md
msgid ""
"Application code has the opposite traits: it has few users, solves a "
"specific problem, and changes often. For application code elaborate "
"documentation quickly becomes outdated and misleading. It is also difficult "
"to extract a positive RoI from boilerplate docs even while they are up to "
"date, because there are only a few users."
msgstr ""
"Kode aplikasi memiliki sifat kebalikannya: penggunanya sedikit, "
"menyelesaikan masalah tertentu, dan sering berubah. Untuk kode aplikasi, "
"dokumentasi yang rinci cepat menjadi kedaluwarsa dan menyesatkan. Selain "
"itu, sulit memperoleh RoI positif dari dokumentasi boilerplate bahkan ketika"
" masih mutakhir, karena penggunanya hanya sedikit."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid "The Anatomy of a Doc Comment"
msgstr "Anatomi Doc Comment"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid "A brief, one-sentence summary."
msgstr "Ringkasan singkat satu kalimat."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid "A more detailed explanation."
msgstr "Penjelasan yang lebih terperinci."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid "Special sections: code examples, panics, errors, safety preconditions."
msgstr "Bagian khusus: contoh kode, panic, error, prasyarat keamanan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"/// Parses a key-value pair from a string.\n"
"///\n"
"/// The input string must be in the format `key=value`. Everything before the\n"
"/// first '=' is treated as the key, and everything after is the value.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Examples\n"
"///\n"
"/// ```\n"
"/// use my_crate::parse_key_value;\n"
"/// let (key, value) = parse_key_value(\"lang=rust\").unwrap();\n"
"/// assert_eq!(key, \"lang\");\n"
"/// assert_eq!(value, \"rust\");\n"
"/// ```\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Panics\n"
"///\n"
"/// Panics if the input is empty.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Errors\n"
"///\n"
"/// Returns a `ParseError::Malformed` if the string does not contain `=`.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// Triggers undefined behavior if...\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Parses a key-value pair from a string.\n"
"///\n"
"/// The input string must be in the format `key=value`. Everything before the\n"
"/// first '=' is treated as the key, and everything after is the value.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Examples\n"
"///\n"
"/// ```\n"
"/// use my_crate::parse_key_value;\n"
"/// let (key, value) = parse_key_value(\"lang=rust\").unwrap();\n"
"/// assert_eq!(key, \"lang\");\n"
"/// assert_eq!(value, \"rust\");\n"
"/// ```\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Panics\n"
"///\n"
"/// Panics if the input is empty.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Errors\n"
"///\n"
"/// Returns a `ParseError::Malformed` if the string does not contain `=`.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// Triggers undefined behavior if...\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"Idiomatic Rust doc comments follow a conventional structure that makes them "
"easier for developers to read."
msgstr ""
"Doc comment Rust yang idiomatis mengikuti struktur konvensional yang "
"memudahkan developer membacanya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"The first line of a doc comment is a single-sentence summary of the "
"function. Keep it concise. `rustdoc` and other tools have a strong "
"expectation about that: it is used as a short summary in module-level "
"documentation and search results."
msgstr ""
"Baris pertama doc comment adalah ringkasan fungsi dalam satu kalimat. "
"Buatlah ringkas. `rustdoc` dan alat lain memiliki ekspektasi kuat tentang "
"hal ini: baris tersebut digunakan sebagai ringkasan singkat dalam "
"dokumentasi tingkat modul dan hasil pencarian."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"Next, you can provide a long, multi-paragraph description of the \"why\" and"
" \"what\" of the function. Use Markdown."
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, Anda dapat memberikan deskripsi panjang beberapa paragraf "
"tentang \"mengapa\" dan \"apa\" fungsi tersebut. Gunakan Markdown."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"Finally, you can use top-level section headers to organize your content. Doc"
" comments commonly use `# Examples`, `# Panics`, `# Errors`, and `# Safety` "
"as section titles. The Rust community expects to see relevant aspects of "
"your API documented in these sections."
msgstr ""
"Terakhir, Anda dapat menggunakan header bagian tingkat atas untuk "
"mengorganisasi konten. Doc comment umumnya menggunakan `# Examples`, `# "
"Panics`, `# Errors`, dan `# Safety` sebagai judul bagian. Komunitas Rust "
"mengharapkan aspek relevan dari API Anda didokumentasikan pada bagian "
"tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"Rust heavily focuses on safety and correctness. Documenting behavior of your"
" code in case of errors is critical for writing reliable software."
msgstr ""
"Rust sangat berfokus pada keamanan dan kebenaran. Mendokumentasikan perilaku"
" kode Anda jika terjadi error sangat penting untuk menulis perangkat lunak "
"yang andal."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"`# Panics`: If your function may panic, you must document the specific "
"conditions when that might happen. Callers need to know what to avoid."
msgstr ""
"`# Panics`: Jika fungsi Anda mungkin panic, Anda harus mendokumentasikan "
"kondisi spesifik kapan hal itu dapat terjadi. Pemanggil perlu mengetahui apa"
" yang harus dihindari."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"**Question:** Ask the class why documenting panics is so important in a "
"language that prefers returning `Result`."
msgstr ""
"**Pertanyaan:** Tanyakan kepada kelas mengapa mendokumentasikan panic begitu"
" penting dalam bahasa yang lebih memilih mengembalikan `Result`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"**Answer:** Panics are for unrecoverable, programming errors. A library "
"should not panic unless a contract is violated by the caller. Documenting "
"these contracts is essential."
msgstr ""
"**Jawaban:** Panic ditujukan untuk error pemrograman yang tidak dapat "
"dipulihkan. Library tidak boleh panic kecuali pemanggil melanggar kontrak. "
"Mendokumentasikan kontrak tersebut sangat penting."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"`# Errors`: For functions returning a `Result`, this section explains what "
"kind of errors can occur and under what circumstances. Callers need this "
"information to write robust error handling logic."
msgstr ""
"`# Errors`: Untuk fungsi yang mengembalikan `Result`, bagian ini menjelaskan"
" jenis error yang dapat terjadi dan dalam keadaan apa. Pemanggil memerlukan "
"informasi ini untuk menulis logika penanganan error yang kokoh."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/anatomy-of-a-doc-comment.md
msgid ""
"`# Safety` comments document safety preconditions on unsafe functions that "
"must be satisfied, or else undefined behavior might result. They are "
"discussed in detail in the Unsafe Rust deep dive."
msgstr ""
"Komentar `# Safety` mendokumentasikan prasyarat keamanan pada fungsi unsafe "
"yang harus dipenuhi, jika tidak dipenuhi, undefined behavior dapat terjadi. "
"Hal ini dibahas secara terperinci dalam pendalaman Unsafe Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid "Name-dropping keywords and signposting topics"
msgstr "Menyebut Keyword dan Memberi Penunjuk Topik"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"/// A parsed representation of a [MARC 21 record leader][leader].\n"
"///\n"
"/// A MARC leader contains metadata that dictates how to interpret the rest  \n"
"/// of the record.\n"
"///\n"
"/// [leader]: https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bdleader.html\n"
msgstr ""
"/// A parsed representation of a [MARC 21 record leader][leader].\n"
"///\n"
"/// A MARC leader contains metadata that dictates how to interpret the rest  \n"
"/// of the record.\n"
"///\n"
"/// [leader]: https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bdleader.html\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"/// Determines the schema and the set of valid subsequent data fields.  \n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// Encoded in byte 6 of the leader.  \n"
msgstr ""
"/// Determines the schema and the set of valid subsequent data fields.  \n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// Encoded in byte 6 of the leader.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"/// Indicates whether to parse relationship fields, such as a \"773 Host  \n"
"    /// Item Entry\" for an article within a larger work.  \n"
"    ///  \n"
"    /// Encoded in byte 7 of the leader.  \n"
msgstr ""
"/// Indicates whether to parse relationship fields, such as a \"773 Host  \n"
"    /// Item Entry\" for an article within a larger work.  \n"
"    ///  \n"
"    /// Encoded in byte 7 of the leader.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid "// ... other fields\n"
msgstr "// ... other fields\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"/// Parses the [leader of a MARC 21 record][leader].\n"
"///  \n"
"/// The leader is encoded as a fixed-length 24-byte field, containing metadata  \n"
"/// that determines the semantic interpretation of the rest of the record.  \n"
"/// \n"
"/// [leader]: https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bdleader.html\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Parses the [leader of a MARC 21 record][leader].\n"
"///  \n"
"/// The leader is encoded as a fixed-length 24-byte field, containing metadata  \n"
"/// that determines the semantic interpretation of the rest of the record.  \n"
"/// \n"
"/// [leader]: https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bdleader.html\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: Readers of documentation will not be closely reading most of "
"your doc comments like they would dialogue in a novel they love."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Pembaca dokumentasi tidak akan membaca sebagian besar doc comment "
"Anda dengan saksama seperti membaca dialog dalam novel favorit mereka."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Users will most likely be skimming and scan-reading to find the part of the "
"documentation that is relevant to whatever problem they're trying to solve "
"in the moment."
msgstr ""
"Pengguna kemungkinan besar akan membaca sekilas dan memindai untuk menemukan"
" bagian dokumentasi yang relevan dengan masalah yang sedang mereka coba "
"selesaikan saat itu."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Once a user has found a keyword or potential signpost that's relevant to "
"them they will begin to search for context surrounding what is being "
"documented."
msgstr ""
"Setelah pengguna menemukan keyword atau penunjuk potensial yang relevan bagi"
" mereka, mereka akan mulai mencari konteks di sekitar hal yang "
"didokumentasikan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Ask the class: What do you look for in documentation? Focus on the moment-"
"to-moment searching for information here, not general values in "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada kelas: Apa yang Anda cari dalam dokumentasi? Fokus pada "
"pencarian informasi dari saat ke saat di sini, bukan nilai-nilai umum dalam "
"dokumentasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid "Name-drop keywords close to the beginning of a paragraph."
msgstr "Sebutkan keyword di dekat awal paragraf."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"This aids skimming and scanning, as the first few words of a paragraph stand"
" out the most."
msgstr ""
"Ini membantu membaca sekilas dan memindai, karena beberapa kata pertama "
"paragraf paling menonjol."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Skimming and scanning lets users quickly navigate a text, keeping keywords "
"as close to the beginning of a paragraph as possible lets a user determine "
"if they've found relevant information faster."
msgstr ""
"Membaca sekilas dan memindai memungkinkan pengguna menavigasi teks dengan "
"cepat; menempatkan keyword sedekat mungkin dengan awal paragraf memungkinkan"
" pengguna menentukan lebih cepat apakah mereka telah menemukan informasi "
"yang relevan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid "Signpost, but don't over-explain."
msgstr "Beri penunjuk, tetapi jangan menjelaskan berlebihan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Users will not necessarily have the same domain expertise as an API "
"designer."
msgstr ""
"Pengguna belum tentu memiliki keahlian domain yang sama dengan perancang "
"API."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"If a tangential, specialist term or acronym is mentioned try to bring in "
"enough context such that a novice could quickly do more research."
msgstr ""
"Jika istilah atau akronim spesialis yang tangensial disebutkan, coba berikan"
" konteks yang cukup agar pemula dapat dengan cepat melakukan riset lebih "
"lanjut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Signposting often happens organically, consider a networking library that "
"mentions various protocols. But when it doesn't happen organically, it can "
"be difficult to choose what to mention."
msgstr ""
"Pemberian penunjuk sering terjadi secara organik; pertimbangkan library "
"networking yang menyebutkan berbagai protokol. Tetapi ketika tidak terjadi "
"secara organik, bisa sulit memilih apa yang perlu disebutkan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Rule of thumb: API developers should be asking themselves \"if a novice ran "
"into what they are documenting, what sources would they look up and are "
"there any red herrings they might end up following\"?"
msgstr ""
"Aturan praktis: developer API sebaiknya bertanya pada diri sendiri \"jika "
"seorang pemula menemukan apa yang sedang mereka dokumentasikan, sumber apa "
"yang akan dicari dan apakah ada petunjuk menyesatkan yang mungkin mereka "
"ikuti\"?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"Users should be given enough information to look up subjects on their own."
msgstr ""
"Pengguna sebaiknya diberi informasi yang cukup untuk mencari topik sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md
msgid ""
"What we've already covered, predictability of an API including the naming "
"conventions, is a form of signposting."
msgstr ""
"Apa yang telah kami bahas, yaitu prediktabilitas API termasuk konvensi "
"penamaan, adalah salah satu bentuk pemberian penunjuk."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid "Avoiding Redundancy"
msgstr "Menghindari Redundansi"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Names and type signatures communicate a lot of information, don't repeat it "
"in comments!"
msgstr ""
"Nama dan signature tipe menyampaikan banyak informasi, jangan ulangi di "
"komentar!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"// Repeats name/type information. Can omit!\n"
"/// Parses an ipv4 from a str. Returns an option for failure modes.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Repeats name/type information. Can omit!\n"
"/// Parses an ipv4 from a str. Returns an option for failure modes.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid "// Repeats information obvious from the field name. Can omit!\n"
msgstr "// Repeats information obvious from the field name. Can omit!\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid "/// The customer id.\n"
msgstr "/// The customer id.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"// Mentions the type name first thing, don't do this!\n"
"/// `ServerSynchronizer` is an orchestrator that sends local edits [...]\n"
msgstr ""
"// Mentions the type name first thing, don't do this!\n"
"/// `ServerSynchronizer` is an orchestrator that sends local edits [...]\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"// Better! Focuses on purpose.\n"
"/// Sends local edits [...]\n"
msgstr ""
"// Better! Focuses on purpose.\n"
"/// Sends local edits [...]\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"// Mentions the function name first thing, don't do this!\n"
"/// `sync_to_server` sends local edits [...]\n"
msgstr ""
"// Mentions the function name first thing, don't do this!\n"
"/// `sync_to_server` sends local edits [...]\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"// Better! Focuses on function.\n"
"/// Sends local edits [...]\n"
msgstr ""
"// Better! Focuses on function.\n"
"/// Sends local edits [...]\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: Documentation that merely repeats name/signature information "
"provides nothing new to the API user."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Dokumentasi yang hanya mengulang informasi nama/signature tidak "
"memberikan hal baru kepada pengguna API."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Additionally, signature information may change over time without the "
"documentation being updated accordingly!"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, informasi signature dapat berubah seiring waktu tanpa "
"dokumentasi diperbarui sesuai!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid "This is an understandable pattern to fall into!"
msgstr "Ini adalah pola yang wajar untuk terjebak!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Naive approach to \"always document your code,\" follows this advice "
"literally but does not follow the intent."
msgstr ""
"Pendekatan naif terhadap \"selalu dokumentasikan kode Anda\" mengikuti saran"
" ini secara literal tetapi tidak mengikuti maksudnya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Some tools might enforce documentation coverage, this kind of documentation "
"is an easy fix."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian alat mungkin menegakkan cakupan dokumentasi; dokumentasi semacam "
"ini adalah perbaikan yang mudah."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid "Be aware of the purpose of different modes of documentation:"
msgstr "Sadari tujuan berbagai mode dokumentasi:"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Library code will need to be documented in ways that understand the scope of"
" what it is used for and the breadth of people who are trying to use it."
msgstr ""
"Kode library perlu didokumentasikan dengan cara yang memahami cakupan "
"penggunaannya dan keluasan orang yang mencoba menggunakannya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Application code has a more narrow purpose, it can afford to be more simple "
"and direct."
msgstr ""
"Kode aplikasi memiliki tujuan yang lebih sempit; kode tersebut dapat lebih "
"sederhana dan langsung."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid "The name of an item is part of the documentation of that item."
msgstr "Nama suatu item adalah bagian dari dokumentasi item tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Similarly, the signature of a function is part of the documentation of that "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Serupa dengan itu, signature suatu fungsi adalah bagian dari dokumentasi "
"fungsi tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Therefore: Some aspects of the item are already covered when you start "
"writing doc comments!"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu: Sebagian aspek item sudah tercakup ketika Anda mulai "
"menulis doc comment!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid "Do not repeat information for the sake of an itemized list."
msgstr "Jangan mengulang informasi demi daftar berpoin."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Many areas of the standard library have minimal documentation because the "
"name and types do give enough information."
msgstr ""
"Banyak bagian standard library memiliki dokumentasi minimal karena nama dan "
"tipenya memang memberikan informasi yang cukup."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Rule of Thumb: What information is missing from a user's perspective? Other "
"than name, signature, and irrelevant details of the implementation."
msgstr ""
"Aturan Praktis: Informasi apa yang hilang dari perspektif pengguna? Selain "
"nama, signature, dan detail implementasi yang tidak relevan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"Don't explain the basics of Rust or the standard library. Assume the reader "
"has an intermediate understanding of the language itself. Focus on "
"documenting your API."
msgstr ""
"Jangan menjelaskan dasar-dasar Rust atau standard library. Asumsikan pembaca"
" memiliki pemahaman menengah tentang bahasa itu sendiri. Fokus pada "
"mendokumentasikan API Anda."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"For example, if your function returns `Result`, you don't need to explain "
"how `Result` or the question mark operators work."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, jika fungsi Anda mengembalikan `Result`, Anda tidak perlu "
"menjelaskan cara kerja `Result` atau operator tanda tanya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"The `#![warn(missing_docs)]` lint can be helpful for enforcing the existence"
" of doc comments, but puts a large burden on developers that could lead to "
"leaning onto these patterns of writing low-quality comments."
msgstr ""
"Lint `#![warn(missing_docs)]` dapat membantu menegakkan keberadaan doc "
"comment, tetapi membebani developer secara besar yang dapat membuat mereka "
"bergantung pada pola penulisan komentar berkualitas rendah ini."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/avoid-redundancy.md
msgid ""
"This kind of lint should only be enabled if the people maintaining a project"
" can afford to keep up with its demands, and usually only for library-style "
"crates rather than application code."
msgstr ""
"Lint semacam ini sebaiknya hanya diaktifkan jika orang yang memelihara "
"proyek mampu memenuhi tuntutannya, dan biasanya hanya untuk crate bergaya "
"library, bukan kode aplikasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid "Names and Signatures are not full documentation"
msgstr "Nama dan Signature Bukan Dokumentasi Lengkap"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"// bad\n"
"/// Returns a future that resolves when operation completes.  \n"
msgstr ""
"// bad\n"
"/// Returns a future that resolves when operation completes.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"// good\n"
"/// Sends local edits to the server, overwriting concurrent edits  \n"
"/// if any happened.  \n"
msgstr ""
"// good\n"
"/// Sends local edits to the server, overwriting concurrent edits  \n"
"/// if any happened.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"// bad\n"
"/// Returns an error if sending the email fails.  \n"
msgstr ""
"// bad\n"
"/// Returns an error if sending the email fails.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"// good\n"
"/// Queues the email for background delivery and returns immediately.  \n"
"///\n"
"/// Returns an error immediately if the email is malformed.  \n"
msgstr ""
"// good\n"
"/// Queues the email for background delivery and returns immediately.  \n"
"///\n"
"/// Returns an error immediately if the email is malformed.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: API designers can over-commit to the idea that a function name "
"and signature is enough documentation."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Perancang API dapat terlalu percaya pada gagasan bahwa nama fungsi"
" dan signature sudah cukup sebagai dokumentasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"Again, names and types are _part_ of the documentation. They are not always "
"the full story!"
msgstr ""
"Sekali lagi, nama dan tipe adalah _bagian_ dari dokumentasi. Keduanya tidak "
"selalu menjadi cerita lengkap!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"Consider the behavior of functions that are not covered by the name, "
"parameter names, or signature of that function."
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan perilaku fungsi yang tidak tercakup oleh nama, nama parameter,"
" atau signature fungsi tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"It is not obvious that `sync_to_server()` could overwrite something (leading"
" to a data loss), so document that."
msgstr ""
"Tidak jelas bahwa `sync_to_server()` dapat menimpa sesuatu (menyebabkan "
"kehilangan data), jadi dokumentasikan hal itu."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"In the email example, it is not obvious that the function can return success"
" and still fail to deliver the email."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh email, tidak jelas bahwa fungsi dapat mengembalikan keberhasilan"
" namun tetap gagal mengirim email."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-isnt-docs.md
msgid ""
"Use comments to disambiguate. Nuanced behaviors, behaviors that users of an "
"API could trip up on, should be documented."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan komentar untuk memperjelas. Perilaku bernuansa, perilaku yang dapat "
"membuat pengguna API tersandung, sebaiknya didokumentasikan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid "Why and What, not How and Where"
msgstr "Mengapa dan Apa, bukan Bagaimana dan Di Mana"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid "Avoid documenting irrelevant details that may frequently change."
msgstr ""
"Hindari mendokumentasikan detail tidak relevan yang mungkin sering berubah."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"// bad\n"
"/// Saves a `User` record to the Postgres database.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// This function opens a new connection and begins a transaction. It checks  \n"
"/// if a user with the given ID exists with a `SELECT` query. If a user is  \n"
"/// not found, performs an `INSERT`.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// # Errors  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// Returns an error if any database operation fails.  \n"
msgstr ""
"// bad\n"
"/// Saves a `User` record to the Postgres database.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// This function opens a new connection and begins a transaction. It checks  \n"
"/// if a user with the given ID exists with a `SELECT` query. If a user is  \n"
"/// not found, performs an `INSERT`.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// # Errors  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// Returns an error if any database operation fails.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"// good\n"
"/// Atomically saves a user record.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// # Errors  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// Returns a `db::Error::DuplicateUsername` error if the user (keyed by  \n"
"/// `user.username` field) already exists.  \n"
msgstr ""
"// good\n"
"/// Atomically saves a user record.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// # Errors  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// Returns a `db::Error::DuplicateUsername` error if the user (keyed by  \n"
"/// `user.username` field) already exists.  \n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: Users want to know the contract of the API (what is guaranteed "
"about this function), rather than implementation details."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Pengguna ingin mengetahui kontrak API (apa yang dijamin tentang "
"fungsi ini), bukan detail implementasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: Doc comments that explain implementation details become outdated"
" faster than comments that explain the contract."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Doc comment yang menjelaskan detail implementasi menjadi "
"kedaluwarsa lebih cepat daripada komentar yang menjelaskan kontrak."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"Internal information is likely irrelevant to a user. Imagine explaining in a"
" doc comment for a function that you're using `for` loops to solve a "
"problem, what is the point of this information?"
msgstr ""
"Informasi internal kemungkinan tidak relevan bagi pengguna. Bayangkan "
"menjelaskan dalam doc comment suatu fungsi bahwa Anda menggunakan loop `for`"
" untuk menyelesaikan masalah; apa gunanya informasi itu?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"It could be that the implementation is necessary to explain, but this is "
"likely due to whatever effects or invariants the user of that API needs to "
"be aware of instead."
msgstr ""
"Bisa jadi implementasi memang perlu dijelaskan, tetapi kemungkinan hal itu "
"disebabkan oleh efek atau invariant yang perlu disadari pengguna API "
"tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"Focus on those effects and invariants instead of the implementation details "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
"Fokus pada efek dan invariant tersebut alih-alih detail implementasinya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"Reiterate: Implementation details can and will change, so do not explain "
"these details."
msgstr ""
"Tegaskan kembali: Detail implementasi dapat dan akan berubah, jadi jangan "
"menjelaskan detail tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md
msgid ""
"Don't talk about where something is used, this is another instance where "
"this information can become stale quickly."
msgstr ""
"Jangan membahas di mana sesuatu digunakan; ini contoh lain ketika informasi "
"tersebut cepat menjadi usang."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid "Exercise: Dialog on Details"
msgstr "Latihan: Dialog tentang Detail"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Unnecessary details can sometimes be indicative of something that does need "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Detail yang tidak perlu terkadang dapat menunjukkan sesuatu yang memang "
"perlu didokumentasikan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid "/// Sorts a slice. Implemented using recursive quicksort.\n"
msgstr "/// Sorts a slice. Implemented using recursive quicksort.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid "Ask the class: Is this comment necessary for this function?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada kelas: Apakah komentar ini diperlukan untuk fungsi ini?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Narrative: Playing the part of an intermediary between the class and the "
"author, such as a PM, manager, etc. tell the class that the author of this "
"function is pushing back."
msgstr ""
"Narasi: Berperan sebagai perantara antara kelas dan penulis, seperti PM, "
"manager, dan sebagainya, beri tahu kelas bahwa penulis fungsi ini menolak."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid "Ask the class: Why would an author of this kind of comment push back?"
msgstr "Tanyakan kepada kelas: Mengapa penulis komentar semacam ini menolak?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"If the class asks why the author is pushing back, do not give details yet."
msgstr "Jika kelas bertanya mengapa penulis menolak, jangan beri detail dulu."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Ask the class: Why would the caller need to know the sorting algorithm in "
"use?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada kelas: Mengapa pemanggil perlu mengetahui algoritma "
"pengurutan yang digunakan?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Narrative: \"Come back\" from a meeting with the original author, explain to"
" the class that this function is application code that is called on "
"untrusted data that [could be crafted maliciously to cause quadratic "
"behavior during sorting](https://www.cs.dartmouth.edu/~doug/mdmspe.pdf)."
msgstr ""
"Narasi: \"Kembali\" dari pertemuan dengan penulis asli, jelaskan kepada "
"kelas bahwa fungsi ini adalah kode aplikasi yang dipanggil pada data tidak "
"tepercaya yang [dapat direkayasa secara jahat untuk menyebabkan perilaku "
"kuadratik selama pengurutan](https://www.cs.dartmouth.edu/~doug/mdmspe.pdf)."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Ask the class: Now we have more detail, how should we comment this function?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada kelas: Sekarang kita punya lebih banyak detail, bagaimana "
"sebaiknya kita mengomentari fungsi ini?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The point being implementation detail vs not depends a lot on what the "
"public contract is (e.g., can you supply untrusted data or not), and this "
"requires careful judgement."
msgstr ""
"Apakah sesuatu itu detail implementasi atau bukan sangat bergantung pada apa"
" kontrak publiknya (misalnya, apakah Anda dapat memasok data tidak tepercaya"
" atau tidak), dan ini memerlukan pertimbangan yang cermat."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Consider if a comment is explaining that a for-loop is used (unnecessary "
"detail) or if it is explaining that the algorithms used internally have "
"known exploits (documentation draws attention to the wrong thing)."
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan apakah komentar menjelaskan bahwa loop for digunakan (detail "
"tidak perlu) atau apakah menjelaskan bahwa algoritma yang digunakan secara "
"internal memiliki eksploit yang diketahui (dokumentasi menarik perhatian ke "
"hal yang salah)."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api.md
msgid ""
"Keep your APIs predictable through naming conventions and implementing "
"common traits."
msgstr ""
"Jaga API Anda tetap dapat diprediksi melalui konvensi penamaan dan "
"pengimplementasian trait umum."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api.md
msgid "/* What traits should this implement? */"
msgstr "/* What traits should this implement? */"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api.md
msgid "// What should this method be called?\n"
msgstr "// What should this method be called?\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api.md
msgid ""
"A predictable API is one where a user's can make assumptions about a part of"
" the API based on surface-level details like names, types, and signatures."
msgstr ""
"API yang dapat diprediksi adalah API ketika pengguna dapat membuat asumsi "
"tentang bagian API berdasarkan detail permukaan seperti nama, tipe, dan "
"signature."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api.md
msgid ""
"We'll be looking at common naming conventions in Rust, which allow users to "
"search for methods that fit their needs quickly and be able to understand "
"existing code quickly."
msgstr ""
"Kami akan melihat konvensi penamaan umum di Rust, yang memungkinkan pengguna"
" mencari method yang sesuai kebutuhan dengan cepat dan memahami kode yang "
"sudah ada dengan cepat."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api.md
msgid ""
"We will also be looking at common traits that types implement, and when to "
"implement them for types you define."
msgstr ""
"Kami juga akan melihat trait umum yang diimplementasikan tipe, dan kapan "
"mengimplementasikannya untuk tipe yang Anda definisikan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions.md
msgid "Naming Conventions"
msgstr "Konvensi Penamaan"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions.md
msgid ""
"A formal and consistently-applied naming convention lets developers treat "
"names like a domain-specific language and quickly understand the "
"functionality and use cases of a method."
msgstr ""
"Konvensi penamaan yang formal dan diterapkan secara konsisten memungkinkan "
"developer memperlakukan nama seperti domain-specific language dan dengan "
"cepat memahami fungsionalitas serta kasus penggunaan suatu method."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions.md
msgid ""
"Rust's community developed naming conventions early, making them mostly "
"consistent in places like the standard library."
msgstr ""
"Komunitas Rust mengembangkan konvensi penamaan sejak awal, membuatnya "
"sebagian besar konsisten di tempat seperti standard library."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions.md
msgid ""
"Here we'll learn common components of Rust method names, giving examples "
"from the standard library and some context to go with them."
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita akan mempelajari komponen umum nama method Rust, dengan contoh "
"dari standard library dan sedikit konteks pendukungnya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/new.md
msgid "`new`: Constructor functions"
msgstr "`new`: Fungsi Constructor"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/new.md
msgid ""
"Rust does not have a `new` keyword, instead `new` is a common prefix or "
"whole method name."
msgstr ""
"Rust tidak memiliki keyword `new`; sebaliknya `new` adalah prefiks umum atau"
" nama method utuh."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/new.md
msgid ""
"There's no `new` keyword for Rust to initialize a new value, only functions "
"you call or values you directly populate."
msgstr ""
"Tidak ada keyword `new` bagi Rust untuk menginisialisasi nilai baru, hanya "
"fungsi yang Anda panggil atau nilai yang Anda isi langsung."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/new.md
msgid ""
"`new` is conventional for the \"default\" constructor function for a type. "
"It holds no special syntactic meaning."
msgstr ""
"`new` adalah konvensi untuk fungsi constructor \"default\" bagi suatu tipe. "
"Kata ini tidak memiliki makna sintaksis khusus."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/new.md
msgid "This is sometimes a prefix, it sometimes takes arguments."
msgstr "Kadang ini berupa prefiks, kadang menerima argumen."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/is.md
msgid "`is_[condition]`: Boolean Check"
msgstr "`is_[condition]`: Pemeriksaan Boolean"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/is.md
msgid "Check a condition about a datatype."
msgstr "Memeriksa kondisi tentang suatu tipe data."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/is.md
msgid "A boolean condition on a value."
msgstr "Kondisi boolean pada suatu nilai."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/is.md
msgid ""
"`is` prefix is preferred over methods with `not` in the name. There are no "
"instances of `is_not_` in standard library methods, just use "
"`!value.is_[condition]`."
msgstr ""
"Prefiks `is` lebih disukai daripada method dengan `not` pada namanya. Tidak "
"ada instance `is_not_` pada method standard library, cukup gunakan "
"`!value.is_[condition]`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/mut.md
msgid "`[method]_mut`: Mutable reference access"
msgstr "`[method]_mut`: Akses Reference Mutable"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/mut.md
msgid "Suffix for access-style methods."
msgstr "Sufiks untuk method bergaya akses."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/mut.md
msgid "Suffix that signifies the method gives access to a mutable reference."
msgstr "Sufiks yang menandakan method memberikan akses ke reference mutable."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/mut.md
msgid "Requires mutable access to the value you're calling this method on."
msgstr ""
"Memerlukan akses mutable ke nilai yang menjadi sasaran pemanggilan method "
"ini."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/mut.md
msgid ""
"Rust can't abstract over mutability, so there's no way to write a method "
"that can be used both mutably and immutably. Instead, we write pairs of "
"functions, where the immutable version gets the shorter name and the mutable"
" version gets the `_mut` suffix."
msgstr ""
"Rust tidak dapat mengabstraksi mutability, sehingga tidak ada cara menulis "
"satu method yang dapat digunakan secara mutable maupun immutable. Sebagai "
"gantinya, kita menulis pasangan fungsi, dengan versi immutable mendapat nama"
" lebih pendek dan versi mutable mendapat sufiks `_mut`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid "`with` as constructor"
msgstr "`with` sebagai Constructor"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid ""
"`with` as a constructor sets one value among a type while using default "
"values for the rest."
msgstr ""
"`with` sebagai constructor menetapkan satu nilai pada suatu tipe sambil "
"menggunakan nilai default untuk sisanya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid "`with` as in \"`<Type>` with specific setting.\""
msgstr "`with` seperti dalam \"`<Type>` dengan pengaturan tertentu.\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid "// Initializes memory for at least N elements, len is still 0.\n"
msgstr "// Initializes memory for at least N elements, len is still 0.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid ""
"`with` can appear as a constructor prefix, most commonly when initializing "
"heap memory for container types."
msgstr ""
"`with` dapat muncul sebagai prefiks constructor, paling umum saat "
"menginisialisasi memori heap untuk tipe container."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid ""
"In this case, it's distinct from `new` constructors because it specifies the"
" value for something that is not usually cared about by API users."
msgstr ""
"Dalam kasus ini, with berbeda dari constructor `new` karena menentukan nilai"
" untuk sesuatu yang biasanya tidak diperhatikan pengguna API."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid "Ask the class: Why not `from_capacity`?"
msgstr "Tanyakan kepada kelas: Mengapa bukan `from_capacity`?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-constructor.md
msgid ""
"Answer: `Vec::with_capacity` as a method call scans well as creating a \"Vec"
" with capacity\". Consider how `Vec::new_capacity` or `Vec::from_capacity` "
"scan when written down, they do not communicate what's going on well."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban: `Vec::with_capacity` sebagai pemanggilan method mudah dibaca "
"sebagai membuat \"Vec dengan capacity\". Pertimbangkan bagaimana "
"`Vec::new_capacity` atau `Vec::from_capacity` terbaca saat dituliskan; "
"keduanya tidak mengomunikasikan maksudnya dengan baik."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md
msgid "`with` as copy-and-set"
msgstr "`with` sebagai Copy-dan-Set"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md
msgid ""
"`with` appears when a value is being copied, but also changed in a specific "
"way."
msgstr ""
"`with` muncul ketika suatu nilai disalin, tetapi juga diubah dengan cara "
"tertentu."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md
msgid "`with` as in \"like `<value>`, but with something different.\""
msgstr ""
"`with` seperti dalam \"seperti `<value>`, tetapi dengan sesuatu yang "
"berbeda.\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md
msgid ""
"// Simplified. \"/home/me/mortgage.pdf\".with_extension(\"mov\") =>\n"
"    // \"/home/me/mortgage.mov\"\n"
msgstr ""
"// Simplified. \"/home/me/mortgage.pdf\".with_extension(\"mov\") =>\n"
"    // \"/home/me/mortgage.mov\"\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md
msgid ""
"`with` can be used for methods that copy a value, but then change a specific"
" part of that value."
msgstr ""
"`with` dapat digunakan untuk method yang menyalin suatu nilai, lalu mengubah"
" bagian tertentu dari nilai tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md
msgid ""
"In the example here, `with_extension` copies the data of a `&Path` into a "
"new `PathBuf`, but changes the extension to something else."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh ini, `with_extension` menyalin data `&Path` ke `PathBuf` baru, "
"tetapi mengubah ekstensinya menjadi sesuatu yang lain."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md
msgid "The original `Path` is unchanged."
msgstr "`Path` asli tidak berubah."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-closure.md
msgid "`with`: Working with Closures"
msgstr "`with`: Bekerja dengan Closure"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-closure.md
msgid "`with` as in \"do X, but with this specific way of computing things.\""
msgstr ""
"`with` seperti dalam \"lakukan X, tetapi dengan cara menghitung yang "
"spesifik ini.\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-closure.md
msgid ""
"// Simplified. If the resize is larger than the current vec size, use the\n"
"    // closure to populate elements.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Simplified. If the resize is larger than the current vec size, use the\n"
"    // closure to populate elements.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-closure.md
msgid "// Create an infinite, lazy iterator using a closure.\n"
msgstr "// Create an infinite, lazy iterator using a closure.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-closure.md
msgid ""
"`with` can appear as a suffix to communicate there is a specific function or"
" closure that can be used instead of a \"sensible default\" for a "
"computation."
msgstr ""
"`with` dapat muncul sebagai sufiks untuk mengomunikasikan bahwa ada fungsi "
"atau closure tertentu yang dapat digunakan alih-alih \"default yang wajar\" "
"untuk suatu komputasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-closure.md
msgid "Similar to [`by`](./by.md)."
msgstr "Serupa dengan [`by`](./by.md)."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/try.md
msgid "`try_[method]`: Fallible methods with Specific Errors"
msgstr "`try_[method]`: Method Fallible dengan Error Spesifik"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/try.md
msgid "Prefix for fallible methods that return a `Result`."
msgstr "Prefiks untuk method fallible yang mengembalikan `Result`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/try.md
msgid "Prefix for methods that can fail, returning a `Result`."
msgstr "Prefiks untuk method yang dapat gagal, mengembalikan `Result`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/try.md
msgid ""
"`TryFrom` is a `From`\\-like trait for types whose single-value constructors"
" might fail in some way."
msgstr ""
"`TryFrom` adalah trait mirip `From` untuk tipe yang constructor nilai "
"tunggalnya mungkin gagal dengan cara tertentu."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/try.md
msgid "Ask: Why aren't `Vec::get` and other similar methods called `try_get`?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Mengapa `Vec::get` dan method serupa lainnya tidak dinamai "
"`try_get`?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/try.md
msgid ""
"Methods are named `get` if they return a reference to an existing value and "
"return an `Option` instead of `Result` because there is only one failure "
"mode. For example, only \"index out of bounds\" for `Vec::get`, and \"key "
"does not exist\" for `HashMap::get`."
msgstr ""
"Method dinamai `get` jika mengembalikan reference ke nilai yang ada dan "
"mengembalikan `Option` alih-alih `Result` karena hanya ada satu mode "
"kegagalan. Misalnya, hanya \"index out of bounds\" untuk `Vec::get`, dan "
"\"key does not exist\" untuk `HashMap::get`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/from.md
msgid "`from`"
msgstr "`from`"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/from.md
msgid "A constructor function, strongly implying \"type conversion\"."
msgstr "Fungsi constructor, sangat menyiratkan \"konversi tipe\"."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/from.md
msgid "Prefix for constructor-style, `From`\\-trait-style functions."
msgstr "Prefiks untuk fungsi bergaya constructor dan bergaya trait `From`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/from.md
msgid ""
"These functions can take multiple arguments, but usually imply the user is "
"doing more of the work than a usual constructor would."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi ini dapat menerima beberapa argumen, tetapi biasanya menyiratkan "
"pengguna melakukan lebih banyak pekerjaan daripada constructor biasa."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/from.md
msgid ""
"`new` is still preferred for most constructor-style functions, the "
"implication for `from` is transformation of one data type to another."
msgstr ""
"`new` tetap lebih disukai untuk sebagian besar fungsi bergaya constructor; "
"implikasi `from` adalah transformasi satu tipe data ke tipe lain."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/into.md
msgid "`into`"
msgstr "`into`"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/into.md
msgid ""
"Prefix for methods that convert `self` into another type. Consumes `self`, "
"returns an owned value."
msgstr ""
"Prefiks untuk method yang mengonversi `self` menjadi tipe lain. Mengonsumsi "
"`self`, mengembalikan nilai owned."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/into.md
msgid ""
"Prefix for a function that consumes an owned value and transforms it into a "
"value of another type."
msgstr ""
"Prefiks untuk fungsi yang mengonsumsi nilai owned dan mentransformasinya "
"menjadi nilai bertipe lain."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/into.md
msgid ""
"Not reinterpret cast! The data can be rearranged, reallocated, changed in "
"any way, including losing information."
msgstr ""
"Bukan reinterpret cast! Data dapat ditata ulang, dialokasikan ulang, diubah "
"dengan cara apa pun, termasuk kehilangan informasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/into.md
msgid ""
"`into_iter` consumes a collection (like a vec, or a btreeset, or a hashmap) "
"and produces an iterator over owned values, unlike `iter` and `iter_mut` "
"which produce iterators over reference values."
msgstr ""
"`into_iter` mengonsumsi koleksi (seperti vec, btreeset, atau hashmap) dan "
"menghasilkan iterator atas nilai owned, berbeda dari `iter` dan `iter_mut` "
"yang menghasilkan iterator atas nilai reference."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid "`to`: Non-consuming Conversion"
msgstr "`to`: Konversi Non-consuming"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"Prefix to a function that takes a borrowed value and creates an owned value"
msgstr ""
"Prefiks untuk fungsi yang menerima nilai yang dipinjam dan membuat nilai "
"owned"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid "// Take an owned self because `u32` implements `Copy`\n"
msgstr "// Take an owned self because `u32` implements `Copy`\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"Methods that create a new owned value without consuming `self`, and imply a "
"type conversion, are named starting with `to`."
msgstr ""
"Method yang membuat nilai owned baru tanpa mengonsumsi `self`, dan "
"menyiratkan konversi tipe, dinamai dengan awalan `to`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"Methods that start with \"to\" return a different type, and strongly imply a"
" non-trivial type conversion, or even a data transformation. For example, "
"`str::to_uppercase`."
msgstr ""
"Method yang diawali \"to\" mengembalikan tipe berbeda, dan sangat "
"menyiratkan konversi tipe yang tidak sepele, atau bahkan transformasi data. "
"Misalnya, `str::to_uppercase`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"\"to\" methods most commonly take `&self`. However they can take `self` by "
"value if the type implements `Copy`: this also ensures that the conversion "
"method call does not consume `self`."
msgstr ""
"Method \"to\" paling umum menerima `&self`. Namun method tersebut dapat "
"menerima `self` by value jika tipe mengimplementasikan `Copy`: ini juga "
"memastikan pemanggilan method konversi tidak mengonsumsi `self`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"If you simply want to define a method that takes `&self` and returns an "
"owned value of the same type, implement [`Clone`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/clone/trait.Clone.html) or [`ToOwned`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/borrow/trait.ToOwned.html)."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda hanya ingin mendefinisikan method yang menerima `&self` dan "
"mengembalikan nilai owned bertipe sama, implementasikan "
"[`Clone`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/clone/trait.Clone.html) atau "
"[`ToOwned`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/borrow/trait.ToOwned.html)."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"If you want to define a method that consumes the source value, use the "
"\"into\" naming pattern."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda ingin mendefinisikan method yang mengonsumsi nilai sumber, gunakan"
" pola penamaan \"into\"."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"Also seen in functions that convert the endianness of primitives, or copy "
"and expose the value of a newtype."
msgstr ""
"Juga terlihat pada fungsi yang mengonversi endianness primitif, atau "
"menyalin dan mengekspos nilai newtype."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"Ask the class: What's the difference between `to_owned` and `into_owned`?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada kelas: Apa perbedaan antara `to_owned` dan `into_owned`?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"Answer: `to_owned` appears on reference values like `&str`, whereas "
"`into_owned` appears on owned values that hold reference types, like `Cow` "
"(copy-on-write)."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban: `to_owned` muncul pada nilai reference seperti `&str`, sedangkan "
"`into_owned` muncul pada nilai owned yang menyimpan tipe reference, seperti "
"`Cow` (copy-on-write)."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md
msgid ""
"Types like `Cow` can be owned while containing references that are borrowed,"
" so the owned value of `Cow` is consumed to create an owned value of the "
"reference type it was holding onto."
msgstr ""
"Tipe seperti `Cow` dapat berupa owned sekaligus berisi reference yang "
"dipinjam, sehingga nilai owned `Cow` dikonsumsi untuk membuat nilai owned "
"dari tipe reference yang dipegangnya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid "`as_` and `_ref`: reference conversions"
msgstr "`as_` dan `_ref`: Konversi Reference"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid "// Very common on container types, see how it's also on Option.\n"
msgstr "// Very common on container types, see how it's also on Option.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid "Method that returns a borrow of the primary piece of contained data."
msgstr ""
"Method yang mengembalikan pinjaman atas bagian data utama yang terkandung."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid ""
"The borrowing relationship is most often straightforward: the return value "
"is a reference that borrows `self`."
msgstr ""
"Hubungan borrowing-nya paling sering lugas: nilai kembalian adalah reference"
" yang meminjam `self`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid ""
"The returned value could borrow `self` only logically, for example, "
"`as_ptr()` methods return an unsafe pointer. The borrow checker does not "
"track borrowing for pointers."
msgstr ""
"Nilai yang dikembalikan dapat meminjam `self` hanya secara logis; misalnya, "
"method `as_ptr()` mengembalikan pointer unsafe. Borrow checker tidak melacak"
" borrowing untuk pointer."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid ""
"The type implementing an \"as\" method should contain one primary piece of "
"data that is being borrowed out."
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang mengimplementasikan method \"as\" sebaiknya berisi satu bagian "
"data utama yang dipinjamkan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid ""
"The \"as\" naming convention does not work if the data type is an aggregate "
"of many fields without an obvious primary one."
msgstr ""
"Konvensi penamaan \"as\" tidak berlaku jika tipe data merupakan agregat "
"banyak field tanpa satu field utama yang jelas."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md
msgid ""
"If you have two reference getters that you need to distinguish, use the "
"`_ref` suffix."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda memiliki dua getter reference yang perlu dibedakan, gunakan sufiks"
" `_ref`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/by.md
msgid "`by`: custom comparator or projection"
msgstr "`by`: Komparator atau Proyeksi Khusus"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/by.md
msgid ""
"Component for methods that take a custom projection or comparison function."
msgstr ""
"Komponen untuk method yang menerima fungsi proyeksi atau perbandingan "
"khusus."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/by.md
msgid ""
"`sort_by` takes a custom comparator function that replaces the normal `Ord` "
"comparison logic."
msgstr ""
"`sort_by` menerima fungsi komparator khusus yang menggantikan logika "
"perbandingan `Ord` biasa."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/by.md
msgid ""
"`sort_by_key` takes a projection function that takes the original element "
"and returns an alternate value to use for sorting. This allow us to do "
"things like sort by a particular field of a struct."
msgstr ""
"`sort_by_key` menerima fungsi proyeksi yang mengambil elemen asli dan "
"mengembalikan nilai alternatif untuk pengurutan. Ini memungkinkan kita "
"melakukan hal seperti mengurutkan berdasarkan field tertentu dari struct."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/by.md
msgid "Sometimes the \"by\" preposition is simply a preposition:"
msgstr "Kadang preposisi \"by\" hanyalah preposisi:"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/by.md
msgid ""
"[`Read::by_ref()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/io/trait.Read.html#method.by_ref)"
msgstr ""
"[`Read::by_ref()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/io/trait.Read.html#method.by_ref)"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/by.md
msgid ""
"[`Iterator::advance_by()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html#method.advance_by) iterator method "
"(nightly feature)"
msgstr ""
"[`Iterator::advance_by()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html#method.advance_by) method iterator "
"(fitur nightly)"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/exercise.md
msgid "What do these names imply they do?"
msgstr "Apa yang disiratkan nama-nama ini tentang fungsinya?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/exercise.md
msgid "What should we name these signatures?"
msgstr "Bagaimana sebaiknya kita menamai signature ini?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/exercise.md
