"`fn inner(&self) -> Option<&InnerType>` or `as_ref`, depending on context"
msgstr ""
"`fn inner(&self) -> Option<&InnerType>` atau `as_ref`, bergantung konteks"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/exercise.md
msgid "`fn with_string(self, String) -> Self`"
msgstr "`fn with_string(self, String) -> Self`"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/exercise.md
msgid ""
"`fn inner_mut(&mut self) -> Option<&mut InnerType>` or `as_ref_mut`, "
"depending on context"
msgstr ""
"`fn inner_mut(&mut self) -> Option<&mut InnerType>` atau `as_ref_mut`, "
"bergantung konteks"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits.md
msgid "Common Traits to Implement"
msgstr "Trait Umum untuk Diimplementasikan"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits.md
msgid ""
"Traits are one of the most potent tools in the Rust language. The language "
"and ecosystem expects you to use them, and so a big part of _predictability_"
" is what traits are implemented for a type!"
msgstr ""
"Trait adalah salah satu alat paling ampuh dalam bahasa Rust. Bahasa dan "
"ekosistem mengharapkan Anda menggunakannya, sehingga sebagian besar "
"_prediktabilitas_ ditentukan oleh trait apa yang diimplementasikan untuk "
"suatu tipe!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits.md
msgid ""
"Traits should be liberally implemented on types you author, but there are "
"caveats!"
msgstr ""
"Trait sebaiknya diimplementasikan secara liberal pada tipe yang Anda buat, "
"tetapi ada peringatan!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits.md
msgid ""
"Remember, many traits have the ability to be _derived_: to have a compiler "
"plugin (macro) write the implementation for you!"
msgstr ""
"Ingat, banyak trait dapat _di-derive_: meminta plugin compiler (macro) "
"menuliskan implementasinya untuk Anda!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits.md
msgid ""
"Authors of ecosystem traits (like De/Serialize) have made derive "
"implementations for traits available to users, leading to very little "
"commitment needed on the developer side for implementing these kinds of "
"traits!"
msgstr ""
"Penulis trait ekosistem (seperti De/Serialize) telah menyediakan "
"implementasi derive bagi pengguna, sehingga developer hanya perlu komitmen "
"sangat sedikit untuk mengimplementasikan trait semacam ini!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid "\"Write to string\" trait, for debug purposes."
msgstr "Trait \"write to string\", untuk tujuan debug."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/hash.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/serde.md
msgid "Derivable: ✅"
msgstr "Dapat di-derive: ✅"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid "\"PlainTextPassword\""
msgstr "\"PlainTextPassword\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid "\"hint\""
msgstr "\"hint\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid "\"password\""
msgstr "\"password\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid "\"[omitted]\""
msgstr "\"[omitted]\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid "\"{user:?}\""
msgstr "\"{user:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid "\"Password123\""
msgstr "\"Password123\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid "\"Used it for years\""
msgstr "\"Used it for years\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid "Provides trivial \"write to string\" functionality."
msgstr "Menyediakan fungsionalitas \"write to string\" yang sederhana."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid ""
"Formatting for _debug information_ for programmers during development, not "
"appearance or serialization."
msgstr ""
"Pemformatan untuk _informasi debug_ bagi programmer selama pengembangan, "
"bukan untuk tampilan atau serialisasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid ""
"Allows for use of `{:?}` and `{#?}` interpolation in string formatting "
"macros."
msgstr ""
"Memungkinkan penggunaan interpolasi `{:?}` dan `{#?}` dalam macro "
"pemformatan string."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid ""
"When to not derive/implement: If a struct holds sensitive data, investigate "
"if you should implement `Debug` for it."
msgstr ""
"Kapan tidak melakukan derive/implementasi: Jika struct menyimpan data "
"sensitif, selidiki apakah Anda sebaiknya mengimplementasikan `Debug` "
"untuknya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/debug.md
msgid ""
"If `Debug` is needed, consider manually implementing `Debug` rather than "
"deriving it. Omit the sensitive data from the implementation."
msgstr ""
"Jika `Debug` diperlukan, pertimbangkan mengimplementasikan `Debug` secara "
"manual alih-alih melakukan derive. Hilangkan data sensitif dari "
"implementasinya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "\"Write to string\" trait, prioritizing readability for an end user."
msgstr "Trait \"write to string\", mengutamakan keterbacaan bagi pengguna akhir."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "Derivable: ❌, without crates like `derive_more`."
msgstr "Dapat di-derive: ❌, tanpa crate seperti `derive_more`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "\"HTTP Error code {code}\""
msgstr "\"HTTP Error code {code}\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "\"Whale attack detected – call Ishmael\""
msgstr "\"Whale attack detected – call Ishmael\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "\"http debug: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"http debug: {:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "\"http display: {}\""
msgstr "\"http display: {}\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "\"whale debug: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"whale debug: {:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "\"whale display: {}\""
msgstr "\"whale display: {}\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid "A trait similar to `Debug`, but with a focus on end-user readability."
msgstr ""
"Trait serupa `Debug`, tetapi berfokus pada keterbacaan bagi pengguna akhir."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid ""
"Prerequisite for the `Error` trait. If implementing for an error type, focus"
" on providing a descriptive error for users and programmers other than you."
msgstr ""
"Prasyarat bagi trait `Error`. Jika mengimplementasikannya untuk tipe error, "
"fokuslah memberikan error yang deskriptif bagi pengguna dan programmer "
"selain Anda."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid ""
"Same security considerations as Debug, consider the ways that sensitive data"
" could be exposed in UI or logs."
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangan keamanan sama dengan Debug; pertimbangkan cara data sensitif "
"dapat terekspos di UI atau log."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid ""
"Types that implement `Display` automatically have `ToString` implemented for"
" them."
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang mengimplementasikan `Display` secara otomatis mendapatkan "
"implementasi `ToString`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/display.md
msgid ""
"Compare the behavior of `Debug` and `Display` for our example error type. "
"Show that the `Debug` impl more directly represents the data as it appears "
"in code, whereas `Display` provides a more friendly message to non-"
"programmers."
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan perilaku `Debug` dan `Display` untuk tipe error contoh kami. "
"Tunjukkan bahwa implementasi `Debug` lebih langsung merepresentasikan data "
"seperti yang tampak dalam kode, sedangkan `Display` memberikan pesan yang "
"lebih ramah bagi non-programmer."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid "Partial equality & Total equality."
msgstr "Kesetaraan Parsial & Kesetaraan Total."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid "\"alice\""
msgstr "\"alice\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid "\"bob\""
msgstr "\"bob\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid ""
"Equality-related methods. If a type implements `PartialEq` then you can use "
"the `==`/`!=` operator with that type."
msgstr ""
"Method terkait kesetaraan. Jika suatu tipe mengimplementasikan `PartialEq`, "
"Anda dapat menggunakan operator `==`/`!=` dengan tipe tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid "A type can't implement `Eq` without implementing `PartialEq`."
msgstr ""
"Suatu tipe tidak dapat mengimplementasikan `Eq` tanpa mengimplementasikan "
"`PartialEq`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid ""
"Reminder: Partial means \"there are invalid members of this set for this "
"function.\""
msgstr ""
"Pengingat: Partial berarti \"ada anggota himpunan ini yang tidak valid untuk"
" fungsi ini.\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid ""
"This doesn't mean that equality will panic, or that it returns a result, "
"just that there may be values that may not behave as you expect equality to "
"behave."
msgstr ""
"Ini tidak berarti kesetaraan akan panic, atau mengembalikan result, hanya "
"saja mungkin ada nilai yang tidak berperilaku seperti yang Anda harapkan "
"dari kesetaraan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid ""
"For example, with floating point values `NaN` is an outlier: `NaN == NaN` is"
" false, despite bitwise equality."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, pada nilai floating point, `NaN` adalah outlier: `NaN == "
"NaN` bernilai false, meskipun secara bitwise sama."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid ""
"`PartialEq` exists to separate types like `f32`/`f64` from types with Total "
"Equality."
msgstr ""
"`PartialEq` ada untuk memisahkan tipe seperti `f32`/`f64` dari tipe dengan "
"Kesetaraan Total."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialeq-eq.md
msgid ""
"You can implement `PartialEq` between different types, but this is mostly "
"useful for reference/smart pointer types."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mengimplementasikan `PartialEq` antartipe berbeda, tetapi ini "
"terutama berguna untuk tipe reference/smart pointer."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid "Partial ordering & Total ordering."
msgstr "Pengurutan Parsial & Pengurutan Total."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid "\"charlie\""
msgstr "\"charlie\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid ""
"Comparison-related methods. If a type implements `PartialOrd`/`Ord` then you"
" can use comparison operators (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`) with that type."
msgstr ""
"Method terkait perbandingan. Jika suatu tipe mengimplementasikan "
"`PartialOrd`/`Ord`, Anda dapat menggunakan operator perbandingan (`<`, `<=`,"
" `>`, `>=`) dengan tipe tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid "`Ord` gives access to `min`, `max`, and `clamp` methods."
msgstr "`Ord` memberikan akses ke method `min`, `max`, dan `clamp`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid "When derived, compares things in the order they are defined."
msgstr "Saat di-derive, membandingkan hal-hal dalam urutan definisinya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid ""
"For enums this means each variant is considered \"greater than\" the last as"
" they are written."
msgstr ""
"Untuk enum, ini berarti setiap varian dianggap \"lebih besar dari\" varian "
"sebelumnya sesuai urutan penulisannya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid ""
"For structs this means fields are compared as they are written, so `id` "
"fields are compared before `name` fields in `Totally`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk struct, ini berarti field dibandingkan sesuai urutan penulisannya, "
"sehingga field `id` dibandingkan sebelum field `name` pada `Totally`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid "Prerequisites: `PartialEq` for `PartialOrd`, `Eq` for `Ord`."
msgstr "Prasyarat: `PartialEq` untuk `PartialOrd`, `Eq` untuk `Ord`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid ""
"To implement `Ord`, a type must also implement `PartialEq`, `Eq`, and "
"`PartialOrd`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengimplementasikan `Ord`, suatu tipe juga harus mengimplementasikan "
"`PartialEq`, `Eq`, dan `PartialOrd`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid ""
"Like with `PartialEq` and `Eq`, a type cannot implement `Ord` without "
"implementing `PartialOrd`."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada `PartialEq` dan `Eq`, suatu tipe tidak dapat "
"mengimplementasikan `Ord` tanpa mengimplementasikan `PartialOrd`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid ""
"Like those equality traits, `PartialOrd` exists to separate types with non-"
"total ordering (particularly floating-point numbers) from types with total "
"ordering."
msgstr ""
"Seperti trait kesetaraan tersebut, `PartialOrd` ada untuk memisahkan tipe "
"dengan pengurutan nontotal (khususnya bilangan floating-point) dari tipe "
"dengan pengurutan total."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/partialord-ord.md
msgid ""
"Used for sorting/searching algorithms and maintaining the ordering of "
"`BTreeMap`/`BTreeSet` style data types."
msgstr ""
"Digunakan untuk algoritma pengurutan/pencarian dan menjaga urutan tipe data "
"bergaya `BTreeMap`/`BTreeSet`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/hash.md
msgid "Performing a hash on a type."
msgstr "Melakukan hash pada suatu tipe."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/hash.md
msgid "\"value\""
msgstr "\"value\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/hash.md
msgid ""
"Allows a type to be used in hash algorithms, most commonly used with data "
"structures like `HashMap`."
msgstr ""
"Memungkinkan suatu tipe digunakan dalam algoritma hash, paling umum dengan "
"struktur data seperti `HashMap`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/hash.md
msgid ""
"Makes it very easy for us to use custom types as the keys in a `HashMap`!"
msgstr "Memudahkan kita menggunakan tipe khusus sebagai key dalam `HashMap`!"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/hash.md
msgid ""
"`Hash` doesn't define any of the hashing logic itself, instead it just feeds"
" the type's data into a `Hasher`. This allows us to use different hash "
"algorithms without changing a type's `Hash` impl."
msgstr ""
"`Hash` tidak mendefinisikan logika hashing itu sendiri; trait ini hanya "
"memasukkan data tipe ke `Hasher`. Ini memungkinkan kita menggunakan "
"algoritma hash berbeda tanpa mengubah implementasi `Hash` tipe."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md
msgid "Deep-copy a type or duplicate a smart, shareable pointer."
msgstr ""
"Menyalin tipe secara mendalam atau menduplikasi smart pointer yang dapat "
"dibagikan."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md
msgid "// Deep copy of all of the data in `lots_of_data`.\n"
msgstr "// Deep copy of all of the data in `lots_of_data`.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md
msgid "// Copies the reference-counted pointer, not the value.\n"
msgstr "// Copies the reference-counted pointer, not the value.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md
msgid ""
"\"Deep copy\" a value, or in the case of reference counting pointers like "
"`Rc`/`Arc` create a new instance of that pointer."
msgstr ""
"\"Deep copy\" suatu nilai, atau untuk pointer reference counting seperti "
"`Rc`/`Arc`, membuat instance baru dari pointer tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md
msgid ""
"When to not implement/derive: For types that, to maintain an invariant, the "
"value should not be duplicated. We'll touch on this later in Idiomatic Rust."
msgstr ""
"Kapan tidak mengimplementasikan/melakukan derive: Untuk tipe yang, demi "
"menjaga invariant, nilainya tidak boleh diduplikasi. Kami akan membahasnya "
"nanti di Idiomatic Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid "Like `Clone`, but indicates the type is can be bitwise copied."
msgstr ""
"Seperti `Clone`, tetapi menandakan bahwa tipe dapat disalin secara bitwise."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid "// Implicit copy operation\n"
msgstr "// Implicit copy operation\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"`Clone` represents an explicit, user-defined copy operation. `Copy` "
"represents an implicit, bitwise copy."
msgstr ""
"`Clone` merepresentasikan operasi salin eksplisit yang ditentukan pengguna. "
"`Copy` merepresentasikan salinan bitwise implisit."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Should generally only be implemented on \"plain data\" types that should act"
" like primitive values. For example, primitive numeric types for a linear "
"algebra library."
msgstr ""
"Umumnya sebaiknya hanya diimplementasikan pada tipe \"plain data\" yang "
"seharusnya berperilaku seperti nilai primitif. Misalnya, tipe numerik "
"primitif untuk library aljabar linear."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Has the same caveat as `Clone`: If duplicating the values would break an "
"invariant, the type shouldn't implement `Copy`."
msgstr ""
"Memiliki peringatan yang sama dengan `Clone`: Jika menduplikasi nilai akan "
"merusak invariant, tipe tersebut tidak boleh mengimplementasikan `Copy`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Always derive `Clone` and `Copy` together! Do _not_ manually implement "
"`Clone` when implementing `Copy`."
msgstr ""
"Selalu lakukan derive `Clone` dan `Copy` bersama-sama! _Jangan_ "
"mengimplementasikan `Clone` secara manual saat mengimplementasikan `Copy`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Copy operations do not invoke the `clone` method, so a custom `Clone` impl "
"can have different behavior than an implicit copy operation. Deriving both "
"`Clone` and `Copy` together ensures that calling `clone` will give the same "
"result as invoking a copy."
msgstr ""
"Operasi copy tidak memanggil method `clone`, sehingga implementasi `Clone` "
"khusus dapat berperilaku berbeda dari operasi copy implisit. Melakukan "
"derive `Clone` dan `Copy` bersama-sama memastikan pemanggilan `clone` "
"memberikan hasil yang sama dengan melakukan copy."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid "Cannot be implemented on types with `Drop` or non-`Copy` fields."
msgstr ""
"Tidak dapat diimplementasikan pada tipe dengan `Drop` atau field non-`Copy`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Ask the class: Why can't a type with heap data (`Vec`, `BTreeMap`, `Rc`, "
"etc.) be `Copy`?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada kelas: Mengapa tipe dengan data heap (`Vec`, `BTreeMap`, "
"`Rc`, dan sebagainya) tidak dapat bersifat `Copy`?"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Bitwise copying on these types would mean types with heap data would no "
"longer have exclusive ownership of a pointer, breaking the invariants "
"usually upheld by Rust and its ecosystem."
msgstr ""
"Copy bitwise pada tipe ini berarti tipe dengan data heap tidak lagi memiliki"
" ownership eksklusif atas pointer, merusak invariant yang biasanya dijaga "
"Rust dan ekosistemnya."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Multiple `Vec`s would point to the same data in memory. Adding and removing "
"data would only update individual `Vec`s length and capacity values. The "
"same for `BTreeMap`."
msgstr ""
"Beberapa `Vec` akan menunjuk data yang sama di memori. Menambah dan "
"menghapus data hanya akan memperbarui nilai length dan capacity masing-"
"masing `Vec`. Hal yang sama berlaku untuk `BTreeMap`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/copy.md
msgid ""
"Bitwise copying of `Rc`s would not update the reference counting value "
"within the pointers, meaning there could be two instances of a `Rc` value "
"that believe themselves to be the only `Rc` for that pointer. Once one of "
"them is destroyed, the reference count will become 0 on one of them and the "
"inner value dropped despite there being another `Rc` still alive."
msgstr ""
"Copy bitwise pada `Rc` tidak akan memperbarui nilai reference counting di "
"dalam pointer, sehingga bisa ada dua instance nilai `Rc` yang sama-sama "
"menganggap dirinya satu-satunya `Rc` untuk pointer tersebut. Setelah salah "
"satunya dihancurkan, reference count pada salah satunya akan menjadi 0 dan "
"nilai di dalamnya di-drop meskipun masih ada `Rc` lain yang hidup."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "From & Into"
msgstr "From & Into"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "Conversion from one type to another."
msgstr "Konversi dari satu tipe ke tipe lain."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "// `Into` is more natural to use as a trait bound.\n"
msgstr "// `Into` is more natural to use as a trait bound.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "// `Wrapper` can be construct from `&str` and `i32`.\n"
msgstr "// `Wrapper` can be construct from `&str` and `i32`.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "\"Hello, obvious!\""
msgstr "\"Hello, obvious!\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "// A From implementation implies an Into implementation.\n"
msgstr "// A From implementation implies an Into implementation.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "\"Hello, implementation!\""
msgstr "\"Hello, implementation!\""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid "Provides conversion functionality to types."
msgstr "Menyediakan fungsionalitas konversi bagi tipe."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid ""
"`From` provides a constructor-style function, whereas `Into` provides a "
"method on an existing value."
msgstr ""
"`From` menyediakan fungsi bergaya constructor, sedangkan `Into` menyediakan "
"method pada nilai yang sudah ada."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid ""
"Prefer writing `From<T>` implementations for a type you're authoring instead"
" of `Into<T>`."
msgstr ""
"Utamakan menulis implementasi `From<T>` untuk tipe yang Anda buat alih-alih "
"`Into<T>`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid ""
"The `Into` trait is implemented for any type that implements `From` "
"automatically."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Into` diimplementasikan secara otomatis untuk tipe apa pun yang "
"mengimplementasikan `From`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/from-into.md
msgid ""
"`Into` is preferred as a trait bound for arguments to functions for clarity "
"of intent for what the function can take: `T: Into<String>` has clearer "
"intent than `String: From<T>`."
msgstr ""
"`Into` lebih disukai sebagai trait bound untuk argumen fungsi demi kejelasan"
" maksud tentang apa yang dapat diterima fungsi: `T: Into<String>` memiliki "
"maksud yang lebih jelas daripada `String: From<T>`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/try-from-into.md
msgid "TryFrom/TryInto"
msgstr "TryFrom/TryInto"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/try-from-into.md
msgid "Fallible conversion from one type to another."
msgstr "Konversi fallible dari satu tipe ke tipe lain."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/try-from-into.md
msgid "Derivable: ❌"
msgstr "Dapat di-derive: ❌"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/try-from-into.md
msgid "Provides conversion that can fail, returning a result type."
msgstr "Menyediakan konversi yang dapat gagal, mengembalikan tipe result."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/try-from-into.md
msgid ""
"Like `From`/`Into`, prefer implementing `TryFrom` for types rather than "
"`TryInto`."
msgstr ""
"Seperti `From`/`Into`, utamakan mengimplementasikan `TryFrom` untuk tipe "
"alih-alih `TryInto`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/try-from-into.md
msgid "Implementations can specify what the error type of the `Result`."
msgstr "Implementasi dapat menentukan tipe error dari `Result`."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/serde.md
msgid "Serialize/Deserialize style traits"
msgstr "Trait bergaya Serialize/Deserialize"

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/serde.md
msgid "Crates like `serde` can implement serialization automatically."
msgstr ""
"Crate seperti `serde` dapat mengimplementasikan serialisasi secara otomatis."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/serde.md
msgid ""
"Provides serialization and deserialization functionality for a type, "
"allowing for Rust data types to be converted to/from data formats like JSON."
msgstr ""
"Menyediakan fungsionalitas serialisasi dan deserialisasi untuk suatu tipe, "
"memungkinkan tipe data Rust dikonversi ke/dari format data seperti JSON."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/serde.md
msgid ""
"The standard library doesn't have serialization functionality built-in, but "
"the serde crate is the community standard interface for doing serialization."
msgstr ""
"Standard library tidak memiliki fungsionalitas serialisasi bawaan, tetapi "
"crate serde adalah antarmuka standar komunitas untuk melakukan serialisasi."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/serde.md
msgid ""
"When not to implement: If a type contains sensitive data that should not be "
"erroneously saved to disk or sent over a network, consider not implementing "
"Serialize/Deserialize for that type."
msgstr ""
"Kapan tidak mengimplementasikan: Jika suatu tipe berisi data sensitif yang "
"tidak boleh secara keliru disimpan ke disk atau dikirim melalui jaringan, "
"pertimbangkan untuk tidak mengimplementasikan Serialize/Deserialize untuk "
"tipe tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/serde.md
msgid ""
"Shares security concerns with `Debug`, but given serialization is often used"
" in networking there can be higher stakes."
msgstr ""
"Memiliki kekhawatiran keamanan yang sama dengan `Debug`, tetapi karena "
"serialisasi sering digunakan dalam networking, risikonya bisa lebih tinggi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"Rust's type system is _expressive_: you can use types and traits to build "
"abstractions that make your code harder to misuse."
msgstr ""
"Sistem tipe Rust bersifat _ekspresif_: Anda dapat menggunakan tipe dan trait"
" untuk membangun abstraksi yang membuat kode Anda lebih sulit "
"disalahgunakan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"In some cases, you can go as far as enforcing correctness at _compile-time_,"
" with no runtime overhead."
msgstr ""
"Dalam beberapa kasus, Anda dapat menegakkan kebenaran hingga pada _waktu "
"kompilasi_, tanpa overhead runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"Types and traits can model concepts and constraints from your business "
"domain. With careful design, you can improve the clarity and maintainability"
" of the entire codebase."
msgstr ""
"Tipe dan trait dapat memodelkan konsep dan batasan dari domain bisnis Anda. "
"Dengan desain yang cermat, Anda dapat meningkatkan kejelasan dan kemudahan "
"pemeliharaan seluruh basis kode."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid "Additional items speaker may mention:"
msgstr "Hal tambahan yang mungkin disebutkan pembicara:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"Rust's type system borrows a lot of ideas from functional programming "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Sistem tipe Rust meminjam banyak gagasan dari bahasa pemrograman fungsional."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"For example, Rust's enums are known as \"algebraic data types\" in languages"
" like Haskell and OCaml. You can take inspiration from learning material "
"geared towards functional languages when looking for guidance on how to "
"design with types. [\"Domain Modeling Made "
"Functional\"](https://pragprog.com/titles/swdddf/domain-modeling-made-"
"functional/) is a great resource on the topic, with examples written in F#."
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, enum Rust dikenal sebagai \"algebraic data type\" di bahasa "
"seperti Haskell dan OCaml. Anda dapat mengambil inspirasi dari materi "
"pembelajaran yang ditujukan untuk bahasa fungsional saat mencari panduan "
"tentang cara mendesain dengan tipe. [\"Domain Modeling Made "
"Functional\"](https://pragprog.com/titles/swdddf/domain-modeling-made-"
"functional/) adalah sumber yang bagus tentang topik ini, dengan contoh yang "
"ditulis dalam F#."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"Despite Rust's functional roots, not all functional design patterns can be "
"easily translated to Rust."
msgstr ""
"Meskipun Rust berakar pada gaya fungsional, tidak semua pola desain "
"fungsional dapat dengan mudah diterjemahkan ke Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"For example, you must have a solid grasp on a broad selection of advanced "
"topics to design APIs that leverage higher-order functions and higher-kinded"
" types in Rust."
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, Anda harus memiliki pemahaman yang kokoh tentang berbagai topik "
"lanjutan untuk merancang API yang memanfaatkan higher-order function dan "
"higher-kinded type di Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"Evaluate, on a case-by-case basis, whether a more imperative approach may be"
" easier to implement. Consider using in-place mutation, relying on Rust's "
"borrow-checker and type system to control what can be mutated, and where."
msgstr ""
"Evaluasi, secara kasus per kasus, apakah pendekatan yang lebih imperatif "
"mungkin lebih mudah diimplementasikan. Pertimbangkan penggunaan mutasi in-"
"place, dengan mengandalkan borrow checker dan sistem tipe Rust untuk "
"mengontrol apa yang dapat dimutasi, dan di mana."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"The same caution should be applied to object-oriented design patterns. Rust "
"doesn't support inheritance, and object decomposition should take into "
"account the constraints introduced by the borrow checker."
msgstr ""
"Kehati-hatian yang sama sebaiknya diterapkan pada pola desain berorientasi "
"objek. Rust tidak mendukung inheritance, dan dekomposisi objek sebaiknya "
"mempertimbangkan batasan yang diperkenalkan borrow checker."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid ""
"Mention that type-level programming can be often used to create \"zero-cost "
"abstractions\", although the label can be misleading: the impact on compile "
"times and code complexity may be significant."
msgstr ""
"Sebutkan bahwa pemrograman tingkat tipe sering dapat digunakan untuk membuat"
" \"zero-cost abstraction\", meskipun label tersebut bisa menyesatkan: "
"dampaknya terhadap waktu kompilasi dan kompleksitas kode bisa signifikan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid "This segment should take about 7 hours and 40 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Segmen ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 7 jam 40 menit. Segmen ini "
"berisi:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system.md
msgid "1 hour and 30 minutes"
msgstr "1 jam 30 menit"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid "A _newtype_ is a wrapper around an existing type, often a primitive:"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah _newtype_ adalah wrapper di sekitar tipe yang sudah ada, sering kali "
"primitif:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid "/// A unique user identifier, implemented as a newtype around `u64`.\n"
msgstr "/// A unique user identifier, implemented as a newtype around `u64`.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid ""
"Unlike type aliases, newtypes aren't interchangeable with the wrapped type:"
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dari type alias, newtype tidak dapat dipertukarkan dengan tipe yang "
"dibungkusnya:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid "// 🛠️❌\n"
msgstr "// 🛠️❌\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid ""
"The Rust compiler won't let you use methods or operators defined on the "
"underlying type either:"
msgstr ""
"Compiler Rust juga tidak akan mengizinkan Anda menggunakan method atau "
"operator yang didefinisikan pada tipe dasar."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid ""
"Students should have encountered the newtype pattern in the \"Fundamentals\""
" course, when they learned about [tuple structs](../../user-defined-"
"types/tuple-structs.md)."
msgstr ""
"Siswa seharusnya sudah menemui pola newtype dalam kursus \"Fundamentals\", "
"saat mempelajari [tuple struct](../../user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid "Run the example to show students the error message from the compiler."
msgstr ""
"Jalankan contoh untuk menunjukkan pesan error dari compiler kepada siswa."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid ""
"Modify the example to use a typealias instead of a newtype, such as `type "
"MessageId = u64`. The modified example should compile, thus highlighting the"
" differences between the two approaches."
msgstr ""
"Ubah contoh agar menggunakan typealias alih-alih newtype, seperti `type "
"MessageId = u64`. Contoh yang diubah seharusnya dapat dikompilasi, sehingga "
"menyoroti perbedaan antara kedua pendekatan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md
msgid ""
"Stress that newtypes, out of the box, have no behaviour attached to them. "
"You need to be intentional about which methods and operators you are willing"
" to forward from the underlying type. In our `UserId` example, it is "
"reasonable to allow comparisons between `UserId`s, but it wouldn't make "
"sense to allow arithmetic operations like addition or subtraction."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa newtype, secara bawaan, tidak memiliki perilaku yang melekat."
" Anda perlu sengaja memilih method dan operator mana yang bersedia "
"diteruskan dari tipe dasar. Pada contoh `UserId` kami, wajar mengizinkan "
"perbandingan antar-`UserId`, tetapi tidak masuk akal mengizinkan operasi "
"aritmetika seperti penjumlahan atau pengurangan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid ""
"When a function takes multiple arguments of the same type, call sites are "
"unclear:"
msgstr ""
"Ketika fungsi menerima beberapa argumen bertipe sama, lokasi pemanggilan "
"menjadi tidak jelas:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/root.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/struct.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/property.md
msgid "// [...]\n"
msgstr "// [...]\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid "\"username\""
msgstr "\"username\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid ""
"// In another part of the codebase, we swap arguments by mistake.\n"
"    // Bug (best case), security vulnerability (worst case)\n"
msgstr ""
"// In another part of the codebase, we swap arguments by mistake.\n"
"    // Bug (best case), security vulnerability (worst case)\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid "The newtype pattern can prevent this class of errors at compile time:"
msgstr "Pola newtype dapat mencegah kelas error ini pada waktu kompilasi:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid ""
"Run both examples to show students the successful compilation for the "
"original example, and the compiler error returned by the modified example."
msgstr ""
"Jalankan kedua contoh untuk menunjukkan kompilasi yang berhasil pada contoh "
"asli, dan error compiler yang dihasilkan contoh yang diubah."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid ""
"Stress the _semantic_ angle. The newtype pattern should be leveraged to use "
"distinct types for distinct concepts, thus ruling out this class of errors "
"entirely."
msgstr ""
"Tekankan sudut _semantik_. Pola newtype sebaiknya dimanfaatkan untuk "
"menggunakan tipe berbeda bagi konsep berbeda, sehingga menyingkirkan kelas "
"error ini sepenuhnya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid ""
"Nonetheless, note that there are legitimate scenarios where a function may "
"take multiple arguments of the same type. In those scenarios, if correctness"
" is of paramount importance, consider using a struct with named fields as "
"input:"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun demikian, perhatikan bahwa ada skenario sah ketika fungsi menerima "
"beberapa argumen bertipe sama. Dalam skenario tersebut, jika kebenaran "
"sangat penting, pertimbangkan menggunakan struct dengan field bernama "
"sebagai input:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid ""
"// No need to check the definition of the `login` function to spot the "
"issue.\n"
msgstr ""
"// No need to check the definition of the `login` function to spot the "
"issue.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/semantic-confusion.md
msgid ""
"Users are forced, at the callsite, to assign values to each field, thus "
"increasing the likelihood of spotting bugs."
msgstr ""
"Pengguna dipaksa, di lokasi pemanggilan, untuk menetapkan nilai ke setiap "
"field, sehingga meningkatkan kemungkinan menemukan bug."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/parse-don-t-validate.md
msgid "Enforce Invariants at Construction"
msgstr "Menegakkan Invariant saat Konstruksi"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/parse-don-t-validate.md
msgid "The newtype pattern can be leveraged to enforce _invariants_."
msgstr "Pola newtype dapat dimanfaatkan untuk menegakkan _invariant_."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/parse-don-t-validate.md
msgid ""
"The newtype pattern, combined with Rust's module and visibility system, can "
"be used to _guarantee_ that instances of a given type satisfy a set of "
"invariants."
msgstr ""
"Pola newtype, dikombinasikan dengan sistem modul dan visibilitas Rust, dapat"
" digunakan untuk _menjamin_ bahwa instance tipe tertentu memenuhi "
"serangkaian invariant."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/parse-don-t-validate.md
msgid ""
"In the example above, the raw `String` stored inside the `Username` struct "
"can't be accessed directly from other modules or crates, since it's not "
"marked as `pub` or `pub(in ...)`. Consumers of the `Username` type are "
"forced to use the `new` method to create instances. In turn, `new` performs "
"validation, thus ensuring that all instances of `Username` satisfy those "
"checks."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh di atas, `String` mentah yang disimpan di dalam struct "
"`Username` tidak dapat diakses langsung dari modul atau crate lain, karena "
"tidak ditandai `pub` atau `pub(in ...)`. Konsumen tipe `Username` dipaksa "
"menggunakan method `new` untuk membuat instance. Kemudian, `new` melakukan "
"validasi, sehingga memastikan semua instance `Username` memenuhi pemeriksaan"
" tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/parse-don-t-validate.md
msgid ""
"The `as_str` method allows consumers to access the raw string representation"
" (e.g., to store it in a database). However, consumers can't modify the "
"underlying value since `&str`, the returned type, restricts them to read-"
"only access."
msgstr ""
"Method `as_str` memungkinkan konsumen mengakses representasi string mentah "
"(misalnya, untuk menyimpannya di database). Namun, konsumen tidak dapat "
"mengubah nilai dasarnya karena `&str`, tipe yang dikembalikan, membatasi "
"mereka pada akses read-only."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/parse-don-t-validate.md
msgid "Type-level invariants have second-order benefits."
msgstr "Invariant tingkat tipe memiliki manfaat tingkat kedua."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/parse-don-t-validate.md
msgid ""
"The input is validated once, at the boundary, and the rest of the program "
"can rely on the invariants being upheld. We can avoid redundant validation "
"and \"defensive programming\" checks throughout the program, reducing noise "
"and improving performance."
msgstr ""
"Input divalidasi sekali, di batas, dan bagian program lainnya dapat "
"mengandalkan invariant yang terjaga. Kita dapat menghindari validasi "
"redundan dan pemeriksaan \"defensive programming\" di seluruh program, "
"mengurangi noise dan meningkatkan performa."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid "Is It Truly Encapsulated?"
msgstr "Apakah Benar-Benar Terenkapsulasi?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid ""
"You must evaluate _the entire API surface_ exposed by a newtype to determine"
" if invariants are indeed bullet-proof. It is crucial to consider all "
"possible interactions, including trait implementations, that may allow users"
" to bypass validation checks."
msgstr ""
"Anda harus mengevaluasi _seluruh permukaan API_ yang diekspos newtype untuk "
"menentukan apakah invariant benar-benar kuat. Sangat penting "
"mempertimbangkan semua interaksi yang mungkin, termasuk implementasi trait, "
"yang dapat memungkinkan pengguna melewati pemeriksaan validasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid "// Validation checks...\n"
msgstr "// Validation checks...\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid "// ‼️\n"
msgstr "// ‼️\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid ""
"`DerefMut` allows users to get a mutable reference to the wrapped value."
msgstr ""
"`DerefMut` memungkinkan pengguna mendapatkan reference mutable ke nilai yang"
" dibungkus."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid ""
"The mutable reference can be used to modify the underlying data in ways that"
" may violate the invariants enforced by `Username::new`!"
msgstr ""
"Reference mutable tersebut dapat digunakan untuk mengubah data dasar dengan "
"cara yang mungkin melanggar invariant yang ditegakkan `Username::new`!"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid ""
"When auditing the API surface of a newtype, you can narrow down the review "
"scope to methods and traits that provide mutable access to the underlying "
"data."
msgstr ""
"Saat mengaudit permukaan API newtype, Anda dapat mempersempit cakupan "
"tinjauan ke method dan trait yang memberikan akses mutable ke data dasar."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid "Remind students of privacy boundaries."
msgstr "Ingatkan siswa tentang batas privasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md
msgid ""
"In particular, functions and methods defined in the same module of the "
"newtype can access its underlying data directly. If possible, move the "
"newtype definition to its own separate module to reduce the scope of the "
"audit."
msgstr ""
"Secara khusus, fungsi dan method yang didefinisikan dalam modul yang sama "
"dengan newtype dapat mengakses data dasarnya secara langsung. Jika "
"memungkinkan, pindahkan definisi newtype ke modul terpisah untuk mengurangi "
"cakupan audit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "RAII: `Drop` trait"
msgstr "RAII: Trait `Drop`"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"RAII (**R**esource **A**cquisition **I**s **I**nitialization) ties the "
"lifetime of a resource to the lifetime of a value."
msgstr ""
"RAII (**R**esource **A**cquisition **I**s **I**nitialization) mengikat "
"lifetime suatu resource ke lifetime suatu nilai."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"[Rust uses RAII to manage memory](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-"
"example/scope/raii.html), and the `Drop` trait allows you to extend this to "
"other resources, such as file descriptors or locks."
msgstr ""
"[Rust menggunakan RAII untuk mengelola memori](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/rust-by-example/scope/raii.html), dan trait `Drop` memungkinkan "
"Anda memperluasnya ke resource lain, seperti file descriptor atau lock."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "b\"example\""
msgstr "b\"example\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "\"example.txt\""
msgstr "\"example.txt\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "\"content: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"content: {:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"Easy to miss: `file.close()` is never called. Ask the class if they noticed."
msgstr ""
"Mudah terlewat: `file.close()` tidak pernah dipanggil. Tanyakan kepada kelas"
" apakah mereka menyadarinya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"To release the file descriptor correctly, `file.close()` must be called "
"after the last use — and also in early-return paths in case of errors."
msgstr ""
"Untuk melepaskan file descriptor dengan benar, `file.close()` harus "
"dipanggil setelah penggunaan terakhir — dan juga pada jalur early return "
"jika terjadi error."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"Instead of relying on the user to call `close()`, we can implement the "
"`Drop` trait to release the resource automatically. This ties cleanup to the"
" lifetime of the `File` value."
msgstr ""
"Alih-alih mengandalkan pengguna memanggil `close()`, kita dapat "
"mengimplementasikan trait `Drop` untuk melepaskan resource secara otomatis. "
"Ini mengikat pembersihan ke lifetime nilai `File`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "// libc::close(...);\n"
msgstr "// libc::close(...);\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "\"file descriptor was closed\""
msgstr "\"file descriptor was closed\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"Note that `Drop::drop()` cannot return a `Result`. Any failures must be "
"handled internally or ignored. In the standard library, errors during FD "
"closure inside `Drop` are silently discarded. See the implementation: "
"<https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/os/fd/owned.rs.html#169-196>"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `Drop::drop()` tidak dapat mengembalikan `Result`. "
"Kegagalan apa pun harus ditangani secara internal atau diabaikan. Di "
"standard library, error saat penutupan FD di dalam `Drop` dibuang secara "
"diam-diam. Lihat implementasinya: <https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/src/std/os/fd/owned.rs.html#169-196>"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "When is `Drop::drop` called?"
msgstr "Kapan `Drop::drop` dipanggil?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"Normally, when the `file` variable in `main()` goes out of scope (either on "
"return or due to a panic), `drop()` is called automatically."
msgstr ""
"Biasanya, ketika variabel `file` di `main()` keluar dari scope (baik saat "
"return atau karena panic), `drop()` dipanggil secara otomatis."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"If the file is moved into another function (as is this case with "
"`File::close()`), the value is dropped when that function returns — not in "
"`main`."
msgstr ""
"Jika file dipindahkan ke fungsi lain (seperti pada kasus `File::close()`), "
"nilai di-drop saat fungsi tersebut kembali — bukan di `main`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"In contrast, C++ runs destructors in the original scope even for moved-from "
"values."
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, C++ menjalankan destructor di scope asal bahkan untuk nilai yang"
" telah dipindahkan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"Demo: insert `panic!(\"oops\")` at the start of `read_to_end()` and run it. "
"`drop()` still runs during unwinding."
msgstr ""
"Demo: sisipkan `panic!(\"oops\")` di awal `read_to_end()` dan jalankan. "
"`drop()` tetap berjalan selama unwinding."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid "The `Drop` trait has another important limitation: it is not `async`."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Drop` memiliki keterbatasan penting lainnya: trait ini tidak `async`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"This means you cannot `await` inside a destructor, which is often needed "
"when cleaning up asynchronous resources like sockets, database connections, "
"or tasks that must signal completion to another system."
msgstr ""
"Ini berarti Anda tidak dapat `await` di dalam destructor, yang sering "
"diperlukan saat membersihkan resource asinkron seperti socket, koneksi "
"database, atau task yang harus memberi sinyal penyelesaian ke sistem lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"Learn more: <https://rust-lang.github.io/async-fundamentals-"
"initiative/roadmap/async_drop.html>"
msgstr ""
"Pelajari lebih lanjut: <https://rust-lang.github.io/async-fundamentals-"
"initiative/roadmap/async_drop.html>"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii.md
msgid ""
"There is an experimental `AsyncDrop` trait available on nightly: "
"<https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/future/trait.AsyncDrop.html>"
msgstr ""
"Ada trait `AsyncDrop` eksperimental yang tersedia di nightly: "
"<https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/future/trait.AsyncDrop.html>"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid "Drop can be skipped"
msgstr "Drop Dapat Dilewati"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid "There are cases where destructors will not run."
msgstr "Ada kasus ketika destructor tidak akan berjalan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid "\"OwnedFd::drop() called with raw fd: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"OwnedFd::drop() called with raw fd: {:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid "\"TmpFile::drop() called with owned fd: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"TmpFile::drop() called with owned fd: {:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"// libc::unlink(\"/tmp/file\")\n"
"        // panic!(\"TmpFile::drop() panics\");\n"
msgstr ""
"// libc::unlink(\"/tmp/file\")\n"
"        // panic!(\"TmpFile::drop() panics\");\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid "\"TmpFile::close(): not implemented yet\""
msgstr "\"TmpFile::close(): not implemented yet\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid "// std::mem::forget(file);\n"
msgstr "// std::mem::forget(file);\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid "// file.close();\n"
msgstr "// file.close();\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"Drop is not guaranteed to always run. There is a number of cases when drop "
"is skipped: the program can crash or exit, the value with the drop "
"implementation can be leaked etc."
msgstr ""
"Drop tidak dijamin selalu berjalan. Ada sejumlah kasus ketika drop dilewati:"
" program dapat crash atau exit, nilai dengan implementasi drop dapat di-"
"leak, dan sebagainya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"In the version that calls [`std::process::exit`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/process/fn.exit.html), `TmpFile::drop()` is never run because "
"`exit()` terminates the process immediately without any opportunity for a "
"`drop()` method to be called."
msgstr ""
"Pada versi yang memanggil [`std::process::exit`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/process/fn.exit.html), `TmpFile::drop()` tidak pernah berjalan "
"karena `exit()` menghentikan proses segera tanpa memberi kesempatan method "
"`drop()` dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"You can prevent accidental use of `exit` by denying the "
"[`clippy::exit`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-"
"clippy/stable/index.html#exit) lint."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mencegah penggunaan `exit` yang tidak disengaja dengan men-deny "
"lint [`clippy::exit`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-"
"clippy/stable/index.html#exit)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"If you remove the `std::process::exit(0)` line, each `drop()` method in this"
" simple case will run in turn."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda menghapus baris `std::process::exit(0)`, setiap method `drop()` "
"dalam kasus sederhana ini akan berjalan bergantian."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"Try uncommenting the [`std::mem::forget`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/fn.forget.html) call. What do you think will happen?"
msgstr ""
"Coba buka komentar pemanggilan [`std::mem::forget`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/fn.forget.html). Menurut Anda apa yang akan terjadi?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"`mem::forget()` takes ownership and \"forgets\" about the value `file` "
"without running its **destructor** `Drop::drop()`. The destructor of "
"`owned_fd` is still run."
msgstr ""
"`mem::forget()` mengambil ownership dan \"melupakan\" nilai `file` tanpa "
"menjalankan **destructor** `Drop::drop()`-nya. Destructor `owned_fd` tetap "
"berjalan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"Remove the `mem::forget()` call, then uncomment the `file.close()` call "
"below it. What do you expect now?"
msgstr ""
"Hapus pemanggilan `mem::forget()`, lalu buka komentar pemanggilan "
"`file.close()` di bawahnya. Sekarang apa yang Anda harapkan?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"With the default `panic = \"unwind\"` setting, the stack still unwinds and "
"destructors run, even when the panic starts in `main`."
msgstr ""
"Dengan pengaturan default `panic = \"unwind\"`, stack tetap unwinding dan "
"destructor berjalan, bahkan ketika panic dimulai di `main`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"With [`panic = \"abort\"`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html#panic) no destructors are run."
msgstr ""
"Dengan [`panic = \"abort\"`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html#panic), tidak ada destructor yang "
"dijalankan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"As a last step, uncomment the `panic!` inside `TmpFile::drop()` and run it. "
"Ask the class: which destructors run before the abort?"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai langkah terakhir, buka komentar `panic!` di dalam `TmpFile::drop()` "
"dan jalankan. Tanyakan kepada kelas: destructor mana yang berjalan sebelum "
"abort?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"After a double panic, Rust no longer guarantees that remaining destructors "
"will run:"
msgstr ""
"Setelah double panic, Rust tidak lagi menjamin destructor yang tersisa akan "
"berjalan:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"Some cleanup that was already in progress may still complete (for example, "
"field destructors of the value currently being dropped),"
msgstr ""
"Sebagian pembersihan yang sudah berlangsung mungkin tetap selesai (misalnya,"
" destructor field dari nilai yang sedang di-drop),"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"but anything scheduled later in the unwind path might be skipped entirely."
msgstr ""
"tetapi apa pun yang dijadwalkan kemudian dalam jalur unwind mungkin dilewati"
" sepenuhnya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"This is why we say you cannot rely solely on `drop()` for critical external "
"cleanup, nor assume that a double panic aborts without running any further "
"destructors."
msgstr ""
"Inilah sebabnya kami katakan Anda tidak dapat mengandalkan `drop()` saja "
"untuk pembersihan eksternal yang kritis, juga tidak dapat mengasumsikan "
"double panic akan abort tanpa menjalankan destructor lebih lanjut."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"Some languages forbid or restrict exceptions in destructors. Rust allows "
"panicking in `Drop::drop`, but it is almost never a good idea, since it can "
"disrupt unwinding and lead to unpredictable cleanup. It is best avoided "
"unless there is a very specific need, such as in the case of a **drop "
"bomb**."
msgstr ""
"Beberapa bahasa melarang atau membatasi exception di destructor. Rust "
"mengizinkan panic di `Drop::drop`, tetapi hampir tidak pernah merupakan ide "
"bagus, karena dapat mengganggu unwinding dan menyebabkan pembersihan yang "
"tidak dapat diprediksi. Sebaiknya dihindari kecuali ada kebutuhan yang "
"sangat spesifik, seperti pada kasus **drop bomb**."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"Drop is suitable for cleaning up resources within the scope of a process, "
"but it is not the right tool for providing hard guarantees that something "
"happens outside of the process (e.g., on local disk, or in another service "
"in a distributed system)."
msgstr ""
"Drop cocok untuk membersihkan resource dalam lingkup suatu proses, tetapi "
"bukan alat yang tepat untuk memberikan jaminan keras bahwa sesuatu terjadi "
"di luar proses (misalnya, pada disk lokal, atau di layanan lain dalam sistem"
" terdistribusi)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"For example, deleting a temporary file in `drop()` is fine in a toy example,"
" but in a real program you would still need an external cleanup mechanism "
"such as a temp file reaper."
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, menghapus berkas sementara di `drop()` tidak masalah dalam contoh "
"mainan, tetapi dalam program nyata Anda tetap memerlukan mekanisme "
"pembersihan eksternal seperti temp file reaper."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_skipped.md
msgid ""
"In contrast, we can rely on `drop()` to unlock a mutex, since it is a "
"process-local resource. If `drop()` is skipped and the mutex is left locked,"
" it has no lasting effects outside the process."
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, kita dapat mengandalkan `drop()` untuk membuka lock mutex, "
"karena mutex adalah resource lokal proses. Jika `drop()` dilewati dan mutex "
"tetap terkunci, tidak ada efek yang bertahan di luar proses."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid "Mutex and MutexGuard"
msgstr "Mutex dan MutexGuard"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid ""
"In earlier examples, RAII was used to manage concrete resources like file "
"descriptors. With a `Mutex`, the \"resource\" is mutable access to a value. "
"You access the value by calling `lock`, which then returns a `MutexGuard` "
"which will unlock the `Mutex` automatically when dropped."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh sebelumnya, RAII digunakan untuk mengelola resource konkret "
"seperti file descriptor. Dengan `Mutex`, \"resource\"-nya adalah akses "
"mutable ke suatu nilai. Anda mengakses nilai dengan memanggil `lock`, yang "
"kemudian mengembalikan `MutexGuard` yang akan membuka lock `Mutex` secara "
"otomatis saat di-drop."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid "\"{guard:?}\""
msgstr "\"{guard:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid ""
"A `Mutex` controls exclusive access to a value. Unlike earlier RAII "
"examples, the resource here is logical: temporary exclusive access to the "
"data inside."
msgstr ""
"`Mutex` mengontrol akses eksklusif ke suatu nilai. Berbeda dari contoh RAII "
"sebelumnya, resource di sini bersifat logis: akses eksklusif sementara ke "
"data di dalamnya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid ""
"This right is represented by a `MutexGuard`. Only one guard for this mutex "
"can exist at a time. While it lives, it provides `&mut T` access."
msgstr ""
"Hak ini direpresentasikan oleh `MutexGuard`. Hanya satu guard untuk mutex "
"ini yang dapat ada pada satu waktu. Selama guard hidup, ia menyediakan akses"
" `&mut T`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid ""
"Although `lock()` takes `&self`, it returns a `MutexGuard` with mutable "
"access. This works through _interior mutability_, where a type manages its "
"own borrowing rules internally to allow mutation through `&self`."
msgstr ""
"Meskipun `lock()` menerima `&self`, method ini mengembalikan `MutexGuard` "
"dengan akses mutable. Ini bekerja melalui _interior mutability_, ketika "
"suatu tipe mengelola aturan borrowing-nya sendiri secara internal untuk "
"memungkinkan mutasi melalui `&self`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid ""
"`MutexGuard` implements `Deref` and `DerefMut`, making access ergonomic. You"
" lock the mutex and use the guard like a `&mut T`."
msgstr ""
"`MutexGuard` mengimplementasikan `Deref` dan `DerefMut`, membuat akses "
"ergonomis. Anda mengunci mutex dan menggunakan guard seperti `&mut T`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/mutex.md
msgid ""
"The mutex is released by `MutexGuard::drop()`. You never call an explicit "
"unlock function."
msgstr ""
"Mutex dilepaskan oleh `MutexGuard::drop()`. Anda tidak pernah memanggil "
"fungsi unlock eksplisit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"A **drop guard** in Rust is a temporary object that performs some kind of "
"cleanup when it goes out of scope. In the case of `Mutex`, the `lock` method"
" returns a `MutexGuard` that automatically unlocks the mutex on `drop`:"
msgstr ""
"**Drop guard** di Rust adalah objek sementara yang melakukan semacam "
"pembersihan ketika keluar dari scope. Dalam kasus `Mutex`, method `lock` "
"mengembalikan `MutexGuard` yang secara otomatis membuka lock mutex saat "
"`drop`:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid "The example above shows a simplified `Mutex` and its associated guard."
msgstr ""
"Contoh di atas menunjukkan `Mutex` yang disederhanakan dan guard terkaitnya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"Even though it is not a production-ready implementation, it illustrates the "
"core idea:"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun bukan implementasi siap produksi, contoh ini mengilustrasikan "
"gagasan intinya:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid "the guard represents exclusive access,"
msgstr "guard merepresentasikan akses eksklusif,"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"and its `Drop` implementation releases the lock when it goes out of scope."
msgstr ""
"dan implementasi `Drop`-nya melepaskan lock ketika guard keluar dari scope."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"This example shows a C++ style mutex that does not contain the data it "
"protects. While this is non-idiomatic in Rust, the goal here is only to "
"illustrate the core idea of a drop guard, not to demonstrate a proper Rust "
"mutex design."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini menunjukkan mutex bergaya C++ yang tidak berisi data yang "
"dilindunginya. Meskipun tidak idiomatis di Rust, tujuannya di sini hanya "
"mengilustrasikan gagasan inti drop guard, bukan menunjukkan desain mutex "
"Rust yang tepat."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid "For brevity, several features are omitted:"
msgstr "Demi keringkasan, beberapa fitur dihilangkan:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"A real `Mutex<T>` stores the protected value inside the mutex.  \n"
"This toy example omits the value entirely to focus only on the drop guard mechanism."
msgstr ""
"`Mutex<T>` sungguhan menyimpan nilai yang dilindungi di dalam mutex.  \n"
"Contoh mainan ini menghilangkan nilai tersebut sepenuhnya untuk berfokus hanya pada mekanisme drop guard."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"Ergonomic access via `Deref` and `DerefMut` on `MutexGuard` (letting the "
"guard behave like a `&T` or `&mut T`)."
msgstr ""
"Akses ergonomis melalui `Deref` dan `DerefMut` pada `MutexGuard` (membuat "
"guard berperilaku seperti `&T` atau `&mut T`)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"A fully blocking `.lock()` method and a non-blocking `try_lock` variant."
msgstr ""
"Method `.lock()` yang sepenuhnya memblokir dan varian `try_lock` yang non-"
"blocking."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_guards.md
msgid ""
"You can explore the [`Mutex` implementation in Rust’s std "
"library](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html) as an example"
" of a production-ready mutex. The [`Mutex` from the `parking_lot` "
"crate](https://docs.rs/parking_lot/latest/parking_lot/type.Mutex.html) is "
"another worthwhile reference."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menelusuri [implementasi `Mutex` di standard library "
"Rust](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html) sebagai contoh "
"mutex siap produksi. [`Mutex` dari crate "
"`parking_lot`](https://docs.rs/parking_lot/latest/parking_lot/type.Mutex.html)"
" adalah referensi lain yang bermanfaat."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid "Drop Bombs: Enforcing API Correctness"
msgstr "Drop Bomb: Menegakkan Kebenaran API"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"Use `Drop` to enforce invariants and detect incorrect API usage. A \"drop "
"bomb\" panics if a value is dropped without being explicitly finalized."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `Drop` untuk menegakkan invariant dan mendeteksi penggunaan API yang"
" keliru. \"Drop bomb\" akan panic jika suatu nilai di-drop tanpa "
"difinalisasi secara eksplisit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"This pattern is often used when the finalizing operation (like `commit()` or"
" `rollback()`) needs to return a `Result`, which cannot be done from `Drop`."
msgstr ""
"Pola ini sering digunakan ketika operasi finalisasi (seperti `commit()` atau"
" `rollback()`) perlu mengembalikan `Result`, yang tidak dapat dilakukan dari"
" `Drop`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid "\"COMMIT\""
msgstr "\"COMMIT\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid "\"Transaction dropped without commit!\""
msgstr "\"Transaction dropped without commit!\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid ""
"// Use `tx` to build the transaction, then commit it.\n"
"    // Comment out the call to `commit` to see the panic.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Use `tx` to build the transaction, then commit it.\n"
"    // Comment out the call to `commit` to see the panic.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"In some systems, a value must be finalized by a specific API before it is "
"dropped."
msgstr ""
"Pada beberapa sistem, suatu nilai harus difinalisasi oleh API tertentu "
"sebelum di-drop."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"For example, a `Transaction` might need to be committed or rolled back."
msgstr "Misalnya, `Transaction` mungkin perlu di-commit atau di-rollback."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"A drop bomb ensures that a value like `Transaction` cannot be silently "
"dropped in an unfinished state. The destructor panics if the transaction has"
" not been explicitly finalized (for example, with `commit()`)."
msgstr ""
"Drop bomb memastikan nilai seperti `Transaction` tidak dapat di-drop secara "
"diam-diam dalam keadaan belum selesai. Destructor akan panic jika transaksi "
"belum difinalisasi secara eksplisit (misalnya, dengan `commit()`)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"The finalizing operation (such as `commit()`) usually takes `self` by value."
" This ensures that once the transaction is finalized, the original object "
"can no longer be used."
msgstr ""
"Operasi finalisasi (seperti `commit()`) biasanya menerima `self` by value. "
"Ini memastikan bahwa setelah transaksi difinalisasi, objek asli tidak dapat "
"digunakan lagi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"A common reason to use this pattern is when cleanup cannot be done in "
"`Drop`, either because it is fallible or asynchronous."
msgstr ""
"Alasan umum penggunaan pola ini adalah ketika pembersihan tidak dapat "
"dilakukan di `Drop`, baik karena fallible maupun asinkron."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"This pattern is appropriate even in public APIs. It can help users catch "
"bugs early when they forget to explicitly finalize a transactional object."
msgstr ""
"Pola ini juga sesuai untuk API publik. Pola ini dapat membantu pengguna "
"menangkap bug lebih awal ketika mereka lupa memfinalisasi objek "
"transaksional secara eksplisit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"If cleanup can safely happen in `Drop`, some APIs choose to panic only in "
"debug builds. Whether this is appropriate depends on the guarantees your API"
" must enforce."
msgstr ""
"Jika pembersihan dapat dilakukan dengan aman di `Drop`, sebagian API memilih"
" panic hanya pada build debug. Apakah ini sesuai bergantung pada jaminan "
"yang harus ditegakkan API Anda."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"Panicking in release builds is reasonable when silent misuse would cause "
"major correctness or security problems."
msgstr ""
"Panic pada build release wajar dilakukan ketika penyalahgunaan diam-diam "
"akan menyebabkan masalah kebenaran atau keamanan yang besar."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"Question: Why do we need an `active` flag inside `Transaction`? Why can't "
"`drop()` panic unconditionally?"
msgstr ""
"Pertanyaan: Mengapa kita memerlukan flag `active` di dalam `Transaction`? "
"Mengapa `drop()` tidak dapat panic tanpa syarat?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"Expected answer: `commit()` takes `self` by value and runs `drop()`, which "
"would panic."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban yang diharapkan: `commit()` menerima `self` by value dan menjalankan"
" `drop()`, yang akan panic."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid "More to explore"
msgstr "Untuk Dieksplorasi Lebih Lanjut"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"Several related patterns help enforce correct teardown or prevent accidental"
" drops."
msgstr ""
"Beberapa pola terkait membantu menegakkan teardown yang benar atau mencegah "
"drop yang tidak disengaja."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb.md
msgid ""
"The [`drop_bomb` crate](https://docs.rs/drop_bomb/latest/drop_bomb/): A "
"small utility that panics if dropped unless explicitly defused with "
"`.defuse()`. Comes with a `DebugDropBomb` variant that only activates in "
"debug builds."
msgstr ""
"[Crate `drop_bomb`](https://docs.rs/drop_bomb/latest/drop_bomb/): Utility "
"kecil yang panic jika di-drop kecuali secara eksplisit dinonaktifkan dengan "
"`.defuse()`. Tersedia varian `DebugDropBomb` yang hanya aktif pada build "
"debug."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid "Drop Bombs: using `std::mem::forget`"
msgstr "Drop Bomb: Menggunakan `std::mem::forget`"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid "// Defuse the drop bomb by preventing Drop from ever running.\n"
msgstr "// Defuse the drop bomb by preventing Drop from ever running.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid "// This is the \"drop bomb\"\n"
msgstr "// This is the \"drop bomb\"\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid ""
"This example removes the flag from the previous slide and makes the drop "
"method panic unconditionally. To avoid that panic on a successful commit, "
"the commit method now takes ownership of the transaction and calls "
"[`std::mem::forget`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/mem/fn.forget.html), "
"which prevents the `Drop::drop()` method from running."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini menghapus flag dari slide sebelumnya dan membuat method drop "
"panic tanpa syarat. Untuk menghindari panic tersebut pada commit yang "
"berhasil, method commit sekarang mengambil ownership transaksi dan memanggil"
" [`std::mem::forget`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/mem/fn.forget.html), "
"yang mencegah method `Drop::drop()` berjalan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid ""
"If the forgotten value owned heap allocated memory that would normally be "
"freed in its `drop()` implementation, one consequence is a memory leak. That"
" is not the case for the `Transaction` in the example above, since it does "
"not own any heap memory."
msgstr ""
"Jika nilai yang dilupakan memiliki memori heap yang biasanya dibebaskan "
"dalam implementasi `drop()`-nya, salah satu konsekuensinya adalah memory "
"leak. Itu bukan kasus untuk `Transaction` pada contoh di atas, karena tidak "
"memiliki memori heap."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_bomb_forget.md
msgid ""
"We can avoid needing a runtime flag by using `mem::forget()` in a tactical "
"way. When the transaction commits successfully, we can defuse the drop bomb "
"by calling `std::mem::forget` on the value, which prevents its `Drop` "
"implementation from running."
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat menghindari kebutuhan flag runtime dengan menggunakan "
"`mem::forget()` secara taktis. Ketika transaksi berhasil di-commit, kita "
"dapat menonaktifkan drop bomb dengan memanggil `std::mem::forget` pada nilai"
" tersebut, yang mencegah implementasi `Drop`-nya berjalan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid ""
"Below are the signatures for the [`drop()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/fn.drop.html) and [`forget()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/fn.forget.html) functions:"
msgstr ""
"Berikut signature untuk fungsi [`drop()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/fn.drop.html) dan [`forget()`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/fn.forget.html):"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid "// std::mem::forget\n"
msgstr "// std::mem::forget\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid "// std::mem::drop\n"
msgstr "// std::mem::drop\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid ""
"Both `mem::forget()` and `mem::drop()` take ownership of the value `t`."
msgstr ""
"`mem::forget()` dan `mem::drop()` sama-sama mengambil ownership nilai `t`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid ""
"Despite having the same function signature, they have opposite effects:"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun memiliki signature fungsi yang sama, keduanya memiliki efek "
"berlawanan:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid ""
"`forget()` uses [`ManuallyDrop`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/struct.ManuallyDrop.html) to prevent the destructor "
"`Drop::drop()` from being invoked."
msgstr ""
"`forget()` menggunakan [`ManuallyDrop`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/struct.ManuallyDrop.html) untuk mencegah destructor "
"`Drop::drop()` dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid ""
"This is useful for scenarios such as implementing a drop bomb or otherwise "
"opting out of destructor behavior."
msgstr ""
"Ini berguna untuk skenario seperti mengimplementasikan drop bomb atau "
"memilih keluar dari perilaku destructor."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid ""
"Be careful though, since any resources the value exclusively owns such as "
"heap allocated memory or file handles will remain in an unreachable state."
msgstr ""
"Namun berhati-hatilah, karena resource apa pun yang dimiliki secara "
"eksklusif oleh nilai tersebut, seperti memori heap atau file handle, akan "
"tetap berada dalam keadaan tidak dapat dijangkau."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/forget_and_drop.md
msgid ""
"`drop()` is a convenience function for disposing of a value. Because `t` is "
"moved into the function, it is automatically dropped which triggers its "
"`Drop::drop()` implementation before the parent function returns."
msgstr ""
"`drop()` adalah fungsi kemudahan untuk membuang suatu nilai. Karena `t` "
"dipindahkan ke dalam fungsi, nilai tersebut otomatis di-drop yang memicu "
"implementasi `Drop::drop()` sebelum fungsi induk kembali."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "Scope Guards"
msgstr "Scope Guard"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"A scope guard uses the `Drop` trait to run cleanup code automatically when a"
" scope exits, even during unwinding."
msgstr ""
"Scope guard menggunakan trait `Drop` untuk menjalankan kode pembersihan "
"secara otomatis saat scope keluar, bahkan selama unwinding."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "\"download.tmp\""
msgstr "\"download.tmp\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "\"cannot create temporary file\""
msgstr "\"cannot create temporary file\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "// Set up cleanup immediately after file creation\n"
msgstr "// Set up cleanup immediately after file creation\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "\"download failed, deleting: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"download failed, deleting: {:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "\"partial data...\""
msgstr "\"partial data...\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "// Download succeeded, keep the file\n"
msgstr "// Download succeeded, keep the file\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "\"Download '{path}' complete!\""
msgstr "\"Download '{path}' complete!\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "// Otherwise, the guard runs and deletes the file\n"
msgstr "// Otherwise, the guard runs and deletes the file\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"This example models a download workflow. We create a temporary file first, "
"then use a scope guard to ensure that the file is deleted if the download "
"fails."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini memodelkan alur unduhan. Kami membuat berkas sementara terlebih "
"dahulu, lalu menggunakan scope guard untuk memastikan berkas dihapus jika "
"unduhan gagal."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"The `scopeguard` crate allows you to conveniently define a single-use "
"`Drop`\\-based cleanup without defining a custom type with a custom `Drop` "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"Crate `scopeguard` memungkinkan Anda mendefinisikan pembersihan berbasis "
"`Drop` sekali pakai dengan mudah tanpa mendefinisikan tipe khusus dengan "
"implementasi `Drop` khusus."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"The guard is created directly after creating the file, so even if "
"`writeln!()` fails, the file will still be cleaned up. This ordering is "
"essential for correctness."
msgstr ""
"Guard dibuat tepat setelah berkas dibuat, sehingga bahkan jika `writeln!()` "
"gagal, berkas tetap dibersihkan. Urutan ini penting untuk kebenaran."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"The `guard()` creates a `ScopeGuard` instance. It takes a user-defined value"
" (in this case, `path`) and the cleanup closure that later receives this "
"value."
msgstr ""
"`guard()` membuat instance `ScopeGuard`. Fungsi ini menerima nilai yang "
"ditentukan pengguna (dalam hal ini, `path`) dan closure pembersihan yang "
"nantinya menerima nilai tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"The guard's closure runs on scope exit unless it is _defused_ with "
"`ScopeGuard::into_inner` (removing the value so the guard does nothing on "
"drop). In the success path, we call `into_inner` so the guard will not "
"delete the file."
msgstr ""
"Closure guard berjalan saat scope keluar kecuali _dinonaktifkan_ dengan "
"`ScopeGuard::into_inner` (mengeluarkan nilai sehingga guard tidak melakukan "
"apa pun saat drop). Pada jalur keberhasilan, kami memanggil `into_inner` "
"agar guard tidak menghapus berkas."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid "A scope guard is similar to the `defer` feature in Go."
msgstr "Scope guard serupa dengan fitur `defer` di Go."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"This pattern is ideal for \"cleanup on failure\" scenarios, where a cleanup "
"should run by default unless a success path is explicitly taken."
msgstr ""
"Pola ini ideal untuk skenario \"cleanup on failure\", ketika pembersihan "
"sebaiknya berjalan secara default kecuali jalur keberhasilan diambil secara "
"eksplisit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"This pattern is also useful when you don't control the cleanup strategy of "
"the resource object. In this example, `File::drop()` closes the file but "
"does not delete it."
msgstr ""
"Pola ini juga berguna ketika Anda tidak mengontrol strategi pembersihan "
"objek resource. Dalam contoh ini, `File::drop()` menutup berkas tetapi tidak"
" menghapusnya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/scope_guard.md
msgid ""
"The `scopeguard` crate also supports cleanup strategies via the "
"[`Strategy`](https://docs.rs/scopeguard/latest/scopeguard/trait.Strategy.html)"
" trait. You can choose to run the guard on unwind only, or on success only, "
"not just always."
msgstr ""
"Crate `scopeguard` juga mendukung strategi pembersihan melalui trait "
"[`Strategy`](https://docs.rs/scopeguard/latest/scopeguard/trait.Strategy.html)."
" Anda dapat memilih menjalankan guard hanya saat unwind, atau hanya saat "
"berhasil, bukan hanya selalu."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid "Drop: Option"
msgstr "Drop: Option"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid ""
"// We have to go through the `Option` to get the `Handle`\n"
"        // before we can use it.\n"
msgstr ""
"// We have to go through the `Option` to get the `Handle`\n"
"        // before we can use it.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid "\"write '{data}' to file '{}'\""
msgstr "\"write '{data}' to file '{}'\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid "\"Closing {}\""
msgstr "\"Closing {}\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid ""
"In this example we want to call `close` on the inner `Handle` in our `Drop` "
"impl, but `close` requires ownership of the `Handle`. We can't do this "
"normally, because we don't get ownership of the `File` object in `drop`, and"
" therefore can't move out of the field."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini kami ingin memanggil `close` pada `Handle` di dalam "
"implementasi `Drop` kami, tetapi `close` memerlukan ownership atas `Handle`."
" Kami tidak dapat melakukannya secara normal, karena kami tidak mendapatkan "
"ownership objek `File` di `drop`, sehingga tidak dapat memindahkan keluar "
"dari field."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid ""
"Wrapping the handle in an `Option` gives us a way to move out of the field "
"through a mutable reference."
msgstr ""
"Membungkus handle dalam `Option` memberi kami cara untuk memindahkan keluar "
"dari field melalui reference mutable."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid ""
"The main downside is ergonomics. `Option` forces us to handle both the "
"`Some` and `None` case even in places where, logically, `None` cannot occur."
" Rust’s type system cannot express that relationship between `File` and its "
"`Handle`, so we handle both cases manually."
msgstr ""
"Kelemahan utamanya adalah ergonomi. `Option` memaksa kami menangani kasus "
"`Some` dan `None` bahkan di tempat yang secara logis `None` tidak mungkin "
"terjadi. Sistem tipe Rust tidak dapat mengekspresikan hubungan antara `File`"
" dan `Handle`-nya, sehingga kami menangani kedua kasus secara manual."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid ""
"Instead of `Option` we could use [`ManuallyDrop`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/struct.ManuallyDrop.html), which suppresses automatic "
"destruction by preventing Rust from calling `Drop` for the value; you must "
"handle teardown yourself."
msgstr ""
"Alih-alih `Option`, kami dapat menggunakan "
"[`ManuallyDrop`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/mem/struct.ManuallyDrop.html), yang menekan penghancuran "
"otomatis dengan mencegah Rust memanggil `Drop` untuk nilai tersebut; Anda "
"harus menangani teardown sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid ""
"The [_scopeguard_ example](./scope_guard.md) on the previous slide shows how"
" `ManuallyDrop` can replace `Option` to avoid handling `None` in places "
"where the value should always exist."
msgstr ""
"[Contoh _scopeguard_](./scope_guard.md) pada slide sebelumnya menunjukkan "
"bagaimana `ManuallyDrop` dapat menggantikan `Option` untuk menghindari "
"penanganan `None` di tempat yang nilainya seharusnya selalu ada."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/raii/drop_option.md
msgid ""
"In such designs we typically track the drop state with a separate flag next "
"to the `ManuallyDrop<Handle>`, which lets us track whether the handle has "
"already been manually consumed."
msgstr ""
"Dalam desain semacam itu kami biasanya melacak state drop dengan flag "
"terpisah di samping `ManuallyDrop<Handle>`, yang memungkinkan kami melacak "
"apakah handle sudah dikonsumsi secara manual."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"It may desirable to **extend** foreign types with new methods. For example, "
"allow your code to check if a string is a palindrome using method-calling "
"syntax: `s.is_palindrome()`."
msgstr ""
"Mungkin diinginkan untuk **memperluas** tipe eksternal dengan method baru. "
"Misalnya, memungkinkan kode Anda memeriksa apakah suatu string adalah "
"palindrom menggunakan sintaks pemanggilan method: `s.is_palindrome()`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid "It might feel natural to reach out for an `impl` block:"
msgstr "Mungkin terasa wajar untuk menggunakan block `impl`:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"The Rust compiler won't allow it, though. But you can use the **extension "
"trait pattern** to work around this limitation."
msgstr ""
"Namun, compiler Rust tidak mengizinkannya. Tetapi Anda dapat menggunakan "
"**pola extension trait** untuk mengatasi keterbatasan ini."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid "A Rust item (be it a trait or a type) is referred to as:"
msgstr "Item Rust (baik trait maupun tipe) disebut sebagai:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid "**foreign**, if it isn't defined in the current crate"
msgstr "**foreign**, jika tidak didefinisikan dalam crate saat ini"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid "**local**, if it is defined in the current crate"
msgstr "**local**, jika didefinisikan dalam crate saat ini"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"The distinction has significant implications for [coherence and orphan "
"rules](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/items/implementations.html#r-items.impl.trait.orphan-"
"rule), as we'll get a chance to explore in this section of the course."
msgstr ""
"Perbedaan ini memiliki implikasi signifikan bagi [coherence dan orphan "
"rule](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/items/implementations.html#r-items.impl.trait.orphan-"
"rule), yang akan kita jelajahi pada bagian kursus ini."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid "Compile the example to show the compiler error that's emitted."
msgstr "Kompilasi contoh untuk menunjukkan error compiler yang dihasilkan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"Highlight how the compiler error message nudges you towards the extension "
"trait pattern."
msgstr ""
"Soroti bagaimana pesan error compiler mendorong Anda menuju pola extension "
"trait."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"Explain how many type-system restrictions in Rust aim to prevent "
"_ambiguity_."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa banyak batasan sistem tipe di Rust bertujuan mencegah "
"_ambiguitas_."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"What would happen if you were allowed to define new inherent methods on "
"foreign types? Different crates in your dependency tree might end up "
"defining different methods on the same foreign type with the same name."
msgstr ""
"Apa yang akan terjadi jika Anda diizinkan mendefinisikan inherent method "
"baru pada tipe eksternal? Crate berbeda dalam pohon dependensi Anda mungkin "
"akhirnya mendefinisikan method berbeda pada tipe eksternal yang sama dengan "
"nama yang sama."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"As soon as there is room for ambiguity, there must be a way to disambiguate."
" If disambiguation happens implicitly, it can lead to surprising or "
"otherwise unexpected behavior. If disambiguation happens explicitly, it can "
"increase the cognitive load on developers who are reading your code."
msgstr ""
"Segera setelah ada ruang untuk ambiguitas, harus ada cara untuk memperjelas."
" Jika disambiguasi terjadi secara implisit, hal itu dapat menyebabkan "
"perilaku mengejutkan atau tak terduga. Jika disambiguasi terjadi secara "
"eksplisit, hal itu dapat meningkatkan beban kognitif developer yang membaca "
"kode Anda."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"Furthermore, every time a crate defines a new inherent method on a foreign "
"type, it may cause compilation errors in _your_ code, as you may be forced "
"to introduce explicit disambiguation."
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, setiap kali suatu crate mendefinisikan inherent method baru pada"
" tipe eksternal, hal itu dapat menyebabkan error kompilasi pada kode _Anda_,"
" karena Anda mungkin dipaksa memperkenalkan disambiguasi eksplisit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"Rust has decided to avoid the issue altogether by forbidding the definition "
"of new inherent methods on foreign types."
msgstr ""
"Rust memutuskan menghindari masalah ini sepenuhnya dengan melarang definisi "
"inherent method baru pada tipe eksternal."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits.md
msgid ""
"Other languages (e.g, Kotlin, C#, Swift) allow adding methods to existing "
"types, often called \"extension methods.\" This leads to different trade-"
"offs in terms of potential ambiguities and the need for global reasoning."
msgstr ""
"Bahasa lain (misalnya, Kotlin, C#, Swift) mengizinkan penambahan method pada"
" tipe yang sudah ada, sering disebut \"extension method\". Ini menghasilkan "
"trade-off berbeda dalam hal potensi ambiguitas dan kebutuhan penalaran "
"global."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"What prevents users from writing arbitrary trait implementations for any "
"type?"
msgstr ""
"Apa yang mencegah pengguna menulis implementasi trait arbitrer untuk tipe "
"apa pun?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "// Crate `postgresql-bindings`\n"
msgstr "// Crate `postgresql-bindings`\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "/* details */"
msgstr "/* details */"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "// Crate `database-traits`, depends on `postgresql-bindings`\n"
msgstr "// Crate `database-traits`, depends on `postgresql-bindings`\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid "/* methods */"
msgstr "/* methods */"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "// ✅, `DbConnection` is local.\n"
msgstr "// ✅, `DbConnection` is local.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "// Crate `mycoolnewdb` depends on `database-traits`\n"
msgstr "// Crate `mycoolnewdb` depends on `database-traits`\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "// ✅, `MyCoolNewDbConn` is local.\n"
msgstr "// ✅, `MyCoolNewDbConn` is local.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"// Neither `PostgresqlConn` or `DbConnection` are local to `mycoolnewdb`.\n"
"// This would lead to two implementations of `DbConnection` for PostgresqlConn!\n"
msgstr ""
"// Neither `PostgresqlConn` or `DbConnection` are local to `mycoolnewdb`.\n"
"// This would lead to two implementations of `DbConnection` for PostgresqlConn!\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "// ❌🔨\n"
msgstr "// ❌🔨\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"Rust traits should never be able to be implemented twice in its ecosystem. "
"Two implementations of the same trait for the same type is a conflict with "
"no solution."
msgstr ""
"Trait Rust tidak boleh dapat diimplementasikan dua kali dalam ekosistemnya. "
"Dua implementasi trait yang sama untuk tipe yang sama adalah konflik tanpa "
"solusi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"We can prevent this within a crate by detecting if there are multiple "
"definitions and disallowing it, but what about between crates in the entire "
"Rust ecosystem?"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat mencegahnya dalam satu crate dengan mendeteksi apakah ada "
"beberapa definisi dan melarangnya, tetapi bagaimana antarcrate di seluruh "
"ekosistem Rust?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"Types are either _local_ to a crate, they are defined there, or they're not."
msgstr ""
"Tipe bersifat _local_ terhadap suatu crate—didefinisikan di sana—atau tidak."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"In the example's \"crates\", `PostgresqlConn` is local to `postgresql-"
"bindings`, `MyCoolNewDbConn` is local to `mycoolnewdb`."
msgstr ""
"Pada \"crate\" dalam contoh, `PostgresqlConn` bersifat local terhadap "
"`postgresql-bindings`, `MyCoolNewDbConn` bersifat local terhadap "
"`mycoolnewdb`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"Traits are also either _local_ to a crate, they are defined there, or "
"they're not."
msgstr ""
"Trait juga bersifat _local_ terhadap suatu crate—didefinisikan di sana—atau "
"tidak."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"Again in the example, the `DbConnection` trait is local to `database-"
"traits`."
msgstr ""
"Sekali lagi pada contoh, trait `DbConnection` bersifat local terhadap "
"`database-traits`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "If something is local, you can write trait implementations for it."
msgstr ""
"Jika sesuatu bersifat local, Anda dapat menulis implementasi trait untuknya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"If the trait is local, you can write implementations of that trait for any "
"type."
msgstr ""
"Jika trait bersifat local, Anda dapat menulis implementasi trait tersebut "
"untuk tipe apa pun."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"If the type is local, you can write any trait implementations for that type."
msgstr ""
"Jika tipe bersifat local, Anda dapat menulis implementasi trait apa pun "
"untuk tipe tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid "Outside of these boundaries, trait implementations cannot be written."
msgstr "Di luar batas tersebut, implementasi trait tidak dapat ditulis."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"This keeps implementations \"coherent\": Only one implementation of a trait "
"for a type can exist across crates."
msgstr ""
"Ini menjaga implementasi tetap \"coherent\": Hanya satu implementasi trait "
"untuk suatu tipe yang dapat ada di seluruh crate."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid "ref:"
msgstr "ref:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/orphan-rule.md
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/items/implementations.html#r-items.impl.trait.orphan-"
"rule"
msgstr ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/items/implementations.html#r-items.impl.trait.orphan-"
"rule"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"An **extension trait** is a local trait definition whose primary purpose is "
"to attach new methods to foreign types."
msgstr ""
"**Extension trait** adalah definisi trait local yang tujuan utamanya "
"melekatkan method baru pada tipe eksternal."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid "// Bring the extension trait into scope...\n"
msgstr "// Bring the extension trait into scope...\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid "// ...then invoke its methods as if they were inherent methods\n"
msgstr "// ...then invoke its methods as if they were inherent methods\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "\"dad\""
msgstr "\"dad\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid "\"grandma\""
msgstr "\"grandma\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"The `Ext` suffix is conventionally attached to the name of extension traits."
msgstr "Sufiks `Ext` secara konvensi dilekatkan pada nama extension trait."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"It communicates that the trait is primarily used for extension purposes, and"
" it is therefore not intended to be implemented outside the crate that "
"defines it."
msgstr ""
"Sufiks ini mengomunikasikan bahwa trait terutama digunakan untuk tujuan "
"ekstensi, dan karena itu tidak dimaksudkan untuk diimplementasikan di luar "
"crate yang mendefinisikannya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"Refer to the [\"Extension Trait\" RFC](https://rust-"
"lang.github.io/rfcs/0445-extension-trait-conventions.html) as the "
"authoritative source for naming conventions."
msgstr ""
"Rujuk [\"Extension Trait\" RFC](https://rust-"
"lang.github.io/rfcs/0445-extension-trait-conventions.html) sebagai sumber "
"otoritatif untuk konvensi penamaan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"The extension trait implementation for a foreign type must be in the same "
"crate as the trait itself, otherwise you'll be blocked by Rust's [_orphan "
"rule_](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/2451-re-"
"rebalancing-coherence.md#what-is-coherence-and-why-do-we-care)."
msgstr ""
"Implementasi extension trait untuk tipe eksternal harus berada dalam crate "
"yang sama dengan trait itu sendiri, jika tidak Anda akan terhalang oleh "
"[_orphan rule_](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/2451-re-"
"rebalancing-coherence.md#what-is-coherence-and-why-do-we-care) Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid "The extension trait must be in scope when its methods are invoked."
msgstr "Extension trait harus berada dalam scope saat method-nya dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"Comment out the `use` statement in the example to show the compiler error "
"that's emitted if you try to invoke an extension method without having the "
"corresponding extension trait in scope."
msgstr ""
"Beri komentar pada statement `use` dalam contoh untuk menunjukkan error "
"compiler yang muncul jika Anda mencoba memanggil extension method tanpa "
"memiliki extension trait terkait dalam scope."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"The example above uses an [_underscore import_](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/items/use-declarations.html#r-items.use.as-"
"underscore) (`use ext::StringExt as _`) to minimize the likelihood of a "
"naming conflict with other imported traits."
msgstr ""
"Contoh di atas menggunakan [_underscore import_](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/items/use-declarations.html#r-items.use.as-"
"underscore) (`use ext::StringExt as _`) untuk meminimalkan kemungkinan "
"konflik penamaan dengan trait lain yang diimpor."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"With an underscore import, the trait is considered to be in scope and you're"
" allowed to invoke its methods on types that implement the trait. Its "
"_symbol_, instead, is not directly accessible. This prevents you, for "
"example, from using that trait in a `where` clause."
msgstr ""
"Dengan underscore import, trait dianggap berada dalam scope dan Anda "
"diizinkan memanggil method-nya pada tipe yang mengimplementasikan trait "
"tersebut. Namun _simbol_-nya tidak dapat diakses secara langsung. Ini "
"mencegah Anda, misalnya, menggunakan trait tersebut dalam klausa `where`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-foreign-types.md
msgid ""
"Since extension traits aren't meant to be used in `where` clauses, they are "
"conventionally imported via an underscore import."
msgstr ""
"Karena extension trait tidak dimaksudkan untuk digunakan dalam klausa "
"`where`, trait tersebut secara konvensi diimpor melalui underscore import."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"What happens when you have a name conflict between an inherent method and an"
" extension method?"
msgstr ""
"Apa yang terjadi jika ada konflik nama antara inherent method dan extension "
"method?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"// Which `count_ones` method is invoked?\n"
"    // The one from `CountOnesExt`? Or the inherent one from `i32`?\n"
msgstr ""
"// Which `count_ones` method is invoked?\n"
"    // The one from `CountOnesExt`? Or the inherent one from `i32`?\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"A foreign type may, in a newer version, add a new inherent method with the "
"same name as our extension method."
msgstr ""
"Tipe eksternal mungkin, pada versi yang lebih baru, menambahkan inherent "
"method baru dengan nama yang sama dengan extension method kita."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"Ask: What will happen in the example above? Will there be a compiler error? "
"Will one of the two methods be given higher priority? Which one?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Apa yang akan terjadi pada contoh di atas? Apakah akan ada error "
"compiler? Apakah salah satu dari dua method akan diberi prioritas lebih "
"tinggi? Yang mana?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"Add a `panic!(\"Extension trait\");` in the body of "
"`CountOnesExt::count_ones` to clarify which method is being invoked."
msgstr ""
"Tambahkan `panic!(\"Extension trait\");` pada body "
"`CountOnesExt::count_ones` untuk memperjelas method mana yang dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"When an inherent method and a trait method have the same name and receiver "
"type, Rust's [method resolution](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/expressions/method-call-expr.html) rules will "
"choose one automatically. Generally it will prioritize the inherent method "
"over the trait method, but the method resolution rules can be subtle and "
"surprising."
msgstr ""
"Ketika inherent method dan trait method memiliki nama dan tipe receiver yang"
" sama, aturan [resolusi method](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/expressions/method-call-expr.html) Rust akan "
"memilih salah satunya secara otomatis. Umumnya inherent method "
"diprioritaskan di atas trait method, tetapi aturan resolusi method bisa "
"halus dan mengejutkan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Change the call to `(&-1i32).count_ones()` and demonstrate that"
" the trait method is now called instead. Then change the trait method to "
"take `self` (instead of `&self`) and show that the inherent method is once "
"again called."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Ubah pemanggilan menjadi `(&-1i32).count_ones()` dan "
"tunjukkan bahwa trait method sekarang yang dipanggil. Kemudian ubah trait "
"method agar menerima `self` (bukan `&self`) dan tunjukkan bahwa inherent "
"method kembali dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"Avoid naming conflicts between extension trait methods and inherent methods."
" Rust's method resolution algorithm is complex and may surprise users of "
"your code."
msgstr ""
"Hindari konflik penamaan antara method extension trait dan inherent method. "
"Algoritma resolusi method Rust kompleks dan dapat mengejutkan pengguna kode "
"Anda."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/method-resolution-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"The interaction between the priority search used by Rust's method resolution"
" algorithm and automatic `Deref`ing can be used to emulate "
"[specialization](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/31844) on the "
"stable toolchain, primarily in the context of macro-generated code. Check "
"out [\"Autoref Specialization\"](https://github.com/dtolnay/case-"
"studies/blob/master/autoref-specialization/README.md) for the specific "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Interaksi antara pencarian prioritas yang digunakan algoritma resolusi "
"method Rust dan `Deref` otomatis dapat digunakan untuk meniru "
"[specialization](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/31844) pada "
"toolchain stable, terutama dalam konteks kode yang dihasilkan macro. Lihat "
"[\"Autoref Specialization\"](https://github.com/dtolnay/case-"
"studies/blob/master/autoref-specialization/README.md) untuk detail "
"spesifiknya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"What happens when you have a name conflict between two different trait "
"methods implemented for the same type?"
msgstr ""
"Apa yang terjadi jika ada konflik nama antara dua method trait berbeda yang "
"diimplementasikan untuk tipe yang sama?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"// Which method is invoked?\n"
"// The one from `Ext1`? Or the one from `Ext2`?\n"
msgstr ""
"// Which method is invoked?\n"
"// The one from `Ext1`? Or the one from `Ext2`?\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"The trait you are extending may, in a newer version, add a new trait method "
"with the same name as your extension method. Or another extension trait for "
"the same type may define a method with a name that conflicts with your own "
"extension method."
msgstr ""
"Trait yang Anda perluas mungkin, pada versi yang lebih baru, menambahkan "
"method trait baru dengan nama yang sama dengan extension method Anda. Atau "
"extension trait lain untuk tipe yang sama mungkin mendefinisikan method "
"dengan nama yang berkonflik dengan extension method Anda."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"Ask: what will happen in the example above? Will there be a compiler error? "
"Will one of the two methods be given higher priority? Which one?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: apa yang akan terjadi pada contoh di atas? Apakah akan ada error "
"compiler? Apakah salah satu dari dua method akan diberi prioritas lebih "
"tinggi? Yang mana?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"The compiler rejects the code because it cannot determine which method to "
"invoke. Neither `Ext1` nor `Ext2` has a higher priority than the other."
msgstr ""
"Compiler menolak kode karena tidak dapat menentukan method mana yang harus "
"dipanggil. Baik `Ext1` maupun `Ext2` tidak memiliki prioritas lebih tinggi "
"satu sama lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"To resolve this conflict, you must specify which trait you want to use."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menyelesaikan konflik ini, Anda harus menentukan trait mana yang ingin"
" digunakan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: call `Ext1::is_palindrome(\"dad\")` or "
"`Ext2::is_palindrome(\"dad\")` instead of `\"dad\".is_palindrome()`."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: panggil `Ext1::is_palindrome(\"dad\")` atau "
"`Ext2::is_palindrome(\"dad\")` alih-alih `\"dad\".is_palindrome()`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"For methods with more complex signatures, you may need to use a more "
"explicit [fully-qualified syntax](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/expressions/call-expr.html#disambiguating-function-"
"calls)."
msgstr ""
"Untuk method dengan signature lebih kompleks, Anda mungkin perlu menggunakan"
" [fully-qualified syntax](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/expressions/call-expr.html#disambiguating-function-calls)"
" yang lebih eksplisit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/trait-method-conflicts.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: replace `\"dad\".is_palindrome()` with `<str as "
"Ext1>::is_palindrome(\"dad\")` or `<str as Ext2>::is_palindrome(\"dad\")`."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: ganti `\"dad\".is_palindrome()` dengan `<str as "
"Ext1>::is_palindrome(\"dad\")` atau `<str as Ext2>::is_palindrome(\"dad\")`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"As with types, it may be desirable to **extend foreign traits**. In "
"particular, to attach new methods to _all_ implementors of a given trait."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada tipe, mungkin diinginkan untuk **memperluas trait eksternal**. "
"Khususnya, untuk melekatkan method baru pada _semua_ implementor trait "
"tertentu."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "\"'{}'\""
msgstr "\"'{}'\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "\"'dad'\""
msgstr "\"'dad'\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "\"'4'\""
msgstr "\"'4'\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "\"'true'\""
msgstr "\"'true'\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Highlight how we added new behavior to _multiple_ types at once. `.quoted()`"
" can be called on string slices, numbers, and booleans since they all "
"implement the `Display` trait."
msgstr ""
"Soroti bagaimana kami menambahkan perilaku baru ke _beberapa_ tipe "
"sekaligus. `.quoted()` dapat dipanggil pada string slice, angka, dan boolean"
" karena semuanya mengimplementasikan trait `Display`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"This flavor of the extension trait pattern uses [_blanket "
"implementations_](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/glossary.html#blanket-implementation)."
msgstr ""
"Varian pola extension trait ini menggunakan [_blanket "
"implementation_](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/glossary.html#blanket-implementation)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"A blanket implementation implements a trait for all types `T` that satisfy "
"the trait bounds specified in the `impl` block. In this case, the only "
"requirement is that `T` implements the `Display` trait."
msgstr ""
"Blanket implementation mengimplementasikan trait untuk semua tipe `T` yang "
"memenuhi trait bound yang ditentukan dalam block `impl`. Dalam kasus ini, "
"satu-satunya persyaratan adalah `T` mengimplementasikan trait `Display`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Draw the students' attention to the implementation of `DisplayExt::quoted`: "
"we can't make any assumptions about `T` other than that it implements "
"`Display`. All our logic must either use methods from `Display` or "
"functions/macros that don't require other traits."
msgstr ""
"Arahkan perhatian siswa ke implementasi `DisplayExt::quoted`: kita tidak "
"dapat membuat asumsi apa pun tentang `T` selain bahwa tipe tersebut "
"mengimplementasikan `Display`. Semua logika kita harus menggunakan method "
"dari `Display` atau fungsi/macro yang tidak memerlukan trait lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"For example, we can call `format!` with `T`, but can't call "
"`.to_uppercase()` because it is not necessarily a `String`."
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, kita dapat memanggil `format!` dengan `T`, tetapi tidak dapat "
"memanggil `.to_uppercase()` karena nilainya belum tentu `String`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"We could introduce additional trait bounds on `T`, but it would restrict the"
" set of types that can leverage the extension trait."
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat menambahkan trait bound tambahan pada `T`, tetapi itu akan "
"membatasi himpunan tipe yang dapat memanfaatkan extension trait."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Conventionally, the extension trait is named after the trait it extends, "
"followed by the `Ext` suffix. In the example above, `DisplayExt`."
msgstr ""
"Secara konvensi, extension trait dinamai menurut trait yang diperluas, "
"diikuti sufiks `Ext`. Pada contoh di atas, `DisplayExt`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Note that it's still possible to manually implement `DisplayExt` on "
"non-`Display` types. If you want to prevent direct implementations of the "
"trait, you can make `Display` a supertrait of `DisplayExt`. This would lock "
"out non-`Display` types from implementing the trait."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa masih mungkin mengimplementasikan `DisplayExt` secara "
"manual pada tipe non-`Display`. Jika Anda ingin mencegah implementasi "
"langsung trait tersebut, Anda dapat menjadikan `Display` sebagai supertrait "
"`DisplayExt`. Ini akan mengunci tipe non-`Display` dari mengimplementasikan "
"trait tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"There are entire crates that extend standard library traits with new "
"functionality."
msgstr ""
"Ada crate khusus yang memperluas trait standard library dengan "
"fungsionalitas baru."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"`itertools` crate provides the `Itertools` trait that extends `Iterator`. It"
" adds many iterator adapters, such as `interleave` and `unique`. It provides"
" new algorithmic building blocks for iterator pipelines built with method "
"chaining."
msgstr ""
"Crate `itertools` menyediakan trait `Itertools` yang memperluas `Iterator`. "
"Crate ini menambahkan banyak iterator adapter, seperti `interleave` dan "
"`unique`. Crate ini menyediakan blok bangunan algoritmik baru untuk pipeline"
" iterator yang dibangun dengan method chaining."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"`futures` crate provides the `FutureExt` trait, which extends the `Future` "
"trait with new combinators and helper methods."
msgstr ""
"Crate `futures` menyediakan trait `FutureExt`, yang memperluas trait "
"`Future` dengan combinator dan method helper baru."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Extension traits can be used by libraries to distinguish between stable and "
"experimental methods."
msgstr ""
"Extension trait dapat digunakan library untuk membedakan method stabil dan "
"eksperimental."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "Stable methods are part of the trait definition."
msgstr "Method stabil merupakan bagian dari definisi trait."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Experimental methods are provided via an extension trait defined in a "
"different library, with a less restrictive stability policy. Some utility "
"methods are then \"promoted\" to the core trait definition once they have "
"been proven useful and their design has been refined."
msgstr ""
"Method eksperimental disediakan melalui extension trait yang didefinisikan "
"di library lain, dengan kebijakan stabilitas yang lebih longgar. Beberapa "
"method utilitas kemudian \"dipromosikan\" ke definisi trait inti setelah "
"terbukti berguna dan desainnya disempurnakan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Extension traits can be used to split a [dyn-incompatible "
"trait](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/items/traits.html#r-items.traits.dyn-compatible) in two:"
msgstr ""
"Extension trait dapat digunakan untuk memisahkan [trait yang tidak "
"kompatibel dengan dyn](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/items/traits.html#r-items.traits.dyn-compatible) menjadi "
"dua:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"A **dyn-compatible core**, restricted to the methods that satisfy dyn-"
"compatibility requirements."
msgstr ""
"**Inti yang kompatibel dengan dyn**, dibatasi pada method yang memenuhi "
"persyaratan kompatibilitas dyn."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"An **extension trait**, containing the remaining methods that are not dyn-"
"compatible (e.g., methods with a generic parameter)."
msgstr ""
"**Extension trait**, berisi method yang tersisa yang tidak kompatibel dengan"
" dyn (misalnya, method dengan parameter generic)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid ""
"Concrete types that implement the core trait will be able to invoke all "
"methods, thanks to the blanket impl for the extension trait. Trait objects "
"(`dyn CoreTrait`) will be able to invoke all methods on the core trait as "
"well as those on the extension trait that don't require `Self: Sized`."
msgstr ""
"Tipe konkret yang mengimplementasikan trait inti akan dapat memanggil semua "
"method, berkat blanket impl untuk extension trait. Trait object (`dyn "
"CoreTrait`) akan dapat memanggil semua method pada trait inti serta method "
"pada extension trait yang tidak memerlukan `Self: Sized`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid ""
"In what scenarios should you prefer an extension trait over a free function?"
msgstr ""
"Dalam skenario apa Anda sebaiknya memilih extension trait daripada free "
"function?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid "// vs\n"
msgstr "// vs\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid "The main advantage of extension traits is **ease of discovery**."
msgstr "Keunggulan utama extension trait adalah **kemudahan ditemukan**."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid ""
"**Discoverability:** Extension methods are easier to discover than free "
"functions. Language servers (e.g., `rust-analyzer`) will suggest them if you"
" type `.` after an instance of the foreign type."
msgstr ""
"**Discoverability:** Extension method lebih mudah ditemukan daripada free "
"function. Language server (misalnya, `rust-analyzer`) akan menyarankannya "
"jika Anda mengetik `.` setelah instance tipe eksternal."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid ""
"**Method Chaining:** A major ergonomic win for extension traits is method "
"chaining. This is the foundation of the `Iterator` trait, allowing for "
"fluent calls like `data.iter().filter(...).map(...)`. Achieving this with "
"free functions would be far more cumbersome (`map(filter(iter(data), ...), "
"...)`)."
msgstr ""
"**Method Chaining:** Keunggulan ergonomis utama extension trait adalah "
"method chaining. Ini adalah fondasi trait `Iterator`, yang memungkinkan "
"pemanggilan lancar seperti `data.iter().filter(...).map(...)`. Mencapainya "
"dengan free function akan jauh lebih rumit (`map(filter(iter(data), ...), "
"...)`)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid ""
"**Generics and `dyn`:** A trait can be used as a trait bound in a generic or"
" part of a `dyn Trait`, whereas a free function can't necessarily be used in"
" a generic context."
msgstr ""
"**Generic dan `dyn`:** Trait dapat digunakan sebagai trait bound dalam "
"generic atau bagian dari `dyn Trait`, sedangkan free function belum tentu "
"dapat digunakan dalam konteks generic."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid ""
"**API Cohesion:** Extension traits help create a cohesive API. If you have "
"several related functions for a foreign type (e.g., `is_palindrome`, "
"`word_count`, `to_kebab_case`), grouping them in a single `StrExt` trait is "
"often cleaner than having multiple free functions for a user to import."
msgstr ""
"**Kohesi API:** Extension trait membantu menciptakan API yang kohesif. Jika "
"Anda memiliki beberapa fungsi terkait untuk tipe eksternal (misalnya, "
"`is_palindrome`, `word_count`, `to_kebab_case`), mengelompokkannya dalam "
"satu trait `StrExt` sering lebih bersih daripada memiliki beberapa free "
"function yang harus diimpor pengguna."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/should-i-define-an-extension-trait.md
msgid ""
"**Trade-offs:** Despite these advantages, a bespoke extension trait might be"
" overkill for a single, simple function. Both approaches require an "
"additional import, and the familiar method syntax may not justify the "
"boilerplate of a full trait definition."
msgstr ""
"**Trade-off:** Meskipun ada keunggulan tersebut, extension trait khusus "
"mungkin berlebihan untuk satu fungsi sederhana. Kedua pendekatan memerlukan "
"import tambahan, dan sintaks method yang familiar mungkin tidak cukup "
"membenarkan boilerplate definisi trait lengkap."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid "Typestate Pattern: Problem"
msgstr "Pola Typestate: Masalah"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid ""
"How can we ensure that only valid operations are allowed on a value based on"
" its current state?"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana kita dapat memastikan bahwa hanya operasi valid yang diizinkan "
"pada suatu nilai berdasarkan state-nya saat ini?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/root.md
