msgid "\"{name} {{\""
msgstr "\"{name} {{\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "\"  {key}={value};\""
msgstr "\"  {key}={value};\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "\"}\\n\""
msgstr "\"}\\n\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "\"User\""
msgstr "\"User\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "\"id\""
msgstr "\"id\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "\"42\""
msgstr "\"42\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "\"name\""
msgstr "\"name\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid "// serializer.serialize_struct_end(); // ← Oops! Forgotten\n"
msgstr "// serializer.serialize_struct_end(); // ← Oops! Forgotten\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid "This `Serializer` is meant to write a structured value."
msgstr "`Serializer` ini dimaksudkan untuk menulis nilai terstruktur."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid ""
"However, in this example we forgot to call `serialize_struct_end()` before "
"`finish()`. As a result, the serialized output is incomplete or "
"syntactically incorrect."
msgstr ""
"Namun, dalam contoh ini kami lupa memanggil `serialize_struct_end()` sebelum"
" `finish()`. Akibatnya, output yang diserialisasi tidak lengkap atau tidak "
"valid secara sintaksis."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid ""
"One approach to fix this would be to track internal state manually, and "
"return a `Result` from methods like `serialize_struct_field()` or `finish()`"
" if the current state is invalid."
msgstr ""
"Salah satu pendekatan untuk memperbaikinya adalah melacak state internal "
"secara manual, dan mengembalikan `Result` dari method seperti "
"`serialize_struct_field()` atau `finish()` jika state saat ini tidak valid."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid "But this has downsides:"
msgstr "Tetapi ini memiliki kekurangan:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid ""
"It is easy to get wrong as an implementer. Rust’s type system cannot help "
"enforce the correctness of our state transitions."
msgstr ""
"Mudah salah bagi implementor. Sistem tipe Rust tidak dapat membantu "
"menegakkan kebenaran transisi state kita."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid ""
"It also adds unnecessary burden on the user, who must handle `Result` values"
" for operations that are misused in source code rather than at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Ini juga menambah beban yang tidak perlu bagi pengguna, yang harus menangani"
" nilai `Result` untuk operasi yang disalahgunakan dalam kode sumber, bukan "
"pada runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid ""
"A better solution is to model the valid state transitions directly in the "
"type system."
msgstr ""
"Solusi yang lebih baik adalah memodelkan transisi state yang valid langsung "
"dalam sistem tipe."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md
msgid ""
"In the next slide, we will apply the **typestate pattern** to enforce "
"correct usage at compile time and make it impossible to call incompatible "
"methods or forget to do a required action."
msgstr ""
"Pada slide berikutnya, kami akan menerapkan **pola typestate** untuk "
"menegakkan penggunaan yang benar pada waktu kompilasi dan membuatnya "
"mustahil memanggil method yang tidak kompatibel atau lupa melakukan tindakan"
" yang diperlukan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "Typestate Pattern: Example"
msgstr "Pola Typestate: Contoh"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"The typestate pattern encodes part of a value’s runtime state into its type."
" This allows us to prevent invalid or inapplicable operations at compile "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Pola typestate mengodekan sebagian state runtime suatu nilai ke dalam "
"tipenya. Ini memungkinkan kita mencegah operasi tidak valid atau tidak dapat"
" diterapkan pada waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "`Serializer` usage flowchart:"
msgstr "Diagram alur penggunaan `Serializer`:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"This example is inspired by Serde’s [`Serializer` "
"trait](https://docs.rs/serde/latest/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html). Serde "
"uses typestates internally to ensure serialization follows a valid "
"structure. For more, see: <https://serde.rs/impl-serializer.html>"
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini terinspirasi oleh [trait "
"`Serializer`](https://docs.rs/serde/latest/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html) "
"milik Serde. Serde menggunakan typestate secara internal untuk memastikan "
"serialisasi mengikuti struktur yang valid. Untuk informasi lebih lanjut, "
"lihat: <https://serde.rs/impl-serializer.html>"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"The key idea behind typestate is that state transitions happen by consuming "
"a value and producing a new one. At each step, only operations valid for "
"that state are available."
msgstr ""
"Gagasan kunci di balik typestate adalah transisi state terjadi dengan "
"mengonsumsi suatu nilai dan menghasilkan nilai baru. Pada setiap langkah, "
"hanya operasi yang valid untuk state tersebut yang tersedia."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid "In this example:"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"We begin with a `Serializer`, which only allows us to start serializing a "
"struct."
msgstr ""
"Kami mulai dengan `Serializer`, yang hanya memungkinkan kami memulai "
"serialisasi struct."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"Once we call `.serialize_struct(...)`, ownership moves into a "
"`SerializeStruct` value. From that point on, we can only call methods "
"related to serializing struct fields."
msgstr ""
"Setelah kami memanggil `.serialize_struct(...)`, ownership berpindah ke "
"nilai `SerializeStruct`. Sejak saat itu, kami hanya dapat memanggil method "
"terkait serialisasi field struct."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"The original `Serializer` is no longer accessible — preventing us from "
"mixing modes (such as starting another _struct_ mid-struct) or calling "
"`finish()` too early."
msgstr ""
"`Serializer` asli tidak lagi dapat diakses — mencegah kami mencampur mode "
"(seperti memulai _struct_ lain di tengah struct) atau memanggil `finish()` "
"terlalu awal."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"Only after calling `.finish_struct()` do we receive the `Serializer` back. "
"At that point, the output can be finalized or reused."
msgstr ""
"Hanya setelah memanggil `.finish_struct()` kami menerima `Serializer` "
"kembali. Pada titik itu, output dapat difinalisasi atau digunakan kembali."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"If we forget to call `finish_struct()` and drop the `SerializeStruct` early,"
" the `Serializer` is also dropped. This ensures incomplete output cannot "
"leak into the system."
msgstr ""
"Jika kami lupa memanggil `finish_struct()` dan men-drop `SerializeStruct` "
"lebih awal, `Serializer` juga di-drop. Ini memastikan output yang tidak "
"lengkap tidak dapat bocor ke sistem."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-example.md
msgid ""
"By contrast, if we had implemented everything on `Serializer` directly — as "
"seen on the previous slide, nothing would stop someone from skipping "
"important steps or mixing serialization flows."
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, jika kami mengimplementasikan semuanya langsung pada "
"`Serializer` — seperti pada slide sebelumnya, tidak ada yang mencegah "
"seseorang melewati langkah penting atau mencampur alur serialisasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-advanced.md
msgid ""
"How do we manage increasingly complex configuration flows with many possible"
" states and transitions, while still preventing incompatible operations?"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana kita mengelola alur konfigurasi yang semakin kompleks dengan "
"banyak state dan transisi yang mungkin, sambil tetap mencegah operasi yang "
"tidak kompatibel?"

