#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/complete.md
msgid ""
"While this API is powerful, it’s not always ergonomic. Production "
"serializers typically favor simpler APIs and reserve the typestate pattern "
"for enforcing critical invariants."
msgstr ""
"Meskipun API ini ampuh, tidak selalu ergonomis. Serializer produksi biasanya"
" lebih memilih API yang lebih sederhana dan menyimpan pola typestate untuk "
"menegakkan invariant kritis."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern/typestate-generics/complete.md
msgid ""
"One excellent real-world example is "
"[`rustls::ClientConfig`](https://docs.rs/rustls/latest/rustls/client/struct.ClientConfig.html#method.builder),"
" which uses typestate with generics to guide the user through safe and "
"correct configuration steps."
msgstr ""
"Salah satu contoh nyata yang sangat baik adalah "
"[`rustls::ClientConfig`](https://docs.rs/rustls/latest/rustls/client/struct.ClientConfig.html#method.builder),"
" yang menggunakan typestate dengan generic untuk memandu pengguna melalui "
"langkah konfigurasi yang aman dan benar."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid "Using the Borrow checker to enforce Invariants"
msgstr "Menggunakan Borrow Checker untuk Menegakkan Invariant"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"The borrow checker, while added to enforce memory ownership, can model other"
" problems and prevent API misuse."
msgstr ""
"Borrow checker, meskipun ditambahkan untuk menegakkan ownership memori, "
"dapat memodelkan masalah lain dan mencegah penyalahgunaan API."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"/// Doors can be open or closed, and you need the right key to lock or unlock\n"
"/// one. Modelled with a Shared key and Owned door.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Doors can be open or closed, and you need the right key to lock or unlock\n"
"/// one. Modelled with a Shared key and Owned door.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
