msgstr "\"Door wasn't opened! Your key only opens locks with shape '{}'\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"We've seen the borrow checker prevent memory safety bugs (use-after-free, "
"data races)."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah melihat borrow checker mencegah bug keamanan memori (use-after-"
"free, data race)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"We've also used types to shape and restrict APIs already using [the "
"Typestate pattern](../leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md)."
msgstr ""
"Kita juga telah menggunakan tipe untuk membentuk dan membatasi API "
"menggunakan [pola Typestate](../leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-"
"pattern.md)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid "Language features are often introduced for a specific purpose."
msgstr "Fitur bahasa sering diperkenalkan untuk tujuan tertentu."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"Over time, users may develop ways of using a feature in ways that were not "
"predicted when they were introduced."
msgstr ""
"Seiring waktu, pengguna dapat mengembangkan cara menggunakan fitur yang "
"tidak diprediksi saat fitur tersebut diperkenalkan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"Java 5 introduced Generics in 2004 with the [main stated purpose of enabling"
" type-safe collections](https://jcp.org/en/jsr/detail?id=14)."
msgstr ""
"Java 5 memperkenalkan Generic pada 2004 dengan [tujuan utama yang dinyatakan"
" adalah memungkinkan koleksi type-"
"safe](https://jcp.org/en/jsr/detail?id=14)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"Adoption was slow at first, but some new projects began designing their APIs"
" around generics from the beginning."
msgstr ""
"Adopsinya awalnya lambat, tetapi beberapa proyek baru mulai merancang API "
"mereka dengan generic sejak awal."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"Since then, users and developers of the language expanded the use of "
"generics to other areas of type-safe API design:"
msgstr ""
"Sejak itu, pengguna dan developer bahasa tersebut memperluas penggunaan "
"generic ke area lain desain API type-safe:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"Class information can be held onto via Java's `Class<T>` or Guava's "
"`TypeToken<T>`."
msgstr ""
"Informasi class dapat disimpan melalui `Class<T>` Java atau `TypeToken<T>` "
"Guava."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid "The Builder pattern can be implemented using Recursive Generics."
msgstr "Pola Builder dapat diimplementasikan menggunakan Recursive Generic."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"We aim to do something similar here: Even though the borrow checker was "
"introduced to prevent use-after-free and data races, we treat it as just "
"another API design tool."
msgstr ""
"Kami bertujuan melakukan hal serupa di sini: Meskipun borrow checker "
"diperkenalkan untuk mencegah use-after-free dan data race, kami "
"memperlakukannya sebagai alat desain API biasa."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"It can be used to model program properties that have nothing to do with "
"preventing memory safety bugs."
msgstr ""
"Borrow checker dapat digunakan untuk memodelkan properti program yang tidak "
"ada hubungannya dengan mencegah bug keamanan memori."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"To use the borrow checker as a problem solving tool, we will need to "
"\"forget\" that the original purpose of it is to prevent mutable aliasing in"
" the context of preventing use-after-frees and data races."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menggunakan borrow checker sebagai alat pemecahan masalah, kita perlu "
"\"melupakan\" bahwa tujuan aslinya adalah mencegah aliasing mutable dalam "
"konteks mencegah use-after-free dan data race."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"We should imagine working within situations where the rules are the same but"
" the meaning is slightly different."
msgstr ""
"Kita sebaiknya membayangkan bekerja dalam situasi ketika aturannya sama "
"tetapi maknanya sedikit berbeda."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"This example uses ownership and borrowing are used to model the state of a "
"physical door."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini menggunakan ownership dan borrowing untuk memodelkan state pintu "
"fisik."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"`open_door` **consumes** a `LockedDoor` and returns a new `OpenDoor`. The "
"old `LockedDoor` value is no longer available."
msgstr ""
"`open_door` **mengonsumsi** `LockedDoor` dan mengembalikan `OpenDoor` baru. "
"Nilai `LockedDoor` lama tidak lagi tersedia."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"If the wrong key is used, the door is left locked. It is returned as an "
"`Err` case of the `Result`."
msgstr ""
"Jika kunci yang salah digunakan, pintu tetap terkunci. Hal ini dikembalikan "
"sebagai kasus `Err` dari `Result`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"It is a compile-time error to try and use a door that has already been "
"opened."
msgstr ""
"Mencoba menggunakan pintu yang sudah dibuka adalah error waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"Similarly, `lock_door` consumes an `OpenDoor`, preventing closing the door "
"twice at compile time."
msgstr ""
"Serupa dengan itu, `lock_door` mengonsumsi `OpenDoor`, mencegah menutup "
"pintu dua kali pada waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"The rules of the borrow checker exist to prevent memory safety bugs, but the"
" underlying logical system does not \"know\" what memory is."
msgstr ""
"Aturan borrow checker ada untuk mencegah bug keamanan memori, tetapi sistem "
"logika yang mendasarinya tidak \"mengetahui\" apa itu memori."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"All the borrow checker does is enforce a specific set of rules of how users "
"can order operations."
msgstr ""
"Yang dilakukan borrow checker hanyalah menegakkan serangkaian aturan "
"spesifik tentang bagaimana pengguna dapat mengurutkan operasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants.md
msgid ""
"This is just one case of piggy-backing onto the rules of the borrow checker "
"to design APIs to be harder or impossible to misuse."
msgstr ""
"Ini hanyalah satu kasus menumpang pada aturan borrow checker untuk merancang"
" API agar lebih sulit atau mustahil disalahgunakan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid "// An internal data type to have something to hold onto.\n"
msgstr "// An internal data type to have something to hold onto.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid "// The \"outer\" data.\n"
msgstr "// The \"outer\" data.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid "// let exclusive = exclusive_use(&mut value); // ❌🔨\n"
msgstr "// let exclusive = exclusive_use(&mut value); // ❌🔨\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid "// let shared = shared_use(&value); // ❌🔨\n"
msgstr "// let shared = shared_use(&value); // ❌🔨\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"This example re-frames the borrow checker rules away from references and "
"towards semantic meaning in non-memory-safety settings."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini membingkai ulang aturan borrow checker dari reference menuju "
"makna semantik dalam konteks non-keamanan memori."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid "Nothing is being mutated, nothing is being sent across threads."
msgstr "Tidak ada yang dimutasi, tidak ada yang dikirim antar-thread."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"In Rust's borrow checker we have access to three different ways of "
"\"taking\" a value:"
msgstr ""
"Dalam borrow checker Rust, kita memiliki akses ke tiga cara berbeda untuk "
"\"mengambil\" nilai:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"Owned value `T`. Value is dropped when the scope ends, unless it is not "
"returned to another scope."
msgstr ""
"Nilai owned `T`. Nilai di-drop saat scope berakhir, kecuali tidak "
"dikembalikan ke scope lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"Shared Reference `&T`. Allows aliasing but prevents mutable access while "
"shared references are in use."
msgstr ""
"Shared Reference `&T`. Memungkinkan aliasing tetapi mencegah akses mutable "
"selama shared reference digunakan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"Mutable Reference `&mut T`. Only one of these is allowed to exist for a "
"value at any one point, but can be used to create shared references."
msgstr ""
"Mutable Reference `&mut T`. Hanya satu yang diizinkan ada untuk suatu nilai "
"pada satu waktu, tetapi dapat digunakan untuk membuat shared reference."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"Ask: The two commented-out lines in the `demo` functions would cause "
"compilation errors, Why?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Dua baris yang dikomentari dalam fungsi `demo` akan menyebabkan "
"error kompilasi. Mengapa?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"`demo_exclusive`: Because the `shared` value is still aliased after the "
"`exclusive` reference is taken."
msgstr ""
"`demo_exclusive`: Karena nilai `shared` masih menjadi alias setelah "
"reference `exclusive` diambil."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"`demo_denied`: Because `value` is consumed the line before the "
"`shared_again_again` reference is taken from `&value`."
msgstr ""
"`demo_denied`: Karena `value` dikonsumsi pada baris sebelum reference "
"`shared_again_again` diambil dari `&value`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"Remember that every `&T` and `&mut T` has a lifetime, just one the user "
"doesn't have to annotate or think about most of the time."
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa setiap `&T` dan `&mut T` memiliki lifetime, hanya saja pengguna "
"tidak perlu menganotasi atau memikirkannya sebagian besar waktu."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md
msgid ""
"We rarely specify lifetimes because the Rust compiler allows us to _elide_ "
"them in most cases. See: [Lifetime Elision](../../../lifetimes/lifetime-"
"elision.md)"
msgstr ""
"Kami jarang menentukan lifetime karena compiler Rust memungkinkan kita "
"_menghilangkannya_ dalam sebagian besar kasus. Lihat: [Lifetime "
"Elision](../../../lifetimes/lifetime-elision.md)"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Sometimes we want values that _can only be used once_. One critical example "
"of this is in cryptography: A \"Nonce.\""
msgstr ""
"Kadang kita menginginkan nilai yang _hanya dapat digunakan sekali_. Salah "
"satu contoh kritisnya adalah dalam kriptografi: \"Nonce\"."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "/* specifics omitted */"
msgstr "/* specifics omitted */"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "/// A single-use number suitable for cryptographic purposes.\n"
msgstr "/// A single-use number suitable for cryptographic purposes.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "/// A cryptographically sound random generator function.\n"
msgstr "/// A cryptographically sound random generator function.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "// chosen by a fair dice roll, https://xkcd.com/221/\n"
msgstr "// chosen by a fair dice roll, https://xkcd.com/221/\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "/// Consume a nonce, but not the key or the data.\n"
msgstr "/// Consume a nonce, but not the key or the data.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "// The key and data can be re-used, copied, etc. but the nonce cannot.\n"
msgstr ""
"// The key and data can be re-used, copied, etc. but the nonce cannot.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "// encrypt(nonce, &key, &data_2); // 🛠️❌\n"
msgstr "// encrypt(nonce, &key, &data_2); // 🛠️❌\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "Problem: How can we guarantee a value is used only once?"
msgstr ""
"Masalah: Bagaimana kita dapat menjamin suatu nilai hanya digunakan sekali?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: A nonce is a piece of random, unique data used in cryptographic "
"protocols to prevent replay attacks."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Nonce adalah data acak dan unik yang digunakan dalam protokol "
"kriptografi untuk mencegah serangan replay."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Background: In practice people have ended up accidentally re-using nonces. "
"Most commonly, this causes the cryptographic protocol to completely break "
"down and stop fulfilling its function."
msgstr ""
"Latar belakang: Dalam praktik, orang pernah secara tidak sengaja menggunakan"
" ulang nonce. Paling umum, hal ini menyebabkan protokol kriptografi "
"sepenuhnya rusak dan berhenti menjalankan fungsinya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Depending on the specifics of nonce reuse and cryptography at hand, private "
"keys can also become computable by attackers."
msgstr ""
"Bergantung pada spesifikasi penggunaan ulang nonce dan kriptografi yang "
"digunakan, private key juga dapat menjadi dapat dihitung oleh penyerang."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Rust has an obvious tool for achieving the invariant \"Once you use this, "
"you can't use it again\": passing a value as an _owned argument_."
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki alat yang jelas untuk mencapai invariant \"Setelah Anda "
"menggunakan ini, Anda tidak dapat menggunakannya lagi\": meneruskan nilai "
"sebagai _argumen owned_."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Highlight: the `encrypt` function takes `nonce` by value (an owned "
"argument), but `key` and `data` by reference."
msgstr ""
"Soroti: fungsi `encrypt` menerima `nonce` by value (argumen owned), tetapi "
"`key` dan `data` by reference."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "The technique for single-use values is as follows:"
msgstr "Teknik untuk nilai sekali pakai adalah sebagai berikut:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Keep constructors private, so a user can't construct values with the same "
"inner value twice."
msgstr ""
"Jaga constructor tetap privat, agar pengguna tidak dapat membangun nilai "
"dengan nilai dalam yang sama dua kali."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Don't implement `Clone`/`Copy` traits or equivalent methods, so a user can't"
" duplicate data we want to keep unique."
msgstr ""
"Jangan mengimplementasikan trait `Clone`/`Copy` atau method setaranya, agar "
"pengguna tidak dapat menduplikasi data yang ingin kami jaga unik."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Make the interior type opaque (like with the newtype pattern), so the user "
"cannot modify an existing value on their own."
msgstr ""
"Buat tipe interior menjadi opaque (seperti pada pola newtype), agar pengguna"
" tidak dapat mengubah nilai yang ada sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "Ask: What are we missing from the newtype pattern in the slide's code?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Apa yang kurang dari pola newtype pada kode slide ini?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "Expect: Module boundary."
msgstr "Harapkan: Batas modul."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Without a module boundary a user can construct a nonce on their"
" own."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Tanpa batas modul, pengguna dapat membangun nonce sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid "Fix: Put `Key`, `Nonce`, and `new_nonce` behind a module."
msgstr "Perbaikan: Tempatkan `Key`, `Nonce`, dan `new_nonce` di balik modul."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/single-use-values.md
msgid ""
"Cryptography Nuance: A nonce might still be used twice if it was created "
"through pseudo-random process with no actual randomness. That can't be "
"prevented through this method. This API design prevents one nonce "
"duplication, but not all logic bugs."
msgstr ""
"Nuansa Kriptografi: Nonce masih mungkin digunakan dua kali jika dibuat "
"melalui proses pseudo-random tanpa keacakan sebenarnya. Hal itu tidak dapat "
"dicegah melalui metode ini. Desain API ini mencegah satu duplikasi nonce, "
"tetapi tidak semua bug logika."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/aliasing-xor-mutability.md
msgid ""
"We can use the mutual exclusion of `&T` and `&mut T` references to prevent "
"data from being used before it is ready."
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat menggunakan saling eksklusif antara reference `&T` dan `&mut T` "
"untuk mencegah data digunakan sebelum siap."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/aliasing-xor-mutability.md
