#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid ""
"Here we're using a type parameter and gating permissions behind \"tag\" "
"types that implement different permission traits."
msgstr ""
"Di sini kami menggunakan parameter tipe dan membatasi izin di balik tipe "
"\"tag\" yang mengimplementasikan trait izin berbeda."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid ""
"Tag types, or marker types, are zero-sized types that have some semantic "
"meaning to users and API designers."
msgstr ""
"Tag type, atau marker type, adalah tipe berukuran nol yang memiliki makna "
"semantik bagi pengguna dan perancang API."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid ""
"Ask: What issues does having it be an actual instance of that type pose?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Masalah apa yang timbul jika menjadikannya instance aktual dari "
"tipe tersebut?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid ""
"Answer: If it's not a zero-sized type (like `()` or `struct MyTag;`), then "
"we're allocating more memory than we need to when all we care for is type "
"information that is only relevant at compile-time."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban: Jika bukan tipe berukuran nol (seperti `()` atau `struct MyTag;`), "
"maka kita mengalokasikan memori lebih banyak dari yang diperlukan padahal "
"yang kita pedulikan hanyalah informasi tipe yang hanya relevan pada waktu "
"kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
