"Demonstrasikan: Buka komentar impor `PhantomData`, lalu buat `ChatId<T>` "
"menjadi berikut:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid ""
"`PhantomData<T>` is a zero-sized type with a type parameter. We can "
"construct values of it like other ZSTs with `let phantom: "
"PhantomData<UserTag> = PhantomData;` or with the `PhantomData::default()` "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"`PhantomData<T>` adalah tipe berukuran nol dengan parameter tipe. Kita dapat"
" membangun nilainya seperti ZST lain dengan `let phantom: "
"PhantomData<UserTag> = PhantomData;` atau dengan implementasi "
"`PhantomData::default()`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: implement `From<u64>` for `ChatId<T>`, emphasizing the "
"construction of `PhantomData`"
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: implementasikan `From<u64>` untuk `ChatId<T>`, dengan "
"menekankan konstruksi `PhantomData`"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid "// Or `PhantomData::default()`\n"
msgstr "// Or `PhantomData::default()`\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md
msgid ""
"`PhantomData` can be used as part of the Typestate pattern to have data with"
" the same structure but different methods, e.g., have `TaggedData<Start>` "
"implement methods or trait implementations that `TaggedData<End>` doesn't."
msgstr ""
"`PhantomData` dapat digunakan sebagai bagian dari pola Typestate untuk "
"memiliki data dengan struktur sama tetapi method berbeda, misalnya membuat "
"`TaggedData<Start>` mengimplementasikan method atau implementasi trait yang "
"tidak dimiliki `TaggedData<End>`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid "PhantomData 3/4: Lifetimes for External Resources"
msgstr "PhantomData 3/4: Lifetime untuk Resource Eksternal"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"The invariants of external resources often match what we can do with "
"lifetime rules."
msgstr ""
"Invariant resource eksternal sering sesuai dengan apa yang dapat kita "
"lakukan dengan aturan lifetime."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"/// Direct FFI to a database library in C.\n"
"/// We got this API as is, we have no influence over it.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Direct FFI to a database library in C.\n"
"/// We got this API as is, we have no influence over it.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid "// maximum 255 databases open at the same time\n"
msgstr "// maximum 255 databases open at the same time\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid "// ... etc.\n"
msgstr "// ... etc.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Remember the transaction API from the [Aliasing XOR Mutability](./aliasing-"
"xor-mutability.md) example."
msgstr ""
"Ingat API transaksi dari contoh [Aliasing XOR Mutability](./aliasing-xor-"
"mutability.md)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"We held onto a mutable reference to the database connection within the "
"transaction type to lock out the database while a transaction is active."
msgstr ""
"Kami menyimpan reference mutable ke koneksi database di dalam tipe transaksi"
" untuk mengunci database selama transaksi aktif."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"In this example, we want to implement a `Transaction` API on top of an "
"external, non-Rust API."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, kami ingin mengimplementasikan API `Transaction` di atas "
"API eksternal non-Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"We start by defining a `Transaction` type that holds onto `&mut "
"DatabaseConnection`."
msgstr ""
"Kami mulai dengan mendefinisikan tipe `Transaction` yang menyimpan `&mut "
"DatabaseConnection`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Ask: What are the limits of this implementation? Assume the `u8` is accurate"
" implementation-wise and enough information for us to use the external API."
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Apa batasan implementasi ini? Asumsikan `u8` akurat dari segi "
"implementasi dan cukup informasinya bagi kami untuk menggunakan API "
"eksternal."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Indirection takes up 7 bytes more than we need to on a 64-bit platform, as "
"well as costing a pointer dereference at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Indirection memakan 7 byte lebih banyak dari yang diperlukan pada platform "
"64-bit, serta membutuhkan dereference pointer pada runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Problem: We want the transaction to borrow the database connection that "
"created it, but we don't want the `Transaction` object to store a real "
"reference."
msgstr ""
"Masalah: Kami ingin transaksi meminjam koneksi database yang membuatnya, "
"tetapi kami tidak ingin objek `Transaction` menyimpan reference sungguhan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Ask: What happens when we remove the mutable reference in `Transaction` "
"while keeping the lifetime parameter?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Apa yang terjadi jika kita menghapus reference mutable di "
"`Transaction` sambil mempertahankan parameter lifetime?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid "Expect: Unused lifetime parameter!"
msgstr "Harapkan: Parameter lifetime tidak digunakan!"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Like with the type tagging from the previous slides, we can bring in "
"`PhantomData` to capture this unused lifetime parameter for us."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada type tagging dari slide sebelumnya, kita dapat menggunakan "
"`PhantomData` untuk menangkap parameter lifetime yang tidak digunakan ini."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"The difference is that we will need to use the lifetime alongside another "
"type, but that other type does not matter too much."
msgstr ""
"Perbedaannya adalah kita perlu menggunakan lifetime bersama tipe lain, "
"tetapi tipe lain itu tidak terlalu penting."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid "Demonstrate: change `Transaction` to the following:"
msgstr "Demonstrasikan: ubah `Transaction` menjadi berikut:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid "Update the `DatabaseConnection::new_transaction()` method:"
msgstr "Perbarui method `DatabaseConnection::new_transaction()`:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"This gives an owned database connection that is tied to the "
"`DatabaseConnection` that created it, but with less runtime memory footprint"
" that the store-a-reference version did."
msgstr ""
"Ini memberikan koneksi database owned yang terikat pada `DatabaseConnection`"
" yang membuatnya, tetapi dengan jejak memori runtime lebih kecil daripada "
"versi yang menyimpan reference."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Because `PhantomData` is a zero-sized type (like `()` or `struct "
"MyZeroSizedType;`), the size of `Transaction` is now the same as `u8`."
msgstr ""
"Karena `PhantomData` adalah tipe berukuran nol (seperti `()` atau `struct "
"MyZeroSizedType;`), ukuran `Transaction` sekarang sama dengan `u8`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"The implementation that held onto a reference instead was as large as a "
"`usize`."
msgstr ""
"Implementasi yang menyimpan reference sebaliknya berukuran sebesar `usize`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"This way of encoding relationships between types and values is very powerful"
" when combined with unsafe, as the ways one can manipulate lifetimes becomes"
" almost arbitrary. This is also dangerous, but when combined with tools like"
" external, mechanically-verified proofs we can safely encode cyclic/self-"
"referential types while encoding lifetime & safety expectations in the "
"relevant data types."
msgstr ""
"Cara mengodekan hubungan antara tipe dan nilai ini sangat ampuh bila "
"dikombinasikan dengan unsafe, karena cara seseorang memanipulasi lifetime "
"menjadi hampir arbitrer. Ini juga berbahaya, tetapi bila dikombinasikan "
"dengan alat seperti bukti eksternal yang diverifikasi secara mekanis, kita "
"dapat dengan aman mengodekan tipe siklik/self-referential sekaligus "
"mengodekan ekspektasi lifetime & keamanan pada tipe data terkait."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-03-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"The [GhostCell (2021)](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/) paper "
"and its [relevant implementation](https://gitlab.mpi-sws.org/FP/ghostcell) "
"show this kind of work off. While the borrow checker is restrictive, there "
"are still ways to use escape hatches and then _show that the ways you used "
"those escape hatches are consistent and safe._"
msgstr ""
"Paper [GhostCell (2021)](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/) dan "
"[implementasi terkaitnya](https://gitlab.mpi-sws.org/FP/ghostcell) "
"memamerkan jenis pekerjaan ini. Meskipun borrow checker membatasi, masih ada"
" cara menggunakan escape hatch lalu _menunjukkan bahwa cara Anda menggunakan"
" escape hatch tersebut konsisten dan aman._"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "PhantomData 4/4: OwnedFd & BorrowedFd"
msgstr "PhantomData 4/4: OwnedFd & BorrowedFd"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "`BorrowedFd` is a prime example of `PhantomData` in action."
msgstr "`BorrowedFd` adalah contoh utama `PhantomData` dalam aksi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"// Create a file with a raw syscall with write-only and create "
"permissions.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Create a file with a raw syscall with write-only and create "
"permissions.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "\"c_str.txt\""
msgstr "\"c_str.txt\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"// Pass the ownership of an integer file descriptor to an `OwnedFd`.\n"
"    // `OwnedFd::drop()` closes the file descriptor.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Pass the ownership of an integer file descriptor to an `OwnedFd`.\n"
"    // `OwnedFd::drop()` closes the file descriptor.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "\"Could not open file with syscall!\""
msgstr "\"Could not open file with syscall!\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"// Create a `BorrowedFd` from an `OwnedFd`.\n"
"    // `BorrowedFd::drop()` does not close the file because it doesn't own it!\n"
msgstr ""
"// Create a `BorrowedFd` from an `OwnedFd`.\n"
"    // `BorrowedFd::drop()` does not close the file because it doesn't own it!\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "// std::mem::drop(owned_fd); // ❌🔨\n"
msgstr "// std::mem::drop(owned_fd); // ❌🔨\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "// owned_fd will be dropped here, and the file will be closed.\n"
msgstr "// owned_fd will be dropped here, and the file will be closed.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "A file descriptor represents a specific process's access to a file."
msgstr ""
"File descriptor merepresentasikan akses proses tertentu ke suatu berkas."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"Reminder: Device and OS-specific features are exposed as if they were files "
"on unix-style systems."
msgstr ""
"Pengingat: Perangkat dan fitur spesifik OS diekspos seolah-olah sebagai "
"berkas pada sistem bergaya unix."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"[`OwnedFd`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3128-io-safety.html#ownedfd-"
"and-borrowedfdfd) is an owned wrapper type for a file descriptor. It _owns_ "
"the file descriptor, and closes it when dropped."
msgstr ""
"[`OwnedFd`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3128-io-safety.html#ownedfd-"
"and-borrowedfdfd) adalah tipe wrapper owned untuk file descriptor. Tipe ini "
"_memiliki_ file descriptor, dan menutupnya saat di-drop."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"Note: We have our own implementation of it here, draw attention to the "
"explicit `Drop` implementation."
msgstr ""
"Catatan: Kami memiliki implementasinya sendiri di sini; tarik perhatian ke "
"implementasi `Drop` eksplisit."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"`BorrowedFd` is its borrowed counterpart, it does not need to close the file"
" when it is dropped."
msgstr ""
"`BorrowedFd` adalah pasangan pinjamannya; tipe ini tidak perlu menutup "
"berkas saat di-drop."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid "Note: We have not explicitly implemented `Drop` for `BorrowedFd`."
msgstr ""
"Catatan: Kami tidak mengimplementasikan `Drop` secara eksplisit untuk "
"`BorrowedFd`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"`BorrowedFd` uses a lifetime captured with a `PhantomData` to enforce the "
"invariant \"if this file descriptor exists, the OS file descriptor is still "
"open even though it is not responsible for closing that file descriptor.\""
msgstr ""
"`BorrowedFd` menggunakan lifetime yang ditangkap dengan `PhantomData` untuk "
"menegakkan invariant \"jika file descriptor ini ada, file descriptor OS "
"masih terbuka meskipun tipe ini tidak bertanggung jawab menutup file "
"descriptor tersebut.\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"The lifetime parameter of `BorrowedFd` demands that there exists another "
"value in your program that lasts as long as that specific `BorrowedFd` or "
"outlives it (in this case an `OwnedFd`)."
msgstr ""
"Parameter lifetime `BorrowedFd` menuntut adanya nilai lain dalam program "
"Anda yang bertahan selama `BorrowedFd` tersebut atau lebih lama (dalam kasus"
" ini `OwnedFd`)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Uncomment the `std::mem::drop(owned_fd)` line and try to "
"compile to show that `borrowed_fd` relies on the lifetime of `owned_fd`."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Buka komentar baris `std::mem::drop(owned_fd)` dan coba "
"kompilasi untuk menunjukkan bahwa `borrowed_fd` bergantung pada lifetime "
"`owned_fd`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"This has been encoded by the API designers to mean _that other value is what"
" keeps the access to the file open_."
msgstr ""
"Hal ini telah dikodekan oleh perancang API untuk berarti _nilai lain itulah "
"yang menjaga akses ke berkas tetap terbuka_."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md
msgid ""
"Because Rust's borrow checker enforces this relationship where one value "
"must last at least as long as another, users of this API do not need to "
"worry about handling this correct file descriptor aliasing and closing logic"
" themselves."
msgstr ""
"Karena borrow checker Rust menegakkan hubungan ini ketika satu nilai harus "
"bertahan setidaknya selama nilai lain, pengguna API ini tidak perlu khawatir"
" menangani logika aliasing dan penutupan file descriptor yang benar sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"Types with private constructors can be used to act as proof of invariants."
msgstr ""
"Tipe dengan constructor privat dapat digunakan sebagai bukti invariant."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid "// A public type with private fields behind a module boundary.\n"
msgstr "// A public type with private fields behind a module boundary.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid "\"We have a token, so we can make assumptions.\""
msgstr "\"We have a token, so we can make assumptions.\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid "// We have a token, so we can do this work.\n"
msgstr "// We have a token, so we can do this work.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid "// We could not get a token, so we can't call `protected_work`.\n"
msgstr "// We could not get a token, so we can't call `protected_work`.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: We want to be able to restrict user's access to functionality "
"until they've performed a specific task."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Kami ingin dapat membatasi akses pengguna ke fungsionalitas hingga"
" mereka melakukan tugas tertentu."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"We can do this by defining a type the API consumer cannot construct on their"
" own, through the privacy rules of structs and modules."
msgstr ""
"Kami dapat melakukannya dengan mendefinisikan tipe yang tidak dapat dibangun"
" sendiri oleh konsumen API, melalui aturan privasi struct dan modul."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"[Newtypes](./newtype-pattern.md) use the privacy rules in a similar way, to "
"restrict construction unless a value is guaranteed to hold up an invariant "
"at runtime."
msgstr ""
"[Newtype](./newtype-pattern.md) menggunakan aturan privasi dengan cara "
"serupa, untuk membatasi konstruksi kecuali suatu nilai dijamin "
"mempertahankan invariant pada runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid "Ask: What is the purpose of the `proof: ()` field here?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Apa tujuan field `proof: ()` di sini?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"Without `proof: ()`, `Token` would have no private fields and users would be"
" able to construct values of `Token` arbitrarily."
msgstr ""
"Tanpa `proof: ()`, `Token` tidak akan memiliki field privat dan pengguna "
"dapat membangun nilai `Token` secara arbitrer."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Try to construct the token manually in `main` and show the "
"compilation error. Demonstrate: Remove the `proof` field from `Token` to "
"show how users would be able to construct `Token` if it had no private "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Coba bangun token secara manual di `main` dan tunjukkan "
"error kompilasinya. Demonstrasikan: Hapus field `proof` dari `Token` untuk "
"menunjukkan bagaimana pengguna dapat membangun `Token` jika tidak memiliki "
"field privat."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"By putting the `Token` type behind a module boundary (`token`), users "
"outside that module can't construct the value on their own as they don't "
"have permission to access the `proof` field."
msgstr ""
"Dengan menempatkan tipe `Token` di balik batas modul (`token`), pengguna di "
"luar modul tersebut tidak dapat membangun nilainya sendiri karena mereka "
"tidak memiliki izin mengakses field `proof`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"The API developer gets to define methods and functions that produce these "
"tokens. The user does not."
msgstr ""
"Developer API yang berhak mendefinisikan method dan fungsi yang menghasilkan"
" token ini. Pengguna tidak."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"The token becomes a proof that one has met the API developer's conditions of"
" access for those tokens."
msgstr ""
"Token menjadi bukti bahwa seseorang telah memenuhi kondisi akses developer "
"API untuk token tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"Ask: How might an API developer accidentally introduce ways to circumvent "
"this?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Bagaimana developer API dapat secara tidak sengaja memperkenalkan "
"cara untuk melewati ini?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types.md
msgid ""
"Expect answers like \"serialization implementations\", other parser/\"from "
"string\" implementations, or an implementation of `Default`."
msgstr ""
"Harapkan jawaban seperti \"implementasi serialisasi\", implementasi "
"parser/\"from string\" lain, atau implementasi `Default`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid "Token types work well as a proof of checked permission."
msgstr "Tipe token berfungsi baik sebagai bukti izin yang telah diperiksa."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid ""
"// We don't have to check that we have permissions, because\n"
"// the AdminToken argument is equivalent to such a check.\n"
msgstr ""
"// We don't have to check that we have permissions, because\n"
"// the AdminToken argument is equivalent to such a check.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid "\"CoolUser\""
msgstr "\"CoolUser\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid "\"Incorrect password! Could not prove privileges.\""
msgstr "\"Incorrect password! Could not prove privileges.\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid ""
"This example shows modelling gaining administrator privileges for a chat "
"client with a password and giving a user a moderator rank once those "
"privileges are gained. The `AdminToken` type acts as \"proof of correct user"
" privileges.\""
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini menunjukkan pemodelan perolehan hak administrator untuk client "
"chat dengan password dan pemberian peran moderator kepada pengguna setelah "
"hak tersebut diperoleh. Tipe `AdminToken` berperan sebagai \"bukti hak "
"pengguna yang benar.\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid ""
"The user asked for a password in-code and if we get the password correct, we"
" get a `AdminToken` to perform administrator actions within a specific "
"environment (here, a chat client)."
msgstr ""
"Pengguna diminta memasukkan password dalam kode, dan jika password benar, "
"kami mendapatkan `AdminToken` untuk melakukan tindakan administrator dalam "
"lingkungan tertentu (di sini, client chat)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid ""
"Once the permissions are gained, we can call the `add_moderator` function."
msgstr "Setelah izin diperoleh, kami dapat memanggil fungsi `add_moderator`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid ""
"We can't call that function without the token type, so by being able to call"
" it at all all we can assume we have permissions."
msgstr ""
"Kami tidak dapat memanggil fungsi tersebut tanpa tipe token, jadi karena "
"dapat memanggilnya sama sekali, kita dapat mengasumsikan kami memiliki izin."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/permission-tokens.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Try to construct the `AdminToken` in `main` again to reiterate "
"that the foundation of useful tokens is preventing their arbitrary "
"construction."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Coba bangun `AdminToken` di `main` lagi untuk menegaskan "
"bahwa fondasi token yang berguna adalah mencegah konstruksi arbitrer-nya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"Sometimes, a token type needs additional data. A mutex guard is an example "
"of a token that represents permission + data."
msgstr ""
"Kadang, tipe token memerlukan data tambahan. Mutex guard adalah contoh token"
" yang merepresentasikan izin + data."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid "// The acquired MutexGuard is proof of exclusive access.\n"
msgstr "// The acquired MutexGuard is proof of exclusive access.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"Mutexes enforce mutual exclusion of read/write access to a value. We've "
"covered Mutexes earlier in this course already (See: RAII/Mutex), but here "
"we're looking at `MutexGuard` specifically."
msgstr ""
"Mutex menegakkan mutual exclusion akses baca/tulis ke suatu nilai. Kami "
"telah membahas Mutex sebelumnya dalam kursus ini (Lihat: RAII/Mutex), tetapi"
" di sini kami melihat `MutexGuard` secara khusus."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"`MutexGuard` is a value generated by a `Mutex` that proves you have "
"read/write access at that point in time."
msgstr ""
"`MutexGuard` adalah nilai yang dihasilkan `Mutex` yang membuktikan Anda "
"memiliki akses baca/tulis pada titik waktu tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"`MutexGuard` also holds onto a reference to the `Mutex` that generated it, "
"with `Deref` and `DerefMut` implementations that give access to the data of "
"`Mutex` while the underlying `Mutex` keeps that data private from the user."
msgstr ""
"`MutexGuard` juga menyimpan reference ke `Mutex` yang menghasilkannya, "
"dengan implementasi `Deref` dan `DerefMut` yang memberikan akses ke data "
"`Mutex` sementara `Mutex` yang mendasarinya menjaga data tersebut tetap "
"privat dari pengguna."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"If `mutex.lock()` does not return a `MutexGuard`, you don't have permission "
"to change the value within the mutex."
msgstr ""
"Jika `mutex.lock()` tidak mengembalikan `MutexGuard`, Anda tidak memiliki "
"izin untuk mengubah nilai di dalam mutex."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"Not only do you have no permission, but you have no means to access the "
"mutex data unless you gain a `MutexGuard`."
msgstr ""
"Anda tidak hanya tidak memiliki izin, tetapi juga tidak memiliki cara "
"mengakses data mutex kecuali memperoleh `MutexGuard`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"This contrasts with C++, where mutexes and lock guards do not control access"
" to the data itself, acting only as a flag that a user must remember to "
"check every time they read or manipulate data."
msgstr ""
"Ini berbeda dari C++, ketika mutex dan lock guard tidak mengontrol akses ke "
"data itu sendiri, hanya berperan sebagai flag yang harus diingat pengguna "
"untuk diperiksa setiap kali membaca atau memanipulasi data."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/mutex-guard.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: make the `mutex` variable mutable then try to dereference it to"
" change its value. Show how there's no deref implementation for it, and no "
"other way to get to the data held by it other than getting a mutex guard."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: buat variabel `mutex` menjadi mutable lalu coba lakukan "
"dereference untuk mengubah nilainya. Tunjukkan bahwa tidak ada implementasi "
"deref untuknya, dan tidak ada cara lain untuk mencapai data yang dipegangnya"
" selain memperoleh mutex guard."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid "Variable-Specific Tokens (Branding 1/4)"
msgstr "Token Khusus Variabel (Branding 1/4)"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid "What if we want to tie a token to a specific variable?"
msgstr "Bagaimana jika kita ingin mengikat token ke variabel tertentu?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid "// Works fine!\n"
msgstr "// Works fine!\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"// let data_2 = Bytes { bytes: vec![0, 1] };\n"
"        // data_2.get_proven(&token_1); // Panics! Can we prevent this?\n"
msgstr ""
"// let data_2 = Bytes { bytes: vec![0, 1] };\n"
"        // data_2.get_proven(&token_1); // Panics! Can we prevent this?\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"What if we want to tie a token to a _specific variable_ in our code? Can we "
"do this in Rust's type system?"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana jika kita ingin mengikat token ke _variabel tertentu_ dalam kode "
"kita? Dapatkah kita melakukannya dalam sistem tipe Rust?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: We want to have a Token Type that represents a known, valid "
"index into a byte array."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Kami ingin memiliki Token Type yang merepresentasikan indeks yang "
"diketahui dan valid ke dalam array byte."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"Once we have these proven indexes we would be able to avoid bounds checks "
"entirely, as the tokens would act as the _proof of an existing index_."
msgstr ""
"Setelah memiliki indeks yang terbukti ini, kami dapat sepenuhnya menghindari"
" pemeriksaan bounds, karena token akan berperan sebagai _bukti indeks yang "
"ada_."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"Since the index is known to be valid, `get_proven()` can skip the bounds "
"check."
msgstr ""
"Karena indeks diketahui valid, `get_proven()` dapat melewati pemeriksaan "
"bounds."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"In this example there's nothing stopping the proven index of one array being"
" used on a different array. If an index is out of bounds in this case, it is"
" undefined behavior."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini tidak ada yang mencegah indeks terbukti dari satu array "
"digunakan pada array berbeda. Jika indeks di luar bounds dalam kasus ini, "
"itu adalah undefined behavior."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid "Demonstrate: Uncomment the `data_2.get_proven(&token_1);` line."
msgstr "Demonstrasikan: Buka komentar baris `data_2.get_proven(&token_1);`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"The code here panics! We want to prevent this \"crossover\" of token types "
"for indexes at compile time."
msgstr ""
"Kode di sini panic! Kami ingin mencegah \"crossover\" tipe token untuk "
"indeks ini pada waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid "Ask: How might we try to do this?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Bagaimana kita dapat mencoba melakukannya?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"Expect students to not reach a good implementation from this, but be willing"
" to experiment and follow through on suggestions."
msgstr ""
"Harapkan siswa tidak mencapai implementasi yang baik dari ini, tetapi "
"bersedia bereksperimen dan menindaklanjuti saran."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid "Ask: What are the alternatives, why are they not good enough?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Apa alternatifnya, mengapa alternatif tersebut tidak cukup baik?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"Expect runtime checking of index bounds, especially as both `Vec::get` and "
"`Bytes::get_index` already uses runtime checking."
msgstr ""
"Harapkan pemeriksaan bounds indeks pada runtime, terutama karena `Vec::get` "
"dan `Bytes::get_index` sudah menggunakan pemeriksaan runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"Runtime bounds checking does not prevent the erroneous crossover in the "
"first place, it only guarantees a panic."
msgstr ""
"Pemeriksaan bounds runtime tidak mencegah crossover yang keliru sejak awal; "
"pemeriksaan itu hanya menjamin panic."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"The kind of token-association we will be doing here is called Branding. This"
" is an advanced technique that expands applicability of token types to more "
"API designs."
msgstr ""
"Jenis asosiasi token yang akan kami lakukan di sini disebut Branding. Ini "
"adalah teknik lanjutan yang memperluas penerapan tipe token ke lebih banyak "
"desain API."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-01-motivation.md
msgid ""
"[`GhostCell`](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/paper.pdf) is a "
"prominent user of this, later slides will touch on it."
msgstr ""
"[`GhostCell`](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/paper.pdf) adalah "
"pengguna terkemuka teknik ini; slide berikutnya akan menyinggungnya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "`PhantomData` and Lifetime Subtyping (Branding 2/4)"
msgstr "`PhantomData` dan Lifetime Subtyping (Branding 2/4)"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "Idea:"
msgstr "Ide:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "Use a lifetime as a unique brand for each token."
msgstr "Gunakan lifetime sebagai brand unik untuk setiap token."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Make lifetimes sufficiently distinct so that they don't implicitly convert "
"into each other."
msgstr ""
"Buat lifetime cukup berbeda sehingga tidak secara implisit dikonversi satu "
"sama lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "// The main focus\n"
msgstr "// The main focus\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "// We want this to NOT compile\n"
msgstr "// We want this to NOT compile\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "In Rust, lifetimes can have subtyping relations between one another."
msgstr "Di Rust, lifetime dapat memiliki hubungan subtyping satu sama lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"This kind of relation allows the compiler to determine if one lifetime "
"outlives another."
msgstr ""
"Hubungan semacam ini memungkinkan compiler menentukan apakah satu lifetime "
"hidup lebih lama dari yang lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Determining if a lifetime outlives another also allows us to say _the "
"shortest common lifetime is the one that ends first_."
msgstr ""
"Menentukan apakah suatu lifetime hidup lebih lama dari yang lain juga "
"memungkinkan kita mengatakan _lifetime bersama terpendek adalah yang "
"berakhir lebih dahulu_."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"This is useful in many cases, as it means two different lifetimes can be "
"treated as if they were the same in the regions they do overlap."
msgstr ""
"Ini berguna dalam banyak kasus, karena berarti dua lifetime berbeda dapat "
"diperlakukan seolah-olah sama di region tempat keduanya tumpang tindih."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"This is usually what we want. But here we want to use lifetimes as a way to "
"distinguish values so we say that a token only applies to a single variable "
"without having to create a newtype for every single variable we declare."
msgstr ""
"Ini biasanya yang kita inginkan. Tetapi di sini kami ingin menggunakan "
"lifetime sebagai cara membedakan nilai, sehingga kami mengatakan token hanya"
" berlaku untuk satu variabel tanpa harus membuat newtype untuk setiap "
"variabel yang dideklarasikan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"**Goal**: We want two lifetimes that the Rust compiler cannot determine if "
"one outlives the other."
msgstr ""
"**Tujuan**: Kami menginginkan dua lifetime yang tidak dapat ditentukan "
"compiler Rust apakah salah satunya hidup lebih lama dari yang lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"We are using `try_coerce_lifetimes` as a compile-time check to see if the "
"lifetimes have a common shorter lifetime (AKA being subtyped)."
msgstr ""
"Kami menggunakan `try_coerce_lifetimes` sebagai pemeriksaan waktu kompilasi "
"untuk melihat apakah lifetime memiliki lifetime bersama yang lebih pendek "
"(alias di-subtype)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Note: This slide compiles, by the end of this slide it should only compile "
"when `try_coerce_lifetimes` is commented out."
msgstr ""
"Catatan: Slide ini dapat dikompilasi; pada akhir slide ini, kode seharusnya "
"hanya dapat dikompilasi ketika `try_coerce_lifetimes` dikomentari."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "There are two important parts of this code:"
msgstr "Ada dua bagian penting dari kode ini:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"The `impl for<'a>` bound on the closure passed to `lifetime_separator`."
msgstr ""
"Bound `impl for<'a>` pada closure yang diteruskan ke `lifetime_separator`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "The way lifetimes are used in the parameter for `PhantomData`."
msgstr "Cara lifetime digunakan pada parameter untuk `PhantomData`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "`for<'a>` bound on a Closure"
msgstr "Bound `for<'a>` pada Closure"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"We are using `for<'a>` as a way of introducing a lifetime generic parameter "
"to a function type and asking that the body of the function to work for all "
"possible lifetimes."
msgstr ""
"Kami menggunakan `for<'a>` sebagai cara memperkenalkan parameter generic "
"lifetime pada tipe fungsi dan meminta isi fungsi bekerja untuk semua "
"lifetime yang mungkin."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"What this also does is remove some ability of the compiler to make "
"assumptions about that specific lifetime for the function argument, as it "
"must meet Rust's borrow checking rules regardless of the \"real\" lifetime "
"its arguments are going to have. The caller is substituting in actual "
"lifetime, the function itself cannot."
msgstr ""
"Ini juga menghilangkan sebagian kemampuan compiler untuk membuat asumsi "
"tentang lifetime spesifik tersebut bagi argumen fungsi, karena fungsi harus "
"memenuhi aturan borrow checking Rust terlepas dari lifetime \"nyata\" yang "
"akan dimiliki argumennya. Pemanggil yang menggantikan lifetime aktual; "
"fungsi itu sendiri tidak dapat."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"This is analogous to a forall (Ɐ) quantifier in mathematics, or the way we "
"introduce `<T>` as type variables, but only for lifetimes in trait bounds."
msgstr ""
"Ini analog dengan kuantifier forall (Ɐ) dalam matematika, atau cara kami "
"memperkenalkan `<T>` sebagai variabel tipe, tetapi hanya untuk lifetime "
"dalam trait bound."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"When we write a function generic over a type `T`, we can't determine that "
"type from within the function itself. Even if we call a function `fn foo<T, "
"U>(first: T, second: U)` with two arguments of the same type, the body of "
"this function cannot determine if `T` and `U` are the same type."
msgstr ""
"Saat menulis fungsi generic atas tipe `T`, kita tidak dapat menentukan tipe "
"itu dari dalam fungsi itu sendiri. Bahkan jika kita memanggil fungsi `fn "
"foo<T, U>(first: T, second: U)` dengan dua argumen bertipe sama, body fungsi"
" ini tidak dapat menentukan apakah `T` dan `U` adalah tipe yang sama."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"This also prevents _the API consumer_ from defining a lifetime themselves, "
"which would allow them to circumvent the restrictions we want to impose."
msgstr ""
"Ini juga mencegah _konsumen API_ mendefinisikan lifetime sendiri, yang akan "
"memungkinkan mereka melewati batasan yang ingin kami terapkan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "PhantomData and Lifetime Variance"
msgstr "PhantomData dan Lifetime Variance"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"We already know `PhantomData`, which can introduce a formal no-op usage of "
"an otherwise unused type or a lifetime parameter."
msgstr ""
"Kita sudah mengenal `PhantomData`, yang dapat memperkenalkan penggunaan no-"
"op formal atas tipe atau parameter lifetime yang sebenarnya tidak digunakan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "Ask: What can we do with `PhantomData`?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Apa yang dapat kita lakukan dengan `PhantomData`?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Expect mentions of the Typestate pattern, tying together the lifetimes of "
"owned values."
msgstr "Harapkan penyebutan pola Typestate, mengikat lifetime nilai owned."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "Ask: In other languages, what is subtyping?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Dalam bahasa lain, apa itu subtyping?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Expect mentions of inheritance, being able to use a value of type `B` when a"
" asked for a value of type `A` because `B` is a \"subtype\" of `A`."
msgstr ""
"Harapkan penyebutan inheritance, kemampuan menggunakan nilai bertipe `B` "
"ketika diminta nilai bertipe `A` karena `B` adalah \"subtype\" dari `A`."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid "Rust does have Subtyping! But only for lifetimes."
msgstr "Rust memang memiliki Subtyping! Tetapi hanya untuk lifetime."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Ask: If one lifetime is a subtype of another lifetime, what might that mean?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Jika satu lifetime adalah subtype dari lifetime lain, apa artinya?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"A lifetime is a \"subtype\" of another lifetime when it _outlives_ that "
"other lifetime."
msgstr ""
"Suatu lifetime adalah \"subtype\" dari lifetime lain ketika lifetime "
"tersebut _hidup lebih lama_ dari lifetime lainnya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"The way that lifetimes used by `PhantomData` behave depends not only on "
"where the lifetime \"comes from\" but on how the reference is defined too."
msgstr ""
"Cara lifetime yang digunakan `PhantomData` berperilaku tidak hanya "
"bergantung pada dari mana lifetime itu \"berasal\", tetapi juga pada "
"bagaimana reference didefinisikan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"The reason this compiles is that the [**Variance**](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/subtyping.html#r-subtyping.variance) of the "
"lifetime inside of `InvariantLifetime` is too lenient."
msgstr ""
"Alasan kode ini dapat dikompilasi adalah [**Variance**](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/subtyping.html#r-subtyping.variance) lifetime di "
"dalam `InvariantLifetime` terlalu longgar."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Note: Do not expect to get students to understand variance entirely here, "
"just treat it as a kind of ladder of restrictiveness on the ability of "
"lifetimes to establish subtyping relations."
msgstr ""
"Catatan: Jangan mengharapkan siswa sepenuhnya memahami variance di sini; "
"perlakukan ini sebagai semacam tangga keketatan terhadap kemampuan lifetime "
"membentuk hubungan subtyping."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Ask: How can we make it more restrictive? How do we make a reference type "
"more restrictive in Rust?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Bagaimana kita dapat membuatnya lebih ketat? Bagaimana kita "
"membuat tipe reference lebih ketat di Rust?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Expect or demonstrate: Making it `&'id mut ()` instead. This will not be "
"enough!"
msgstr ""
"Harapkan atau demonstrasikan: Membuatnya menjadi `&'id mut ()`. Ini tidak "
"akan cukup!"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"We need to use a [**Variance**](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/subtyping.html#r-subtyping.variance) on lifetimes "
"where subtyping cannot be inferred except on _identical lifetimes_. That is,"
" the only subtype of `'a` the compiler can know is `'a` itself."
msgstr ""
"Kita perlu menggunakan [**Variance**](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/reference/subtyping.html#r-subtyping.variance) pada lifetime"
" di mana subtyping tidak dapat disimpulkan kecuali pada _lifetime yang "
"identik_. Artinya, satu-satunya subtype `'a` yang dapat diketahui compiler "
"adalah `'a` itu sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Note: Again, do not try to get the whole class to understand variance. Treat"
" it as a ladder of restrictiveness for now."
msgstr ""
"Catatan: Sekali lagi, jangan mencoba membuat seluruh kelas memahami "
"variance. Untuk saat ini, perlakukan ini sebagai tangga keketatan."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Move from `&'id ()` (covariant in lifetime and type), `&'id mut"
" ()` (covariant in lifetime, invariant in type), `*mut &'id mut ()` "
"(invariant in lifetime and type), and finally `*mut &'id ()` (invariant in "
"lifetime but not type)."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Bergerak dari `&'id ()` (covariant pada lifetime dan tipe), "
"`&'id mut ()` (covariant pada lifetime, invariant pada tipe), `*mut &'id mut"
" ()` (invariant pada lifetime dan tipe), dan akhirnya `*mut &'id ()` "
"(invariant pada lifetime tetapi tidak pada tipe)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Those last two should not compile, which means we've finally found "
"candidates for how to bind lifetimes to `PhantomData` so they can't be "
"compared to one another in this context."
msgstr ""
"Dua yang terakhir seharusnya tidak dapat dikompilasi, yang berarti kita "
"akhirnya menemukan kandidat cara mengikat lifetime ke `PhantomData` sehingga"
" keduanya tidak dapat dibandingkan satu sama lain dalam konteks ini."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Reason: `*mut` means [mutable raw pointer](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/types/pointer.html#r-type.pointer.raw). Rust has mutable "
"pointers! But you cannot reason about them in safe Rust. Making this a "
"mutable raw pointer to a reference that has a lifetime complicates the "
"compiler's ability subtype because it cannot reason about mutable raw "
"pointers within the borrow checker."
msgstr ""
"Alasan: `*mut` berarti [mutable raw pointer](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/types/pointer.html#r-type.pointer.raw). Rust memiliki "
"mutable pointer! Tetapi Anda tidak dapat menalar tentangnya dalam safe Rust."
" Menjadikannya mutable raw pointer ke reference yang memiliki lifetime "
"mempersulit kemampuan compiler melakukan subtyping karena compiler tidak "
"dapat menalar mutable raw pointer di dalam borrow checker."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"Wrap up: We've introduced ways to stop the compiler from deciding that "
"lifetimes are \"similar enough\" by choosing a Variance for a lifetime in "
"`PhantomData` that is restrictive enough to prevent this slide from "
"compiling."
msgstr ""
"Penutup: Kami telah memperkenalkan cara menghentikan compiler memutuskan "
"bahwa lifetime \"cukup mirip\" dengan memilih Variance untuk lifetime dalam "
"`PhantomData` yang cukup ketat untuk mencegah slide ini dikompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"That is, we can now create variables that can exist in the same scope as "
"each other, but whose types are automatically made different from one "
"another per-variable without much boilerplate."
msgstr ""
"Artinya, kita sekarang dapat membuat variabel yang dapat berada dalam scope "
"yang sama satu sama lain, tetapi tipenya secara otomatis dibuat berbeda satu"
" sama lain per variabel tanpa banyak boilerplate."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-02-phantomdata.md
msgid ""
"The `for<'a>` quantifier is not just for function types. It is a [**Higher-"
"ranked trait bound**](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/subtyping.html?search=Hiher#r-subtype.higher-ranked)."
msgstr ""
"Kuantifier `for<'a>` bukan hanya untuk tipe fungsi. Ini adalah [**Higher-"
"ranked trait bound**](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/subtyping.html?search=Hiher#r-subtype.higher-ranked)."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "Implementing Branded Types (Branding 3/4)"
msgstr "Mengimplementasikan Branded Type (Branding 3/4)"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"Constructing branded types is different to how we construct non-branded "
"types."
msgstr ""
"Mengonstruksi branded type berbeda dari cara kita mengonstruksi tipe non-"
"branded."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "// The data we want to modify in this context.\n"
msgstr "// The data we want to modify in this context.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "// The function that uniquely brands the lifetime of a `Bytes`\n"
msgstr "// The function that uniquely brands the lifetime of a `Bytes`\n"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: We want to have \"proven indexes\" for a type, and we don't want"
" those indexes to be usable by different variables of the same type. We also"
" don't want those indexes to escape a scope."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Kami ingin memiliki \"proven index\" untuk suatu tipe, dan kami "
"tidak ingin indeks tersebut dapat digunakan oleh variabel berbeda bertipe "
"sama. Kami juga tidak ingin indeks tersebut keluar dari scope."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "Our Branded Type will be `Bytes`: a byte array."
msgstr "Branded Type kami adalah `Bytes`: array byte."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"Our Branded Token will be `ProvenIndex`: an index known to be in range."
msgstr ""
"Branded Token kami adalah `ProvenIndex`: indeks yang diketahui berada dalam "
"rentang."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "There are several notable parts to this implementation:"
msgstr "Ada beberapa bagian penting dalam implementasi ini:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"`new` does not return a `Bytes`, instead asking for \"starting data\" and a "
"use-once Closure that is passed a `Bytes` when it is called."
msgstr ""
"`new` tidak mengembalikan `Bytes`, melainkan meminta \"starting data\" dan "
"Closure sekali pakai yang menerima `Bytes` saat dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "That `new` function has a `for<'a>` on its trait bound."
msgstr "Fungsi `new` tersebut memiliki `for<'a>` pada trait bound-nya."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"We have both a getter for an index and a getter for a values with a proven "
"index."
msgstr ""
"Kami memiliki getter untuk indeks dan getter untuk nilai dengan indeks yang "
"telah terbukti."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "Ask: Why does `new` not return a `Bytes`?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Mengapa `new` tidak mengembalikan `Bytes`?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"Answer: Because we need `Bytes` to have a unique lifetime controlled by the "
"API."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban: Karena kami ingin `Bytes` memiliki lifetime unik yang dikendalikan "
"API."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"Ask: So what if `new()` returned `Bytes`, what is the specific harm that it "
"would cause?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Jadi bagaimana jika `new()` mengembalikan `Bytes`, apa kerugian "
"spesifik yang ditimbulkannya?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "Answer: Think about the signature of that hypothetical `new()` method:"
msgstr "Jawaban: Pikirkan signature method `new()` hipotetis tersebut:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "`fn new<'a>() -> Bytes<'a> { ... }`"
msgstr "`fn new<'a>() -> Bytes<'a> { ... }`"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"This would allow the API user to choose what the lifetime `'a` is, removing "
"our ability to guarantee that the lifetimes between different instances of "
"`Bytes` are unique and unable to be subtyped to one another."
msgstr ""
"Ini akan memungkinkan pengguna API memilih lifetime `'a`, menghilangkan "
"kemampuan kami untuk menjamin bahwa lifetime antarinstance `Bytes` yang "
"berbeda bersifat unik dan tidak dapat di-subtype satu sama lain."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "Ask: Why do we need both a `get_index` and a `get_proven`?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Mengapa kita memerlukan `get_index` dan `get_proven`?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "Expect \"Because we can't know if an index is occupied at compile time\""
msgstr ""
"Harapkan \"Karena kita tidak dapat mengetahui apakah suatu indeks terisi "
"pada waktu kompilasi\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid "Ask: Then what's the point of the proven indexes?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Lalu apa gunanya proven index?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"Answer: Avoiding bounds checking while keeping knowledge of what indexes are"
" occupied specific to individual variables, unable to erroneously be used on"
" the wrong one."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban: Menghindari pemeriksaan bounds sambil menjaga pengetahuan tentang "
"indeks mana yang terisi tetap spesifik untuk variabel masing-masing, "
"sehingga tidak dapat secara keliru digunakan pada variabel yang salah."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-03-impl.md
msgid ""
"Note: The focus is not on only on avoiding overuse of bounds checks, but "
"also on preventing that \"cross over\" of indexes."
msgstr ""
"Catatan: Fokusnya bukan hanya menghindari penggunaan pemeriksaan bounds "
"secara berlebihan, tetapi juga mencegah \"crossover\" indeks."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "Branded Types in Action (Branding 4/4)"
msgstr "Branded Type dalam Aksi (Branding 4/4)"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"// bytes_2.get_proven(&index_1); // ❌🔨\n"
"            \"Computations done!\""
msgstr ""
"// bytes_2.get_proven(&index_1); // ❌🔨\n"
"            \"Computations done!\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "\"{result}\""
msgstr "\"{result}\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"We now have the implementation ready, we can now write a program where token"
" types that are proofs of existing indexes cannot be shared between "
"variables."
msgstr ""
"Implementasi sekarang sudah siap; kita dapat menulis program ketika tipe "
"token yang menjadi bukti indeks yang ada tidak dapat dibagikan "
"antarvariabel."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"Demonstration: Uncomment the `bytes_2.get_proven(&index_1);` line and show "
"that it does not compile when we use indexes from different variables."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasi: Buka komentar baris `bytes_2.get_proven(&index_1);` dan "
"tunjukkan bahwa kode tidak dapat dikompilasi ketika kami menggunakan indeks "
"dari variabel berbeda."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"Ask: What operations can we perform that we can guarantee would produce a "
"proven index?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Operasi apa yang dapat kita lakukan yang dapat dijamin "
"menghasilkan proven index?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "Expect a \"push\" implementation, suggested demo:"
msgstr "Harapkan implementasi \"push\", demo yang disarankan:"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"Ask: Can we make this not just about a byte array, but as a general wrapper "
"on `Vec<T>`?"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: Dapatkah kita membuat ini bukan hanya tentang array byte, tetapi "
"sebagai wrapper umum untuk `Vec<T>`?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "Trivial: Yes!"
msgstr "Sepele: Ya!"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "Maybe demonstrate: Generalising `Bytes<'id>` into `BrandedVec<'id, T>`"
msgstr ""
"Mungkin demonstrasikan: Menggeneralisasi `Bytes<'id>` menjadi "
"`BrandedVec<'id, T>`"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid "Ask: What other areas could we use something like this?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Area lain apa yang dapat menggunakan sesuatu seperti ini?"

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"The resulting token API is **highly restrictive**, but the things that it "
"makes possible to prove as safe within the Rust type system are meaningful."
msgstr ""
"API token yang dihasilkan **sangat membatasi**, tetapi hal-hal yang dapat "
"dibuktikan aman dalam sistem tipe Rust menjadi bermakna."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"[GhostCell](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/paper.pdf), a "
"structure that allows for safe cyclic data structures in Rust (among other "
"previously difficult to represent data structures), uses this kind of token "
"type to make sure cells can't \"escape\" a context where we know where "
"operations similar to those shown in these examples are safe."
msgstr ""
"[GhostCell](https://plv.mpi-sws.org/rustbelt/ghostcell/paper.pdf), struktur "
"yang memungkinkan struktur data siklik yang aman di Rust (antara lain "
"struktur data yang sebelumnya sulit direpresentasikan), menggunakan jenis "
"tipe token ini untuk memastikan cell tidak dapat \"keluar\" dari konteks "
"tempat kita mengetahui bahwa operasi serupa dengan yang ditunjukkan pada "
"contoh ini aman."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"This \"Branded Types\" sequence of slides is based off their `BrandedVec` "
"implementation in the paper, which covers many of the implementation details"
" of this use case in more depth as a gentle introduction to how `GhostCell` "
"itself is implemented and used in practice."
msgstr ""
"Rangkaian slide \"Branded Types\" ini didasarkan pada implementasi "
"`BrandedVec` mereka dalam paper tersebut, yang membahas banyak detail "
"implementasi kasus penggunaan ini lebih dalam sebagai pengantar yang mudah "
"tentang bagaimana `GhostCell` sendiri diimplementasikan dan digunakan dalam "
"praktik."

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/token-types/branded-04-in-action.md
msgid ""
"GhostCell also uses formal checks outside of Rust's type system to prove "
"that the things it allows within this kind of context (lifetime branding) "
"are safe."
msgstr ""
"GhostCell juga menggunakan pemeriksaan formal di luar sistem tipe Rust untuk"
" membuktikan bahwa hal-hal yang diizinkannya dalam konteks semacam ini "
"(lifetime branding) aman."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism.md
msgid ""
"Rust has plenty of mechanisms for writing and using polymorphic code, but "
"they're somewhat different from other popular languages!"
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki banyak mekanisme untuk menulis dan menggunakan kode "
"polimorfik, tetapi mekanismenya agak berbeda dari bahasa populer lainnya!"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism.md
msgid ""
"This chapter will cover the details of Rust's polymorphism and how it's "
"similar, or different to, other languages."
msgstr ""
"Bab ini akan membahas detail polimorfisme Rust dan bagaimana kesamaan atau "
"perbedaannya dengan bahasa lain."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/python.md
msgid ""
"In a dynamic language like Python, we don't have to do anything special to "
"allow a function to accept arguments of different types:"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bahasa dinamis seperti Python, kita tidak perlu melakukan hal khusus "
"agar fungsi menerima argumen bertipe berbeda:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/python.md
msgid ""
"But Rust's static type system requires us to specify the types of our "
"functions' arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Tetapi sistem tipe statis Rust mengharuskan kita menentukan tipe argumen "
"fungsi:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/python.md
msgid "// print_value(\"hello\"); // ❌ Mismatched types!\n"
msgstr "// print_value(\"hello\"); // ❌ Mismatched types!\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/python.md
msgid ""
"If you are coming from a dynamic language like Python, the concept of "
"polymorphism may be new to you because in dynamic languages all functions "
"are implicitly polymorphic. But in Rust, functions only accept arguments of "
"the exact types they expect, and we must use a mechanism like generics to "
"support polymorphism."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda berasal dari bahasa dinamis seperti Python, konsep polimorfisme "
"mungkin baru bagi Anda karena dalam bahasa dinamis semua fungsi secara "
"implisit bersifat polimorfik. Tetapi di Rust, fungsi hanya menerima argumen "
"dengan tipe persis yang diharapkan, dan kita harus menggunakan mekanisme "
"seperti generic untuk mendukung polimorfisme."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/python.md
msgid ""
"Static typing is a powerful tool that allows the compiler to enforce correct"
" usage of our APIs: If your function needs to be given an `i32` in order to "
"function correctly, the compiler won't allow a user of that function to pass"
" in a string."
msgstr ""
"Static typing adalah alat ampuh yang memungkinkan compiler menegakkan "
"penggunaan API yang benar: Jika fungsi Anda perlu diberi `i32` agar "
"berfungsi dengan benar, compiler tidak akan mengizinkan pengguna fungsi "
"tersebut meneruskan string."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/python.md
msgid ""
"But static typing is restrictive in cases where we want to write code that "
"is flexible in its handling of types. In the example on this slide, we might"
" want our `print_value` function to be able to print both numbers and "
"strings, but as written it can only accept `i32` values."
msgstr ""
"Tetapi static typing membatasi dalam kasus ketika kita ingin menulis kode "
"yang fleksibel dalam menangani tipe. Pada contoh di slide ini, kami mungkin "
"ingin fungsi `print_value` dapat mencetak angka maupun string, tetapi "
"seperti ditulis fungsi tersebut hanya dapat menerima nilai `i32`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/python.md
msgid ""
"Edit `print_value` to make it generic using `Display` to print different "
"kinds of values:"
msgstr ""
"Edit `print_value` agar menjadi generic menggunakan `Display` untuk mencetak"
" berbagai jenis nilai:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid "In Rust we have 3 different mechanisms for writing polymorphic code:"
msgstr ""
"Di Rust kita memiliki 3 mekanisme berbeda untuk menulis kode polimorfik:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"**Generics** - Static polymorphism where code abstracts over types but the "
"types are fully known at compile time."
msgstr ""
"**Generic** - Polimorfisme statis ketika kode diabstraksi atas tipe tetapi "
"tipenya sepenuhnya diketahui pada waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"**Enums** - Dynamic polymorphism where a fixed set of known types are "
"selected between at runtime."
msgstr ""
"**Enum** - Polimorfisme dinamis ketika himpunan tipe yang diketahui secara "
"tetap dipilih pada runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"**`dyn`** - Dynamic polymorphism where any type meeting a particular trait "
"interface can be used."
msgstr ""
"**`dyn`** - Polimorfisme dinamis ketika tipe apa pun yang memenuhi antarmuka"
" trait tertentu dapat digunakan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"When discussing polymorphism in Rust, it's helpful to differentiate between "
"**static** polymorphism and **dynamic** polymorphism."
msgstr ""
"Saat membahas polimorfisme di Rust, akan membantu untuk membedakan antara "
"polimorfisme **statis** dan **dinamis**."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"**static polymorphism** is when we abstract over types, but the type "
"information is fully known by the compiler. This allows us to reuse code in "
"different type contexts without needing to add any runtime overhead, and we "
"have access to the full set of features that traits expose. This is "
"accomplished with **generics** in Rust."
msgstr ""
"**polimorfisme statis** adalah ketika kita mengabstraksi atas tipe, tetapi "
"informasi tipe sepenuhnya diketahui compiler. Ini memungkinkan kita "
"menggunakan kembali kode dalam konteks tipe berbeda tanpa perlu menambahkan "
"overhead runtime, dan kita memiliki akses ke seluruh fitur yang diekspos "
"trait. Ini dicapai dengan **generic** di Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"**dynamic polymorphism** is when we need to select between different types "
"at runtime, and we don't know at compile time which specific type will be "
"used."
msgstr ""
"**polimorfisme dinamis** adalah ketika kita perlu memilih antara tipe "
"berbeda pada runtime, dan kita tidak mengetahui pada waktu kompilasi tipe "
"spesifik mana yang akan digunakan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"When we have a fixed set of known types to choose from, we can use **enums**"
" to track at runtime which one we have."
msgstr ""
"Ketika kita memiliki himpunan tipe diketahui yang tetap untuk dipilih, kita "
"dapat menggunakan **enum** untuk melacak pada runtime mana yang kita miliki."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/polymorphism-kinds.md
msgid ""
"When we don't know ahead of time which types may be used, e.g. if downstream"
" users may introduce new types that we don't know about, then we use "
"**`dyn`** to allow extensibility."
msgstr ""
"Ketika kita tidak mengetahui sebelumnya tipe mana yang mungkin digunakan, "
"misalnya jika pengguna hilir dapat memperkenalkan tipe baru yang tidak kita "
"ketahui, maka kita menggunakan **`dyn`** untuk memungkinkan ekstensibilitas."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics.md
msgid ""
"Generics are used when we want to abstract over types, but we expect the "
"users of our code to know the concrete types."
msgstr ""
"Generic digunakan ketika kita ingin mengabstraksi atas tipe, tetapi kita "
"mengharapkan pengguna kode kita mengetahui tipe konkretnya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics.md
msgid ""
"Generics are our mechanism for **static polymorphism**, which is "
"polymorphism where the types are fully known at compile time."
msgstr ""
"Generic adalah mekanisme kami untuk **polimorfisme statis**, yaitu "
"polimorfisme ketika tipenya sepenuhnya diketahui pada waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics.md
msgid ""
"One example of this is `Vec`, which is generic over the type of element it "
"stores. `Vec` itself is polymorphic: It's written in such a way that it "
"doesn't know what type of element will be stored in it. But in order to use "
"a `Vec`, you must specify a concrete type to use for the element."
msgstr ""
"Salah satu contohnya adalah `Vec`, yang generic atas tipe elemen yang "
"disimpannya. `Vec` sendiri bersifat polimorfik: Ditulis sedemikian rupa "
"sehingga tidak mengetahui tipe elemen apa yang akan disimpan. Tetapi untuk "
"menggunakan `Vec`, Anda harus menentukan tipe konkret untuk elemennya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics.md
msgid ""
"Generics are a mechanism for **code reuse**: You have some common logic that"
" is fundamentally the same regardless of what specific type it handles, and "
"generics give you a way to abstract over those different types **without "
"duplicating logic**."
msgstr ""
"Generic adalah mekanisme untuk **penggunaan ulang kode**: Anda memiliki "
"logika umum yang secara fundamental sama terlepas dari tipe spesifik yang "
"ditanganinya, dan generic memberi Anda cara mengabstraksi atas tipe berbeda "
"tersebut **tanpa menduplikasi logika**."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics.md
msgid ""
"Note that there's no dynamism: The types must be fully known at compile "
"time, there's no way to select a type for `Vec`'s element at runtime. This "
"means that generics are not an option when we need **runtime polymorphism**."
" Later we will look at two mechanisms for doing dynamic polymorphism: Enums "
"and `dyn`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa tidak ada dinamisme: Tipe harus sepenuhnya diketahui pada "
"waktu kompilasi, tidak ada cara memilih tipe untuk elemen `Vec` pada "
"runtime. Ini berarti generic bukan pilihan ketika kita memerlukan **runtime "
"polymorphism**. Nanti kita akan melihat dua mekanisme untuk melakukan "
"polimorfisme dinamis: Enum dan `dyn`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "Trait Bounds on Generics"
msgstr "Trait Bound pada Generic"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "\"Item: {}\""
msgstr "\"Item: {}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "// Works with integers\n"
msgstr "// Works with integers\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "\"Hello, Rust!\""
msgstr "\"Hello, Rust!\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "// Works with strings\n"
msgstr "// Works with strings\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid ""
"Generic functions rely on traits to determine what operations are valid for "
"a generic type."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi generic bergantung pada trait untuk menentukan operasi apa yang valid"
" bagi tipe generic."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid ""
"Without a trait bound on a generic type parameter, we don't have access to "
"any behavior for that type. Remove the trait bound on `print_with_length` "
"and demonstrate that we're not allowed to make assumptions about what "
"methods it has."
msgstr ""
"Tanpa trait bound pada parameter tipe generic, kita tidak memiliki akses ke "
"perilaku apa pun untuk tipe tersebut. Hapus trait bound pada "
"`print_with_length` dan tunjukkan bahwa kita tidak diizinkan membuat asumsi "
"tentang method yang dimilikinya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/trait-bounds.html"
msgstr "https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/trait-bounds.html"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid ""
"// Many traits have simple implementations that can be generated "
"automatically.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Many traits have simple implementations that can be generated "
"automatically.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid ""
"Many traits have trivial implementations that would be easy to mechanically "
"write. For these traits, it's possible to have the compiler generate the "
"implementation for us using a derive macro."
msgstr ""
"Banyak trait memiliki implementasi trivial yang mudah ditulis secara "
"mekanis. Untuk trait ini, compiler dapat menghasilkan implementasinya untuk "
"kita menggunakan derive macro."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid ""
"For example, the `Clone` trait is commonly implemented by simply cloning all"
" fields of the struct. If this is the behavior we want for our type, we "
"don't need to write out the boilerplate ourselves. Replace the manual "
"implementation with the corresponding derive."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, trait `Clone` umumnya diimplementasikan dengan hanya meng-"
"clone semua field struct. Jika ini perilaku yang kami inginkan untuk tipe "
"kami, kami tidak perlu menulis boilerplate sendiri. Ganti implementasi "
"manual dengan derive yang sesuai."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid ""
"Derived trait implementations automatically stay in sync with your type "
"definition. Demonstrate adding a field to `DrawingBuffer` and show that the "
"derived `Clone` impl is automatically updated, whereas the manual impl has "
"to be updated by hand."
msgstr ""
"Implementasi trait hasil derive otomatis tetap selaras dengan definisi tipe "
"Anda. Demonstrasikan penambahan field ke `DrawingBuffer` dan tunjukkan bahwa"
" implementasi `Clone` hasil derive otomatis diperbarui, sedangkan "
"implementasi manual harus diperbarui sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid ""
"Many standard library traits support being derived, and it's common for "
"traits defined in the ecosystem to also support this."
msgstr ""
"Banyak trait standard library mendukung derive, dan trait yang didefinisikan"
" di ekosistem juga umum mendukungnya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid ""
"Traits do not support being derived by default, but you can implement derive"
" support for your own traits with a macro. Doing so is covered in the Macros"
" course."
msgstr ""
"Trait tidak mendukung derive secara default, tetapi Anda dapat "
"mengimplementasikan dukungan derive untuk trait Anda sendiri dengan macro. "
"Hal ini dibahas dalam kursus Macro."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid "references:"
msgstr "referensi:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/attributes/derive.html#r-attributes.derive"
msgstr ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/attributes/derive.html#r-attributes.derive"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid "Default Method Implementations"
msgstr "Implementasi Method Default"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid "// Required Method\n"
msgstr "// Required Method\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid "// Default implementation\n"
msgstr "// Default implementation\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid ""
"Traits often have methods that are implemented for you already, once you "
"implement the required methods."
msgstr ""
"Trait sering memiliki method yang sudah diimplementasikan untuk Anda setelah"
" Anda mengimplementasikan method yang diwajibkan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid ""
"A trait method has a default implementation if the function body is present."
" This implementation can be written in terms of other methods available, "
"such as other methods in the trait or methods of a supertrait."
msgstr ""
"Method trait memiliki implementasi default jika body fungsi ada. "
"Implementasi ini dapat ditulis berdasarkan method lain yang tersedia, "
"seperti method lain dalam trait atau method dari supertrait."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid ""
"Often you'll see methods that provide the broad functionality that is "
"necessary to implement (like `Ord`'s `compare`) with default implementations"
" for functions that can be implemented in terms of those methods (like "
"`Ord`'s `max`/`min`/`clamp`)."
msgstr ""
"Sering Anda akan melihat method yang menyediakan fungsionalitas luas yang "
"perlu diimplementasikan (seperti `compare` milik `Ord`) beserta implementasi"
" default untuk fungsi yang dapat diimplementasikan berdasarkan method "
"tersebut (seperti `max`/`min`/`clamp` milik `Ord`)."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid ""
"Default methods can be overridden by derive macros, as derive macros produce"
" arbitrary ASTs in the implementation."
msgstr ""
"Method default dapat di-override oleh derive macro, karena derive macro "
"menghasilkan AST arbitrer dalam implementasinya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/default-impls.md
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/items/traits.html#r-items.traits.associated-item-decls"
msgstr ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/items/traits.html#r-items.traits.associated-item-decls"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid "Supertraits / Trait Dependencies"
msgstr "Supertrait / Dependensi Trait"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid "Traits can be extended by new traits."
msgstr "Trait dapat diperluas oleh trait baru."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid "/* methods common to all animals */"
msgstr "/* methods common to all animals */"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid "/* methods only for mammals */"
msgstr "/* methods only for mammals */"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid "// From stdlib\n"
msgstr "// From stdlib\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid "/* methods for Ord */"
msgstr "/* methods for Ord */"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"When authoring a trait, you can specify traits that a type must also "
"implement. These are called _supertraits_."
msgstr ""
"Saat membuat trait, Anda dapat menentukan trait yang juga harus "
"diimplementasikan suatu tipe. Trait tersebut disebut _supertrait_."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"For the example above, any type that implements `Mammal` must also implement"
" `Animal`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk contoh di atas, tipe apa pun yang mengimplementasikan `Mammal` juga "
"harus mengimplementasikan `Animal`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"These hierarchies of traits let us design systems around the behavior of "
"complex real-world taxonomies (like fauna, machine hardware, operating "
"system specifics, etc)."
msgstr ""
"Hierarki trait ini memungkinkan kita merancang sistem berdasarkan perilaku "
"taksonomi dunia nyata yang kompleks (seperti fauna, hardware mesin, "
"spesifikasi sistem operasi, dan sebagainya)."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid "This is distinct from object inheritance! But it looks similar."
msgstr "Ini berbeda dari inheritance objek! Tetapi tampak serupa."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"Object inheritance allows for overrides and brings in the behavior of the "
"inherited types by default."
msgstr ""
"Inheritance objek memungkinkan override dan membawa perilaku tipe yang "
"diwarisi secara default."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"A trait having a supertrait doesn't mean that trait can override method "
"implementations as default implementations."
msgstr ""
"Trait yang memiliki supertrait tidak berarti trait tersebut dapat meng-"
"override implementasi method sebagai implementasi default."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/items/traits.html?highlight=supertrait#r-items.traits.supertraits"
msgstr ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/items/traits.html?highlight=supertrait#r-items.traits.supertraits"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid "Blanket Trait Implementations"
msgstr "Implementasi Trait Blanket"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"We can use a generic `impl` block to implement a trait for multiple types at"
" once, generally based on the behavior provided by another trait. These are "
"referred to as **blanket implementations**."
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat menggunakan block `impl` generic untuk mengimplementasikan trait "
"bagi beberapa tipe sekaligus, umumnya berdasarkan perilaku yang disediakan "
"trait lain. Ini disebut **blanket implementation**."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"// A blanket implementation! If something implements Display, it implements\n"
"// PrettyPrint.\n"
msgstr ""
"// A blanket implementation! If something implements Display, it implements\n"
"// PrettyPrint.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid "\"{self}\""
msgstr "\"{self}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"`impl` blocks can be generic, which allow us to apply an implementation to "
"multiple types at once. This is commonly used when applying an `impl` block "
"to a generic type, but can also be used to implement a trait for multiple "
"types at once."
msgstr ""
"Block `impl` dapat bersifat generic, yang memungkinkan kita menerapkan "
"implementasi ke beberapa tipe sekaligus. Ini umum digunakan saat menerapkan "
"block `impl` pada tipe generic, tetapi juga dapat digunakan untuk "
"mengimplementasikan trait bagi beberapa tipe sekaligus."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"When an `impl` block applies to multiple types, we refer this as a \"blanket"
" impl\"."
msgstr ""
"Ketika block `impl` berlaku untuk beberapa tipe, kami menyebutnya \"blanket "
"impl\"."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"In the example above we have a blanket implementation for all types that "
"implement `Display`."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh di atas kami memiliki blanket implementation untuk semua tipe "
"yang mengimplementasikan `Display`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"Blanket impls can restrict how traits are implemented. Rust prevents a type "
"from implementing the same trait twice, so a blanket impl prevents the trait"
" from being implemented directly on a covered type."
msgstr ""
"Blanket impl dapat membatasi bagaimana trait diimplementasikan. Rust "
"mencegah suatu tipe mengimplementasikan trait yang sama dua kali, sehingga "
"blanket impl mencegah trait diimplementasikan langsung pada tipe yang "
"tercakup."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate this by adding an implementation for `String` and show the "
"resulting error."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan hal ini dengan menambahkan implementasi untuk `String` dan "
"tunjukkan error yang dihasilkan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"Avoid a blanket impl if users are likely to want to customize the behavior "
"of the implementation beyond what the blanket impl provides."
msgstr ""
"Hindari blanket impl jika pengguna kemungkinan ingin menyesuaikan perilaku "
"implementasi melebihi yang disediakan blanket impl."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/blanket-impls.md
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/glossary.html#blanket-implementation"
msgstr ""
"https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/glossary.html#blanket-implementation"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid "Conditional Method Implementations"
msgstr "Implementasi Method Kondisional"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid "// No trait bounds on the type definition.\n"
msgstr "// No trait bounds on the type definition.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid "// Instead bounds are put on the implementations for the type.\n"
msgstr "// Instead bounds are put on the implementations for the type.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid "// alternatively\n"
msgstr "// alternatively\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid "// Specifies the trait bound in a where expression\n"
msgstr "// Specifies the trait bound in a where expression\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid ""
"When authoring a type with generic parameters, we can write implementations "
"for that type that depend on what the parameters are or what traits they "
"implement."
msgstr ""
"Saat membuat tipe dengan parameter generic, kita dapat menulis implementasi "
"untuk tipe tersebut yang bergantung pada parameter apa atau trait apa yang "
"diimplementasikannya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid "These methods are only available when the type meets those conditions."
msgstr "Method ini hanya tersedia ketika tipe memenuhi kondisi tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid ""
"For things like ordered sets, where you'd want the inner type to always be "
"`Ord`, this is the preferred way of putting a trait bound on a parameter of "
"a type."
msgstr ""
"Untuk hal seperti ordered set, ketika Anda ingin tipe dalamnya selalu `Ord`,"
" ini adalah cara yang disukai untuk meletakkan trait bound pada parameter "
"suatu tipe."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid ""
"We don't put the definition on the type itself as this would cause "
"downstream issues for everywhere the type is mentioned with a generic "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Kami tidak meletakkan definisi pada tipe itu sendiri karena akan menyebabkan"
" masalah hilir di setiap tempat tipe tersebut disebut dengan parameter "
"generic."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/conditional-methods.md
msgid ""
"We can maintain invariants just fine with conditional method "
"implementations."
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat menjaga invariant dengan baik menggunakan implementasi method "
"kondisional."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid "Statically Sized and Dynamically Sized Types"
msgstr "Tipe Berukuran Statis dan Berukuran Dinamis"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid "/* : Sized */"
msgstr "/* : Sized */"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: Being able to specify between types whose size are known and "
"compile time and types whose size are known at runtime is useful for"
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Kemampuan membedakan antara tipe yang ukurannya diketahui pada "
"waktu kompilasi dan tipe yang ukurannya diketahui pada runtime berguna untuk"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid ""
"The Sized trait is automatically implemented by types with a known size at "
"compile-time."
msgstr ""
"Trait Sized secara otomatis diimplementasikan oleh tipe dengan ukuran yang "
"diketahui pada waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid ""
"This trait is also automatically added to any type parameter that doesn't "
"opt-out of being sized."
msgstr ""
"Trait ini juga secara otomatis ditambahkan ke parameter tipe apa pun yang "
"tidak menonaktifkan batasan Sized."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid "Most types implement `Sized`: they have a compile-time known size."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar tipe mengimplementasikan `Sized`: ukurannya diketahui pada "
"waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid ""
"Types like `[T]`, `str` and `dyn Trait` are all dynamically sized types. "
"Their size is stored as part of the reference to the value of that type."
msgstr ""
"Tipe seperti `[T]`, `str`, dan `dyn Trait` semuanya adalah tipe berukuran "
"dinamis. Ukurannya disimpan sebagai bagian dari reference ke nilai bertipe "
"tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid "Type parameters automatically implement `Sized` unless specified."
msgstr ""
"Parameter tipe secara otomatis mengimplementasikan `Sized` kecuali "
"ditentukan lain."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sized.md
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/reference/dynamically-sized-"
"types.html#r-dynamic-sized"
msgstr ""
"https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/reference/dynamically-sized-"
"types.html#r-dynamic-sized"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/monomorphization.md
msgid "// instance one, &Vec<u32> -> ()\n"
msgstr "// instance one, &Vec<u32> -> ()\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/monomorphization.md
msgid "// instance two, &Vec<f32> -> ()\n"
msgstr "// instance two, &Vec<f32> -> ()\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/monomorphization.md
msgid ""
"Each instance of a function or type with generics gets transformed into a "
"unique, concrete version of that function at compile time. Generics do not "
"exist at runtime, only specific types."
msgstr ""
"Setiap instance fungsi atau tipe dengan generic ditransformasi menjadi versi"
" konkret unik dari fungsi tersebut pada waktu kompilasi. Generic tidak ada "
"pada runtime, hanya tipe spesifik."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/monomorphization.md
msgid ""
"This comes with a strong baseline performance and capacity for optimization,"
" but at a cost of binary size and compile time."
msgstr ""
"Ini memberikan performa dasar yang kuat dan kapasitas optimasi, tetapi "
"dengan biaya ukuran binary dan waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/monomorphization.md
msgid ""
"There are plenty of ways to trim binary size and compilation times, but "
"we're not covering them here."
msgstr ""
"Ada banyak cara untuk memangkas ukuran binary dan waktu kompilasi, tetapi "
"kami tidak membahasnya di sini."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/monomorphization.md
msgid ""
"Pay for what you use: Binary size increase of monomorphization is only "
"incurred for instances of a type or functions on a type used in the final "
"program or dynamic library."
msgstr ""
"Bayar sesuai penggunaan: Peningkatan ukuran binary akibat monomorphization "
"hanya terjadi untuk instance tipe atau fungsi pada tipe yang digunakan dalam"
" program akhir atau library dinamis."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/monomorphization.md
msgid ""
"When to care: Monomorphization impacts compile times and binary size. In "
"circumstances like WebAssembly in-browser or embedded systems development, "
"you may want to be mindful about designing with generics in mind."
msgstr ""
"Kapan perlu diperhatikan: Monomorphization memengaruhi waktu kompilasi dan "
"ukuran binary. Dalam keadaan seperti WebAssembly di browser atau "
"pengembangan sistem embedded, Anda mungkin perlu berhati-hati saat merancang"
" dengan mempertimbangkan generic."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid ""
"Traits are normally extensible, meaning that downstream users can implement "
"our traits for their own types, and then our generic code can handle those "
"downstream types. Usually this is what we want, but sometimes we want to "
"define a trait where we control all of the implementations. To do this, we "
"can create a **sealed trait**."
msgstr ""
"Trait biasanya dapat diperluas, artinya pengguna hilir dapat "
"mengimplementasikan trait kita untuk tipe mereka sendiri, lalu kode generic "
"kita dapat menangani tipe hilir tersebut. Biasanya ini yang kita inginkan, "
"tetapi kadang kita ingin mendefinisikan trait di mana kita mengontrol semua "
"implementasinya. Untuk itu, kita dapat membuat **sealed trait**."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid "// Private module, preventing users from accessing the `Sealed` trait.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Private module, preventing users from accessing the `Sealed` trait.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid ""
"// The trait itself must be public, or we can't use it as\n"
"    // part of our public API.\n"
msgstr ""
"// The trait itself must be public, or we can't use it as\n"
"    // part of our public API.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid ""
"// Implement `Sealed` for types that should implement our\n"
"    // public public.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Implement `Sealed` for types that should implement our\n"
"    // public public.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid "// Use `Sealed` as the supertrait for our public trait.\n"
msgstr "// Use `Sealed` as the supertrait for our public trait.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: We want trait-driven code in a crate, but we don't want projects"
" that depend on this crate to be able to implement a trait."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: Kami ingin kode berbasis trait dalam suatu crate, tetapi kami "
"tidak ingin proyek yang bergantung pada crate ini dapat mengimplementasikan "
"trait."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid ""
"The mechanism we use to do this is restricting access to a supertrait, "
"preventing downstream users from being able to implement that trait for "
"their types."
msgstr ""
"Mekanisme yang kami gunakan adalah membatasi akses ke supertrait, mencegah "
"pengguna hilir mengimplementasikan trait tersebut untuk tipe mereka."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md
msgid ""
"This is similar to enums, which inherently wrap a limited set of types, but "
"applies to traits, which by default are extensible."
msgstr ""
"Ini serupa dengan enum, yang secara inheren membungkus himpunan tipe "
"terbatas, tetapi berlaku untuk trait, yang secara default dapat diperluas."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid ""
"Sometimes we need to handle multiple different types at runtime. Enums are a"
" powerful tool that allows us to safely and robustly describe situations "
"like this."
msgstr ""
"Kadang kita perlu menangani beberapa tipe berbeda pada runtime. Enum adalah "
"alat ampuh yang memungkinkan kita mendeskripsikan situasi seperti ini secara"
" aman dan kokoh."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid "\"123\""
msgstr "\"123\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid "\"[456, true, false]\""
msgstr "\"[456, true, false]\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid "r#\"{ \"key\": \"value\" }\"#"
msgstr "r#\"{ \"key\": \"value\" }\"#"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid "\"Parse the JSON string...\""
msgstr "\"Parse the JSON string...\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid ""
"The other category of polymorphism is **dynamic polymorphism**, where we can"
" have different types of value at runtime, and we can't know statically "
"which type we'll have at any given time."
msgstr ""
"Kategori polimorfisme lainnya adalah **polimorfisme dinamis**, ketika kita "
"dapat memiliki tipe nilai berbeda pada runtime, dan kita tidak dapat "
"mengetahui secara statis tipe mana yang akan kita miliki pada waktu "
"tertentu."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid ""
"As an example, consider parsing a JSON string. There are several different "
"types of JSON value, and which one we return depends on the contents of the "
"input string."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, pertimbangkan parsing string JSON. Ada beberapa tipe nilai "
"JSON yang berbeda, dan tipe mana yang dikembalikan bergantung pada isi "
"string input."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums.md
msgid ""
"Our `parse_json` function has to return a single, concrete type, and that "
"type needs to describe all of the possible types a JSON value can be. Enums "
"are a natural way of describing this kind of situation in Rust."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `parse_json` kami harus mengembalikan satu tipe konkret, dan tipe "
"tersebut perlu mendeskripsikan semua tipe yang mungkin dari nilai JSON. Enum"
" adalah cara alami untuk mendeskripsikan situasi semacam ini di Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid ""
"We can easily inspect the contents of an enum using **pattern matching**:"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat dengan mudah memeriksa isi enum menggunakan **pattern matching**:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid "\"We got an object: {obj:?}\""
msgstr "\"We got an object: {obj:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid "\"We got an array: {array:?}\""
msgstr "\"We got an array: {array:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid "\"We got a string: {string:?}\""
msgstr "\"We got a string: {string:?}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid "\"We got a number: {num}\""
msgstr "\"We got a number: {num}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid "\"We got a bool: {b}\""
msgstr "\"We got a bool: {b}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid "\"We got a null\""
msgstr "\"We got a null\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid ""
"Continuing with our JSON parsing example, we can easily determine which kind"
" of value we got by pattern matching on the resulting enum."
msgstr ""
"Melanjutkan contoh parsing JSON kami, kita dapat dengan mudah menentukan "
"jenis nilai yang diperoleh dengan pattern matching pada enum hasilnya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid ""
"This makes enums a good fit for scenarios where we want to handle different "
"types at runtime, but want to retain type information and the ability to "
"directly inspect the concrete value."
msgstr ""
"Ini menjadikan enum cocok untuk skenario ketika kita ingin menangani tipe "
"berbeda pada runtime, tetapi ingin mempertahankan informasi tipe dan "
"kemampuan memeriksa nilai konkretnya secara langsung."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/inspecting.md
msgid ""
"This is a big advantage enums have over `dyn`: With `dyn` we can't easily "
"downcast to the specific concrete type, and are generally restricted to "
"going through the trait interface. Later we'll see that we can support "
"downcasting with `dyn`, but doing so requires extra setup that isn't "
"necessary with enums."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah keunggulan besar enum dibandingkan `dyn`: Dengan `dyn` kita tidak"
" dapat dengan mudah melakukan downcast ke tipe konkret spesifik, dan umumnya"
" terbatas pada antarmuka trait. Nanti kita akan melihat bahwa kita dapat "
"mendukung downcasting dengan `dyn`, tetapi hal itu memerlukan penyiapan "
"tambahan yang tidak diperlukan pada enum."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/heterogeneous.md
msgid "Heterogeneous Collections with Enums"
msgstr "Koleksi Heterogen dengan Enum"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"Enums give us a way to create collections that can store different types of "
"element at runtime:"
msgstr ""
"Enum memberi kita cara membuat koleksi yang dapat menyimpan berbagai tipe "
"elemen pada runtime:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"A common situation where we might need dynamic polymorphism is when we want "
"to store different types of value in the same collection."
msgstr ""
"Situasi umum ketika kita mungkin memerlukan polimorfisme dinamis adalah saat"
" ingin menyimpan berbagai tipe nilai dalam koleksi yang sama."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"In the above example, we want to store both `Cat`s and `Dog`s in the same "
"list. `Vec` doesn't support this directly: All elements of the `Vec` must be"
" the same type."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh di atas, kami ingin menyimpan `Cat` dan `Dog` dalam list yang "
"sama. `Vec` tidak mendukungnya secara langsung: Semua elemen `Vec` harus "
"bertipe sama."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"Wrapping our two different pet types into a single `AnyPet` enum gives us a "
"unified type representation that can be stored in a `Vec`, while allowing "
"individual elements of the `Vec` to be different types."
msgstr ""
"Membungkus dua tipe hewan peliharaan kami yang berbeda ke dalam satu enum "
"`AnyPet` memberi kami representasi tipe terpadu yang dapat disimpan dalam "
"`Vec`, sekaligus memungkinkan elemen individual `Vec` bertipe berbeda."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"This requires that we know all possible pet types up front, as we need to "
"explicitly list them as different variants of the `AnyPet` enum. This works "
"well for libraries or applications that define the full set of possible "
"types, but does not allow downstream users to extend our list of pet types."
msgstr ""
"Ini mengharuskan kita mengetahui semua tipe hewan peliharaan yang mungkin "
"sejak awal, karena kita perlu mencantumkannya secara eksplisit sebagai "
"varian berbeda dari enum `AnyPet`. Ini berfungsi baik untuk library atau "
"aplikasi yang mendefinisikan seluruh himpunan tipe yang mungkin, tetapi "
"tidak memungkinkan pengguna hilir memperluas daftar tipe hewan peliharaan "
"kami."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"Later we will see that we can do the same thing with `dyn`, which allows "
"downstream extension at the cost of being harder to downcast and requiring "
"dynamic dispatch."
msgstr ""
"Nanti kita akan melihat bahwa kita dapat melakukan hal yang sama dengan "
"`dyn`, yang memungkinkan ekstensi hilir dengan konsekuensi lebih sulit di-"
"downcast dan memerlukan dynamic dispatch."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"Sometimes we use an enum to abstract over multiple types that implement the "
"same trait, and want the enum to also re-expose the trait's interface."
msgstr ""
"Kadang kita menggunakan enum untuk mengabstraksi beberapa tipe yang "
"mengimplementasikan trait yang sama, dan ingin enum tersebut juga mengekspos"
" ulang antarmuka trait itu."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid "\"Woof! My name is {}~!\""
msgstr "\"Woof! My name is {}~!\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid "\"Meow! I am {} years old\""
msgstr "\"Meow! I am {} years old\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"One drawback of using an enum for dynamic polymorphism is that if our "
"underlying types (`Cat` and `Dog` in this case) implement a trait (`Pet`), "
"our wrapper enum doesn't automatically expose that same trait interface."
msgstr ""
"Salah satu kekurangan penggunaan enum untuk polimorfisme dinamis adalah jika"
" tipe dasar kami (`Cat` dan `Dog` dalam kasus ini) mengimplementasikan trait"
" (`Pet`), enum wrapper kami tidak otomatis mengekspos antarmuka trait yang "
"sama."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"We can generally implement the trait for the wrapper enum by matching on the"
" enum and dispatching to the corresponding trait method on the underlying "
"types."
msgstr ""
"Kita umumnya dapat mengimplementasikan trait untuk enum wrapper dengan "
"mencocokkan enum tersebut dan mengirim ke method trait terkait pada tipe "
"dasar."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"This is dynamic dispatch, but using the enum's discriminant instead of a "
"vtable in order to lookup the correct function to call."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah dynamic dispatch, tetapi menggunakan diskriminan enum alih-alih "
"vtable untuk mencari fungsi yang benar untuk dipanggil."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"This is an ergonomic drawback of an enum vs `dyn`: The implementation of "
"`Pet` for `AnyPet` is pure boilerplate that we need to repeat each time we "
"have a situation like this, whereas `dyn` gives us this behavior purely from"
" the `Pet` impls on `Cat` and `Dog`."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah kekurangan ergonomis enum dibandingkan `dyn`: Implementasi `Pet` "
"untuk `AnyPet` adalah boilerplate murni yang perlu kita ulangi setiap kali "
"menghadapi situasi seperti ini, sedangkan `dyn` memberikan perilaku ini "
"murni dari implementasi `Pet` pada `Cat` dan `Dog`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"To avoid writing this boilerplate ourselves, we can use a crate like "
"[enum_dispatch](https://crates.io/crates/enum_dispatch), which handles the "
"work of generating the wrapper enum and implementing the trait."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menghindari menulis boilerplate ini sendiri, kita dapat menggunakan "
"crate seperti [enum_dispatch](https://crates.io/crates/enum_dispatch), yang "
"menangani pembuatan enum wrapper dan implementasi trait."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"The advantage of this approach is that we retain the useful properties of an"
" enum (e.g. the ability to pattern match on it) while also exposing a way to"
" do dynamic dispatch through the trait's interface."
msgstr ""
"Keunggulan pendekatan ini adalah kita mempertahankan properti berguna enum "
"(misalnya kemampuan melakukan pattern matching) sekaligus mengekspos cara "
"melakukan dynamic dispatch melalui antarmuka trait."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enums/traits.md
msgid ""
"This also enables us to use `AnyPet` with generic functions like "
"`do_pet_stuff`, which we can also do with `dyn`."
msgstr ""
"Ini juga memungkinkan kita menggunakan `AnyPet` dengan fungsi generic "
"seperti `do_pet_stuff`, yang juga dapat dilakukan dengan `dyn`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn.md
msgid "`dyn Trait` for Dynamic Dispatch in Rust"
msgstr "`dyn Trait` untuk Dynamic Dispatch di Rust"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn.md
msgid "\"Hello dyn!\""
msgstr "\"Hello dyn!\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn.md
msgid ""
"Our other main mechanism of doing dynamic polymorphism is `dyn`, which gives"
" us dynamic dispatch through a trait interface."
msgstr ""
"Mekanisme utama kami yang lain untuk melakukan polimorfisme dinamis adalah "
"`dyn`, yang memberi kita dynamic dispatch melalui antarmuka trait."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn.md
msgid ""
"For any trait that is _dyn compatible_ we can coerce a reference to a value "
"of that trait into a `dyn Trait` value."
msgstr ""
"Untuk trait apa pun yang _kompatibel dengan dyn_, kita dapat melakukan "
"coercion reference ke nilai bertipe trait tersebut menjadi nilai `dyn "
"Trait`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn.md
msgid ""
"We call these _trait objects_. Their type is not known at compile time, but "
"their behavior is: what is implemented by the trait itself."
msgstr ""
"Kita menyebutnya _trait object_. Tipenya tidak diketahui pada waktu "
"kompilasi, tetapi perilakunya diketahui: apa yang diimplementasikan oleh "
"trait itu sendiri."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn.md
msgid ""
"When you _need_ OOP-style heterogeneous data structures, you can reach for "
"`Box<dyn Trait>`, but try to keep it homogeneous and generic-based first!"
msgstr ""
"Ketika Anda _membutuhkan_ struktur data heterogen bergaya OOP, Anda dapat "
"menggunakan `Box<dyn Trait>`, tetapi cobalah utamakan yang homogen dan "
"berbasis generic terlebih dahulu!"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid "Dyn-compatible traits"
msgstr "Trait yang Kompatibel dengan Dyn"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid "// dyn compatible\n"
msgstr "// dyn compatible\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid "// dyn compatible, but you can't use this method when it's dyn\n"
msgstr "// dyn compatible, but you can't use this method when it's dyn\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid "// no longer dyn compatible\n"
msgstr "// no longer dyn compatible\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"Not all traits are able to be invoked as trait objects. A trait that can be "
"invoked is referred to as a _dyn compatible_ trait."
msgstr ""
"Tidak semua trait dapat dipanggil sebagai trait object. Trait yang dapat "
"dipanggil disebut trait _kompatibel dyn_."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid "This was previously called _object safe traits_ or _object safety_."
msgstr "Sebelumnya ini disebut _object safe trait_ atau _object safety_."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"Dynamic dispatch offloads a lot of compile-time type information into "
"runtime vtable information."
msgstr ""
"Dynamic dispatch memindahkan banyak informasi tipe waktu kompilasi menjadi "
"informasi vtable runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"If a concept is incompatible with what we can meaningfully store in a "
"vtable, either the trait stops being dyn compatible or those methods are "
"excluded from being able to be used in a dyn context."
msgstr ""
"Jika suatu konsep tidak kompatibel dengan apa yang dapat kita simpan secara "
"bermakna dalam vtable, trait tersebut berhenti kompatibel dengan dyn atau "
"method tersebut dikecualikan dari penggunaan dalam konteks dyn."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"A trait is dyn-compatible when all its supertraits are dyn-compatible and "
"when it has no associated constants/types, and no methods that depend on "
"generics."
msgstr ""
"Trait kompatibel dengan dyn ketika semua supertrait-nya kompatibel dengan "
"dyn dan trait tersebut tidak memiliki associated constant/type, serta tidak "
"memiliki method yang bergantung pada generic."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"You'll most frequently run into dyn incompatible traits when they have "
"associated types/constants or return values of `Self` (i.e. the Clone trait "
"is not dyn compatible.)"
msgstr ""
"Anda paling sering menemui trait yang tidak kompatibel dengan dyn ketika "
"trait tersebut memiliki associated type/constant atau nilai kembalian `Self`"
" (yaitu trait Clone tidak kompatibel dengan dyn.)"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"This is because the associated data would have to be stored in vtables, "
"taking up extra memory."
msgstr ""
"Ini karena data terkait harus disimpan dalam vtable, memakan memori "
"tambahan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"For methods like `clone`, this disqualifies dyn compatibility because the "
"output type depends on the concrete type of `self`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk method seperti `clone`, ini menggugurkan kompatibilitas dyn karena "
"tipe output bergantung pada tipe konkret `self`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-compatible.md
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/1.91.1/reference/items/traits.html#r-items.traits.dyn-compatible"
msgstr ""
"https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/1.91.1/reference/items/traits.html#r-items.traits.dyn-compatible"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid "Generic Function Parameters vs dyn Trait"
msgstr "Parameter Fungsi Generic vs dyn Trait"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid ""
"We have two means of writing polymorphic functions, how do they compare?"
msgstr ""
"Kita memiliki dua cara menulis fungsi polimorfik; bagaimana perbandingannya?"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid "// Two functions are generated, each using static dispatch.\n"
msgstr "// Two functions are generated, each using static dispatch.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid "// One function for both input types using dynamic dispatch.\n"
msgstr "// One function for both input types using dynamic dispatch.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid ""
"We can write polymorphic functions over generics or over trait objects."
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat menulis fungsi polimorfik atas generic atau atas trait object."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid ""
"When writing functions with generic parameters, for each unique type that "
"substitutes a parameter a new version of that function is generated."
msgstr ""
"Saat menulis fungsi dengan parameter generic, untuk setiap tipe unik yang "
"menggantikan parameter, versi baru fungsi tersebut dihasilkan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid ""
"We went over this in monomorphization: in exchange for binary size, we gain "
"a greater capacity for optimization."
msgstr ""
"Kami membahas ini pada monomorphization: dengan menukar ukuran binary, kami "
"memperoleh kapasitas optimasi yang lebih besar."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid ""
"When writing functions that take a trait object, only one version of that "
"function will exist in the final binary (not counting inlining.)"
msgstr ""
"Saat menulis fungsi yang menerima trait object, hanya satu versi fungsi "
"tersebut yang akan ada dalam binary akhir (tidak menghitung inlining.)"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/dyn-vs-generics.md
msgid ""
"Generic parameters are zero-cost other than binary size. Types must be "
"homogenous (all instances of T can only be the same type)."
msgstr ""
"Parameter generic bersifat zero-cost selain ukuran binary. Tipe harus "
"homogen (semua instance T hanya dapat bertipe sama)."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid "// 4 bytes, owned value\n"
msgstr "// 4 bytes, owned value\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid "// 8 bytes, reference\n"
msgstr "// 8 bytes, reference\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid "// 16 bytes, wide pointer\n"
msgstr "// 16 bytes, wide pointer\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid "Trait objects are a limited way of solving problems."
msgstr "Trait object adalah cara terbatas untuk menyelesaikan masalah."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid ""
"If you want to downcast to a concrete type from a trait object, you will "
"need to specify that the trait in question has Any as a supertrait or that "
"the trait object is over the main trait and `Any`."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda ingin melakukan downcast ke tipe konkret dari trait object, Anda "
"perlu menentukan bahwa trait tersebut memiliki Any sebagai supertrait atau "
"trait object-nya atas trait utama dan `Any`."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid "Even then, you will still need to cast a `dyn MyTrait` to `dyn Any`"
msgstr ""
"Bahkan setelah itu, Anda tetap perlu melakukan cast `dyn MyTrait` ke `dyn "
"Any`"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid ""
"Trait objects have overhead in memory, they are \"wide pointers\" that need "
"to hold not just the pointer to the data itself but another pointer for the "
"vtable."
msgstr ""
"Trait object memiliki overhead memori; mereka adalah \"wide pointer\" yang "
"perlu menyimpan bukan hanya pointer ke data itu sendiri tetapi juga pointer "
"lain untuk vtable."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid ""
"Trait objects, being dynamically sized types, can only be used practically "
"via reference or pointer types."
msgstr ""
"Trait object, sebagai tipe berukuran dinamis, hanya dapat digunakan secara "
"praktis melalui tipe reference atau pointer."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/limits.md
msgid ""
"There is a baseline overhead of dereferencing the value and relevant trait "
"methods when using trait objects."
msgstr ""
"Ada overhead dasar untuk melakukan dereference nilai dan method trait "
"terkait saat menggunakan trait object."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid "Heterogeneous data with `dyn trait`"
msgstr "Data Heterogen dengan `dyn trait`"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid "\"λ\""
msgstr "\"λ\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid "\"Woah\""
msgstr "\"Woah\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid "// We know \"item\" implements Display, but we know nothing else!\n"
msgstr "// We know \"item\" implements Display, but we know nothing else!\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid "\"Display output: {}\""
msgstr "\"Display output: {}\""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"`dyn Trait`, being a dynamic dispatch tool, lets us store heterogeneous data"
" in collections."
msgstr ""
"`dyn Trait`, sebagai alat dynamic dispatch, memungkinkan kita menyimpan data"
" heterogen dalam koleksi."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid ""
"In this example, we're storing types that all implement `std::fmt::Display` "
"and printing all items in that collection to screen."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh ini, kami menyimpan tipe yang semuanya mengimplementasikan "
"`std::fmt::Display` dan mencetak semua item dalam koleksi tersebut ke layar."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/heterogeneous.md
msgid "Compare this to how we did heterogenous collections with enums."
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan ini dengan cara kami membuat koleksi heterogen menggunakan enum."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid "Any Trait and Downcasting"
msgstr "Trait Any dan Downcasting"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid "// We can get a unique identifier for the type.\n"
msgstr "// We can get a unique identifier for the type.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid "// We can check if our object is a particular type.\n"
msgstr "// We can check if our object is a particular type.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid "// We can attempt to downcast to a concrete type.\n"
msgstr "// We can attempt to downcast to a concrete type.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"By default, trait objects cannot be downcasted to their concrete type. This "
"is because they do not have any runtime type information that would allow us"
" to determine what the concrete type is, and Rust won't allow us to blindly "
"cast to a type that may not be correct."
msgstr ""
"Secara default, trait object tidak dapat di-downcast ke tipe konkretnya. Ini"
" karena mereka tidak memiliki informasi tipe runtime yang memungkinkan kita "
"menentukan tipe konkretnya, dan Rust tidak mengizinkan kita melakukan cast "
"secara buta ke tipe yang mungkin tidak benar."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"The `Any` trait allows us to downcast values back from dyn values into "
"concrete values by adding the necessary runtime type information."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Any` memungkinkan kita melakukan downcast nilai dari nilai dyn "
"kembali menjadi nilai konkret dengan menambahkan informasi tipe runtime yang"
" diperlukan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"This is an auto trait: like Send/Sync/Sized, it is automatically implemented"
" for any type that meets specific criteria."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah auto trait: seperti Send/Sync/Sized, trait ini secara otomatis "
"diimplementasikan untuk tipe apa pun yang memenuhi kriteria tertentu."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"The criteria for Any is that a type is `'static`. That is, the type does not"
" contain any non-`'static` lifetimes within it."
msgstr ""
"Kriteria untuk Any adalah tipe bersifat `'static`. Artinya, tipe tersebut "
"tidak mengandung lifetime non-`'static` di dalamnya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"Any offers two related behaviors: downcasting, and runtime checking of types"
" being the same."
msgstr ""
"Any menawarkan dua perilaku terkait: downcasting, dan pemeriksaan runtime "
"apakah tipe-tipe sama."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"In the example above, we see the ability to downcast from `Any` into "
"`ThisImplementsAny` automatically."
msgstr ""
"Pada contoh di atas, kita melihat kemampuan melakukan downcast dari `Any` "
"menjadi `ThisImplementsAny` secara otomatis."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"We also see `Any::is` being used to check to see what type the value is."
msgstr ""
"Kita juga melihat `Any::is` digunakan untuk memeriksa tipe nilai tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"`Any` does not implement reflection for a type, it just adds the runtime "
"type information necessary to safely determine the concrete type at runtime."
msgstr ""
"`Any` tidak mengimplementasikan reflection untuk suatu tipe; trait ini hanya"
" menambahkan informasi tipe runtime yang diperlukan untuk menentukan tipe "
"konkret secara aman pada runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"You can add downcasting support to your own traits by using `Any` as a "
"supertrait."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menambahkan dukungan downcasting ke trait Anda sendiri dengan "
"menggunakan `Any` sebagai supertrait."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/any-trait.md
msgid ""
"This also works for generics! We can use `Any` as a trait bound in our "
"generic code, and then \"downcast\" to a concrete type. This is uncommon, "
"though, as generics already have full type information and access to all "
"functionality provided by traits."
msgstr ""
"Ini juga berlaku untuk generic! Kita dapat menggunakan `Any` sebagai trait "
"bound dalam kode generic kami, lalu \"downcast\" ke tipe konkret. Namun ini "
"jarang, karena generic sudah memiliki informasi tipe lengkap dan akses ke "
"semua fungsionalitas yang disediakan trait."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/sealing-with-enums.md
msgid ""
"Motivation: API is designed around a specific list of types that are valid "
"for it, users of the API are not expected to extend it."
msgstr ""
"Motivasi: API dirancang berdasarkan daftar tipe spesifik yang valid "
"untuknya; pengguna API tidak diharapkan memperluasnya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/sealing-with-enums.md
msgid ""
"Enums in Rust are _algebraic data types_, we can define different structures"
" for each variant."
msgstr ""
"Enum di Rust adalah _algebraic data type_; kita dapat mendefinisikan "
"struktur berbeda untuk setiap varian."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/sealing-with-enums.md
msgid ""
"For some domains, this might be enough polymorphism for the problem. "
"Experiment and see what works, what solutions seem to make more sense."
msgstr ""
"Untuk sebagian domain, ini mungkin sudah cukup polimorfisme untuk "
"masalahnya. Bereksperimenlah dan lihat apa yang berhasil, solusi apa yang "
"tampak lebih masuk akal."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/sealing-with-enums.md
msgid ""
"By having the user-facing part of the API refer to an enum, users know what "
"types are valid inputs and can construct those types using the available "
"methods to do so."
msgstr ""
"Dengan membuat bagian API yang menghadap pengguna merujuk enum, pengguna "
"mengetahui tipe apa yang valid sebagai input dan dapat membangun tipe "
"tersebut menggunakan method yang tersedia."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/sealing-with-enums.md
msgid ""
"If the types that make up the enum have invariants that the API internally "
"upholds, and the only way users can construct those types is through "
"constructors that build and maintain those invariants, then you can be sure "
"that inputs to a generic method uphold their invariants."
msgstr ""
"Jika tipe yang menyusun enum memiliki invariant yang dijaga API secara "
"internal, dan satu-satunya cara pengguna membangun tipe tersebut adalah "
"melalui constructor yang membangun dan mempertahankan invariant tersebut, "
"maka Anda dapat yakin bahwa input ke method generic mempertahankan "
"invariant-nya."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/dyn/sealing-with-enums.md
msgid ""
"If the types that make up the enum instead are types the user can freely "
"construct, then sanitisation and interpretation may need to be taken into "
"consideration."
msgstr ""
"Jika tipe yang menyusun enum sebaliknya adalah tipe yang dapat dibangun "
"pengguna dengan bebas, maka sanitasi dan interpretasi mungkin perlu "
"dipertimbangkan."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md
msgid ""
"Enums and `dyn` provide two different approaches to dynamic polymorphism, "
"and in many cases both approaches can be used to solve the same problem. The"
" main trade-offs between the two are:"
msgstr ""
"Enum dan `dyn` menyediakan dua pendekatan berbeda untuk polimorfisme "
"dinamis, dan dalam banyak kasus keduanya dapat digunakan untuk menyelesaikan"
" masalah yang sama. Trade-off utama antara keduanya adalah:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md
msgid ""
"Enums make \"downcasting\" to a subtype easy via pattern matching. "
"Downcasting is possible with `dyn` but is more cumbersome."
msgstr ""
"Enum memudahkan \"downcasting\" ke subtype melalui pattern matching. "
"Downcasting dimungkinkan dengan `dyn` tetapi lebih rumit."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md
msgid ""
"`dyn` allows for downstream code to introduce new types, whereas enums do "
"not."
msgstr ""
"`dyn` memungkinkan kode hilir memperkenalkan tipe baru, sedangkan enum "
"tidak."

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md
msgid ""
"When deciding whether to use an enum or `dyn`, there are two questions to "
"ask:"
msgstr ""
"Saat memutuskan apakah akan menggunakan enum atau `dyn`, ada dua pertanyaan:"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md
msgid ""
"Do I need to be able to downcast to the concrete subtype? Or do I primarily "
"expect to go through a trait interface without needing to know the concrete "
"type?"
msgstr ""
"Apakah saya perlu dapat melakukan downcast ke subtype konkret? Atau apakah "
"saya terutama mengharapkan melewati antarmuka trait tanpa perlu mengetahui "
"tipe konkretnya?"

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md
msgid ""
"Do I know the full set of types up front, or do I need to allow downstream "
"code to extend the set of types I will be handling?"
msgstr ""
"Apakah saya mengetahui seluruh himpunan tipe sejak awal, atau apakah saya "
"perlu mengizinkan kode hilir memperluas himpunan tipe yang akan saya "
"tangani?"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust.md
msgid "From OOP to Rust: Composition, Not Inheritance"
msgstr "Dari OOP ke Rust: Komposisi, Bukan Inheritance"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust.md
msgid ""
"Inheritance is key to OOP's success as a paradigm. Decades of successful "
"software engineering has been done with Inheritance as a core part of "
"business logic."
msgstr ""
"Inheritance adalah kunci keberhasilan OOP sebagai paradigma. Puluhan tahun "
"rekayasa perangkat lunak yang sukses telah dilakukan dengan Inheritance "
"sebagai bagian inti logika bisnis."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust.md
msgid "So why did Rust avoid inheritance?"
msgstr "Jadi mengapa Rust menghindari inheritance?"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust.md
msgid ""
"How do we move from inheritance-based problem solving to Rust's approach?"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana kita beralih dari pemecahan masalah berbasis inheritance ke "
"pendekatan Rust?"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust.md
msgid "How do you represent heterogeneous collections in Rust?"
msgstr "Bagaimana Anda merepresentasikan koleksi heterogen di Rust?"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust.md
msgid ""
"In this section we'll be looking at how to move from thinking about "
"polymorphic problem solving with types in OOP languages like java, C++ etc. "
"to Rust's trait-based approach to Polymorphism."
msgstr ""
"Pada bagian ini kita akan melihat cara beralih dari pemikiran pemecahan "
"masalah polimorfik dengan tipe di bahasa OOP seperti java, C++, dan "
"sebagainya ke pendekatan polimorfisme berbasis trait milik Rust."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust.md
msgid ""
"There will be differences, but there are also plenty of areas in common – "
"especially with modern standards of OOP development. Remember to keep an "
"open mind."
msgstr ""
"Akan ada perbedaan, tetapi juga banyak area kesamaan – terutama dengan "
"standar pengembangan OOP modern. Ingatlah untuk tetap berpikiran terbuka."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "Inheritance in OOP languages"
msgstr "Inheritance di Bahasa OOP"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "// Base class\n"
msgstr "// Base class\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "// Inheriting class\n"
msgstr "// Inheriting class\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "// Create a Car object\n"
msgstr "// Create a Car object\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "// Inherited method\n"
msgstr "// Inherited method\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "// Car's own method\n"
msgstr "// Car's own method\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid ""
"This should be a short reminder for students about what inheritance is in "
"other languages."
msgstr ""
"Ini seharusnya menjadi pengingat singkat bagi siswa tentang apa itu "
"inheritance di bahasa lain."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid ""
"Inheritance is a mechanism where a \"child\" type gains the fields and "
"methods of the \"parent\" types it is inheriting from."
msgstr ""
"Inheritance adalah mekanisme ketika tipe \"anak\" memperoleh field dan "
"method dari tipe \"induk\" yang diwarisinya."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "Methods are able to be overridden as-needed by the inheriting type."
msgstr "Method dapat di-override sesuai kebutuhan oleh tipe yang mewarisi."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/inheritance.md
msgid "Can call methods of inherited-from classes with `super`."
msgstr "Dapat memanggil method class yang diwarisi dengan `super`."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "// methods\n"
msgstr "// methods\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "// 🔨❌, Rust does not have inheritance!\n"
msgstr "// 🔨❌, Rust does not have inheritance!\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "// Inherited \"id\" field\n"
msgstr "// Inherited \"id\" field\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid ""
"// methods, but also includes Id's methods, or maybe overrides to\n"
"    // those methods.\n"
msgstr ""
"// methods, but also includes Id's methods, or maybe overrides to\n"
"    // those methods.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "// ✅\n"
msgstr "// ✅\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "// All of data's methods that aren't from traits.\n"
msgstr "// All of data's methods that aren't from traits.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "// Implementations for traits in separate impl blocks.\n"
msgstr "// Implementations for traits in separate impl blocks.\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "Inheritance comes with a number of downsides."
msgstr "Inheritance memiliki sejumlah kekurangan."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "Heterogeneous by default:"
msgstr "Heterogen secara default:"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid ""
"Class inheritance implicitly allows types of different classes to be used "
"interchangeably, without being able to specify a concrete type or if a type "
"is identical to another."
msgstr ""
"Inheritance class secara implisit memungkinkan tipe dari class berbeda "
"digunakan secara bergantian, tanpa dapat menentukan tipe konkret atau apakah"
" suatu tipe identik dengan tipe lain."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid ""
"For operations like equality or comparison this allows for comparison and "
"equality that throws an error or otherwise panics."
msgstr ""
"Untuk operasi seperti kesetaraan atau perbandingan, ini memungkinkan "
"perbandingan dan kesetaraan yang melempar error atau panic."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid ""
"Multiple sources of truth for what makes up a data structure and how it "
"behaves:"
msgstr ""
"Banyak sumber kebenaran tentang apa yang menyusun struktur data dan "
"bagaimana perilakunya:"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "A type's fields are obscured by the inheritance hierarchy."
msgstr "Field suatu tipe tersembunyi oleh hierarki inheritance."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid ""
"A type's methods could be overriding a parent type or be overridden by a "
"child type, it's hard to tell what the behavior of a type is in complex "
"codebases maintained by multiple parties."
msgstr ""
"Method suatu tipe bisa meng-override tipe induk atau di-override oleh tipe "
"anak; sulit menentukan perilaku suatu tipe dalam basis kode kompleks yang "
"dipelihara banyak pihak."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid "Dynamic dispatch as default adds overhead from vtable lookups:"
msgstr ""
"Dynamic dispatch sebagai default menambah overhead dari pencarian vtable:"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid ""
"For dynamic dispatch to work, there needs to be somewhere to store "
"information on what methods to call and other pieces of runtime-known pieces"
" of information on the type."
msgstr ""
"Agar dynamic dispatch berfungsi, perlu ada tempat menyimpan informasi "
"tentang method apa yang harus dipanggil dan informasi lain tentang tipe yang"
" diketahui pada runtime."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/why-no-inheritance.md
msgid ""
"This store is the `vtable` for a value. Method calls will require more "
"dereferences than calling a method for a type that is known at compile time."
msgstr ""
"Tempat penyimpanan ini adalah `vtable` untuk suatu nilai. Pemanggilan method"
" akan memerlukan lebih banyak dereference daripada memanggil method untuk "
"tipe yang diketahui pada waktu kompilasi."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid "// Data\n"
msgstr "// Data\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid "// Concrete behavior\n"
msgstr "// Concrete behavior\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid "// Abstract behavior\n"
msgstr "// Abstract behavior\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid "// Instanced behavior\n"
msgstr "// Instanced behavior\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid ""
"From Rust's perspective, one where Inheritance was never there, introducing "
"inheritance would look like muddying the water between types and traits."
msgstr ""
"Dari perspektif Rust, yang tidak pernah memiliki Inheritance, memperkenalkan"
" inheritance akan tampak seperti mengaburkan batas antara tipe dan trait."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid "A type is a concrete piece of data and its associated behavior."
msgstr "Tipe adalah bagian data konkret dan perilaku terkaitnya."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid "A trait is abstract behavior that must be implemented by a type."
msgstr ""
"Trait adalah perilaku abstrak yang harus diimplementasikan oleh suatu tipe."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid ""
"A class is a combination of data, behavior, and overrides to that behavior."
msgstr ""
"Class adalah kombinasi data, perilaku, dan override terhadap perilaku "
"tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid ""
"Coming from Rust, an inheritable class looks like a type that is also a "
"trait."
msgstr ""
"Dari sudut pandang Rust, class yang dapat diwarisi tampak seperti tipe yang "
"sekaligus trait."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid ""
"This is not an upside, as we can no longer reason about concrete types."
msgstr ""
"Ini bukan keunggulan, karena kita tidak lagi dapat menalar tentang tipe "
"konkret."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid ""
"Without being able to separate the two, it becomes difficult to reason about"
" generic behavior vs concrete specifics, because in OOP these two concepts "
"are tied up in each other."
msgstr ""
"Tanpa dapat memisahkan keduanya, menjadi sulit menalar perilaku generic "
"versus spesifik konkret, karena dalam OOP kedua konsep ini saling terikat."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/switch-perspective.md
msgid ""
"The convenience of flat field access and DRY in type definitions is not "
"worth the loss in specificity between writing code that delineates between "
"behavior and data."
msgstr ""
"Kemudahan akses field datar dan DRY dalam definisi tipe tidak sebanding "
"dengan hilangnya spesifisitas dalam menulis kode yang membedakan perilaku "
"dan data."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid "\"Inheritance\" in Rust: Supertraits"
msgstr "\"Inheritance\" di Rust: Supertrait"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"In Rust, traits can depend on other traits. We're already familiar with "
"Traits being able to have Supertraits."
msgstr ""
"Di Rust, trait dapat bergantung pada trait lain. Kita sudah mengenal Trait "
"yang dapat memiliki Supertrait."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid "This looks superficially similar to inheritance."
msgstr "Ini tampak serupa dengan inheritance secara permukaan."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"This is a mechanism like inheritance, but separates the data from the "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah mekanisme seperti inheritance, tetapi memisahkan data dari "
"perilaku."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid "Keeps behavior in a state where it's easy to reason about."
msgstr "Menjaga perilaku dalam keadaan yang mudah dinalar."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid "Makes what we aim to achieve with \"multiple inheritance\" easier too:"
msgstr "Juga memudahkan pencapaian tujuan \"multiple inheritance\":"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"We only care about what behavior a type is capable of at the point where we "
"clarify we want that behavior (when bounding a generic by traits)."
msgstr ""
"Kita hanya peduli pada perilaku apa yang mampu dilakukan suatu tipe pada "
"titik ketika kita menyatakan menginginkan perilaku tersebut (saat membatasi "
"generic dengan trait)."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"By specifying multiple traits on a generic, we know that the type has the "
"methods of all those traits."
msgstr ""
"Dengan menentukan beberapa trait pada generic, kita mengetahui bahwa tipe "
"memiliki method dari semua trait tersebut."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/supertraits.md
msgid ""
"Does not involve inheritance of fields. A trait doesn't expose fields, only "
"methods and associated types / constants."
msgstr ""
"Tidak melibatkan pewarisan field. Trait tidak mengekspos field, hanya method"
" dan associated type / constant."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/composition.md
msgid ""
"Rather than mixins or inheritance, we compose types by creating fields of "
"different types."
msgstr ""
"Alih-alih mixin atau inheritance, kami menyusun tipe dengan membuat field "
"bertipe berbeda."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/composition.md
msgid ""
"This has downsides, largely in ergonomics of field access, but gives "
"developers a lot of control and clarity over what a type does and it has "
"access to."
msgstr ""
"Ini memiliki kekurangan, terutama pada ergonomi akses field, tetapi memberi "
"developer banyak kontrol dan kejelasan tentang apa yang dilakukan suatu tipe"
" dan apa yang dapat diaksesnya."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/composition.md
msgid ""
"When deriving traits, make sure all the field types of a struct or variant "
"types of an enum implement that trait. Derive macros often assume all types "
"that compose a new type implement that trait already."
msgstr ""
"Saat melakukan derive trait, pastikan semua tipe field struct atau tipe "
"varian enum mengimplementasikan trait tersebut. Derive macro sering "
"mengasumsikan semua tipe yang menyusun tipe baru sudah mengimplementasikan "
"trait itu."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid "// Problem: implementing a GUI API\n"
msgstr "// Problem: implementing a GUI API\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid "// Question: What's the minimum useful behavior for a drawing API?\n"
msgstr "// Question: What's the minimum useful behavior for a drawing API?\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid "\"arc of radius \""
msgstr "\"arc of radius \""

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid "// Question: What's a good API for users?\n"
msgstr "// Question: What's a good API for users?\n"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"You're already adept at breaking down problems, but you're likely used to "
"reaching for OOP-style methods."
msgstr ""
"Anda sudah mahir memecah masalah, tetapi kemungkinan terbiasa menggunakan "
"method bergaya OOP."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"This isn't a drastic change, it just requires re-ordering the way you "
"approach things."
msgstr ""
"Ini bukan perubahan drastis; hanya memerlukan penataan ulang cara Anda "
"mendekati masalah."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid "Try to solve the problem with either Generics & Traits or Enums first."
msgstr ""
"Coba selesaikan masalah dengan Generic & Trait atau Enum terlebih dahulu."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"Does the problem require a specific set of types? An enum may be the "
"cleanest way of solving this problem."
msgstr ""
"Apakah masalah memerlukan himpunan tipe tertentu? Enum mungkin cara paling "
"bersih untuk menyelesaikannya."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"Does the problem really care about the specifics of the types involved, or "
"can behavior be focused on?"
msgstr ""
"Apakah masalah benar-benar peduli pada spesifik tipe yang terlibat, atau "
"dapatkah fokus pada perilaku?"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"Organize your problem solving around finding a minimum viable amount of "
"knowledge to implement something."
msgstr ""
"Atur pemecahan masalah Anda di sekitar pencarian pengetahuan minimum yang "
"layak untuk mengimplementasikan sesuatu."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid "Does a trait already exist for this use case? If so, use it!"
msgstr "Apakah trait sudah ada untuk kasus penggunaan ini? Jika ya, gunakan!"

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"If you really do need heterogeneous collections, use them! They exist in "
"Rust as a tool for a reason."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda benar-benar memerlukan koleksi heterogen, gunakanlah! Koleksi "
"tersebut ada di Rust sebagai alat karena suatu alasan."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"Be aware of the XY problem: a problem may seem most easily addressable by "
"one solution, but it might not tackle the root cause and could lead to new "
"difficult problems popping up in the future."
msgstr ""
"Sadari XY problem: suatu masalah mungkin tampak paling mudah diatasi dengan "
"satu solusi, tetapi solusi itu mungkin tidak menangani akar masalah dan "
"dapat memunculkan masalah sulit baru di masa mendatang."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"That is, be certain that dynamic dispatch with trait objects is what you "
"need before you commit to using them."
msgstr ""
"Artinya, pastikan dynamic dispatch dengan trait object adalah yang Anda "
"butuhkan sebelum memutuskan menggunakannya."

#: src/idiomatic/from-oop-to-rust/problem-solving.md
msgid ""
"Be certain that traits are what you need before you commit to using them."
msgstr ""
"Pastikan trait adalah yang Anda butuhkan sebelum memutuskan menggunakannya."

