#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction.md src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid "Outline"
msgstr "Garis Besar"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction.md
msgid "25 minutes"
msgstr "25 menit"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "“Unsafe Rust is a superset of Safe Rust.”"
msgstr "“Unsafe Rust adalah superset dari Safe Rust.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid ""
"“Unsafe Rust adds extra capabilities, such as allowing you to dereference "
"raw pointers and call functions that can break Rust’s safety guarantees if "
"called incorrectly.”"
msgstr ""
"“Unsafe Rust menambahkan kemampuan ekstra, seperti memungkinkan Anda "
"melakukan dereference raw pointer dan memanggil fungsi yang dapat melanggar "
"jaminan keamanan Rust jika dipanggil secara keliru.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "“These extra capabilities are referred to as _unsafe operations_.”"
msgstr "“Kemampuan ekstra ini disebut _unsafe operation_.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid ""
"“Unsafe operations provide the foundation that the Rust standard library is "
"built on. For example, without the ability to dereference a raw pointer, it "
"would be impossible to implement `Vec` or `Box`.”"
msgstr ""
"“Unsafe operation menyediakan fondasi tempat standard library Rust dibangun."
" Misalnya, tanpa kemampuan melakukan dereference raw pointer, mustahil "
"mengimplementasikan `Vec` atau `Box`.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid ""
"“The compiler will still assist you while writing Unsafe Rust. Borrow "
"checking and type safety still apply. Unsafe operations have their own "
"rules, which we’ll learn about in this class.”"
msgstr ""
"“Compiler tetap akan membantu Anda saat menulis Unsafe Rust. Borrow checking"
" dan type safety tetap berlaku. Unsafe operation memiliki aturannya sendiri,"
" yang akan kita pelajari di kelas ini.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid ""
"The unsafe operations from the [Rust Reference](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/unsafety.html) (Avoid spending too much time):"
msgstr ""
"Unsafe operation dari [Rust Reference](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/unsafety.html) (Hindari menghabiskan terlalu banyak "
"waktu):"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid ""
"The following language level features cannot be used in the safe subset of "
"Rust:"
msgstr ""
"Fitur tingkat bahasa berikut tidak dapat digunakan dalam subset safe Rust:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "Dereferencing a raw pointer."
msgstr "Melakukan dereference raw pointer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "Reading or writing a mutable or unsafe external static variable."
msgstr ""
"Membaca atau menulis variabel static eksternal yang mutable atau unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "Accessing a field of a union, other than to assign to it."
msgstr "Mengakses field union, selain untuk menetapkan nilainya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "Calling an `unsafe` function."
msgstr "Memanggil fungsi `unsafe`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid ""
"Calling a safe function marked with a `<target_feature>` from a function "
"that does not have a `<target_feature>` attribute enabling the same "
"features."
msgstr ""
"Memanggil fungsi safe yang ditandai dengan `<target_feature>` dari fungsi "
"yang tidak memiliki atribut `<target_feature>` yang mengaktifkan fitur yang "
"sama."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "Implementing an unsafe trait."
msgstr "Mengimplementasikan trait unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "Declaring an extern block."
msgstr "Mendeklarasikan block extern."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/definition.md
msgid "Applying an unsafe attribute to an item."
msgstr "Menerapkan atribut unsafe pada item."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid "Why the unsafe keyword exists"
msgstr "Mengapa Keyword unsafe Ada"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid "Rust ensures safety"
msgstr "Rust Menjamin Keamanan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid "But there are limits to what the compiler can do"
msgstr "Tetapi Ada Batas pada Apa yang Dapat Dilakukan Compiler"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid ""
"The unsafe keyword allows programmers to assume responsibility for Rust’s "
"rules"
msgstr ""
"Keyword unsafe memungkinkan programmer mengambil tanggung jawab atas aturan "
"Rust"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid "“A fundamental goal of Rust is to ensure memory safety.”"
msgstr "“Tujuan fundamental Rust adalah memastikan keamanan memori.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid ""
"“But, there are limits. Some safety considerations cannot be expressed in a "
"programming language. Even if they could be, there are limits to what the "
"Rust compiler can control.”"
msgstr ""
"“Tetapi ada batas. Sebagian pertimbangan keamanan tidak dapat diekspresikan "
"dalam bahasa pemrograman. Bahkan jika bisa, ada batas pada apa yang dapat "
"dikendalikan compiler Rust.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid ""
"“The `unsafe` keyword shifts the burden of upholding Rust’s rules from the "
"compiler to the programmer.”"
msgstr ""
"“Keyword `unsafe` memindahkan beban menegakkan aturan Rust dari compiler ke "
"programmer.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/purpose.md
msgid ""
"“When you see the `unsafe` keyword, you are seeing responsibility shift from"
" the compiler to the programmer."
msgstr ""
"“Saat Anda melihat keyword `unsafe`, Anda melihat pergeseran tanggung jawab "
"dari compiler ke programmer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "The unsafe keyword has two roles"
msgstr "Keyword unsafe Memiliki Dua Peran"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "_Creating_ APIs with safety considerations"
msgstr "_Membuat_ API dengan pertimbangan keamanan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "unsafe functions: `unsafe fn get_unchecked(&self) { ... }`"
msgstr "fungsi unsafe: `unsafe fn get_unchecked(&self) { ... }`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "unsafe traits: `unsafe trait Send {}`"
msgstr "trait unsafe: `unsafe trait Send {}`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "_Using_ APIs with safety considerations"
msgstr "_Menggunakan_ API dengan pertimbangan keamanan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "invoking built-in unsafe operators: `unsafe { *ptr }`"
msgstr "memanggil operator unsafe bawaan: `unsafe { *ptr }`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "calling unsafe functions: `unsafe { x.get_unchecked() }`"
msgstr "memanggil fungsi unsafe: `unsafe { x.get_unchecked() }`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "implementing unsafe traits: `unsafe impl Send for Counter {}`"
msgstr "mengimplementasikan trait unsafe: `unsafe impl Send for Counter {}`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "Two roles:"
msgstr "Dua peran:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"**Creating** APIs with safety considerations and defining what needs to be "
"considered"
msgstr ""
"**Membuat** API dengan pertimbangan keamanan dan mendefinisikan apa yang "
"perlu dipertimbangkan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"**Using** APIs with safety considerations and confirming that the "
"consideration has been made"
msgstr ""
"**Menggunakan** API dengan pertimbangan keamanan dan memastikan pertimbangan"
" tersebut telah dilakukan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "Creating APIs with safety considerations"
msgstr "Membuat API dengan Pertimbangan Keamanan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“First, the unsafe keyword enables you to create APIs that can break Rust’s "
"safety guarantees. Specifically, you need to use the unsafe keyword when "
"defining unsafe functions and unsafe traits."
msgstr ""
"“Pertama, keyword unsafe memungkinkan Anda membuat API yang dapat melanggar "
"jaminan keamanan Rust. Secara khusus, Anda perlu menggunakan keyword unsafe "
"saat mendefinisikan fungsi unsafe dan trait unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“When used in this role, you’re informing users of your API that they need "
"to be careful.”"
msgstr ""
"“Saat digunakan dalam peran ini, Anda memberi tahu pengguna API Anda bahwa "
"mereka perlu berhati-hati.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“The creator of the API should communicate what care needs to be taken. "
"Unsafe APIs are not complete without documentation about safety "
"requirements. Callers need to know that they have satisfied any "
"requirements, and that’s impossible if they’re not written down.”"
msgstr ""
"“Pembuat API sebaiknya mengomunikasikan kehati-hatian apa yang diperlukan. "
"API unsafe tidak lengkap tanpa dokumentasi tentang persyaratan keamanan. "
"Pemanggil perlu mengetahui bahwa mereka telah memenuhi persyaratan apa pun, "
"dan itu mustahil jika tidak dituliskan.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid "Using APIs with safety considerations"
msgstr "Menggunakan API dengan Pertimbangan Keamanan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“The unsafe keyword adopts its other role, using APIs, when it is used "
"nearby to a curly brace."
msgstr ""
"“Keyword unsafe mengambil peran lainnya, yaitu menggunakan API, ketika "
"digunakan di dekat kurung kurawal."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“When used in this role, the unsafe keyword means that the author has been "
"careful. They have verified that the code is safe and is providing an "
"assurance to others.”"
msgstr ""
"“Saat digunakan dalam peran ini, keyword unsafe berarti penulis telah "
"berhati-hati. Mereka telah memverifikasi bahwa kode aman dan memberikan "
"jaminan kepada pihak lain.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“Unsafe blocks are most common. They allow you to invoke unsafe functions "
"that have been defined using the first role."
msgstr ""
"“Block unsafe paling umum. Block ini memungkinkan Anda memanggil fungsi "
"unsafe yang telah didefinisikan menggunakan peran pertama."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“Unsafe blocks also allow you to perform operations which the compiler knows"
" are unsafe, such as dereferencing a raw pointer.”"
msgstr ""
"“Block unsafe juga memungkinkan Anda melakukan operasi yang diketahui "
"compiler tidak aman, seperti melakukan dereference raw pointer.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/two-roles.md
msgid ""
"“You might also see the unsafe keyword being used to implement unsafe "
"traits."
msgstr ""
"“Anda mungkin juga melihat keyword unsafe digunakan untuk "
"mengimplementasikan trait unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up.md
msgid "Warm-up examples"
msgstr "Contoh Pemanasan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up.md
msgid "Examples to demonstrate:"
msgstr "Contoh untuk didemonstrasikan:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up.md
msgid "using an [unsafe block](warm-up/unsafe-block.md) (`unsafe { ... }`)"
msgstr ""
"menggunakan [block unsafe](warm-up/unsafe-block.md) (`unsafe { ... }`)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up.md
msgid "defining an [unsafe function](warm-up/unsafe-fn.md) (`unsafe fn`)"
msgstr "mendefinisikan [fungsi unsafe](warm-up/unsafe-fn.md) (`unsafe fn`)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up.md
msgid ""
"[implementing](warm-up/unsafe-impl.md) an unsafe trait (`unsafe impl { ... "
"}`)"
msgstr ""
"[mengimplementasikan](warm-up/unsafe-impl.md) trait unsafe (`unsafe impl { "
"... }`)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up.md
msgid "defining an [unsafe trait](warm-up/unsafe-trait.md) (`unsafe trait`)"
msgstr ""
"mendefinisikan [trait unsafe](warm-up/unsafe-trait.md) (`unsafe trait`)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-block.md
msgid ""
"Walk through the code. Confirm that the audience is familiar with the "
"dereference operator."
msgstr "Telusuri kodenya. Pastikan audiens mengenal operator dereference."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-block.md
msgid "Attempt to compile the code, trigger the compiler error."
msgstr "Coba kompilasi kode, picu error compiler."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-block.md
msgid "Add the unsafe block:"
msgstr "Tambahkan block unsafe:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-block.md
msgid ""
"Prompt audience for a code review. Guide learners towards adding a safety "
"comment."
msgstr ""
"Ajak audiens melakukan code review. Pandu pembelajar untuk menambahkan "
"komentar safety."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-block.md
msgid "Add the safety comment:"
msgstr "Tambahkan komentar safety:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-block.md
msgid "// SAFETY: `i` must be within 0..numbers.len()\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: `i` must be within 0..numbers.len()\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-block.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/c-library-example.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/cpp-library-example.md
msgid "_Suggested Solution_"
msgstr "_Solusi yang Disarankan_"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"/// Convert a nullable pointer to a reference.\n"
"///\n"
"/// Returns `None` when `p` is null, otherwise wraps `val` in `Some`.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Convert a nullable pointer to a reference.\n"
"///\n"
"/// Returns `None` when `p` is null, otherwise wraps `val` in `Some`.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid "// SAFETY: `ptr` is non-null\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: `ptr` is non-null\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“This looks as though it’s safe code, however it actually requires an unsafe"
" block.”"
msgstr ""
"“Ini tampak seperti kode safe, tetapi sebenarnya memerlukan block unsafe.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"Highlight the dereference operation, i.e. `*p` within the unsafe block."
msgstr "Soroti operasi dereference, yaitu `*p` di dalam block unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“Callers must ensure that the `ptr` is null, or that it may be converted to "
"a reference."
msgstr ""
"“Pemanggil harus memastikan bahwa `ptr` bernilai null, atau bahwa pointer "
"tersebut dapat dikonversi menjadi reference."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“It may be counter-intuitive, but many pointers cannot be converted to "
"references."
msgstr ""
"“Mungkin berlawanan dengan intuisi, tetapi banyak pointer tidak dapat "
"dikonversi menjadi reference."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“Among other issues, a pointer could be created that points to some "
"arbitrary bits rather than a valid value. That’s not something that Rust "
"allows and something that this function needs to protect itself against."
msgstr ""
"“Antara lain, pointer dapat dibuat untuk menunjuk ke bit arbitrer alih-alih "
"nilai yang valid. Itu bukan sesuatu yang diizinkan Rust dan merupakan hal "
"yang perlu dilindungi fungsi ini."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“So we, as API designers, have two paths. We can either try to assume "
"responsibility for guarding against invalid inputs, or we can shift that "
"responsibility to the caller with the unsafe keyword.”"
msgstr ""
"“Jadi kami, sebagai perancang API, memiliki dua jalur. Kami dapat mencoba "
"mengambil tanggung jawab untuk menjaga terhadap input tidak valid, atau "
"mengalihkan tanggung jawab itu kepada pemanggil dengan keyword unsafe.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“The first path is a difficult one. We’re accepting a generic type T, which "
"is all possible types that implement Sized. That’s a lot of types!"
msgstr ""
"“Jalur pertama sulit. Kami menerima tipe generic T, yaitu semua tipe yang "
"mungkin mengimplementasikan Sized. Itu banyak sekali tipe!"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid "“Therefore, the second path makes more sense."
msgstr "“Oleh karena itu, jalur kedua lebih masuk akal."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid "_Extra content (time permitting)_"
msgstr "_Konten Tambahan (jika waktu memungkinkan)_"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“By the way, if you’re interested in the details of pointers and what the "
"rules of converting them to references are, the standard library has a lot "
"of useful documentation. You should also look into the source code of many "
"of the methods on std::pointer."
msgstr ""
"“Ngomong-ngomong, jika Anda tertarik pada detail pointer dan aturan "
"konversinya menjadi reference, standard library memiliki banyak dokumentasi "
"berguna. Anda juga sebaiknya melihat kode sumber banyak method pada "
"std::pointer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"“For example, the `ptr_to_ref` function on this slide actually exists in the"
" standard library as the `as_mut` method on pointers.”"
msgstr ""
"“Misalnya, fungsi `ptr_to_ref` pada slide ini sebenarnya ada di standard "
"library sebagai method `as_mut` pada pointer.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-fn.md
msgid ""
"Open the documentation for [std::pointer.as_mut](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/primitive.pointer.html#method.as_mut) and highlight the Safety "
"section."
msgstr ""
"Buka dokumentasi [std::pointer.as_mut](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/primitive.pointer.html#method.as_mut) dan soroti bagian Safety."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid ""
"“Before we take a look at the code, we should double check that everyone "
"knows what a trait is. Is anyone able to explain traits for the rest of the "
"class?"
msgstr ""
"“Sebelum kita melihat kode, kita sebaiknya memastikan semua orang mengetahui"
" apa itu trait. Adakah yang dapat menjelaskan trait kepada seluruh kelas?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid ""
"“Traits are often described as a way to create shared behavior. Thinking "
"about traits as shared behavior focuses on the syntax of methods and their "
"signatures."
msgstr ""
"“Trait sering dijelaskan sebagai cara menciptakan perilaku bersama. "
"Memikirkan trait sebagai perilaku bersama berfokus pada sintaks method dan "
"signature-nya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid ""
"“There’s also a deeper way to think of traits: as sets of requirements. This"
" emphasizes the shared semantics of the implementing types."
msgstr ""
"“Ada juga cara yang lebih mendalam untuk memahami trait: sebagai himpunan "
"persyaratan. Ini menekankan semantik bersama dari tipe yang "
"mengimplementasikannya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid "“Can anyone explain what the `Send` and `Sync` traits are?"
msgstr "“Adakah yang dapat menjelaskan apa itu trait `Send` dan `Sync`?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid "If no"
msgstr "Jika tidak ada"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid ""
"“Send and Sync relate to concurrency. There are many details, but broadly "
"speaking, Send types can be shared between threads by value. Sync types must"
" be shared by reference."
msgstr ""
"“Send dan Sync berkaitan dengan konkurensi. Ada banyak detail, tetapi secara"
" umum, tipe Send dapat dibagikan antar-thread by value. Tipe Sync harus "
"dibagikan by reference."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid ""
"There are many rules to follow to ensure that it’s safe to share data across"
" thread boundaries. Those rules cannot be checked by the compiler, and "
"therefore the code author must take responsibility for upholding them."
msgstr ""
"Ada banyak aturan yang harus diikuti untuk memastikan aman membagikan data "
"melintasi batas thread. Aturan tersebut tidak dapat diperiksa compiler, "
"sehingga penulis kode harus bertanggung jawab menegakkannya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid ""
"Arc implements Send and Sync, therefore it’s safe for our clock to as well."
msgstr ""
"Arc mengimplementasikan Send dan Sync, sehingga clock kami juga aman untuk "
"mengimplementasikan keduanya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-impl.md
msgid ""
"It may be useful to point out that the word _atomic_ has the meaning of "
"“indivisible” or “whole” from Ancient Greek, rather than the contemporary "
"English sense of “tiny particle”."
msgstr ""
"Mungkin berguna untuk menunjukkan bahwa kata _atomic_ memiliki makna “tidak "
"dapat dibagi” atau “utuh” dari bahasa Yunani Kuno, bukan makna bahasa "
"Inggris kontemporer “partikel kecil”."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-trait.md
msgid "/// Indicates that the type uses 32 bits of memory.\n"
msgstr "/// Indicates that the type uses 32 bits of memory.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-trait.md
msgid "“Now let’s define our own unsafe trait.”"
msgstr "“Sekarang mari kita definisikan trait unsafe kita sendiri.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-trait.md
msgid "Add the unsafe keyword and compile the code."
msgstr "Tambahkan keyword unsafe dan kompilasi kodenya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-trait.md
msgid ""
"“If the requirements of the trait are semantic, then your trait may not need"
" any methods at all. The documentation is essential, however.”"
msgstr ""
"“Jika persyaratan trait bersifat semantik, trait Anda mungkin tidak "
"memerlukan method sama sekali. Namun dokumentasinya tetap penting.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-trait.md
msgid ""
"“Traits without methods are called marker traits. When implementing them for"
" types, you are adding information to the type system. You have now given "
"the compiler the ability to talk about types that meet the requirements "
"described in the documentation.”"
msgstr ""
"“Trait tanpa method disebut marker trait. Saat mengimplementasikannya untuk "
"tipe, Anda menambahkan informasi ke sistem tipe. Anda sekarang memberi "
"compiler kemampuan membahas tipe yang memenuhi persyaratan yang dijelaskan "
"dalam dokumentasi.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust.md
msgid "Characteristics of unsafe"
msgstr "Karakteristik unsafe"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust.md
msgid "[Dangerous](characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md)"
msgstr "[Berbahaya](characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust.md
msgid ""
"[Sometimes necessary](characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md)"
msgstr ""
"[Kadang Diperlukan](characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust.md
msgid "[Sometimes useful](characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-useful.md)"
msgstr "[Kadang Berguna](characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-useful.md)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md
msgid "Unsafe is dangerous"
msgstr "Unsafe Itu Berbahaya"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md
msgid ""
"“Use-after-free (UAF), integer overflows, and out of bounds (OOB) "
"reads/writes comprise 90% of vulnerabilities with OOB being the most "
"common.”"
msgstr ""
"“Use-after-free (UAF), integer overflow, dan pembacaan/penulisan out of "
"bounds (OOB) mencakup 90% kerentanan, dengan OOB sebagai yang paling umum.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md
msgid ""
"\\--- **Jeff Vander Stoep and Chong Zang**, Google. \"[Queue the Hardening "
"Enhancements](https://security.googleblog.com/2019/05/queue-hardening-"
"enhancements.html)\""
msgstr ""
"\\--- **Jeff Vander Stoep dan Chong Zang**, Google. \"[Queue the Hardening "
"Enhancements](https://security.googleblog.com/2019/05/queue-hardening-"
"enhancements.html)\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md
msgid ""
"“The software industry has gathered lots of evidence that unsafe code is "
"difficult to write correctly and creates very serious problems.”"
msgstr ""
"“Industri perangkat lunak telah mengumpulkan banyak bukti bahwa kode unsafe "
"sulit ditulis dengan benar dan menimbulkan masalah yang sangat serius.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md
msgid ""
"“The issues in this list are eliminated by Rust. The unsafe keyword lets "
"them back into your source code.”"
msgstr ""
"“Masalah dalam daftar ini dieliminasi oleh Rust. Keyword unsafe "
"membiarkannya masuk kembali ke kode sumber Anda.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/dangerous.md
msgid "“Be careful.”"
msgstr "“Berhati-hatilah.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid "Unsafe is sometimes necessary"
msgstr "Unsafe Kadang Diperlukan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid ""
"The Rust compiler can only enforce its rules for code that it has compiled."
msgstr ""
"Compiler Rust hanya dapat menegakkan aturannya untuk kode yang telah "
"dikompilasinya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid "\"{pid}\""
msgstr "\"{pid}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid "“There are some activities that _require_ unsafe."
msgstr "“Ada beberapa aktivitas yang _memerlukan_ unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid ""
"“The Rust compiler cannot verify that external functions comply with Rust's "
"memory guarantees. Therefore, invoking external functions requires an unsafe"
" block.”"
msgstr ""
"“Compiler Rust tidak dapat memverifikasi bahwa fungsi eksternal mematuhi "
"jaminan memori Rust. Oleh karena itu, memanggil fungsi eksternal memerlukan "
"block unsafe.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid "Optional:"
msgstr "Opsional:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid ""
"“Working with the external environment often involves sharing memory. The "
"interface that computers provide is a memory address (a pointer).”"
msgstr ""
"“Bekerja dengan lingkungan eksternal sering melibatkan berbagi memori. "
"Antarmuka yang disediakan komputer adalah alamat memori (pointer).”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid ""
"“Here's an example that asks the Linux kernel to write to memory that we "
"control:"
msgstr ""
"“Berikut contoh yang meminta kernel Linux menulis ke memori yang kami "
"kendalikan:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid "\"{buf:?}\""
msgstr "\"{buf:?}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-necessary.md
msgid ""
"“This FFI call reaches into the operating system to fill our buffer (`buf`)."
" As well as calling an external function, we must mark the boundary as "
"`unsafe` because the compiler cannot verify how the OS touches that memory.”"
msgstr ""
"“Pemanggilan FFI ini menjangkau sistem operasi untuk mengisi buffer kami "
"(`buf`). Selain memanggil fungsi eksternal, kita harus menandai batas "
"tersebut sebagai `unsafe` karena compiler tidak dapat memverifikasi "
"bagaimana OS menyentuh memori itu.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-useful.md
msgid "Unsafe is sometimes useful"
msgstr "Unsafe Kadang Berguna"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-useful.md
msgid "Your code can go faster!"
msgstr "Kode Anda dapat berjalan lebih cepat!"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-useful.md
msgid "Code using `unsafe` _might_ be faster."
msgstr "Kode yang menggunakan `unsafe` _mungkin_ lebih cepat."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-useful.md
msgid ""
"`fast_sum()` skips bounds checks. However, benchmarking is necessary to "
"validate performance claims. For cases like this, Rust's iterators can "
"usually elide bounds checks anyway."
msgstr ""
"`fast_sum()` melewati pemeriksaan bounds. Namun, benchmarking diperlukan "
"untuk memvalidasi klaim performa. Untuk kasus seperti ini, iterator Rust "
"biasanya dapat menghilangkan pemeriksaan bounds."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/characteristics-of-unsafe-rust/sometimes-useful.md
msgid ""
"Optional: [show identical generated "
"assembly](https://rust.godbolt.org/z/d48v1Y5aj) for the two functions."
msgstr ""
"Opsional: [tunjukkan assembly yang dihasilkan "
"identik](https://rust.godbolt.org/z/d48v1Y5aj) untuk kedua fungsi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Unsafe keyword shifts responsibility"
msgstr "Keyword unsafe Menggeser Tanggung Jawab"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Is Memory Safe?"
msgstr "Apakah Memori Aman?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Responsibility for Memory Safety"
msgstr "Tanggung Jawab atas Keamanan Memori"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Compiler"
msgstr "Compiler"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Programmer"
msgstr "Programmer"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Who has responsibility for memory safety?"
msgstr "Siapa yang bertanggung jawab atas keamanan memori?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Safe Rust → compiler"
msgstr "Safe Rust → compiler"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid "Unsafe Rust → programmer"
msgstr "Unsafe Rust → programmer"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid ""
"“While writing safe Rust, you cannot create memory safety problems. The "
"compiler will ensure that a program with mistakes will not build.”"
msgstr ""
"“Saat menulis safe Rust, Anda tidak dapat menciptakan masalah keamanan "
"memori. Compiler akan memastikan program yang bermasalah tidak akan di-"
"build.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid ""
"“The `unsafe` keyword shifts responsibility for maintaining memory safety "
"from the compiler to programmers. It signals that there are preconditions "
"that must be satisfied."
msgstr ""
"“Keyword `unsafe` mengalihkan tanggung jawab menjaga keamanan memori dari "
"compiler ke programmer. Ini menandakan bahwa ada prasyarat yang harus "
"dipenuhi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid ""
"“To uphold that responsibility, programmers must ensure that they've "
"understood what the preconditions are and that their code will always "
"satisfy them."
msgstr ""
"“Untuk memikul tanggung jawab itu, programmer harus memastikan mereka "
"memahami apa prasyaratnya dan bahwa kode mereka akan selalu memenuhinya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/responsibility-shift.md
msgid ""
"“Throughout this course, we'll use the term _safety preconditions_ to "
"describe this situation.”"
msgstr ""
"“Sepanjang kursus ini, kami akan menggunakan istilah _safety precondition_ "
"untuk mendeskripsikan situasi ini.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid "Impact on workflow"
msgstr "Dampak pada Alur Kerja"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid "While writing code"
msgstr "Saat Menulis Kode"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid ""
"Verify that you understand the preconditions of any `unsafe` "
"functions/traits"
msgstr "Pastikan Anda memahami prasyarat fungsi/trait `unsafe` apa pun"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid "Check that the preconditions are satisfied"
msgstr "Periksa bahwa prasyarat terpenuhi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid "Document your reasoning in safety comments"
msgstr "Dokumentasikan penalaran Anda dalam komentar safety"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid "Enhanced code review"
msgstr "Code Review yang Ditingkatkan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid "Self-review → peer reviewer → unsafe Rust expert (when needed)"
msgstr "Self-review → peer reviewer → ahli Unsafe Rust (bila diperlukan)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid "Escalate to a person who is comfortable with your code and reasoning"
msgstr "Eskalasi ke orang yang memahami kode dan penalaran Anda"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid ""
"“The unsafe keyword places more responsibility on the programmer; therefore "
"it requires a stronger development workflow."
msgstr ""
"“Keyword unsafe menempatkan lebih banyak tanggung jawab pada programmer; "
"karena itu diperlukan alur kerja pengembangan yang lebih kuat."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid ""
"“This class assumes a specific software development workflow where code "
"review is mandatory, and where the author and primary reviewer have access "
"to an unsafe Rust expert.”"
msgstr ""
"“Kelas ini mengasumsikan alur kerja pengembangan perangkat lunak tertentu di"
" mana code review wajib, dan penulis serta reviewer utama memiliki akses ke "
"ahli Unsafe Rust.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid ""
"“The author and primary reviewer will verify simple unsafe Rust code "
"themselves, and punt to an unsafe expert when necessary.”"
msgstr ""
"“Penulis dan reviewer utama akan memverifikasi kode Unsafe Rust sederhana "
"sendiri, dan menyerahkannya kepada ahli unsafe bila perlu.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md
msgid ""
"“There are only a few unsafe Rust experts, and they are very busy, so we "
"need to optimally use their time.”"
msgstr ""
"“Hanya ada sedikit ahli Unsafe Rust, dan mereka sangat sibuk, jadi kita "
"perlu memanfaatkan waktu mereka secara optimal.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid "Example: may_overflow function"
msgstr "Contoh: Fungsi may_overflow"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"/// Adds 2^31 - 1 to negative numbers without checking for overflow.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// Calling this with `a >= 1` causes signed integer overflow, which is\n"
"/// undefined behavior with `unchecked_add`.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Adds 2^31 - 1 to negative numbers without checking for overflow.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// Calling this with `a >= 1` causes signed integer overflow, which is\n"
"/// undefined behavior with `unchecked_add`.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid "\"{x}\""
msgstr "\"{x}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"“The `unsafe` keyword may have a subtly different meaning than what some "
"people assume.”"
msgstr ""
"“Keyword `unsafe` mungkin memiliki makna yang sedikit berbeda dari yang "
"diasumsikan sebagian orang.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"“The code author believes that the code is correct. In principle, the code "
"is safe.”"
msgstr ""
"“Penulis kode percaya bahwa kodenya benar. Pada prinsipnya, kode itu aman.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"“In this toy example, the `may_overflow` function is only intended to be "
"called with negative numbers."
msgstr ""
"“Dalam contoh mainan ini, fungsi `may_overflow` hanya dimaksudkan untuk "
"dipanggil dengan angka negatif."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"Ask learners if they can explain why `may_overflow` requires the unsafe "
"keyword."
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan kepada pembelajar apakah mereka dapat menjelaskan mengapa "
"`may_overflow` memerlukan keyword unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"“In case you’re unsure what the problem is, let’s pause briefly to explain. "
"An `i32` only has 31 bits available for positive numbers."
msgstr ""
"“Jika Anda belum yakin apa masalahnya, mari berhenti sebentar untuk "
"menjelaskan. `i32` hanya memiliki 31 bit untuk angka positif."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"In standard safe Rust, integer overflow (`a + i32::MAX`) is not undefined "
"behavior: it panics with overflow checks enabled (debug mode) and performs "
"two's-complement wrapping in release mode. However, `unchecked_add` is an "
"`unsafe` operation that omits overflow checks entirely and declares overflow"
" to be undefined behavior (UB). Compilers optimize code on the assumption "
"that undefined behavior is impossible, which can cause dead-code elimination"
" and unexpected runtime behavior."
msgstr ""
"Dalam safe Rust standar, integer overflow (`a + i32::MAX`) bukan undefined "
"behavior: operasi ini panic dengan pemeriksaan overflow aktif (mode debug) "
"dan melakukan wrapping two's-complement pada mode release. Namun, "
"`unchecked_add` adalah operasi `unsafe` yang menghilangkan pemeriksaan "
"overflow sepenuhnya dan menyatakan overflow sebagai undefined behavior (UB)."
" Compiler mengoptimalkan kode dengan asumsi undefined behavior tidak mungkin"
" terjadi, yang dapat menyebabkan dead-code elimination dan perilaku runtime "
"tak terduga."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"Compile and run the code: in debug mode, the standard library catches the "
"violated safety precondition and panics (`unsafe precondition(s) violated: "
"i32::unchecked_add cannot overflow`). In release mode, `unchecked_add` "
"produces actual UB."
msgstr ""
"Kompilasi dan jalankan kode: pada mode debug, standard library menangkap "
"safety precondition yang dilanggar dan panic (`unsafe precondition(s) "
"violated: i32::unchecked_add cannot overflow`). Pada mode release, "
"`unchecked_add` menghasilkan UB sebenarnya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"“This code can be used correctly, however, improper usage is highly "
"dangerous.”"
msgstr ""
"“Kode ini dapat digunakan dengan benar, tetapi penggunaan yang keliru sangat"
" berbahaya.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"“And it's impossible for the compiler to verify that the usage is correct.”"
msgstr ""
"“Dan mustahil bagi compiler untuk memverifikasi bahwa penggunaannya benar.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/may_overflow.md
msgid ""
"This is what we mean when we say that the `unsafe` keyword marks the "
"location where responsibility for memory safety shifts from the compiler to "
"the programmer."
msgstr ""
"Inilah yang kami maksud ketika mengatakan keyword `unsafe` menandai lokasi "
"pergeseran tanggung jawab keamanan memori dari compiler ke programmer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Safety preconditions are conditions on an action that must be satisfied "
"before that action will be safe."
msgstr ""
"Safety precondition adalah kondisi pada suatu tindakan yang harus dipenuhi "
"sebelum tindakan tersebut aman."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
msgid ""
"“Safety preconditions are conditions on code that must be satisfied to "
"maintain Rust's safety guarantees"
msgstr ""
"“Safety precondition adalah kondisi pada kode yang harus dipenuhi untuk "
"mempertahankan jaminan keamanan Rust"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
msgid ""
"“You're likely to see a strong affinity between safety preconditions and the"
" rules of Safe Rust.”"
msgstr ""
"“Anda kemungkinan akan melihat keterkaitan kuat antara safety precondition "
"dan aturan Safe Rust.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions.md
msgid "Q: Can you list any?"
msgstr "T: Dapatkah Anda menyebutkan beberapa?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions.md
msgid "(Fuller list in the next slide)"
msgstr "(Daftar lebih lengkap pada slide berikutnya)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Common safety preconditions"
msgstr "Safety Precondition Umum"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Aliasing and Mutability"
msgstr "Aliasing dan Mutability"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Alignment"
msgstr "Alignment"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Array access is in-bound"
msgstr "Akses array berada dalam bounds"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Pointer provenance"
msgstr "Pointer provenance"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Validity"
msgstr "Validity"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Memory"
msgstr "Memori"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Avoid spending too much time explaining every precondition: we will be "
"working through the details during the course. The intent is to show that "
"there are several."
msgstr ""
"Hindari menghabiskan terlalu banyak waktu menjelaskan setiap precondition: "
"kami akan membahas detailnya selama kursus. Tujuannya adalah menunjukkan "
"bahwa ada beberapa."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"\"An incomplete list, but these are a few of the major safety preconditions "
"to get us thinking.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Daftar yang tidak lengkap, tetapi ini beberapa safety precondition utama "
"untuk memancing pemikiran kita.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Validity. Values must be valid values of the type that they represent. "
"Rust's references may not be null. Creating one with `unsafe` causes the."
msgstr ""
"Validity. Nilai harus berupa nilai valid dari tipe yang "
"direpresentasikannya. Reference Rust tidak boleh null. Membuatnya dengan "
"`unsafe` menyebabkan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Alignment. References to values must be well-aligned, which means th"
msgstr "Alignment. Reference ke nilai harus selaras dengan baik, yang berarti"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Aliasing. All Rust code must uphold Rust's borrowing rules. If you are "
"manually creating mutable references (`&mut T`) from pointers, then you may "
"only create one"
msgstr ""
"Aliasing. Semua kode Rust harus menegakkan aturan borrowing Rust. Jika Anda "
"membuat reference mutable (`&mut T`) secara manual dari pointer, maka Anda "
"hanya boleh membuat satu"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Initialization. All instances of Rust types must be fully initialized. To "
"create a value from raw memory, we need to make sure that we've written"
msgstr ""
"Initialization. Semua instance tipe Rust harus diinisialisasi sepenuhnya. "
"Untuk membuat nilai dari memori mentah, kita perlu memastikan bahwa kita "
"telah menulis"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Pointer provenance. The origin of a pointer is important. Casting a `usize` "
"to a raw pointer is no longer allowed."
msgstr ""
"Pointer provenance. Asal pointer itu penting. Cast `usize` ke raw pointer "
"tidak lagi diizinkan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Lifetimes. References must not outlive their referent."
msgstr "Lifetime. Reference tidak boleh hidup lebih lama dari referent-nya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Some conditions are even more subtle than they first seem."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian kondisi bahkan lebih halus daripada yang terlihat pertama kali."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Consider \"in-bounds array access\". Reading from the memory location, i.e. "
"dereferencing, is not required to break the program. Creating an out-of-"
"bounds reference already breaks the compiler's assumptions, leading to "
"erratic behavior."
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan \"akses array dalam bounds\". Membaca dari lokasi memori, "
"yaitu melakukan dereference, tidak diperlukan untuk merusak program. Membuat"
" reference di luar bounds sudah merusak asumsi compiler, menyebabkan "
"perilaku tidak menentu."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Rust tells LLVM to use its `getelementptr inbounds` assumption. That "
"assumption will cause later optimization passes within the compiler to "
"misbehave (because out-of-bounds memory access cannot occur)."
msgstr ""
"Rust memberi tahu LLVM untuk menggunakan asumsi `getelementptr inbounds`. "
"Asumsi itu akan menyebabkan pass optimasi berikutnya dalam compiler "
"berperilaku salah (karena akses memori di luar bounds tidak mungkin "
"terjadi)."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Optional: open [the playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=release&edition=2024&gist=4116c4de01c863cac918f193448210b1),"
" which shows the code below. Explain that this is essentially a C function "
"written in Rust syntax that gets items from an array. Generate the LLVM IR "
"with the **Show LLVM IR** button. Highlight `getelementptr inbounds i32, ptr"
" %array, i64 %offset`."
msgstr ""
"Opsional: buka [playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=release&edition=2024&gist=4116c4de01c863cac918f193448210b1),"
" yang menampilkan kode di bawah. Jelaskan bahwa ini pada dasarnya adalah "
"fungsi C yang ditulis dalam sintaks Rust yang mengambil item dari array. "
"Hasilkan LLVM IR dengan tombol **Show LLVM IR**. Soroti `getelementptr "
"inbounds i32, ptr %array, i64 %offset`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid "Expected output (the line to highlight starts with \\`%\\_3):"
msgstr "Output yang diharapkan (baris yang disorot dimulai dengan \\`%\\_3):"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/common-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"Bounds: You correctly noted that creating an out-of-bounds pointer (beyond "
"the \"one-past-the-end\" rule) is UB, even without dereferencing, due to "
"LLVM's inbounds assumptions."
msgstr ""
"Bounds: Anda dengan benar mencatat bahwa membuat pointer di luar bounds "
"(melampaui aturan \"one-past-the-end\") adalah UB, bahkan tanpa dereference,"
" karena asumsi inbounds LLVM."

