msgstr "Tanyakan: “Apa safety precondition dari `get`?”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
msgid ""
"The pointer `arr` is non-null, well-aligned and refers to an array of `i32`"
msgstr ""
"Pointer `arr` tidak null, selaras dengan baik, dan merujuk array `i32`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
msgid "`index` is in-bounds"
msgstr "`index` berada dalam bounds"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Add safety comments:"
msgstr "Tambahkan komentar safety:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
msgid ""
"/// Return the element at `index` from `arr`\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// - `arr` is non-null, correctly aligned and points to a valid `i32`\n"
"/// - `index` is in-bounds for the array\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Return the element at `index` from `arr`\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// - `arr` is non-null, correctly aligned and points to a valid `i32`\n"
"/// - `index` is in-bounds for the array\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
msgid "// SAFETY: Caller guarantees that index is inbounds\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: Caller guarantees that index is inbounds\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/getter.md
msgid ""
"Optional: Add runtime checks can be added in debug builds to provide some "
"extra robustness."
msgstr ""
"Opsional: Pemeriksaan runtime dapat ditambahkan pada build debug untuk "
"memberikan ketahanan ekstra."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "Determining Preconditions"
msgstr "Menentukan Precondition"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "Where do you find the safety preconditions?"
msgstr "Di mana Anda menemukan safety precondition?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid ""
"Attempt to compile the program to trigger the compiler error "
"(\"error\\[E0133\\]: call to unsafe function ...\")."
msgstr ""
"Coba kompilasi program untuk memicu error compiler (\"error\\[E0133\\]: call"
" to unsafe function ...\")."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid ""
"Ask: “Where would you look if you wanted to know the preconditions for a "
"function? Here we need to understand when it's safe to convert from a null "
"pointer to a mutable reference.”"
msgstr ""
"Tanyakan: “Di mana Anda akan mencari jika ingin mengetahui precondition "
"suatu fungsi? Di sini kita perlu memahami kapan aman mengonversi dari null "
"pointer ke mutable reference.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "Locations to look:"
msgstr "Tempat yang perlu diperiksa:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "A function's API documentation, especially its safety section"
msgstr "Dokumentasi API fungsi, terutama bagian safety-nya"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "The source code and its internal safety comments"
msgstr "Kode sumber dan komentar safety internalnya"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "Module documentation"
msgstr "Dokumentasi modul"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "Rust Reference"
msgstr "Rust Reference"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid ""
"Consult [the documentation](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/primitive.pointer.html#method.as_mut) for the `as_mut` method."
msgstr ""
"Rujuk [dokumentasi](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/primitive.pointer.html#method.as_mut) untuk method `as_mut`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "Highlight Safety section."
msgstr "Soroti bagian Safety."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid "**Safety**"
msgstr "**Safety**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid ""
"When calling this method, you have to ensure that either the pointer is null"
" or the pointer is convertible to a reference."
msgstr ""
"Saat memanggil method ini, Anda harus memastikan bahwa pointer bernilai null"
" atau pointer dapat dikonversi menjadi reference."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid ""
"Click the \"convertible to a reference\" hyperlink to the \"Pointer to "
"reference conversion\""
msgstr ""
"Klik hyperlink \"convertible to a reference\" menuju \"Pointer to reference "
"conversion\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid ""
"Track down the rules for converting a pointer to a reference, i.e., whether "
"it is \"dereferenceable\"."
msgstr ""
"Telusuri aturan konversi pointer menjadi reference, yaitu apakah pointer "
"tersebut \"dereferenceable\"."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/determining.md
msgid ""
"Consider the implications of this excerpt (Rust 1.90.0) \"You must enforce "
"Rust’s aliasing rules. The exact aliasing rules are not decided yet, ...\""
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan implikasi kutipan ini (Rust 1.90.0) \"Anda harus menegakkan "
"aturan aliasing Rust. Aturan aliasing yang tepat belum ditetapkan, ...\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Example: References"
msgstr "Contoh: Reference"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Confirm understanding of the syntax"
msgstr "Pastikan pemahaman sintaks"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"`Box<i32>` type is a reference to an integer on the heap that is owned by "
"the box."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `Box<i32>` adalah reference ke integer di heap yang dimiliki oleh box."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"`*mut i32` type is a so-called raw pointer to an integer that the compiler "
"does not know the ownership of. Programmers need to ensure the rules are "
"enforced without assistance from the compiler."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `*mut i32` adalah yang disebut raw pointer ke integer yang ownership-"
"nya tidak diketahui compiler. Programmer perlu memastikan aturan ditegakkan "
"tanpa bantuan compiler."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"Note: raw pointers do not provide ownership info to Rust. A pointer can be "
"semantically owning the data, or semantically borrowing, but that "
"information only exists in the programmer's mind."
msgstr ""
"Catatan: raw pointer tidak memberikan info ownership kepada Rust. Pointer "
"dapat secara semantik memiliki data, atau secara semantik meminjam, tetapi "
"informasi itu hanya ada di pikiran programmer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "`&mut *boxed as *mut _` expression:"
msgstr "Expression `&mut *boxed as *mut _`:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "`*boxed` is ..."
msgstr "`*boxed` adalah ..."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "`&mut *boxed` is ..."
msgstr "`&mut *boxed` adalah ..."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "finally, `as *mut i32` casts the reference to a pointer."
msgstr "akhirnya, `as *mut i32` melakukan cast reference menjadi pointer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"References, such as `&mut i32`, \"borrow\" their referent. This is Rust's "
"ownership system."
msgstr ""
"Reference, seperti `&mut i32`, \"meminjam\" referent-nya. Ini adalah sistem "
"ownership Rust."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Confirm understanding of ownership"
msgstr "Pastikan pemahaman ownership"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Step through code:"
msgstr "Telusuri kode langkah demi langkah:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"(Line 3) Creates raw pointer to the `123` by dereferencing the box, creating"
" a new reference and casting the new reference as a pointer."
msgstr ""
"(Baris 3) Membuat raw pointer ke `123` dengan melakukan dereference box, "
"membuat reference baru, dan melakukan cast reference baru sebagai pointer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "(Line 4) Creates raw pointer with a NULL value"
msgstr "(Baris 4) Membuat raw pointer dengan nilai NULL"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "(Line 7) Converts the raw pointer to an Option with `.as_mut()`"
msgstr "(Baris 7) Mengonversi raw pointer menjadi Option dengan `.as_mut()`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Highlight that pointers are nullable in Rust (unlike references)."
msgstr ""
"Soroti bahwa pointer dapat bernilai null di Rust (berbeda dari reference)."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Compile to reveal the error messages."
msgstr "Kompilasi untuk menampilkan pesan error."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Discuss"
msgstr "Diskusikan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "(Line 6) `println!(\"{:?}\", *a);`"
msgstr "(Baris 6) `println!(\"{:?}\", *a);`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Prefix star dereferences a raw pointer."
msgstr "Awalan bintang melakukan dereference raw pointer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"It is an explicit operation. Whereas regular references have implicit "
"dereferencing most of the time thanks to the Deref trait. This is referred "
"to as \"auto-deref\"."
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah operasi eksplisit. Sedangkan reference biasa memiliki dereference"
" implisit sebagian besar waktu berkat trait Deref. Ini disebut \"auto-"
"deref\"."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Dereferencing a raw pointer is an unsafe operation."
msgstr "Melakukan dereference raw pointer adalah operasi unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Requires an unsafe block."
msgstr "Memerlukan block unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "(Line 7) `println!(\"{:?}\", b.as_mut());`"
msgstr "(Baris 7) `println!(\"{:?}\", b.as_mut());`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "`as_mut()` is an unsafe function."
msgstr "`as_mut()` adalah fungsi unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Calling an unsafe function requires an unsafe block."
msgstr "Memanggil fungsi unsafe memerlukan block unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Fix the code (add unsafe blocks) and compile again to show the "
"working program."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Perbaiki kode (tambahkan block unsafe) dan kompilasi lagi "
"untuk menunjukkan program yang berfungsi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Replace `as *mut i32` with `as *mut _`, show that it compiles."
msgstr ""
"Demonstrasikan: Ganti `as *mut i32` dengan `as *mut _`, tunjukkan bahwa kode"
" dapat dikompilasi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"We can partially omit the target type in the cast. The Rust compiler knows "
"that the source of the cast is a `&mut i32`. This reference type can only be"
" converted to one pointer type, `*mut i32`."
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat sebagian menghilangkan tipe target dalam cast. Compiler Rust "
"mengetahui bahwa sumber cast adalah `&mut i32`. Tipe reference ini hanya "
"dapat dikonversi ke satu tipe pointer, `*mut i32`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"We said that the unsafe code marks the responsibility shift from the "
"compiler to the programmer."
msgstr ""
"Kami mengatakan bahwa kode unsafe menandai pergeseran tanggung jawab dari "
"compiler ke programmer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"How do we convey that we thought about our unusual responsibilities while "
"writing unsafe code? Safety comments."
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana kami menyampaikan bahwa kami telah memikirkan tanggung jawab tidak"
" biasa kami saat menulis kode unsafe? Komentar safety."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Safety comments explain why unsafe code is correct."
msgstr "Komentar safety menjelaskan mengapa kode unsafe benar."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Without a safety comment, unsafe code is not safe."
msgstr "Tanpa komentar safety, kode unsafe tidak aman."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Discuss: Whether to use one large unsafe block or two smaller ones:"
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan: Apakah menggunakan satu block unsafe besar atau dua block lebih "
"kecil:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Possibility of using a single unsafe block rather than multiple."
msgstr "Kemungkinan menggunakan satu block unsafe alih-alih beberapa."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "Using more allows safety comments as specific as possible."
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan lebih banyak block memungkinkan komentar safety sespesifik "
"mungkin."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: `a` is a non-null pointer to i32, it is initialized and still\n"
"    // allocated.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: `a` is a non-null pointer to i32, it is initialized and still\n"
"    // allocated.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/references.md
msgid "// SAFETY: `b` is a null pointer, which `as_mut()` converts to `None`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: `b` is a null pointer, which `as_mut()` converts to `None`.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/defining.md
msgid "User-defined types are entitled to have their own safety preconditions"
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang ditentukan pengguna berhak memiliki safety precondition sendiri"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/defining.md
msgid ""
"Include documentation so that they can later be determined and satisfied"
msgstr ""
"Sertakan dokumentasi agar prasyarat tersebut dapat ditentukan dan dipenuhi "
"kemudian"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/ascii.md
msgid "/// Text that is guaranteed to be encoded within 7-bit ASCII.\n"
msgstr "/// Text that is guaranteed to be encoded within 7-bit ASCII.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/ascii.md
msgid ""
"/// Creates a new `Ascii` from a byte slice without checking for ASCII\n"
"    /// validity.\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// Providing non-ASCII bytes results in undefined behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Creates a new `Ascii` from a byte slice without checking for ASCII\n"
"    /// validity.\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// Providing non-ASCII bytes results in undefined behavior.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/ascii.md
msgid ""
"\"The `Ascii` type is a minimal wrapper around a byte slice. Internally, "
"they share the same representation. However, `Ascii` requires that the high "
"bit must not be used.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Tipe `Ascii` adalah wrapper minimal di sekitar byte slice. Secara "
"internal, keduanya berbagi representasi yang sama. Namun, `Ascii` "
"mengharuskan bit tinggi tidak boleh digunakan.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/safety-preconditions/ascii.md
msgid ""
"Optional: Extend the example to mention that it's possible to use "
"`debug_assert!` to test the preconditions during tests without impacting "
"release builds."
msgstr ""
"Opsional: Perluas contoh untuk menyebutkan bahwa `debug_assert!` dapat "
"digunakan untuk menguji prasyarat selama test tanpa memengaruhi build "
"release."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game.md
msgid ""
"“We've seen many examples of code that has problems in the class, but we "
"lack consistent terminology."
msgstr ""
"“Kami telah melihat banyak contoh kode bermasalah di kelas, tetapi kami "
"belum memiliki terminologi yang konsisten."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game.md
msgid ""
"“The goal of the next section is to introduce some terms that describe many "
"of the concepts that we have been thinking about."
msgstr ""
"“Tujuan bagian berikutnya adalah memperkenalkan beberapa istilah yang "
"mendeskripsikan banyak konsep yang telah kita pikirkan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game.md
msgid "undefined behavior"
msgstr "undefined behavior"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game.md
msgid "sound"
msgstr "sound"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game.md
msgid "unsound"
msgstr "unsound"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game.md
msgid ""
"“Given that many safety preconditions are semantic rather than syntactic, "
"it's important to use a shared vocabulary. That way we can agree on "
"semantics."
msgstr ""
"“Karena banyak safety precondition bersifat semantik, bukan sintaksis, "
"penting untuk menggunakan kosakata bersama. Dengan begitu kita dapat "
"menyepakati semantiknya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game.md
msgid ""
"“The overarching goal is to develop a mental framework of what soundness is "
"and ensure that Rust code that contains unsafe remains sound.”"
msgstr ""
"“Tujuan utamanya adalah mengembangkan kerangka mental tentang apa itu "
"soundness dan memastikan kode Rust yang mengandung unsafe tetap sound.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid "Soundness is fundamental to Rust"
msgstr "Soundness adalah Fundamental bagi Rust"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid "Soundness ≈ impossible to cause memory safety problems"
msgstr "Soundness ≈ mustahil menyebabkan masalah keamanan memori"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid "Sound functions have common “shapes”"
msgstr "Fungsi sound memiliki “bentuk” umum"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid "“A fundamental principle of Rust code is that it is sound."
msgstr "“Prinsip fundamental kode Rust adalah bahwa kode tersebut sound."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid ""
"“We’ll create a formal definition of the term soundness shortly. In the "
"meantime, think of sound code as code that cannot trigger memory safety "
"problems."
msgstr ""
"“Kami akan membuat definisi formal istilah soundness sebentar lagi. "
"Sementara itu, anggap kode sound sebagai kode yang tidak dapat memicu "
"masalah keamanan memori."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid "“Sound code is made up of _sound functions_ and _sound operations_."
msgstr "“Kode sound terdiri atas _fungsi sound_ dan _operasi sound_."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid ""
"“A sound function is a function where none of its possible inputs could "
"provoke soundness problems."
msgstr ""
"“Fungsi sound adalah fungsi yang tidak ada input yang mungkin dapat memicu "
"masalah soundness."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid "Sound functions have common shapes."
msgstr "Fungsi sound memiliki bentuk umum."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid "Those shapes are what we’ll look at now."
msgstr "Bentuk-bentuk itulah yang akan kita lihat sekarang."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/rust-is-sound.md
msgid ""
"“We’ll start with one that’s implemented in Safe Rust, and then see what "
"could happen when we introduce `unsafe` to different parts."
msgstr ""
"“Kami akan mulai dengan salah satu yang diimplementasikan dalam Safe Rust, "
"lalu melihat apa yang dapat terjadi ketika kami memasukkan `unsafe` ke "
"berbagai bagian."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory.md
msgid "Copying memory - Introduction"
msgstr "Menyalin Memori - Pendahuluan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory.md
msgid "/// Reads bytes from `source` and writes them to `dest`\n"
msgstr "/// Reads bytes from `source` and writes them to `dest`\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory.md
msgid "“Here is our initial function prototype.”"
msgstr "“Berikut prototipe fungsi awal kami.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory.md
msgid ""
"“`copy` accepts two slices as arguments. `dest` (destination) is mutable, "
"whereas `source` is not.”"
msgstr ""
"“`copy` menerima dua slice sebagai argumen. `dest` (destination) bersifat "
"mutable, sedangkan `source` tidak.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory.md
msgid "“Let's see the shapes of sound Rust code.”"
msgstr "“Mari kita lihat bentuk-bentuk kode Rust yang sound.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid "“The implementation only uses safe Rust."
msgstr "“Implementasinya hanya menggunakan safe Rust."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid "What can we learn from this?"
msgstr "Apa yang dapat kita pelajari dari ini?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid ""
"“It is impossible for `copy` to trigger memory safety issues when "
"implemented in Safe Rust. This is true for all possible input arguments.”"
msgstr ""
"“Mustahil bagi `copy` memicu masalah keamanan memori bila diimplementasikan "
"dalam Safe Rust. Ini berlaku untuk semua argumen input yang mungkin.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid ""
"“For example, by using Rust’s iterators, we can ensure that we’ll never "
"trigger errors relating to handling pointers directly, such as needing null "
"pointer or bounds checks.”"
msgstr ""
"“Misalnya, dengan menggunakan iterator Rust, kita dapat memastikan tidak "
"akan pernah memicu error terkait penanganan pointer secara langsung, seperti"
" kebutuhan pemeriksaan null pointer atau bounds.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid "Ask: “Can you think of any others?”"
msgstr "Tanyakan: “Dapatkah Anda memikirkan yang lain?”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid "No aliasing issues"
msgstr "Tidak ada masalah aliasing"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid "Dangling pointers are impossible"
msgstr "Dangling pointer mustahil terjadi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid "Alignment will be correct"
msgstr "Alignment akan benar"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid "Cannot accidentally read from uninitialized memory"
msgstr ""
"Tidak dapat secara tidak sengaja membaca dari memori yang belum "
"diinisialisasi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid ""
"“We can say that the `copy` function is _sound_ because Rust ensures that "
"all of the safety preconditions are satisfied.”"
msgstr ""
"“Kita dapat mengatakan fungsi `copy` bersifat _sound_ karena Rust memastikan"
" semua safety precondition terpenuhi.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid ""
"“From the point of view of the programmer, as this function is implemented "
"in safe Rust, we can think of it as having no safety preconditions.”"
msgstr ""
"“Dari sudut pandang programmer, karena fungsi ini diimplementasikan dalam "
"safe Rust, kita dapat menganggapnya tidak memiliki safety precondition.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md
msgid ""
"“This does not mean that `copy` will always do what the caller might want. "
"If there is insufficient space available in the `dest` slice, then data will"
" not be copied across.”"
msgstr ""
"“Ini tidak berarti `copy` akan selalu melakukan apa yang mungkin diinginkan "
"pemanggil. Jika ruang yang tersedia di slice `dest` tidak cukup, data tidak "
"akan disalin.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/encapsulated-unsafe.md
msgid "// SAFETY: `i` must be in-bounds as it was produced by source.len()\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: `i` must be in-bounds as it was produced by source.len()\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/encapsulated-unsafe.md
msgid "// SAFETY: `i` must be in-bounds as it was produced by dest.len()\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: `i` must be in-bounds as it was produced by dest.len()\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/encapsulated-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“Here we have a safe function that encapsulates unsafe blocks that are used "
"internally."
msgstr ""
"“Di sini kita memiliki fungsi safe yang mengenkapsulasi block unsafe yang "
"digunakan secara internal."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/encapsulated-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“This implementation avoids iterators. Instead, the implementor is accessing"
" memory manually.”"
msgstr ""
"“Implementasi ini menghindari iterator. Sebagai gantinya, implementor "
"mengakses memori secara manual.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/encapsulated-unsafe.md
msgid "“Is this correct?” “Are there any problems?”"
msgstr "“Apakah ini benar?” “Apakah ada masalah?”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/encapsulated-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“Who has responsibility for ensuring that correctness? The author of the "
"function."
msgstr ""
"“Siapa yang bertanggung jawab memastikan kebenaran itu? Penulis fungsi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/encapsulated-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“A Safe Rust function that contains unsafe blocks remains sound if it’s "
"impossible for an input to cause memory safety issues."
msgstr ""
"“Fungsi Safe Rust yang berisi block unsafe tetap sound jika mustahil input "
"menyebabkan masalah keamanan memori."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"The functionality of copying bytes from one place to the next remains the "
"same."
msgstr ""
"Fungsionalitas menyalin byte dari satu tempat ke tempat lain tetap sama."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“However, we need to manually create a slice. To do that, we first need to "
"find the end of the data."
msgstr ""
"“Namun, kita perlu membuat slice secara manual. Untuk itu, kita harus "
"menemukan akhir data terlebih dahulu."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“As we’re working with text, we’ll use the C convention of a null-terminated"
" string."
msgstr ""
"“Karena kita bekerja dengan teks, kita akan menggunakan konvensi C string "
"yang diakhiri null."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "Compile the code. See that the output remains the same."
msgstr "Kompilasi kode. Lihat bahwa outputnya tetap sama."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“An unsound function can still work correctly for some inputs. Just because "
"your tests pass, does not mean that you have a sound function.”"
msgstr ""
"“Fungsi unsound masih dapat bekerja dengan benar untuk sebagian input. "
"Lulusnya test tidak berarti fungsi Anda sound.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "“Can anyone spot any issues?”"
msgstr "“Adakah yang dapat menemukan masalah?”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "Readability: difficult to quickly scan code"
msgstr "Keterbacaan: sulit memindai kode dengan cepat"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "`source` pointer might be null"
msgstr "Pointer `source` mungkin null"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"`source` pointer might be dangling, i.e. point to freed or uninitialized "
"memory"
msgstr ""
"Pointer `source` mungkin dangling, yaitu menunjuk memori yang telah "
"dibebaskan atau belum diinisialisasi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "`source` might not be null-terminated"
msgstr "`source` mungkin tidak diakhiri null"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“Assume that we cannot change the function signature, what improvements "
"could we make to the code to address these issues?”"
msgstr ""
"“Asumsikan kita tidak dapat mengubah signature fungsi, perbaikan apa yang "
"dapat kita lakukan pada kode untuk mengatasi masalah ini?”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"Null pointer: Add null check with early return (`if source.is_null() { "
"return; }`)"
msgstr ""
"Null pointer: Tambahkan pemeriksaan null dengan early return (`if "
"source.is_null() { return; }`)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"Readability: Use a well-tested library rather than implementing “find first "
"null byte” ourselves"
msgstr ""
"Keterbacaan: Gunakan library yang teruji dengan baik alih-alih "
"mengimplementasikan “cari byte null pertama” sendiri"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"“Some safety requirements are impossible to defensively check for, however, "
"i.e.:”"
msgstr ""
"“Namun, sebagian persyaratan keamanan mustahil diperiksa secara defensif, "
"yaitu:”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "dangling pointer"
msgstr "dangling pointer"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "no null termination byte"
msgstr "tidak ada byte terminator null"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "“How can we make this function sound?”"
msgstr "“Bagaimana kita dapat membuat fungsi ini sound?”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "Either"
msgstr "Salah satu"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid ""
"Change the type of the `source` input argument to something that has a known"
" length, i.e. use a slice like the previous example."
msgstr ""
"Ubah tipe argumen input `source` menjadi sesuatu yang memiliki panjang "
"diketahui, yaitu gunakan slice seperti contoh sebelumnya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "Or"
msgstr "Atau"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "Mark the function as unsafe"
msgstr "Tandai fungsi sebagai unsafe"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md
msgid "Document the safety preconditions"
msgstr "Dokumentasikan safety precondition"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"/// ...\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// This function can easily trigger undefined behavior. Ensure that:\n"
"///\n"
"///  - `source` pointer is non-null and non-dangling\n"
"///  - `source` data ends with a null byte within its memory allocation\n"
"///  - `source` data is not freed (its lifetime invariants are preserved)\n"
"///  - `source` data contains fewer than `isize::MAX` bytes\n"
msgstr ""
"/// ...\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// This function can easily trigger undefined behavior. Ensure that:\n"
"///\n"
"///  - `source` pointer is non-null and non-dangling\n"
"///  - `source` data ends with a null byte within its memory allocation\n"
"///  - `source` data is not freed (its lifetime invariants are preserved)\n"
"///  - `source` data contains fewer than `isize::MAX` bytes\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "// SAFETY: Caller has provided a non-null pointer\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: Caller has provided a non-null pointer\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "// SAFETY: Caller has provided a data with length < isize:MAX\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: Caller has provided a data with length < isize:MAX\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "// SAFETY: Caller maintains lifetime and aliasing requirements\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: Caller maintains lifetime and aliasing requirements\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "Changes to previous iterations:"
msgstr "Perubahan dari iterasi sebelumnya:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "`copy` marked as unsafe"
msgstr "`copy` ditandai sebagai unsafe"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "Safety preconditions are documented"
msgstr "Safety precondition didokumentasikan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "inline safety comments"
msgstr "komentar safety inline"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"An unsafe function is sound when both its safety preconditions and its "
"internal unsafe blocks are documented."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi unsafe bersifat sound ketika safety precondition dan block unsafe "
"internalnya keduanya didokumentasikan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "Fixes needed in `main`."
msgstr "Perbaikan yang diperlukan di `main`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid ""
"`a` does not satisfy one of the preconditions of `copy` (source\\` data ends"
" with a null byte within its memory allocation)"
msgstr ""
"`a` tidak memenuhi salah satu precondition `copy` (source\\` data berakhir "
"dengan byte null dalam alokasi memorinya)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/documented-safety-preconditions.md
msgid "SAFETY comment needed"
msgstr "Komentar SAFETY diperlukan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/crying-wolf.md
msgid "“It is also possible to create so-called crying wolf functions."
msgstr "“Dimungkinkan juga membuat yang disebut fungsi crying wolf."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/crying-wolf.md
msgid ""
"“These are functions which are tagged as unsafe, but which have no safety "
"preconditions that programmers need to check."
msgstr ""
"“Ini adalah fungsi yang ditandai sebagai unsafe, tetapi tidak memiliki "
"safety precondition yang perlu diperiksa programmer."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "3 Shapes of Sound Rust"
msgstr "3 Bentuk Rust yang Sound"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "Functions written only in Safe Rust"
msgstr "Fungsi yang ditulis hanya dalam Safe Rust"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "Functions that contain `unsafe` blocks which are impossible to misuse"
msgstr "Fungsi yang berisi block `unsafe` yang mustahil disalahgunakan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "Unsafe functions that have their safety preconditions documented"
msgstr "Fungsi unsafe yang safety precondition-nya didokumentasikan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "We want to write sound code."
msgstr "Kami ingin menulis kode yang sound."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "Sound code can only have the following shapes:"
msgstr "Kode sound hanya dapat memiliki bentuk berikut:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "safe functions that contain no unsafe blocks"
msgstr "fungsi safe yang tidak berisi block unsafe"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid ""
"safe functions that completely encapsulate unsafe blocks, meaning that the "
"caller does not need to know about them"
msgstr ""
"fungsi safe yang sepenuhnya mengenkapsulasi block unsafe, artinya pemanggil "
"tidak perlu mengetahuinya"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid ""
"unsafe functions that contain unsafe blocks but don't encapsulate them, and "
"pass the proof burden to their caller"
msgstr ""
"fungsi unsafe yang berisi block unsafe tetapi tidak mengenkapsulasinya, dan "
"memindahkan beban pembuktian kepada pemanggilnya"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "Burden of proof"
msgstr "Beban Pembuktian"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "safe functions with only Safe Rust -> compiler"
msgstr "fungsi safe dengan hanya Safe Rust -> compiler"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "safe functions with unsafe blocks -> function author"
msgstr "fungsi safe dengan block unsafe -> penulis fungsi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/3-shapes-of-sound-rust.md
msgid "unsafe functions -> function caller"
msgstr "fungsi unsafe -> pemanggil fungsi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/soundness.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/unsoundness.md
msgid ""
"A sound function is one that can't trigger UB if its safety preconditions "
"are satisfied."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi sound adalah fungsi yang tidak dapat memicu UB jika safety "
"precondition-nya terpenuhi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/soundness.md
msgid "Read the definition of sound functions."
msgstr "Baca definisi fungsi sound."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/soundness.md
msgid ""
"Remind the students that the programmer who implements the caller is "
"responsible for satisfying the safety precondition; the compiler is not "
"helping."
msgstr ""
"Ingatkan siswa bahwa programmer yang mengimplementasikan pemanggil "
"bertanggung jawab memenuhi safety precondition; compiler tidak membantu."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/soundness.md
msgid ""
"Translate into informal terms. Soundness means that the function is nice and"
" plays by the rules. It documents its safety preconditions, and when the "
"caller satisfies them, the function behaves well (no UB)."
msgstr ""
"Terjemahkan ke istilah informal. Soundness berarti fungsi tersebut baik dan "
"mengikuti aturan. Fungsi mendokumentasikan safety precondition-nya, dan "
"ketika pemanggil memenuhinya, fungsi berperilaku baik (tidak ada UB)."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "Soundness Proof (Part 2)"
msgstr "Bukti Soundness (Bagian 2)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "Corollary: All functions implemented in pure safe Rust are sound."
msgstr ""
"Korolari: Semua fungsi yang diimplementasikan dalam safe Rust murni bersifat"
" sound."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "Proof:"
msgstr "Bukti:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "Safe Rust code has no safety preconditions."
msgstr "Kode Safe Rust tidak memiliki safety precondition."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid ""
"Therefore, callers of functions implemented in pure safe Rust always "
"trivially satisfy the empty set of preconditions."
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu, pemanggil fungsi yang diimplementasikan dalam safe Rust "
"murni selalu secara trivial memenuhi himpunan precondition kosong."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "Safe Rust code can't trigger UB."
msgstr "Kode Safe Rust tidak dapat memicu UB."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "QED."
msgstr "QED."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "Read the corollary."
msgstr "Baca korolari."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid "Explain the proof."
msgstr "Jelaskan buktinya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md
msgid ""
"Translate into informal terms: all safe Rust code is nice. It does not have "
"safety preconditions that the programmer has to think of, always plays by "
"the rules, and never triggers UB."
msgstr ""
"Terjemahkan ke istilah informal: semua kode safe Rust itu baik. Kode "
"tersebut tidak memiliki safety precondition yang harus dipikirkan "
"programmer, selalu mengikuti aturan, dan tidak pernah memicu UB."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/unsoundness.md
msgid ""
"An unsound function can trigger UB even if you satisfy the documented safety"
" preconditions."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi unsound dapat memicu UB bahkan jika Anda memenuhi safety precondition"
" yang didokumentasikan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/unsoundness.md
msgid "Unsound code is _bad_."
msgstr "Kode unsound itu _buruk_."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/unsoundness.md
msgid "Read the definition of unsound functions."
msgstr "Baca definisi fungsi unsound."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/unsoundness.md
msgid ""
"Translate into informal terms: unsound code is not nice. No, that's an "
"understatement. Unsound code is BAD. Even if you play by the documented "
"rules, unsound code can still trigger UB!"
msgstr ""
"Terjemahkan ke istilah informal: kode unsound itu tidak baik. Bukan, itu "
"pernyataan yang terlalu ringan. Kode unsound itu BURUK. Bahkan jika Anda "
"mengikuti aturan yang didokumentasikan, kode unsound tetap dapat memicu UB!"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/unsoundness.md
msgid "We don't want any unsound code in our repositories."
msgstr "Kami tidak menginginkan kode unsound di repositori kami."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/unsoundness.md
msgid "Finding unsound code is the **primary** goal of the code review."
msgstr "Menemukan kode unsound adalah tujuan **utama** code review."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid ""
"Memory moves through different phases as objects (values) are created and "
"destroyed."
msgstr ""
"Memori melewati berbagai fase saat objek (nilai) dibuat dan dihancurkan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid "Memory State"
msgstr "State Memori"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid "Readable from Safe Rust?"
msgstr "Dapat Dibaca dari Safe Rust?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid "Available"
msgstr "Tersedia"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid "Allocated"
msgstr "Dialokasikan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid "Initialized"
msgstr "Diinisialisasi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid ""
"This section discusses what happens as memory from the operating system "
"becomes a valid variable in the program."
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini membahas apa yang terjadi saat memori dari sistem operasi menjadi"
" variabel valid dalam program."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid ""
"When memory is available, the operating system has provided our program with"
" it."
msgstr ""
"Saat memori tersedia, sistem operasi telah menyediakannya untuk program "
"kita."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid ""
"When memory is allocated, it is reserved for values to be written to it. We "
"call this uninitialized memory."
msgstr ""
"Saat memori dialokasikan, memori dicadangkan agar nilai dapat ditulis ke "
"dalamnya. Kami menyebutnya memori yang belum diinisialisasi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/memory-lifecycle.md
msgid "When memory is initialized, it is safe to read from."
msgstr "Saat memori diinisialisasi, memori aman untuk dibaca."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit.md
msgid "`MaybeUninit<T>` allows Rust to refer to uninitialized memory."
msgstr ""
"`MaybeUninit<T>` memungkinkan Rust merujuk memori yang belum diinisialisasi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit.md
msgid "\"{uninit:?}\""
msgstr "\"{uninit:?}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit.md
msgid ""
"“Safe Rust is unable to refer to data that’s potentially uninitialized”"
msgstr ""
"“Safe Rust tidak dapat merujuk data yang berpotensi belum diinisialisasi”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit.md
msgid "“Yet, all data arrives at the program as uninitialized.”"
msgstr ""
"“Namun, semua data tiba di program dalam keadaan belum diinisialisasi.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit.md
msgid ""
"“Therefore, we need some bridge in the type system to allow memory to "
"transition. `MaybeUninit<T>` is that type.”"
msgstr ""
"“Oleh karena itu, kita memerlukan jembatan dalam sistem tipe untuk "
"memungkinkan transisi memori. `MaybeUninit<T>` adalah tipe tersebut.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit.md
msgid ""
"“`MaybeUninit<T>` is very similar to the `Option<T>` type, although its "
"semantics are very different. The equivalent of `Option::None` for "
"`MaybeUninit<T>` is uninitialized memory, which is only safe to write to.”"
msgstr ""
"“`MaybeUninit<T>` sangat mirip dengan tipe `Option<T>`, meskipun semantiknya"
" sangat berbeda. Padanan `Option::None` untuk `MaybeUninit<T>` adalah memori"
" yang belum diinisialisasi, yang hanya aman untuk ditulisi.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit.md
msgid ""
"“Reading from memory that may be uninitialized is extremely dangerous.”"
msgstr ""
"“Membaca dari memori yang mungkin belum diinisialisasi sangat berbahaya.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid "MaybeUninit and arrays"
msgstr "MaybeUninit dan Array"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid "b\"RUST\""
msgstr "b\"RUST\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid "// Initialize elements by writing values to the memory\n"
msgstr "// Initialize elements by writing values to the memory\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"// When a portion of an array is initialized, one can\n"
"    // use unsafe to isolate it\n"
msgstr ""
"// When a portion of an array is initialized, one can\n"
"    // use unsafe to isolate it\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid "\"{text}\""
msgstr "\"{text}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid "// We must manually drop the initialized elements\n"
msgstr "// We must manually drop the initialized elements\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"To create an array of uninitialized memory, the `::uninit()` constructor can"
" be used within a `const` context."
msgstr ""
"Untuk membuat array memori yang belum diinisialisasi, constructor "
"`::uninit()` dapat digunakan dalam konteks `const`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid "Use `ptr::write` to initialize values as per normal."
msgstr "Gunakan `ptr::write` untuk menginisialisasi nilai seperti biasa."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"`.assume_init()` does not work as easily for arrays. It requires every value"
" to be initialized, which may not occur when reusing a buffer. This example "
"uses a pointer to isolate the initialized bytes to create a string slice."
msgstr ""
"`.assume_init()` tidak bekerja semudah itu untuk array. Method ini "
"mengharuskan setiap nilai diinisialisasi, yang mungkin tidak terjadi saat "
"menggunakan ulang buffer. Contoh ini menggunakan pointer untuk mengisolasi "
"byte yang telah diinisialisasi guna membuat string slice."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"When creating a sub-slice of a partially-initialized array, be careful with "
"ownership and correctly implementing drop. Reminder: `MaybeUninit<T>` will "
"not call drop on its `T`."
msgstr ""
"Saat membuat sub-slice dari array yang sebagian diinisialisasi, berhati-"
"hatilah dengan ownership dan implementasi drop yang benar. Pengingat: "
"`MaybeUninit<T>` tidak akan memanggil drop pada `T`-nya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"`MaybeUninit<[u8;2048]>` is distinct from `[MaybeUninit::<u8>; 2048]`. This "
"is the difference between an array of uninitialized memory and an array that"
" contains uninitialized elements."
msgstr ""
"`MaybeUninit<[u8;2048]>` berbeda dari `[MaybeUninit::<u8>; 2048]`. Ini "
"adalah perbedaan antara array memori yang belum diinisialisasi dan array "
"yang berisi elemen yang belum diinisialisasi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"`MaybeUninit<[u8;2048]>` is \"all or nothing\". You either fully initialize "
"the whole array and then call `assume_init`, or you must keep it as "
"`MaybeUninit<[u8; 2048]>` and avoid touching it as `[u8; 2048]`."
msgstr ""
"`MaybeUninit<[u8;2048]>` bersifat \"semua atau tidak sama sekali\". Anda "
"harus menginisialisasi seluruh array lalu memanggil `assume_init`, atau "
"menyimpannya sebagai `MaybeUninit<[u8; 2048]>` dan menghindari "
"memperlakukannya sebagai `[u8; 2048]`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"`[MaybeUninit<u8>; 2048]` lets you initialize elements one at a time, then "
"take a sub-slice of just the initialized prefix and treat it as `[u8]` via "
"`std::slice::from_raw_parts`."
msgstr ""
"`[MaybeUninit<u8>; 2048]` memungkinkan Anda menginisialisasi elemen satu per"
" satu, lalu mengambil sub-slice hanya dari prefiks yang telah diinisialisasi"
" dan memperlakukannya sebagai `[u8]` melalui `std::slice::from_raw_parts`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"`slice_assume_init_ref` is safe only when every element in the slice is "
"initialized. For this example, we only pass `&buf[..input.len()]` after "
"writing exactly those bytes."
msgstr ""
"`slice_assume_init_ref` aman hanya ketika setiap elemen dalam slice telah "
"diinisialisasi. Untuk contoh ini, kami hanya meneruskan "
"`&buf[..input.len()]` setelah menulis tepat byte tersebut."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/arrays.md
msgid ""
"When `T` needs drop, you must manually call `assume_init_drop()` for the "
"initialized elements. Skipping this leaks memory. However, calling it on an "
"uninitialized element is undefined behavior."
msgstr ""
"Saat `T` memerlukan drop, Anda harus memanggil `assume_init_drop()` secara "
"manual untuk elemen yang telah diinisialisasi. Melewati ini menyebabkan "
"memory leak. Namun, memanggilnya pada elemen yang belum diinisialisasi "
"adalah undefined behavior."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/zeroed-method.md
msgid "// SAFETY: All values of `x` have been written to\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: All values of `x` have been written to\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/zeroed-method.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "\"{x:?}\""
msgstr "\"{x:?}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/zeroed-method.md
msgid ""
"“MaybeUninit<T>::zeroed() is an alternative constructor to "
"MaybeUninit<T>::uninit(). It instructs the compiler to fill the bits of T "
"with zeros.”"
msgstr ""
"“MaybeUninit<T>::zeroed() adalah constructor alternatif bagi "
"MaybeUninit<T>::uninit(). Constructor ini menginstruksikan compiler untuk "
"mengisi bit T dengan nol.”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/zeroed-method.md
msgid ""
"Q: “Although the memory has been written to, the type remains "
"`MaybeUninit<T>`. Can anyone think of why?”"
msgstr ""
"T: “Meskipun memori telah ditulisi, tipenya tetap `MaybeUninit<T>`. Adakah "
"yang tahu mengapa?”"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/zeroed-method.md
msgid ""
"A: Some types require their values to be non-zero or non-null. The classic "
"case is references, but this applies to many other types as well. Consider "
"the `NonZeroUsize` integer type and others in its family."
msgstr ""
"J: Sebagian tipe mengharuskan nilainya bukan nol atau bukan null. Kasus "
"klasiknya adalah reference, tetapi ini juga berlaku untuk banyak tipe lain. "
"Pertimbangkan tipe integer `NonZeroUsize` dan tipe lain dalam keluarganya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "MaybeUninit.write() vs assignment"
msgstr "MaybeUninit.write() vs Penugasan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "// Initialize\n"
msgstr "// Initialize\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "// Overwrite\n"
msgstr "// Overwrite\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "\"Hi again\""
msgstr "\"Hi again\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "// Assignment replaces the whole MaybeUninit value.\n"
msgstr "// Assignment replaces the whole MaybeUninit value.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "\"Goodbye\""
msgstr "\"Goodbye\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid "// Ensure inner value is dropped\n"
msgstr "// Ensure inner value is dropped\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid ""
"Replacing inner values can cause memory leaks because the drop semantics "
"differ from most types. `MaybeUninit<T>` does not call the destructor on its"
" `T`."
msgstr ""
"Mengganti nilai dalam dapat menyebabkan memory leak karena semantik drop "
"berbeda dari sebagian besar tipe. `MaybeUninit<T>` tidak memanggil "
"destructor pada `T`-nya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid ""
"`MaybeUninit::write()` uses `ptr::write`: it initializes the memory in place"
" without reading or dropping the old contents. That is exactly what you want"
" when the memory might be uninitialized, but it also means you will leak if "
"there was already a live value there."
msgstr ""
"`MaybeUninit::write()` menggunakan `ptr::write`: method ini menginisialisasi"
" memori di tempat tanpa membaca atau men-drop isi lama. Itulah yang Anda "
"inginkan ketika memori mungkin belum diinisialisasi, tetapi ini juga berarti"
" Anda akan mengalami leak jika sudah ada nilai live di sana."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid ""
"Assignment, e.g. `buf = MaybeUninit::new(value)`, replaces the whole "
"`MaybeUninit`. The old `MaybeUninit` is moved and then dropped, but "
"`MaybeUninit` has no destructor for `T`, so the inner value is not dropped. "
"If the old slot held an initialized value, it is leaked just like with "
"`write()`."
msgstr ""
"Penugasan, misalnya `buf = MaybeUninit::new(value)`, menggantikan seluruh "
"`MaybeUninit`. `MaybeUninit` lama dipindahkan lalu di-drop, tetapi "
"`MaybeUninit` tidak memiliki destructor untuk `T`, sehingga nilai dalamnya "
"tidak di-drop. Jika slot lama berisi nilai yang telah diinisialisasi, nilai "
"itu mengalami leak seperti pada `write()`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/maybeuninit/write-vs-assignment.md
msgid ""
"If you need normal drop behavior, you need to tell Rust that the value is "
"initialized with `assume_init` or one of the related methods."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda memerlukan perilaku drop normal, Anda perlu memberi tahu Rust "
"bahwa nilai telah diinisialisasi dengan `assume_init` atau salah satu method"
" terkait."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "How to Initialize Memory"
msgstr "Cara Menginisialisasi Memori"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "Steps:"
msgstr "Langkah-langkah:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "Create `MaybeUninit<T>`"
msgstr "Buat `MaybeUninit<T>`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "Write a value to it"
msgstr "Tulis nilai ke dalamnya"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "Notify Rust that the memory is initialized"
msgstr "Beri tahu Rust bahwa memori telah diinisialisasi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "// Step 1: Create MaybeUninit\n"
msgstr "// Step 1: Create MaybeUninit\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "// Step 2: Write a valid value to the memory\n"
msgstr "// Step 2: Write a valid value to the memory\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "// Step 3: Inform the type system that the memory location is valid\n"
msgstr "// Step 3: Inform the type system that the memory location is valid\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid "\"{init}\""
msgstr "\"{init}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid ""
"To work with uninitialized memory, follow this general workflow: create, "
"write, confirm."
msgstr ""
"Untuk bekerja dengan memori yang belum diinisialisasi, ikuti alur kerja umum"
" ini: buat, tulis, konfirmasi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid ""
"Create `MaybeUninit<T>`. The `::uninit()` constructor is the most general-"
"purpose one, but there are others which perform a write as well."
msgstr ""
"Buat `MaybeUninit<T>`. Constructor `::uninit()` adalah yang paling umum, "
"tetapi ada constructor lain yang juga melakukan penulisan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid ""
"Write a value of T. Notice that this is available from safe Rust. Staying in"
" safe Rust is useful because you must ensure that the value you write is "
"valid."
msgstr ""
"Tulis nilai T. Perhatikan bahwa ini tersedia dari safe Rust. Tetap di safe "
"Rust bermanfaat karena Anda harus memastikan nilai yang Anda tulis valid."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/how-to-initialize-memory.md
msgid ""
"Confirm to the type system that the memory is now initialized with the "
"`.assume_init()` method."
msgstr ""
"Konfirmasikan kepada sistem tipe bahwa memori sekarang telah diinisialisasi "
"dengan method `.assume_init()`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid "Partial Initialization"
msgstr "Inisialisasi Parsial"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid "// let mut buf = [0u8; 2048];\n"
msgstr "// let mut buf = [0u8; 2048];\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid "b\"Hello, Rust!\""
msgstr "b\"Hello, Rust!\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid "// SAFETY: We initialized exactly 'len' bytes of `buf` with UTF-8 text\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: We initialized exactly 'len' bytes of `buf` with UTF-8 text\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid "This code simulates receiving data from some external source."
msgstr "Kode ini mensimulasikan penerimaan data dari suatu sumber eksternal."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid ""
"When reading bytes from an external source into a buffer, you typically "
"don't know how many bytes you'll receive. Using `MaybeUninit<T>` lets you "
"allocate the buffer once without paying for a redundant initialization pass."
msgstr ""
"Saat membaca byte dari sumber eksternal ke buffer, Anda biasanya tidak "
"mengetahui berapa byte yang akan diterima. Menggunakan `MaybeUninit<T>` "
"memungkinkan Anda mengalokasikan buffer sekali tanpa membayar pass "
"inisialisasi yang redundan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid ""
"If we were to create the array with the standard syntax (`buf = [0u8; "
"2048]`), the whole buffer would be flushed with zeroes. `MaybeUninit<T>` "
"tells the compiler to reserve space, but not to touch the memory yet."
msgstr ""
"Jika kita membuat array dengan sintaks standar (`buf = [0u8; 2048]`), "
"seluruh buffer akan diisi nol. `MaybeUninit<T>` memberi tahu compiler untuk "
"mencadangkan ruang, tetapi belum menyentuh memori."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid ""
"Q: Which part of the code snippet is performing a similar role to "
"`.assume_init()`? A: The pointer cast and the implicit read."
msgstr ""
"T: Bagian mana dari potongan kode yang menjalankan peran serupa dengan "
"`.assume_init()`? J: Cast pointer dan pembacaan implisit."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/initialization/partial-initialization.md
msgid ""
"We cannot call `assume_init()` on the whole array. That would be unsound "
"because most elements remain uninitialized. Instead, we cast the pointer "
"from `*const MaybeUninit<u8>` to `*const u8` and build a slice covering only"
" the initialised portion."
msgstr ""
"Kita tidak dapat memanggil `assume_init()` pada seluruh array. Itu akan "
"tidak sound karena sebagian besar elemen tetap belum diinisialisasi. Sebagai"
" gantinya, kami melakukan cast pointer dari `*const MaybeUninit<u8>` ke "
"`*const u8` dan membangun slice yang hanya mencakup bagian yang telah "
"diinisialisasi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid "This segment of the course covers:"
msgstr "Segmen kursus ini mencakup:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid "What \"pinning\" is"
msgstr "Apa itu \"pinning\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid "Why it is necessary"
msgstr "Mengapa hal itu diperlukan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid "How Rust implements it"
msgstr "Bagaimana Rust mengimplementasikannya"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid "How it interacts with unsafe and FFI"
msgstr "Bagaimana interaksinya dengan unsafe dan FFI"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid "This segment should take about 1 hour and 20 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Segmen ini seharusnya memakan waktu sekitar 1 jam 20 menit. Segmen ini "
"berisi:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/definition-of-pin.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid "Definition of Pin"
msgstr "Definisi Pin"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/phantompinned.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid "PhantomPinned"
msgstr "PhantomPinned"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid "Pin<Ptr> and Drop"
msgstr "Pin<Ptr> dan Drop"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid ""
"\"Pinning, or holding a value's memory address in a fixed location,is one of"
" the more challenging concepts in Rust.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Pinning, atau menahan alamat memori suatu nilai di lokasi tetap, adalah "
"salah satu konsep yang lebih menantang di Rust.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid ""
"\"Normally only seen within async code, i.e. [`poll(self: Pin<&mut "
"Self>)`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/future/trait.Future.html#tymethod.poll), pinning has wider "
"applicability.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Biasanya hanya terlihat dalam kode async, yaitu [`poll(self: Pin<&mut "
"Self>)`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/future/trait.Future.html#tymethod.poll), pinning memiliki "
"penerapan yang lebih luas.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid ""
"Some data structures that are difficult or impossible to write without the "
"unsafe keyword, including self-referential structs and intrusive data "
"structures."
msgstr ""
"Beberapa struktur data yang sulit atau mustahil ditulis tanpa keyword "
"unsafe, termasuk struct self-referential dan struktur data intrusive."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid ""
"FFI with C++ is a prominent use case that's related to this. Rust must "
"assume that any C++ with a reference might be a self-referential data "
"structure."
msgstr ""
"FFI dengan C++ adalah kasus penggunaan menonjol yang terkait dengan ini. "
"Rust harus mengasumsikan bahwa C++ apa pun yang memiliki reference mungkin "
"merupakan struktur data self-referential."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning.md
msgid ""
"\"To understand this conflict in more detail, we'll first need to make sure "
"that we have a strong understanding of Rust's move semantics.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Untuk memahami konflik ini lebih terperinci, kita perlu memastikan "
"pemahaman yang kuat tentang semantik move Rust.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid "A pinned type cannot change its memory address (move)"
msgstr "Tipe yang di-pin tidak dapat mengubah alamat memorinya (move)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid "The pointed-to value cannot be moved by safe code"
msgstr "Nilai yang ditunjuk tidak dapat dipindahkan oleh kode safe"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid ""
"`Pin<Ptr>` makes use of the ownership system to control how the pinned value"
" is accessed. Rather than changing the language, Rust's ownership system is "
"used to enforce pinning. `Pin` owns its contents and nothing in its safe API"
" triggers a move."
msgstr ""
"`Pin<Ptr>` memanfaatkan sistem ownership untuk mengontrol cara nilai yang "
"di-pin diakses. Alih-alih mengubah bahasa, sistem ownership Rust digunakan "
"untuk menegakkan pinning. `Pin` memiliki isinya dan tidak ada bagian dari "
"API safe-nya yang memicu move."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid "This is explained in"
msgstr "Ini dijelaskan dalam"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid "Conceptually, pinning prevents the default movement behavior."
msgstr "Secara konseptual, pinning mencegah perilaku perpindahan default."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid "This appears to be a change in the language itself."
msgstr "Ini tampak seperti perubahan pada bahasa itu sendiri."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid ""
"However, the `Pin` wrapper doesn't actually change anything fundamental "
"about the language."
msgstr ""
"Namun, wrapper `Pin` sebenarnya tidak mengubah apa pun yang fundamental pada"
" bahasa."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid ""
"`Pin` doesn't expose safe APIs that would allow a move. Thus, it can prevent"
" bitwise copy."
msgstr ""
"`Pin` tidak mengekspos API safe yang memungkinkan move. Dengan demikian, Pin"
" dapat mencegah copy bitwise."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid ""
"Unsafe APIs allow library authors to wrap types that do not implement "
"`Unpin`, but they must uphold the same guarantees."
msgstr ""
"API unsafe memungkinkan penulis library membungkus tipe yang tidak "
"mengimplementasikan `Unpin`, tetapi mereka harus menegakkan jaminan yang "
"sama."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid "The documentation of `Pin` uses the term \"pointer types\"."
msgstr "Dokumentasi `Pin` menggunakan istilah \"pointer type\"."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid ""
"The term \"pointer type\" is much more broad than the pointer primitive type"
" in the language."
msgstr ""
"Istilah \"pointer type\" jauh lebih luas daripada tipe primitif pointer "
"dalam bahasa."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid ""
"A \"pointer type\" wraps every type that implements `Deref` with a target "
"that implements `Unpin`."
msgstr ""
"\"Pointer type\" mencakup setiap tipe yang mengimplementasikan `Deref` "
"dengan target yang mengimplementasikan `Unpin`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-pinning-is.md
msgid ""
"Rust style note: This trait bound is enforced through trait bounds on the "
"`::new()` constructor, rather than on the type itself."
msgstr ""
"Catatan gaya Rust: Trait bound ini ditegakkan melalui trait bound pada "
"constructor `::new()`, bukan pada tipe itu sendiri."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "What a move is in Rust"
msgstr "Apa Itu Move di Rust"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "Always a bitwise copy, even for types that do not implement `Copy`:"
msgstr ""
"Selalu copy bitwise, bahkan untuk tipe yang tidak mengimplementasikan "
"`Copy`:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "b'R'"
msgstr "b'R'"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "b'U'"
msgstr "b'U'"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "b'S'"
msgstr "b'S'"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "b'T'"
msgstr "b'T'"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid ""
"Generated [LLVM IR](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=6f587283e8e0ec02f1ea8e871fc9ac72)"
" for calling `move_and_expect()`:"
msgstr ""
"[LLVM IR](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=6f587283e8e0ec02f1ea8e871fc9ac72)"
" yang dihasilkan untuk memanggil `move_and_expect()`:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "`memcpy` from variable `%b` to `%_12`"
msgstr "`memcpy` dari variabel `%b` ke `%_12`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "Call to `move_and_inspect` with `%_12` (the copy)"
msgstr "Pemanggilan `move_and_inspect` dengan `%_12` (salinannya)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "Note that `DynamicBuffer` does not implement `Copy`."
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa `DynamicBuffer` tidak mengimplementasikan `Copy`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid "Implication: a value's memory address is not stable."
msgstr "Implikasi: alamat memori suatu nilai tidak stabil."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/what-a-move-is.md
msgid ""
"To show movement as a bitwise copy, either [open the code in the "
"playground](https://play.rust-"
"lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=6f587283e8e0ec02f1ea8e871fc9ac72)"
" and look at the or [the Compiler "
"Explorer](https://rust.godbolt.org/z/6o6nP7do4)."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menunjukkan perpindahan sebagai copy bitwise, [buka kode di "
"playground](https://play.rust-"
