#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/definition-of-pin.md
msgid ""
"`Pin` is a minimal wrapper around a _pointer type_, which is defined as a "
"type that implements `Deref`."
msgstr ""
"`Pin` adalah wrapper minimal di sekitar _pointer type_, yang didefinisikan "
"sebagai tipe yang mengimplementasikan `Deref`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/definition-of-pin.md
msgid ""
"However, `Pin::new()` only accepts types that dereference into a target that"
" implements `Unpin` (`Deref<Target: Unpin>`). This allows `Pin` to rely on "
"the type system to enforce its guarantees."
msgstr ""
"Namun, `Pin::new()` hanya menerima tipe yang melakukan dereference ke target"
" yang mengimplementasikan `Unpin` (`Deref<Target: Unpin>`). Ini memungkinkan"
" `Pin` mengandalkan sistem tipe untuk menegakkan jaminannya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/definition-of-pin.md
msgid ""
"Types that do not implement `Unpin`, i.e., types that require pinning, must "
"create a `Pin` via the unsafe `Pin::new_unchecked()`."
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang tidak mengimplementasikan `Unpin`, yaitu tipe yang memerlukan "
"pinning, harus membuat `Pin` melalui `Pin::new_unchecked()` yang unsafe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/definition-of-pin.md
msgid ""
"Aside: Unlike other `new()`/`new_unchecked()` method pairs, `new` does not "
"do any runtime checking. The check is a zero-cost compile-time check."
msgstr ""
"Catatan samping: Berbeda dari pasangan method `new()`/`new_unchecked()` "
"lainnya, `new` tidak melakukan pemeriksaan runtime. Pemeriksaannya adalah "
"pemeriksaan waktu kompilasi zero-cost."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid "Why Pin is difficult to use"
msgstr "Mengapa Pin Sulit Digunakan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid "`Pin<Ptr>` is \"just\" a type defined in the standard library"
msgstr "`Pin<Ptr>` \"hanyalah\" tipe yang didefinisikan di standard library"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid ""
"This satisfied the needs of its original audience, the creators of async "
"runtimes, without needing to extending the core language"
msgstr ""
"Ini memenuhi kebutuhan audiens aslinya, para pembuat async runtime, tanpa "
"perlu memperluas bahasa inti"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid ""
"That audience could accept some of its ergonomic downsides, as users of "
"`async` would rarely interact with `Pin` directly"
msgstr ""
"Audiens tersebut dapat menerima sebagian kekurangan ergonomisnya, karena "
"pengguna `async` jarang berinteraksi langsung dengan `Pin`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid ""
"\"You might wonder why Pin is so awkward to use. The answer is largely "
"historical.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Anda mungkin bertanya-tanya mengapa Pin begitu canggung digunakan. "
"Jawabannya sebagian besar bersifat historis.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid ""
"\"`Pin<Ptr>` offered a simpler implementation for the Rust project than "
"alternatives\"."
msgstr ""
"\"`Pin<Ptr>` menawarkan implementasi yang lebih sederhana bagi proyek Rust "
"dibandingkan alternatifnya\"."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid ""
"\"Pin was designed primarily for the ~100 people in the world who write "
"async runtimes. The Rust team chose a simpler (for the compiler) but less "
"ergonomic design.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Pin dirancang terutama untuk ~100 orang di dunia yang menulis async "
"runtime. Tim Rust memilih desain yang lebih sederhana (bagi compiler) tetapi"
" kurang ergonomis.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/why-difficult.md
msgid ""
"\"More user-friendly proposals existed but were rejected as too complex for "
"the primary audience, who could handle the complexity.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ada proposal yang lebih ramah pengguna, tetapi ditolak karena terlalu "
"kompleks bagi audiens utama, yang justru mampu menangani kompleksitas.\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "Unpin trait"
msgstr "Trait Unpin"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid ""
"`Unpin` type allows types to move freely, even when they're wrapped by a "
"`Pin`"
msgstr ""
"Tipe `Unpin` memungkinkan tipe bergerak bebas, bahkan saat dibungkus oleh "
"`Pin`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "Most types implement `Unpin`, because it is an \"`auto trait`\""
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar tipe mengimplementasikan `Unpin`, karena ini adalah \"`auto "
"trait`\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "`auto trait` behavior can be changed:"
msgstr "Perilaku `auto trait` dapat diubah:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "`!Unpin` types must never move"
msgstr "Tipe `!Unpin` tidak boleh pernah bergerak"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid ""
"Types containing a `PhantomPinned` field do not implement `Unpin` by default"
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang berisi field `PhantomPinned` tidak mengimplementasikan `Unpin` "
"secara default"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid ""
"Explain that when a trait implements `Unpin`, the pinning behavior of "
"`Pin<Ptr>` does not get invoked. The value is free to move."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa ketika suatu tipe mengimplementasikan `Unpin`, perilaku "
"pinning dari `Pin<Ptr>` tidak dipicu. Nilai bebas bergerak."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid ""
"Explain that almost all types implement `Unpin`; automatically implemented "
"by the compiler."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa hampir semua tipe mengimplementasikan `Unpin`; "
"diimplementasikan otomatis oleh compiler."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid ""
"Types implementing `Unpin` are saying: 'I promise I have no self-references,"
" so moving me is always safe.'"
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang mengimplementasikan `Unpin` menyatakan: 'Saya berjanji tidak "
"memiliki self-reference, jadi memindahkan saya selalu aman.'"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "Ask: What types might be `!Unpin`?"
msgstr "Tanyakan: Tipe apa yang mungkin `!Unpin`?"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "Compiler-generated futures"
msgstr "Future yang dihasilkan compiler"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "Types containing a `PhantomPinned` field"
msgstr "Tipe yang berisi field `PhantomPinned`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "Some types wrapping C++ objects"
msgstr "Beberapa tipe yang membungkus objek C++"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/unpin-trait.md
msgid "`!Unpin` types cannot be moved once pinned"
msgstr "Tipe `!Unpin` tidak dapat dipindahkan setelah di-pin"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/phantompinned.md
msgid "Definition"
msgstr "Definisi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/phantompinned.md
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "Penggunaan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/phantompinned.md
msgid "`PhantomPinned` is a marker type."
msgstr "`PhantomPinned` adalah marker type."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/phantompinned.md
msgid ""
"If a type contains a `PhantomPinned`, it will not implement `Unpin` by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Jika suatu tipe berisi `PhantomPinned`, tipe tersebut tidak akan "
"mengimplementasikan `Unpin` secara default."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/phantompinned.md
msgid ""
"This has the effect of enforcing pinning when `DynamicBuffer` is wrapped by "
"`Pin`."
msgstr ""
"Ini berefek menegakkan pinning saat `DynamicBuffer` dibungkus oleh `Pin`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid ""
"A \"self-referential buffer\" is a type that has a reference to one of its "
"own fields:"
msgstr ""
"\"Self-referential buffer\" adalah tipe yang memiliki reference ke salah "
"satu field-nya sendiri:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid ""
"This kind of structure is not typical in Rust, because there's no way to "
"update the cursor's address when instances of `SelfReferentialBuffer` move."
msgstr ""
"Struktur semacam ini tidak lazim di Rust, karena tidak ada cara memperbarui "
"alamat cursor saat instance `SelfReferentialBuffer` dipindahkan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer.md
msgid ""
"However, this kind of setup is more natural in other languages that provide "
"garbage collection, and also C++ that allows users to define their own "
"behavior during moves and copies."
msgstr ""
"Namun, penyiapan semacam ini lebih alami di bahasa lain yang menyediakan "
"garbage collection, dan juga C++ yang memungkinkan pengguna mendefinisikan "
"perilaku sendiri selama move dan copy."

