msgstr ""
"Tekankan bahwa `unsafe` muncul sering. Ini petunjuk bahwa desain lain "
"mungkin lebih tepat."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-raw-pointers.md
msgid "`unsafe` blocks lack safety comments. Therefore, this code is unsound."
msgstr ""
"Block `unsafe` tidak memiliki komentar safety. Karena itu, kode ini tidak "
"sound."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-raw-pointers.md
msgid ""
"`unsafe` blocks are too broad. Good practice uses smaller `unsafe` blocks "
"with specific behavior, specific preconditions and specific safety comments."
msgstr ""
"Block `unsafe` terlalu luas. Praktik yang baik menggunakan block `unsafe` "
"lebih kecil dengan perilaku spesifik, prasyarat spesifik, dan komentar "
"safety spesifik."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-raw-pointers.md
msgid "Questions:"
msgstr "Pertanyaan:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-raw-pointers.md
msgid ""
"Q: Should the `read()` and `write()` methods be marked as unsafe?  \n"
"A: Yes, because `self.cursor` will be a null pointer unless written to."
msgstr ""
"T: Haruskah method `read()` dan `write()` ditandai sebagai unsafe?  \n"
"J: Ya, karena `self.cursor` akan menjadi null pointer kecuali ditulisi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-offset.md
msgid "With Offset"
msgstr "Dengan Offset"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-offset.md
msgid ""
"In Rust, it's more idiomatic to use an offset variable and to create "
"references on-demand."
msgstr ""
"Di Rust, lebih idiomatis menggunakan variabel offset dan membuat reference "
"sesuai kebutuhan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-pin.md
msgid ""
"Pinning allows Rust programmers to create a type which is much more similar "
"to C++ classes."
msgstr ""
"Pinning memungkinkan programmer Rust membuat tipe yang jauh lebih mirip "
"class C++."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-pin.md
msgid "/// A self-referential buffer that cannot be moved.\n"
msgstr "/// A self-referential buffer that cannot be moved.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-pin.md
msgid ""
"Note that the function signatures have now changed. For example, `::new()` "
"returns `Pin<Box<Self>>` rather than `Self`. This incurs a heap allocation "
"because `Pin<Ptr>` must work with a pointer type like `Box`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa signature fungsi sekarang berubah. Misalnya, `::new()` "
"mengembalikan `Pin<Box<Self>>` alih-alih `Self`. Ini menimbulkan alokasi "
"heap karena `Pin<Ptr>` harus bekerja dengan tipe pointer seperti `Box`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/self-referential-buffer/rust-pin.md
msgid ""
"In `::new()`, we use `Pin::get_unchecked_mut()` to get a mutable reference "
"to the buffer _after_ it has been pinned. This is `unsafe` because we are "
"breaking the pinning guarantee for a moment to initialize the `cursor`. We "
"must make sure not to move the `SelfReferentialBuffer` after this point. The"
" safety contract of `Pin` is that once a value is pinned, its memory "
"location is fixed until it is dropped."
msgstr ""
"Dalam `::new()`, kami menggunakan `Pin::get_unchecked_mut()` untuk "
"mendapatkan reference mutable ke buffer _setelah_ buffer di-pin. Ini "
"`unsafe` karena kami melanggar jaminan pinning sesaat untuk menginisialisasi"
" `cursor`. Kami harus memastikan tidak memindahkan `SelfReferentialBuffer` "
"setelah titik ini. Kontrak keamanan `Pin` adalah setelah suatu nilai di-pin,"
" lokasi memorinya tetap hingga di-drop."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid "<code>Pin\\<Ptr\\></code> and <code>Drop</code>"
msgstr "<code>Pin\\<Ptr\\></code> dan <code>Drop</code>"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid ""
"A key challenge with pinned, `!Unpin` types is implementing the `Drop` "
"trait. The `drop` method takes `&mut self`, which allows moving the value. "
"However, pinned values must not be moved."
msgstr ""
"Tantangan utama dengan tipe `!Unpin` yang di-pin adalah mengimplementasikan "
"trait `Drop`. Method `drop` menerima `&mut self`, yang memungkinkan "
"pemindahan nilai. Namun, nilai yang di-pin tidak boleh dipindahkan."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid "An Incorrect `Drop` Implementation"
msgstr "Implementasi `Drop` yang Salah"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid ""
"It's easy to accidentally move a value inside `drop`. Operations like "
"assignment, `ptr::read`, and `mem::replace` can silently break the pinning "
"guarantee."
msgstr ""
"Mudah secara tidak sengaja memindahkan nilai di dalam `drop`. Operasi "
"seperti penugasan, `ptr::read`, dan `mem::replace` dapat secara diam-diam "
"merusak jaminan pinning."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid ""
"// BAD: `ptr::read` moves `self.data` out of `self`.\n"
"        // When `_dupe` is dropped at the end of the function, it's a double free!\n"
msgstr ""
"// BAD: `ptr::read` moves `self.data` out of `self`.\n"
"        // When `_dupe` is dropped at the end of the function, it's a double free!\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid ""
"Pinned types make guarantees about memory stability. Operations like "
"`ptr::read` and `mem::replace` can silently break these guarantees by moving"
" or duplicating data, invalidating internal pointers without the type "
"system's knowledge."
msgstr ""
"Tipe yang di-pin memberikan jaminan tentang stabilitas memori. Operasi "
"seperti `ptr::read` dan `mem::replace` dapat secara diam-diam merusak "
"jaminan tersebut dengan memindahkan atau menduplikasi data, membuat pointer "
"internal tidak valid tanpa sepengetahuan sistem tipe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid ""
"In this `drop()` method, `_dupe` is a bitwise copy of `self.data`. At the "
"end of the method, it will be dropped along with `self`. This double drop is"
" undefined behavior."
msgstr ""
"Dalam method `drop()` ini, `_dupe` adalah salinan bitwise dari `self.data`. "
"Di akhir method, _dupe akan di-drop bersama `self`. Double drop ini adalah "
"undefined behavior."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid "A Correct `Drop` Implementation"
msgstr "Implementasi `Drop` yang Benar"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid ""
"To implement `Drop` correctly for a `!Unpin` type, you must ensure that the "
"value is not moved. A common pattern is to create a helper function that "
"operates on `Pin<&mut T>`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengimplementasikan `Drop` dengan benar bagi tipe `!Unpin`, Anda harus"
" memastikan nilainya tidak dipindahkan. Pola umumnya adalah membuat fungsi "
"helper yang beroperasi pada `Pin<&mut T>`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid "// SAFETY: `this` is pinned before we create the self-reference.\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: `this` is pinned before we create the self-reference.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid "// This function can only be called on a pinned `SelfRef`.\n"
msgstr "// This function can only be called on a pinned `SelfRef`.\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/pinning/pin-and-drop.md
msgid "// `self` is pinned, so we must not move out of it.\n"
msgstr "// `self` is pinned, so we must not move out of it.\n"

