msgid "C"
msgstr "C"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "**Errors**"
msgstr "**Error**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "`Result<T, E>`, `Option<T>`"
msgstr "`Result<T, E>`, `Option<T>`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Magic return values, out-parameters, global `errno`"
msgstr "Nilai kembalian ajaib, out-parameter, `errno` global"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "**Strings**"
msgstr "**String**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "`&str`/`String` (UTF-8, length-known)"
msgstr "`&str`/`String` (UTF-8, panjang diketahui)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Null-terminated `char*`, encoding undefined"
msgstr "`char*` diakhiri null, encoding tidak ditentukan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "**Nullability**"
msgstr "**Nullability**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Explicit via `Option<T>`"
msgstr "Eksplisit melalui `Option<T>`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Any pointer may be null"
msgstr "Pointer apa pun mungkin null"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "**Ownership**"
msgstr "**Ownership**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Affine types, lifetimes"
msgstr "Tipe affine, lifetime"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr "Konvensi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "**Callbacks**"
msgstr "**Callback**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "`Fn`/`FnMut`/`FnOnce` closures"
msgstr "`Fn`/`FnMut`/`FnOnce` closures"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Function pointer + `void* userdata`"
msgstr "Function pointer + `void* userdata`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "**Panics**"
msgstr "**Panic**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Stack unwinding (or abort)"
msgstr "Stack unwinding (atau abort)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Abort"
msgstr "Abort"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Errors: Must convert `Result` to abide by C conventions; easy to forget to "
"check errors on C side."
msgstr ""
"Error: Harus mengonversi `Result` agar sesuai konvensi C; mudah lupa "
"memeriksa error di sisi C."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Strings: Conversion cost; null bytes in Rust strings cause truncation; UTF-8"
" validation on ingress."
msgstr ""
"String: Biaya konversi; byte null dalam string Rust menyebabkan truncation; "
"validasi UTF-8 saat masuk."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Nullability: Every pointer from C must be checked to create an "
"`Option<NonNull<T>>`, implying unsafe blocks or runtime cost."
msgstr ""
"Nullability: Setiap pointer dari C harus diperiksa untuk membuat "
"`Option<NonNull<T>>`, yang menyiratkan block unsafe atau biaya runtime."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid "Ownership: Must document and enforce object lifetimes manually."
msgstr ""
"Ownership: Harus mendokumentasikan dan menegakkan lifetime objek secara "
"manual."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Callbacks: Must decompose closures into fn pointer + context; lifetime of "
"context is manual."
msgstr ""
"Callback: Harus menguraikan closure menjadi fn pointer + context; lifetime "
"context ditangani manual."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Panics: Panic across FFI boundary is undefined behavior; must catch at "
"boundary with `catch_unwind`."
msgstr ""
"Panic: Panic melintasi batas FFI adalah undefined behavior; harus ditangkap "
"di batas dengan `catch_unwind`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "C++"
msgstr "C++"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "**Overloading**"
msgstr "**Overloading**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "Manual/ad-hoc"
msgstr "Manual/ad-hoc"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr "Otomatis"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "**Exceptions**"
msgstr "**Exception**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "\\-"
msgstr "\\-"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "Stack unwinding"
msgstr "Stack unwinding"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "**Destructors**"
msgstr "**Destructor**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "Manual cleanup"
msgstr "Pembersihan manual"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "Automatic via destructors (RAII)"
msgstr "Otomatis melalui destructor (RAII)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "**Non-POD types**"
msgstr "**Tipe non-POD**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "Objects with constructors, vtables, virtual bases"
msgstr "Objek dengan constructor, vtable, virtual base"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "**Templates**"
msgstr "**Template**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid "Compile-time code generation"
msgstr "Pembuatan kode waktu kompilasi"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid ""
"C++ includes a number of features that don't exist in C with an FFI impact:"
msgstr "C++ mencakup sejumlah fitur yang tidak ada di C dengan dampak FFI:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Overloading: Overloads become impossible to express because of name mangling"
msgstr ""
"Overloading: Overload menjadi mustahil diekspresikan karena name mangling"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Exceptions: Must catch exceptions at the FFI boundary and convert them to "
"error codes, as escaping exceptions in `extern \"C\"` functions constitute "
"undefined behavior"
msgstr ""
"Exception: Harus menangkap exception di batas FFI dan mengonversinya menjadi"
" kode error, karena exception yang lolos dari fungsi `extern \"C\"` "
"merupakan undefined behavior"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Destructors: C callers won't run destructors; must expose explicit "
"`*_destroy()` functions"
msgstr ""
"Destructor: Pemanggil C tidak akan menjalankan destructor; harus mengekspos "
"fungsi `*_destroy()` eksplisit"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Non-POD types: Must use opaque pointers across the FFI boundary as pass by "
"value does not make sense"
msgstr ""
"Tipe non-POD: Harus menggunakan opaque pointer melintasi batas FFI karena "
"pass by value tidak masuk akal"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md
msgid ""
"Templates: Cannot expose directly; must instantiate explicitly and wrap each"
" specialization"
msgstr ""
"Template: Tidak dapat diekspos secara langsung; harus diinstansiasi secara "
"eksplisit dan setiap spesialisasi dibungkus"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "**Trivial relocatability**"
msgstr "**Trivial relocatability**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "All moves are `memcpy`"
msgstr "Semua move adalah `memcpy`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "Self-referential types, move constructors can have side effects"
msgstr "Tipe self-referential, move constructor dapat memiliki efek samping"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "**Destruction safety**"
msgstr "**Keamanan destruction**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "`Drop::drop()` on original location only"
msgstr "`Drop::drop()` hanya pada lokasi asli"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "Destructor may run on moved-from objects"
msgstr "Destructor dapat berjalan pada objek yang telah dipindahkan"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "**Exception safety**"
msgstr "**Exception safety**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "Panics (abort or unwind)"
msgstr "Panic (abort atau unwind)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "Exceptions (unwind)"
msgstr "Exception (unwind)"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "**ABI stability**"
msgstr "**Stabilitas ABI**"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "Explicitly unstable"
msgstr "Secara eksplisit tidak stabil"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "Vendor-specific"
msgstr "Spesifik vendor"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Even if it were possible to avoid interop via C, there are still some areas "
"of the languages that impact FFI:"
msgstr ""
"Bahkan jika interop melalui C dapat dihindari, masih ada beberapa area "
"bahasa yang memengaruhi FFI:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "_Trivial relocatability_"
msgstr "_Trivial relocatability_"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Cannot safely move C++ objects on the Rust side; must pin or keep in C++ "
"heap."
msgstr ""
"Tidak dapat memindahkan objek C++ dengan aman di sisi Rust; harus di-pin "
"atau disimpan di heap C++."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid ""
"In Rust, object movement, which occurs during assignment or by being passed "
"by value, always copies values bit by bit."
msgstr ""
"Di Rust, perpindahan objek, yang terjadi saat penugasan atau saat diteruskan"
" by value, selalu menyalin nilai bit demi bit."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid ""
"C++ allows users to define their own semantics by allowing them to overload "
"the assignment operator and create move and copy constructors."
msgstr ""
"C++ memungkinkan pengguna mendefinisikan semantik sendiri dengan mengizinkan"
" overload operator penugasan serta membuat move dan copy constructor."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid ""
"This impacts interop because self-referential types become natural in high-"
"performance C++. Custom constructors can uphold safety invariants even when "
"the object moves its position in memory."
msgstr ""
"Ini memengaruhi interop karena tipe self-referential menjadi wajar dalam C++"
" berperforma tinggi. Constructor khusus dapat mempertahankan invariant "
"keamanan bahkan saat objek berpindah posisi di memori."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "Objects with the same semantics are impossible to define in Rust."
msgstr "Objek dengan semantik yang sama mustahil didefinisikan di Rust."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "_Destruction safety_"
msgstr "_Keamanan destruction_"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Moved-from C++ object semantics don't map; must prevent Rust from \"moving\""
" C++ types."
msgstr ""
"Semantik objek C++ yang telah dipindahkan tidak dapat dipetakan; harus "
"mencegah Rust \"memindahkan\" tipe C++."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid "_Exception safety_"
msgstr "_Exception safety_"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/rust-and-cpp.md
msgid ""
"Neither can cross into the other safely; both must catch at the boundary."
msgstr ""
"Keduanya tidak dapat menyeberang ke yang lain dengan aman; keduanya harus "
"menangkap di batas."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Wrapping `abs(3)`"
msgstr "Membungkus `abs(3)`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "In this slide, we’re establishing a pattern for writing wrappers."
msgstr "Pada slide ini, kami menetapkan pola untuk menulis wrapper."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Find the external definition of a function’s signature Write a matching "
"function in Rust within an `extern` block Confirm which safety invariants "
"need to be upheld Decide whether it’s possible to mark the function as safe"
msgstr ""
"Temukan definisi eksternal signature fungsi. Tulis fungsi yang cocok di Rust"
" dalam block `extern`. Konfirmasikan invariant keamanan mana yang perlu "
"ditegakkan. Putuskan apakah fungsi dapat ditandai sebagai safe."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Note that this doesn’t work _yet_."
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa ini _belum_ berfungsi."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Add the extern block:"
msgstr "Tambahkan block extern:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Explain that many POSIX functions are available in Rust because Cargo links "
"against the C standard library (libc) by default, which brings its symbols "
"into the program’s scope."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa banyak fungsi POSIX tersedia di Rust karena Cargo secara "
"default menautkan ke standard library C (libc), yang membawa simbolnya ke "
"scope program."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Show `man 3 abs` in the terminal or [a "
"webpage](https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/abs.3.html)."
msgstr ""
"Tampilkan `man 3 abs` di terminal atau [halaman "
"web](https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/abs.3.html)."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Explain that our function signature must match its definition: `int abs(int "
"j);`."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa signature fungsi kita harus cocok dengan definisinya: `int "
"abs(int j);`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Update the code block to use the C types."
msgstr "Perbarui block kode agar menggunakan tipe C."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Discuss rationale: using `ffi::c_int` increases the portability of our code."
" When the standard library is compiled for the target platform, the platform"
" can determine the widths. According to the C standard, a `c_int` may be "
"defined as an `i16` rather than the much more common `i32`."
msgstr ""
"Diskusikan alasannya: menggunakan `ffi::c_int` meningkatkan portabilitas "
"kode kita. Saat standard library dikompilasi untuk platform target, platform"
" dapat menentukan lebarnya. Menurut standar C, `c_int` dapat didefinisikan "
"sebagai `i16` alih-alih `i32` yang jauh lebih umum."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"(Optional) Show the [documentation for c_int](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/ffi/type.c_int.html) to reveal that it is a type alias for "
"`i32`."
msgstr ""
"(Opsional) Tampilkan [dokumentasi c_int](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/ffi/type.c_int.html) untuk menunjukkan bahwa itu adalah type "
"alias untuk `i32`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Attempt to compile to trigger “error: extern blocks must be unsafe” error "
"message."
msgstr ""
"Coba kompilasi untuk memicu pesan error “error: extern blocks must be "
"unsafe”."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Add the unsafe keyword to the block:"
msgstr "Tambahkan keyword unsafe ke block:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Check that learners understand the significance of this change. We are "
"required to uphold type safety and other safety preconditions."
msgstr ""
"Pastikan pembelajar memahami pentingnya perubahan ini. Kita diwajibkan "
"menegakkan type safety dan safety precondition lainnya."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Recompile."
msgstr "Kompilasi ulang."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Add safe keyword to the abs function:"
msgstr "Tambahkan keyword safe ke fungsi abs:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid ""
"Explain that the `safe fn` marks `abs` as safe to call without an `unsafe` "
"block."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa `safe fn` menandai `abs` aman dipanggil tanpa block `unsafe`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/abs.md
msgid "Completed program for reference:"
msgstr "Program lengkap sebagai referensi:"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid "Wrapping `srand(3)` and `rand(3)`"
msgstr "Membungkus `srand(3)` dan `rand(3)`"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid ""
"// unsafe extern \"C\" {\n"
"//     /// Seed the rng\n"
"//     fn srand(seed: std::ffi::c_uint);\n"
msgstr ""
"// unsafe extern \"C\" {\n"
"//     /// Seed the rng\n"
"//     fn srand(seed: std::ffi::c_uint);\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid ""
"//     fn rand() -> std::ffi::c_int;\n"
"// }\n"
msgstr ""
"//     fn rand() -> std::ffi::c_int;\n"
"// }\n"

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid "\"{a:?}\""
msgstr "\"{a:?}\""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid ""
"This slide attempts to demonstrate that it is very easy for wrappers to "
"trigger undefined behavior if they are written incorrectly. We’ll see how "
"easy it is to trigger type safety problems."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini mencoba menunjukkan bahwa sangat mudah bagi wrapper memicu "
"undefined behavior jika ditulis secara keliru. Kita akan melihat betapa "
"mudahnya memicu masalah type safety."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid ""
"Explain that `rand` and `srand` functions are provided by the C standard "
"library (libc)."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa fungsi `rand` dan `srand` disediakan oleh standard library C "
"(libc)."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid ""
"Explain that the functions are exported by the libc crate, but we can also "
"write an FFI wrapper for them manually."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa fungsi tersebut diekspor oleh crate libc, tetapi kita juga "
"dapat menulis wrapper FFI secara manual."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid "Show calling the functions from the exported."
msgstr "Tunjukkan pemanggilan fungsi dari yang diekspor."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid "Code compiles because libc is linked to Rust programs by default."
msgstr ""
"Kode dapat dikompilasi karena libc ditautkan ke program Rust secara default."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid "Explain that Rust will trust you if you use the wrong type(s)."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa Rust akan mempercayai Anda jika menggunakan tipe yang salah."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid "Modify `fn rand() -> std::ffi::c_int;` to return `char`."
msgstr "Ubah `fn rand() -> std::ffi::c_int;` agar mengembalikan `char`."

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/rand.md
msgid ""
"Avoiding type safety issues is a reason for using tools for generating "
"wrappers, rather than doing it by hand."
msgstr ""
"Menghindari masalah type safety adalah alasan menggunakan alat untuk "
"menghasilkan wrapper, bukan melakukannya secara manual."

