#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"The following is a glossary which aims to give a short definition of many "
"Rust terms. For translations, this also serves to connect the term back to "
"the English original."
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah glosarium yang bertujuan memberikan definisi singkat untuk "
"banyak istilah Rust. Untuk terjemahan, glosarium ini juga berfungsi "
"menghubungkan istilah kembali ke bahasa Inggris aslinya."

#. Please add the English term in italic after your translated term. Also,
#. please keep the hard line breaks to ensure a nice formatting.
#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"allocate:  \n"
"Dynamic memory allocation on [the heap](memory-management/review.md)."
msgstr ""
"allocate:  \n"
"Alokasi memori dinamis di [heap](memory-management/review.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"array:  \n"
"A fixed-size collection of elements of the same type, stored contiguously in memory. See [Arrays](tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md)."
msgstr ""
"array:  \n"
"Koleksi elemen bertipe sama berukuran tetap, disimpan secara bersebelahan di memori. Lihat [Array](tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"associated type:  \n"
"A type associated with a specific trait. Useful for defining the relationship between types."
msgstr ""
"associated type:  \n"
"Tipe yang terkait dengan trait tertentu. Berguna untuk mendefinisikan hubungan antartipe."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"Bare-metal Rust:  \n"
"Low-level Rust development, often deployed to a system without an operating system. See [Bare-metal Rust](bare-metal.md)."
msgstr ""
"Bare-metal Rust:  \n"
"Pengembangan Rust tingkat rendah, sering diterapkan pada sistem tanpa sistem operasi. Lihat [Bare-metal Rust](bare-metal.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"block:  \n"
"See [Blocks](control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md) and _scope_."
msgstr ""
"block:  \n"
"Lihat [Block](control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md) dan _scope_."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"borrow:  \n"
"See [Borrowing](borrowing/shared.md)."
msgstr ""
"borrow:  \n"
"Lihat [Borrowing](borrowing/shared.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"borrow checker:  \n"
"The part of the Rust compiler which checks that all [borrows](borrowing/borrowck.md) are valid."
msgstr ""
"borrow checker:  \n"
"Bagian compiler Rust yang memeriksa bahwa semua [borrow](borrowing/borrowck.md) valid."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"brace:  \n"
"`{` and `}`. Also called _curly brace_, they delimit [_blocks_](control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md)."
msgstr ""
"brace:  \n"
"`{` dan `}`. Juga disebut _curly brace_, keduanya membatasi [_block_](control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"channel:  \n"
"Used to safely pass messages [between threads](concurrency/channels.md)."
msgstr ""
"channel:  \n"
"Digunakan untuk meneruskan pesan secara aman [antar-thread](concurrency/channels.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"concurrency:  \n"
"The execution of multiple tasks or processes at the same time. See [Welcome to Concurrency in Rust](concurrency/welcome.md)."
msgstr ""
"concurrency:  \n"
"Eksekusi beberapa task atau proses pada waktu yang sama. Lihat [Selamat Datang di Konkurensi di Rust](concurrency/welcome.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"constant:  \n"
"A value that does not change during the execution of a program. See [const](user-defined-types/const.md)."
msgstr ""
"constant:  \n"
"Nilai yang tidak berubah selama eksekusi program. Lihat [const](user-defined-types/const.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"control flow:  \n"
"The order in which the individual statements or instructions are executed in a program. See [Control Flow Basics](control-flow-basics.md)."
msgstr ""
"control flow:  \n"
"Urutan eksekusi statement atau instruksi individual dalam program. Lihat [Dasar-Dasar Control Flow](control-flow-basics.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"crash:  \n"
"An unexpected and unhandled failure or termination of a program. See [panic](error-handling/panics.md)."
msgstr ""
"crash:  \n"
"Kegagalan atau penghentian program yang tidak terduga dan tidak tertangani. Lihat [panic](error-handling/panics.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"enumeration:  \n"
"A data type that holds one of several named constants, possibly with an associated tuple or struct. See [enum](user-defined-types/enums.md)."
msgstr ""
"enumeration:  \n"
"Tipe data yang berisi salah satu dari beberapa konstanta bernama, mungkin dengan tuple atau struct terkait. Lihat [enum](user-defined-types/enums.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"error:  \n"
"An unexpected condition or result that deviates from the expected behavior. See [Error Handling](error-handling.md)."
msgstr ""
"error:  \n"
"Kondisi atau hasil tak terduga yang menyimpang dari perilaku yang diharapkan. Lihat [Error Handling](error-handling.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"error handling:  \n"
"The process of managing and responding to [errors](error-handling.md) that occur during program execution."
msgstr ""
"error handling:  \n"
"Proses mengelola dan merespons [error](error-handling.md) yang terjadi selama eksekusi program."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"function:  \n"
"A reusable block of code that performs a specific task. See [Functions](control-flow-basics/functions.md)."
msgstr ""
"function:  \n"
"Blok kode yang dapat digunakan kembali dan menjalankan tugas tertentu. Lihat [Fungsi](control-flow-basics/functions.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"garbage collector:  \n"
"A mechanism that automatically frees up memory occupied by objects that are no longer in use. See [Approaches to Memory Management](memory-management/approaches.md)."
msgstr ""
"garbage collector:  \n"
"Mekanisme yang secara otomatis membebaskan memori yang ditempati objek yang tidak lagi digunakan. Lihat [Pendekatan Manajemen Memori](memory-management/approaches.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"generics:  \n"
"A feature that allows writing code with placeholders for types, enabling code reuse with different data types. See [Generics](generics.md)."
msgstr ""
"generics:  \n"
"Fitur yang memungkinkan penulisan kode dengan placeholder untuk tipe, sehingga kode dapat digunakan kembali dengan tipe data berbeda. Lihat [Generic](generics.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"immutable:  \n"
"Unable to be changed after creation. See [Variables](types-and-values/variables.md)."
msgstr ""
"immutable:  \n"
"Tidak dapat diubah setelah dibuat. Lihat [Variabel](types-and-values/variables.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"integration test:  \n"
"A type of test that verifies the interactions between different parts or components of a system. See [Other Types of Tests](testing/other.md)."
msgstr ""
"integration test:  \n"
"Jenis test yang memverifikasi interaksi antarbagian atau komponen sistem yang berbeda. Lihat [Jenis Test Lain](testing/other.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"library:  \n"
"A collection of precompiled routines or code that can be used by programs. See [Modules](modules.md)."
msgstr ""
"library:  \n"
"Kumpulan rutin atau kode yang telah dikompilasi yang dapat digunakan oleh program. Lihat [Modul](modules.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"macro:  \n"
"Rust [macros](control-flow-basics/macros.md) can be recognized by a `!` in the name. Macros are used when normal functions are not enough. A typical example is `format!`, which takes a variable number of arguments, which isn't supported by Rust functions."
msgstr ""
"macro:  \n"
"[Macro](control-flow-basics/macros.md) Rust dapat dikenali dengan `!` pada namanya. Macro digunakan ketika fungsi biasa tidak cukup. Contoh khasnya adalah `format!`, yang menerima jumlah argumen bervariasi, yang tidak didukung fungsi Rust."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"`main` function:  \n"
"Rust programs start executing with the [`main` function](types-and-values/hello-world.md)."
msgstr ""
"`main` function:  \n"
"Program Rust mulai dieksekusi dengan [fungsi `main`](types-and-values/hello-world.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"match:  \n"
"A control flow construct in Rust that allows for [pattern matching](pattern-matching.md) on the value of an expression."
msgstr ""
"match:  \n"
"Konstruk control flow di Rust yang memungkinkan [pattern matching](pattern-matching.md) pada nilai suatu expression."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"memory leak:  \n"
"A situation where a program fails to release memory that is no longer needed, leading to a gradual increase in memory usage. See [Approaches to Memory Management](memory-management/approaches.md)."
msgstr ""
"memory leak:  \n"
"Situasi ketika program gagal melepaskan memori yang tidak lagi diperlukan, menyebabkan peningkatan penggunaan memori secara bertahap. Lihat [Pendekatan Manajemen Memori](memory-management/approaches.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"method:  \n"
"A function associated with an object or a type in Rust. See [Methods](methods-and-traits/methods.md)."
msgstr ""
"method:  \n"
"Fungsi yang terkait dengan objek atau tipe di Rust. Lihat [Method](methods-and-traits/methods.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"module:  \n"
"A namespace that contains definitions, such as functions, types, or traits, to organize code in Rust. See [Modules](modules.md)."
msgstr ""
"module:  \n"
"Namespace yang berisi definisi, seperti fungsi, tipe, atau trait, untuk mengorganisasi kode di Rust. Lihat [Modul](modules.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"move:  \n"
"The transfer of ownership of a value from one variable to another in Rust. See [Move Semantics](memory-management/move.md)."
msgstr ""
"move:  \n"
"Pemindahan ownership suatu nilai dari satu variabel ke variabel lain di Rust. Lihat [Semantik Move](memory-management/move.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"mutable:  \n"
"A property in Rust that allows [variables](types-and-values/variables.md) to be modified after they have been declared."
msgstr ""
"mutable:  \n"
"Properti di Rust yang memungkinkan [variabel](types-and-values/variables.md) diubah setelah dideklarasikan."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"ownership:  \n"
"The concept in Rust that defines which part of the code is responsible for managing the memory associated with a value. See [Ownership](memory-management/ownership.md)."
msgstr ""
"ownership:  \n"
"Konsep di Rust yang menentukan bagian kode mana yang bertanggung jawab mengelola memori terkait suatu nilai. Lihat [Ownership](memory-management/ownership.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"panic:  \n"
"An unrecoverable error condition in Rust that results in the termination of the program. See [Panics](error-handling/panics.md)."
msgstr ""
"panic:  \n"
"Kondisi error yang tidak dapat dipulihkan di Rust yang mengakibatkan penghentian program. Lihat [Panic](error-handling/panics.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"pattern:  \n"
"A combination of values, literals, or structures that can be matched against an expression in Rust. See [Pattern Matching](pattern-matching.md)."
msgstr ""
"pattern:  \n"
"Kombinasi nilai, literal, atau struktur yang dapat dicocokkan dengan suatu expression di Rust. Lihat [Pattern Matching](pattern-matching.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"payload:  \n"
"The data or information carried by a message, event, or data structure."
msgstr ""
"payload:  \n"
"Data atau informasi yang dibawa oleh pesan, event, atau struktur data."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"receiver:  \n"
"The first parameter in a Rust [method](methods-and-traits/methods.md) that represents the instance on which the method is called."
msgstr ""
"receiver:  \n"
"Parameter pertama dalam [method](methods-and-traits/methods.md) Rust yang merepresentasikan instance tempat method dipanggil."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"reference:  \n"
"A non-owning pointer to a value that borrows it without transferring ownership. References can be [shared (immutable)](references/shared.md) or [exclusive (mutable)](references/exclusive.md)."
msgstr ""
"reference:  \n"
"Pointer non-owning ke suatu nilai yang meminjamnya tanpa memindahkan ownership. Reference dapat berupa [shared (immutable)](references/shared.md) atau [exclusive (mutable)](references/exclusive.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"reference counting:  \n"
"A memory management technique in which the number of references to an object is tracked, and the object is deallocated when the count reaches zero. See [Rc](smart-pointers/rc.md)."
msgstr ""
"reference counting:  \n"
"Teknik manajemen memori ketika jumlah reference ke suatu objek dilacak, dan objek dibebaskan ketika jumlahnya mencapai nol. Lihat [Rc](smart-pointers/rc.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"Rust:  \n"
"A systems programming language that focuses on safety, performance, and concurrency. See [What is Rust?](hello-world/what-is-rust.md)."
msgstr ""
"Rust:  \n"
"Bahasa pemrograman sistem yang berfokus pada keamanan, performa, dan konkurensi. Lihat [Apa Itu Rust?](hello-world/what-is-rust.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"safe:  \n"
"Refers to code that adheres to Rust's ownership and borrowing rules, preventing memory-related errors. See [Unsafe Rust](unsafe-rust.md)."
msgstr ""
"safe:  \n"
"Merujuk kode yang mematuhi aturan ownership dan borrowing Rust, sehingga mencegah error terkait memori. Lihat [Unsafe Rust](unsafe-rust.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"slice:  \n"
"A dynamically-sized view into a contiguous sequence, such as an array or vector. Unlike arrays, slices have a size determined at runtime. See [Slices](references/slices.md)."
msgstr ""
"slice:  \n"
"View berukuran dinamis ke rangkaian bersebelahan, seperti array atau vector. Berbeda dari array, ukuran slice ditentukan pada runtime. Lihat [Slice](references/slices.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"scope:  \n"
"The region of a program where a variable is valid and can be used. See [Blocks and Scopes](control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md)."
msgstr ""
"scope:  \n"
"Region program tempat variabel valid dan dapat digunakan. Lihat [Block dan Scope](control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"standard library:  \n"
"A collection of modules providing essential functionality in Rust. See [Standard Library](std-types/std.md)."
msgstr ""
"standard library:  \n"
"Kumpulan modul yang menyediakan fungsionalitas esensial di Rust. Lihat [Standard Library](std-types/std.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"static:  \n"
"A keyword in Rust used to define static variables or items with a `'static` lifetime. See [static](user-defined-types/static.md)."
msgstr ""
"static:  \n"
"Keyword di Rust yang digunakan untuk mendefinisikan variabel static atau item dengan lifetime `'static`. Lihat [static](user-defined-types/static.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"string:  \n"
"A data type storing textual data. See [Strings](references/strings.md)."
msgstr ""
"string:  \n"
"Tipe data yang menyimpan data teks. Lihat [String](references/strings.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"struct:  \n"
"A composite data type in Rust that groups together variables of different types under a single name. See [Structs](user-defined-types/named-structs.md)."
msgstr ""
"struct:  \n"
"Tipe data komposit di Rust yang mengelompokkan variabel bertipe berbeda di bawah satu nama. Lihat [Struct](user-defined-types/named-structs.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"test:  \n"
"A function that tests the correctness of other code. Rust has a built-in test runner. See [Testing](testing.md)."
msgstr ""
"test:  \n"
"Fungsi yang menguji kebenaran kode lain. Rust memiliki test runner bawaan. Lihat [Testing](testing.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"thread:  \n"
"A separate sequence of execution in a program, allowing concurrent execution. See [Threads](concurrency/threads.md)."
msgstr ""
"thread:  \n"
"Urutan eksekusi terpisah dalam program, memungkinkan eksekusi konkuren. Lihat [Thread](concurrency/threads.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"thread safety:  \n"
"The property of a program that ensures correct behavior in a multithreaded environment. See [Send and Sync](concurrency/send-sync.md)."
msgstr ""
"thread safety:  \n"
"Properti program yang memastikan perilaku benar dalam lingkungan multithread. Lihat [Send dan Sync](concurrency/send-sync.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"trait:  \n"
"A collection of methods defined for an unknown type, providing a way to achieve polymorphism in Rust. See [Traits](methods-and-traits/traits.md)."
msgstr ""
"trait:  \n"
"Kumpulan method yang didefinisikan untuk tipe yang tidak diketahui, menyediakan cara mencapai polimorfisme di Rust. Lihat [Trait](methods-and-traits/traits.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"trait bound:  \n"
"An abstraction where you can require types to implement some traits of your interest. See [Trait Bounds](generics/trait-bounds.md)."
msgstr ""
"trait bound:  \n"
"Abstraksi ketika Anda dapat mewajibkan tipe mengimplementasikan beberapa trait yang Anda minati. Lihat [Trait Bound](generics/trait-bounds.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"tuple:  \n"
"A composite data type that contains variables of different types. Tuple fields have no names, and are accessed by their ordinal numbers. See [Tuples](tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md)."
msgstr ""
"tuple:  \n"
"Tipe data komposit yang berisi variabel bertipe berbeda. Field tuple tidak memiliki nama, dan diakses berdasarkan nomor urutnya. Lihat [Tuple](tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"type:  \n"
"A classification that specifies which operations can be performed on values of a particular kind in Rust. See [Types and Values](types-and-values.md)."
msgstr ""
"type:  \n"
"Klasifikasi yang menentukan operasi apa yang dapat dilakukan pada nilai jenis tertentu di Rust. Lihat [Tipe dan Nilai](types-and-values.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"type inference:  \n"
"The ability of the Rust compiler to deduce the type of a variable or expression. See [Type Inference](types-and-values/inference.md)."
msgstr ""
"type inference:  \n"
"Kemampuan compiler Rust menyimpulkan tipe suatu variabel atau expression. Lihat [Type Inference](types-and-values/inference.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"undefined behavior:  \n"
"Actions or conditions in Rust that have no specified result, often leading to unpredictable program behavior. See [Unsafe Rust](unsafe-rust.md)."
msgstr ""
"undefined behavior:  \n"
"Tindakan atau kondisi di Rust yang tidak memiliki hasil yang ditentukan, sering menyebabkan perilaku program tak terduga. Lihat [Unsafe Rust](unsafe-rust.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"union:  \n"
"A data type that can hold values of different types but only one at a time. See [Unions](unsafe-rust/unions.md)."
msgstr ""
"union:  \n"
"Tipe data yang dapat menyimpan nilai bertipe berbeda tetapi hanya satu pada satu waktu. Lihat [Union](unsafe-rust/unions.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"unit test:  \n"
"Rust comes with built-in support for running small unit tests and larger integration tests. See [Unit Tests](testing/unit-tests.md)."
msgstr ""
"unit test:  \n"
"Rust hadir dengan dukungan bawaan untuk menjalankan unit test kecil dan integration test yang lebih besar. Lihat [Unit Test](testing/unit-tests.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"unit type:  \n"
"Type that holds no data, written as a tuple with no members. See speaker notes on [Functions](control-flow-basics/functions.html)."
msgstr ""
"unit type:  \n"
"Tipe yang tidak menyimpan data, ditulis sebagai tuple tanpa anggota. Lihat catatan pembicara tentang [Fungsi](control-flow-basics/functions.html)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"unsafe:  \n"
"The subset of Rust which allows you to trigger _undefined behavior_. See [Unsafe Rust](unsafe-rust/unsafe.md)."
msgstr ""
"unsafe:  \n"
"Subset Rust yang memungkinkan Anda memicu _undefined behavior_. Lihat [Unsafe Rust](unsafe-rust/unsafe.md)."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"variable:  \n"
"A memory location storing data. Variables are valid in a _scope_. See [Variables](types-and-values/variables.md)."
msgstr ""
"variable:  \n"
"Lokasi memori yang menyimpan data. Variabel valid dalam suatu _scope_. Lihat [Variabel](types-and-values/variables.md)."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid "Other Rust Resources"
msgstr "Sumber Daya Rust Lain"

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"The Rust community has created a wealth of high-quality and free resources "
"online."
msgstr ""
"Komunitas Rust telah menciptakan banyak sumber daya daring berkualitas "
"tinggi dan gratis."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid "Official Documentation"
msgstr "Dokumentasi Resmi"

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid "The Rust project hosts many resources. These cover Rust in general:"
msgstr ""
"Proyek Rust menghosting banyak sumber daya. Sumber daya ini mencakup Rust "
"secara umum:"

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[The Rust Programming Language](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/): the "
"canonical free book about Rust. Covers the language in detail and includes a"
" few projects for people to build."
msgstr ""
"[The Rust Programming Language](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/): buku "
"gratis kanonis tentang Rust. Membahas bahasa ini secara terperinci dan "
"menyertakan beberapa proyek untuk dibangun."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Rust By Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/): covers the "
"Rust syntax via a series of examples which showcase different constructs. "
"Sometimes includes small exercises where you are asked to expand on the code"
" in the examples."
msgstr ""
"[Rust By Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/): membahas "
"sintaks Rust melalui rangkaian contoh yang memamerkan berbagai konstruk. "
"Kadang menyertakan latihan kecil yang meminta Anda memperluas kode dalam "
"contoh."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Rust Standard Library](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/): full documentation "
"of the standard library for Rust."
msgstr ""
"[Rust Standard Library](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/): dokumentasi lengkap"
" standard library Rust."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[The Rust Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/): an incomplete "
"book which describes the Rust grammar and memory model."
msgstr ""
"[The Rust Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/): buku yang belum "
"lengkap yang mendeskripsikan tata bahasa dan model memori Rust."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Rust API Guidelines](https://rust-lang.github.io/api-guidelines/): "
"recommendations on how to design APIs."
msgstr ""
"[Rust API Guidelines](https://rust-lang.github.io/api-guidelines/): "
"rekomendasi tentang cara merancang API."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid "More specialized guides hosted on the official Rust site:"
msgstr "Panduan yang lebih khusus yang dihosting di situs resmi Rust:"

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[The Rustonomicon](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/): covers unsafe Rust, "
"including working with raw pointers and interfacing with other languages "
"(FFI)."
msgstr ""
"[The Rustonomicon](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/): membahas Unsafe "
"Rust, termasuk bekerja dengan raw pointer dan berinteraksi dengan bahasa "
"lain (FFI)."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Asynchronous Programming in Rust](https://rust-lang.github.io/async-book/):"
" covers the new asynchronous programming model which was introduced after "
"the Rust Book was written."
msgstr ""
"[Asynchronous Programming in Rust](https://rust-lang.github.io/async-book/):"
" membahas model pemrograman asinkron baru yang diperkenalkan setelah Rust "
"Book ditulis."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[The Embedded Rust Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/embedded-book/): "
"an introduction to using Rust on embedded devices without an operating "
"system."
msgstr ""
"[The Embedded Rust Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/embedded-book/): "
"pengantar penggunaan Rust pada perangkat embedded tanpa sistem operasi."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid "Unofficial Learning Material"
msgstr "Materi Pembelajaran Tidak Resmi"

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid "A small selection of other guides and tutorial for Rust:"
msgstr "Pilihan kecil panduan dan tutorial lain untuk Rust:"

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Learn Rust the Dangerous Way](http://cliffle.com/p/dangerust/): covers Rust"
" from the perspective of low-level C programmers."
msgstr ""
"[Learn Rust the Dangerous Way](http://cliffle.com/p/dangerust/): membahas "
"Rust dari perspektif programmer C tingkat rendah."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Rust for Embedded C "
"Programmers](https://opentitan.org/book/doc/rust_for_c_devs.html): covers "
"Rust from the perspective of developers who write firmware in C."
msgstr ""
"[Rust for Embedded C "
"Programmers](https://opentitan.org/book/doc/rust_for_c_devs.html): membahas "
"Rust dari perspektif developer yang menulis firmware dalam C."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Rust for professionals](https://overexact.com/rust-for-professionals/): "
"covers the syntax of Rust using side-by-side comparisons with other "
"languages such as C, C++, Java, JavaScript, and Python."
msgstr ""
"[Rust for professionals](https://overexact.com/rust-for-professionals/): "
"membahas sintaks Rust menggunakan perbandingan berdampingan dengan bahasa "
"lain seperti C, C++, Java, JavaScript, dan Python."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Rust on Exercism](https://exercism.org/tracks/rust): 100+ exercises to help"
" you learn Rust."
msgstr ""
"[Rust on Exercism](https://exercism.org/tracks/rust): 100+ latihan untuk "
"membantu Anda mempelajari Rust."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Ferrous Teaching Material](https://ferrous-systems.github.io/teaching-"
"material/index.html): a series of small presentations covering both basic "
"and advanced part of the Rust language. Other topics such as WebAssembly, "
"and async/await are also covered."
msgstr ""
"[Ferrous Teaching Material](https://ferrous-systems.github.io/teaching-"
"material/index.html): rangkaian presentasi kecil yang mencakup bagian dasar "
"dan lanjutan bahasa Rust. Topik lain seperti WebAssembly dan async/await "
"juga dibahas."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Advanced testing for Rust applications](https://rust-"
"exercises.com/advanced-testing/): a self-paced workshop that goes beyond "
"Rust's built-in testing framework. It covers `googletest`, snapshot testing,"
" mocking as well as how to write your own custom test harness."
msgstr ""
"[Advanced testing for Rust applications](https://rust-"
"exercises.com/advanced-testing/): workshop mandiri yang melampaui framework "
"testing bawaan Rust. Workshop ini mencakup `googletest`, snapshot testing, "
"mocking, serta cara menulis test harness khusus Anda sendiri."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Beginner's Series to Rust](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-"
"us/shows/beginners-series-to-rust/) and [Take your first steps with "
"Rust](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/learn/paths/rust-first-steps/): two "
"Rust guides aimed at new developers. The first is a set of 35 videos and the"
" second is a set of 11 modules which covers Rust syntax and basic "
"constructs."
msgstr ""
"[Beginner's Series to Rust](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-"
"us/shows/beginners-series-to-rust/) dan [Take your first steps with "
"Rust](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/learn/paths/rust-first-steps/): dua "
"panduan Rust yang ditujukan bagi developer baru. Yang pertama adalah "
"rangkaian 35 video dan yang kedua adalah rangkaian 11 modul yang mencakup "
"sintaks dan konstruk dasar Rust."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[Learn Rust With Entirely Too Many Linked Lists](https://rust-"
"unofficial.github.io/too-many-lists/): in-depth exploration of Rust's memory"
" management rules, through implementing a few different types of list "
"structures."
msgstr ""
"[Learn Rust With Entirely Too Many Linked Lists](https://rust-"
"unofficial.github.io/too-many-lists/): eksplorasi mendalam aturan manajemen "
"memori Rust, melalui implementasi beberapa jenis struktur list yang berbeda."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"[The Little Book of Rust Macros](https://danielkeep.github.io/tlborm/): "
"covers many details on Rust macros with practical examples."
msgstr ""
"[The Little Book of Rust Macros](https://danielkeep.github.io/tlborm/): "
"membahas banyak detail tentang macro Rust dengan contoh praktis."

#: src/other-resources.md
msgid ""
"Please see the [Little Book of Rust Books](https://lborb.github.io/book/) "
"for even more Rust books."
msgstr ""
"Silakan lihat [Little Book of Rust Books](https://lborb.github.io/book/) "
"untuk lebih banyak buku Rust."

#: src/credits.md
msgid ""
"The material here builds on top of the many great sources of Rust "
"documentation. See the page on [other resources](other-resources.md) for a "
"full list of useful resources."
msgstr ""
"Materi di sini dibangun di atas banyak sumber dokumentasi Rust yang hebat. "
"Lihat halaman [sumber daya lain](other-resources.md) untuk daftar lengkap "
"sumber daya berguna."

#: src/credits.md
msgid ""
"The material of Comprehensive Rust is licensed under the terms of the Apache"
" 2.0 license, please see "
"[`LICENSE`](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-rust/blob/main/LICENSE) "
"for details."
msgstr ""
"Materi Comprehensive Rust dilisensikan di bawah ketentuan lisensi Apache "
"2.0; lihat [`LICENSE`](https://github.com/google/comprehensive-"
"rust/blob/main/LICENSE) untuk detailnya."

#: src/credits.md
msgid "CXX"
msgstr "CXX"

#: src/credits.md
msgid ""
"The [Interoperability with C++](android/interoperability/cpp.md) section "
"uses an image from [CXX](https://cxx.rs/). Please see the `third_party/cxx/`"
" directory for details, including the license terms."
msgstr ""
"Bagian [Interoperabilitas dengan C++](android/interoperability/cpp.md) "
"menggunakan gambar dari [CXX](https://cxx.rs/). Lihat direktori "
"`third_party/cxx/` untuk detailnya, termasuk ketentuan lisensinya."

